\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Biden visit Hurricane Helene sites \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh ,Maya Yang, Joanna Walters and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 11,263 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par 02:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can find our latest US elections coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed, thanks for following along. You can find our latest US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Over 1.1m homes and businesses were still without power in the U.S. Southeast and Midwest on Wednesday after Helene slammed into the Florida Panhandle as a major hurricane on Sept. 26, according to data from PowerOutage.us.\par \par \uc2 Those outages were down from about 1.7 million on Tuesday as utilities continued to restore power. In total, the storm knocked out service to about 5.5 million customers, predominantly in the south-east. Helene\u8217\'20\'19s winds, rain and storm surge killed more than 160 people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris visit areas affected by Hurricane Helene\par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have visited Georgia and North Carolina, which were both acutely affected by Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who was in North Carolina, announced additional funding for debris removal and emergency protective measures.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the hurricane would cost billions of dollars. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress has an obligation\u8221\'20\'1D to make sure states have the necessary resources, he said.\par \par \uc2 Harris, in Georgia, handed out meals and said she wanted to, \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonally take a look at the devastation, which is extraordinary.\u8221\'20\'1D She expressed admiration for how \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople are coming together. People are helping perfect strangers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here for the long haul,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Harris also toured a Red Cross relief center and received a briefing from local officials, praising those working to \u8220\'20\'1Cmeet the needs of people who must be seen and must be heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just tuning in: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cresorted to crimes\u8221\'20\'1D in a failed bid to cling to power after losing the 2020 election, federal prosecutors said in a newly unsealed court filing that argues that the former US president is not entitled to immunity from prosecution.\par \par \uc2 The filing was unsealed on Wednesday. It was submitted by special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team following a supreme court opinion that conferred broad immunity on former presidents and narrowed the scope of the prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team have employed a delaying strategy in all the numerous legal cases that Trump faces that has mostly been successful.\par \par \uc2 The 165-page filing is probably the last opportunity for prosecutors to detail their case against Trump before the 5 November election given there will not be a trial before Trump faces the Democratic vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors laid out details including an allegation that a White House staffer heard Trump tell family members that it did not matter if he won or lost the election, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou still have to fight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The new filing cites previously unknown accounts offered by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest aides to paint a portrait of an \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly desperate\u8221\'20\'1D president who, while losing his grip on the White House, \u8220\'20\'1Cused deceit to target every stage of the electoral process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo what?\u8221\'20\'1D the filing quotes Trump as telling an aide after being alerted that his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , was in potential danger after a crowd of violent supporters stormed the US Capitol on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe details don\u8217\'20\'19t matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, when told by an adviser that a lawyer who was mounting his legal challenges would not be able to prove the false allegations in court, the filing states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/trump-crimes-2020-election-unsealed-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel reveals new details of Trump bid to overturn 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Per the press pool report: Governor Roy Cooper, who was seated directly to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s right, introduced Biden, saying that an entire region of the state was still in a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cooper said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful\u8221\'20\'1D for the \u8220\'20\'1Cquick\u8221\'20\'1D action and the \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive surge of help.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. President, we know we\u8217\'20\'19ve made a lot of asks of you \u8211\'20\'13 and we are grateful,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to be a long and difficult recovery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is what Biden said in North Carolina, according to the press pool report:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a moment like this we put politics aside,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1COur job is to help as many people as we can, as quickly as we can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said he\u8217\'20\'19d flown over a lot of disaster areas before, but was struck by the scenes he saw earlier today in the Asheville area. He said he could not \u8220\'20\'1Cimagine what it must have been like\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Call that rain came down,\u8221\'20\'1D remarking about how much of Asheville is underwater.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the hurricane would cost billions of dollars. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress has an obligation\u8221\'20\'1D to make sure states have the necessary resources, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody can deny the impact of the climate crisis any more, at least I hope they don\u8217\'20\'19t. They must be brain dead if they do,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CStorm like Helene are getting stronger and stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in North Carolina, where he has \u8220\'20\'1Cmade additional disaster assistance available to the State of North Carolina by authorizing an increase in the level of federal funding for emergency work undertaken in the State of North Carolina as a result of Tropical Storm Helene\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the President\u8217\'20\'19s order today, the Federal funds for debris removal and emergency protective measures, including direct Federal assistance has been increased to 100 percent of the total eligible costs for 180 days from the start of the incident period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visits Georgia in wake of Hurricane Helene\par \par \uc2 Here is the Associated Press\u8217\'20\'19s report on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visiting Augusta, Georgia:\par \par \uc2 Harris handed out meals, embraced a shaken family and surveyed Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary\u8221\'20\'1D path of destruction through Georgia on Wednesday as she left the campaign trail to pledge federal help and personally take in scenes of toppled trees, damaged homes and lives upended.\par \par \uc2 She visited Augusta, where power lines stretched along the sidewalk and utility poles lay cracked and broken. The vice president spoke from a lectern erected in front of a house with a fallen tree teetering on its roof, acknowledging those who had died in the disaster while also trying to project a tone of unity and hope for communities now facing long and expensive rebuilds.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she wanted to, \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonally take a look at the devastation, which is extraordinary.\u8221\'20\'1D She expressed admiration for how \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople are coming together. People are helping perfect strangers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic presidential nominee said that shows \u8220\'20\'1Cthe vast majority of us have so much more in common than what separates us,\u8221\'20\'1D an echo of a line she frequently uses on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 Before delivering her remarks, Harris could be seen embracing and huddling with a family of five grappling with the storm\u8217\'20\'19s aftermath.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here for the long haul,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Harris also toured a Red Cross relief center and received a briefing from local officials, praising those working to \u8220\'20\'1Cmeet the needs of people who must be seen and must be heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am now listening,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz is speaking in Reading, the Pennsylvanian city with the highest number of Latino voters.\par \par \uc2 The Latino vote could be key to this election.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Joseph Contreras explains, their importance in presidential races has been steadily growing over the past 50 years, and Latinos are projected to represent nearly 15% of eligible voters nationwide by November.\par \par \uc2 Historically, Latinos have ranked among the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s most reliable sources of votes, in about the same league as Black and Jewish voters. But the party\u8217\'20\'19s once commanding advantage has been shrinking. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  trounced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  among Latinos nationwide in 2016 by a factor of 81% to 16%, yet four years later the former president upped his share to one out of every four votes cast by Latinos.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is expected to hold a campaign event in Pennsylvania any minute as he campaigns in the swing state with the highest number of electoral college votes (19) \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring that to you live.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US politics coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance took a self-proclaimed victory lap after his vice-presidential debate against the Democrat \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , appearing on Wednesday at a campaign rally in the crucial battleground state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vance told supporters in Auburn Hills that he thought the debate went \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty well\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cbs-news-vp-debate-poll-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 snap}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/02/politico-snap-poll-division-debate-00182131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  showed viewers considered it to be a tie between the two vice-presidential candidates.\par \par \uc2 Departing from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/vice-presidential-debate-walz-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generally civil}}}\uc2  tone of the debate, Vance mocked Walz over his biggest gaffe of the night, in which the Democratic governor said he was friends with school shooters. (Walz seemingly meant to say he was friends with victims of school shootings.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was probably only the third or fourth dumbest comment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  made that night,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be honest, I feel a little bad for Governor Walz. And the reason I feel bad for him is because he has to defend the indefensible, and that is the record of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his prepared remarks, Vance did not touch on his weakest moment in the debate, when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused}}}\uc2  to acknowledge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s loss in the 2020 presidential race. But when Vance took questions from the media after his speech, a reporter did ask him about the exchange, and he again sidestepped the question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe media is obsessed with talking about the election of four years ago. I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on the election of 33 days from now because I want to throw \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  out of office and get back to commonsense economic policies,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/walz-vance-debate-victory-lap-michigan-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance takes victory lap and mocks Tim Walz over debate gaffe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cresorted to crimes\u8221\'20\'1D in a failed attempt to keep power after losing the 2020 election, federal prosecutors said in newly unsealed evidence arguing that the former president shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be immune from prosecution. Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  unsealed the filing, which was submitted by submitted by special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team following a supreme court opinion that conferred broad immunity on former presidents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to visit communities in Florida and Georgia tomorrow that have been hit by Hurricane Helene, the White House has announced. That follows his visit to the Carolinas today. The president approved a major disaster declaration for the state of Virginia amid the devastating impacts of Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Implementing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation campaign could cost the federal government as much as $88b per year on average, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanimmigrationcouncil.org/research/mass-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new analysis released on Wednesday.}}}\uc2  If elected, Trump has vowed to carry out the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation operation\u8221\'20\'1D in US history, but he has offered few concrete details about how he would achieve a campaign of such scale \u8211\'20\'13 and at what cost.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden has approved a major disaster declaration for the state of Virginia amid the devastating impacts of Hurricane Helene. The White House said the president ordered federal aid to supplement commonwealth and local recovery efforts in the areas affected by Helene.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-presidential hopefuls debated for 90 minutes on Tuesday night, but the Harris campaign wants Americans to remember one moment, a split-second reply that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  called a \u8220\'20\'1Cdamning non-answer\u8221\'20\'1D. Just hours after the primetime event concluded, with viewers split over a winner and analysts praising JD Vance for the more polished performance, the Harris campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ax0KIhHFnaE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  launched an ad }}}\uc2  highlighting the moment the Republican refused to say whether Trump lost the 2020 election. (He did.)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vance returned to the sharper tone that\u8217\'20\'19s more his norm on the campaign trail during a rally in Michigan. Walz, meanwhile, at a Pennsylvania rally said that Vance\u8217\'20\'19s obfuscations about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies and legacy amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cgaslighting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The youth-led March for Our Lives gun control movement which emerged following the deadly Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school shooting in 2018 has condemned JD Vance for his \u8220\'20\'1Chypocrisy\u8221\'20\'1D on gun violence prevention, after he suggested schools build \u8220\'20\'1Cstronger doors\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent shooters,.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There was no clear winner of last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate among registered voters quizzed in another snap poll last night, this one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/02/politics/election-poll-walz-vance-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  for CNN by polling firm SSRS. After Walz and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance}}}\uc2  had a constructive debate, CNN reported that their viewers who were polled thought better of both candidates after the debate than they had before.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes show on \uc2 CBS\uc2  will feature an interview solely with Harris, after the network said Trump accepted an invitation and then backed out. \u8220\'20\'1CA 60 Minutes candidate hour will feature only \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19d previously agreed to be on the show, decided not to participate in the Monday, October 7 special,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-election-special-harris-trump-oct-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House national security adviser Jake Sullivan called Iran\u8217\'20\'19s missile attack on Israel yesterday a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant escalation\u8221\'20\'1D in the Middle East conflict, although he said it was ultimately \u8220\'20\'1Cdefeated and ineffective\u8221\'20\'1D, in part because of assistance from the US military in shooting down some of the inbound missiles. Biden said his administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully supportive\u8221\'20\'1D of Israel and that he\u8217\'20\'19s in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussion\u8221\'20\'1D with aides about what the appropriate response should be.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Harris faces triple trouble, even before October\u8217\'20\'19s inevitable surprises\par \par \uc2 100\u8221\'20\'1D was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1841171575451570672"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spelled out in giant numbers}}}\uc2  on the White House north lawn on Tuesday. It was a birthday tribute to the former US president \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , who served only one term after being buffeted by external events such as high inflation and a hostage crisis in Iran.\par \par \uc2 The current occupant of the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , must know the feeling as he fights three fires at once. Iran has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/01/israel-vows-to-retaliate-after-iran-launches-unprecedented-missile-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched at least 180 missiles}}}\uc2  into Israel, six US states are still reeling from Hurricane Helene, and ports from Maine to Texas shut down as about 45,000 dockworkers went on strike.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Carter, Biden already knows his fate: he is not seeking re-election next month. But what remains uncertain is whether the trio of troubles will drag down his vice-president and would-be successor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 . Certainly her rival, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , smells an opportunity to tar her with the same brush of chaos.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world is on fire and spiralling out of control,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a written statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no leadership, no one running the country. We have a non-existent president in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and a completely absent vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , who is too busy fundraising in San Francisco.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Will it stick? No one can be sure. Democrats must again be breathing a sigh of relief that they jettisoned Biden after his miserable debate performance in June. The president steeped in foreign policy is running at one catastrophe a year: the botched Afghanistan withdrawal of 2021, the Russian invasion of Ukraine in 2022 and the deadly \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack on Israel in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/middle-east-hurricane-helene-dockworker-strikes-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris faces triple trouble, even before October\u8217\'20\'19s inevitable surprises}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the unsealed court documents released today, prosecutors detail each time Trump tried to pressure his former vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to accept that their was fraud in the 2020 elections.\par \par \uc2 enltrHere are all the times \u8212\'20\'14 according to Jack Smith \u8212\'20\'14 Trump tried to pressure \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  said he saw no evidence of fraud. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cDKD4xGgPb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cDKD4xGgPb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1841584984521359457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has reaised more than $160m in September, according to Reuters, and have about $283m of cash on hand.\par \par \uc2 The campaign raised $130 million in August \u8211\'20\'13 just a third of that Harris raised ($361m) that month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Exclusive: Melania Trump passionately defends \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in upcoming memoir\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump made an extraordinary declaration in an eagerly awaited memoir to be published a month from election day: she is a passionate supporter of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her own body \u8211\'20\'13 including the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is imperative to guarantee that women have autonomy in deciding their preference of having children, based on their own convictions, free from any intervention or pressure from the government,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican nominee\u8217\'20\'19s wife writes, amid a campaign in which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s threats to women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights have played a central role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy should anyone other than the woman herself have the power to determine what she does with her own body? A woman\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental right of individual liberty, to her own life, grants her the authority to terminate her pregnancy if she wishes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRestricting a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose whether to terminate an unwanted pregnancy is the same as denying her control over her own body. I have carried this belief with me throughout my entire adult life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump has rarely expressed political views in public. The book, which reveals the former first lady to be so firmly out of step with most of her own party, Melania, will be published in the US next Tuesday. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/melania-trump-memoir-defends-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania Trump passionately defends \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in upcoming memoir}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 An estimated 43.15 million viewers watched the vice-presidential debate last night, according to Nielsen.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, about 67.1 million tuned into the presidential debate between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in September.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz compares Vance to Pence in first rally since debate\par \par \uc2 At his rally in Pennsylvania, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  warned that JD Vance seems much more willing than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to interfere with electoral integrity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a reason \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t on that stage with me,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said of his debate last night. \u8220\'20\'1CHe chose the constitution over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 Senator Vance made it clear he will always make a different choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence certified the 2020 election results, as required by the constitution, despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s suggestions that he could have resisted.\par \par \uc2 Vance has said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have done as Pence did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I had been vice-president, I would have told the states, like Pennsylvania, Georgia and so many others, that we needed to have multiple slates of electors, and I think the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  should have fought over it from there,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/jd-vance-defends-trump-claims-invoking-jean-carroll/story?id=106925954"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with ABC News}}}\uc2  earlier this year. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the legitimate way to deal with an election that a lot of folks, including me, think had a lot of problems in 2020. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s what we should have done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The 165-page document details prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is facing criminal charges accusing him of a conspiracy to obstruct the certification of the election, defraud the US and interfere with Americans\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 It will likely be their last opportunity to lay out their case before the upcoming election day on 5 November. Trump, JD Vance and their supporters have continued to spread doubts about the system.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Sam Levine laid out the stakes here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-overturn-result-presidential-election-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A different level than 2020\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to steal election is taking shape}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge unseals new evidence in Trump election case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cresorted to crimes\u8221\'20\'1D in a failed attempt to keep power after losing the 2020 election, federal prosecutors said in newly unsealed evidence arguing that the former president shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be immune from prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2  unsealed the filing, which was submitted by submitted by special counsel Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team following a supreme court opinion that conferred broad immunity on former presidents.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors argue that Trump in this case should not be immune because he was acting in the capacity of a candidate, not president, when he attempted to challenge the election results. The prosecutors allege:\par \par \uc2 Working with a team of private co-conspirators, the defendant acted as a candidate when he pursued multiple criminal means to disrupt, through fraud and deceit, the government function by which votes are collected and counted \u8212\'20\'14 a function in which the defendant, as President, had no official role.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/trump-crimes-2020-election-unsealed-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump \u8216\'20\'18resorted to crimes\u8217\'20\'19 after losing 2020 election, federal prosecutors say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, who took a much less copacetic tone at his rally today than at the debate last night, again refused to admit the validity of the 2020 election results earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: Why did you not answer the question last night during the debate about who won the 2020 presidential election?\par \par \uc2 Vance: The media is obsessed with talking about the election from four years ago\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LTmvyUPRGf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LTmvyUPRGf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1841556470502195365?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz accuses JD Vance of 'gaslighting'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assessment of the debate last night: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s gaslighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Vance is a slick talker,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walz, who said he and his opponent had a \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil but spirited debate\u8221\'20\'1D. But be also criticized Vance\u8217\'20\'19s many obfuscations last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe moment that really stuck out is I just asked the simplest of all questions that that every single American should be able to answer. I asked him if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 election,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe refused to answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has just made his entrance at the rally in York, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The crowd cheered loudly with many craning their necks to get a glimpse of the governor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  of Pennsylvania is currently addressing a rally in York, Pennsylvania where \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is set to make an appearance.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to an energized audience, Fetterman said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou delivered to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 and now your next mission is to ensure that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  [wins].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors could bring more charges against Eric Adams\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors said they may bring additional charges against New York City mayor Eric Adams.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, federal prosecutors said they are pursing \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral related investigations\u8221\'20\'1D surrounding Adams\u8217\'20\'19s corruption probe after he was charged last week with taking bribes and foreign campaign contributions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/new-york-city-mayor-eric-adams-be76fce59764a33968d1bb5014fa6550"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to }}}\uc2  the Associated Press, assistant US attorney Hagan Scotten said that it is \u8220\'20\'1Cquite likely\u8221\'20\'1D that prosecutors will seek a superseding indictment and that it is \u8220\'20\'1Cpossible\u8221\'20\'1D that more charges will be brought against Adams.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are several related investigations here,\u8221\'20\'1D Scotten told US district judge Dale Ho during a status hearing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 March for Our Lives decries Vance's 'hypocrisy' on gun violence prevention\par \par \uc2 The youth-led March for Our Lives gun control movement which emerged following the deadly Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school shooting in 2018 has condemned JD Vance for his \u8220\'20\'1Chypocrisy\u8221\'20\'1D on gun violence prevention.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Wednesday following last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice presidential debate where Vance urged schools build \u8220\'20\'1Cstronger doors\u8221\'20\'1D to prevent shooters, the movement said:\par \par \uc2 Despite clear evidence that loose gun laws lead to more deaths, Vance doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to talk about guns \u8211\'20\'13 he wants to talk about \u8216\'20\'18mental health\u8217\'20\'19 and armed guards at schools. Let\u8217\'20\'19s talk about it. Vance opposed the Bipartisan Safer Communities Act that invested billions in school-based mental wellness, instead arguing that we should arm teachers. And from Parkland to Uvalde, time and time again, armed school officers do not prevent school shootings.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Vance, who believes school shootings are a \u8216\'20\'18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw2.nyl.as/t1/255/52ju6mbcwyyo0noquar8cwq7k/3/2cef5f064be4bfac1a1b31e1181c72796db33d2dd03c813756c48adeb8f3ecbf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact of life}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19, Walz recognizes we can and must end gun violence. As the Minnesota governor, Walz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw2.nyl.as/t1/255/52ju6mbcwyyo0noquar8cwq7k/4/e924fad4430277d9fe839b222ce08c531009135ca8a4d52fd2e0305a51be8361"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  commonsense laws that prevent gun violence long before someone picks up a gun.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance mocks Walz's 'friends with school shooters' debate remark\par \par \uc2 Abandoning the civil tone of the VP debate last night, JD Vance came out swinging against \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as he campaigned in the battleground state of Michigan this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to voters in Auburn Hills, Vance said he thought the debate went \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty well,\u8221\'20\'1D as snap polls indicated voters considered it to be a tie between the two vice-presidential candidates.\par \par \uc2 Vance then mocked Walz over the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s biggest gaffe of the night, in which he said he was friends with school shooters. (Walz seemingly meant to say he was friends with victims of school shootings.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was probably only the third or fourth dumbest comment \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  made that night,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CI gotta be honest, I feel a little bad for Governor Walz. And the reason I feel bad for him is because he has to defend the indefensible, and that is the record of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance at first rally since debate praises own performance\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee for vice-president, JD Vance, is in Auburn Hills, Michigan, and has just taken the stage for a rally in this crucial battleground state, the day after his debate last night against his Democratic rival, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After his relatively amiable presentation last night in what has been dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1Cmidwest nice\u8221\'20\'1D debate between the US senator from Ohio and the governor from Michigan, Vance returned to the sharper tone that\u8217\'20\'19s more his norm on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 First, he nodded to the debate last night and said: \u8220\'20\'1CI thought it went pretty well,\u8221\'20\'1D as the crowd at a manufacturing facility he\u8217\'20\'19s visiting began chanting \u8220\'20\'1CJD, JD, JD.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance said he talked to the man at the top of the GOP ticket, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after the debate and Trump seized on Walz\u8217\'20\'19s presumed slip of the tongue that he is friends with school shooters \u8211\'20\'13 when it\u8217\'20\'19s widely understood he meant the victims of school shooters, having been talking at the debate about meeting with parents who\u8217\'20\'19d lost their children to the school shooting at Sandy Hook, Connecticut in 2012.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s probably the third or fourth dumbest comment he made that night,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said, adding that he feels \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit bad\u8221\'20\'1D for Walz because he has to defend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s something of a contrast to his relatively convivial style with Walz last night, when he was critical of Harris but less so about and to Walz.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Security for America\u8217\'20\'19s election systems has become so robust that Russia, Iran or any other foreign adversary will not be able to alter the outcome of this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential race, the head of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s cybersecurity agency said today.\par \par \uc2 Jen Easterly told the Associated Press in an interview that voting, ballot-counting and other election infrastructure is more secure today than it\u8217\'20\'19s ever been.\par \par \uc2 Malicious actors, even if they tried, could not have an impact at scale such that there would be a material effect on the outcome of the election,\u8221\'20\'1D said Easterly, director of the \uc2 US Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Federal agencies have warned of growing attempts by Russia and Iran in particular to influence voters before the November 5 election and election conspiracy theories have left millions of Americans doubting the validity of election results.\par \par \uc2 Easterly said those efforts are primarily aimed at sowing discord among Americans and undermining faith in the security of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello again, US politics live blog readers, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is en route to the Carolinas to survey and be briefed on the appalling damage and death toll from the aftermath of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is en route to Georgia for the same reason.\par \par \uc2 Fresh from last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, JD Vance is about to speak at a rally in Michigan and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is joining \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  in Pennsylvania and will appear at a rally in about an hour.\par \par \uc2 So much news to come and we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you posted as it happens. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to visit communities in Florida and Georgia tomorrow that have been hit by Hurricane Helene, the White House has announced. That follows his visit to the Carolinas today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Implementing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation campaign could cost the federal government as much as $88b per year on average, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanimmigrationcouncil.org/research/mass-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new analysis released on Wednesday.}}}\uc2  If elected, Trump has vowed to carry out the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation operation\u8221\'20\'1D in US history, but he has offered few concrete details about how he would achieve a campaign of such scale \u8211\'20\'13 and at what cost.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden has approved a major disaster declaration for the state of Virginia amid the devastating impacts of Hurricane Helene. The White House said the president ordered federal aid to supplement commonwealth and local recovery efforts in the areas affected by Helene.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-presidential hopefuls debated for 90 minutes on Tuesday night, but the Harris campaign wants Americans to remember one moment, a split-second reply that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  called a \u8220\'20\'1Cdamning non-answer\u8221\'20\'1D. Just hours after the primetime event concluded, with viewers split over a winner and analysts praising JD Vance for the more polished performance, the Harris campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ax0KIhHFnaE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  launched an ad }}}\uc2  highlighting the moment the Republican refused to say whether Trump lost the 2020 election. (He did.)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes show on \uc2 CBS\uc2  will feature an interview solely with Harris, after the network said Trump accepted an invitation and then backed out. \u8220\'20\'1CA 60 Minutes candidate hour will feature only \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19d previously agreed to be on the show, decided not to participate in the Monday, October 7 special,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-election-special-harris-trump-oct-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There was no clear winner of last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate among registered voters quizzed in another snap poll last night, this one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/02/politics/election-poll-walz-vance-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  for CNN by polling firm SSRS. After Walz and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance}}}\uc2  had a constructive debate, CNN reported that their viewers who were polled thought better of both candidates after the debate than they had before.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House national security adviser Jake Sullivan called Iran\u8217\'20\'19s missile attack on Israel yesterday a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant escalation\u8221\'20\'1D in the Middle East conflict, although he said it was ultimately \u8220\'20\'1Cdefeated and ineffective\u8221\'20\'1D, in part because of assistance from the US military in shooting down some of the inbound missiles. Biden said his administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully supportive\u8221\'20\'1D of Israel and that he\u8217\'20\'19s in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussion\u8221\'20\'1D with aides about what the appropriate response should be.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris to visit communities hit by hurricane\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will visit communities in Florida and Georgia that have been hit by Hurricane Helene, the White House has announced.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming visits will follow his stops in North and South Carolina on Wednesday where he is set to survey the damage caused by the storm.\par \par \uc2 More than $10m has been provided directly to those who have been affected by the storm, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be in neighboring Georgia. Helene was one of the deadliest storms in recent US history and knocked out power and cellular service for millions. The death toll is nearing 180 people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP leaders are vexed as Republican Senate challengers are falling behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in voter polling.\par \par \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis reports for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, Trump is polling at an average of 8.7 percentage points above the Republican Senate nominee Bernie Moreno, RealClear Politics averages suggest. In Wisconsin, Trump has polled 2.2 points ahead of the Senate candidate \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2 ; they also both remain under 50% in the polls.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, Trump is at 49.3% compared with Kari Lake\u8217\'20\'19s 43.4%. In Nevada, Sam Brown is at 40.7% while Trump has 47.6%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democratic Senate contenders are still besting Republican candidates in \u8220\'20\'1Cevery key battleground\u8221\'20\'1D in the presidential race, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/survey-research/2024-swing-state-project/swing-state-polling-finds-deadlocked-presidential"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Cook Political report}}}\uc2 . But the site noted that their leads were tighter than in August, and that Wisconsin and Michigan Senate races could be prime opportunities for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/republican-senate-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans vexed as Senate challengers fall behind Trump in polls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has ordered the defense department to approve the deployment of up to 1,000 active-duty soldiers to reinforce the North Carolina National Guard amid the deadly impacts of Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 In an announcement issued on Wednesday, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese soldiers will speed up the delivery of life-saving supplies of food, water, and medicine to isolated communities in North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 they have the manpower and logistical capabilities to get this vital job done, and fast. They will join hundreds of North Carolina National Guard members deployed under state authorities in support of the response.\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Helene has been a storm of historic proportion. My heart goes out to everyone who has experienced unthinkable loss. We are here for you \u8211\'20\'13 and we will stay here for as long as it takes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has released the following statement on the \uc2 International Longshoremen\u8217\'20\'19s Association\uc2  port workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike is about fairness. Foreign-owned shipping companies have made record profits and executive compensation has grown. The Longshoremen, who play a vital role transporting essential goods across America, deserve a fair share of these record profits.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on the other hand, wants to pull us back to a time before workers had the freedom to organize. As president, he blocked overtime benefits for millions of workers, he appointed union busters to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and just recently, he said striking workers should be fired.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  makes empty promise after empty promise to American workers, but never delivers. He thinks our economy should only work for those who own the big skyscrapers, not those who actually build them.\par \par \uc2 As president, I will have workers\u8217\'20\'19 backs and finally pass the PRO [Protecting the Right to Organize] Act. And I will fight for an opportunity economy - where every person has the chance not just to get by but to get ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate, JD Vance is continuing his talking point of \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D by tweeting on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night was fun!\par \par \uc2 Remember: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been in power for the last 3.5 years. She opened the border. She cast the deciding vote on trillions in new spending. The border and affordability crisis is on her.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , by contrast, governed with common sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With only five weeks left till Election Day, the repeated messaging of \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D by Vance appears to be in contrast to the Harris-Walz strategy of framing their own campaign as \u8220\'20\'1Cjoy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 After JD Vance refused to acknowledge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s loss in the 2020 election during the VP debate last night, one of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s senior advisers doubled down on that stance this morning.\par \par \uc2 When CNN anchor Jim Acosta asked Trump campaign adviser \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2  whether Trump lost the 2020 race, Lewandowski sidestepped the question in much the same manner that Vance did last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy is this so difficult for the Trump campaign to answer?\u8221\'20\'1D Acosta asked. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean it\u8217\'20\'19s 2024. Did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose the 2020 election? Can you answer that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJim, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very simple. The American people are past the 2020 election,\u8221\'20\'1D Lewandowski replied. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can go back and relitigate the 2020 election, or we can look at what we can do to make America better for the everyday Americans who are struggling under Bidenomics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Acosta interjected, \u8220\'20\'1CBut, Corey, it\u8217\'20\'19s not relitigating. It\u8217\'20\'19s just a simple question: did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose the 2020 election?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lewandowski replied, \u8220\'20\'1CWhy are we talking about 2020 anymore? [Do] the American people care about the 2020 election more, or do they care about being able to put food on their table?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Acosta and Lewandowski then sparred over the definition of \u8220\'20\'1Cwidespread fraud\u8221\'20\'1D, as Trump has presented no evidence of widespread fraud in the 2020 race. Ammar Moussa, a spokesperson for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 campaign, said of the exchange: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 election. It shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be this hard to say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Wednesday following JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to acknowledge that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 presidential election during last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn January 6, the former president incited an attack on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s democracy because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 If you stand for country, democracy, and the rule of law\u8212\'20\'14our campaign has a place for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOn January 6, the former president incited an attack on our nation's democracy because he didn't like the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 If you stand for country, democracy, and the rule of law\u8212\'20\'14our campaign has a place for you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1841488310998319417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's mass deportations could cost up to $88bn a year, analysis suggests\par \par \uc2 Implementing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation campaign could cost the federal government as much as $88b per year on average, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanimmigrationcouncil.org/research/mass-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new analysis released on Wednesday.}}}\par \par \uc2 If elected, Trump has vowed to carry out the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation operation\u8221\'20\'1D in US history, but he has offered few concrete details about how he would achieve a campaign of such scale \u8211\'20\'13 and at what cost.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew! ?? We {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/immcouncil?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @immcouncil}}}\uc2  published new estimates of the costs of mass deportations. We find:\par \par \uc2 - Mass deportations would cause GDP to drop by 4.2-6.8%, more than the Great Recession.\par \par \uc2 - The annual cost to arrest, detain, process, and remove 1 million people would be $88 billion. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ram7bqCJFE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ram7bqCJFE}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xeU0Nvn9df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xeU0Nvn9df}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Aaron Reichlin-Melnick\uc2  (@ReichlinMelnick) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReichlinMelnick/status/1841467079297294481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven that in the modern immigration enforcement era the United States has never deported more than half a million immigrants per year \u8211\'20\'13 and many of those have been migrants apprehended trying to enter the US, not just those already living here\u8211\'20\'13any mass deportation proposal raises obvious questions: how, exactly, would the United States possibly carry out the largest law enforcement operation in world history? And at what cost?\u8221\'20\'1D ask the authors of the analysis, published by the \uc2 American Immigration Council\uc2 , an advocacy group for immigrant rights.\par \par \uc2 The analysis estimates the costs based on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to deport the roughly 11 million people living in the US who as of 2022 lacked permanent legal status and faced the possibility of removal. (Trump has suggested the eligible population is as high as 20 million people.)\par \par \uc2 The largest share of the cost would be spent on building detention camps to arrest, detain, process, and remove immigrants from the US. It would also likely require the government to hire additional law enforcement officers and immigration judges.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the logistical challenges, the analysis also highlights the impact it would have on the economy, especially sectors like construction and hospitality that employ large numbers of undocumented workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDue to the loss of workers across US industries, we found that mass deportation would reduce the U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) by 4.2 to 6.8%,\u8221\'20\'1D it states. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would also result in significant reduction in tax revenues for the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance and Walz to return to campaign trail following VP debate\par \par \uc2 Following last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate where both candidates kept things fairly civil, JD Vance and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are set to return to the campaign trail today.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Vance is set to deliver remarks at a campaign event in Auburn Hills, Michigan at around 1:30pm ET before delivering another set of remarks in Marne, Michigan at 5:30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Vance will kick off a bus tour through central Pennsylvania and will make stops in Harrisburg, Reading, and York where he will be joined by York native senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walz is set to deliver remarks in York at 3pm ET and will join a political engagement with local Latino leaders in Reading at 6pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden approves major disaster declaration for Virginia\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has approved a major disaster declaration for the state of Virginia amid the devastating impacts of Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the White House released a statement, saying:\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden\uc2 , Jr. declared that a major disaster exists in the Commonwealth of Virginia and ordered Federal aid to supplement Commonwealth and local recovery efforts in the areas affected by Tropical Storm Helene beginning on September 25, 2024, and continuing.\par \par \uc2 The President\u8217\'20\'19s action makes Federal funding available to affected individuals in the counties of Giles, Grayson, Smyth, Tazewell, Washington, and Wythe and the independent city of Galax.\par \par \uc2 Assistance can include grants for temporary housing and home repairs, low-cost loans to cover uninsured property losses, and other programs to help individuals and business owners recover from the effects of the disaster.\par \par \uc2 Federal funding also is available to State and eligible local governments and certain private nonprofit organizations on a cost-sharing basis for emergency work in the counties of Bedford, Bland, Buchanan, Carroll, Craig, Dickenson, Giles, Grayson, Montgomery, Pittsylvania, Pulaski, Russell, Scott, Smyth, Tazewell, Washington, \uc2 Wise\uc2 , and Wythe and the independent cities of Bristol, Covington, Danville, Galax, Norton, and Radford.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign ad boosts Vance's 'damning non-answer' on Trump election loss\par \par \uc2 The vice-presidential hopefuls debated for 90 minutes on Tuesday night, but the Harris campaign wants Americans to remember one moment, a split-second reply that \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  called a \u8220\'20\'1Cdamning non-answer \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Just hours after the primetime event concluded, with viewers split over a winner and analysts praising JD Vance for the more polished performance, the Harris campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ax0KIhHFnaE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  launched an ad }}}\uc2  highlighting the moment the Republican refused to say whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 election. (He did.)\par \par \uc2 During the final moments of the debate, Walz asked Vance to answer the question. Did Trump lose the 2020 election to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Vance replied that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfocused on the future\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a damning non-answer,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz replied.\par \par \uc2 The ad features that exchange, overlaid with images of the January 6 assault on the US Capitol. It ends with Walz telling viewers: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, I think you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a really clear choice of who\u8217\'20\'19s going to honor democracy and who\u8217\'20\'19s going to honor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the Harris campaign, their internal focus group of undecided battleground state voters said the moment was Vance\u8217\'20\'19s worst of the night.\par \par \uc2 Harris hasn\u8217\'20\'19t centered her campaign around democracy the way Biden had. But the issue still has high salience for voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz heading for Pennsylvania battleground bus tour\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is heading directly from his debate with rival JD Vance in New York last night for the crucial election battleground of Pennsylvania today to begin a bus tour with one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s two Democratic US Senators, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walz and Fetterman are starting out in south central Pennsylvania with a rally in the city of York.\par \par \uc2 York county {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/2020-election/results/pennsylvania/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted heavily}}}\uc2  for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, even as the state flipped from Republican in 2016 to Democratic in 2020.\par \par \uc2 This is a further case of Dems campaigning in deeply red counties in swing states, hoping that reducing the margin of their likely loss will help to tip the finely-balanced statewide race to their party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations Security Council\uc2  has called an emergency meeting today in New York to address the spiraling conflict in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The region moved closer to a long-feared regional war on Wednesday, a day after Iran fired a barrage of missiles at Israel and Israel said it began limited ground incursions into Lebanon targeting the Iran-backed \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  militia, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, vowed late Tuesday to retaliate against Iran, which he said \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a big mistake tonight and it will pay for it\u8221\'20\'1D. An Iranian commander threatened wider strikes on infrastructure if Israel retaliates against Iran\u8217\'20\'19s territory.\par \par \uc2 Israel and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  have traded fire across the Lebanon border almost daily since the day after \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 cross-border attack on 7 October 2023, which killed 1,200 Israelis and took 250 others hostage. Israel declared war on the militant group in the Gaza Strip in response. More than 41,000 Palestinians have been killed in the territory, and just over half the dead have been women and children, according to local health officials.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is running a global live blog on the Middle East and covering all the developments as they happen. You can follow that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/02/israel-iran-attacks-latest-updates-live-hezbollah-lebanon-beirut-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump backs out of 60 Minutes interview; Harris to go ahead\par \par \uc2 There is no sign that there will be another presidential debate before the election, between Democratic nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We had the only planned vice-presidential debate last night between the Dems\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Now Monday\u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes show on \uc2 CBS\uc2  will feature an interview solely with Harris, after the network said Trump accepted an invitation and then backed out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA 60 Minutes candidate hour will feature only \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19d previously agreed to be on the show, decided not to participate in the Monday, October 7 special,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-election-special-harris-trump-oct-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . \uc2 CBS\uc2  pointed out that the show has had the tradition for half a century of inviting the two presidential candidates to sit for interviews as voters head to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Late last month, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/21/kamala-harris-second-debate-cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  an invitation from CNN for a second debate, but Trump declined. The broad consensus is that Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/14/harris-poll-debate-win-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the lone debate}}}\uc2  between her and Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican JD Vance gave more misleading statements than Democrat \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in the sole vice-presidential debate last night, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/fact-check/walz-vs-vance-debate-12-statements-examined-2024-10-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a check}}}\uc2  of some of the main facts claimed by both candidates, carried out by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The news agency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/fact-check/walz-vs-vance-debate-12-statements-examined-2024-10-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called out}}}\uc2  Vance, the US Senator from Ohio, on a key environmental point, when he said the US is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe cleanest economy in the entire world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is false. According to the \uc2 European Union\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Emissions Database for Global Atmospheric Research {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/report_2024?vis=ghgtot#emissions_table"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 report}}}\uc2 , the US was second only to China as the highest emitter of greenhouse gas emissions globally last year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance mostly dodged talking directly about the climate crisis and related solutions.\par \par \uc2 The candidates talked about school shootings, where Reuters also found fault with Vance saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe gross majority, close to 90% in some of the statistics I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen, of the gun violence in this country is committed with illegally obtained firearms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters said:\par \par \uc2 This is misleading. Most public mass shootings \u8211\'20\'13 a shooting that kills four or more people \u8211\'20\'13 between 1966 and 2019 were carried out by legally obtained handguns, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nij.ojp.gov/topics/articles/public-mass-shootings-database-amasses-details-half-century-us-mass-shootings#:~:text=most%20used%20legally%20obtained%20handguns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research, opens new tab}}}\uc2  funded by the \uc2 National Institute of Justice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reuters did not find any of the Walz statements it examined to be false. On topics including energy production, taxes, trade, poverty and healthcare costs, Reuters found Walz to be true or mostly true, with one point it declared \u8220\'20\'1Cunknown\u8221\'20\'1D and another \u8220\'20\'1Cit depends\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fact-checking the US vice-presidential debate: \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , immigration, climate and more}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz, Vance neck-and-neck among voters after debate \u8211\'20\'13 CNN poll\par \par \uc2 There was no clear winner of last night\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate among registered voters quizzed in another snap poll last night, this one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/02/politics/election-poll-walz-vance-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducted}}}\uc2  for CNN by polling firm SSRS.\par \par \uc2 After both Democrat \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and Republican JD Vance had a constructive debate, CNN reported that their viewers who were polled thought better of both candidates after the debate than they had before.\par \par \uc2 Vance, who has donned a controversial, right-wing platform and persona on the campaign trail, was very measured last night, conciliatory at times. Walz was less cheery than his rally self, but more consistent with his usual reputation of being a \u8220\'20\'1Cjoyful warrior\u8221\'20\'1D exuding reason.\par \par \uc2 CNN reported: \u8220\'20\'1CAmong debate watchers, Walz remains the candidate who\u8217\'20\'19s seen more positively and as more in touch with their needs and vision for the country. Vance \u8230\'20\'26boosted his standing \u8230\'20\'26 outperforming expectations and gaining ground on the share who perceive him as qualified. Both men, the poll finds, are viewed by a majority of debate watchers as qualified to assume the presidency if needed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Crucially, though, the cable TV network added that almost no respondents felt the need to change the way they\u8217\'20\'19ve decided to vote after watching the debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 In another interesting finding from the Politico/Focaldata snap poll conducted straight after the vice-presidential debate last night, Minnesota governor and Democratic nominee \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  polled better with younger voters, despite his being 60 years old.\par \par \uc2 GOP nominee and Ohio Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  did better with voters over 55, while he was a youthful pick for running mate by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , having just turned 40 last month.\par \par \uc2 The findings track broadly with their tickets.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/02/politico-snap-poll-division-debate-00182131?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that: \u8220\'20\'1CWalz\u8217\'20\'19s strongest ratings came from younger people, particularly those ages 25-34, those with college degrees, and Black and Latino respondents \u8211\'20\'13 all key components of the Democratic coalition that powered President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory}}}\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/13/us-election-most-secure-history-voter-fraud-false-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2020}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As we\u8217\'20\'19re talking ages, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , the Dems\u8217\'20\'19 nominee for president, will turn 60 later this month, having replaced Biden, 81, when the US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quit his re-election}}}\uc2  bid in July.\par \par \uc2 Trump is 78. Politico found from its debate poll that: \u8220\'20\'1CVance performed best with people over the age of 55, white voters and those without a college degree.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voters split 50-50 over whether Walz or Vance won debate\par \par \uc2 In a snap poll after the vice-presidential debate, voters declared there was no decisive winner and were split on who performed better, the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  or the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 JD Vanc e, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/02/politico-snap-poll-division-debate-00182131?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAsked who won Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate, voters were split 50-50 over whether it was \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  or \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , according to a POLITICO/Focaldata snap poll of likely voters conducted just after the two faced off in a studio in New York City,\u8221\'20\'1D the political news site said.\par \par \uc2 It added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe dead-heat results are a fitting reflection of the country\u8217\'20\'19s hyper-polarized politics \u8212\'20\'14 particularly as it enters the final stretch of the closest presidential election in years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats mostly thought Walz won and GOP-ers mostly thought Vance won. However, there was in interesting divergence when it came to independents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWalz had a commanding advantage with independents, 58 percent of whom sided with the Minnesota governor while 42 percent gave Vance the edge,\u8221\'20\'1D the site said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration heaped pressure on US port employers to raise their offer to secure a labor deal with dockworkers on strike for a second day on Wednesday, choking half the country\u8217\'20\'19s ocean shipping, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 The strike by the \uc2 International Longshoremen\u8217\'20\'19s Association\uc2  (ILA) union has blocked everything from food to automobile shipments across dozens of ports from Maine to Texas in a disruption analysts warn will cost the economy billions of dollars a day.\par \par \uc2 More than 38 container vessels were already backed up at US ports by Tuesday, compared with just three on Sunday before the strike, according to \uc2 Everstream Analytics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CForeign ocean carriers have made record profits since the pandemic, when Longshoremen put themselves at risk to keep ports open. It\u8217\'20\'19s time those ocean carriers offered a strong and fair contract that reflects ILA workers\u8217\'20\'19 contribution to our economy and to their record profits,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a post on X late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He directed his team to monitor for potential price gouging activity that benefits foreign ocean carriers, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House calls Iran missile attack 'significant escalation'\par \par \uc2 Iran launched at least 180 missiles into Israel on Tuesday, the latest in a series of rapidly escalating attacks between Israel and Iran and its Arab allies that threatens to push the Middle East closer to a regionwide war.\par \par \uc2 White House National Security adviser Jake Sullivan called Iran\u8217\'20\'19s missile attack a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant escalation,\u8221\'20\'1D although he said it was ultimately \u8220\'20\'1Cdefeated and ineffective,\u8221\'20\'1D in part because of assistance from the US military in shooting down some of the inbound missiles.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said his administration is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully supportive\u8221\'20\'1D of Israel and that he\u8217\'20\'19s in \u8220\'20\'1Cactive discussion\u8221\'20\'1D with aides about what the appropriate response should be to Tehran.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three weeks on from the presidential debate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance took to the stage on Tuesday night for a vice-presidential head-to-head. The two candidates largely avoided attacks on each other in what was a more policy-driven discussion.\par \par \uc2 If you live in a swing state such as Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania or Wisconsin, we would like to hear what you thought of the debate.\par \par \uc2 How do you think it went and do you feel the candidates addressed the issues important to you? What other issues would you like them to have addressed in the debate? What was your favourite moment? Did anything change your mind in any way?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/us-swing-state-voters-share-your-reaction-to-the-vice-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US swing state voters: share your reaction to the vice-presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic candidate for vice-president, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , and his Republican counterpart, JD Vance, clashed over border policy and the January 6 Capitol attack, with Walz at one point asking point blank if Vance believed former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had lost the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45am BST\par \par \uc2 There was a strange feeling as the vice-presidential debate got under way in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS}}}\uc2  News studios on Tuesday night that only intensified as 90 minutes of detailed policy discussion unfolded: was the United States in danger of regaining its sanity?\par \par \uc2 After weeks and months of being assailed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dystopian evocation of a country on the verge of self-destruction, amplified by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dire warnings of democracy in peril, here was something very different. The two vice-presidential nominees were embracing that most endangered of American political species: agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTim, I actually think I agree with you,\u8221\'20\'1D said JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, addressing his opposite number {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  during the discussion on immigration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMuch of what the senator said right there, I\u8217\'20\'19m in agreement with him,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walz, the Minnesota governor and Democratic nominee, as they turned to trade policy.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t true, of course. The two men were no closer to agreement than their bosses, who in their own presidential debate last month showed themselves to be worlds apart.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday it was as if the CBS News studio in midtown Manhattan had been transported back to a prelapsarian \u8211\'20\'13 or at least, pre-Maga \u8211\'20\'13 times. To an era when politicians could be civil, and to get on you didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to castigate your opponent as an enemy of the people.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/trump-vance-vp-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walz and Vance embrace an endangered US political species: agreement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  faced each other for the first and only vice-presidential debate of this election cycle \u8211\'20\'13 and clashed on issues including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , childcare, the cost of living and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election claims.\par \par \uc2 Here are the facts on some of the false or misleading claims offered during Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fact-checking the US vice-presidential debate: \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , immigration, climate and more}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Helene death toll now at least 166 as Biden plans to visit ravaged Carolinas\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will survey the devastation in North and South Carolina on Wednesday as rescuers continue their search for anyone still unaccounted for after Hurricane Helene caused catastrophic damage across the south-east and killed at least 166 people.\par \par \uc2 Many residents in both states were still without running water, cellular service and electricity as flood waters receded and revealed more of the death and destruction left in Helene\u8217\'20\'19s path, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to jump start this recovery process,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said Tuesday, estimating it will cost billions. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are scared to death. This is urgent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Biden is in the Carolinas, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be in neighboring Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Helene, one of the deadliest storms in recent US history, knocked out power and cellular service for millions. More than 1.2 million customers still were in the dark early Wednesday in the Carolinas and Georgia. Some residents cooked food on charcoal grills or hiked to high ground in the hopes of finding a signal to let loved ones know they are alive.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, cadaver dogs and search crews trudged through knee-deep muck and debris in the mountains of western North Carolina looking for more victims. At least 57 people were killed in Buncombe County alone, home to city of Asheville, a tourism haven known for its art galleries, breweries and outdoor activities.\par \par \uc2 In Swannanoa, a small community outside Asheville, receding flood waters revealed cars stacked on top of others and trailer homes that had floated away during the storm. Roads were caked with mud and debris and pockmarked by sinkholes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Key moments from the debate\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance refuses to say Trump lost the 2020 election in Walz debate\par \par \uc2 JD Vance refused to say whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  lost the 2020 election and continued to sidestep questions over whether he would certify a Trump loss this fall during the vice-presidential debate on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The exchange brought out some of the sharpest attacks from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential candidate and Minnesota governor, in what was otherwise a muted and civil back-and-forth with the Ohio senator.\par \par \uc2 Walz asked Vance directly whether Trump lost the 2020 election. Vance responded: \u8220\'20\'1CTim, I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on the future. Did \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  censor Americans from speaking their minds in the wake of the 2020 Covid situation?\u8221\'20\'1D Walz then cut in with one of his most aggressive attack lines of the evening: \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a damning non-answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/10/vance-electors-2020-election-00178266"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has previously said}}}\uc2  that he would have asked states to submit alternative slates of electors to Congress to continue to debate allegations of election irregularities in 2020. By the time Congress met during the last election to consider electoral votes, courts, state officials and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  had all turned away efforts to block legitimate slates of electors from being sent to Congress.\par \par \uc2 Pressed by \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderator Norah O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell on whether he would again refuse to certify the vote this year, Vance declined to answer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat President Trump has said is that there were problems in 2020, and my own belief is that we should fight about those issues, debate those issues peacefully in the public square,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s all I\u8217\'20\'19ve said and that\u8217\'20\'19s all that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said.\u8221\'20\'1D He later said that if Walz won the election with Harris, Walz would have his support.\par \par \uc2 Trump has warned of a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/trump-verbal-gaffes-ohio-rally-bloodbath"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bloodbath}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t win the election. He has also said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/donald-trump-wont-have-to-vote-anymore-fox-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporters won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote anymore}}}\uc2  if he wins in November. Both the Trump campaign and Republican allies are seeding the ground to contest a possible election loss in November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance refuses to say Trump lost the 2020 election in Walz debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s senior aides saw JD Vance as having a slick debate performance over \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , according to people close to Trump, that made his campaign appear palatable despite the former president\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly caustic threats such as vowing to prosecute his perceived enemies.\par \par \uc2 The campaign aides also believed that Vance reset the narrative over his image and likely came across in a more favorable light to undecided voters after a brutal few months of being hammered for making disparaging remarks about women as \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s favorability issue was perhaps the principal priority for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s senior aides because they saw it as potentially fixable and if so, beneficial to the Trump campaign with fewer than five weeks until election day in what has become a vanishingly close race against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Afterwards, Trump predictably claimed Vance won the debate, but a CBS News poll confirmed how vice-presidential? debates matter increasingly less in close elections compared to ground game efforts to drive turnout.\par \par \uc2 In the post-debate poll, 42% of respondents said Vance won the debate, 41% gave the win to Walz, while 17% said it was tied \u8211\'20\'13 suggesting the main takeaway remains that it is unlikely to play any material role in which campaign wins each of the seven battleground states in November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/vp-debate-jd-vance-performance-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump aides believe a polished JD Vance made campaign more palatable}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  took to the stage on Tuesday night for a vice-presidential debate that served up less drama than September\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential debate}}}\uc2 , but offered revealing differences on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , school shootings, and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Three weeks ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  had endured a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contentious hour-and-a-half}}}\uc2 , with an emotional Trump being goaded into ranting about the number of people who attend his rallies and declaring the vice-president to be a \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D, before reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/politics/trump-reportedly-planning-to-sue-abcs-david-muir-in-publicity-stunt-over-debate-faceplant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatening to sue}}}\uc2  one of the debate moderators. Harris enjoyed a brief polling uptick from that performance.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, Walz and Vance largely avoided attacks on each other, and instead concentrated their fire on each other\u8217\'20\'19s running mates. It was a more policy-driven discussion than that of their running mates\u8217\'20\'19, but one with a few gaffes that might overshadow some of the substance in coming days.\par \par \uc2 In a key exchange over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Walz, the governor of Minnesota, followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/abortion-harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s lead}}}\uc2  in using personal stories.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbrags about how great it was that he put the judges in and overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, Walz said. He noted the case of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-abortion-ban-zurawski-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Zurawski}}}\uc2 , who was denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas despite serious health complications during pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 Zurawski is now part of a group of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/texas-zurawski-women-denied-abortions-election-reproductive-rights-rcna158571"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing the state of Texas}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and a girl in Kentucky who as a child was raped by her stepfather and became pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t know [women like this], you soon will. Their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  is going to have a registry of pregnancies,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, which Vance contested.\par \par \uc2 Walz also criticized the Trump-Vance position that states should decide whether women have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not how this works. This is basic human rights. We have seen maternal mortality skyrocket in Texas, outpacing many other countries in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/vice-presidential-debate-walz-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walz and Vance clash over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and immigration in vice-presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Walz and Vance clash, politely, at policy-heavy vice presidential debate\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the blog as we wake up to reaction to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate which offered revealing differences on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , school shootings, and immigration.\par \par \uc2 It was a debate that was surprisingly civil in the final stretch of an ugly election campaign marred by inflammatory rhetoric and two assassination attempts.\par \par \uc2 The two rivals, who have forcefully attacked each other on the campaign trail, mostly struck a cordial tone, instead saving their fire for the candidates at the top of their tickets, democratic vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The most tense exchange occurred near the end of the debate, when Vance \u8211\'20\'13 who has said he would not have voted to certify the results of the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 avoided a question about whether he would challenge this year\u8217\'20\'19s vote if Trump loses.\par \par \uc2 Walz responded by blaming Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims of voter fraud for instigating the 6 January 2021, mob that attacked the US Capitol in an unsuccessful effort to prevent the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is still saying he didn\u8217\'20\'19t lose the election,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, before turning to Vance. \u8220\'20\'1CDid he lose the 2020 election?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance again sidestepped the question, instead accusing Harris of pursuing online censorship of opposing viewpoints. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a damning non-answer,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s snap poll has viewers split over who won the debate \u8211\'20\'13 but Vance narrowly wins. The poll of 574 registered voters saw 51% say that Vance won the debate, with 49% choosing Walz.\par \par \uc2 Polled before the debate, 54% of voters thought Walz was likelier to win.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241002eka200108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
