\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Fact-checking the US vice-presidential debate:  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , immigration, climate and more\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Guardian staff \par \uc2 1,034 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par 18:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Follow for fact-checking updates on statements made during the Walz and Vance debate and where they fell short\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  faced each other for the first and only vice-presidential debate of this election cycle \u8211\'20\'13 and clashed on issues including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , childcare, the cost of living and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election claims.\par \par \uc2 Here are the facts on some of the false or misleading claims offered during Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Vance on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s record as \u8216\'20\'18border\par \par \uc2 tsar\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Vance attacked Harris\u8217\'20\'19s record on the border. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that she did when she became the vice-president, when she became the appointed border tsar, was to undo \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  executive actions that opened the border,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 This contains inaccuracies.\par \par \uc2 First, Harris was never a \u8220\'20\'1Cborder tsar\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s a term invented by her critics. She had a role in the Biden administration to look into addressing the root causes of migration to the US, including safety and economic turmoil in Central American countries.\par \par \uc2 Second, she did not \u8220\'20\'1Cundo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  executive actions\u8221\'20\'1D. Presidents sign executive orders, and she was not president. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  did reverse some Trump executive orders on the border. He initially kept in place Trump-era restrictions known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/11/what-is-title-42-explainer-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Title 42}}}\uc2 , which allowed the US to turn away immigrants at the border on the grounds of preventing the spread of Covid-19, before eventually lifting them.\par \par \uc2 Vance on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role on January 6\par \par \uc2 Vance defended Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role on the day of the insurrection at the US Capitol. The Ohio senator picked out one line of his running mate\u8217\'20\'19s speech on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6 January 2021 }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 prior to the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 According to Vance, Trump \u8220\'20\'1Csaid on January 6 the protesters ought to protest peacefully\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Trump also repeatedly encouraged supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe fight like hell. And if you don\u8217\'20\'19t {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/02/trump-capitol-riot-powder-keg-impeachment-prosecutors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight like hell}}}\uc2 , you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have a country anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Vance on Trump and the Affordable Care Act\par \par \uc2 Vance claimed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  bolstered or salvaged the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\par \par \uc2 The former president cut millions in funding for helping people enroll in healthcare, repeatedly supported efforts in Congress to repeal the law and asked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  to overturn the law.\par \par \uc2 Vance on immigrants and housing prices\par \par \uc2 Vance twice implicated immigrants in driving up housing prices, though when pressed, agreed that immigration was not the \u8220\'20\'1Conly\u8221\'20\'1D contributor.\par \par \uc2 A nonpartisan analysis found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/trump-mass-deportations-detention-camps-military-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vow of mass deportation}}}\uc2  would drive up prices in several sectors and affect the availability of labor. The \uc2 Peterson Institute for International Economics\uc2  projects that the policy would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca major shock to the US economy, with substantial disruption across all sectors, especially agriculture, mining, and manufacturing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Vance said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has supported states making their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Vance claimed that Trump has said that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe proper way to handle this \u8230\'20\'26 is to let voters make these decisions, let the individual states make their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not quite right. \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to say}}}\uc2  whether he would sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban during the last debate.\par \par \uc2 Walz on Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s ambitions\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor claimed that Project 2025, the ambitious blueprint from \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  to remake the federal government under a second Trump term, would require people to register their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir Project 2025 is going to have a registry of pregnancies,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 That claim is false. Project 2025 calls for a number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictive policies on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , including reversing \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, rolling back privacy protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients and increasing surveillance by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it does not call for all pregnant people to register.\par \par \uc2 The CDC already collects information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from most of the country, but its reports are incomplete, as some states do not supply the data. Project 2025 suggests that the CDC should go so far as to cut funds from a state if it does not tell the CDC \u8220\'20\'1Cexactly how many abortions take place within its borders, at what gestational age of the child, for what reason, the mother\u8217\'20\'19s state of residence, and by what method\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance on immigrants in Springfield, Ohio\par \par \uc2 Referring to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/springfield-ohio-republicans-haitian-immigrants-lies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Springfield, Ohio}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where a number of Haitian immigrants have recently settled \u8211\'20\'13 Vance referred to immigrants with legal status as \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got schools that are overwhelmed, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got hospitals that are overwhelmed, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got housing that\u8217\'20\'19s totally unaffordable because we brought in millions of illegal immigrants to compete with Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/neo-nazis-springfield-ohio-haitian-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haitian immigrants in Springfield}}}\uc2 , as \uc2 CBS\uc2  moderator Margaret Brennan noted, have legal status. Their arrival, local residents and leaders have said, has helped revive the town, which has lost a quarter of its population since the 1960s.\par \par \uc2 Vance on the climate crisis\par \par \uc2 and manufacturing\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator has repeatedly expressed skepticism about the reality that carbon emissions have caused global heating.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, he was a bit subtle: \u8220\'20\'1COne of the things that I\u8217\'20\'19ve noticed some of our Democratic friends talking a lot about is a concern about carbon emissions, this idea that carbon emissions drives all the climate change \u8230\'20\'26 let\u8217\'20\'19s just say that\u8217\'20\'19s true, just for the sake of argument.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Vance\u8217\'20\'19s skepticism, it is indeed true. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.carbonbrief.org/analysis-why-scientists-think-100-of-global-warming-is-due-to-humans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One hundred percent}}}\uc2  of global heating since 1950 is due to human activity such as burning fossil fuels and deforestation.\par \par \uc2 Vance also took viewers on a circuitous journey to suggest that if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  really cared about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the climate crisis}}}\uc2 , she would bring back manufacturing jobs to the US.\par \par \uc2 Carbon emissions, whether they are manufactured in the US or overseas, contribute to global heating. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/biden-climate-bill-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2  of 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s landmark climate legislation \u8211\'20\'13 is greatly aimed at incentivizing domestic manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 Read more about the 2024 US election:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/01/election-vance-walz-harris-trump-vp-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance-Walz vice-presidential debate \u8211\'20\'13 live updates}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What we know so far about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance and Tim Walz\u8217\'20\'19s debate styles}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241002eka20005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
