\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 School shootings, childcare and cost of living: key takeaways from the Walz-Vance debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett \par \uc2 1,578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par 13:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As the Middle East spiraled towards full-scale war, the US vice-presidential debate focused largely on domestic issuesUS swing state voters: share your reaction to the vice-presidential debate\par \par \uc2 As the Middle East spiraled towards full-scale war, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/vice-presidential-debate-walz-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US vice presidential debate}}}\uc2  focused largely on domestic issues, like school shootings and the cost of housing, healthcare, and childcare.\par \par \uc2 The CBS News debate moderators largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to}}}\uc2  factcheck {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , asking them instead to respond to each other.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways from the debate between the Republican senator from Ohio who wrote a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/article/2024/jul/19/jd-vance-hillbilly-elegy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bestselling memoir about poverty}}}\uc2  in Appalachia and the Democratic football-coach-turned-governor of Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 Walz was plodding and failed to attack Vance. Vance was polished and played nice\par \par \uc2 Walz won his place on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in part because of his zesty and energetic attacks on Vance, whom he accused of being a faux supporter of struggling rural Americans, and of simply being \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But in the days before this debate, Walz also tried to manage expectations about his face-off with Vance, with news outlets running stories about Walz\u8217\'20\'19s nerves and his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/28/politics/tim-walz-vice-president-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 belief that he is a bad debater}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And, in fact, Walz appeared anxious and uncomfortable in his debate with Vance. Instead of mocking or attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unpopular vice-presidential pick, the Minnesota governor appeared to be working hard to land his prepared talking points, while a more relaxed Vance easily maneuvered around him.\par \par \uc2 Walz admitted that he \u8220\'20\'1Cmisspoke\u8221\'20\'1D in past comments, when he repeatedly recalled being in Hong Kong during the Tiananmen Square massacre, though news outlets found evidence he could not have been there at that exact time. Walz also said in a garbled comment on gun violence that \u8220\'20\'1Che became friends with mass shooters\u8221\'20\'1D, a gaffe that is now widely circulating in conservative media.\par \par \uc2 Vance, who has faced intense criticism for spreading racist misinformation about Haitian immigrants in Ohio, and has refused to apologize, appeared to be trying to present both himself and Trump as genial and affable moderates, describing Trump, for instance, as the savior of Obamacare, though fact-checkers noted the former president consistently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/walz-vance-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked and undermined}}}\uc2  Obamacare.\par \par \uc2 By the end of the debate, both candidates appeared to be making some efforts to be cordial to each other, and to note moments of agreement with each other, as if trying to win points for \u8220\'20\'1Ccivility\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance refused to say whether Trump had lost the 2020 election\par \par \uc2 In one of Walz\u8217\'20\'19s stronger moments, he asked Vance to state clearly whether Trump had lost the 2020 election, which the former president still denies.\par \par \uc2 Vance would not say whether Trump had won or lost.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTim, I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said, trying to pivot to accusing Harris of censoring Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a damning non-answer,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 WALZ: Did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose the 2020 election?\par \par \uc2 VANCE: Tim, I'm focused on the future\par \par \uc2 WALZ: That's a damning non-answer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D6tVg8HOFC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D6tVg8HOFC}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1841306806347350107?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 When questioned about threats to democracy and January 6, Vance responded by drawing a false equivalence between a violent mob storming the Capitol and forcing members of Congress to flee and hide, and Democrats protesting and complaining after previous presidential elections. Vance argued it was unfair for Democrats to describe Trump\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to admit he had lost the 2020 election as undermining democracy, and said the claim \u8220\'20\'1Cthat this is just a problem that Republicans have had \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t buy that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6 was not \uc2 Facebook\uc2  ads,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz responded, referring to Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 allegations that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s buying of ads in 2016 influenced the election. \u8220\'20\'1CI think a revisionist history on this \u8211\'20\'13 look, I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how we got to this point, but the issue was, that happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance blamed a wide swathe of problems, from school shootings to the housing crisis, on undocumented immigrants and US border policy\par \par \uc2 Is there a social problem in America that, according to JD Vance, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t come back to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s supposed failure to secure the US-Mexico border?\par \par \uc2 Vance asserted that the US housing crisis was a result of undocumented immigrants competing with US citizens for homes, and suggested that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to conduct mass deportations of undocumented people in the US would bring down rents and housing costs, a repeated suggestion that struck many commentators as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/alex_shephard/status/1841279803900506399"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubling}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 listing \u8220\'20\'1Cmass deportation\u8221\'20\'1D as a housing proposal is literally fascistic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XzNG4sDwGS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XzNG4sDwGS}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Shephard (@alex_shephard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alex_shephard/status/1841279803900506399?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwenty five million illegal aliens competing with Americans for scarce homes is one of the most significant drivers of home prices in the country. It\u8217\'20\'19s why we have a massive increase in home prices that have happened right alongside massive increases in illegal alien populations under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be kicking out illegal immigrants who are competing for those homes, and we should be building more homes for the American citizens who deserve to be here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at another point.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press\u8217\'20\'19s factcheckers noted that, \u8220\'20\'1CMost economists blame a long-term {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/housing-treasury-homelessness-yellen-interest-rates-9055dd9394a0e01609d04294f40ae6a7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decline in the housing supply}}}\uc2  for the steady increase in home prices\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CHomebuilders say they need the immigrants to build the homes,\u8221\'20\'1D meaning that mass deportations of workers would not in fact increase the supply of housing in the US.\par \par \uc2 When asked about school shootings and his opposition to gun control laws, Vance endorsed adding more security measures to schools. In response to gunmen opening fire at schools, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to make the doors stronger. We have to make the windows stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he also pointed a finger at Mexico, asserting that most gun violence in the US is carried out with illegally obtained firearms, and drawing a connection between the \u8220\'20\'1Copen border\u8221\'20\'1D with Mexico and a rise in illegal guns in the US.\par \par \uc2 There is official data that shows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wilsoncenter.org/article/infographics-arms-trafficking-across-us-mexico-border#:~:text=Mexico's%20Secretariat%20of%20Foreign%20Relations,and%20ultimately%20found%20in%20Mexico."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising number of guns used in crimes}}}\uc2  have crossed the US-Mexico border in recent years. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not Mexico sending guns to the US: it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.watson.brown.edu/research/research-briefs/exit-wounds-how-americas-guns-fuel-violence-across-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guns}}}\uc2  from the US fueling crime and violence in Mexico. As Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/investigates/special-report/mexico-usa-guns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported last year}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe great majority of illegal guns in Mexico come from the United States, Mexican and US authorities say,\u8221\'20\'1D noting that, \u8220\'20\'1CMexico, a country of 127 million people, has tight gun laws \u8211\'20\'13 and just a single gun store, located on a military base.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance talked a lot about the GOP needing to regain women\u8217\'20\'19s trust on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy\par \par \uc2 Vance paired a lot of soft rhetoric acknowledging American women\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies with a reiteration of his support for leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to the states, many of which have passed laws that criminalize women who seek abortions and medical providers who assist them.\par \par \uc2 He opened his comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by talking about a friend who told him, years after having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a young woman, that her ability to have that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been crucial to her life, and allowed her to escape an abusive relationship.\par \par \uc2 He also said that the state of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s 2023 referendum enshrining access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a right in the state constitution, when \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople in Ohio voted overwhelmingly against my position\u8221\'20\'1D, taught him \u8220\'20\'1Cthat we have to do a better job at winning back people\u8217\'20\'19s trust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When Walz mentioned one of the Georgia women who died of what an investigation found to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D death that experts linked to a state law criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures, Vance agreed with Walz: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/19/georgia-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Thurman}}}\uc2  should still be alive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, of course, leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to the states resulted in the Georgia law that Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s family, as well as experts, blame for her death.\par \par \uc2 Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s family was having none of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric. In a comment shared after the debate, they praised Walz for defending women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and criticized Republican policies.\par \par \uc2 The family of Amber Thurman has issued a statement following discussions during the Vice Presidential debate about Amber and women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights:\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we commend Governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Tim_Walz}}}\uc2  for telling Amber\u8217\'20\'19s story and for his unwavering commitment to defending women\u8217\'20\'19s\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SRUihCKvw2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SRUihCKvw2}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Crump (@AttorneyCrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AttorneyCrump/status/1841315023068533233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 There was only one question about the Middle East, which is on the brink of a regional war\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Iran launched a major missile attack on Israel. Israel pledged revenge. On Tuesday night, as Israeli missiles struck neighborhoods across Beirut, and Israel warned Lebanese civilians to flee their homes at 3am, the US vice-presidential debate largely ignored the escalating global crisis, instead focusing on questions about the economy and the priorities of US consumers.\par \par \uc2 Vance and Walz faced a single opening question about the Middle East: would they support a pre-emptive US strike on Iran? Both candidates more or less dodged the question, while emphasizing that they supported Israel. Walz added that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own defense advisers had decided he was unfit for office, and that the US needed a \u8220\'20\'1Csteady\u8221\'20\'1D leader like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Vance said it was up to Israel to decide the best way to keep themselves safe, and: \u8220\'20\'1CWe should support our allies wherever they are when they\u8217\'20\'19re fighting the bad guys.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241002eka2000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
