\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Walz and Vance clash over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and immigration in vice-presidential debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt in New York \par \uc2 1,364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par 13:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 VP candidates serve up less drama than Harris-Trump debate but still have a few gaffes in policy-driven discussionKey takeaways from the Walz-Vance debate\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  took to the stage on Tuesday night for a vice-presidential debate that served up less drama than September\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential debate}}}\uc2 , but offered revealing differences on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , school shootings, and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Three weeks ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  had endured a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contentious hour and a half}}}\uc2 , with an emotional Trump being goaded into ranting about the number of people who attend his rallies and declaring the vice-president to be a \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D, before reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/politics/trump-reportedly-planning-to-sue-abcs-david-muir-in-publicity-stunt-over-debate-faceplant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatening to sue}}}\uc2  one of the debate moderators. Harris enjoyed a brief polling uptick from that performance.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, Walz and Vance largely avoided attacks on each other, and instead concentrated their fire on each other\u8217\'20\'19s running mates. It was a more policy-driven discussion than that of their running mates\u8217\'20\'19, but one with a few gaffes that might overshadow some of the substance in coming days.\par \par \uc2 In a key exchange over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Walz, the governor of Minnesota, followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/abortion-harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s lead}}}\uc2  in using personal stories.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cbrags about how great it was that he put the judges in and overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, Walz said. He noted the case of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-abortion-ban-zurawski-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Zurawski}}}\uc2 , who was denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas despite serious health complications during pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 Zurawski is now part of a group of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/womens-health/texas-zurawski-women-denied-abortions-election-reproductive-rights-rcna158571"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing the state of Texas}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and a girl in Kentucky who as a child was raped by her stepfather and became pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t know [women like this], you soon will. Their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  is going to have a registry of pregnancies,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, which Vance contested.\par \par \uc2 Walz also criticized the Trump-Vance position that states should decide whether women have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not how this works. This is basic human rights. We have seen maternal mortality skyrocket in Texas, outpacing many other countries in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 When Harris was considering Walz as her vice-presidential candidate, he reportedly told her that he was a bad debater, and at the outset Vance, wearing a sharp blue suit, a pink tie, plenty of make-up and hair gel, looked the more polished performer. Walz, a former high school teacher and football coach, cut a more bustling figure in a loose black suit.\par \par \uc2 Vance, the Ohio senator who has been a regular on rightwing news channels for years, was polished from the off, comfortably dodging a question about whether he believes the climate crisis is a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D to lament how much money has been spent on solar panels.\par \par \uc2 Walz rose to the vice-presidential nomination, in part, through his confident appearances on cable news \u8211\'20\'13 it was from there that his famous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Tim_Walz/status/1815951829479330211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D characterization }}}\uc2  of Vance and Trump was born \u8211\'20\'13 but appeared initially nervous, and did not reprise his searing critique of his opponents.\par \par \uc2 Both men also frequently referenced their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/29/election-walz-vance-vp-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upbringing in the midwest.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will be the first to tell you I have poured my heart into my community, trying to do the best I can, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve not been perfect and I\u8217\'20\'19m a knucklehead at times,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, while attempting to navigate a question about his time in China. \u8220\'20\'1CBut [Minnesotans] elected me to Congress for 12 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz also criticized Trump and Vance for demonizing immigrants in Springfield, Ohio; the two have falsely claimed that Haitian immigrants are eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets, which has led to bomb threats and children in the city having to be escorted to school by police.\par \par \uc2 Asked about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/vance-walz-vice-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2 , one of the key issues in November, Walz discussed Harris\u8217\'20\'19s history in California, demonstrating that the real goal here was for both him and Vance to talk up their bosses\u8217\'20\'19 records rather than sell their own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was the attorney general of the largest border state in California. She\u8217\'20\'19s the only person in this race who prosecuted transnational gangs for human trafficking and drug interventions,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 Vance blamed Harris for the number of people who have crossed the border under the Biden administration, which prompted Walz to raise the issue of a bipartisan border bill, endorsed by the National Border Patrol Council, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/06/joe-biden-congress-mexico-border-security-bill-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 torpedoed by Trump}}}\uc2  earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as that was getting ready to pass and actually tackle this, Trump said \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19, told them to vote against it, because it gives them a campaign issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 The immigration conversation led to an uncomfortable moment for Vance. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/13/trump-deportation-immigrants-springfield-ohio-aurora-colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  that if he is elected he will carry out \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest deportation in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D, but in a country where some families\u8217\'20\'19 children may be US citizens born to non-citizen parents, he has failed to explain how that would work.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether a Trump administration would separate immigrant parents from their US-citizen children, Vance twice refused to answer.\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s missteps, meanwhile, were largely style not substance but could prove fodder for the right in coming days. He was asked about his false claim that he was in Hong Kong \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen Tiananmen happened\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the anti-government protests that culminated in the massacre of hundreds of people in June 1989. It emerged this week that Walz had traveled to China in August, two months later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I grew up in small, rural Nebraska, a town of 400, a town that you rode your bike with your buddies until the street lights come on, and I\u8217\'20\'19m proud of that service,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz\u8217\'20\'19s answer began, as he attempted to avoid the question entirely.\par \par \uc2 Pressed further, Walz said: \u8220\'20\'1CI got there that summer and misspoke on this. So I will just \u8230\'20\'26 that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ve said. So I was in Hong Kong and China during the democracy protests. And from that I learned a lot of what needed to be in governance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the debate drew towards a close, both men were asked about the issue of school shootings, and whether AR-15 style guns, which have been used in several mass shootings, should be banned.\par \par \uc2 Vance called school shootings \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible stuff\u8221\'20\'1D before he sought to blame Harris for gun violence. He claimed there has been a \u8220\'20\'1Ca massive influx in the number of illegal guns run by the Mexican drug cartels\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 although in the majority of school shootings the weapons used have been legally purchased. Democrats have pushed for stricter gun controls to curb mass shootings, but Vance took a different approach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do we do to protect our kids? And I think the answer is, and I say this not loving the answer, because I don\u8217\'20\'19t want my kids to go to school in a school that feels unsafe or there are visible signs of security, but I unfortunately think that we have to increase security in our schools. We have to make the doors lock better. We have to make the door stronger. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to make the windows stronger,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 Walz was more forthright. He said he had met with the parents of children killed in the Sandy Hook school shooting, and said \u8220\'20\'1Cour first responsibility is to our kids,\u8221\'20\'1D detailing his red flag policies in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI ask all of you out there: your schools hardened to look like a fort \u8211\'20\'13 is that, is that what we have to go through?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what we end up doing is we start looking for a scapegoat. Sometimes it\u8217\'20\'19s just the guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But his strong answer on gun reform was eclipsed on social media when he accidentally said he \u8220\'20\'1Cbefriended school shooters\u8221\'20\'1D rather than victims.\par \par \uc2 Vice-presidents, and their debates, have typically been viewed as unimportant, and it remains to be seen how much impact this debate will have. But with the election expected to be extremely close, if either Vance or Walz managed to convince a few voters, then the hour and a half of scrutiny, and even the gaffes, will have been worth it.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241002eka2000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
