\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Doctors issue stark warning as Louisiana reclassifies  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 570 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par 11:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Officials class mifepristone and misoprostol as \u8216\'20\'18controlled substances\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 which medics say could imperil women\u8217\'20\'19s lives\par \par \uc2 Two common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are, as of Tuesday, classified as \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrolled substances\u8221\'20\'1D in Louisiana, due to a first-of-its-kind law that medical professionals warn will endanger the lives of women by restricting medication used to treat postpartum hemorrhage and other conditions.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana, which already bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/14/louisiana-abortion-pills-dangerous-substances-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a law reclassifying}}}\uc2  mifepristone and misoprostol as schedule IV drugs \u8211\'20\'13 a designation typically reserved for drugs that carry a risk of abuse or dependence. People caught with the drugs without a valid prescription could face up to five years in prison, although pregnant women who procure it for their own use are exempted from punishment under the law.\par \par \uc2 Although the drugs are typically used in US medication abortions, they are also regularly used in an array of other circumstances, such as to help with miscarriage management, treat ulcers and soften the cervix during labor and other procedures.\par \par \uc2 Normally, at the Louisiana hospital where OB-GYN Dr Nicole Freehill works, misoprostol is kept in so-called hemorrhage carts, which can be easily wheeled into the rooms where patients deliver babies and which carry medications normally used to treat hemorrhaging, including misoprostol. It takes about 15 seconds to pull the misoprostol out of the cart, Freehill said.\par \par \uc2 Now, due to the security requirements placed on schedule IV drugs, the hospital must keep misoprostol stocked outside of patients\u8217\'20\'19 rooms. When the hospital ran a drill to see how long it took nurses to grab the misoprostol under the new rules, it took nurses two minutes, Freehill said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people might go: \u8216\'20\'18Oh, two minutes, that\u8217\'20\'19s really fast.\u8217\'20\'19 And yes, in the long scheme of things, that\u8217\'20\'19s fast. But when you have someone who is actively hemorrhaging \u8211\'20\'13 in two minutes, they can lose hundreds of cc\u8217\'20\'19s of blood,\u8221\'20\'1D Freehill said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo those seconds count. I\u8217\'20\'19m definitely worried about what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen to patients who are hemorrhaging.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Compared to other wealthy nations, the United States already has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/jun/05/maternal-mortality-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far higher maternal mortality rate}}}\uc2 , particularly among Black Americans.\par \par \uc2 Before the law\u8217\'20\'19s passage, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/rosiewestwood/status/1788281803532300710"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 200 doctors wrote a letter}}}\uc2  to the state legislator behind the law, asking him to reconsider it. \u8220\'20\'1CControlled substances require more complex coordination by pharmacists, patients and providers, with increased documentation and often longer waits for patients,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1COverall, this results in fear and confusion among patients, doctors, and pharmacists, which delays care and worsens outcomes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, more than a dozen states, including Louisiana, have banned almost all abortions. However, the number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/24/us-abortion-rates-post-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions performed in US clinics rose}}}\uc2 , as did the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/self-managed-abortions-avoid-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number of self-induced abortions}}}\uc2  using pills. (Self-managed abortions are usually safe and effective in the first trimester of pregnancy.) In response, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have tried to narrow access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which are used in two-thirds of all US abortions.\par \par \uc2 However, there is no medical reason to reclassify mifepristone and misoprostol as schedule IV drugs, Freehill said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt could be five out of seven days of the week that I\u8217\'20\'19m utilizing this medication, and obviously not for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D Freehill said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see how this is going to help my patients be safer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241001eka1001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
