\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Georgia judge says women aren\u8217\'20\'19t \u8216\'20\'18community property\u8217\'20\'19 as  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban struck down \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Lois Beckett, Chris Stein and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 7,545 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2024\par 23:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read the full story on Georgia overturning its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban below: Georgia judge strikes down state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, allowing care to resume\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re wrapping up our live coverage of US politics for today, but our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/30/israel-attacks-live-blog-lebanon-yemen-hamas-hezbollah-news-updates-middle-east-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live coverage of what is happening now in Israel and Lebanon}}}\uc2  will continue.\par \par \uc2 Some of today\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Georgia judge struck down Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive ban on abortions after roughly six weeks of pregnancy, and ruled that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care could once again be provided until around 22 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The ruling follows weeks of national scrutiny after a \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  investigation of what experts called the \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D deaths of two Georgia women, related to the state\u8217\'20\'19s punitive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fulton County superior court judge Robert McBurney \u8217\'20\'19s ruling overturning the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was strongly worded, arguing that, \u8220\'20\'1C Women are not some piece of collectively owned community property the disposition of which is decided by majority vote,\u8221\'20\'1D and that forcing women to remain pregnant is a kind of \u8220\'20\'1C involuntary servitude, \u8221\'20\'1D which forces \u8220\'20\'1C primarily poor women, which means in Georgia primarily black and brown women \u8211\'20\'13 to engage in compulsory labor, ie, the carrying of a pregnancy to term at the government\u8217\'20\'19s behest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Hurricane Helene, as many as 600 people are still unaccounted for, and at least 100 confirmed dead, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/30/us-election-hurricane-helene-trump-biden-harris-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66fafdeb8f08441851819309#block-66fafdeb8f08441851819309"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  White House said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a series of baseless claims related to the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of Hurricane Helene, asserting without evidence that his Democratic rivals \u8220\'20\'1Cleft Americans to drown\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/30/us-election-hurricane-helene-trump-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66faead48f0894769732d0a1#block-66faead48f0894769732d0a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming}}}\uc2  at an election event that Biden had not spoken with Republican Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in the wake of the storm. (Kemp told reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-georgia-governor-brian-kemp-unable-talk-biden-hurricane-helene-rcna173236"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they had spoken}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expressed support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/30/us-election-hurricane-helene-trump-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66fae56c8f08441851819219#block-66fae56c8f08441851819219"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalizing marijuana}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Democratic presidential nominee, has won the endorsement of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s daughter, who declared: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been grieving the loss of my dad to [Donald] Trump. I cannot bear to lose our country to him too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Caroline Rose Giuliani was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/caroline-giuliani-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing in Vanity Fair}}}\uc2 , where she lamented how her father, who was once the former president\u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney and trusted adviser, became caught up in the \u8220\'20\'1Cdestructive trail\u8221\'20\'1D and chaos of the Trump administration and its aftermath.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m unfortunately well suited to remind Americans of just how calamitous being associated with Trump can be, even for those who are convinced he\u8217\'20\'19s on their side,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Giuliani, a California-based film-maker and activist who has frequently taken issue with her father\u8217\'20\'19s political positions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am constantly asking myself how America is back here, even considering the possibility of electing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  again, after all of the damage he has caused, both in office and since. There are unmistakable reminders of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s destructive trail all around us, and it has broken my heart to watch my dad become one of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who became an immensely popular mayor of New York after guiding the city through the terrorist attacks of 11 September 2001, paid a severe price for promoting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies that his 2020 election defeat was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/rudy-giuliani-daughter-supports-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s daughter backs Harris and grieves \u8216\'20\'18loss of my dad to Trump\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Democratic Vice-Presidential candidate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will debate Republican Vice-Presidential candidate JD Vance for the first time. That debate takes place at 9pm EDT and we will bring it to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is more on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments, from the press pool report:\par \par \uc2 Asked about comments from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has accused him and Governor Cooper of ignoring Republican-voting areas in their response to Helene, POTUS angrily interjected before pool finished asking the question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s lying, and the governor told him he was lying. The governor told him he\u8217\'20\'19s lying. I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken to the governor, spent time with him, and he told him he\u8217\'20\'19s lying. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know why he does it \u8230\'20\'26 that\u8217\'20\'19s simply not true, and it\u8217\'20\'19s irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 POTUS also defended spending the weekend in Delaware when asked about the matter. He said Wilmington, Delaware is \u8220\'20\'1C90 miles from here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was on the phone the whole time,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 He also held up what he said was \u8220\'20\'1Ca list of every resource we\u8217\'20\'19re getting in there\u8221\'20\'1D and said the question of most import was \u8220\'20\'1Chow to get it in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to get it from point A to point B. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to get if somebody\u8217\'20\'19s roads are wiped out. None of these are wiped out. There\u8217\'20\'19s no ability to land, there\u8217\'20\'19s no ability to get trucks, and no ability to get a whole range of things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke in front of a furniture store gutted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  in Valdosta, Georgia, on Monday, claiming falsely that Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor had not been able to reach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Upon landing in Valdosta, Trump claimed to reporters the president was \u8220\'20\'1Csleeping\u8221\'20\'1D and that \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , the governor, was \u8220\'20\'1Ccalling the president and hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been able to get him\u8221\'20\'1D. He repeated the claim when speaking in front of the store.\par \par \uc2 Kemp refuted the allegation earlier in the day. He said he had been playing phone tag with vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , but also said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president just called me yesterday afternoon and he just said \u8216\'20\'18Hey, what do you need?\u8217\'20\'19 \u8230\'20\'26 He offered that if there\u8217\'20\'19s other things we need, just to call him directly, which, I appreciate that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the White House press briefing on Monday, the homeland security adviser Elizabeth Sherwood-Randall said the president offered Kemp \u8220\'20\'1Canything\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  needed in terms of storm response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, if the governor would like to speak to the president again, of course, the president will take his call,\u8221\'20\'1D Sherwood-Randall said.\par \par \uc2 Trump traveled to the area with evangelist \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2  and truckloads of relief supplies in tow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe brought many, many wagons of resources,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, without really describing what those resources were beyond a tanker of gasoline and some water. The Billy Graham Evangelical Association did not respond to a request for comment, though its website notes that it has sent chaplains to the affected areas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/trump-visits-georgia-after-hurricane-helene-false-biden-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump visits hurricane-ravaged Georgia and makes false claims about Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Kaitlan Collins says that Biden has responded to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims earlier saying that Governor Kemp Biden had not spoken with Republican Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in the wake of Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 Collins reports that, speaking in the Oval Office, Biden said Trump was lying. Collins said Biden spoke angrily, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHe is lying. Let me get this straight: he\u8217\'20\'19s lying...I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken to the governor. I\u8217\'20\'19ve spent time with him and he told me he\u8217\'20\'19s lying. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know why he does this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden, seated in the Oval Office, angrily says Trump is lying. "He is lying. Let me get this straight: he's lying...I've spoken to the governor. I've spent time with him and he told me he's lying. I don't know why he does this."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1840876925411103073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a statement on crime rates, noting that the rates of homicide and violent crimes have declined, and that the homicide rate, in particular, is falling at \u8220\'20\'1Crecord speed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The rate of violent crime has declined to its lowest level in 55 years, Biden says.\par \par \uc2 The comments come as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is accused of invoking plotlines similar to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Purge_(2013_film)#:~:text=In%202014%2C%20a%20political%20party,are%20unavailable%20for%2012%20hours."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Purge}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a dystopian horror film in which officially sanctioned murder is occasionally legal \u8211\'20\'13 as a possible solution to crime in the US after saying it could be eradicated in \u8220\'20\'1Cone really violent day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden said, in part:\par \par \uc2 This year, the homicide and violent crime rates have continued their rapid decline from their peaks during the last administration. According to new preliminary data submitted to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , in the first half of this year, the homicide rate continued to fall at record speed, declining by 22.7%, while the violent crime rate fell by 10.3% to its lowest level since 1969. These record decreases follow the historic declines in crime in 2023, including the largest-ever decrease in the homicide rate. Communities across our country are safer now than when I took office.\par \par \uc2 Under the previous administration, we saw the biggest increase in murder rates on record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US politics coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claims today that Democratic leaders were failing to help Americans in storm-damageed Republican areas of North Carolina, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s lying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s White House pool reporter noted that, when asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments, Biden \u8220\'20\'1C angrily interjected\u8221\'20\'1D before the reporter was even done with the question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s lying, and the governor told him he was lying,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe governor told him he\u8217\'20\'19s lying. I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken to the governor, spent time with him, and he told him he\u8217\'20\'19s lying. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know why he does it \u8230\'20\'26 that\u8217\'20\'19s simply not true, and it\u8217\'20\'19s irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 After a Georgia judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling struck down the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive 2019 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after roughly around six weeks of pregnancy, advocates and analysts have highlighted the order\u8217\'20\'19s bold arguments, which invoked the Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale and compared certain kinds of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans to \u8220\'20\'1Cinvoluntary servitude\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Ccompulsory labor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some advocates, like senator Tina Smith of Minnesota, have highlighted the broader importance of Georgia allowing access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care through 22 weeks of pregnancy, since many surrounding states in the south also have very restrictive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis map does a great job of explaining why blocking the enforcement of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is so important \u8212\'20\'14 especially for women in the South. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iDqN32mmRB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iDqN32mmRB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jGCP8FEfqf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jGCP8FEfqf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tina Smith (@TinaSmithMN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TinaSmithMN/status/1840856754961142052?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Others, like my colleague Carter Sherman, have noted that this ruling comes after Georgia has made national headlines after a \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  investigation into the deaths of two Georgia women, Amber Thurman and Candi Miller, who died what experts called \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D deaths after delays in care that were related to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 enltrA Georgia committee of experts in maternal health deemed Candi Miller\u8217\'20\'19s death \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable.\u8221\'20\'1D The group, which includes 10 doctors, directly blamed the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SohvOopPxp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SohvOopPxp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  (@propublica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/propublica/status/1840753470703292528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThurman died after waiting 20 hours for emergency care under the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Sen. \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  demanded records his committee could review to determine whether the hospital violated the law. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not even a question,\u8221\'20\'1D one expert said. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/42Z3meMpT1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/42Z3meMpT1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  (@propublica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/propublica/status/1840511896379703801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia judge describes \u8216\'20\'18subtext of involuntary servitude\u8217\'20\'19 in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate\par \par \uc2 Another key quote from the order, by Fulton county superior court judge Robert McBurney, that overturned Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around six weeks of pregnancy, which state legislators passed in 2019:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is an uncomfortable and usually unspoken subtext of involuntary servitude swirling about this debate, symbolically illustrated by the composition of the legal teams in this case. It is generally men who promote and defend laws like the Life Act, the effect of which is to require only women \u8211\'20\'13 and, given the socio-economic and demographic evidence presented at trial, primarily poor women, which means in Georgia primarily black and brown women \u8211\'20\'13 to engage in compulsory labor, ie, the carrying of a pregnancy to term at the government\u8217\'20\'19s behest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read my colleague Carter Sherman\u8217\'20\'19s full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/georgia-abortion-ban-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia judge strikes down state\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban, allowing care to resume}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who is Judge Robert McBurney, who struck down Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time Robert C I McBurney, a Fulton county superior court judge based in Atlanta, has made national headlines.\par \par \uc2 McBurney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/23/georgia-abortion-ban-state-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously struck down}}}\uc2  Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s very restrictive ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around six weeks of pregnancy and he also presided over parts of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/08/14/politics/fulton-county-judge-robert-mcburney-trump/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia election interference case}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and key allies, a case that is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-fani-willis-georgia-election-indictment-cd810f67a76dc4c64ec3ee64749bf897"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently stalled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McBurney, a former federal prosecutor, was appointed to his role in 2012 by Republican governor Nathan Deal, to fill the seat of a judge who was retiring. He has since run for reelection and won.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, a columnist for the Atlanta Journal-Constitution called McBurney \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/opinion/columnists/opinion-fultons-judge-mcburney-still-the-hardest-working-judge-in-georgia/YTQQGZY5SNCZ7NKNHDKZHC7X5U/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the hardest working judge in Georgia}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and said that a joke recently at the Atlanta courthouse was , \u8220\'20\'1CAren\u8217\'20\'19t there any other judges in the county?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McBurney is also set to hear a key case on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/georgia-state-election-board-rules-certification-trial-3b478ece3ed6437f0bc8499c77341bec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  election regulations }}}\uc2  in Georgia tomorrow, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/georgia-state-election-board-rules-certification-trial-3b478ece3ed6437f0bc8499c77341bec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia judge: \u8216\'20\'18Women are not some piece of collectively owned community property\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Some key quotes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25178645-final-order_5cce1275?responsive=1&title=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  from the order}}}\uc2  in which Judge Robert McBurney struck down Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s extremely restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban:\par \par \uc2 Women are not some piece of collectively owned community property the disposition of which is decided by majority vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 [T]he liberty of privacy means that they alone should choose whether they serve as human incubators for the five months leading up to viability. It is not for a legislator, a judge, or a Commander from The Handmaid\u8217\'20\'19s Tale to tell these women what to do with their bodies during this period when the fetus cannot survive outside the womb any more so than society could \u8211\'20\'13 or should \u8211\'20\'13 force them to serve as a human tissue bank or to give up a kidney for the benefit of another.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 [L]iberty in Georgia includes in its meaning, in its protections, and in its bundle of rights the power of a woman to control her own body, to decide what happens to it and in it, and to reject state interference with her healthcare choices.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why a judge in Georgia struck down the state\u8217\'20\'19s very early \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 More from the Associated Press on the legal reasoning behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25178645-final-order_5cce1275?responsive=1&title=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the order}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert McBurney wrote in his order that \u8216\'20\'18liberty in Georgia includes in its meaning, in its protections, and in its bundle of rights the power of a woman to control her own body, to decide what happens to it and in it, and to reject state interference with her healthcare choices.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 McBurney wrote that his ruling means the law in the state returns to what it was before the law was passed in 2019:\par \par \uc2 When a fetus growing inside a woman reaches viability, when society can assume care and responsibility for that separate life, then \u8211\'20\'13 and only then \u8211\'20\'13 may society intervene.\par \par \uc2 An \u8220\'20\'1Carbitrary six-week ban\u8221\'20\'1D on abortions \u8220\'20\'1Cis inconsistent with these rights and the proper balance that a viability rule establishes between a woman\u8217\'20\'19s rights of liberty and privacy and society\u8217\'20\'19s interest in protecting and caring for unborn infants\u8221\'20\'1D, the order says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Abortions in Georgia can once again be performed through 22 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 After a judge in Georgia struck down the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on abortions once a doctor can detect a fetal heartbeat, which is usually about six weeks into pregnancy, the procedure is once again legal in Georgia through about 22 weeks of pregnancy, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/30/us-election-hurricane-helene-trump-biden-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal-Constitution }}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 More context from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 and ended a national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it opened the door for state bans. Fourteen states now bar \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy, with some exceptions. Georgia was one of four where the bans kick in after about the first six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 which is often before women realize they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge strikes down Georgia's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban - report\par \par \uc2 A judge in Georgia struck down the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy, the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports.\par \par \uc2 The law was similar to many passed by Republican-led states after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. Democrats, including \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , have recently seized on the law as an example of the consequences of electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Republicans, after a woman was reported to have died in the state after being denied lifesaving care due to the law. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris blames Trump for Georgia \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related death: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s what we feared\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Up to 600 people unaccounted for in Hurricane Helene, White House says\par \par \uc2 As many as 600 people remain missing after Hurricane Helene swept through the south-eastern United States, White House homeland security adviser Elizabeth Sherwood-Randall told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe current data we have is that it looks like there could be as many as 600 loss of lives, but we don\u8217\'20\'19t have any confirmation of that. We know there are 600 who are either lost or unaccounted for, and so that work is ongoing,\u8221\'20\'1D Sherwood-Randall said at the White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 She added that there\u8217\'20\'19s a high degree of uncertainty to the numbers:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll caution you, because we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this before. Those numbers vary widely. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of reporting that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t add up about the numbers. And so, while we may see the numbers go up as we get to more locations that have not yet been fully developed in terms of disaster immediate emergency response operations, we may see more people who unfortunately perished, but we may also not see the numbers skyrocket as people have predicted they might.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in Georgia, Florida, North Carolina and elsewhere have already confirmed more than 100 deaths from the storm that swept in from the Gulf of Mexico:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/hurricane-helene-deaths-damage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene leaves more than 100 dead and a million without power}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dystopian vision for the United States took a new turn on Sunday, when he mulled adopting something only seen in horror films to fight crime. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  has more:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has been accused of invoking plotlines similar to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Purge_(2013_film)#:~:text=In%202014%2C%20a%20political%20party,are%20unavailable%20for%2012%20hours."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Purge}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a dystopian horror film in which officially sanctioned murder is occasionally legal \u8211\'20\'13 as a possible solution to crime in the US after saying it could be eradicated in \u8220\'20\'1Cone really violent day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In what was seen as an extreme display of demagoguery even by his standards, Trump drew cheers from an audience in Erie, Pennsylvania, with a picture of an out-of-control crime spree that he said could be ended \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately\u8221\'20\'1D with one \u8220\'20\'1Creal rough, nasty day\u8221\'20\'1D, or \u8220\'20\'1Cone rough hour\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou see these guys walking out with air conditioners with refrigerators on their back, the craziest thing,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the police aren\u8217\'20\'19t allowed to do their job. They\u8217\'20\'19re told, if you do anything, you\u8217\'20\'19re gonna lose your pension.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not allowed to do it because the liberal left won\u8217\'20\'19t let them do it. The liberal left wants to destroy them, and they want to destroy our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a passage that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/highbrow_nobrow/status/1840489889130823695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked a storm on social media}}}\uc2 , the former president and Republican nominee then said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you had one day, like one real rough, nasty day with the drug stores as an example, where, when they start walking out with \u8230\'20\'26 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/trump-crime-the-purge-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump condemned for suggesting \u8216\'20\'18one really violent day\u8217\'20\'19 to combat crime}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Further evidence that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has no intention of giving the politicking a rest in the wake of Hurricane Helene can be found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1840779255786955251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on X}}}\uc2 , where he implies, once again without evidence, that North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  is frustrating the humanitarian response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll be there shortly, but don\u8217\'20\'19t like the reports that I\u8217\'20\'19m getting about the Federal Government, and the Democrat Governor of the State, going out of their way to not help people in Republican areas,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina is considered a swing state in this election, though it has not voted for a Democratic candidate since 2008, and polls there have lately shown Trump with a narrow lead.\par \par \uc2 The governorship seems to be slipping away from GOP candidate Mark Robinson, after CNN broke the news that he had a long history of making lewd and offensive comments on a pornography websites\u8217\'20\'19s message board. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on that fiasco:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/22/lindsey-graham-mark-robinson-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham calls reports of Mark Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18black Nazi\u8217\'20\'19 posts \u8216\'20\'18beyond unnerving\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump makes baseless claim that Biden administration 'left Americans to drown'\par \par \uc2 When he spoke before a furniture store gutted by Hurricane Helene in Valdosta, Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/30/us-election-hurricane-helene-trump-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66faead48f0894769732d0a1#block-66faead48f0894769732d0a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisted}}}\uc2  he was not there for political purposes. His social media posts tell a different story.\par \par \uc2 About an hour ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113227495028998124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2 , he seized on the below tweet from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrI was just briefed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FEMA_Deanne?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FEMA_Deanne}}}\uc2  Criswell on the latest developments about the ongoing impacts of Hurricane Helene. We also discussed our Administration's continued actions to support emergency response and recovery.\par \par \uc2 I also spoke with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NC_Governor?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NC_Governor}}}\uc2  Cooper about the ongoing\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nlZPB0h3mO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nlZPB0h3mO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1840589803789934809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The former president wrote that the photo of the president was \u8220\'20\'1CFAKE and STAGED\u8221\'20\'1D, without providing evidence, then went on to accuse both Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of leaving \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans to drown in North Carolina, Georgia, Tennessee, Alabama, and elsewhere in the South\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder this Administration, Americans always come last, because we have \u8216\'20\'18leaders\u8217\'20\'19 who have no idea how to lead!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Americans died in hurricanes that struck {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/jun/12/climate-crisis-to-blame-for-67bn-of-hurricane-harvey-damage-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , Puerto Rico, and elsewhere during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. After he left office, a report found that his administration unnecessarily delayed emergency money for Puerto Rico, after it was devastated by Hurricane Maria:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/22/hurricane-maria-puerto-rico-trump-delayed-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump delayed $20bn in aid to Puerto Rico after Hurricane Maria, report finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attempted to put politics aside as he spoke before a furniture store damaged by Hurricane Helene in Valdosta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s despite the fact that he had minutes earlier accused \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of not speaking to the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  following the storm, even though the White House said the two men spoke on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you know, our country is in the final weeks of a hard-fought national election, but in a time like this, when a crisis hits, when our fellow citizens cry out in need, none of that matters. We\u8217\'20\'19re not talking about politics now. We have to all get together and get this solved,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris signals support for marijuana legalization in interview\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made a little bit of news earlier today, saying in an interview that she supported legalizing marijuana \u8211\'20\'13 a step even the cannabis-friendly administration of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hesitated to embrace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just feel strongly people should not be going to jail for smoking weed. And we know historically what that has meant and who has gone to jail,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bzThwqnQJDY&list=PL6fkKAMsPY-HOH4B2Gz6vcOavn-JwOqxx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 All the Smoke podcast}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSecond, I just think we have come to a point where we have to understand that we need to legalize it and stop criminalizing this behavior.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice-president added: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a new position for me. I have felt for a long time we need to legalize it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement represents a break with Biden, who moved to lower restrictions on cannabis while still keeping it broadly illegal at the federal level. Full decriminalization would solve the array of conflicts that have developed as states have moved to legalize marijuana for medicinal and recreational purposes. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/biden-administration-reclassify-marijuana-low-risk-drug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration plans to reclassify marijuana as lower-risk drug}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In about 30 minutes, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak from a furniture store in Valdosta, Georgia, a town affected by Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 The former president began his visit to the swing state by falsely claiming that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had not spoken to Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of the remark, from the Atlanta Journal-Constitution:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump in Valdosta on the Hurricane Helene response: "The governor is doing a good job, but he's having a hard time getting the president on the phone. They're being very non-responsive." Kemp said he's playing "phone tag" with the VP but praised the bipartisan response. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rWtctr3iLK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rWtctr3iLK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1840803388071526483?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House announced yesterday that Biden had spoken to Kemp, a Republican, along with \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, and Valdosta mayor Scott Matheson.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance take the debate stage tomorrow night, expect to see two very different styles of debating, and two equally different views of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s future, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  square off as vice-presidential picks on Tuesday, it will be the biggest debate stage for both of the politicians who are newly becoming household names.\par \par \uc2 Walz, the Democratic governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2 , and Vance, a Republican senator from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , have been honing their public-speaking skills \u8211\'20\'13 and their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/11/vance-targets-harris-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed barbs}}}\uc2  at each other \u8211\'20\'13 in TV appearances and at events around the country in the past few months.\par \par \uc2 Their experiences in electoral debates haven\u8217\'20\'19t reached the levels or notoriety that come along with a presidential campaign, but both have faced opponents in public debates in past elections.\par \par \uc2 Given the tightness of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential race}}}\uc2 , and how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-cnn-presidential-debate-reaction-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poorly the first presidential debate}}}\uc2  between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  went, there will probably be more people tuned in to the vice-presidential debate than in past cycles. While VP debates don\u8217\'20\'19t usually tip the scales much, they could matter in a close race \u8211\'20\'13 and they build profiles for lower-profile politicians who will probably stay on the national scene for years to come.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What we know so far about JD Vance and Tim Walz\u8217\'20\'19s debate styles}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 On a press call this morning, \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 , the Republican representative from Minnesota, confirmed he has been playing \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s debate prep.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are seeking to frame Walz, the folksy Minnesota governor who has proved to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/favorability/tim-walz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most popular figure}}}\uc2  in the presidential race, as a mean-spirited, ogreish figure.\par \par \uc2 Asked about his portrayal of Walz, Emmer said: \u8220\'20\'1CQuite frankly, it\u8217\'20\'19s tough because he is really good on the debate stage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emmer, who ran unsuccessfully for Minnesota governor in 2010, added: \u8220\'20\'1C[Walz] is going to stand there and he lies with conviction, and he has these little mannerisms where he\u8217\'20\'19s just, hey, I\u8217\'20\'19m the nice guy, but he\u8217\'20\'19s not nice at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emmer predicted that Vance \u8220\'20\'1Cis prepared to wipe the floor with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and expose him for the radical liberal he is\u8221\'20\'1D. He added: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is nothing more than \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  [the governor of California] in a flannel shirt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 , a senior adviser to the Trump campaign, predicted that Walz is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to look to stick the shiv into JD Vance at every opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D and predicted that: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  we see tomorrow night will be a completely different character from what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen so far on the 2024 campaign trail.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would agree to debate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for a second time, Miller said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas made it pretty clear where he is\u8221\'20\'1D. Harris has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/22/harris-trump-second-debate-excuse-cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  an invitation to debate on CNN on 23 October, but Trump, who was widely viewed to have lost the first debate, has claimed that it is \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo late\u8221\'20\'1D for a second debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  has agreed to pay $22.6 million to settle a lawsuit by 34 women who claim they were wrongly dismissed from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s agent training academy because of their sex, according to a court filing today.\par \par \uc2 The settlement, which must be approved by a federal judge in Washington DC, would resolve a 2019 class action claiming the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2 , which is part of the Justice Department, had a widespread practice of forcing out female trainees, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs say that they were found unsuitable to graduate from the training academy even though they performed as well as or better than many male trainees on academic, physical fitness, and firearms tests. Some of them also say they were subjected to sexual harassment and sexist jokes and comments.\par \par \uc2 Along with the payout, the proposed settlement would allow eligible class members to seek reinstatement to the agent training program and require the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to hire outside experts to ensure that its evaluation process for trainees is fair.\par \par \uc2 Department\u8217\'20\'19s internal watchdog released a report in 2022 finding that female \uc2 FBI\uc2  trainees were disproportionately likely to be dismissed and to be cited for conduct \u8220\'20\'1Cunsuitable\u8221\'20\'1D for an agent. Less than one-quarter of \uc2 FBI\uc2  special agents are women, the agency said in a report released in April.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Man enters plea denying attempt to assassinate Trump in Florida\par \par \uc2 The man charged with attempting to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after allegedly positioning himself with a rifle outside one of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Florida golf courses on 15 September pleaded not guilty this morning to five federal charges.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Routh, 58, entered the plea to charges that include attempted assassination of a major presidential candidate during a hearing in federal court. He has already been ordered to remain in jail to await a trial, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have said Routh intended to kill Trump as he golfed at Trump International Golf Club in West Palm Beach. Routh, a struggling roofing contractor, condemned the Republican presidential candidate in a self-published book and dropped off a letter months earlier with an associate referencing an attempted assassination on Trump, according to prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 This was an assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but I failed you,\u8221\'20\'1D the suspect wrote, according to a court filing by prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for Routh suggested at a 23 September {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/24/man-charged-trump-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court hearing}}}\uc2  that the letter may have been an attempt by their client at gaining publicity and highlighted what they called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/16/putin-here-i-am-ryan-wesley-routh-man-accused-of-trying-to-shoot-trump-had-delusional-ideas-about-helping-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Routh\u8217\'20\'19s efforts}}}\uc2  to promote democracy in Ukraine and Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 Routh is accused of poking a rifle through a fence at the course with the intention to kill Trump. When a federal agent spotted it and fired shots, the suspect fled but was arrested.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  finished up his remarks on the impact of Hurricane Helene by saying that as US president he ha d seen many disasters and heard \u8220\'20\'1Cdozens of stories from survivors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know how it feels to be left with nothing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cnot even knowing where or when you\u8217\'20\'19re back on track. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to tell every single survivor in these impacted areas that we will be there with you as long as it takes \u8230\'20\'26 I urge everyone returning to their communities and homes to listen to the local officials and follow all the safety instructions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CTake this seriously, please be safe, your nation has your back and the Biden-Harris administration will be there until the job is done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In answer to a press question, Biden said no decision has been made yet on whether to ask the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  (which is in recess) to come back for a special session to approve additional emergency funding as a result of what he described as the \u8220\'20\'1Creally, really devastating\u8221\'20\'1D storm.\par \par \uc2 He said he had spoken to the governor of North Carolina [Democrat \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  ] and expects to visit the state on Wednesday or Thursday of this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been taunting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for not rushing to the areas affected by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  and the storm\u8217\'20\'19s aftermath.\par \par \uc2 Harris has returning early to Washington DC from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election campaigning}}}\uc2  out west, as the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president since Biden, the sitting president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quit his race}}}\uc2  for re-election in July.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the Republican nominee for president, plans to go to Valdosta, Georgia, this afternoon to see storm damage. He\u8217\'20\'19s blasted the US president and vice president, saying Biden was \u8220\'20\'1Csleeping\u8221\'20\'1D on the beach at the weekend instead of marshaling recovery efforts in the devastated areas, while Harris, instead of campaigning in the western US \u8220\'20\'1Cought to be down in the area\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t possible from the live audio to make out what Biden\u8217\'20\'19s response was to a question about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring it to you as soon as possible. Biden said he had spoken to all the affected state governors, has promised help to all those affected for \u8220\'20\'1Cas long as it takes\u8221\'20\'1D and had explained how a White House visit to an emergency area too soon can be counterproductive, because it is such a complicated operation.\par \par \uc2 Biden has signed disaster declarations that free up more federal resources for affected areas \u8211\'20\'13 and Politico also said he spoke to the mayor of Valdosta at the weekend, as well as state governors.\par \par \uc2 Harris said in Las Vegas, Nevada: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will stand with these communities for as long as it takes to make sure that they are able to recover and rebuild.\u8221\'20\'1D She also plans to visit affected areas in due course.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to visit areas affected by Helene 'later this week'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he expects to visit areas affected by the aftermath of Hurricane Helene \u8220\'20\'1Clater this week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US president is now taking some questions from the press gathered at the White House.\par \par \uc2 He called it a historic storm, \u8220\'20\'1Cnever seen anything like it before\u8221\'20\'1D. He said he expected to go down to the area \u8220\'20\'1CWednesday or Thursday\u8221\'20\'1D, saying that, including with a press entourage, a presidential visit in the middle of an emergency can be disruptive if made too soon.\par \par \uc2 Biden said at least 10 states had been affected. Despite saying he would only talk about the storm, he did take a question about the Middle East and said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe should have a ceasefire now\u8221\'20\'1D in the conflict in Lebanon that has suddenly intensified since Israel has launched fierce airborne attacks in the last almost two weeks on the Iran-backed \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  militia based in Lebanon, labelled as a counteroffensive to \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attacks on its neighbor Israel since last October, in solidarity with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Asked about reports that Israel plans a ground invasion of Lebanon and if he was comfortable with that, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m comfortable with them stopping.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Our Middle East live blog is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/30/israel-attacks-live-blog-lebanon-yemen-hamas-hezbollah-news-updates-middle-east-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , talking about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe broad and devastating\u8221\'20\'1D impacts of the storm that made landfall as Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCommunities are devastated, loved ones waiting to hear if [folks] are OK, many unsure if they can return to their homes, when or ever. There is nothing like wondering, is my husband, wife, son, daughter, mother, father alive, many more who remain without electricity, water, food and communications,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that the death toll from the storm was over 100 and more than 600 were unaccounted for.\par \par \uc2 He is speaking from the White House and explained that he had not gone to the areas of destruction and emergency yet because, in line with normal presidential practice, he does not want to get in the way of the local authorities\u8217\'20\'19 recovery efforts just now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still awaiting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remarks from the White House about the aftermath of Hurricane Helene and the impact of as it roared across Georgia and North and South Carolina and its effects spread across 10 states even as it was downgraded from hurricane status last week.\par \par \uc2 The US president is behind schedule, as he was due to begin speaking half an hour ago, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you abreast of developments.\par \par \uc2 Biden is due to talk to US Olympic athletes at 11.30am and then the White House daily media briefing with press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is due at 2pm, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep an eye on whether those times are pushed back.\par \par \uc2 CNN just said the death toll from the storm has now reached 115 in the US, and rising, as more deaths are discovered, with whole towns devastated and some blocked off and parts of western North Carolina, in particular, just flattened. Flooding has been the worst lingering effect after the initial 140mph winds began slowing once the hurricane came ashore in north-western Florida late last Thursday as a category 4.\par \par \uc2 The federal government said yesterday that the \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric flooding\u8221\'20\'1D was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/29/hurricane-helene-historic-flooding-global-heating-fema"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made worse}}}\uc2  because of global heating as the major part of the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to give update on Hurricane Helene response\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to imminently begin speaking from the White House about the response to Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s devastation in North Carolina, Georgia and elsewhere in the southeast.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the president has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican former Arizona Senator \uc2 Jeff Flake\uc2  endorses Harris\par \par \uc2 Jeff Flake\uc2 , a Republican who represented swing state Arizona in the Senate and House of Representatives, endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president yesterday:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ll be supporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  for President and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Tim_Walz}}}\uc2  for Vice President. My full statement below. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6b28mkBPMD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6b28mkBPMD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jeff Flake\uc2  (@JeffFlake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeffFlake/status/1840347576823902338?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Flake clashed with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his presidency, and opted not to run for re-election in 2018, paving the way for then-Democrat \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  to take his place. The former senator has made his peace with the Democrats, and until earlier this month served as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to Turkey.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may dismiss it as a \u8220\'20\'1Cscam\u8221\'20\'1D, but the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  believes the climate crisis made Hurricane Helene more severe, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The head of the US disaster relief agency has called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2 , which has killed nearly 100 people, a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue multi-state event\u8221\'20\'1D that caused \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant infrastructure damage\u8221\'20\'1D and had been made worse because of global heating.\par \par \uc2 The storm killed at least 91 people, according to state and local officials in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2 , Florida, Georgia, North Carolina and Virginia. Officials feared more bodies would be discovered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to be a really complicated recovery in each of the five states\u8221\'20\'1D of Florida, Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2 , South Carolina and Tennessee, said the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) administrator, \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She noted that a 15ft storm surge hit Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Taylor county, where Helene came ashore as a category 4 hurricane late Thursday with winds of 140mph (225km/h), and pointed out that areas of western North Carolina, where search and rescue operations are continuing, recorded 29in (74cm) of rain when the storm stalled over the region.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is historic flooding up in North Carolina,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/deanne-criswell-fema-administrator-face-the-nation-transcript-09-29-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Criswell told the CBS show Face the Nation}}}\uc2  on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that anybody could be fully prepared for the amount of flooding and landslides they are having right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/29/hurricane-helene-historic-flooding-global-heating-fema"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18historic flooding\u8217\'20\'19 made worse by global heating, Fema says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris intends to visits areas affected by Hurricane Helene 'as soon as it is possible'\par \par \uc2 Despite \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s insistence to the contrary, the White House says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was briefed on Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s impacts as she was campaigning over the weekend on the west coast.\par \par \uc2 Harris has canceled campaign events in Las Vegas today so she can head to Fema headquarters in Washington DC for a briefing on the storm, a White House official said. She has also spoken to North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , a Democrat, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccontacted\u8221\'20\'1D Georgia and Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governors \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president intends to visit impacted communities as soon as it is possible without disrupting emergency response operations,\u8221\'20\'1D the official added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attacks Biden and Harris over Helene response at lengthy Pennsylvania rally\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Erie, Pennsylvania yesterday stretched for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?538747-1/president-trump-campaigns-erie-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly two hours}}}\uc2 , and began with the former president accusing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of failing to respond as Hurricane Helene struck the southeastern United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden is in Delaware sleeping right now in one of his many estates,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, before alleging Harris was \u8220\'20\'1Cat fundraising events with her radical left lunatic donors, when big parts of our country have been devastated by that massive hurricane and are underwater, with many, many people dead\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment:\par \par \uc2 enltrWestern North Carolina is currently under water.\par \par \uc2 Kamala is at a fundraiser in San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 Biden is once again sleeping at the beach.\par \par \uc2 America's "leaders" are absent. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pV63bl7ENs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pV63bl7ENs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1840460215659249715?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has thus far held back on making similar statements about Trump, but did seize on his comments downplaying the link between worsening natural disasters and climate change:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump in the deadly aftermath of Hurricane Helene: \u8220\'20\'1C[Climate change] is one of the great scams of all time\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AW9mYeUjln"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AW9mYeUjln}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1840475679319642471?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to address Hurricane Helene damage as Trump seeks to turn storm into campaign issue\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. After churning across the southern US and causing massive destruction and dozens of deaths in North Carolina, Georgia and elsewhere, Hurricane Helene appears set to collide with the presidential campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  will speak this afternoon in Valdosta, Georgia about the storm, undoubtedly with an eye on turning the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s voters away from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  . The former president has already made the hurricane\u8217\'20\'19s destruction into an attack line on the Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/29/trump-hurricane-helene-2024-campaign-00181599"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  accusing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Csleeping\u8221\'20\'1D as the storm raged. Speaking at a rally in Pennsylvania yesterday he also accused Harris of turning a blind eye to the destruction.\par \par \uc2 Biden plans to speak from the White House at 10.30am ET about his administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to the storm, while Harris has announced the cancellation of campaign events in Las Vegas today so she can return to Washington DC and be briefed on the storm\u8217\'20\'19s impact at Fema headquarters. She\u8217\'20\'19ll arrive just after 5pm.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris \u8217\'20\'19s economic policies are more popular with voters than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/harris-trump-economic-proposals-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new polling}}}\uc2  commissioned by the Guardian finds. The vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/harris-opportunity-economic-plan-middle-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid out}}}\uc2  her plans in a major speech last week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vice-presidential debate}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  between }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  and }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/jd-vance-tim-walz-vice-presidential-debate-styles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is set for tomorrow evening}}}\uc2 , with both candidates preparing for what is currently the last scheduled debate before the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel may or may not be on the verge of launching a ground invasion of Lebanon. We have a live blog covering the crisis, and you can read it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/30/israel-attacks-live-blog-lebanon-yemen-hamas-hezbollah-news-updates-middle-east-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240930ek9u001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
