\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Hamas\uc2  says Israeli airstrike has killed head of its operation in Lebanon\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,031 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 September 2024\par 10:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Fatah Sharif Abu al-Amine has reportedly been killed in an Israeli attack in the south. Plus, New Zealand reclaims haka world recordDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  said on Monday the leader of its operation in Lebanon, Fatah Sharif Abu al-Amine, had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/30/israel-attacks-live-blog-lebanon-yemen-hamas-hezbollah-news-updates-middle-east-crisis?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66fa3c0f8f08441851818975#block-66fa3c0f8f08441851818975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed in an Israeli airstrike}}}\uc2  in the country\u8217\'20\'19s south, with Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s national news agency reporting that the bombing struck a Palestinian refugee camp.\par \par \uc2 In the past two weeks 1,000 people have been killed and 6,000 wounded by Israeli airstrikes in Lebanon, the health ministry says, including about 100 people killed on Sunday. The government said a million people \u8211\'20\'13 a fifth of the population \u8211\'20\'13 have fled their homes.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Israel launched a wave of airstrikes against Houthi targets in Yemen on Sunday, attacking the port of Hodeidah and targeting fuel facilities, power plants and docks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Israeli politics? The opposition lawmaker \uc2 Gideon Saar\uc2  rejoined the government on Sunday, a step that is likely to strengthen the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did Netanyahu tell the \uc2 UN\uc2 ? On Friday he shrugged off global appeals for a ceasefire in a defiant speech delivered barely an hour before massive airstrikes targeting \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leader {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/27/israel-air-attack-beirut-lebanon-hezbollah-hassan-nasrallah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 levelled}}}\uc2  several apartment blocks in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Follow our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/30/israel-attacks-live-blog-lebanon-yemen-hamas-hezbollah-news-updates-middle-east-crisis?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66fa3c0f8f08441851818975#block-66fa3c0f8f08441851818975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live blog here}}}\uc2 . Today Israel has launched an apparent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/30/lebanon-beirut-israel-strikes-yemen-hezbollah-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rare strike on central Beirut}}}\uc2 . If confirmed it would be the first attack by Israel on the centre of the Lebanese capital since 2006.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 accused of \u8216\'20\'18intimidation campaign\u8217\'20\'19 against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is making a concerted effort to maintain draconian limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Florida, sparking accusations the Republican governor is conducting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/29/desantis-abortion-election-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cstate-sponsored intimidation campaign\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and trampling on civil liberties.\par \par \uc2 A near-total ban on abortions after the first six weeks of pregnancy took effect in Florida in May, after its supreme court ruled that the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no longer covered by the privacy clause in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Registered voters in Florida have recently reported unannounced visits from law enforcement personnel, which appear to be part of a drive by DeSantis to use state government agencies and public funds to block the passage of Amendment 4, which would enshrine the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is Amendment 4? A referendum, held on 5 November, on whether to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Passage of Amendment 4 would change the state constitution to prohibit government interference with the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the \u8220\'20\'1Cviability\u8221\'20\'1D of a fetus, which typically begins at about the 24th week of a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Putin says Russia will accomplish \u8216\'20\'18all goals set\u8217\'20\'19 in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has vowed that Moscow will accomplish all goals it has set for itself in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is on our side. All goals set will be achieved,\u8221\'20\'1D the Russian president said in a video message released to mark the second anniversary of what Russia calls Reunification Day, when Moscow annexed four Ukrainian regions.\par \par \uc2 Kyiv, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s capital, was targeted by several waves of Russian attack drones overnight, with air raid sirens sounding in the capital just after 1am local time. The Ukrainian air force said it shot down 67 of 73 drones and one of three missiles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is Moscow\par \par \uc2 stepping up its attacks? It appears that way. Russian drone attacks on Kyiv have intensified as Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s forces target Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical energy, military and transport infrastructure in the run-up to winter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How is the US responding? It has accused Iran and North Korea of aiding Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The far right won the most votes in an Austrian election for the first time since the Nazi era.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/29/far-right-freedom-party-winning-austrian-election-first-results-show"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Freedom party}}}\uc2  rode a tide of public anger over migration and the cost of living.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Flooding and landslides caused by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/28/at-least-66-killed-and-69-missing-as-flooding-and-landslides-hit-nepal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continuous rainfall}}}\uc2  have killed at least 101 people in Nepal, according to officials, while 64 people are missing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kris Kristofferson\par \par \uc2 , the country singer and\par \par \uc2 actor, has died. His family said he died {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/sep/30/kris-kristofferson-us-country-singer-and-actor-dies-aged-88"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 peacefully}}}\uc2  at the age of 88.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Poverty in Argentina soars to nearly 53% as \u8216\'20\'18anarcho-capitalist\u8217\'20\'19 Milei\u8217\'20\'19s austerity measures hit hard\par \par \uc2 Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s poverty rate has soared to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/27/poverty-rate-argentina-milei"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost 53% of the 46 million population}}}\uc2  in the first six months of \uc2 Javier Milei\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, with 3.4 million people pushed into poverty this year. Since taking office, the rightwing Milei has frozen pensions, reduced aid to soup kitchens, cut welfare programmes and stopped all public works projects. Tens of thousands of public employees have been fired, reduced energy and transportation subsidies have pushed costs up, and purchasing power has eroded.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Six days of horror \u8211\'20\'13\par \par \uc2 the US\u8217\'20\'19s thirst for executions returns with a vengeance\par \par \uc2 Five executions, five states, six days. A spate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/29/america-executions-death-penalty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judicial killings}}}\uc2  not seen in 20 years took place last week \u8211\'20\'13 and there was nothing random about it. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a radical shift in the legal culture as it relates to the death penalty in the past six years,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Bryan Stevenson\uc2 , the founder of the Equal Justice Initiative. \u8220\'20\'1CThe refs are gone, there is no more oversight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18historic flooding\u8217\'20\'19 made worse by global heating, Fema says\par \par \uc2 The head of the US disaster relief agency, \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 , called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/29/hurricane-helene-historic-flooding-global-heating-fema"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue multi-state event\u8221\'20\'1D that caused significant infrastructure damage, made worse because of global heating. Nearly 100 people have been killed with many more unaccounted for.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: New Zealand reclaims haka world record\par \par \uc2 New Zealand has reclaimed the world record for the largest mass haka after 6,531 people performed the Maori dance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/29/new-zealand-reclaims-world-record-for-largest-mass-haka"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dethroning France}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to bring the mana [pride] of the haka back home,\u8221\'20\'1D the organizer said.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240930ek9u001bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
