\par\par \uc2 Music\par \b \uc2 Stevie Nicks releases song inspired by fight for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights: \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t let them take your power\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Ben Beaumont-Thomas \par \uc2 840 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2024\par 09:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Fleetwood Mac singer addresses American women in The Lighthouse, encouraging them to make a stand as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights dominate US election campaigning\par \par \uc2 Stevie Nicks has released a forthright new single, The Lighthouse, inspired by the fight to reinstate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 Nicks wrote the robust, swaggering rock song in the aftermath of the June 2022 decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling}}}\uc2  that Americans had a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seemed like overnight, people were saying, \u8216\'20\'18What can we, as a collective force, do about this?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, it was to write a song. It took a while because I was on the road. Then early one morning I was watching the news on TV and a certain newscaster said something that felt like she was talking to me \u8211\'20\'13 explaining what the loss of Roe v Wade would come to mean. I wrote the song the next morning and recorded it that night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was September 6, 2022. I have been working on it ever since. I have often said to myself, \u8216\'20\'18This may be the most important thing I ever do. To stand up for the women of the United States and their daughters and granddaughters \u8211\'20\'13 and the men that love them.\u8217\'20\'19 This is an anthem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the song, Nicks casts herself as the titular lighthouse, guiding women to campaign for their rights. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to teach them to fight / I want to tell them this has happened before, don\u8217\'20\'19t let it happen again,\u8221\'20\'1D she sings.\par \par \uc2 The chorus is similarly a call to action: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ll take your soul, take your power, unless you stand up, take it back / Try to see the future and get mad / It\u8217\'20\'19s slipping through your fingers, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have what you had / And you don\u8217\'20\'19t have much time to get it back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nicks is backed by Sheryl Crow, who plays guitar and bass as well as singing backing vocals. Crow also co-produced the song with 13-time Grammy winning Dave Cobb.\par \par \uc2 The Lighthouse has been released amid a US election campaign where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has been at the forefront of campaigning.\par \par \uc2 Trump installed the supreme court justices who overturned the decision during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, and has boasted about it: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter 50 years of failure, with nobody coming even close, I was able to kill Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in May. In August he said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno regrets\u8221\'20\'1D about the court decision, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe federal government should have nothing to do with this issue. It\u8217\'20\'19s being solved at the state level and people are very happy about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has repeatedly criticised Trump on the issue, characterising him earlier this week as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe person who said women should be punished for exercising a decision that they, rightly, should be able to make about their own body and future\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law now decided at a state level, 14 states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with another 11 described as \u8220\'20\'1Chostile\u8221\'20\'1D to it by the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 . Research published this month by Advancing New Standards in Reproductive Health found that doctors are being forced to provide substandard care by making women take unviable pregnancies to full term.\par \par \uc2 Nicks, 76, has been using her music to focus on civil rights struggles in recent years. Her one-off track Show Them the Way, in 2020, was inspired by watching documentaries about the civil rights movement and has Nicks imagining performing at a political benefit attended by \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 , John Lennon, John F Kennedy and others. She followed it with a cover of Buffalo Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s For What It\u8217\'20\'19s Worth, which was originally inspired by clashes between police and young people over LA curfew laws, and became synonymous with the anti-Vietnam war movement.\par \par \uc2 The Lighthouse is a rare entirely new song for Nicks, whose last album of brand new material was 2011\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2011/jun/24/stevie-nicks-in-your-dreams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Your Dreams}}}\uc2 . She followed that with new recordings of earlier demos, 24 Karat Gold: Songs from the Vault, in 2014.\par \par \uc2 She has continued to tour in recent years, including in a co-headline tour with Billy Joel in 2023 and 2024. She will be the musical guest on the 12 October edition of Saturday Night Live, where she is likely to perform The Lighthouse.\par \par \uc2 While her new song certainly rebukes Trumpism, Nicks has not explicitly endorsed Harris. Instead she has called for people to register to vote, and in a recent \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post she alluded to Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Harris, writing: \u8220\'20\'1CAs my friend Taylor Swift so eloquently stated, now is the time to research and choose the candidate that speaks to you and your beliefs.\u8221\'20\'1D She signed off \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless dog lady\u8221\'20\'1D in a nod to Swift\u8217\'20\'19s own characterisation of herself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat lady\u8221\'20\'1D, JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s derisive description of US Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240927ek9r0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
