\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris calls for end to Senate filibuster to restore US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Tait in Washington \par \uc2 795 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 19:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic nominee focuses campaign on \u8216\'20\'18reproductive freedom\u8217\'20\'19 and says 60-vote threshold should be abolished\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  has called for an end to the Senate filibuster to make good on her pledge to restore the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through legislation.\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president, herself a former senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/news/kamala-harris-presidential-campaign-vice-president-housing-affordability-pfas-pollution-wpr-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a radio station in Wisconsin that eliminating the filibuster \u8211\'20\'13 which sets a 60-vote threshold in the 100-seat upper chamber of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 would be necessary to codify the rights that were enshrined in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 supreme court ruling that upheld the right to legal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  throughout the US until it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  by a ruling two years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we should eliminate the filibuster for Roe and get us to the point where 51 votes would be what we need to actually put back in law the protections for reproductive freedom, and for the ability of every person and every woman to make decisions about their own body \u8211\'20\'13 and not have their government tell them what to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told WPR, an affiliate of National Public Radio, on a campaign trip to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , a key midwestern swing state where she has a wafer-thin lead over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to recent polls}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her remarks accentuated her determination to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the heart of her campaign message amid polling evidence that it is a priority for many women voters.\par \par \uc2 However, it cost her the support of the outgoing West Virginia senator, Joe Manchin \u8211\'20\'13 a former Democrat who left the party this year to become an independent \u8211\'20\'13 who said he would not endorse her candidacy because of her pledge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShame on her,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin, who is retiring from the Senate at the end of the year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/24/politics/joe-manchin-not-endorse-harris-filibuster/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe knows the filibuster is the holy grail of democracy. It\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing that keeps us talking and working together. If she gets rid of that, then this would be the House on steroids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has been on the defensive on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  ruling was achieved with the votes of three conservative justices he appointed to the bench when he was president. Harris has claimed that Trump would sign a nationwide ban if he re-captured the White House, although he insists he would leave it to individual states.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s use of a radio interview to underline her commitment follows criticism that she was deliberately avoiding high-profile interviews \u8211\'20\'13 a charge Harris has sought to counter by making herself available to selected media in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-66f2115d8f080a0d348dd953#block-66f2115d8f080a0d348dd953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/trump-rally-pennsylvania-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania on Monday that he would be women\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cprotectors\u8221\'20\'1D and that they would not \u8220\'20\'1Cbe thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D if he won a second term.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s filibuster remarks echoed a similar comment by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  immediately after Roe v Wade was struck down, when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/30/filibuster-abortion-vote-exception-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  an exception to the time-honoured Senate rule had to be made to guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe we have to codify Roe v Wade in the law,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/06/30/politics/biden-abortion-rights-filibuster/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the way to do that is to make sure the Congress votes to do that. And if the filibuster gets in the way, it\u8217\'20\'19s like voting rights \u8211\'20\'13 it should be (that) we provide an exception to this \u8230\'20\'26 requiring an exception to the filibuster for this action to deal with the supreme court decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/09/10/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-at-the-2022-democratic-national-committee-summer-meeting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocated}}}\uc2  overriding the filibuster to pass additional voting rights laws and Green New Deal legislation.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, \uc2 Barack Obama{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2020/07/30/barack-obama-john-lewis-filibuster-388600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  the filibuster as a \u8220\'20\'1CJim Crow relic\u8221\'20\'1D from America\u8217\'20\'19s racially segregated past and argued that it should be eliminated if used to block voting reform.\par \par \uc2 The filibuster describes the use of prolonged debate to delay or prevent a vote on a bill. It can be invoked by any senator objecting to a bill and has been used with increasing regularity in recent decades.\par \par \uc2 It can only be overridden by triggering \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/how-does-the-filibuster-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cloture}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, which requires a three-fifths majority vote \u8211\'20\'13 or 60 of the 100 senators. If cloture passes, it enables a vote on the original measure the filibuster was designed to block.\par \par \uc2 The longest filibuster in Senate history was achieved by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2003/jun/27/usa.guardianobituaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strom Thurmond}}}\uc2 , the pro-segregationist South Carolina senator, when he spoke for 24 hours and 18 minutes in an effort to block civil rights legislation in 1957.\par \par \uc2 Thurmond\u8217\'20\'19s speech \u8211\'20\'13 described by his biographer as a \u8220\'20\'1Curological mystery\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 was reportedly achieved with help of prior steam baths to dehydrate his body and preclude the need for regular bathroom breaks. He was also reported by a staffer to have had himself fitted with a catheter to relieve himself while he spoke.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240924ek9o0030e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
