\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Pennsylvania crucial to White House hopes, Trump says at campaign rally\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 995 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 13:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-president gives meandering address in swing state and paints dark vision of US under Democratic rule\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to Pennsylvania, telling his rally attendees that their state was critical to his ability to win back the White House and encouraging them to turn out to vote, though he also called early voting \u8220\'20\'1Cstupid stuff\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we win Pennsylvania, we win the whole thing,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, soon after taking the stage more than 45 minutes later than scheduled. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very simple.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania swung for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, delivering its 20 electoral votes and helping Biden secure the victory in one of the few states that help decide US elections. This year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls on average}}}\uc2  have shown \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with a slight lead over Trump \u8211\'20\'13 though the state is clearly in play, and both candidates are campaigning through it frequently in the final two months before November.\par \par \uc2 Trump has held his signature rallies significantly less this year than he did in 2016, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/22/trump-2024-rallies-schedule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently reported}}}\uc2 , which said his campaign promises Trump will ramp up the rallies in the final stretch. Earlier in the day, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-2024-trump-harris-china-dc1e402d7d829acc904a4326370ac04a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 listened}}}\uc2  to farmers talk about the problems they\u8217\'20\'19re facing and boosted his ideas about imposing tariffs on foreign countries as a way to improve economics in the US.\par \par \uc2 While he\u8217\'20\'19s on the road for large rallies less, he\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly known for his frequent digressions, a longtime fixture of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speaking style that appear to be increasing this year. At the rally at \uc2 Indiana University of Pennsylvania\uc2  in Indiana, Pennsylvania, on Monday, he hopped around at breakneck pace and was difficult to follow. When coherent, he painted a dark vision of America under Democratic rule and starkly laid out what he would do if he won, including mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/election-trump-speeches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started defending}}}\uc2  his meandering rambles as a storytelling technique called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weave\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a sign of his oratory brilliance. Critics say his tangents about bacon sales or Hannibal Lecter, and his defense of them as intentional and smart, show a salesman trying to rebrand his disarray.\par \par \uc2 After starting on claims that Harris would turn the US into Venezuela at Monday\u8217\'20\'19s rally, Trump then moved into \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere they cure the tar\u8221\'20\'1D, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the environmentalists, you know where they cure the tar, where they take the tar and they make it into beautiful oil, Houston, Texas, and it all goes flying up in the air.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump joked that he nearly called Pennsylvania a \u8220\'20\'1Cstate\u8221\'20\'1D rather than a commonwealth, saving himself from a gaffe that he claimed would invite negative headlines. He caught himself before calling it a state, though, because \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m cognitively very strong.\u8221\'20\'1D He also called Harris \u8220\'20\'1Ca very dumb person\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWinston Churchill was this great speaker \u8211\'20\'13 great,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at one point. \u8220\'20\'1CI get much bigger crowds than him, but nobody ever says I\u8217\'20\'19m a great speaker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite his nonstop verbal wandering, he bragged about his lack of a script: \u8220\'20\'1CIsn\u8217\'20\'19t it nice to have a president that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to use a teleprompter?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He repeated a spate of false claims, such as that crime is up. Crime is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/violent-crime-murder-rate-fbi-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 down}}}\uc2 . He alleged he won the 2020 election by millions of votes. He lost. He wove an alternate reality where wars between Russia and Ukraine and between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  do not exist because he had won in 2020.\par \par \uc2 He lashed out at Biden and Harris. He said he was again calling Biden \u8220\'20\'1Csleepy Joe\u8221\'20\'1D, regressing back to that insult instead of \u8220\'20\'1Ccrooked Joe\u8221\'20\'1D because he is not smart and is not acting as president any more. Harris, for her part, is a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery dumb person\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump said, and cannot answer basic questions.\par \par \uc2 He brought up a recent interview Harris did with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 , who Trump claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cused to love me until I decided to run for politics\u8221\'20\'1D. He said some people believe \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who Trump called \uc2 Barack Hussein Obama\uc2  with an emphasis on his middle name, is leading the country instead of Biden. And he surfaced the unproven claim that Harris did not actually work at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  as a student, something that recently has irked him as rightwing accounts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2024/09/09/mcdonalds-statement-harris-job-fact-check/75105207007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spread rumors}}}\uc2  questioning her fast-food work history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to go to a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s next week,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to go to a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to work the french fry job for about a half an hour. I want to see how it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He brought up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a key liability for Trump and other Republicans after the overturning of Roe v Wade. Several states have direct ballot measures that would protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Democrats have made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access a major plank of the 2024 race. He praised the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  for overturning Roe, saying the decision took \u8220\'20\'1Ccourage\u8221\'20\'1D. He added that there should be unspecified \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptions\u8221\'20\'1D to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s all they talk about. The country is falling apart. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to end up in world war three, and all they can talk about is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The stop in the critical swing state comes after two assassination attempts, including one in Butler, Pennsylvania, in July. Trump will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-rally-butler-pennsylvania-oct-5-rcna172329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returning}}}\uc2  to Butler in early October, some news outlets reported Monday. He displayed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/dissecting-immigration-chart-trump-saved-life/story?id=112112815"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration chart}}}\uc2  that he says saved his life from the Butler shooter during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s rally, joking that he \u8220\'20\'1Csleeps with that page\u8221\'20\'1D at night. \u8220\'20\'1CImmigration saved my life,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Later in the speech, he again railed against immigration and migrants, bringing up towns that have received increases of people in recent years and saying those places are \u8220\'20\'1Clawless\u8221\'20\'1D, full of gangs and irreparably damaged. He promised that all migrant flights to Pennsylvania and elsewhere would be ended if he wins.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to get them the hell out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of migrants.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240924ek9o0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
