\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  measures are on the ballot in 10 states this year. Democrats can win them\b0\par\par\uc2 Katrina vanden Heuvel \par \uc2 953 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 worst fear is voters turning up in droves to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in ballot referendums in swing states\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re tired of breathlessly following the horserace polling of the presidential and congressional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 races}}}\uc2 , you might consider instead breathlessly following the horserace polling of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2024/09/12/abortion-ballot-measures-states-november/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot initiatives}}}\uc2  to protect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . In a sense, they\u8217\'20\'19re more revealing.\par \par \uc2 Pending some outstanding court challenges from Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 whose dogged commitment to \u8220\'20\'1Cleaving this issue to the states\u8221\'20\'1D curiously disappears when they realize they\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose \u8211\'20\'13 up to 10 states will have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-election-2024-roe-ballot-4403190b898e501b0834053c3417d072"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  referendums}}}\uc2  on the ballot this year. And it happens that they\u8217\'20\'19ll share that ballot with competitive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate races}}}\uc2  in states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailymontanan.com/2024/07/19/three-ballot-measures-cross-signature-threshold-to-be-included-in-montanas-november-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/nevada-adds-proposed-constitutional-amendment-for-abortion-rights-to-2024-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/13/g-s1-16714/arizona-abortion-access-measure-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wfla.com/news/florida/desantis-florida-abortion-rights-amendment-built-on-fraud/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/baltimore/news/maryland-reproductive-freedom-amendment-abortion-ballot-2024-roe-wade-baltimore/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Nevada and Arizona, which could also play a decisive role in the presidential race, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/official-polls/fox-news-poll-harris-closes-gap-trump-sun-belt-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News poll}}}\uc2  found that over 70% of voters in both states plan to vote in favor of codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Giving voters the opportunity to vote directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is a strategic win for progressives on a few levels. Of course, in a time when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 22 state legislatures have acted}}}\uc2  to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since Dobbs, it\u8217\'20\'19s a powerfully effective way to protect the right to choose. It also helps keep the subject in headlines when the Trump campaign would prefer voters to be distracted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mythical, racist claims}}}\uc2  about Haitian immigrants. And perhaps most significantly, it could motivate otherwise unenthusiastic voters to show up for what seems to be yet another excruciatingly close election.\par \par \uc2 Ballot initiatives are a useful exercise in revealed preference. It has long been observed that millions of Americans end up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/14/opinion/elites-populists-political-beliefs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting against their economic self-interest}}}\uc2  each election cycle. In presidential elections, voters choose candidates, not policy papers. It\u8217\'20\'19s why swing voters were not compelled by the argument that Joe Biden could serve four more years as president because he \u8220\'20\'1Csurrounds himself with the right people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Yet when voters have the chance to vote up or down on an issue that will directly impact their lives, they aren\u8217\'20\'19t in the habit of denying themselves civil rights or quality of life improvements. And in the wake of Roe v Wade getting overturned, that has proved especially true.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, every state referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a victory for pro-choice advocates. Voters in California, Michigan and Vermont voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2022/11/us-midterm-elections-resounding-victories-abortion-state-ballot-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine reproductive rights}}}\uc2  in their respective constitutions, while voters in Kentucky and Montana decisively voted down measures that would have restricted them. This coincided with progressive overperformance in gubernatorial and congressional races, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/11/25/1139040227/abortion-midterm-elections-2022-republicans-democrats-roe-dobbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly salient}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ballot initiatives on other issues have also demonstrated sizable majorities for the right progressive priorities, even in so-called conservative states. Since 2012, measures to legalize recreational marijuana have passed in over a dozen states \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2014/nov/05/oregon-legalises-marijuana-recreational"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaska}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://norml.org/blog/2020/10/30/montanans-vote-yes-on-marijuana-legalization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stltoday.com/business/local/surprise-recreational-marijuana-sales-become-legal-in-missouri-on-friday/article_8aa59c2f-6250-59ac-8c6a-7dccfb6907f9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/ohio-recreational-marijuana-sales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Minimum_wage_on_the_ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ballotpedia}}}\uc2 , there have been 22 statewide measures to raise the minimum wage since 1998; they\u8217\'20\'19ve all passed.\par \par \uc2 In this election, too, there are opportunities for waves of support for progress in unexpected places.\par \par \uc2 Take Florida (please). The citizen-led group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridiansprotectingfreedom.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Floridians Protecting Freedom}}}\uc2  has been tirelessly pushing for amendment 4, which would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/health/2024-09-12-coalition-fighting-protect-abortion-florida/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine the right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution if it can garner 60% of the vote. One poll found that the initiative is positioned nicely to pass, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/08/14/florida-abortion-amendment-poll/74766606007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 69% support}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Florida amendment 3, which would legalize marijuana in the state, has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.ballotpedia.org/2024/09/18/florida-amendment-3-exceeds-previous-records-for-marijuana-legalization-campaign-contributions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broken the record}}}\uc2  for the most money spent on any state cannabis measure, with more than $100m raised and counting. On that issue, the Republican party seems to recognize which way the smoke is blowing, since Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/19/trump-desantis-florida-marijuana-legalization-ballot-measure-00179847"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come out in favor of it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For all the talk of Florida falling out of reach for progressives, these amendments could serve as yet another signal that the left shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t give up on the state. This is the same state that voted to restore the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/nov/09/florida-amendment-4-felons-voting-rights-response-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting rights of more than 1 million felons}}}\uc2  in 2018 (despite immediate efforts that followed by the Republican government to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/in-florida-the-gutting-of-a-landmark-law-leaves-few-felons-likely-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subvert the will of the people}}}\uc2  ). There is such a sizable bloc for progress, in fact, that despite Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 60% threshold for constitutional amendments being the highest in the country, Republicans have proposed raising it even higher, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/breaking/2023/02/14/florida-republicans-push-to-make-it-harder-for-citizens-to-pass-amendments/69899128007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 66.67%}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Beyond the Sunshine state, putting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights front and center could also help address the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s nationwide challenges with younger voters. While \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has managed to earn back some of the support that Biden lost among voters under 30, she still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/cnn-data-guru-says-harris-struggling-underperformance-from-young-voters-amid-taylor-swift-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 isn\u8217\'20\'19t matching his 2020 performance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sure, maybe touting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement on Instagram}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4884398-barack-obama-young-voter-push-tik-tok-videos/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending Barack Obama to juice voter registration on TikTok}}}\uc2  will move the needle. But with women under 45 citing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/31/us/elections/abortion-polls-women-trump-harris.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motivating issue this election}}}\uc2 , it would seem wise to keep spotlighting a rare issue that is both persuasive to swing voters and galvanizing for young activists.\par \par \uc2 At the St Petersburg campus of the \uc2 University of South Florida\uc2 , the 20-year-old college senior Alexis Hobbs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://health.wusf.usf.edu/health-news-florida/2024-09-11/florida-abortion-restrictions-drive-these-college-students-to-activism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can be found}}}\uc2  wearing a pink T-shirt behind a pink table recruiting her peers to vote \u8220\'20\'1CYes on 4.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an interview with New York Magazine, Hobbs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/florida-abortion-law-amendment-4.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared}}}\uc2  just how motivated her fellow young people are to fight this fight: \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want to live out their entire adulthood this way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Katrina vanden Heuvel is editorial director and publisher of the Nation, a member of \uc2 the Council on Foreign Relations\uc2 , and has contributed to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240924ek9o001e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
