\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump tells supporters at campaign rally \u8216\'20\'18if we win Pennsylvania, we win the whole thing\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos, Chris Stein and Anna Betts \par \uc2 8,991 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 02:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read our latest story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Thanks for reading. Rachel Leingang\u8217\'20\'19s story from the Trump rally is here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/trump-rally-pennsylvania-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania crucial to White House hopes, Trump says at campaign rally }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  delivered a speech in Indiana, Pennsylvania, telling supporters: \u8216\'20\'18If we win Pennsylvania, we win the whole thing.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, refused to take a stance on the scandal involving North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor during a Charlotte visit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A key Nebraska lawmaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/republican-bid-change-nebraskas-electoral-system-trump-fails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a Trump-backed effort}}}\uc2  to change state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral vote rules.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A government shutdown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f18fe48f08a5bb140a7f59#block-66f18fe48f08a5bb140a7f59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems}}}\uc2  to have been averted, with Republican speaker Mike Johnson heading off the politically damaging disruption by agreeing to a spending deal that does not include measures against non-citizen voting, which Trump had demanded.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f195188f080a0d348dd578#block-66f195188f080a0d348dd578"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the endorsements}}}\uc2  of hundreds of former national security and military officials, who said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas proven he is not up to the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f19faf8f082ee6d991244c#block-66f19faf8f082ee6d991244c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid out}}}\uc2  how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will spend his final months in office, dubbing it the \u8220\'20\'1Csprint to the finish\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign also reacted to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump: Nobody should want a federal law protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D reads a tweet.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: Nobody should want a federal law protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zbZig3rEn5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zbZig3rEn5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1838387672433271012?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ended his 96-minute speech in Indiana, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign reacted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to close the Department of Education.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a key goal of Project 2025 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0fFTrHznXG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0fFTrHznXG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1838385310901899557?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump later started using athletes in the Olympics to make anti-trans remarks and false claims. There were no transgender athletes who were competing outside of the gender they were assigned at birth at this year\u8217\'20\'19s Olympic games.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to keep men out of women\u8217\'20\'19s sports,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so demeaning to women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump praises 'brilliant and brave' supreme court justices over Roe decision\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou will no longer be thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said to the women in the room. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is now where it always had to be: with the states, and the vote of the people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the federal government and into the states,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSix brilliant and very brave justices of the United States supreme court were able to do that for you, and they did it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  turned his attention to women, claiming \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen are poorer than they were four years ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He claimed women are less healthy, less safe, and more depressed than during his administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am your protector,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs president, I have to be your protector.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for her history as a prosecutor and attorney general in California, as well as the environmental policies she plans to put in place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe wants to ban the sale of gas-powered vehicles, which will destroy the Pennsylvania way of life,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Attorney General, she destroyed San Francisco and she destroyed all of California,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow she\u8217\'20\'19s coming to destroy the United States of America, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to let it happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  brought Republican David McCormick to the stage. McCormick is running against the Democratic Senator Bob Casey in an uphill battle for the senatorial seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a battle between common sense and these radical liberal policies,\u8221\'20\'1D McCormick said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued making anti-immigrant remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins this election, she will flood Pennsylvania cities and towns with illegal migrants from all over the world, and Pennsylvania will never be the same, you will never be the same,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I\u8217\'20\'19m president, all migrant flights to Pennsylvania will stop immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He then claimed that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  never worked at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , a detail in her resum\u233\'00\'E9 she uses to win over a powerful bloc of working-class voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe never worked there, and these fake news reporters will never report it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 After attacking Haitian migrants in Springfield, Ohio, the crowd in Pennsylvania chanted \u8220\'20\'1Csend them back!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  later attacked Venezuelan migrants, generalizing the community and calling them \u8220\'20\'1Clawless gangs,\u8221\'20\'1D while blaming them for problems in the housing market and with crime.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to his claim that the city of Aurora, Colorado, has been overrun by Venezuelan immigrants. Trump has been using Aurora and Springfield, Ohio, as examples of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s mistakes on immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris has inundated small towns all across America with hundreds of thousands of migrants,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He bragged about not using a teleprompter before asking: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think Springfield will ever be the same?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump and JD Vance, his running mate, have falsely claimed that Haitian migrants were eating pets in Springfield \u8211\'20\'13 a statement that has been debunked.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 The former president also touched on the famed Pennsylvania steel industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be strong and powerful again, and we must put tariffs on foreign predators,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to make US steel great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration, he imposed several rounds of tariffs on steel, aluminum, washing machines, solar panels, and goods from China. He has said that, if elected, he will would impose 10% worldwide tariff and a 60% tariff on Chinese goods.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump touched a nerve with fracking in Pennsylvania, saying \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is planning to ban it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf anybody here believes that she will let your energy industry continue fracking, you should immediately go to a psychiatrist,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will get Pennsylvania energy workers pumping, fracking, drilling and producing like never before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  claimed that, during his presidency, foreign countries wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t fight each other without his permission.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey would call me up to ask whether or not they could go to war with some other country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump took a stab at Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 , calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest salesman in history\u8221\'20\'1D and said \u8220\'20\'1Che wants them to win this election so badly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump promises tax cuts if he wins in November\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he promises to deliver tax cuts, attacking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for her plans to raise the corporate income tax rate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the tax queen, and she\u8217\'20\'19s coming for your money,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s coming for your pensions, and she\u8217\'20\'19s coming for your savings, unless you defeat her in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump then focused his speech on inflation, pointing to higher prices for energy and groceries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVote Trump, and your incomes will soar,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CYour net worth will skyrocket, your energy costs and grocery prices will come tumbling down, and we will bring back the American dream, bigger, better and stronger than ever before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  once again falsely claimed that crime is going up, by 45 percent, despite recently released \uc2 FBI\uc2  statistics stating otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more context:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/violent-crime-murder-rate-fbi-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI confirms US murders declined in 2023, contrary to Republican claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 During his speech in Pennsylvania, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunist\u8221\'20\'1D and criticized her border policies.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he thinks he won the 2016 elections because of his harsh border policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have a great country any more,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hate to say it, but America soon will be greater than ever before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump: 'If we win Pennsylvania, we win the whole thing'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur entire nation is counting on the people of this great commonwealth,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said about Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe got to take our country back from these horrible people because, if we win Pennsylvania, we win the whole thing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that the 7 October attacks on Israel and the Russian attack on Ukraine wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have happened if the Biden administration hadn\u8217\'20\'19t been elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThink of how different this world would have been,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump then attacked Harris for dodging questions during her interviews.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump urges supporters to 'get out and vote'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here today because early voting begins in Pennsylvania over the next two weeks, and we need each and every one of you to go out,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said at the start of his speech in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGo out and make a plan to vote early, vote absentee or vote in person on election day, but you gotta get out and vote,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks at campaign rally in Indiana, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started his speech 50 minutes late instead of the scheduled 7pm slot in Indiana, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He walked out to Lee Greenwood\u8217\'20\'19s God Bless the USA.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaigns have ramped up efforts in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 In 2008, the state voted for the Democratic candidate, and again in 2012. But in 2016, Pennsylvania voted in favor of the Republican candidate. The state then voted Democratic in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Trump participated at a roundtable in Pennsylvania to garner support from American farmers. Trump said he would impose a national sales tax with or without Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running 20 minutes late for his speech.\par \par \uc2 He was slated to start at 7pm ET/4pm PT in Indiana, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 In a few minutes, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak at an event at \uc2 Indiana University of Pennsylvania\uc2 , about 55 miles east of Pittsburgh. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  condemned Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  after accusing Michigan attorney general Dana Nessel of potential bias in bringing charges against pro-Palestinian protesters at the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 . Nessel later said Tlaib\u8217\'20\'19s comments were antisemitic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe suggestion that Attorney General Nessel would make charging decisions based on her religion as opposed to the rule of law is antisemitic,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jaketapper/status/1838294708717486389"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper, host of State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAttorney General Nessel has always conducted her work with integrity and followed the rule of law. We must all use our platform and voices to call out hateful rhetoric and racist tropes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York Republican representative Anthony D\u8217\'20\'19Esposito gave part-time jobs to his lover and his fianc\u233\'00\'E9e\u8217\'20\'19s daughter after winning his seat in Congress in 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/23/nyregion/anthony-desposito-affair-congress.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 D\u8217\'20\'19Esposito\u8217\'20\'19s hiring decisions are possible violations to congressional ethics rules, especially those against nepotism and engaging in relationships with employees under one\u8217\'20\'19s supervision.\par \par \uc2 Both were employed in his district office, with the fianc\u233\'00\'E9e\u8217\'20\'19s daughter earning $3,800 a month and the woman involved in the affair earning $2,000 a month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked about his plan to install a blanket tariff on all imports, with additional higher tariffs on goods brought in from China, as a way to extract money from rival nations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t need Congress, but they\u8217\'20\'19ll approve it,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll have the right to impose them myself if they don\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign responded to these remarks: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the core tenet of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 playbook: seize power for himself, squeeze the middle class to the tune of nearly $4,000 a year, and make high costs even worse \u8211\'20\'13 all as he and his billionaire friends get another tax giveaway,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance dodges questions about Mark Robinson during North Carolina campaign event\par \par \uc2 JD Vance kept getting asked by reporters about Mark Robinson. The crowd booed each time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I\u8217\'20\'19ve said, that is Mark Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s case to make to the people of North Carolina,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to make it for him and the people of North Carolina, they get to be the judges of whether they believe him or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in North Carolina, has faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/mark-robinson-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing pressure}}}\uc2  to drop out from the gubernatorial race after a damning CNN story reported that he made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lewd and sexually explicit comments}}}\uc2  on the pornography site Nude Africa between 2008 and 2012.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI really cannot believe that the American media is so much more focused on this than on the struggles of their fellow citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after, Vance ended his speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his rally in Charlotte, JD Vance called gubernatorial candidate Mark Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s reported comments uncovered by CNN (among others, referring to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D), \u8220\'20\'1Cgross\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But he added that Robinson had claimed he had never made the comments, which appeared on a porn forum in 2010.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s up to Mark Robinson to make his case to the state of North Carolina that those weren\u8217\'20\'19t his statements.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says his 'responsibility' to 'listen to the people' when asked about false pet-eating claim\par \par \uc2 JD Vance was asked whether he would change anything about the way he spreads the debunked false claims of pets being abducted and eaten in Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy responsibility is to listen to the people that I serve and not a biased media, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19ll keep on doing in Springfield, Ohio,\u8221\'20\'1D he answered. \u8220\'20\'1CTo the people of this great state of North Carolina, I will always listen to you even when the media attacks me. I will listen to you about what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in your communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish the American media was half as interested in the stress on the local schools, the stress on the hospitals and unaffordable housing as they are, and debunking a story that comes from the residents of Springfield,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 During a Charlotte, North Carolina rally, JD Vance tapped into a well of grievance, blaming \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D for the opioid epidemic and the scourge of fentanyl in the US.\par \par \uc2 Vance has drawn condemnation for his unfounded claim that Haitian migrants in Springfield, Ohio were stealing cats and dogs from community members and eating them. He has since doubled down on his claims, suggesting during an interview on CNN that he had license to \u8220\'20\'1Ccreate stories\u8221\'20\'1D to garner interest in a topic like immigration.\par \par \uc2 During his rally in North Carolina, Vance said that Harris was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad person for causing this border crisis\u8221\'20\'1D and that he and others \u8220\'20\'1Care not bad people for complaining about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the end of his speech, JD Vance supported Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan around environmental policy. Trump plans to scrap the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Inflation Reduction Act and its cleantech subsidies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou want to talk about why our farmers are struggling? Because everything from the diesel fuel that they use to the fertilizer they use has gotten more expensive because of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s energy policies,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He is now taking questions from reporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance recounted the story of his mother, who had struggled with opioid addiction, to attack \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she hopes to revive the border compromise law that would close loopholes in the asylum process. She also supports an earned pathway to citizenship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because he\u8217\'20\'19s going to make it possible for us to enforce the border,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 These remarks come after Vance's false, racist rumors of pets being abducted and eaten in a town in his home state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his speech in Charlotte, North Carolina, JD Vance said American families can no longer afford necessities, citing the higher price of a carton of eggs compared to the price during former president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that if you work hard and play by the rules, you ought to be able to afford a nice life for your American family,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He also said prices for gasoline and homes are higher. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just need to get back to common sense economic policies,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American Dream doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist without homeownership,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance attacked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying she dodges media interviews and questions related to the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow can we trust \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to represent us in front of the most dangerous regimes in the world if she won\u8217\'20\'19t even sit for an interview with the American media?\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s funny to try to have her answer what her actual plans are for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says North Carolina could be state that 'turns this country red' in campaign speech\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has taken the stage. The Republican vice presidential pick said North Carolina is one of the race\u8217\'20\'19s most important states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is going to be the state that turns this country red,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to send \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back to the White House, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do it thanks to the great patriots of this state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a record to be proud of, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has a record to be ashamed of, so we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to promote her,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bishop took a stab at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying she \u8220\'20\'1Ccan\u8217\'20\'19t explain how she\u8217\'20\'19ll lower the cost of living or secure the border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He cited high crime rates in North Carolina. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have no ideas or answers that work for the people,\u8221\'20\'1D Bishop said before extending his support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Dan Bishop\uc2 , candidate for attorney general in North Carolina, took the stage before JD Vance in Charlotte.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m your nominee to become the first Republican attorney general for North Carolina since Zeb Walser in 1896,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a few minutes, the Republican vice-presidential nominee, JD Vance, is expected to deliver a speech in Charlotte, North Carolina. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering his remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The sentencing of the disgraced former senator \uc2 Robert Menendez\uc2  has been delayed until 29 January.\par \par \uc2 A judge on Monday delayed the sentencing of the New Jersey Democrat in his federal corruption case, which was originally set for late October.\par \par \uc2 Menendez, 70, a three-term senator, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty}}}\uc2  by a jury in a Manhattan courtroom of 16 counts of corruption, including bribery, extortion and acting as a foreign agent.\par \par \uc2 A years-long investigation found Menendez had accepted bribes in the form of cash and gold bars in exchange for helping the governments of Qatar and Egypt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke at an event hosted by the Protecting America Initiative, which is led by \uc2 Richard Grenell\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former acting director of national intelligence, and former New York congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump discussed his plans to counter the US reliance on China, backing his idea to use massive tariffs on goods imported from China to protect US industries and raise revenues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody\u8217\'20\'19s done for farmers what I\u8217\'20\'19ve done,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance taps Republican \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  to help him with debate prep - report\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the Republican vice-presidential pick, has picked Representative \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  to help him in his upcoming debate preparation against Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential pick, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/23/us/politics/vance-debate-prep-emmer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past month, Vance has been working closely with his team, reviewing strategies for the face-off with Walz.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate will be debating \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate on 1 October in New York City at 9pm, marking their first televised debate.\par \par \uc2 The preparation sessions have taken place at Vance\u8217\'20\'19s home in Cincinnati and via online meetings with his inner circle, including Trump campaign strategist \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 , the Times reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress appears on track to enact a spending bill that will keep the government open through 20 December, after Republican House speaker Mike Johnson dropped his demand for passage of a law requiring voters prove their citizenship before registering.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has demanded passage of that bill, and in remarks on the Senate floor earlier today, majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  condemned his tactics ahead of the election:\par \par \uc2 The matter is now very straightforward: we now have less than a week to pass a funding bill through the House, through the Senate, and on to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 Both sides will have to act celeritously and with continued bipartisan good faith to meet the funding deadline. Any delay or last minute poison pill can still push us into a shutdown. I hope \u8211\'20\'13 and I trust \u8211\'20\'13 that this will not happen.\par \par \uc2 Of course, as we proceed, it\u8217\'20\'19s important to remember that negotiations didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to wait until the last minute. This agreement could have very easily been reached weeks ago, but Speaker Johnson and House Republicans chose to listen to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s partisan demands instead of working with us from the start to reach a bicameral, bipartisan agreement.\par \par \uc2 Remember: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent the entire month urging House Republicans to shut the government down if his poison pills weren\u8217\'20\'19t passed. That is outlandishly cynical: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  knows perfectly well that a shutdown would mean chaos, pain, needless heartache for the American people. But as usual, he just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to care.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the spending negotiations:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/government-spending-shutdown-bill-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress agrees to funding deal to avert shutdown in blow to Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Keeping Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s unique system of allocating electoral votes by congressional district in place improves \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning the election with only the three Great Lakes battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 Wisconsin, Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Those three states combined with an electoral vote from Nebraska \u8211\'20\'13 which seems gettable, as the district encompassing the largest city Omaha leans Democratic \u8211\'20\'13 would send the vice-president to the White House.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/20/trump-union-voters-democrat-fears-00180171?nname=politico-toplines&nid=0000018f-3124-de07-a98f-3be4d1400000&nrid=2f6ae1fe-07cc-4234-89b5-8951cbfae8c6&nlid=2758340"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  declining to endorse any candidate last week, after backing Democrats for years, could be a warning sign for Harris, particularly when it comes to the white voters who will decide the victor in the Great Lakes states. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  withholding an endorsement from Harris this week \u8212\'20\'14 after internal polling showed most respondents backing Trump \u8212\'20\'14 is sparking fresh concerns that the GOP nominee could have higher-than-expected support among union members, especially men. Labor leaders in other sectors attest that, like in 2016 and 2020, the former president has maintained a grip on key parts of their rank-and-file despite his anti-union record. Privately, Democrats say Harris still has work to do to win over older, white, working-class voters who make up a large portion of the electorate in the Rust Belt and have been hit by high prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCandidly, Trump has a solid, solid base of working-class people that have bought into his message,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jimmy Williams, president of the \uc2 International Union of Painters and Allied Trades\uc2 , which has endorsed Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s movable and it\u8217\'20\'19s been moving. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not like some tide that\u8217\'20\'19s turned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  leaders have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/18/teamsters-no-endorsement-2024-election-00179900"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned the methodology}}}\uc2  of the polling showing Trump winning majority support among the union\u8217\'20\'19s members. But one pro-Harris union official, who was granted anonymity to speak freely, spoke in dire terms about it. The person said it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cred flag\u8221\'20\'1D that is reminiscent of the 2016 election, when Hillary Clinton underperformed among union households despite winning the majority of top labor endorsements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHard not to have \uc2 HRC\uc2  flashbacks right now, to be honest, that stuff might be wrong beneath the surface,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope it\u8217\'20\'19s not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic strategists said Harris\u8217\'20\'19 performance in November could come down to the historic gender gap, especially among blue-collar voters, that has so far defined this election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key Nebraska lawmaker rejects Trump-backed effort to change state's electoral vote rules \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 An attempt by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to convince Nebraska state lawmakers to change their system for allocating electoral votes appears to have faltered, after a key legislator said he opposed the campaign.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2024/09/23/state-sen-mike-mcdonnell-deflates-gop-hopes-for-nebraska-winner-take-all-in-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Nebraska Examiner reports}}}\uc2  that Mike McDonnell, an Omaha-area lawmaker who only recently switched his registration to GOP from Democratic, said he will not support changing the state\u8217\'20\'19s rules for allocating electoral votes to a winner-take-all system. Under the current system, electoral votes in Nebraska are allocated by congressional district, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the district around Omaha four years ago. The change would benefit Trump, as it would almost certainly allow him to pick up all five electoral votes in the solidly red state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have taken time to listen carefully to Nebraskans and national leaders on both sides of the issue. After deep consideration, it is clear to me that right now, 43 days from Election Day, is not the moment to make this change,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonnell said.\par \par \uc2 While Republicans control Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s unicameral legislature, dissent within the party has stopped governor \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2  from calling a special session to change the electoral vote rules.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the recent legislative push:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/21/republicans-nebraska-trump-electoral-college"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans step up effort to change Nebraska voting rules to help Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump accuses justice department of 'mishandling and downplaying' second assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  launched a partisan attack on the justice department and \uc2 FBI\uc2  in a just-released statement, accusing the agencies of showing leniency towards the suspect arrested last week for apparently attempting to assassinate him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 /Joe Biden Department of Justice and \uc2 FBI\uc2  are mishandling and downplaying the second assassination attempt on my life since July. The charges brought against the maniac assassin are a slap on the wrist,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president wrote.\par \par \uc2 He went on to accuse the agencies of conspiring against him, mentioning his two impeachments as well as his involvement in the January 6 attack on the Capitol, among other scandals that occurred during his presidency, and after. \u8220\'20\'1CThe DOJ and \uc2 FBI\uc2  have a Conflict of Interest since they have been obsessed with \u8216\'20\'18Getting Trump\u8217\'20\'19 for so long,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican governor of Florida who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s one-time rival but has since endorsed him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/16/trump-assassination-attempt-suspect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has announced}}}\uc2  that the state will open its own investigation of the incident, which occured at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf course in West Palm Beach.\par \par \uc2 Trump said that investigation should be taken precedent:\par \par \uc2 If the DOJ and \uc2 FBI\uc2  cannot do their job honestly and without bias, and hold the aspiring assassin responsible to the full extent of the Law, Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and the State of Florida have already agreed to take the lead on the investigation and prosecution. Florida charges would be much more serious than the ones the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has announced. The TRUTH would be followed, wherever it leads. OUR JUSTICE SYSTEM IS CORRUPT AND DISCREDITED, especially as it pertains to the 45th President of the United States, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 . LET FLORIDA HANDLE THE CASE!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police Leaders for Community Safety, a nonpartisan advocacy organization made up of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://policeleaders.org/advisory-board/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law enforcement leaders}}}\uc2  from across the US, has endorsed Democratic nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://policeleaders.org/police-leaders-for-community-safety-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  posted on Monday, Sue Riseling the chair of the organization, said that the endorsement of Harris \u8220\'20\'1Creflects Harris\u8217\'20\'19 track record and unwavering commitment to public safety and the rule of law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Riseling added that as law enforcement leaders, they \u8220\'20\'1Cknow first-hand what it will take to make our communities safer \u8211\'20\'13 and that includes having \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as our next president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Man suspected of attempting assassination of Trump ordered to remain in jail without bond \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Ryan Routh, 58 \u8211\'20\'13 who was arrested in Florida this month and accused of trying to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his golf course \u8211\'20\'13 was ordered to remain in jail without bond to await trial on two gun-related charges, according to a new report from Reuters.\par \par \uc2 This comes as US prosecutors are seeking to charge Routh with attempting to assassinate a major political candidate, Reuters added.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f16aaa8f088e71adbf7c2a#block-66f16aaa8f088e71adbf7c2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  in a court filing that Routh left behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/trump-golf-club-suspect-assassination-attempt-note"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a note }}}\uc2  where he acknowledged that he intended to kill the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2  reportedly said in a statement that its pro- Mark Robinson advertisements are set to expire on Tuesday, and that no further placements have been made, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/09/23/us/trump-harris-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This comes just days after CNN reported that Robinson, the Republican nominee for governor of North Carolina, had made disturbing comments on a porn message forum, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/22/lindsey-graham-mark-robinson-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 describing himself as a black Nazi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, it was also reported that several of Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s top staffers on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/mark-robinson-north-carolina-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his campaign have quit}}}\uc2  in the days following the media report.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to appear on ABC\u8217\'20\'19s The View talk show on Wednesday, the network {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dgepress.com/abcnews/pressrelease/president-joe-biden-to-visit-the-view-live-in-studio-wednesday-sept-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  announced}}}\uc2 , adding that it will be Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first interview since the Democratic National Convention and the July presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 The network added:\par \par \uc2 The exclusive appearance marks the first live appearance by a sitting president on the show and the second time a sitting president has visited, following former \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s history-making visit which aired July 29, 2010.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The United States is sending additional troops to the Middle East during the sharp surge in violence between Israel and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hezbollah}}}\uc2  forces in Lebanon that has raised the risk of a greater regional war, the Pentagon said moments ago.\par \par \uc2 Pentagon press secretary Maj Gen Pat Ryder would provide no details on how many additional forces or what they would be tasked to do. The US currently has about 40,000 troops in the region, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The new deployments come after significant strikes by Israeli forces against targets inside {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2  that have killed hundreds and as Israel is preparing to conduct further operations and the state department is warning Americans to leave Lebanon as the risk of a regional war increases.\par \par \uc2 Due to the unpredictable nature of ongoing conflict between \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and Israel and recent explosions throughout Lebanon, including Beirut, the US embassy urges US citizens to depart Lebanon while commercial options still remain available,\u8221\'20\'1D the state department had cautioned on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 You can follow the latest updates on the Middle East in our dedicated live blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/23/middle-east-crisis-live-hezbollah-israel-war-lebanon-evacuations-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli airstrike reportedly targets senior Hezbollah commander; Lebanon says more than 270 killed \u8211\'20\'13 Middle East crisis live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The man suspected of attempting an assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wrote a note where he acknowledged that he indeed intended to kill the former president, federal prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f16aaa8f088e71adbf7c2a#block-66f16aaa8f088e71adbf7c2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  in a court filing. The document included several new details of the incident at a Florida golf course where Trump was playing last week, including that the \uc2 FBI{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f16fd18f08a5bb140a7d47#block-66f16fd18f08a5bb140a7d47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 geolocated}}}\uc2  two cellphones belonging to Ryan Wesley Routh to the area around the former president\u8217\'20\'19s properties in the weeks leading to his arrest. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f15f508f080b5a72d8b138#block-66f15f508f080b5a72d8b138"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new poll}}}\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  trailing the former president in three of the four Sun Belt swing states, while another survey has her seeing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f188e58f08a5bb140a7ed2#block-66f188e58f08a5bb140a7ed2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a historic spike}}}\uc2  in her favorability ratings.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A government shutdown{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f18fe48f08a5bb140a7f59#block-66f18fe48f08a5bb140a7f59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems}}}\uc2  to have been averted, with Republican speaker Mike Johnson heading off the politically damaging disruption by agreeing to a spending deal that does not include measures against non-citizen voting, which Trump had demanded.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f195188f080a0d348dd578#block-66f195188f080a0d348dd578"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the endorsements}}}\uc2  of hundreds of former national security and military officials, who said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas proven he is not up to the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/23/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66f19faf8f082ee6d991244c#block-66f19faf8f082ee6d991244c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid out}}}\uc2  how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will spend his final months in office, dubbing it the \u8220\'20\'1Csprint to the finish\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House announces Biden's 'sprint to the finish' in final months of presidency\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to depart the White House next January, after he ended his bid for a second term and endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . This morning, his administration\u8217\'20\'19s communications director Ben LaBolt announced Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csprint to the finish\u8221\'20\'1D, a plan to spend his final months in office doing what he can to achieve his administration\u8217\'20\'19s priorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the president decided to step back from the campaign and endorse the vice-president, he called his senior team together that day and said we need a plan for the next 180 days to finish as strong as we started,\u8221\'20\'1D LaBolt wrote, continuing:\par \par \uc2 Every day the president meets with his team, he is pushing to lay it all out on the field for the remainder of the term. His directives are:\par \par \uc2 Aggressively execute on the rest of his agenda\par \par \uc2 Look for new opportunities to put a stake in the ground for the future\par \par \uc2 Hit the road to highlight the Biden-Harris record\par \par \uc2 Show up as a president for all Americans and communicate directly with them on how the Biden-Harris Agenda will pay dividends now and 10, 20, 30 years into the future\par \par \uc2 LaBolt offered a preview of what Biden would be doing in the days and weeks to come:\par \par \uc2 The week of 9/23, the president will roll out new policy to combat gun violence. This is a president who has taken dozens of executive actions to counter the scourge of gun violence, established the first ever White House Office of Gun Violence Prevention \u8211\'20\'13 overseen by the vice-president, and signed the most significant gun violence prevention legislation in nearly 30 years.\par \par \uc2 The week of 9/23, the president will give a speech on the historic work he has done to tackle the climate crisis and the Biden-Harris administration will make new policy announcements to keep building on this progress\par \par \uc2 The president will keep traveling the country \u8211\'20\'13 highlighting the Biden-Harris record\par \par \uc2 The president will travel internationally as he continues to strengthen our alliances and partnerships on the world stage, which has been a top priority for him as president having restored American leadership on the world stage\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has not voted for a Democratic presidential candidate since 2008, but recent polls have shown \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  within striking distance of taking its 16 electoral votes. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  has a look at why:\par \par \uc2 Landon Simonini found himself standing in the middle of a Charlotte highway lane at 2.30 in the afternoon, stuck in an artificial traffic jam while drivers waited for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plane to land and the motorcade to clear for the rally later that day.\par \par \uc2 He was out of his car, because why not? He wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going anywhere soon. His red Make America great again cap stood out among others cursing the traffic gods.\par \par \uc2 Simonini, born and bred in Charlotte, builds houses. His livelihood depends to some degree on Charlotte\u8217\'20\'19s tremendous growth. But not all growth is great, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a traditionally southern state,\u8221\'20\'1D Simonini said. \u8220\'20\'1COver 100 people move to Charlotte a day. That is changing the election map. I am born and raised in Charlotte, for 33 years. I have lived here my entire life. I went to school at \uc2 UNC Charlotte\uc2 . This is my city. It is a conservative city and I want to keep it that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in America\u8217\'20\'19s nail-biting 2024 presidential election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2  is now in play. It rejoins a select list of crucial swing states whose voters will decide if Harris becomes America\u8217\'20\'19s first woman of color to win the White House or if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the Oval Office from which he wreaked political chaos for four years.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/15/north-carolina-trump-harris-campaigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s such a dramatic contrast\u8217\'20\'19: Harris turns North Carolina into a toss-up}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of former national security officials endorse Harris\par \par \uc2 A group of more than 700 former military and national security officials have released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nsl4a.org/nsl4a-announcements/nsl4a-endorsement-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an open letter}}}\uc2  endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who they write \u8220\'20\'1Chas proven he is not up to the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris has proven she is an effective leader able to advance American national security interests. Her relentless diplomacy with allies around the globe preserved a united front in support of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s fight against Russian aggression. She grasps the reality of American military deterrence, promising to preserve the American military\u8217\'20\'19s status as the most \u8216\'20\'18lethal\u8217\'20\'19 force in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the letter released by National Security Leaders for America.\par \par \uc2 As for Trump, the group writes:\par \par \uc2 Mr Trump threatens our democratic system; he has said so himself. He has called for the \u8220\'20\'1Ctermination\u8221\'20\'1D of parts of the Constitution. He said he wants to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator,\u8221\'20\'1D and his clarification that he would only be a dictator for a day is not reassuring. He has undermined faith in our elections by repeating lies, without evidence, of \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions\u8221\'20\'1D of fraudulent votes.\par \par \uc2 He has shown no remorse for trying to overturn the 2020 election on January 6th, promises to pardon the convicted perpetrators, and has made clear he will not respect the results of the 2024 election should he lose again.\par \par \uc2 That alone proves Mr Trump is unfit to be Commander-in-Chief.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/22/national-security-officials-endorse-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 700 national security officials endorse Kamala Harris for president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Days after the House of Representatives failed to pass a government spending bill coupled with legislation against non-citizen voting demanded by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Republican speaker, Mike Johnson, is making a new attempt to head off a government shutdown without bowing to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s demands. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the legislative maneuvering, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 US congressional leaders have agreed to a short-term funding deal in a move that averts a damaging pre-election government shutdown and also amounts to a snub for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The prospect of a shutdown at the expiration of the current government funding on 30 September had been looming after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  insisted on tying future funding to legislation that would require voters to show proof of US citizenship \u8211\'20\'13 known as the Save Act and backed by Trump but opposed by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of backroom maneuvering, the Republican House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson}}}\uc2 , announced a compromise that provides funding for another three months while decoupling it from the Save Act. Any other path would have been \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical malpractice\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 The new package continues present spending levels while also giving $231m in emergency funds to the beleaguered Secret Service to enable it to provide added protection for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican presidential nominee, who has been the subject of two failed apparent assassination attempts \u8211\'20\'13 as well as his Democratic opponent, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , before the presidential election on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 It represents a climbdown for Johnson, who had previously adhered to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demand that government funding be conditioned on passing the Save Act. The bill \u8211\'20\'13 has become an article of faith for the former president and his supporters due to their belief, unsupported by evidence, that electoral fraud is rife.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/government-spending-shutdown-bill-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress agrees to funding deal to avert shutdown in blow to Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has seen a surge in favorability among voters and is increasingly viewed as the candidate most likely to bring change, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/poll-newly-popular-harris-challenging-trump-change-rcna171308"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a NBC News poll}}}\uc2  released on Sunday found.\par \par \uc2 Among registered voters nationwide, the vice-president is ahead by five percentage points, with 49% support against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 44%. She is also seen as the candidate more likely to bring \u8220\'20\'1Cchange\u8221\'20\'1D, a potentially significant finding given that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1669/general-mood-country.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other surveys}}}\uc2  have found many Americans believe the country is on the wrong track. Among respondents, 47% say Harris represents change, while 38% say the same of Trump.\par \par \uc2 NBC News also found Harris\u8217\'20\'19s favorability jumped 16 points since July, a surge comparable only to what \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  saw after the 9/11 attacks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  continued to goad \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the weekend to debate her again. But, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  report, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign insisted there would be no more debates:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has accepted an invitation from CNN to participate in another debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on 23 October, her campaign said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should have no problem agreeing to this debate. It is the same format and setup as the CNN debate he attended and said he won in June, when he praised CNN\u8217\'20\'19s moderators, rules and ratings,\u8221\'20\'1D the Harris campaign chair, \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will gladly accept a second presidential debate on October 23,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KamalaHarris/status/1837528658275143694"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on X}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI hope \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will join me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debated Joe Biden}}}\uc2  in June when the US president was still running for re-election. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-withdraw-democrat-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performed so badly}}}\uc2  that he ended up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropping out}}}\uc2  of the race in July, and Harris, his vice-president, ascended to the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  invitation, a Trump spokesperson pointed to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s prior statements that there would be no more debates.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/21/kamala-harris-second-debate-cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rejects Harris call for second debate, saying \u8216\'20\'18it\u8217\'20\'19s too late\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will hold a rally in Mint Hill, North Carolina, near Charlotte, on Wednesday afternoon, his campaign announced.\par \par \uc2 It will be the former president\u8217\'20\'19s second rally in the swing state in recent days, after he spoke to supporters in Wilmington over the weekend. North Carolina Republicans are grappling with the fallout from last week\u8217\'20\'19s report that Mark Robinson, their candidate for governor, had a history of making lewd and offensive statements on a pornography site\u8217\'20\'19s message board.\par \par \uc2 The statements were bad enough that most of Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign staff has resigned. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/mark-robinson-north-carolina-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top staffers on Mark Robinson campaign quit after reports of offensive remarks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what we learned from prosecutors today about Ryan Wesley Routh\u8217\'20\'19s motivations to make a suspected second attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s life, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The man accused in the apparent assassination attempt of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at a golf course in Florida left behind a note saying that he intended to kill the former president and maintained in his car a handwritten list of dates and venues where the Republican White House nominee was to appear, the justice department said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The new allegations were included in a detention memo filed ahead of a hearing on Monday at which the justice department was expected to argue that 58-year-old Ryan Wesley Routh should remain locked up while the case is pending.\par \par \uc2 The details are meant to buttress prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 assertions that Routh had set out to kill Trump before the plot was thwarted by a Secret Service agent who spotted a rifle poking out of shrubbery on the West Palm Beach golf course where the former president was playing on 15 September.\par \par \uc2 The note, addressed \u8220\'20\'1CDear World\u8221\'20\'1D, was placed in a box that was dropped at the home of an unidentified person who contacted law enforcement officials after last Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s arrest. It appears to have been based on the premise that the assassination attempt would ultimately be unsuccessful.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/23/trump-golf-club-suspect-assassination-attempt-note"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump golf club suspect left note saying he intended to kill ex-president \u8211\'20\'13 DoJ}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to the geolocation data tying two of his cellphones to the areas around \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s properties, \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents also found in Ryan Wesley Routh\u8217\'20\'19s possession a list of dates where the ex-president would be in August, September and October.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors added that Routh had \u8220\'20\'1Ca notebook with dozens of pages filled with names and phone numbers pertaining to Ukraine, discussions about how to join combat on behalf of Ukraine, and notes criticizing the governments of China and Russia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Suspected second Trump assassin repeatedly visited area around golf course, Mar-a-Lago \u8211\'20\'13 prosecutors\par \par \uc2 Two cellphones found in the car Ryan Wesley Routh was driving when he was arrested were geolocated to areas near \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort and his golf course in Florida in the weeks leading up to his apparent assassination attempt, prosecutors wrote.\par \par \uc2 The phones, part of six that \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents found in Routh\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle, made repeated visits to the vicinity of the two Trump properties between 18 August and 15 September, the court document said.\par \par \uc2 Agents also examined the SKS rifle found in the bushes outside the golf course where Trump was playing, and discovered a fingerprint they matched to Routh.\par \par \uc2 The rifle was found in the bushes outside the fence line near the sixth hole of the golf course, and prosecutors wrote that Trump was playing on the fifth hole when a Secret Service agent saw the rifle\u8217\'20\'19s gun barrel protruding from the bushes, and opened fire.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the rifle, prosecutors wrote that \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents found a backpack and shopping bag attached to the fence that contained plates \u8220\'20\'1Ccapable of stopping small arms fire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents also reviewed a book they believe Routh authored in February 2023 called Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Unwinnable War: The Fatal Flaw of Democracy, World Abandonment and the Global Citizen-Taiwan, Afghanistan, North Korea, WWIII and the End of Humanity , according to the court document.\par \par \uc2 In the book, Routh stated that he:\par \par \uc2 Must take part of the blame for the [person] that we elected for our next president that ended up being brainless, but I am man enough to say that I misjudged and made a terrible mistake and Iran I apologize. You are free to assassinate Trump as well as me for that error in judgment and the dismantling of the deal. No one here in the US seems to have the balls to put natural selection to work or even unnatural selection.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a court document submitted today, prosecutors said Ryan Wesley Routh dropped off a box at a witness\u8217\'20\'19s house months prior to making his attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 After learning of Routh\u8217\'20\'19s arrest, the unnamed witness opened the box and contacted law enforcement. Prosecutors say the box contained \u8220\'20\'1Cammunition, a metal pipe, miscellaneous building materials, tools, four phones, and various letters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One letter was addressed to \u8220\'20\'1CThe World\u8221\'20\'1D and read, in part:\par \par \uc2 This was an assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but I failed you. I tried my best and gave it all the gumption I could muster. It is up to you now to finish the job; and I will offer $150,000 to whomever can complete the job.\par \par \uc2 He [the former President] ended relations with Iran like a child and now the Middle East has unraveled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Man suspected of second assassination attempt on Trump acknowledged plot - prosecutors\par \par \uc2 The man suspected of making a second attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s life last week acknowledged that was his intention in a note discovered by police, prosecutors wrote on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was an assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but I failed you,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryan Wesley Routh wrote in the note, which was included in a package he gave to an unnamed witness before his arrest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump leads Harris in Sun belt battleground states, poll finds\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Broadly speaking, there are two groups of swing states expected to decide the presidential election: the Great Lakes states of Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania, and the Sun belt states of Nevada, Arizona, Georgia and North Carolina. The closely watched pollsters at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/23/us/politics/times-siena-polls-arizona-georgia-north-carolina.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  today released new data from three of the latter group, showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  preferred by voters over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ,}}}\uc2  albeit to varying degrees. The poll finds the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s standing is weakest against Trump in Arizona, where she now has a five-point polling deficit after the same pollsters showed her with a five-point lead last month. The race in Georgia is tighter but the tightest state is North Carolina, which has not supported a Democratic candidate for president since 2008.\par \par \uc2 The survey is the latest sign of the the presidential race remaining in toss-up territory two months after Harris took over as the Democratic candidate from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The Times and Siena College poll is just one data point among many others, but if its findings bear out, it would leave the vice-president reliant on the Great Lakes states as well as Nevada, the fourth Sun belt state that was not surveyed, or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/21/republicans-nebraska-trump-electoral-college"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a single Nebraska congressional district}}}\uc2  to win the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The government appears to have dodged the threat of another shutdown, after congressional leaders reached a spending agreement that expires on 20 December, defying Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demands that they also approve legislation to require voters to prove their citizenship when registering.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden honors women\u8217\'20\'19s soccer champions Gotham F.C. at 10.30am ET, then meets with president Sheikh Mohammed bin Zayed Al Nahyan of the United Arab Emirates at 12.20pm before heading to New York City for the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel has launched a volley of airstrikes at Lebanon today, again raising fears of a regional conflict. You can read out live blog all about it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/23/middle-east-crisis-live-hezbollah-israel-war-lebanon-evacuations-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is delivering remarks in Charlotte, North Carolina at 5pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will hold a rally in Indiana, Pennsylvania at 7pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240923ek9n001s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
