\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are staying in this race\u8217\'20\'19: behind the unraveling of Mark Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in North Carolina\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi in Marion, North Carolina \par \uc2 1,831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2024\par 16:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate for governor\u8217\'20\'19s own words have been landing him in trouble long before the latest reports\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s tub-thumping Republican candidate for governor, had been trying to extricate himself from problems caused by his own words long before CNN dumped a truckload of dirt on him Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Robinson has treated outrage over his ever-increasing litany of racist, sexist, homophobic and antisemitic offense as a badge of honor during the course of the campaign and his term as the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor. But CNN\u8217\'20\'19s report tilled his pornographic internet history, unearthing comments that still managed the power to shock.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/19/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-black-nazi-pro-slavery-porn-forum/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s report}}}\uc2  connects Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s name, email address and biographical details to the \u8220\'20\'1Cminisoldr\u8221\'20\'1D persona, where Robinson described himself as a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack NAZI!\u8221\'20\'1D, praised Hitler, described \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  in racially offensive terms, expressed sexual interest in transgender pornography and described peeping on girls in a public shower when he was 14.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSlavery is not bad,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson reportedly wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CSome people need to be slaves. I wish they would bring it [slavery] back. I would certainly buy a few.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CNN refrained from exposing the entirety of its findings because some of it was too disturbing to address in public, the news organization said.\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the report came out, Robinson claimed he would remain in the race. If Robinson did not drop out before midnight, he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t drop out; the deadline in North Carolina would have passed.\par \par \uc2 Knowing how the left has sought the removal of supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  for receiving questionable largesse from billionaires, it was characteristic of Robinson to liken his situation to Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chi-tech lynching\u8221\'20\'1D 33 years ago over allegations of sexual misconduct with Anita Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to let them do that. We are staying in this race. We\u8217\'20\'19re in it to win it,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said.\par \par \uc2 But the bombastic candidate had already been facing a crushing defeat after a mix of resurfaced remarks and poor polling led the national Republican party, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to back off from their support.\par \par \uc2 Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s apparent interest in transgender pornography stands in sharp contrast to his public opposition for trans rights. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/16/mark-robinson-north-carolina-republican-lgbtq-tirade-filth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Calls for his resignation}}}\uc2  began in 2021 after comments surfaced in which he described education that discussed trans issues as \u8220\'20\'1Cchild abuse\u8221\'20\'1D, LGBTQ+ content as \u8220\'20\'1Cfilth\u8221\'20\'1D and suggested that trans people should be arrested for using the wrong bathroom.\par \par \uc2 Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s opponent, the North Carolina attorney general, \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , has needed to do little more than saturate the airwaves and social media with campaign ads drawing on Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s own rhetoric, while speaking in broad positive terms about the state and his platform and reaffirming his support for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs your next governor, I will veto any further restrictions on reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D Stein said at a rally in Greensboro for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is at the center of Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s appeal to the right and perhaps at the center of the electoral disaster unfolding for Republicans in North Carolina as well. Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s pro-life politics have not just been strident but defiant and accusatory.\par \par \uc2 In one recently unearthed video from a church sermon in 2022, he attacks women\u8217\'20\'19s empowerment and birth control. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy don\u8217\'20\'19t you use some of that building up of your mind and building up of empowerment to move down here, to this region down here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, waving his hand around his crotch. \u8220\'20\'1CGet this under control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Notably, Robinson has admitted to paying for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for his then girlfriend, now wife, in the 80s, something he said he regrets. It is the stridency of his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric that has kept North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s religious right in his corner.\par \par \uc2 Lorra Parker lives in McDowell county, where Republicans have a three-to-one advantage. She went to hear Robinson speak last week. Though she has a broad set of conservative political interests, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was critical to her identity as a voter, she said. Even as Trump appeared to vacillate on this issue in the debate, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to be the perfect candidate, just the better candidate.\par \par \uc2 She applies the same logic to Robinson. Now, she\u8217\'20\'19s reserving judgment while the reporting sorts itself out, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHonestly, I\u8217\'20\'19d need to hear it from a source other than CNN,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think if he\u8217\'20\'19s not guilty of this, then he should fight to prove that he\u8217\'20\'19s not guilty of this. He\u8217\'20\'19s got time to do that. But he\u8217\'20\'19s been lieutenant governor for four years and they just found this out now? That\u8217\'20\'19s a little suspicious to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s public appearances and social media posts are a treasure trove of opposition research for Democrats painting their opponents as extremists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be clearer,\u8221\'20\'1D reads one ad. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Mark Robinson, their vision is one of division, violence and hate. Mark Robinson just fights job-killing culture wars \u8230\'20\'26 Just a few weeks ago, from of all places a church pulpit, he said \u8216\'20\'18some folks need killing.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 On defense from all angles, Robinson went to ground shortly after winning the Republican primary earlier this year, refusing interviews with all but the most stridently conservative publications and broadcasters and largely avoiding public appearances.\par \par \uc2 But a strategy of riding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s coattails and counting on the state\u8217\'20\'19s generally conservative lean had been collapsing as waves of negative press \u8211\'20\'13 about his campaign finances, the maladministration of his wife\u8217\'20\'19s government-funded non-profit, and always his incendiary rhetoric \u8211\'20\'13 flooded the field.\par \par \uc2 Robinson has not led in a poll since June; even before CNN\u8217\'20\'19s revelations, the withdrawal of Joe Biden from the race in July threatened to turn a close race into a rout. The latest poll from Emerson College shows him losing to Stein by eight points.\par \par \uc2 So, Robinson resurfaced a few weeks ago. He had made tentative steps in small venues far from the scrutiny of big-market news reporters to test messaging that retained as much heat as possible without burning people: cayenne rhetoric, not Carolina Reaper.\par \par \uc2 On 11 September, the day after the Harris-Trump debate, Robinson stepped into the back room of Countryside Barbecue in cherry red Marion, North Carolina, looking for friendly territory and as much of a rhetorical rebrand as he might muster under fire.\par \par \uc2 His stump speech touched on gas prices and teacher salaries and state taxes \u8211\'20\'13 policy issues instead of the culture war molotov cocktails about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and guns and gay people which launched his career and won him the nomination.\par \par \uc2 But time and again, his attention turned to how the press and his Democratic opponent, had been lighting him up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a guy named \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2  who wants to talk about any and everything except the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s got something about me from \uc2 Facebook\uc2  eight or nine years ago, where he cut it off just to play about three seconds of it. He didn\u8217\'20\'19t play the whole thing, something about \u8216\'20\'18keep your skirt down.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robinson was referring to the wall-to-wall ads playing across the state replaying a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  video from 2009 in which he says \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cis about killing the child because you weren\u8217\'20\'19t responsible enough to keep your skirt down\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe cut off the part where he said \u8216\'20\'18or keep your pants up\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said to the conservative crowd last week, for whom that was convincing. Then he suggested that ad and others were deceptive. He called his opponent a liar. He dared the press to report it. He also demanded a debate, which Stein has been refusing.\par \par \uc2 Shades of the Robinson bluster lay under the fresh paint of respectability.\par \par \uc2 He spent almost as much time haranguing the president and vice-president in the mountain towns of western North Carolina as he did his actual opponent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe same one that was right there riding shotgun with [Biden] while he was doing it was on TV last night talking about how she was going to fix it all,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said of Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CShe tore it up, but she can\u8217\'20\'19t fix it. What policy has she ever championed since she\u8217\'20\'19s been in any office that will fix the problems that we\u8217\'20\'19re facing right now?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robinson has been walking back his previous, strident calls for a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in North Carolina. Earlier this year, he argued for a six-week \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D law limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier this week, he argued for the public to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/local/charlotte/2024/09/17/north-carolina-mark-robinson-governor-race-abortion-ban-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move on}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D from the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 In a room packed with church-going Republicans in Marion, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody may have a different opinion on that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy opinion is this: no matter where that law sits, as the governor of this state, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to fight to save every single solitary life in the womb. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter whether it\u8217\'20\'19s 12 weeks, six weeks, eight weeks, 20 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight for life in this state.\par \par \uc2 In a reference to Trump and his running mate, JD Vance, Ohio senator and author of Hillbilly Elegy, some of Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s road team wore shirts printed with the words \u8220\'20\'1CFelon / Hillbilly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The shirts reflect the tone of Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s race. He has tied himself for good or ill to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tenor and politics. But even Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team has had enough.\par \par \uc2 According to the conservative Carolina Journal, the Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.carolinajournal.com/robinson-under-pressure-to-withdraw-from-gubernatorial-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been pressuring Robinson to withdraw}}}\uc2 , out of fear that North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s election-deciding swing voters will not just abandon the lieutenant governor but the entire Republican ballot.\par \par \uc2 Citing anonymous campaign sources, the Carolina Journal reported that the Stein campaign leaked the material to CNN, and that the Trump campaign told Robinson that he was no longer welcome at rallies for Trump or Vance. Trump has not mentioned Robinson in the last week. Vance held his first solo rally in North Carolina on Wednesday. Robinson did not appear. His office announced that Robinson had contracted Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign officials denied that they had been pressuring Robinson to quit the race in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/mark-robinson-vows-stay-north-carolina-governor-race-cnn-report-rcna171860"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments to NBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Stein campaign released a terse statement shortly after the CNN piece aired.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNorth Carolinians already know Mark Robinson is completely unfit to be Governor,\u8221\'20\'1D the campaign said. \u8220\'20\'1CJosh remains focused on winning this campaign so that together we can build a safer, stronger North Carolina for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign, however, has gleefully circulated videos with Trump praising Robinson. Trump referred to Robinson as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  on steroids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robinson, in comments under his \u8220\'20\'1Cminisoldr\u8221\'20\'1D persona, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not in the KKK. They don\u8217\'20\'19t let blacks join. If I was in the KKK I would have called him Martin Lucifer Koon!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240920ek9k001gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
