\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  attacks Trump over \u8216\'20\'18immoral\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans at Wisconsin rally\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Herman in Madison, Wisconsin \par \uc2 640 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2024\par 17:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president emphasizes support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at rally in key state, declaring herself \u8216\'20\'18underdog in this race\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaigned in Madison, Wisconsin, the deep blue capital of the state and college town that Democrats hope will turn out enough voters to turn the election in the presidential nominee\u8217\'20\'19s favor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know this is gonna be a tight race until the very end,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the underdog in this race, and we have some hard work ahead of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin voters delivered razor-thin margins during the 2016 and 2020 presidential elections. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the state in 2016 by about 22,000 votes, and in 2020 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  scraped by with just 20,000 more than Trump.\par \par \uc2 Polling in Wisconsin so far shows Harris and Trump neck-and-neck. Three polls conducted this week underscore just how tight the race could be here: polling by AARP, Marist and \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  suggest the race is virtually tied here, with Harris leading Trump by just one point in each.\par \par \uc2 On the trail, Harris has emphasized her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a centerpiece of her campaign and a galvanizing issue for young voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is immoral,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris of the numerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that were implemented after Roe v Wade was overturned. \u8220\'20\'1CLet us agree one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris described meeting with the mother of a young woman who died of sepsis after being denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmber Nicole Thurman,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CI promised her mother I would say her name every time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whoever wins Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s popular vote earns the state\u8217\'20\'19s full 10 electoral votes, giving the state a disproportionate say over the presidential election, and groups such as Madison\u8217\'20\'19s large college-age population will play a critical role in deciding the result. Some of those students attended the Friday rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just so nice to see someone who\u8217\'20\'19s actually joyful,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kaitlin Olson, a sophomore at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2  in Madison. During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s painful debate performance against Trump, Olson said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit was like, \u8216\'20\'18This is scary.\u8217\'20\'19 Now that Kamala is running, I\u8217\'20\'19m like, \u8216\'20\'18OK, a little more joy.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna turn out higher than expected,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jake Leismer, a college freshman who took the bus from campus, joining up with Olson and a group of students at the rally.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic-coordinated campaign, which supports Democrats up and down the ballot, has hired seven full-time campus organizers across the state and a youth organizing coordinator, according to a source familiar with the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s staffing operations in Wisconsin. Kelly Connor, a campus organizer based in Madison, said the campaign has been met with enthusiasm \u8211\'20\'13 even hosting a bonfire to ceremonially burn copies of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s gerrymandered electoral maps, which the state abandoned this year after years of progressive and Democratic party organizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have lots of volunteers that have never volunteered before that want to get out and knock doors,\u8221\'20\'1D said Connor.\par \par \uc2 The young-people effect in Wisconsin came to light fully in 2023, when college students turned out in droves to elect Janet Protasiewicz to the Wisconsin supreme court, creating a liberal majority on the bench. At the heart of the race was \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, which has been caught in a legal snarl since the fall of Roe v Wade triggered a 175-year-old ban in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey know the stakes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Connor. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about fascism versus democracy, and students are willing to do whatever it takes to ensure that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  never sets foot in the White House again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240921ek9l00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
