\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at Wisconsin rally: \u8216\'20\'18Women have died because of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos (now); Chris Stein, Anna Betts and Vicky Graham (earlier) \par \uc2 10,834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2024\par 01:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This liveblog is now closed. You can read our latest story here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing this blog. Thanks for tagging along! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 See all our coverage of the 2024 US elections}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at the day\u8217\'20\'19s political news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  delivered her speech at a campaign rally in Madison, Wisconsin, where she highlighted the case of Amber Thurman, who died in Georgia due to a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Madison, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  restated her plan to give a tax cut to 100 million Americans and expand the child tax credit. This measure aims \u8220\'20\'1Cto help young and new parents buy a car seat, a crib, baby clothes in that most significant phase of their development\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson, the lieutenant governor of North Carolina, will not attend \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally on Saturday after CNN reported on his troubling online posts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris took the stage in Atlanta earlier today, where she also decried the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. She condemned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in her speech, recounting how he appointed three of the justices who would go on to vote for Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s downfall.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779#block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to require that ballots be counted by hand, a move that could complicate and slow down determining whether the swing state has voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service report looking into the 13 July assassination attempt on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  revealed that agents did not have the necessary discussions in advance regarding how the warehouse should be guarded, and about the positioning of a local team on the roof of the warehouse building.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House unanimously approved allowing a bipartisan taskforce investigating the July assassination attempt targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pennsylvania to also scrutinize the apparent second attempt on his life on Sunday in Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican candidate for governor, Mark Robinson, was still in the race for governor on Friday morning after the deadline passed overnight for him to withdraw or be removed from the ballot. He is facing increasing pressure to step down after CNN reported he attacked \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 , backed the reinstatement of slavery and referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D in comments on a pornographic website.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to visit North Carolina tomorrow. When asked about the CNN report by the Associated Press, Trump campaign spokesperson Karoline Leavitt did not mention Robinson by name or answer questions as to whether he would appear with Trump at tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Wilmington, or had been invited to do so.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bemoaned a lack of support from Jewish voters just hours after allegations emerged that a Republican ally had referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornography website.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris wrapped up her speech in Madison by reminding crowd members that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe stakes are even higher\u8221\'20\'1D in this election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWisconsin, it all comes down to this,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here together because we love our country. We love our country and we understand the awesome responsibility that comes with the greatest privilege on Earth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris: 'Women have died because of Trump's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  poses a threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms, specifically on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 She reminded folks in Madison about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s selection of three members of the supreme court with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe v Wade, which they did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are being denied care during miscarriages,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey didn\u8217\'20\'19t want this. And we know that women have died because of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris told the story of Amber Nicole Thurman, a 28-year-old Georgia woman, who died after doctors hesitated to treat her following a complication from a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Harris also recounted Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s story during a speech in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris called her opponent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Can unserious man \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe consequences of putting him back in the White House are extremely serious,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CJust \uc2 Google\uc2  Project 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, referring to \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 -led policy blueprint for the next Republican administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a detailed and dangerous blueprint for what he will do if he were elected president,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 was written by a number of supporters as well as officials who previously served under the former president. The plan calls to defund childcare and overhaul the justice department to give the president and loyalists more power in decisions about who to investigate and prosecute.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Talking about the economy, Harris said she also intends to lower the cost of living.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile our economy is doing well by many measures, prices for everyday necessities like groceries are still too high,\u8221\'20\'1D said the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Harris restated her plan to give a tax cut to 100 million Americans and expand the child tax credit. This measure aims \u8220\'20\'1Cto help young and new parents buy a car seat, a crib, baby clothes in that most significant phase of their development\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris addressed a pressing concern for Americans: affordable housing, particularly problematic in her home state of California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a shortage of housing in America,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith my plan, we are going to cut red tape and work with the private sector to build 3 million new homes by the end of my first term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She pointed to her plan to provide first-time homebuyers with $25,000 in down payment assistance so \u8220\'20\'1Cthey can just get their foot in the door.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris pointed to her professional background as a prosecutor in Oakland, California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stood up for women and children against predators who abused them,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI took on the big banks and delivered $20bn for middle-class families who faced foreclosure because of predatory lending practices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stood up for veterans and students who were being scammed by the big for-profit colleges, and for workers who are being cheated out of the wages they were due, and for seniors facing elder abuse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice-president then addressed concerns for small business owners.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 She addressed last week\u8217\'20\'19s debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , an event filled with falsehood-ridden tangents about crowd sizes, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 It was the same old tired show, the same old tired playbook we\u8217\'20\'19ve heard for years with no plan on how he would address the needs of the American people\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, it\u8217\'20\'19s time to turn the page, and America is ready to start a new way forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said during her speech in Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 'We're the underdog in this race', says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at Wisconsin rally\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s not pay too much attention to the polls, because let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, we are the underdog in this race,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She pointed to her parents\u8217\'20\'19 teaching stint at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Madison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo every time I land, the governor says: \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome home,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has started her speech at a campaign rally in Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The last time the vice-president held a rally in Wisconsin was last month at Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s Fiserv Forum, with her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  tagging along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Aaron Sorkin, the creator of The West Wing, took the stage at the White House to celebrate the TV show\u8217\'20\'19s 25th anniversary and called \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to give up the nomination \u8220\'20\'1Ca selfless act of statesmanship\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the years, I\u8217\'20\'19ve noticed that during times of political tension, pundits will warn us not to expect a West Wing moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Sorkin said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey mean not to expect a selfless act of statesmanship, not to expect anyone to put country first. Don\u8217\'20\'19t expect anyone to swing for the fences or reach for the stars.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut the fact is, West Wing moments do happen, and Dr Biden, we saw proof of that on the morning of July 21. That was the kind of thing we write stories about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The cast and creator of the West Wing attends a 25th anniversary celebration at the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson, the lieutenant governor of North Carolina, will not attend \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally on Saturday after CNN reported on his troubling online posts.\par \par \uc2 His absence shows the risks he poses for Trump and other GOP candidates. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-governor-mark-robinson-trump-kamala-harris-cooper-cnn-stein-c7ee5c23f554f3708619d6b68e208b94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , Robinson is not expected to be at the Wilmington event.\par \par \uc2 He has often joined Trump at campaign stops, and Trump has praised him, even calling him \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  on steroids\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign issued a statement that didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention Robinson, but spoke generally about how North Carolina was key to the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s efforts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s governor, told Bloomberg TV that the recent allegations against North Carolina Republican gubernatorial nominee Mark Robinson aren\u8217\'20\'19t surprising.\par \par \uc2 Cooper said that the allegations may help Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  win the state\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has a history of these kinds of inflammatory comments. We\u8217\'20\'19ve known for a while that he was someone who was unfit for office.\par \par \uc2 enltrNorth Carolina Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  says the recent allegations against North Carolina Republican gubernatorial nominee Mark Robinson aren't surprising, and that they may help Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  win the state.\par \par \uc2 Full interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7eLyBXfodU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7eLyBXfodU}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IkJcfWvygY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IkJcfWvygY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg TV (@BloombergTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BloombergTV/status/1837241073174761754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a similar vein, Bill Carroll, Milwaukee-based Teamsters Joint Council 39 president, will introduce \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s rally tonight, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 This comes two days after the local union endorsed Harris for president, breaking with the national union\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to back a candidate in the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 Carroll called Harris the vice president \u8220\'20\'1Cof the most pro-union administration ever\u8221\'20\'1D and criticized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s labor record.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania Conference of Teamsters has endorsed the vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after the national \uc2 Teamsters union{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/election-teamsters-endorsement-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chose not to back any candidate}}}\uc2  in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 The national union\u8217\'20\'19s decision was seen as a setback for Harris, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saw it as a win for himself.\par \par \uc2 But the endorsement from Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s 95,000 \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , which also includes members from parts of New Jersey and Delaware, could be a strong show of labor support in a key swing state.\par \par \uc2 The PA Conference of Teamsters is committed to vetting candidates and choosing those that are best suited to protect our members\u8217\'20\'19 wages, their rights and their collective bargaining agreements,\u8221\'20\'1D said William Hamilton, president of the PA Conference of Teamsters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president, outspent the former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on digital ads, especially on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , during their debate week, spending $12.2m compared with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s $611,228, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/20/us/politics/kamala-harris-trump-campaign-spending.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This gap has been constant throughout the campaign, raising concerns among Republicans. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s heavy spending in battleground states like Pennsylvania and Michigan highlights her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive digital strategy.\par \par \uc2 While Trump focuses more on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  ads and other digital media, his lighter investment in paid digital advertising could limit his reach.\par \par \uc2 This digital spending difference has prompted Democratic optimism, especially as social media plays a crucial role in engaging undecided and younger voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nebraska Republicans are considering changing how the state distributes its electoral votes to block the Democratic nominee, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , from getting any votes in the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Unlike most states, Nebraska and Maine don\u8217\'20\'19t give all their electoral votes to the statewide winner. Nebraska gives two votes to the statewide winner and one vote for each of its three congressional districts.\par \par \uc2 The second congressional district, which includes Omaha and nearby areas, has leaned more Democratic since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2016 election. In 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the district by 6.5%, and polls show Harris with a similar lead.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/19/nebraska-electoral-system-trump-win-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska may change its electoral system at the last second to help Trump win | Stephen Marche}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dawn Roberts, the co-chair of former GOP presidential candidate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in Iowa, said she\u8217\'20\'19s endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/opinion/columnists/iowa-view/2024/09/20/republicans-for-kamala-harris-dawn-roberts-iowa-campaign-nikki-haley/75306017007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion piece}}}\uc2  in the Des Moines Register, Roberts said Harris impressed her and earned her support through her strong debate performance during the Democratic national convention.\par \par \uc2 The lifelong Republican said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cat a loss\u8221\'20\'1D when both of the presidential candidates were in or near their 80s, referring to President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this month\u8217\'20\'19s debate, she continued to impress, looking at the audience and emphasizing bringing the country together rather than dividing, lifting people up rather than tearing people down,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rally-goers are trickling into a Madison, Wisconsin, venue to hear \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speak later this evening. There are plenty of young faces here \u8211\'20\'13 a positive sign for the campaign, which hopes that college-age voters will help deliver Harris a win in November.\par \par \uc2 According to a source familiar with the Harris campaign, the Democratic-led effort, which advocates for candidates up and down the ballot, has hired seven full-time campus organizers across the state and a youth-organizing director to aid in the effort \u8211\'20\'13 part of the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s 250 staffers across the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , expressed his disappointment at negative rhetoric around immigration and Haitian migrants, especially from former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Republican vice-presidential pick, \uc2 J D Vance\uc2 , in an opinion piece for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/20/opinion/springfield-haitian-migrants-ohio.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He wrote about his personal connection to Springfield, Ohio, and the city\u8217\'20\'19s recent economic resurgence thanks to Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 There have been language barriers and cultural differences, but these Haitians come to work every day, are fitting in with co-workers and have become valuable employees.\par \par \uc2 He stressed the need to address a slew of challenges, such as housing and healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir work will continue long after this fall\u8217\'20\'19s election is over and the national spotlight turns away from Springfield,\u8221\'20\'1D DeWine said, referring to immigrants in the city. \u8220\'20\'1CBut in the meantime, our people and our history deserve better than to be falsely portrayed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/mike-dewine-ohio-trump-vance-haitian-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor condemns Trump and Vance for Springfield claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us now, here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happened in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779#block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has voted}}}\uc2  to require that ballots be counted by hand, a move that could complicate and slow down determining whether the swing state has voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service report looking into the 13 July assassination attempt on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  revealed that agents did not have the necessary discussions in advance regarding how the warehouse should be guarded, and about the positioning of a local team on the roof of the warehouse building.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Secret Service acting director Ronald Rowe Jr said that recent events such as the attempted assassination in July and apparent attempted assassination of the former president on Sunday in Florida highlighted the need for a paradigm shift in the how the Secret Service protects public officials and said that the \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat level is evolving\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House unanimously approved allowing a bipartisan taskforce investigating the July assassination attempt targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pennsylvania to also scrutinize the apparent second attempt on his life on Sunday in Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the stage in Atlanta, where she decried the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which was recently tied to the death of a woman in 2022.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris condemned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in her speech, recounting how he appointed three of the justices who would go on to vote for Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s downfall.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican candidate for governor, Mark Robinson, was still in the race for governor on Friday morning after the deadline passed overnight for him to withdraw or be removed from the ballot. He is facing increasing pressure to step down after CNN reported he attacked \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 , backed the reinstatement of slavery and referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D in comments on a pornographic website.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to visit North Carolina tomorrow. When asked about the CNN report by the Associated Press, Trump campaign spokesperson Karoline Leavitt did not mention Robinson by name or answer questions as to whether he would appear with Trump at tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Wilmington, or had been invited to do so.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bemoaned a lack of support from Jewish voters just hours after allegations emerged that a Republican ally had referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornography website.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before Harris wrapped up her speech, she said she believed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, if elected.\par \par \uc2 Trump has equivocated on whether or not he would do so, saying at the debate last week that he did not think any such legislation would get through Congress.\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 The stakes are so high, because if he is elected again, I am certain he will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every single state, and he would create a national anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordinator. Look at Project 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 enforce states to report on women\u8217\'20\'19s miscarriages and abortions. It\u8217\'20\'19s right there.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls Trump 'the architect of this crisis' for overturning Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then recounted her meeting with Amber Nicole Thurman \u8217\'20\'19s mother, who asked her not to forget who her daughter was:\par \par \uc2 Through the pain and the grief, her mother courageously told her story. I promised her, as she has asked, that we will make sure Amber is not just remembered as a statistic, that she will not just be remembered as a statistic, so that people will know she was a mother and a daughter and a sister, and that she was loved and that she should be alive today.\par \par \uc2 She drew applause by saying that, as president, she would stand with women elsewhere who were suffering the consequences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s happening every day in our country, an untold number of people suffering, women, who are also being made to feel as though they did something wrong. The judgment factor here is outrageous, being made as though to feel as though they are criminals, as though they are alone. So to those women, to those families, I say on behalf of what I believe we all say: we see you, and you are not alone, and we are all here standing with you.\par \par \uc2 Harris added that by appointing the justices who overturned Roe v Wade, Trump created a public health crisis:\par \par \uc2 This is a healthcare crisis, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the architect of this crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris then began discussing the case of Amber Nicole Thurman, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica reported earlier this week}}}\uc2  died after being denied care due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will speak her name, Amber Nicole Thurman,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, as the crowd repeated her name back.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president then made the case that Trump was responsible for her death:\par \par \uc2 When she discovered that she was pregnant, she decided she wanted to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But because of the Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban here in Georgia, she was forced to travel out of state to receive the healthcare that she needed, but when she returned to Georgia, she needed additional care, so she went to a hospital. But you see, under the Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, her doctors could have faced up to a decade in prison for providing Amber the care she needed. Understand what a law like this means: doctors have to wait until the patient is at death\u8217\'20\'19s door before they take action.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris condemns 'hypocrites' who ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while ignoring maternal health\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said lawmakers who have moved to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their states while ignoring the needs of mothers are \u8220\'20\'1Chypocrites\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 One in three women in America lives in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. This includes Georgia and every state in the south except Virginia. Think about that, when you also combine that with what we know has been longstanding neglect around an issue like maternal mortality. Think about that, when you compound that with what has been longstanding neglect of women in communities with a lack of the adequate resources they need for healthcare, prenatal, during their pregnancy, postpartum. Think about that, and these hypocrites want to start talking about this is in the best interest of women and children?\par \par \uc2 As the crowd cheered, Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, where you been? Where you been when it comes to taking care of the women and children of America, where you been? How dare they?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris immediately hit out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , recounting how he appointed three of the justices who would go on to vote for Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s downfall, which paved the way for states like Georgia to enact bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know how we got here. When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president, he hand-selected three members of the United States supreme court, the court of Thurgood and RBG, with the intention that they would overturn the protections of Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 And as he intended, they did, and now more than 20 states have Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, extremists that have passed laws that criminalize healthcare providers, doctors and nurses, and punish women. In two of those states, they provide for prison for life \u8211\'20\'13 prison for life \u8211\'20\'13 for healthcare providers for simply providing reproductive care, the care they so earnestly and rightly believe must be delivered \u8211\'20\'13 all Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. And think about this: many of these bans make no exception, even for rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris speaks in Georgia amid furor over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related death\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just took the stage in Atlanta, where she is expected to decry the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which was recently tied to the death of a woman in 2022, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support for the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 We may also hear from the vice-president about the election board\u8217\'20\'19s rule change today that could slow down the vote-counting process in the battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the death of Amber Nicole Thurman, which Harris blamed on Trump:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris blames Trump for Georgia \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related death: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s what we feared\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Presidential election voting begins in three states\par \par \uc2 Residents of Virginia, South Dakota and Minnesota have hit the polls for early voting today, as the 2024 election gets underway.\par \par \uc2 While the bulk of voters will cast ballots on 5 November, the three states are the first to open their polls, and more will follow throughout October, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/early-voting-presidential-election-trump-harris-7fb7a8ff28490f71cd15529321dfe765#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the weeks to come, millions more Americans will cast absentee ballots by mail. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/us-elections-2024-early-voting-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voting is under way in the 2024 US election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know about early voting and mail-in ballots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin Moncla, a prominent election denier, is holding court on the marble steps just outside the Georgia state board of elections hearing room at the state capitol.\par \par \uc2 Moncla described how state election officials had given him the cold shoulder after the 2020 election. Moncla and fellow activist Joe Rossi filed a complaint alleging that Fulton county had covered up mass election fraud with multiple duplicate ballots, missing ballot images and missing documents.\par \par \uc2 Applause from their supporters occasionally bleeds into the hearing room. Their backers from Georgians for Truth are wearing white T-shirts printed with the words \u8220\'20\'1CPaper Please.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Moncla:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/georgia-election-deniers-trump-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: the election deniers relentlessly hounding Georgia officials}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 House votes to investigate second Trump assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 The House just unanimously approved allowing a bipartisan taskforce investigating the July assassination attempt targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pennsylvania to also scrutinize the apparent second attempt on his life on Sunday in Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no leader in American history who has been attacked as aggressively as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and yet remained so strong and resilient,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, said in a statement after the vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the House is rising to meet this historic moment by voting to formally expand the purview of the taskforce to include the second assassination attempt on his life. The American people deserve answers and accountability for the many security failures that have led to these events \u8211\'20\'13 and this Congress will deliver.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the House unanimously approved the bipartisan Enhanced Presidential Security Act, which would establish universal standards for Secret Service protectees such as the president, former presidents and candidates for the White House, and require a comprehensive review of the agency\u8217\'20\'19s current protection strategy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service acting director Ronald Rowe Jr said on Friday that recents events such as the attempted assassination in July and apparent attempted assassination of the former president on Sunday in Florida, highlighted the need for a paradigm shift in the how the Secret Service protects public officials and said that the \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat level is evolving.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service report states that the site of the rally, the Butler farm show, was seen by the Secret Service and local law enforcement partners \u8220\'20\'1Cas a challenge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The summary of the report reads:\par \par \uc2 Advance personnel and multiple supervisors with oversight of the security plan at the Butler farm show venue recognized line of site concerns.\par \par \uc2 However, the security measures to alleviate these concerns were not carried out on July 13, 2024, as intended.\par \par \uc2 There was a lack of detailed knowledge by Secret Service personnel regarding the state or local law enforcement presence that would be present in and around the AGR complex.\par \par \uc2 There was also a lack of knowledge regarding the specific footprint of resources that would buttress the secure area of the venue and separate it from the AGR complex, which was outside of the site\u8217\'20\'19s secure perimeter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service report looking into the 13 July assassination attempt on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also revealed that agents did not have the necessary discussions in advance regarding how the warehouse should be guarded, and about the positioning of a local team on the roof of the warehouse building, according to the report\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static01.nyt.com/newsgraphics/documenttools/1117755089fb9ff8/a26031cb-full.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive summary}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Another issue that arose on 13 July, according to the report, was that the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s aerial system was experiencing \u8220\'20\'1Ctechnical difficulties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is possible that if the system had \u8220\'20\'1Cfunctioned properly\u8221\'20\'1D the \u8220\'20\'1Cshooter may have been detected as he flew his drone near the Butler farm show venue earlier in the day\u8221\'20\'1D, the summary reads.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a news conference on Friday, the acting director of the Secret Service, Ronald Rowe Jr, said that the findings of the report have prompted the agency to \u8220\'20\'1Cmove into the accountability phase of this process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result of these failures, what has become clear to me is we need a shift in paradigm in how we conduct our protective operations,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrA "shift in paradigm" is needed in how the \uc2 U.S. Secret Service\uc2  conducts protective operations, Acting Director Ronald L. Rowe, Jr. said, after the agency released a report on the Pennsylvania rally where an assassin took a shot at former Pres. Trump. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XZWWdAwU5i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XZWWdAwU5i}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/b15P2iOF8O"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/b15P2iOF8O}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1837180036173947318?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service report released on Friday highlights several shortcomings in the security and preparation of the 13 July rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 It states some local police officers at the rally were unaware of the existence of two communications centers on the grounds, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-secret-service-assassination-attempt-campaign-7dca5e30730287f46cceaa35437f0d47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2  reported, meaning that officers did not know that the Secret Service were not receiving their radio transmissions.\par \par \uc2 The report adds that law enforcement officers were communicating important information outside the Secret Service \u8217\'20\'19 s radio frequencies, per the AP, which resulted in details being transmitted \u8220\'20\'1Cvia mobile/cellular devices in staggered or fragmented fashion\u8221\'20\'1D instead of through the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s own network.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service details communications failures ahead of the July attempted assassination of Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 A Secret Service report looking into the events leading up to the July assassination attempt on the former president was released on Friday, and, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-secret-service-assassination-attempt-campaign-7dca5e30730287f46cceaa35437f0d47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , found fault with both local and federal law enforcement in the run-up to the Pennsylvania rally where a gunman fired at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , injuring him and others, and killing a rally attendee.\par \par \uc2 The report details a series of \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunications deficiencies\u8221\'20\'1D before the shooting occurred, and states that the Secret Service knew even before the shooting that the site of the rally posed a security challenge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important that we hold ourselves to account for the failures of July 13 and that we use the lessons learned to make sure that we do not have another mission failure like this again,\u8221\'20\'1D the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s acting director, Ronald Rowe Jr, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779#block-66ed9d0e8f08f8e7c5dec779"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has voted}}}\uc2  to require that ballots be counted by hand, a move that could complicate and slow down determining whether the swing state has voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the November election. The decision, made after Trump-aligned members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed79038f0801142f281e0c#block-66ed79038f0801142f281e0c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gained a majority}}}\uc2  on the board, comes despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed9a7f8f08f8e7c5dec75b#block-66ed9a7f8f08f8e7c5dec75b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a warning}}}\uc2  from the state attorney general that such a rule would be illegal. The meeting is ongoing, with the election board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66eda2e28f08f8e7c5dec7c4#block-66eda2e28f08f8e7c5dec7c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting down}}}\uc2  a proposal to require the hand counting of early voting ballots. We will let you know what else they decide.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Oprah, Harris, a gun owner, said: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66ed70eb8f08f8e7c5dec485#block-66ed70eb8f08f8e7c5dec485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If somebody breaks into my house they\u8217\'20\'19re getting shot}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic state lawmakers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66eda83c8f086d347dcb5efe#block-66eda83c8f086d347dcb5efe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denounced}}}\uc2  the Georgia election board\u8217\'20\'19s rule change with a press conference held in sight of Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 CNN reported that Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in North Carolina has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history}}}\uc2  of lewd and offensive statements online. Will he appear with Trump during his rally tomorrow? The former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/20/donald-trump-mark-robinson-kamala-harris-us-politics-live?page=with:block-66eda83c8f086d347dcb5efe#block-66eda83c8f086d347dcb5efe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won\u8217\'20\'19t say}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the Georg ia election board\u8217\'20\'19s rule change rallied in the state capitol in Atlanta as the body met.\par \par \uc2 But supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were not far away:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m at the Georgia state Capitol where the state election board are considering new rules, pushed by Trump loyalists, just weeks before the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 At a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/fairfightaction?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @fairfightaction}}}\uc2  press conference Trump loyalists are standing at the back and laughing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WBixtWm5N2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WBixtWm5N2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oliver Laughland (@oliverlaughland) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverlaughland/status/1837167771165069331?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia election board rejects hand-counting ballots from early voting\par \par \uc2 The Georgia state election board just voted 4-1 to table a proposal that would have required hand-counting ballots during early voting.\par \par \uc2 The decision to delay came after member Janelle King raised concerns that people hand-counting the ballots could potentially leak information about who was ahead in certain precincts. Anticipating that this election was going to be contentious, King said she did not want to get the rule wrong.\par \par \uc2 The only member to vote in favor of the rule was Janice Johnston.\par \par \uc2 The state attorney general had advised the board that this rule was likely illegal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Georgia state election board was advised by the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office that the decision to hand -count ballots was likely illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe statutes upon which these rules rely do not reflect any provision enacted by the general assembly for the hand-counting of ballots prior to tabulation,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are thus no provisions in the statutes cited in support of these proposed rules that permit counting the number of ballots by hand at the precinct level prior to delivery to the election superintendent for tabulation. Accordingly, these proposed rules are not tethered to any statute \u8211\'20\'13 and are, therefore, likely the precise type of impermissible legislation that agencies cannot do,\u8221\'20\'1D the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office wrote in a memo.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia election board approves rule change that could delay determining presidential winner\par \par \uc2 The Georgia state election board approved a rule requiring election workers to hand-count ballots on election night. The vote was three in favor, and two opposed.\par \par \uc2 The three Republicans who voted in favor of the proposal were all praised by name by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during an August rally as \u8220\'20\'1Cpit bulls fighting for honesty, transparency and victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The board\u8217\'20\'19s lone Democrat, Sara Tindall Ghazal, and John Fervier, a Republican who serves as the board\u8217\'20\'19s chair, voted against the proposal.\par \par \uc2 The concern among voting advocates and local election officials is that the rule will delay the reporting of election results and open the door for chaos after the presidential vote. It could also make it harder to determine whether \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins the state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Hand counts, long favored by those who question the results of the 2020 election, have been shown to be slower and less reliable than machine counts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia attorney general warns election board that proposed rule changes are illegal\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has obtained a memo from the \uc2 Georgia attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office\uc2  advising the state election board that several of the rules it is voting on today are illegal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA review of the proposed rules reveals several issues including that several of the proposed rules, if passed, very likely exceed the board\u8217\'20\'19s statutory authority and in some instances appear to conflict with the statutes governing the conduct of elections. Where such is the case, and as outlined below, the board risks passing rules that may easily be challenged and determined to be invalid,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25167397-20240919-memo-to-state-election-board-re-proposed-rules-920-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter says}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sara Tindall Ghazal, a Democrat on the state election board, just had a back-and-forth with Sharlene Alexander, a Republican on the Fayette county election board, over whether her proposal to count ballots by hand was feasible.\par \par \uc2 Ghazal noted that no local election officials had told her they supported the rule. Alexander and other Republicans have framed the rule as something that will be a minimal burden to implement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The board is about to vote on a proposal to require hand -counting of ballots on election night.\par \par \uc2 Janice Johnston, a Republican on the board, just went through a lengthy recitation of election rules that were adopted close to an election. She\u8217\'20\'19s trying to rebut criticism from election officials that it\u8217\'20\'19s too close to the election to adopt new rules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe hue and cry about how early or how late it is to adopt these rules, I don\u8217\'20\'19t buy. Rulemaking is good any month of the year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now beginning the part of the meeting during which the board is going to consider rules.\par \par \uc2 First up is perhaps the most controversial change it is considering today: a rule that would require election workers to hand-count ballots on election night.\par \par \uc2 Sharlene Alexander, a member of the board of elections in Fayette county, is presenting the rule and says she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t understand why it\u8217\'20\'19s so controversial \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s just checking the machine counts.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this morning, election officials and poll workers warned against this rule, saying it\u8217\'20\'19s not needed and would only delay tabulation of election results.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the speakers who really stuck out to me this morning was Milton Kidd, the election director in Douglas county, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 He was one of half a dozen local election officials to urge the state election board not to enact rules so close to the election. But Kidd also pointed out that the volunteer board \u8211\'20\'13 whose members are not election experts \u8211\'20\'13 was ignoring the advice of seasoned election experts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to listen to the individuals that are charged with conducting elections is absurd to me,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CMost of us have worked decades in these career paths, and to say that we don\u8217\'20\'19t know what we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about, you wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say that to any other professional.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve stayed at a lot of Waffle Houses in my life, but that does not qualify me to operate a Waffle House,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now wrapping up the morning public comment session of this meeting.\par \par \uc2 The overwhelming majority of speakers have urged the board not to adopt the proposed rules, including around half a dozen local election officials who have spoken.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to move on to discussion of the actual new rules shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Travis Doss, executive director of the Richmond county board of elections in Augusta and the president of the Georgia Association of Voter Registration and Election Officials, urged the board to stop its rulemaking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is simply not the time to implement sweeping changes that could create unnecessary confusion and disruption,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He noted that in previous elections \u8211\'20\'13 the 2018 gubernatorial race and the 2020 presidential race \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , respectively, said last-minute changes contributed to their loss.\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention her by name, but Doss at one point seemed to be appealing directly to Janice Johnston, a retired OB/GYN who is leading the Republican bloc on the board. He said what the board was doing was akin to making changes during the third trimester of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brook Schreiner, the election director in Butts county, Georgia, is the first election official to testify at today\u8217\'20\'19s meeting.\par \par \uc2 Local election officials throughout the state have strongly objected to the way the board has pushed through election rules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we do not oppose many of the rules being processed, the timing could certainly be improved,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She also laid out how a proposal to hand-count ballots in local precincts \u8220\'20\'1Cwould unnecessarily delay election day tabulation\u8221\'20\'1D. She noted that poll managers already have a litany of tasks on election night, including sealing ballots and transporting memory cards.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now beginning the public comment section of the meeting, which is expected last at least an hour.\par \par \uc2 John Fervier, the board\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, called it his favorite portion of the meeting, which may have been said somewhat tongue-in-cheek.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Georgia state election board meeting has only been under way for a few minutes and you can already see the two factions on the board at work.\par \par \uc2 Janice Johnston, the state GOP\u8217\'20\'19s representative on the board, went back and forth with John Fervier, the board chair, over two last-minute additions to the agenda. One was to add a petition for rulemaking to the agenda, which Fervier objected to because he said the board hadn\u8217\'20\'19t had proper time to consider it.\par \par \uc2 Johnston and two other members of the conservative bloc overruled Fervier\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to block the petition from the agenda.\par \par \uc2 Johnston has seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/janice-johnston-election-denier-georgia-elections-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a meteoric rise}}}\uc2  from being a citizen activist to essentially being in control of the three-member majority on the board.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia election board considers last-minute changes that could spark voting chaos in swing state\par \par \uc2 As the Georgia state board of elections convened, Janice Johnston asked the board to amend the agenda to allow a petition for a rule change proposed by Salleigh Grubbs, chairman of the Cobb county GOP, regarding the storage of ballots after the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are talking about debating a rule that no member of the public has seen,\u8221\'20\'1D said member Sara Tindall Ghazal. The proposed rule was submitted to the board a few weeks ago, board member Janice Johnston said\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdding the petition at the last minute is not the responsible thing to do,\u8221\'20\'1D said chairman John Fervier, noting that the board members could have asked for alterations ahead of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 Three board members overruled the chairman\u8217\'20\'19s objection. The three \u8211\'20\'13 Johnston, Janelle King and Rick Jeffares \u8211\'20\'13 were praised by name by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a rally a few months ago.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what the board is considering today, and why it could matter to the outcome of the presidential vote in the state:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/georgia-state-election-board-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears of chaos as Georgia election board considers last-minute voting changes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Members of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state election board held a short press conference ahead of their 9 am meeting this morning.\par \par \uc2 Board member Janelle King asserted that \u8220\'20\'1Ccounty board members have always had the right to certify or not to certify\u8221\'20\'1D, a statement at odds with legal holdings that the act of certification is \u8220\'20\'1Cministerial\u8221\'20\'1D and obligatory. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not ministerial. It is an option. It is an option because of the legal document each must sign,\u8221\'20\'1D King said.\par \par \uc2 The question of delayed certification is at the heart of objections raised by Democratic lawmakers, \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  and others, which are suing the state board of elections to prevent rules they believe will delay certification and potentially create a controversy that denies Georgia voters their delegates in the electoral vote after the November election.\par \par \uc2 Board member Janice Johnston encouraged Georgians to vote early and in person, instead of mailing absentee ballots this election, citing delays in mail delivery reported in the Atlanta area. She noted that \u8211\'20\'13 with the exception of military ballots \u8211\'20\'13 absentee ballots must be at the local election office by 7pm on election day.\par \par \uc2 Those who \u8220\'20\'1Cdesire to use absentee voting, please return the voting ballot directly to the election office\u8221\'20\'1D, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you must rely on the surface mail, please send your voting ballot as early as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris tells Oprah: 'If somebody breaks into my house, they're getting shot'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who recently reminded the public that she owns a gun, told Oprah during their interview yesterday that \u8220\'20\'1Cif somebody breaks into my house, they\u8217\'20\'19re getting shot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris: \u8220\'20\'1CIf somebody breaks into my house, they're getting shot. Probably should not have said that.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hlpGKUZAik"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hlpGKUZAik}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 philip lewis (@Phil_Lewis_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Lewis_/status/1836943518838739182?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris acknowledged owning a weapon as early as 2019, and mentioned it again during her debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week. Her comment to Oprah appeared to be a somewhat rare instance of the relentlessly on-message vice-president slipping: \u8220\'20\'1CProbably should not have said that,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said afterwards.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have moved to capitalize on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s story yesterday finding that Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in North Carolina, has a history of posting lewd and offensive statements online, including referring to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  bought billboards in Charlotte, Raleigh and Greensboro that show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with Robinson, and include quotes from the former president about him, including \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have to cherish Mark\u8221\'20\'1D. North Carolina is a swing state Democrats are hoping to pick up this year, and Trump will campaign in the city of Wilmington on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: Trump has embraced and tied himself to Robinson at every turn. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Mark Robinson are too extreme for North Carolina,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic national committee chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in the final months of his term, will meet with his cabinet to \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss a range of administration priorities\u8221\'20\'1D today, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats controlled Congress for the first two years of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, working with him to pass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/01/democrats-congress-control-achievements-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several significant pieces of legislation}}}\uc2  addressing climate change, prescription drug prices and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure needs, although he did not get everything he wanted passed.\par \par \uc2 That all ended when the GOP took control of the House of Representatives in 2023, and it remains to be seen what more Biden can accomplish before he departs the White House in January of 2025. Perhaps we\u8217\'20\'19ll find out after the meeting at 11.30am ET, where first lady Jill Biden will also provide an update on her initiative to improve women\u8217\'20\'19s health research.\par \par \uc2 Biden will then fly to Wilmington, Delaware, where he will meet with Australian prime minister Anthony Albanese in what the White House says is a \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal meeting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Labelling tweets featuring false claims about election fraud as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisputed\u8221\'20\'1D does little to nothing to change Trump voters\u8217\'20\'19 pre-existing beliefs, and it may make them more likely to believe the lies, according to a new study.\par \par \uc2 The study, authored by John Blanchard, an assistant professor from the \uc2 University of Minnesota, Duluth\uc2 , and Catherine Norris, an associate professor from Swarthmore College, looked at data from a sampling of 1,072 Americans surveyed in December of 2020. The researchers published a peer-reviewed paper on their findings this month in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/trump-twitter-and-truth-judgments-the-effects-of-disputed-tags-and-political-knowledge-on-the-judged-truthfulness-of-election-misinformation/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard Kennedy School\u8217\'20\'19s Misinformation Review}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese \u8216\'20\'18disputed\u8217\'20\'19 tags are meant to alert a reader to false/misinformation, so it\u8217\'20\'19s shocking to find that they may have the opposite effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Norris said.\par \par \uc2 Participants were shown four tweets from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  that made false claims about election fraud and told to rank them from one to seven based on their truthfulness. A control group saw the tweets without \u8220\'20\'1Cdisputed\u8221\'20\'1D tags; the experimental group viewed them with the label. Before and after seeing the tweets, the subjects were also asked to rank their views on election fraud overall.\par \par \uc2 The study found that Trump voters who were initially skeptical about claims of widespread fraud were more likely to rate lies as true when a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisputed\u8221\'20\'1D label appeared next to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tweets. The findings meanwhile showed Biden voters\u8217\'20\'19 beliefs were largely unaffected by the \u8220\'20\'1Cdisputed\u8221\'20\'1D tags.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/sep/20/trump-tweets-false-label-credibility-supporters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labelling Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies as \u8216\'20\'18disputed\u8217\'20\'19 on X makes supporters believe them more, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy: 'I hope Biden supports Ukraine peace plan'\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian leader \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  has said he hopes \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will support his plan to end the war with Russia, ahead of a trip to Washington.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy has promised to present his so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory plan\u8221\'20\'1D to end the fighting, which has killed thousands, to Biden in the coming days, Agence France-Presse reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI really hope that he will support this plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskyy said during a press conference with EU chief \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe plan is designed for decisions that will have to happen from October to December \u8230\'20\'26 We would like that very much. Then we believe that the plan will work,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy will present the plan to the US after a summer of intense fighting, with Moscow advancing in eastern Ukraine and Kyiv holding on to parts of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Kursk region.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian leader is due to meet Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 while Kyiv also says he plans to meet \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has not confirmed their meeting but says it will \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably\u8221\'20\'1D take place. Reuters reports that while Trump and Zelenskyy talked over the phone in July, they have not talked in person since Trump was president.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee has consistently described US aid to its eastern European ally as a waste of money and has declined to say he wants Ukraine to win.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats to \u8216\'20\'18go after\u8217\'20\'19 opponents will subvert rule of law, experts warn\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping threats if he wins the presidency again to name a special prosecutor to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo after\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and take legal action against other foes would subvert the rule of law in America and take the country towards authoritarianism, former justice department officials and scholars have warned.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s escalating legal threats have targeted \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt election officials\u8221\'20\'1D, lawyers, donors and others he falsely deems out to steal November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, and have popped up variously on his Truth Social platform, at campaign events and at an elite police group he addressed this month in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s menacing pledges to essentially weaponize the justice department against opponents would mark a sharp break with the Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s mission statement, which cites as core values \u8220\'20\'1Cindependence and impartiality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ex-justice officials warn that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s barrage of intimidating verbal assaults are unprecedented, and suggest he would undermine longstanding traditions of justice department independence if he wins the presidency, thus badly undermining the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/trump-election-opponents-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats to \u8216\'20\'18go after\u8217\'20\'19 opponents will subvert rule of law, experts warn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the event with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  last night, the family of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Georgia woman who died as a result of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, blamed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his supreme court picks for her death.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey just let her die because of some stupid \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. They treated her like she was just another number,\u8221\'20\'1D Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s older sister said of the medical professionals she had turned to for help.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Associated Press have more on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue ahead of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 speech in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 About half of voters say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the most important issues as they consider their vote \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s more important to women who are registered voters than to male voters, according to a new AP-NORC poll. About six in 10 women voters say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is one of the most important issues to their vote in the upcoming election, compared to about four in 10 male voters.\par \par \uc2 The gender gap doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stop there.\par \par \uc2 About six in 10 women voters trust Harris more than Trump to handle \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while about two in 10 women have more trust in Trump. Half of male voters, by contrast, trust Harris more than Trump on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while about one-third trust Trump more than Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Losing daughter due to Georgia \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban 'worst pain ever', mother tells Harris\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be in Georgia today and is expected to speak about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that now blanket much of the United States, days after news broke that two Georgia mothers died after being unable to access legal abortions and adequate medical care.\par \par \uc2 The deaths of the Georgia mothers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/candi-miller-abortion-ban-death-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candi Miller}}}\uc2 , were first reported earlier this week by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  and occurred as a result of Georgia enacting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/georgia-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 . Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s maternal mortality review committee looked at both women\u8217\'20\'19s cases and deemed their deaths \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  permits abortions in medical emergencies, doctors across the country have said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions are worded so vaguely as to be unworkable. Instead, doctors have said, they are forced to watch until patients get sick enough to legally intervene.\par \par \uc2 Last night, Shanette Williams, Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother, joined a virtual event hosted by \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  where she interviewed Harris.\par \par \uc2 Williams told the audience:\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re looking at a mother that is broken, the worst pain ever that a mother, that a parent can ever feel.\par \par \uc2 Harris responded: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just so sad. And the courage that you all have shown is extraordinary.\u8221\'20\'1D Many in the studio audience of about 400 were in tears.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Republican campaign refuses to say if Robinson will appear with Trump in North Carolina tomorrow\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is due to visit North Carolina tomorrow. It comes as his presidential campaign is rocked by the allegations against the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican gubernatorial nominee, Mark Robinson, that he attacked \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 , backed the reinstatement of slavery and referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D in comments on a pornographic website.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the CNN report by Associated Press, Trump campaign spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt did not mention Robinson by name or answer questions as to whether he would appear with Trump at tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Wilmington, or had been invited to do so.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  state election board is set to meet later today to consider another round of last-minute election changes that could cause delays and confusion after election day in the critical battleground state.\par \par \uc2 The Republican majority on the board is expected to approve a rule that would require three people in every precinct to check machine-vote tallies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ga.gov/sites/default/files/2024-08/seb-notice_of_proposed_rulemaking_183_1_12_.12a5_hand_count.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by hand-counting the election results}}}\uc2 . Voting experts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/10/07/1126796538/voting-explainer-hand-counting-ballots-accuracy-cost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long warned}}}\uc2  that hand-counts are time consuming, costly, and less reliable than machines. It\u8217\'20\'19s a process that nonetheless has been favored by conservative activists who doubt the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The board will also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/georgia-election-board-to-consider-more-last-minute-changes-for-november-vote/5PJWVRI4Q5CXHIS7NYH6F6JFYQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consider proposed rules}}}\uc2  that would mandate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ga.gov/sites/default/files/2024-08/Notice_of_Proposed_Rulemaking_183_1_14_.02_8_13_AB_hand_counting.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 daily hand-counts}}}\uc2  of early votes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ga.gov/sites/default/files/2024-08/seb-notice_of_proposed_rulemaking_183_1_12_.21_daily_reporting.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 require}}}\uc2  public reports of voters who have cast a ballot during early voting, allow for greater poll-watcher access during tabulation, distinguish emergency and mail-in ballots, and require that ballots be tracked through the mail.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/georgia-state-election-board-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears of chaos as Georgia election board considers last-minute voting changes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Also appearing tonight with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Monica Crowley in Arizona will be \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2 , former acting secretary of homeland security when Trump was president.\par \par \uc2 A report by the office of the Department for Homeland Security inspector general released in 2022 found that Wolf interfered with a report on Russian interference in the 2020 election by demanding changes, delaying its dissemination and creating a risk the report might be seen as politicised.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/russian-2020-election-interference-trump-chad-wolf-dhs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump official interfered in report on Russian election meddling \u8211\'20\'13 watchdog}}}\par \par \uc2 Following the release of the report, Wolf {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/trump-appointee-twice-delayed-report-russian-election-interference-fed-rcna27198"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  the watchdog \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not find any credible evidence that I directed anyone to change the substance of the report because it \u8216\'20\'18made President Trump look bad\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Turning away from the Robinson allegations momentarily we can look ahead to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s town hall event in the swing state of Arizona this evening.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee will appear alongside Monica Crowley, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2017/jan/11/monica-crowley-accused-of-plagiarism-as-she-joins-trump-team"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who was accused of plagiarism over her book, What the (Bleep) Just Happened?}}}\par \par \uc2 Crowley has denied the claims and the then Trump administration at the time referred to them as a politically motivated attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53am BST\par \par \uc2 As we have said, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did not comment on the Mark Robinson allegations during last night\u8217\'20\'19s speech to a group of Jewish donors and to the Israeli-American Council in Washington.\par \par \uc2 His campaign issued a statement about the CNN story that did not even mention Robinson, saying instead that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cis focused on winning the White House and saving this country\u8221\'20\'1D and that North Carolina was a \u8220\'20\'1Cvital part of that plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40am BST\par \par \uc2 'Could Robinson cost Trump the White House?' pollster asks\par \par \uc2 The story also could threaten \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning North Carolina, a key battleground state, Associated Press reports. It says that Mark Robinson was already already running well behind his Democratic opponent in public polls before CNN claimed he referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornographic website.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis story is not about the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in North Carolina. It\u8217\'20\'19s about the presidential race,\u8221\'20\'1D said Paul Shumaker, a Republican pollster. He warned that Trump could risk losing a state he won in 2016 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 The question is going to be, does Mark Robinson cost \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the White House?\u8221\'20\'1D Shumaker added.\par \par \uc2 Recent polls of North Carolina voters show Trump and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  locked in a close race. The same polls show Democrat \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2  with a roughly 10-point lead over Robinson in the race to be governor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN report 'very concerning,' says North Carolina Republican\par \par \uc2 At least one North Carolina Republican, US Representative Richard Hudson, called CNN\u8217\'20\'19s reporting \u8220\'20\'1Cvery concerning\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reports. He said he thought Robinson needed to do more to reassure voters the allegations were untrue.\par \par \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , his opponent, has featured some of Robinson\u8216\'20\'18s previous controversial comments in television attack ads and his campaign issued a statement condemning him yesterday. Stein\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said:\par \par \uc2 North Carolinians already know Mark Robinson is completely unfit to be governor. Josh remains focused on winning this campaign so that together we can build a safer, stronger North Carolina for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16am BST\par \par \uc2 As our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 story on the CNN claims states}}}\uc2 , Mark Robinson, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s first Black lieutenant governor, is facing the Democrat \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , the state attorney general, in November.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have reportedly been pressuring Robinson to withdraw from the race as rumors swirled about CNN\u8217\'20\'19s story. North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s deadline for a candidate to drop out was yesterday and the deadline to remove his name from the ballot has passed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump bemoans lack of support from Jewish voters amid claims of ally\u8217\'20\'19s antisemitism\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our blog covering US politics in the run-up to the presidential election following another tumultuous evening where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bemoaned a lack of support from Jewish voters just hours after allegations emerged that a Republican ally had referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornography website.\par \par \uc2 Trump failed to mention the claims in a CNN report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against Mark Robinson, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican gubernatorial nominee}}}\uc2 , during a speech on Thursday at the Israeli-American Council national summit in Washington.\par \par \uc2 In his speech, the former president lamented that he was trailing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  among American Jews. Israel would likely cease to exist within two years should Harris win the election, and Jews would be partly to blame for that outcome because they tend to vote for Democrats, Trump argued.\par \par \uc2 If I don\u8217\'20\'19t win this election - and the Jewish people would really have a lot to do with that if that happens because if 40%, I mean, 60% of the people are voting for the enemy - Israel, in my opinion, will cease to exist within two years.\par \par \uc2 Trump was citing a poll that he said showed Harris polling at 60% among American Jews. You can read our report on his speech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/trump-jewish-voters-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, according to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s reporting, Robinson referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cperv\u8221\'20\'1D in archived messages because he \u8220\'20\'1Cenjoyed watching transgender pornography\u8221\'20\'1D. The messages were made between 2008 and 2012 on \u8220\'20\'1CNude Africa\u8221\'20\'1D, a pornographic website that includes a message board.\par \par \uc2 He also allegedly expressed support for reinstating slavery. \u8220\'20\'1CSlavery is not bad. Some people need to be slaves. I wish they would bring it [slavery] back. I would certainly buy a few,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in October 2010. In March 2012, during the Obama administration, it was claimed he wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d take Hitler over any of the shit that\u8217\'20\'19s in Washington right now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CNN reported that Robinson, who would be North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s first Black governor, also attacked civil rights leader \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  in searing terms and once referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Robinson has denied the report: \u8220\'20\'1CLet me reassure you the things that you will see in that story \u8211\'20\'13 those are not the words of Mark Robinson\u8221\'20\'1D he said on a video posted to X. And said he is staying in the race.\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina Republican party is standing by him. \u8220\'20\'1CMark Robinson has categorically denied the allegations made by CNN but that won\u8217\'20\'19t stop the Left from trying to demonize him via personal attacks,\u8221\'20\'1D the party said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 After allegations against Robinson became public, the Harris campaign posted video clips of Trump praising the candidate.\par \par \uc2 enltrBest friends ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/baS5sRfzIo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/baS5sRfzIo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1836869949505130820?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More on this story later. In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris sat down with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  on Thursday for a \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtual rally\u8221\'20\'1D that included a wide-ranging sit-down interview, during which Harris attacked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on reproductive rights and pledged to sign a border security bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/senate-democrats-immigration-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thwarted by}}}\uc2  Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the vice-president will be attending campaign events in the swing states of Georgia and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the evening, Trump will be in another swing state \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona \u8211\'20\'13at a town hall event. He will appear alongside Monica Crowley, a commentator and former assistant secretary for public affairs, and \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2 , who was an acting secretary for public affairs in his administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240920ek9k0010c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
