\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris condemns Trump in Georgia after news of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -related deaths\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 746 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2024\par 21:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president speaks after news breaks that two women died after being unable to access procedure legally\par \par \uc2 In her first speech dedicated exclusively to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since becoming the presidential nominee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  spoke on Friday afternoon in Atlanta, Georgia, blaming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that now blanket much of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke days after news broke that two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  mothers died after being unable to access legal abortions and adequate medical care in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo women \u8211\'20\'13 and those are only the stories we know \u8211\'20\'13 here in the state of Georgia, died, died, because of a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. She repeatedly referred to \u8220\'20\'1CTrump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\u8221\'20\'1D in the speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSuffering is happening every day in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris continued. \u8220\'20\'1CTo those women, to those families \u8211\'20\'13 I say on behalf on what I believe we all say, we see you and you are not alone and we are all here standing with you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the weeks since becoming the Democratic nominee for president, Harris has made reproductive rights a central {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/kamala-harris-abortion-rights-healthcare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part of her campaign}}}\uc2 . She has toured the country to highlight the healthcare consequences of the 2022 overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which paved the way for more than a dozen states to ban almost all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Harris blamed the former president for Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise because Trump appointed three of the supreme court justices who overturned the landmark decision. She also also condemned Republicans for repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/senate-vote-ivf-bill-democrats-republicans-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocking Senate bills}}}\uc2  that would have guaranteed a federal right to in vitro fertilization, a popular fertility treatment that had its future cast into doubt after Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the one hand, these extremists want to tell women they don\u8217\'20\'19t have the freedom to end an unwanted pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1COn the other hand, these extremists are telling women and their parents they don\u8217\'20\'19t have the freedom to start a family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The raucous crowd grumbled loudly at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s words. \u8220\'20\'1CMake it make sense!\u8221\'20\'1D someone shouted.\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won Georgia in the 2020 presidential election, becoming the first Democrat in decades to take the state, Democrats seemed unlikely to recapture it until Harris replaced Biden as nominee. Now, Georgia is once again a swing state. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the Republican senator from South Carolina and a major Trump surrogate, has said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/25/trump-harris-swing-states-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump must win Georgia}}}\uc2  if he wants to win the White House. Meanwhile, Harris in August embarked on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/28/nx-s1-5090862/harris-walz-georgia-bus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-day bus tour}}}\uc2  of the state and giving her first major network interview there.\par \par \uc2 The deaths of the Georgia mothers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/candi-miller-abortion-ban-death-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candi Miller}}}\uc2 , were first reported earlier this week by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  and occurred after Georgia enacted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/georgia-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 . Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s maternal mortality review committee looked at both women\u8217\'20\'19s cases and deemed their deaths \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although Georgia permits abortions in medical emergencies, doctors across the country have said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions are worded so vaguely as to be unworkable. Instead, doctors have said, they are forced to watch until patients get sick enough to legally intervene.\par \par \uc2 After Thurman took \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to end a pregnancy in 2022, her body failed to expel all of the fetal tissue \u8211\'20\'13 a rare but potentially devastating complication. Doctors delayed giving the 28-year-old a routine procedure for 20 hours, and she developed sepsis. Her heart stopped during an emergency surgery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, her doctors could have faced up to a decade in prison for providing Amber the care she needed,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstand what a law like this means. Doctors have to wait until the patient is at death\u8217\'20\'19s door before they take action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris met with Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother and sisters on Thursday night. \u8220\'20\'1CTheir pain is heartbreaking,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 While on the campaign trail, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/30/trump-ivf-anti-abortion-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has alternated}}}\uc2  between bragging about helping to demolish Roe, complaining about how Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 hardline anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances have cost the Republican elections, and flip-flopping on his own position on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become one of voters\u8217\'20\'19 top issues over the last two years, and Democrats are hoping that outrage over Roe will propel them to victory at the ballot box this November. Ten states, including the key battleground states of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/20/nevada-signatures-abortion-vote-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/13/arizona-abortion-november-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , are set to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures, which could boost turnout among Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 base.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240920ek9k0015t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
