\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  holds star-studded event with Oprah in battleground state of Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh ,Chris Stein, Anna Betts and Lili Bayer (earlier) \par \uc2 11,248 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2024\par 01:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed now, thanks for following along. See all our coverage of the 2024 US elections\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 See all our coverage of the 2024 US elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Oprah concluded by quoting Maya Angelou, saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cif you know better you have to do better\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 That event has now ended.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is asked by Meryl Streep what preparations are being made for the possibility that she wins, but Trump does not accept the result.\par \par \uc2 Harris says many Americans who voted for Trump have decided 6 January was a bridge too far.\par \par \uc2 She says \u8220\'20\'1Cthe lawyers are working\u8221\'20\'1D and that is important to speak to friends and neighbours about misinformation, and to respect poll workers, and to not be afraid to vote.\par \par \uc2 She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really answer the question.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 People who have experienced gun violence are speaking now, again speaking through tears. A woman whose daughter was involved in a school shooting recounts the feeling of not knowing if her daughter, who survived, was alright.\par \par \uc2 Harris says what is needed is common sense, and assault weapons bans, and notes that she owns a gun.\par \par \uc2 If somebody breaks into her house, she says, they\u8217\'20\'19re getting shot. She probably should not have said that, she adds, saying her staff will deal with it later.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Tracee Ellis-Ross points out that women who don\u8217\'20\'19t have children still contribute a lot to society. She is saying this because of JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s childless cat lady comments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Julia Roberts is speaking now via video link.\par \par \uc2 She says she wants to be able to travel and have people think it is a good thing she is American, not a bad one.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris responds to comments from Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother and sister, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CFirst of all, I\u8217\'20\'19m so sorry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s family only recently learned how she died, Harris says.\par \par \uc2 Amber\u8217\'20\'19s mom shared with me over and over that the word preventable keeps coming to her, says Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris points out that Trump chose three members of the supreme court, which then overturned Roe v Wade. She says he did it intentionally.\par \par \uc2 In 2016 Trump said he wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legality to be decided by individual states, while Clinton vowed to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 He has boasted that he \u8220\'20\'1Cwas able to kill Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 More from Donegan on that story:\par \par \uc2 Thurman could have been cured with a D&C, or dilation and curettage, a procedure in which the cervix is dilated to create an opening through which instruments can be inserted to empty out the contents of a uterus. The procedure is a popular form of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is also a routine part of miscarriage and other gynecological care. If the tissue was promptly removed, she probably would have been fine: a D&C requires no special equipment and takes only about 15 minutes.\par \par \uc2 But Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban outlawed the D&C procedure, making it a felony to perform except in cases of managing a \u8220\'20\'1Cspontaneous\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cnaturally occurring\u8221\'20\'1D miscarriage. Because Thurman had taken \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, her miscarriage was illegal to treat. She suffered in a hospital bed for 20 hours, developing sepsis and beginning to experience organ failure. By the time the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  doctors were finally willing to treat her, it was too late.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 A woman named Shanette is speaking now through tears about her daughter, Amber Thurman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are looking at a mother who is broken,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Thurman, a Black 28-year-old mother to a young son died in Georgia after doctors at a hospital there refused to perform a simple procedure that could have saved her life \u8211\'20\'13 because the law did not allow them.\par \par \uc2 Here is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Moira Donegan on the subject:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/19/georgia-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Thurman was killed by Georgia's \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban. There will be others | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Hadley Duvall, 22, is speaking now. She has told the story of being raped and impregnated, at 12, by her stepfather, as she helps Harris campaign for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 When Roe v Wade was overturned, she says, she found that while her abuse was over, her story was not.\par \par \uc2 She thanks Harris for \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding up\u8221\'20\'1D for women, and \u8220\'20\'1Creally showing us that life is not about the hard things you go through\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t bow down,\u8217\'20\'19 she says.\par \par \uc2 Here is Duvall speaking in August:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is asked by a young person about the economy, and the difficulty of going from being a student to an independent adult.\par \par \uc2 She compares her and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans.\par \par \uc2 She has been stronger than at other times on the economy here, waffling less and talking about her policies more.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris references Trump\u8217\'20\'19s response at the debate between the candidates, where he said he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cconcept of a plan\u8221\'20\'1D for healthcare. She will give small businesses a $50,000 grant, she says. She says the current small business grant of $5,000 is for a \u8220\'20\'1Cconcept of a business\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is asked about her plan to tackle the cost of living. The economy is one of the areas where Harris has often been weak in her responses.\par \par \uc2 She talks about policies she has announced. She says she will take on price-gouging to bring down the price of groceries.\par \par \uc2 She says she will bring down the cost of buying a home with a tax credit. She will support small business owners.\par \par \uc2 She takes a swipe at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s family wealth and bankruptcy plans. She says she will extend the child tax credit.\par \par \uc2 She repeats her idea of an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 She says she will sign the bill into law if elected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is asked by a voter what her specific steps would be on strengthening the border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a theoretical issue for me, this is something I have actually worked on,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CI take very seriously the importance of having a secure border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She says she has prosecuted cross-border criminal gangs.\par \par \uc2 She talks about the border security bill that Trump blocked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would have allowed us to stem the flow of fentanyl,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. It would have allowed more agents.\par \par \uc2 Trump prefers to run on a problem instead of fixing a problem, Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Oprah brings up Springfield, and the repeated false claims made by Trump and his running mate JD Vance, about immigrants in the town.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems to us that something happened to you the moment President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stepped aside and withdrew his candidacy, that a veil or something dropped, and you just stepped into your power,\u8221\'20\'1D Oprah says to Harris.\par \par \uc2 Oprah stands up and does an impression of Harris walking confidently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe each have those moments in our lives where it\u8217\'20\'19s time to step up,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 She felt a sense of responsibility, and with that comes a sense of purpose, she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere really is so much at stake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris arrives at star-studded Oprah event\par \par \uc2 Harris walks into the event, hugging Whitmer and Oprah, and taking a seat in an armchair opposite Oprah.\par \par \uc2 She says when we\u8217\'20\'19ve dealt with so much that is exhausting with this movement trying to divide Americans, it is important to remember what unites Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  came onto the stage to encourage people to vote for Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign manager \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley-Dillon\uc2  is speaking now, and warns voters that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are still in a margin of error race\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning that even where Harris is polling ahead of Trump, it is not by more than the margin of error. The race is tied, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 A voter from Win with Black Men says that if he wants to choose someone who will be the best for his family, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want someone with 34 convictions.\par \par \uc2 A voter from White Women Answer the Call says, \u8220\'20\'1Ceven if you are a white woman who is voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s not enough, you have to get off the sidelines and do the work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She calls on white women to persuade other white women to vote for Harris, \u8220\'20\'1Cin women\u8217\'20\'19s best interests\u8221\'20\'1D, and to phone bank.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Stream the event here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Ben Stiller says he supports Harris because his daughter\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights are incredibly important.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Oprah says Rock said there will be \u8220\'20\'1Cweeping in the streets\u8221\'20\'1D when Harris becomes president.\par \par \uc2 Rock says he has been \u8220\'20\'1Cwriting [Harris] checks for a long time\u8221\'20\'1D and that he wants to bring his daughters to the White House to \u8220\'20\'1Cmeet this black woman president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Lopez, Julia Roberts, Meryl Streep and others remotely at Oprah-Harris event\par \par \uc2 Among those at the event are Cat ladies for Kamala, train lovers for Harris-Walz, Republicans for Harris, Swifties for Kamala.\par \par \uc2 Actors Julia Roberts and Meryl Streep are joining via video chat, as are Chris Rock, Ben Stiller, Jennifer Lopez, Tracee Ellis-Ross and Brian Cranston.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Oprah says that there are 400 people in the audience, and thousands more joining via video call.\par \par \uc2 The event is happening in Oakland county, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Michigan is a key swing state, with 15 electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 That event is starting now. You can watch it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iPB0dmWyqZI&ab_channel=Oprah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oprah, an Independent, endorsed Harris at the Democratic National Convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the press pool report from the Harris and Oprah event in Michigan:\par \par \uc2 The pool was let in to the space at 7:40pm. It is a very large sound stage and it\u8217\'20\'19s a big brick facade around the stage. This is being conducted \u8220\'20\'1Cin the round,\u8221\'20\'1D meaning the stage is in the center, with two wood chairs with cream upholstery. The screen on the far wall says \u8220\'20\'1CUnite for America. There is a live studio audience here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  will be speaking at an event in Michigan in ten minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time. We will stream \u8211\'20\'13 and blog \u8211\'20\'13 that live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeated a statement he has made before, that any Jewish person who votes for Harris or the Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cshould have their head examined\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims that the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chasn\u8217\'20\'19t lifted a finger\u8221\'20\'1D to protect Jewish people.\par \par \uc2 In August, the Biden-Harris administration approved a $20bn arms package for Israel. Harris has said she is working \u8220\'20\'1Caround the clock\u8221\'20\'1D to secure a ceasefire deal. Harris has said repeatedly she supports Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself and has condemned anti-sematism.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite presiding over this explosion of antisemitism, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has done nothing. She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t lifted a finger to protect you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1836910246138102233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump meanwhile has said, falsely, that polls that show him ahead of Harris don\u8217\'20\'19t get released.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , met with the families of people held hostage by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walz \u8220\'20\'1Ccondemned the brutality against both Americans and Israelis and reaffirmed his and Vice President Harris\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security,\u8221\'20\'1D and, \u8220\'20\'1CThe group discussed the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to end the war and ensure Israel is secure, all hostages are released, and the suffering in Gaza ends,\u8221\'20\'1D the campaign said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday I met with the loved ones of Americans held hostage by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to hear their heartbreaking stories \u8211\'20\'13 something no family should have to endure.\par \par \uc2 President Biden and Vice President Harris will continue doing everything possible to bring them home. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OxDxsvkeBx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OxDxsvkeBx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@Tim_Walz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz/status/1836909531927924991?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks so far have consisted of him making comments between thanking person after person in the audience for being there. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 David Smith\uc2  is in the room:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to take our country back and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to make America great again and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to make Israel great again.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pC4snoED8r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pC4snoED8r}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1836909627486720324?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Springfield, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , has issued an emergency proclamation following the continued rise in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-nabj-panel-ohio-bomb-threats-gaza-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public safety threats}}}\uc2  over false rightwing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rumors}}}\uc2  about the city\u8217\'20\'19s migrant communities.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Rob Rue released a statement, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CEnsuring the safety of Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s residents is our top priority.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are addressing these threats with the seriousness they warrant and are taking immediate steps to ensure the security of both our community and our employees. Our commitment to preventing harm is unwavering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to a city statement, the proclamation allows Rue and other city officials to \u8220\'20\'1Cswiftly acquire resources needed to address potential threats\u8221\'20\'1D and will \u8220\'20\'1Cenable departments to respond more efficiently to emerging risks, including civil unrest, cyber threats and potential acts of violence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/springfield-ohio-emergency-proclamation-migrant-rumors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor issues emergency order over false migrant rumors}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is stepping up her efforts to win over voters who belong to the \uc2 Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints\uc2 , enlisting prominent members of the faith to make the case in pivotal Arizona that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not align with the church\u8217\'20\'19s values, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Her state campaign announced on Thursday an advisory committee to formalise the outreach to current and former members of the church, widely known as the Mormon church.\par \par \uc2 With nearly 450,000 church members in Arizona, about 6% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s population, Latter-day Saints and former church members could prove critical in what will likely be an extremely close race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s event has started but he is not yet speaking. We will bring you any important news from his comments when they happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 US officials now believe that a Gaza ceasefire deal between Israel and Palestinian Islamist group \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/israel-hamas-deal-unlikely-before-end-of-bidens-term-u-s-officials-say-efc21510?mod=hp_lead_pos1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not expected before the end of President Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s term}}}\uc2  in January, the Wall Street Journal reports.\par \par \uc2 The newspaper cites top-level officials in the White House, State Department and Pentagon without naming them. Those bodies did not immediately respond to a request for comment from Reuters.\par \par \uc2 US Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said two weeks ago that 90% of a ceasefire deal had been agreed upon, while Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has repeatedly said Washington has been working \u8220\'20\'1Caround the clock\u8221\'20\'1D to get to an agreement.\par \par \uc2 The United States and mediators Qatar and Egypt have for months made attempts to reach a ceasefire deal between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  but have failed to arrive at a final agreement.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations have been ongoing to clear two obstacles: Israel\u8217\'20\'19s demand to keep its forces in the Philadelphi corridor to maintain a buffer between Gaza and Egypt, and the specifics of an exchange of Israeli hostages for Palestinian prisoners held by Israel.\par \par \uc2 Biden laid out a three-phase ceasefire proposal on May 31 that he said at the time Israel had agreed to. The deal has run into obstacles and officials have for weeks said a new proposal would soon be presented.\par \par \uc2 Critics and human rights groups have also urged Washington to use its leverage by conditioning military support to Israel but the US has maintained its support for its ally.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18fighting anti-semitism\u8217\'20\'19 event in Washington is now running almost an hour late.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  endorsements, via the Harris campaign:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=e766ce3739&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamster Retirees}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=0b23a8b346&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters National Black Caucus}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=81f1bc5814&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Joint Council 43}}}\uc2  (Michigan)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=b84d4cf896&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Joint Council 39}}}\uc2  (Wisconsin)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=4fb49b4493&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Joint Council 42}}}\uc2  (Southern Nevada)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "htt