sters Local 186}}}\uc2  (Ventura, CA)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=e2bce8318b&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 572}}}\uc2  (Carson, CA)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=3dee7fa7ee&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 769}}}\uc2  (Miami, FL)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=4c42abcfe8&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 848}}}\uc2  (Long Beach, CA)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=49ee5fb26b&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 238}}}\uc2  (Cedar Rapids, IA)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=7766c64e9e&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 237}}}\uc2  (NYC)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=8f117cb193&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 396}}}\uc2  (Southern California)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=50af2490eb&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 89}}}\uc2  (Kentucky and Indiana)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=96ba5616e2&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters Local 202}}}\uc2  (New York)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  expressed frustration Thursday with ongoing criticism by election officials of how it handles mail ballots while also seeking to reassure voters that it\u8217\'20\'19s ready to handle an expected crush of those ballots this fall, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 US Postmaster General \uc2 Louis DeJoy\uc2  told reporters that it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult for the Postal Service to address \u8220\'20\'1Cgeneralities\u8221\'20\'1D about perceived problems and said some election officials don\u8217\'20\'19t fully understand its efforts to deliver ballots in time to be counted.\par \par \uc2 He said the service will collect and deliver mail ballots more frequently in the days before the 5 November presidential election and would keep processing centres open the Sunday before Election Day. The Postal Service, he said, would take extraordinary measures to \u8220\'20\'1Crescue\u8221\'20\'1D ballots that are mailed late and at risk of missing state deadlines to be received by election offices.\par \par \uc2 Elections officials have said for weeks that they are concerned about the Postal Service\u8217\'20\'19s readiness. They\u8217\'20\'19ve cited ballots arriving late or without the postmarks required by some state laws during the primary season.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe engage in heroic efforts intended to beat the clock,\u8221\'20\'1D DeJoy told reporters during a virtual news conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese efforts are designed to be used only when the risk of deviating from our standard processes is necessary to compensate for the ballot being mailed so close to a state\u8217\'20\'19s deadline,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is commonly misunderstood in the media and even by election officials.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is due to speak shortly at an event called \u8220\'20\'1CFighting Anti-Semitism in America\u8221\'20\'1D in Washington. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you anything important from that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Number of \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  members who have endorsed Harris reaches one million\par \par \uc2 A million of the 1.3 million members of the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  have now endorsed Harris, according to Harris spokesperson Lauren Hitt, despite the union\u8217\'20\'19s executive board\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to endorse a candidate for the first time in decades yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The union had endorsed every Democratic candidate since 2000.\par \par \uc2 frltrOne million \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dPrQ94MFgO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dPrQ94MFgO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Hitt (@LaurenHitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaurenHitt/status/1836876231247106146?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 When Harris touched down in Michigan a short while ago, Michigan Teamsters President Kevin Moore was among the people waiting to greet her on the tarmac, according to the press pool report.\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Joint Council 43 endorsed the Harris-Walz ticket yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Oprah to speak at campaign event in Michigan\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will speak at a campaign event in Michigan with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  at 8pm ET: in an hour and forty-five minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring that to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to cut interest rates was \u8220\'20\'1Cpolicital\u8221\'20\'1D, White House economic adviser Jared Bernstein said US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has never spoken to Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  about interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Biden had said earlier on Thursday that he had not spoken to Powell since becoming president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, I\u8217\'20\'19ve never once spoken to the chairman of the Fed since I became president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden had said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 New polling shows that voters are almost evenly split between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the three Great Lakes battlegrounds that could determine the outcome of the election. The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec14e28f089e4a13dfa5ec#block-66ec14e28f089e4a13dfa5ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that the vice-president is tied with Trump in Pennsylvania, though another poll released today by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec1dd48f089e4a13dfa649#block-66ec1dd48f089e4a13dfa649"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Harris had the advantage in that state, but was deadlocked with the former president nationwide.\par \par \uc2 There are signs that Republicans are leaving nothing in this election to chance, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec2d0d8f089e4a13dfa73a#block-66ec2d0d8f089e4a13dfa73a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec357a8f08098f3f16274e#block-66ec357a8f08098f3f16274e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham}}}\uc2  , the South Carolina senator and Trump ally, pushing for the red state\u8217\'20\'19s governor to put in motion a plan to switch its system for allocating electoral votes to a winner-take-all set-up that will surely benefit Trump. Such calls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec31ab8f081d8429b1bdad#block-66ec31ab8f081d8429b1bdad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been made before}}}\uc2 , and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if this latest push makes a difference.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/19/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-black-nazi-pro-slavery-porn-forum/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN has published}}}\uc2  reporting on Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in North Carolina, and found that he called himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack NAZI!\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornography website\u8217\'20\'19s message board. Robinson has denied the lewd commends made in the report, which could tank his already diminishing chances and drag down Trump in the key swing state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former advisers to Trump have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/intelligencer-pro-russia-website-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collaborated to build a website }}}\uc2  that spreads conspiracy theories, including about Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s enemies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said that the US economy has a ways to go before the toll of inflation is eased, but acknowledged yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cut by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  was a milestone in the fight against the price increases that bedeviled his presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is the Secret Service investigating \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for his post on assassinating Harris and Biden? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec43898f08098f3f16284c#block-66ec43898f08098f3f16284c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Perhaps}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White dudes are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec3dde8f08098f3f1627de#block-66ec3dde8f08098f3f1627de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly putting down}}}\uc2  big money to promote Harris in Wisconsin, Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris will next week welcome Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  to the White House. Trump has said he will \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-meet-volodymyr-zelenskiy-un-security-council-russia-ukraine-war-latest-updates?page=with:block-66ebd08f8f08893ca2b3a487#block-66ebd08f8f08893ca2b3a487"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 probably}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D meet with Zelenskyy, who is traveling to the United States to address a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council meeting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The federal government has sent bomb-sniffing dogs to the town of Springfield, Ohio, where residents have been facing ongoing threats after Trump, JD Vance and others on the right spread false rumors that immigrants were killing and eating pets.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the US's nail-biting 2024 presidential election, North Carolina is now in play\par \par \uc2 North Carolina rejoins a list of crucial swing states whose voters will decide if Harris becomes the United States\u8217\'20\'19 first woman of color to win the White House or if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returns to the Oval Office from which he wreaked political chaos for four years.\par \par \uc2 Up until about two months ago, the odds didn\u8217\'20\'19t look like this.\par \par \uc2 Though the margins in North Carolina have been close for decades in presidential races, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2008 was the last Democrat since 1976 to win the state, eking out a win by three-tenths of a percentage point. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s weakness earlier this year threatened to turn North Carolina into an also-ran contest. Every poll through June had Trump beating the president by at least two points, with an average around six.\par \par \uc2 Party affiliation can only tell so much in a state with a storied history of split-ticket voting. Almost four in 10 of North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s 7.6 million registered voters choose not to affiliate with a political party. But between August 2020 and August 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  added about 161,000 new registered voters in North Carolina while Democrats lost about 135,000 registered voters.\par \par \uc2 Trump won the state by about 75,000 votes in 2020, a margin of about 1.3 percentage points, his closest winning state, before losing the election. Biden won the four states with closer margins \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Arizona and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ascent scrambled the math. North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, Elaine Marshall, described the reaction as euphoric.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s such a dramatic contrast from that venom, that poison, that hatred that\u8217\'20\'19s coming from Republican events,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat contrasts so strongly with the hope and the expectations of the future from Democratic party events.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/15/north-carolina-trump-harris-campaigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s such a dramatic contrast\u8217\'20\'19: Harris turns North Carolina into a toss-up}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to hold a rally in Wilmington, North Carolina, on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The former president had invited Mark Robinson to previous campaign events in the state. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether he will address the new report about Robinson.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina would be a key state in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s path to victory. The latest polls have Trump and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tied in a dead heat in the state.\par \par \uc2 Still, expect for 2008, Democrats have not won North Carolina at the presidential level since 1976. But Democratic voter registration has been up in the state, and the vice-president has been investing time and resources to win its 16 electoral votes. If she manages to do so, Trump would have to virtually sweep every other swing state in order to win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/chuck-schumer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chuck Schumer}}}\uc2 , on Thursday took a procedural step toward setting up a vote next week on a government funding extension as the House scrambles to avert a shutdown starting on 1 October.\par \par \uc2 Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s move comes a day after the Republican-led House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/speaker-johnson-funding-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  rejected a proposal by the speaker, Mike Johnson}}}\uc2 , that would have linked a six-month stopgap funding measure, known as a continuing resolution, with a controversial measure backed by conservatives mandating that states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/10/us-house-save-act-citizenship-proof-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 require}}}\uc2  proof of citizenship to register to vote.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 202 to 220, with 14 House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  and all but three House Democrats opposing the bill. Two Republican members voted \u8220\'20\'1Cpresent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on Thursday, Schumer lamented Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s approach, saying that the speaker \u8220\'20\'1Cflopped right on his face\u8221\'20\'1D by pushing a GOP plan. As Congress awaits Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s next move, Schumer said he was setting up a vote for early next week on a legislative vehicle for a bipartisan funding bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the House can\u8217\'20\'19t get its act together, we\u8217\'20\'19re prepared to move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/government-shutdown-schumer-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate leader Schumer moves to avert shutdown after House speaker\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18flop\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  has issued a statement characterizing Mark Robinson as \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged, dangerous and completely unfit\u8221\'20\'1D to serve as governor.\par \par \uc2 The deputy communications director, Izzi Levy, wrote in a statement:\par \par \uc2 This is just the latest proof that Mark Robinson is unhinged, dangerous, and completely unfit to be governor. Now, as many Republicans warn against the damage Robinson would do as governor, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that the stakes have never been higher and we must keep our foot on the gas to defeat him in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robinson has history of controversy\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson has a history of controversy.\par \par \uc2 Prior to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/19/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-black-nazi-pro-slavery-porn-forum/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revelations from CNN}}}\uc2  that he made lewd statements, called for the reinstatement of slavery and called himself a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D on a porn website, Robinson said \u8220\'20\'1Csome folks need killing\u8221\'20\'1D at the Republican national convention, while casting his state\u8217\'20\'19s delegate votes for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrNorth Carolina GOP guv candidate Mark Robinson, who recently said "some folks need killing" in reference to political enemies, casts NC's delegate votes for Trump at the \uc2 RNC{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D22sXp81Ay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D22sXp81Ay}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1812937836565270790?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Read more about Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s history here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hitler-quoting candidate wins North Carolina Republican gubernatorial primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the federal government has sent bomb-sniffing dogs to the town of Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Residents in Springfield have been facing ongoing threats after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , JD Vance and others on the right spread false rumors that immigrants were killing and eating pets. Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s governor has deployed the state highway patrol to provide security to schools in the city in response to more than 30 bomb threats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls had already suggested that Mark Robinson was slightly lagging behind his opponent, Democrat \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has a deeply conservative legislature, but Stein, who had outspent Robinson in his campaign, was boosted by voters who found \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be the second most important issue to them after the economy.\par \par \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , director of the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 center for politics}}}\uc2 , said the new revelations about Robinson would do little to affect his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s ultimate fate \u8211\'20\'13 but that Robinson could drag \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  down with him.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur Crystal Ball rating for NC Governor has been Lean D. Mark Robinson (R) was going to lose even before this new story. The question is whether Robinson brings down the top of the ticket (\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ) with him. Those 16 electoral votes could be the whole election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wrH7Xapw4n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wrH7Xapw4n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2  (@LarrySabato) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LarrySabato/status/1836845248175370490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has seized on the revelations about Mark Robinson, releasing a video of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heaping praise on the North Carolina gubernatorial candidate.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KamalaHQ/status/1836855054688456858"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the video Trump says}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to cherish Mark\u8221\'20\'1D, calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the great leaders in our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: Mark Robinson is \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2  on steroids. He is better than \uc2 Martin Luther King{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GFPWV0zhXx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GFPWV0zhXx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1836851875670331661?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robinson denies referring to himself as a 'black Nazi' and a 'perv'\par \par \uc2 CNN writes that Robinson strenuously denied writing the statements the network attributed to him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not us. These are not our words. And this is not anything that is characteristic of me,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said in an interview with CNN. Presented with evidence that it was, in fact, him, the lieutenant governor replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to get into the minutia of how somebody manufactured this, these salacious tabloid lies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 CNN notes they reached out to Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign on Tuesday morning, and only heard back from him two days later. Shortly before the story was published, the lieutenant governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec79788f089e4a13dfac56#block-66ec79788f089e4a13dfac56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted a video on Twitter/X}}}\uc2  where he denied the reporting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robinson posted lewd statements between 2008 and 2012 on Nude Africa, a pornography website that has a message board, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/19/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-black-nazi-pro-slavery-porn-forum/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They were able to link him to the comments made under the handle \u8220\'20\'1Cminisoldr\u8221\'20\'1D because he has used that name elsewhere online, listed his real name on his profile and an email addressed matched to him.\par \par \uc2 One of the stories CNN reports Robinson recounted on the message board was about spying on a women\u8217\'20\'19s locker room as a 14-year-old:\par \par \uc2 I came to a spot that was a dead end but had two big vent covers over it! It just so happened it overlooked the showers! I sat there for about an hour and watched as several girls came in and showered.\par \par \uc2 Robinson is an opponent of LGBTQ rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/16/mark-robinson-north-carolina-republican-lgbtq-tirade-filth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying in 2021}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no reason anybody anywhere in America should be telling any child about transgenderism, homosexuality, any of that filth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, on Nude Africa, CNN says he wrote:\par \par \uc2 I like watching tranny on girl porn! That\u8217\'20\'19s f*cking hot! It takes the man out while leaving the man in!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina GOP governor candidate Robinson referred to himself as 'black NAZI' on porn website \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/19/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-black-nazi-pro-slavery-porn-forum/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN has published}}}\uc2  their reporting on Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in North Carolina, and found that he called himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack NAZI!\u8221\'20\'1D on a pornography website\u8217\'20\'19s message board.\par \par \uc2 The statements were posted more than 10 years ago, and CNN says Robinson, who is Black and currently serves as the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, also wrote about enjoying transgender porn and referred to himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cperv\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina's GOP governor candidate Mark Robinson denies reportedly damning story\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor in swing state North Carolina, has pre-emptively denied a story CNN and a Raleigh-based broadcaster are reportedly soon to publish regarding statements he made online.\par \par \uc2 In a video shared on X, Robinson, the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe things that you will see in that story \u8211\'20\'13 those are not the words of Mark Robinson\u8221\'20\'1D. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the video:\par \par \uc2 enltrI wanted to take a minute to address the latest outrageous lies coming from my opponent\u8217\'20\'19s dishonest campaign: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ncgov?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ncgov}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ncpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ncpol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RtteVUiozr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RtteVUiozr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Robinson (@markrobinsonNC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/markrobinsonNC/status/1836841409388642512?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former advisers to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have collaborated to build a website that spreads conspiracy theories, including about Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s enemies, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Matt Bernardini reports:\par \par \uc2 Amid the recent crackdown on Russian influence in American media, a group of former Trump advisers and operatives have quietly helped build a pro-Russian website that frequently spreads debunked conspiracy theories about the war in Ukraine, election fraud and vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Working alongside contributors for Kremlin state media, the former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  policy aide George Papadopoulos, his wife, Simona Mangiante, and others have become editorial board members of the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://intelligencer.today/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Intelligencer}}}\uc2 , which is increasingly becoming a source of news for those in the rightwing ecosystem.\par \par \uc2 The growth of the website, which has not been reported on before, comes at a time when the US is seeking to crack down on Russian influence ahead of the 2024 election. Recently, the justice department charged two members of RT (formerly known as \uc2 Russia Today\uc2 ) with violating the Foreign Agents Registration Act and money laundering for payments they allegedly made to \u8220\'20\'1Crecruit unwitting American influencers\u8221\'20\'1D. It also placed sanctions on RT\u8217\'20\'19s editor-in-chief, \uc2 Margarita Simonyan\uc2 , and nine other employees.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/intelligencer-pro-russia-website-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Trump advisers help to grow pro-Russia website that spreads misinformation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice- President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is participating in a live stream with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  and the campaign says it\u8217\'20\'19s anticipating some \u8220\'20\'1Csurprises\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Will Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 make a surprise appearance? Do audience-members get a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pviYWzu0dzk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 car}}}\uc2  ? Is it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PeterHamby/status/1826809739604320420"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leon Panetta}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re not totally sure. You\u8217\'20\'19ll have to tune into the live stream tonight at 8pm to find out. The campaign said 200,000 people had formally RSVPd, but they\u8217\'20\'19re expecting more to join the livestream. There will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cfew hundred\u8221\'20\'1D guests in the studio as well, it said.\par \par \uc2 Oprah endorsed Harris in a rousing speech at the Democratic national convention in which she specifically appealed to independent voters. The campaign argues that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s appearance alongside the TV personality will reach a cross-section of \u8220\'20\'1Cpersuadable\u8221\'20\'1D voters.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s part of the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s voter registration-week organizing push.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Harris to meet with Ukraine's \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will next week welcome Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Thursday, September 26, President Biden will meet with President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  of Ukraine at the White House. Vice-president Harris will also meet separately with President Zelenskyy at the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe leaders will discuss the state of the war between Russia and Ukraine, including Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s strategic planning and U.S. support for Ukraine in its defense against Russian aggression. The President and vice-president will emphasize their unshakeable commitment to stand with Ukraine until it prevails in this war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he will \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-meet-volodymyr-zelenskiy-un-security-council-russia-ukraine-war-latest-updates?page=with:block-66ebd08f8f08893ca2b3a487#block-66ebd08f8f08893ca2b3a487"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 probably}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D meet with Zelenskyy, who is traveling to the United States to address a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council meeting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 A major story may be developing in North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s race for governor, where Republicans earlier this year nominated as their candidate Mark Robinson, the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor who has a history of making inflammatory statements.\par \par \uc2 Citing sources familiar with the reporting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/corner/huge-story-about-to-drop-on-mark-robinson/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Review}}}\uc2  says CNN is working on a story about \u8220\'20\'1Cunsavory comments Robinson made in several online chatrooms\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.carolinajournal.com/robinson-under-pressure-to-withdraw-from-gubernatorial-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Carolina Journal reports}}}\uc2  that Robinson is under pressure from state Republicans and the Trump campaign to withdraw from the race over the story, which contains information leaked to CNN and Raleigh\u8217\'20\'19s WRAL by Democratic attorney general \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign for governor.\par \par \uc2 Today is the deadline for Robinson to drop out, though his campaign has called both the National Review and Carolina Journal\u8217\'20\'19s reporting \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete fiction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Robinson and his troubling past statements:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hitler-quoting candidate wins North Carolina Republican gubernatorial primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden went on to talk about how his administration has addressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/13/joe-biden-supply-chain-ports-bottlenecks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post-pandemic supply chain snarls}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/15/biden-harris-prescription-drug-prices-medicare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prescription drug prices}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jul/02/biden-invest-business-tax-infrastructure-microchips-services"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 semiconductor manufacturing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But in the midst of talking about his respect for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s independence to do its job free of political considerations, Biden fibbed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd unlike my predecessor, I respect the Federal Reserve independence as they pursued its mandate to bring inflation down. That independence has served the country well. By the way, I\u8217\'20\'19ve never once spoken to the chairman of Fed since I became president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 That last part is not true:\par \par \uc2 That said, there are no indications Biden\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with Powell come anywhere near how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  treated the central bank chair during his presidency:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2019/aug/21/trump-raises-pressure-on-federal-reserve-to-cut-interest-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump raises pressure on Federal Reserve to cut interest rates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'we do have more work to do' as he touts economy's recovery\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said that the US economy has a ways to go before the toll of inflation is eased, but acknowledged yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cut by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  was a milestone in the fight against the price increases that bedeviled his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you all know, inflation was 9.1% in the United States. Today, it\u8217\'20\'19s much closer to 2%. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean our work is done. Far from it, far from it. No one should confuse why I\u8217\'20\'19m here. I\u8217\'20\'19m not here to take a victory lap. I\u8217\'20\'19m not here to say a job well done. I\u8217\'20\'19m not here to say we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a hell of a lot more work to do. We do have more work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 He then argued that both consumers and businesses should feel optimistic about the future:\par \par \uc2 The Fed lowering interest rates isn\u8217\'20\'19t a declaration of victory. It\u8217\'20\'19s a declaration of progress. It\u8217\'20\'19s a signal we\u8217\'20\'19ve entered a new phase of our economy and our recovery. You know, I believe it\u8217\'20\'19s important for the country to recognize this progress, because, if we don\u8217\'20\'19t, the progress we made will remain locked in the fear of negative mindset and dominate our economic outlook since the pandemic began, instead of seeing the immense opportunities in front of us right now.\par \par \uc2 This is a moment, in my view, for business to feel greater confidence, to invest higher, to expand. It\u8217\'20\'19s a moment for individuals to feel greater confidence, buying a home, a new car, starting a family, starting a new business.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to promote economic policies after Fed lowers rates in sign of inflation's easing\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just taken the stage at the Economic Club of Washington, where he is expected to take credit for declining inflation that spurred the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to yesterday slash interest rates for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 Lowering rates is a sign the powerful central bank believes the pressures that drove up price growth to levels not seen since the 1980s during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency are easing.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what Biden has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The federal judge overseeing \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s criminal gun case has agreed to delay the sentencing until 4 December, Reuters is reporting.\par \par \uc2 A jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/hunter-biden-gun-charges-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted}}}\uc2  Hunter, the son of president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , earlier this summer on three felony gun charges he faced related to buying and possessing a handgun while being a drug user.\par \par \uc2 He was set to be sentenced on 13 November, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-harris-presidential-election-09-19-24/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 , but Hunter\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys asked the judge to move the sentencing to a later date, in part due to his family members being currently involved with government work, traveling with the current administration and being busy with the 2024 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Uncommitted National Movement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/harris-uncommitted-movement-declines-endorse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Thursday that it would not be endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 In a press conference on Thursday, Abbas Alawieh, an Uncommitted leader and delegate from Michigan, said:\par \par \uc2 Vice-president Harris\u8217\'20\'19s unwillingness to shift on unconditional weapons policy or to even make a clear statement in support of upholding existing US and international human rights law has made it impossible for us to endorse her.\par \par \uc2 The group said that they also opposed a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency, and were not recommending a third-party vote in the presidential election. They urged uncommitted voters \u8220\'20\'1Cto register anti-Trump votes and vote up and down the ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/harris-uncommitted-movement-declines-endorse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uncommitted movement declines to endorse Harris \u8211\'20\'13 but warns against Trump presidency}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rob Rue, the mayor of Springfield, Ohio, issued a proclamation on Thursday, allowing him \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary emergency powers to mitigate public safety concerns\u8221\'20\'1D, in response to recent threats to public safety in the city, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/news/springfield-mayor-adds-temporary-emergency-powers-to-address-safety-issues/NQTLZDB7CZHBBHPSWSIVRHG7GA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Springfield News Sun}}}\uc2  and other local news outlets.\par \par \uc2 The proclamation will allow the city to acquire resources quicker, and allow departments to respond more efficiently to potential threats and emerging risks.\par \par \uc2 Officials said that the proclamation will remain in effect until the city determines risks to public safety have subsided.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnsuring the safety of Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s residents is our top priority,\u8221\'20\'1D Rue said, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://myfox28columbus.com/news/local/springfield-mayor-assumes-emergency-powers-to-address-security-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple local news}}}\uc2  outlets.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are addressing these threats with the seriousness they warrant and are taking immediate steps to ensure the security of both our community and our employees. Our commitment to preventing harm is unwavering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the latest setback for the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to forgive the federal student loans of many Americans, a federal judge has extended the block on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s latest loan forgiveness plan, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/09/19/biden-student-debt-forgiveness-ruling.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  CNBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 US District Judge Randal Hall, who was appointed by former Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , said in a ruling on Wednesday, per CNBC, that he would maintain the order blocking the administration from cancelling any student debt, for another 14 days while litigation continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 New polling shows that voters are almost evenly split between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the three Great Lakes battlegrounds that could determine the outcome of the election. The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec14e28f089e4a13dfa5ec#block-66ec14e28f089e4a13dfa5ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that the vice-president is tied with Trump in Pennsylvania, though another poll released today by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec1dd48f089e4a13dfa649#block-66ec1dd48f089e4a13dfa649"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Harris had the advantage in that state, but was deadlocked with the former president nationwide. There are signs that Republicans are leaving nothing in this election to chance, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec2d0d8f089e4a13dfa73a#block-66ec2d0d8f089e4a13dfa73a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec357a8f08098f3f16274e#block-66ec357a8f08098f3f16274e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham}}}\uc2  , the South Carolina senator and Trump ally, pushing for the red state\u8217\'20\'19s governor to put in motion a plan to switch its system for allocating electoral votes to a winner-take-all set-up that will surely benefit Trump. Such calls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec31ab8f081d8429b1bdad#block-66ec31ab8f081d8429b1bdad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been made before}}}\uc2 , and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if this latest push makes a difference.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec22678f081d8429b1bc86#block-66ec22678f081d8429b1bc86"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tout his economic record}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  yesterday lowered interest rates for the first time in four years, a sign that inflation is ebbing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is the Secret Service investigating \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for his post on assassinating Harris and Biden? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec43898f08098f3f16284c#block-66ec43898f08098f3f16284c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Perhaps}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White dudes are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-rally-apparent-assassination-attempt-new-york-election-campaign-kamala-harris-us-politics-latest-news?page=with:block-66ec3dde8f08098f3f1627de#block-66ec3dde8f08098f3f1627de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly putting down}}}\uc2  big money to promote Harris in Wisconsin, Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Marist released polls of the so-called Blue Wall swing states of Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, that show a tight race between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the traditional Democratic bulwarks.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president saw her best result {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/u-s-presidential-contest-in-michigan-september-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Michigan}}}\uc2 , where Marist found she has a five-percentage-point advantage over Trump, with 52% support to his 47%.\par \par \uc2 But it was nearly a dead heat between the candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/marist-pennsylvania-poll-u-s-presidential-contest-pennsylvania-september-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/u-s-presidential-contest-in-wisconsin-september-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , the pollster says. Trump and Harris are tied with 49% support each in the former state, and in the latter, the vice-president is up by only one percentage point over Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service may be investigating \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  post on assassinating Biden and Harris \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 After a gunman was found in the woods near where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was playing golf on Sunday in what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  would later say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/15/trump-safe-gunshots-golf-course"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be}}}\uc2  another assassination attempt, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the rightwing \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO, made an inflammatory post on X asking why no one had targeted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2024-09-19/musk-x-post-about-biden-harris-threats-leads-to-secret-service-investigation?utm_source=website&utm_medium=share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News}}}\uc2  sought records from the Secret Service regarding Musk\u8217\'20\'19s tweet, and if it was being investigated for it. What the outlet received in response isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite definitive, but does indicate that the agency was aware of what he said:\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service investigates when they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to determine whether a person poses an imminent threat to one of their protectees. Threatening the US president or vice president is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/871"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 felony}}}\uc2  that can carry a hefty fine or up to five years in prison.\par \par \uc2 FOIA Files sent Freedom of Information Act requests to the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s Protective Intelligence and Assessment Division, Office of Protective Operations and Office of Investigations for documents and emails referencing Musk\u8217\'20\'19s post.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the agency responded to the requests by saying records it has about Musk\u8217\'20\'19s post were \u8220\'20\'1Ccompiled for law enforcement purposes\u8221\'20\'1D and are being withheld because \u8220\'20\'1Cdisclosure could reasonably be expected to interfere with enforcement proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We followed up with the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s FOIA division and were told that the Protective Intelligence Division advised that it cannot release any records because of \u8220\'20\'1Cenforcement proceedings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The agency \u8220\'20\'1Cis aware of the social media post made by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nate Herring, a spokesperson for the Secret Service. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a matter of practice, we do not comment on matters involving protective intelligence. We can say, however, that the Secret Service investigates all threats related to our protectees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Musk\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate comment, and the White House\u8217\'20\'19s response:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/sep/16/elon-musk-assassination-tweet-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House blasts Elon Musk for X post about Biden and Harris assassination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 White Dudes For Harris to make $10m TV ad buy in swing states \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 White Dudes For Harris will spend somewhere around $10m on television ads promoting the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy in three battleground states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Backed by a Pac called Beige Rainbow, the group argues in the ad airing in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and Michigan that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made white men look bad, and that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies would offer the country a better future:\par \par \uc2 A previous fundraiser by \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite dudes\u8221\'20\'1D brought in millions for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign shortly after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended his bid for a second term:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/white-dudes-harris-fundraiser-zoom-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Celebrity-studded \u8216\'20\'18White Dudes for Harris\u8217\'20\'19 call raises $4m for vice-president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last week, Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , reiterated that he is in favor of switching to a winner-take-all system of allocating its electoral votes, but would only call a special session if he believed the legislature would approve the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I have consistently made clear, I strongly support statewide unity and joining 48 other states by awarding all five of our electoral college votes to the presidential candidate who wins the majority of Nebraskans\u8217\'20\'19 votes. As I have also made clear, I am willing to convene the legislature for a special session to fix this 30-year-old problem before the 2024 election. However, I must receive clear and public indication that 33 senators are willing to vote in such a session to restore winner-take-all,\u8221\'20\'1D Pillen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.nebraska.gov/press/gov-pillen-offers-statement-status-special-session-winner-take-all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this time, I have not yet received the concrete and public indication that 33 senators would vote for WTA. If that changes, I will enthusiastically call a special session.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One thing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign may want to bear in mind: Democratic lawmakers in Maine, the other state that allocates its electoral votes by congressional district, have raised changing to a winner-take-all system if Nebraska does so, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mainepublic.org/politics/2024-04-29/as-goes-nebraska-so-goes-maine-lawmakers-mull-winner-takes-all-system-for-presidential-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maine Public reports}}}\uc2 . Maine is generally a blue state but one of its congressional districts leans Republican, meaning the change would effectively negate Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s shift, by giving all of Maine\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes to the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign dispatched \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the US senator representing South Carolina who is a close ally of the former president, to Nebraska earlier this week to encourage Governor \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2  and state lawmakers to change to a winner-take-all system for allocating its electoral votes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/lindsey-graham-visits-nebraska-push-electoral-vote-change-rcna171760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Graham\u8217\'20\'19s visit managed to shift the opposition to the switch by some Republican state lawmakers. Pillen has said he will only call the legislature into a special session to make the change if it has the votes to pass.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Graham\u8217\'20\'19s visit, from NBC:\par \par \uc2 Graham, acting on behalf of the Trump campaign, was working to encourage Pillen to call a special legislative session at which lawmakers could consider changing the state\u8217\'20\'19s apportionment of electoral votes, the source said.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska allocates its electoral votes by congressional district. The swing district around Omaha often goes to Democrats in an otherwise ruby red state.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting, previously reported by KOLN-TV, took place in Lincoln. Graham\u8217\'20\'19s office confirmed the local report but declined to comment further.\par \par \uc2 If Nebraska were to switch to a winner-take-all system, it would almost certainly give former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  an extra electoral vote in what is expected to be a tight presidential race.\par \par \uc2 That one electoral vote could prove decisive.\par \par \uc2 If Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin but loses every other swing state, she and Trump would be tied at 269 Electoral College votes under a winner-take-all setup in Nebraska with Trump winning the state. In that scenario, the race would be thrown to the US House, where each state delegation would get one vote for president. Republicans hold a majority of delegations and are favored to retain it, even though the House majority could change hands after the November election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The GOP might dominate Nebraska politics, but there has not been enough support among the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers for changing its system of allocating electoral votes in a way that would almost certainly benefit \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chris-stein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The guy who is also writing this live blog}}}\uc2  traveled to Omaha earlier this year (when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was still running for re-election) to find out why:\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , the road to the White House runs through battleground states clustered along the Great Lakes, and in the fast-growing \u8220\'20\'1Csun belt\u8221\'20\'1D of the south. But if the election turns out to be extremely close, the two candidates\u8217\'20\'19 fortunes may hinge on a few hundred thousand voters clustered in a single congressional district in the middle of the country.\par \par \uc2 This lesser-known front can be found in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nebraska"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska}}}\uc2 , one of only two states in the country, along with Maine, that allocate a portion of their electoral votes by congressional district, rather than giving all of them to the winner of the state.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Biden became the first Democrat in 12 years to win Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s second congressional district, which encompasses the largest city, Omaha, and its suburbs. The pressure to win a majority of its voters is expected to be even higher this year, as Biden looks to fend off a resurgent Trump while reassuring Democrats that he can still do the job after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/04/biden-interview-debate-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his troubling performance}}}\uc2  in their first debate.\par \par \uc2 While much of the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 attention is focused on the seven swing states expected to decide the election (Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Nevada, Arizona, North Carolina and Georgia) the Biden campaign also counts winning the Nebraska district as among its priorities \u8211\'20\'13 so much so that some Trump allies are encouraging the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers to change their rules to ensure the former president wins the entirety of its electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the district is probably going to get more attention this time than it did even in 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ryan Horn, a Republican media strategist who splits his time between Omaha and Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/07/nebraska-presidential-election-congressional-district"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This Nebraska congressional district could be the key to the presidential election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans make new push for Nebraska to change its voting rules in Trump's favor\par \par \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s all-Republican congressional delegation has sent a letter to the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor asking him to call the legislature into a special session to change its system for apportioning electoral votes in a way that would almost certainly benefit \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The midwestern state is one of two in the nation, along with Maine, that allocates votes by congressional district. Nebraska is heavily Republican, but the district around its largest city, Omaha, leans Democratic and voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020. In certain scenarios, the state\u8217\'20\'19s electoral vote could decide the election, and in a letter to the governor, \uc2 Jim Pillen\uc2 , and the speaker of the Nebraska legislature, John Arch, both Republicans, the state\u8217\'20\'19s three representatives and two senators call on them to switch to a winner-take-all system for allocating the state\u8217\'20\'19s votes:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to return Nebraska to winner-take-all. The Nebraska delegation stands with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamPillen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TeamPillen}}}\uc2  and Speaker Arch.\par \par \uc2 Read our full letter here ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VmkRSkMEmY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VmkRSkMEmY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Mike Flood (@USRepMikeFlood) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USRepMikeFlood/status/1836567974678798642?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is heading to the battleground state of Michigan today, for an 8pm rally in Farmington Hills, near Detroit.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19ll then head back to Washington DC, but has campaign events planned for tomorrow in Wisconsin and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 In addition to his speech marking a turning point in the US economy\u8217\'20\'19s battle with inflation, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual gala at 8.45pm this evening, in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to hail 'new milestone' for US economy in speech, as interest rates decline\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the Economic Club of Washington DC today, one day after the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  cut interest rates for the first time in four years, marking a significant turning point for the economy.\par \par \uc2 While the president is expected to hail a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew milestone\u8221\'20\'1D in America\u8217\'20\'19s post-pandemic economic recovery, his top officials said he would acknowledge there remains more work to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not meant to be a declaration of victory,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeff Zients, the White House chief of staff, told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is meant to be a declaration of progress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cknows this is no time for a victory lap\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Zients, and will use his speech to \u8220\'20\'1Clay out how we build on the progress we have made\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lael Brainard\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s top economic adviser, pointed to housing, healthcare and childcare as examples of areas where his administration wanted to improve affordability.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s decision yesterday to drop interest rates by half a percentage point, and signal more cuts will follow in the months to come:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/18/inflation-fed-rate-cut"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve cuts US interest rates for the first time in four years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  poll is something of an outlier, in that it shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  neck and neck nationally.\par \par \uc2 Most national surveys taken recently have given the vice-president the advantage, some with margins bigger than others. Poll aggregator FiveThirtyEight has a good rundown of what other data has found, and you can find it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/national/?ex_cid=abcpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Presidential race deadlocked nationally, but Harris leads in Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 poll\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/19/us/politics/harris-trump-times-siena-poll-pennsylvania.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times}}}\uc2  also released polling data this morning, which contained some better news for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s standing in the vital swing state of Pennsylvania: she leads \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , with 50% support to his 46%.\par \par \uc2 But nationally, the two candidates are in a dead heat, polling at 47% each. The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  poll released earlier today did not include nationwide perceptions of the candidates.\par \par \uc2 Much like the Post\u8217\'20\'19s, the Times poll, conducted with Siena College and the Philadelphia Inquirer, finds voters believe Harris was the winner of last week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate, with 67% saying she did \u8220\'20\'1Cwell\u8221\'20\'1D, compared to 40% who said the same for Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/19/polling-harris-trump-pennsylvania-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post poll}}}\uc2  of Pennsylvania also finds a similarly tight race for the Senate seat currently held by Democrat Bob Casey.\par \par \uc2 Democrats currently control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber, but face an exceptionally difficult task in holding on to it beyond the end of the year. The party can only afford to lose one seat, and will need to win the re-election of senators representing two red states: Ohio and Montana.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the Post poll\u8217\'20\'19s finding that Casey is practically neck and neck with his challenger, \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , is likely to rattle Democrats. Among likely voters, Casey is at 47% support, against McCormick\u8217\'20\'19s 46%. If third-party candidates are excluded, they are tied, at 48% support each.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris tied in vital swing state Pennsylvania, poll suggests\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/19/polling-harris-trump-pennsylvania-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post poll}}}\uc2  published this morning shows that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are essentially tied in Pennsylvania, the swing state viewed as perhaps the most likely to determine the outcome of the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The survey conducted after last week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate found that 48% of likely and registered voters support Harris, and 47% back Trump, with the rest planning to vote for third-party candidates. Excluding other candidates, Harris and Trump are tied at 48% support among likely voters, while among registered voters, Harris has a slight advantage at 48% support to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 47%.\par \par \uc2 However, the vice-president did impress debate watchers in the state: 54% of those surveyed said she won last week\u8217\'20\'19s face-off, with only 27% saying the same about Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is set to participate in a livestream with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  today, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be in Washington to address a Fighting Anti-Semitism in America evening event, and will also speak before the Israeli-American Council.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 US House fails to pass federal funding bill as shutdown deadline nears\par \par \uc2 A government funding package championed by Republican House speaker Mike Johnson failed to pass on Wednesday, with less than two weeks left to prevent a shutdown starting 1 October.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 202 to 220, with 14 House Republicans and all but three House Democrats opposing the bill. Two Republican members voted \u8220\'20\'1Cpresent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bill was not expected to pass, as a number of House Republicans had voiced criticism of the proposal before the vote. Given Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow House majority and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 widespread opposition to the bill, Johnson could only afford a handful of defections within his conference. Johnson delayed a vote on the funding package last week in the hopes of consolidating Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 support, but those efforts could not get the bill across the finish line.\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s proposed bill combined a six-month stopgap funding measure, known as a continuing resolution, with the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (Save) Act, a controversial proposal that would require people to show proof of citizenship when they register to vote.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has championed baseless claims of widespread non-citizen voting, has pressured Johnson to reject any funding measure unless it includes \u8220\'20\'1Celection security\u8221\'20\'1D provisions, a stance that the former president doubled down on hours before the vote.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/speaker-johnson-funding-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45am BST\par \par \uc2 US health system ranks last compared with peer nations, report finds\par \par \uc2 The United States health system ranked dead last in an international comparison of 10 peer nations, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonwealthfund.org/publications/fund-reports/2024/sep/mirror-mirror-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Commonwealth Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In spite of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/mar/13/us-healthcare-costs-causes-drug-prices-salaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paying nearly double}}}\uc2  that of other countries, the system performed poorly on health equity, access to care and outcomes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see the human toll of these shortcomings on a daily basis,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Joseph Betancourt, the president of the \uc2 Commonwealth Fund\uc2 , a foundation with a focus on healthcare research and policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see patients who cannot afford their medications \u8230\'20\'26 I see older patients arrive sicker than they should because they spent the majority of their lives uninsured,\u8221\'20\'1D said Betancourt. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time we finally build a health system that delivers quality affordable healthcare for all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/american-health-system-ranks-last"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Iran sent hacked Trump documents to Biden campaign, \uc2 FBI\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 Iranian hackers sought to interest President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s campaign in information stolen from rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, sending unsolicited emails to people associated with the then-Democratic candidate in an effort to interfere in the 2024 election, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and other US agencies have said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  confirmed on 12 August that it was investigating a complaint from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign that Iran had hacked and distributed a trove of sensitive campaign documents. On 19 August intelligence officials confirmed that Iran was behind the hack.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no indication that any of the recipients in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign team responded, officials said on Wednesday, and several media organisations approached over the summer with leaked stolen information have also said they did not respond.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign called the emails from Iran \u8220\'20\'1Cunwelcome and unacceptable malicious activity\u8221\'20\'1D that were received by only a few people who regarded them as spam or phishing attempts.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/iran-sent-hacked-trump-documents-to-biden-campaign-fbi-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read more here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Associated Press\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump stages first rally since apparent assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday night staged his first rally since he became the target of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/trump-town-hall-flint-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second attempted assassination }}}\uc2  in as many months, telling his supporters in a sports venue outside New York City that what he called \u8220\'20\'1Cthese encounters with death\u8221\'20\'1D had only hardened him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod has now spared my life. It must have been God, not once, but twice,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said to loud cheers from the ecstatic crowd.\par \par \uc2 The former president took his usual ragbag of lies, hyperbole, and dark and racist invective to the Nassau Coliseum in the suburbs of Long Island, just seven miles from the borders of New York City. It was an audacious choice of location, given that there are just 48 days til the election and New York is on neither main party\u8217\'20\'19s list of priorities.\par \par \uc2 The state is reliably Democratic, having last voted for a Republican presidential candidate in 1984 with \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election. Even Nassau county, where the arena is situated, voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 by 54% to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 45%, while the latest New York state polls show \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  comfortably ahead of him by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/new-york/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 double digits}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet Trump clearly saw method in his madness. Long Island, the leafy suburbs that stretch east from the city, has shifted towards the right in recent years, becoming something of an incubator for the Make America Great Again (Maga) upheaval.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/donald-trump-new-york-rally-nassau-coliseum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240919ek9j001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
