\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump appears at town hall in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh ,Chris Stein and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 13,307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par 05:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed now, thanks for following along. You can find the latest US elections coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find the latest US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he\u8217\'20\'19s meeting next week with Indian Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Modi is scheduled to be in the United States next week for the Quad Summit in Delaware in addition to events in New York, according to Indian media reports. There was no meeting with Trump previously reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump referenced his meeting with Modi for the first time while speaking at an unrelated event in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Indian officials did not immediately confirm the meeting when asked.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump ends, stopping to take selfies with people, shaking hands, to the tune of YMCA. This event appeared from the livestream to be well-attended and energetic, with loud cheers \u8211\'20\'13 and boos, for the Democrats \u8211\'20\'13from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Trump veered between topics, as he often does, offering confusing and unsubstantiated answers to questions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 A voter says he is concerned about taxes.\par \par \uc2 Trump says Harris will double your taxes, which is not true.\par \par \uc2 There are, however, big boos from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Trump is winding down. He says \u8220\'20\'1CMichigan is going to be the most fun\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins. He talks about car imports, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can\u8217\'20\'19t flood\u8221\'20\'1D the market with imported cars, to energetic cheers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will be like taking candy from a baby,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. It is unclear whether he is talking about the election or car imports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that never gets obsolete is a wall and a wheel. A wall is what we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust to finish with the border, when I talk about energy, he says, \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the border is of the greatest interest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to follow this response to a question from a voter about the cost of food and groceries, which is veering between energy and immigration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is asked by a nurse how he will bring down the cost of food and groceries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo we have to start always with energy,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you make donuts, if you make cars, whatever you make.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He says is plan is to reduce energy bills by 50% in 12 months. He does not explain how he will do this.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to do what we have to do with the farmers,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He appears to be trying to talk about exporting food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInterest rates, energy, and common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. Then the talks about the border again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 On American women\u8217\'20\'19s feelings about Trump, via the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/candidates/joe-biden-2024/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  won women by 15 points over Trump in 2020, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/interactive/2020/exit-polls/presidential-election-exit-polls/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  exit polls,}}}\uc2  up from former secretary of state Hillary Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s 13-point victory among women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/graphics/politics/2016-election/exit-polls/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2016}}}\uc2 . Polls suggest that this year, women prefer Democratic presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/kamala-harris/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  over Trump by similar margins. Harris led Trump by 13 points among women in an ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll released last Sunday. Before the Democratic National Convention last month, the same poll found her leading him by six points among women.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 He talks about the civilian who took a photograph of the suspect\u8217\'20\'19s number plate, who was a woman. He says \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen are smarter than men\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis woman was unbelievable,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says. \u8220\'20\'1CShe did an amazing job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Huckabee Sanders says the takeaway is that the \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen of this country love \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump talks now about the apparent assassination attempt yesterday.\par \par \uc2 He again thanks the secret service. \u8220\'20\'1CThese guys do a great job. Now, they do need more people,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClosing the border\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby drill\u8221\'20\'1D are two things Trump will get done, he says.\par \par \uc2 He says, \u8220\'20\'1Cunless you have the death penalty for drug dealers you\u8217\'20\'19ll never get rid of that problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 The voter asks what the major threat is to manufacturing in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Trump responds, confusingly, by talking about the threat of nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not going to care so much about making cars\u8221\'20\'1D if that starts to happen, he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is asked his first question from someone in the crowd, who starts by noting that he attended one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rallies and did not fall asleep or leave early.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is repeating false, unsubstantiated or unprovable claims about Covid, the 7 October attacks in Israel, inflation, the stock market, immigration, the price of oil, and the amount of oil in America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the world\u8217\'20\'19s longest answer to a question,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly after taking office in January last year, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  launched a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/15/sarah-sanders-arkansas-governor-ban-critical-race-theory-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 powerful salvo}}}\uc2  in the so-called war on woke being waged by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 She is from a well-known Republican family. Her father, \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , was Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s governor for more than a decade, from 1996 to 2007.\par \par \uc2 She served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary for two years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 A refresher on how US presidents are elected:\par \par \uc2 The popular vote is the overall number of qualified voters who voted for a given candidate: in other words, the number of ballots cast for one candidate or another. The main thing to know about the popular vote is that winning it does not mean you win the presidency. The presidency is won by the candidate who gains the majority of electoral college votes. In other words: the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/03/electoral-votes-swing-state-margins-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election is decided by races in individual states}}}\uc2 . In the 2016 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  received fewer votes than Hillary Clinton but still won the presidency and in 2000, \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  received fewer votes than \uc2 Al Gore\uc2  but also won.\par \par \uc2 The electoral college is a group of 538 people, called electors, who officially cast their votes for the US president after citizens have voted. This is a requirement outlined in the US constitution. The electors are chosen by political parties in each of the US\u8217\'20\'19s 50 states ahead of the election.\par \par \uc2 Different states have different numbers of electoral college votes, with the number decided based on the census. The number of votes is equal to its total congressional delegation: the number of senators plus the number of representatives. While not a state, the District of Columbia \u8211\'20\'13 as in Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 is allocated three electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 A candidate needs more than half \u8211\'20\'13 or at least 270 \u8211\'20\'13 of the electoral college votes to win.\par \par \uc2 In most states, all of the electoral college votes from the state go to the same candidate. The exceptions are Maine and Nebraska, which \u8220\'20\'1Callocate two electoral votes to the state popular vote winner, and then one electoral vote to the popular vote winner in each congressional district\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.270towin.com/content/split-electoral-votes-maine-and-nebraska/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  270towin.\par \par \uc2 This post was clarified on 19 September to explain that Maine and Nebraska have a different way of allocating electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is claiming falsely that he \u8220\'20\'1Cdid much better\u8221\'20\'1D in 2020 than 2016.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  306-232 in the Electoral College in 2020 and had a 4-point margin in the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  won the Electoral College with 304 votes compared to 227 votes for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , and Trump lost the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is being interviewed by Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She says that Trump will win because America \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds a fighter\u8221\'20\'1D. She asks why he wants to be president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you everybody. A lot of love in this room. I love you, you love me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks at town hall in Flint, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Trump is speaking now in Michigan. He claims that there are 8,000 people in the audience, and the same number \u8220\'20\'1Cwalking away\u8221\'20\'1D, who could not get in. This seems unlikely, and Trump has made false claims about his crowd sizes before.\par \par \uc2 Obama has said Trump is obsessed with the sizes of his crowds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is due to speak at town hall in Flint, Michigan\par \par \uc2 Trump will speak soon at a town hall with \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  in the town of Flint, in the swing state of Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 which has 15 electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support the second amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, referring to America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cright to bear arms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Walz is a gun owner and skilled marksman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we don\u8217\'20\'19t get to hide behind that when our first responsibility is to protect children,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese guys talk all the time about families, today they had a vote to protect IVF and they killed it,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz says of the Republicans.\par \par \uc2 He talks about his own experiences with IVF, which led to the birth of his daughter, Hope.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Freedom is not just a song \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  comes out to on stage, \u8220\'20\'1Calthough it is very cool\u8221\'20\'1D when she does that, says Walz.\par \par \uc2 Republicans want to invade your bedroom, who you love, your school library, he says, as well as the freedom to make decisions about your own body.\par \par \uc2 Some people choose to live their lives differently, he says.\par \par \uc2 The lesson is, \u8220\'20\'1CMind your own damn business,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, as he has before \u8211\'20\'13 a lesson from Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz suggests Trump's 'concept of a plan' on healthcare is 'weak answer'\par \par \uc2 Walz says, \u8220\'20\'1Cafter nine long years\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , when asked about healthcare during the debate, \u8220\'20\'1Cgave us a concept of a plan, seriously, none of my students ever gave that weak an answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has compared Trump to the high school students he used to teach a few times during this speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says Trump lost 'thousands of manufacturing jobs' in North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Walz talks about JD Vance saying he is willing \u8220\'20\'1Cto create stories\u8221\'20\'1D on the campaign trail while defending his spreading false, racist rumours of pets being abducted and eaten in a town in his home state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Walz says \u8220\'20\'1Cno kidding\u8221\'20\'1D and that that has been happening for years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is, you know the pain that he caused, he killed thousands of manufacturing jobs across this state,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz is speaking now.\par \par \uc2 He has brought up \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims that images of crowds at Harris events are AI. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what won\u8217\'20\'19t be AI?\u8221\'20\'1D he says: \u8220\'20\'1CYour ballots\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to start speaking in the swing state of North Carolina, here is a refresher on the electoral college:\par \par \uc2 The electoral college is a group of 538 people, called electors, who officially cast their votes for the US president after citizens have voted. This is a requirement outlined in the US constitution. The electors are chosen by political parties in each of the US\u8217\'20\'19s 50 states ahead of the election.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has 16 Electoral College votes, or almost 6%.\par \par \uc2 Different states have different numbers of electoral college votes, with the number decided based on the census. The number of votes is equal to its total congressional delegation: the number of senators plus the number of representatives. While not a state, the District of Columbia \u8211\'20\'13 as in Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 is allocated three electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 This is why the total is 538: 100 senators plus 435 representatives plus three for DC.\par \par \uc2 A candidate needs more than half \u8211\'20\'13 or at least 270 \u8211\'20\'13 of the electoral college votes to win. All the votes from a given state go to the same candidate.\par \par \uc2 The party that wins a state has its electors formally vote for its candidate. This happens a few weeks after the November election \u8211\'20\'13 and after US states have certified their election results \u8211\'20\'13 on the first Monday after the second Wednesday in December.\par \par \uc2 In 2020 \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2020/dec/14/what-is-electoral-college-vote-explainer-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to remove electors}}}\uc2  in some states ahead of the electoral college vote but the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rejected that attempt the week before.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to address crowd in Asheville, North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , is about to begin speaking in Asheville in the swing state of North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 which has 16 electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 We will bring key points from those remarks to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, if you\u8217\'20\'19re just tuning in, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  was interviewed by a panel of three \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) members, during which the vice-president talked about the anti-immigrant sentiment toward Haitians in Springfield, Ohio; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza}}}\uc2  ; domestic economic issues; gun violence; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . The conversation was one of the few interviews Harris has done since becoming the Democratic nominee, and it served as an opportunity for her to reaffirm policies.\par \par \uc2 When asked about \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere [she] sees the line in terms of aggression and defense\u8221\'20\'1D in regards to the war, she said that she supported the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s one-time pause on the delivery of 2,000lb bombs to Israel as \u8220\'20\'1Cleverage\u8221\'20\'1D that they \u8220\'20\'1Chave had and used\u8221\'20\'1D, but that achieving a deal was the real means to ending the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to agree that not only must we end this war, but we have to have a goal of a two-state solution because there must be stability and peace in that region,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cinasmuch as our goal must be to ensure that Israelis have security and Palestinians in equal measure have security, self determination, dignity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked what mechanisms the US has to support Palestinian self-determination, and whether or not it was even possible, as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ally, to support such a goal, Harris responded saying that she believed that it was. She described meetings with Israeli and Arab leaders to \u8220\'20\'1Ctalk about how we can construct a day-after scenario\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-nabj-panel-ohio-bomb-threats-gaza-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris calls Ohio bomb threats \u8216\'20\'18crying shame\u8217\'20\'19 in talk with Black journalists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is speaking during a campaign event in Eau Claire, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Alice Herman is there. She writes:\par \par \uc2 Vance has spoken at length about immigration, invoking a crime committed by an undocumented immigrant in the town of Prairie du Chien that Republicans in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wisconsinexaminer.com/2024/09/09/venezuelan-undocumented-immigrant-arrest-becomes-campaign-fodder-for-van-orden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have already seized on}}}\uc2  to bolster GOP claims about immigrants committing violent crimes. (In fact, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-focuses-migrants-crime-here-is-what-research-shows-2024-04-11/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research shows}}}\uc2  immigrants do not commit crimes at a higher rate than people born in the US).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are closer, in this moment, to a nuclear war, or a third world war, than at any time in our country\u8217\'20\'19s history and we have the chaos and incompetence of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to thank for it,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery community is a border state,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe problems that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has imported through that American Southern border have now gone nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also blamed Harris for the recent apparent assassination attempt at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American media, the Democrats, the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign, they\u8217\'20\'19ve gotta cut this crap out or they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna get somebody killed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vance, alleging that Democrats, who have highlighted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian rhetoric and attempts to overturn the 2020 election, are to blame for the two assassination attempts that Trump has faced so far during his 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans defeated a bill that would have protected access to IVF care, brought by Democrats seeking to pressure Republicans over the politically volatile topic that is sure to be on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds when they head to the presidential polls in 49 days. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 refusal to vote in favor of protecting IVF despite claiming to support access \u8220\'20\'1Cis not an isolated incident\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over in the House, the Republican speaker, Mike Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e993748f086ad2b4929a18#block-66e993748f086ad2b4929a18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  for the chamber to vote tomorrow on a spending bill that will prevent a partial government shutdown but be paired with legislation aimed at cracking down on non-citizen voting, which rarely happens. Democrats have come out against the latter part of the bill, with Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  saying today that Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s proposal will likely meet \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e9a10b8f086ad2b4929b14#block-66e9a10b8f086ad2b4929b14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a dead end}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, though that could increase the possibility of a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just said she called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after the Secret Service on Sunday fended off a gunman discovered outside a golf course where he was playing. \u8220\'20\'1CI checked on him to see if he was okay, and I told him what I have said publicly \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s no place for political violence in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a conversation with the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 , Harris also condemned the campaign against the Haitian immigrant community in Springfield, Ohio, waged by Trump, his running mate, JD Vance, and conservative commentators. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a crying shame,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responding to the shocking report in ProPublica}}}\uc2 , Harris also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e97df68f085fa2473a2bc8#block-66e97df68f085fa2473a2bc8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws supported by Trump were to blame for the death of a 28-year-old Georgia woman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In an interview with popular Spanish radio host Stephanie \u8220\'20\'1CChiquibaby\u8221\'20\'1D Himonidis, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e999e58f08e43e1272b0a0#block-66e999e58f08e43e1272b0a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies would result in the separation of migrant families at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e94b1d8f08f5de71dc27fd#block-66e94b1d8f08f5de71dc27fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery nice\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  when the president called him after the second assassination attempt against him on Sunday, and asked if he had any suggestions for how to improve his security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s top elections official said Tuesday that a newly identified error in the state\u8217\'20\'19s voter registration process needs to be swiftly resolved, as early ballots are scheduled to go out to some voters as soon as this week.\par \par \uc2 Election staff in the Maricopa county recorder\u8217\'20\'19s office identified an issue last week, which concerns voters with old drivers licenses who may never have provided documentary proof of citizenship but were coded as having provided it and therefore were able to vote full ballots. The state has a bifurcated system in which voters who do not provide documentary proof of citizenship cannot vote in local or state elections, only federal ones.\par \par \uc2 Because of the state\u8217\'20\'19s very close elections and status as a swing state, the issue affecting nearly 100,000 voters will likely be the subject of intense scrutiny and litigation in the coming weeks. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  has more than 4.1 million registered voters.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://azgovernor.gov/office-arizona-governor/news/2024/09/governor-katie-hobbs-statement-administrative-issue-avid-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed}}}\uc2  the motor vehicles division to fix the coding error, which the secretary of state, \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , said was already resolved going forward.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if any of these voters have unlawfully cast a ballot or if they have already provided proof of citizenship. People who register to vote check a box on registration forms, under penalty of perjury, declaring they are citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no reason to believe that there are any significant numbers of individuals remaining on this list who are not eligible to vote in Arizona,\u8221\'20\'1D Fontes said in a press conference Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot confirm that at this moment, but we don\u8217\'20\'19t have any reason to believe that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The error, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.votebeat.org/arizona/2024/09/17/citizenship-proof-records-error-federal-only-voter-registration-eligibility/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by Votebeat}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, relates to several quirks of Arizona governance.\par \par \uc2 Since 1996, Arizona residents have been required to show proof of citizenship to get a regular driver\u8217\'20\'19s license. And since 2004, they have been required to show proof of citizenship to vote in state and local elections.\par \par \uc2 State drivers licenses also do not expire until a driver is age 65, meaning for some residents, they will have a valid license for decades before needing renewal. These factors play into the error.\par \par \uc2 The issue has split the Republican recorder in the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest county, Maricopa, and the Democratic secretary of state. Recorder Stephen Richer is arguing that these voters should only be able to cast a federal-only ballot, while Fontes says the state should keep the status quo of allowing them to vote full ballots given how soon the election is. Fontes directed counties to allow these residents to cast full ballots this year.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/10/us-house-save-act-citizenship-proof-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House to vote on bill to require proof of citizenship to vote despite no evidence of non-citizen ballots}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has said that Republicans would do well to help avert a looming government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderMcConnell}}}\uc2  : "The one you cannot have is a government shutdown. It would be politically beyond stupid for us to do that right before the election because certainly we'd get the blame." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Al0yD8ztLM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Al0yD8ztLM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1836129009836404954?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The path to preventing a shutdown, as ever, remains shrouded. House leader Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s current proposal \u8211\'20\'13 which extends funding while also folding in a Republican measure requiring proof of citizenship to register to vote in national elections \u8211\'20\'13 lacks even enough Republican votes to pass.\par \par \uc2 Non-citizen voting is already illegal and voter fraud by non-citizens is virtually non-existent, and the inclusion of the measure, which would add barriers to voting for US citizens, is a nonstarter for Democrats in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, far-right Republicans say Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s proposal doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go far enough in pushing their agenda, and see the threat of shutdown as an opportunity to push Democrats to compromise on immigration and other issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why Republicans are raising double the money in down-ballot races\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  launched her presidential bid in July, Democrats have showered her campaign with cash. Last month alone, the vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/trump-harris-election-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised}}}\uc2  $361m, tripling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fundraising haul of $130m for the month. According to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/09/03/harris-25-million-transfer/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought}}}\uc2  in $540m in the six weeks after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  withdrew from the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressional candidates appear to be benefiting from this financial windfall as well, as Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/03/republican-campaign-money-problems-congress-00176947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sound the alarm}}}\uc2  about their fundraising deficit in key races that will determine control of the House and Senate in November.\par \par \uc2 But in one crucial area, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  maintain a substantial cash advantage over Democrats: state legislative races. In recent years, Republicans have controlled more state legislative chambers than Democrats, giving them more power over those states\u8217\'20\'19 budgets, election laws and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee (DLCC), which supports the party\u8217\'20\'19s state legislative candidates, has raised $35m between the start of 2023 and the end of this June, the committee told the Guardian. In comparison, the Republican State Leadership Committee (RSLC) \u8211\'20\'13 which invests in an array of state-level campaigns, such as supreme court races, in addition to legislative campaigns \u8211\'20\'13 has raised $62m in the same time period.\par \par \uc2 That resource gap is now rearing its head in key battleground states, the DLCC says. In Pennsylvania, a crucial state for the presidential and congressional maps, Republican state legislative candidates have spent $4.5m on paid advertisements, compared with $1.4m for Democratic candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we think about the context of what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake, we think about more than 65 million people being covered by our target map this year,\u8221\'20\'1D said Heather Williams, president of the DLCC. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that means that the rights of all those people will be determined by who\u8217\'20\'19s in power the day after the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/republican-fundraising-local-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why Republicans are raising double the money in down-ballot races}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 A national voter poll from Monmouth has found that there are fewer \u8220\'20\'1Cdouble haters\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 voters that dislike both the Democratic and Republican presidential candidates \u8211\'20\'13 since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  joined the race.\par \par \uc2 Only 7% of voters polled in this latest round favored neither \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nor Harris \u8211\'20\'13 compared to 16% of disliked both Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrNATIONAL VOTER POLL: The double-haters are less of a factor now than they were in the Biden-Trump race. Just 7% have an unfavorable opinion of both Trump and Harris, while 16% dislike both Trump and Biden. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/U2OgSVCw45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/U2OgSVCw45}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LWbtiI19SP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LWbtiI19SP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1836139280114033047?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenate Republicans put politics first and families last again today by blocking the Right to IVF Act for the second time since June,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emilia Rowland, national press secretary for the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rowland warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who claimed to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cleader\u8221\'20\'1D on IVF during his debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last week, would jeopardize access to fertility treatments if he wins in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters know the difference between words and actions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd between now and November, they will turn out against Republicans from the top to bottom of the ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is scheduled to speak in an hour at an event in Eau Claire, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The last time I was at this event space was for one of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inaugural rallies, which was held on the sprawling grounds adjacent to the hall where Vance will speak today.\par \par \uc2 Cathy Weber, a retired farmer and military serviceperson, said she came to see Vance speak to get a better sense of who he is as a politician. When I asked about Vance\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Haitian immigrants, she said she thought \u8220\'20\'1Che misspoke,\u8221\'20\'1D and chalked it up to being a younger politician \u8211\'20\'13 which she viewed as an asset.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s 39,\u8221\'20\'1D said Weber. \u8220\'20\'1CI said to my son: \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s your generation, that\u8217\'20\'19s our future.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Robert Tait reported earlier this month, JD Vance has a history of opposing IVF \u8211\'20\'13 in contradiction to the Republican party and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s current stance that they support it:\par \par \uc2 In 2017, months into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, Vance wrote the foreword to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/2017-index-culture-and-opportunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Index of Culture and Opportunity}}}\uc2 , a collection of essays by conservative authors for \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  that included ideas for encouraging women to have children earlier and promoting a resurgence of \u8220\'20\'1Ctraditional\u8221\'20\'1D family structure.\par \par \uc2 The essays lauded the increase in state laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and included arguments that the practice should become \u8220\'20\'1Cunthinkable\u8221\'20\'1D in the US, a hardline posture the Democrats now say is the agenda of Trump and Vance, who they accuse of harbouring the intent to impose a national ban following a 2022 supreme court ruling overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and annulling the federal right to abort a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The report also includes an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/2017-index-culture-and-opportunity/fading-fertility-ready-or-not"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essay}}}\uc2  lamenting the spread of in vitro fertilisation (IVF) and other fertility treatments, with the author attributing them as reasons for women delaying having children and prioritising higher education rather than starting families.\par \par \uc2 IVF has emerged as an issue in November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential race after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/09/01/republican-senators-trump-ivf-proposal-00176972"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  last week that he favoured it being covered by government funding or private health insurance companies \u8211\'20\'13 a stance seeming at odds with many Republicans, including Vance, who was one of 47 GOP senators to vote against a bill in June intended to expand access to the treatment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/jd-vance-trump-ivf-abortion-heritage-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance endorsed anti-IVF report that contradicts Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new stance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Republicans 'have once again made clear' they won't protect IVF access\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that Senate Republicans refusal to vote in favor of protecting IVF \u8220\'20\'1Cis not an isolated incident\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Every woman in every state must have reproductive freedom. Yet, Republicans in Congress have once again made clear that they will not protect access to the fertility treatments many couples need to fulfill their dream of having a child.\par \par \uc2 Congressional Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 repeated refusal to protect access to IVF is not an isolated incident. Extremist so-called leaders have launched a full-on attack against reproductive freedom across our country. In the more than two years since Roe v Wade was overturned, they have proposed and passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that criminalize doctors and make no exception for rape or incest. They have also blocked legislation to protect the right to contraception and proposed four national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Their opposition to a woman\u8217\'20\'19s freedom to make decisions about her own body is extreme, dangerous and wrong. Our administration will always fight to protect reproductive freedoms, which must include access to IVF. We stand with the majority of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans and Democrats alike \u8211\'20\'13 who support protecting access to fertility treatments. And we continue to call on Congress to finally pass a bill that restores reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, pointed to the failure of the IVF bill today as proof that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 promise to protect access to in vitro fertilization is hollow:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  on IVF vote: "Today Republicans will be called on to answer a very simple question -- do they support Americans family's access to in-vitro fertilization or not." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LQLCzDQpYl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LQLCzDQpYl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1836116339129557198?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , a Republican of South Dakota, called the bill \u8220\'20\'1Can attempt by Democrats to try and create a political issue where there isn\u8217\'20\'19t one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenJohnThune?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenJohnThune}}}\uc2  on IVF vote: "The outcome of that show vote is not going to be any different than it was when we had this same vote three months ago...Republicans support IVF...this is an attempt by Democrats to try and create a political issue where there isn't one." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mk7HFBzt3P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mk7HFBzt3P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1836117512733290517?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Before its convention this year, the Republican party adopted a policy platform that supports states establishing fetal personhood, while also, contradictorily, encouraging support for IVF. But the platform does not explain how IVF could be legally protected if frozen embryos are given the same rights as people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans blocked bill to protect IVF\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans voted to block a bill that would have ensured access to in vitro fertilization nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Every Republican, except \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  of Alaska, voted against the measure. Though a majority of 51 voted in favor, the bill needed 60 votes to pass.\par \par \uc2 Democrats had brought the measure back to the floor after Republicans previously blocked it from advancing in June.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been pushing the issue this year after the Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruled that frozen embryos could be considered children under state law, leading several clinics in the state to suspend IVF treatment.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , have scrambled to counter what could be a deeply unpopular stance against IVF.\par \par \uc2 enltrRepublicans just blocked a bill to protect IVF nationwide. For the second time this year.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s proof positive: Congressional Republicans cannot be trusted when they say they support IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1836132095707541567?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another celebrity endorsement for Harris: Billie Eilish\par \par \uc2 Pop music superstar Billie Eilish along with her brother, producer and musician Finneas O\u8217\'20\'19Connell, have announced their support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a video posted on X, where Eilish has 7.5 million followers, and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , where her followers number 119 million, the siblings say they will vote for Harris because she supports for keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal, and fighting the climate crisis:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s National Voter Registration Day. We are voting for Harris-Walz. The choice is clear. Check your voting status here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZPKcYDR7aF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZPKcYDR7aF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PiFfQpkARW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PiFfQpkARW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 billie eilish (@billieeilish) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/billieeilish/status/1836073476127687112?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 They are the last pop megastars to back the Democratic vice-president, after Taylor Swift announced she would vote for Harris following her debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-harris-endorsement-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s Harris endorsement has thrilled fans \u8211\'20\'13 but will it move the election needle?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier in her conversation with the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked about her message to the young Black voters who polls show are leaning towards voting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because they believe he will provide more economic opportunities.\par \par \uc2 If that dynamic plays out, it could have severe consequences for both Harris and Democrats nationwide, since Black voters have long been a cornerstone voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s very important to not operate from the assumption that Black men are in anybody\u8217\'20\'19s pocket,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris replied. \u8220\'20\'1CBlack men are like any other voting group. You got to earn their vote. So I\u8217\'20\'19m working to earn the vote, not assuming I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have it because I am Black, but because the policies and the perspectives I have understands what we must do to recognize the needs of all communities, and I intend to be a president for all people, specifically as it relates to what we need to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she spoke to Trump after second apparent assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just said she called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  earlier today after the Secret Service on Sunday fended off a gunman discovered outside a golf course where he was playing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI checked on him to see if he was okay, and I told him what I have said publicly, there\u8217\'20\'19s no place for political violence in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am in this election and this race for many reasons, including to fight for our democracy. And in a democracy, there is no place for political violence. We can and should have healthy debates and discussion and disagreements, but not resort to violence to resolve those issues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris also responded \u8220\'20\'1CI do\u8221\'20\'1D, when asked if she had confidence in the Secret Service, then said that rightwing attacks have made groups including migrants and LGBTQ+ people feel unsafe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I feel safe. I have Secret Service protection, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change my perspective on the importance of fighting for the safety of everybody in our country and doing everything we can to again, lift people up and not beat people down so they feel alone and are made to feel small and made to feel like they\u8217\'20\'19re somehow not a part of it or us,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 At that, the conversation wrapped up.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls attacks on Ohio Haitian community 'a crying shame'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has condemned the campaign against the Haitian immigrant community in Springfield, Ohio, waged by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his running mate, JD Vance, and conservative commentators.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a crying shame,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said in her ongoing conversation with Black journalists in Philadelphia. \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart breaks for this community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Without mentioning Trump or Vance, Harris described the baseless allegations that Haitians who moved to the Ohio city were eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets as irresponsible:\par \par \uc2 When you are bestowed with a microphone that is that big, there is a profound responsibility that comes with that. That is an extension of what should not be lost in this moment, this concept of the public trust, to then understand what the public trust means. It means that you have been invested with trust to be responsible in the way you use your words, much less how you conduct yourself, and especially when you have been and then seek to be again president of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 She also decried the wave of threats that have closed schools and other buildings in Springfield, noting the toll it has taken on law enforcement:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a crying shame, literally, what\u8217\'20\'19s happening to those families, those children in that community, not to mention what is happening in terms of, look, you say you care about law enforcement, law enforcement resources being put into this because of these serious threats that are being issued against a community that is living a productive, good life before this happened, and spewing lies that are grounded in tropes that are age old.\par \par \uc2 More on the threats that have disrupted daily life in Springfield for days:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/bomb-threats-springfield-schools-highway-patrol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio city\u8217\'20\'19s schools get extra police as bomb threats follow false Trump claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  defends record on Israel-Gaza war\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was pressed by her interviewers at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  event about what specific changes she would make to US policy towards Israel and its invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the way that we send weapons, in the way that we interact as their ally, are there specific policy changes?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Politico reporter Eugene Daniels, one of three interviewers on the panel.\par \par \uc2 Harris replied:\par \par \uc2 For example, one of the things that we have done that I am entirely supportive of, is the pause that we put on the 2,000lb bombs. And so there is some leverage that we have had and used, but ultimately, the thing that is going to unlock everything else in that region is getting this deal done. And I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to disclose private conversations, but I will tell you, I\u8217\'20\'19ve had direct conversations with the prime minister, with the president of Israel, with Egyptian leaders and with our allies, and I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve made ourselves very clear this deal needs to get done in the best interest of everyone in the region, including getting those hostages out.\par \par \uc2 Washington has supplied many of the bombs used in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s assault on the enclave, but recently blocked a shipment of 2,000lb munitions blamed for strikes that have killed scores of people in Gaza. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/10/biden-resumes-sending-israel-bombs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US to resume sending 500lb bombs to Israel while withholding 2,000lb bombs, official says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris holds live interview with Black journalists\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on stage now in Philadelphia, taking questions from three reporters in a live conservation organized by the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In July, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke at the group\u8217\'20\'19s annual convention, where he said Harris was lying about her racial identity. Here\u8217\'20\'19s our coverage of that infamous moment:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump repeats lies and attacks Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity at panel of Black journalists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance pointing finger at Democrats over Trump assassination attempts 'dangerous' \u8211\'20\'13 White House\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , has condemned as \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D comments made by JD Vance that the difference between Democratic rhetoric and Republican rhetoric in this election is that only \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican party nominee for president \u8211\'20\'13 has been shot at.\par \par \uc2 Vance, the Republican nominee for vice-president, has pointed out on the campaign trail that nobody has tried to assassinate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 nominee for president, only her rival, Trump.\par \par \uc2 Trump was shot at a campaign rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, in July and a man was arrested pointing a rifle through the fence of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf course this last Sunday, as the former president was playing a round.\par \par \uc2 Vance said at a rally in Sparta, Michigan, moments ago that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat\u8217\'20\'19s one-sided is that it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who\u8217\'20\'19s getting shot at\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HowardMortman/status/1835826020730950036"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said}}}\uc2  at a previous event that the difference between the effects of both parties\u8217\'20\'19 rhetoric is that \u8220\'20\'1Cno-one has tried to kill \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the last couple of months\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said at the ongoing press briefing just now: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you are a national leader and you have a community that looks up to your leadership \u8230\'20\'26 and when you have that type of language out there, it\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous \u8230\'20\'26 [and] it opens up an opportunity for people to listen to you and potentially take you very seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"Big difference between conservatives & liberals: No one has tried to kill \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in last couple of months. And 2 people have tried to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last couple months. That's pretty strong evidence left needs to tone down the rhetoric & cut this crap out"\par \par \uc2 - JD Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SzBmmyetAc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SzBmmyetAc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Howard Mortman (@HowardMortman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HowardMortman/status/1835826020730950036?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would travel to New York City next week to attend the \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The press briefing just got under way at the White House. Jean-Pierre made the announcement about the US president at the top of the briefing and will take journalists\u8217\'20\'19 questions shortly.\par \par \uc2 World leaders will descend on the \uc2 UN\uc2  headquarters in New York for the annual gathering.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza will probably be a headline issue at this year\u8217\'20\'19s gathering. The attack on southern Israel lead by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  last 7 October occurred after last fall\u8217\'20\'19s UNGA event.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s counterattack on Gaza, which is controlled by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , has raged since and a lasting ceasefire remains elusive. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/16/israeli-airstrikes-gaza-houthis-netanyahu-gallant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death toll}}}\uc2  among Palestinians has passed 41,000, according to health authorities in the territory.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is covering the latest events in this war and the current news out of Lebanon today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/17/middle-east-crisis-live-netanyahu-expands-gaza-war-aims-blinken-heads-to-egypt#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this live blog}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has called for stepped-up security for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  following two apparent assassination attempts on the former president in the last two months, asking for him to have Secret Service resources equivalent to those afforded to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the sitting US president.\par \par \uc2 Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate on the Republican ticket for this November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, also blamed Democratic party rhetoric criticizing Trump for armed individuals targeting the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats have got to cut this crap out,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He repeatedly criticized \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Democratic party nominee for president, across policy platforms ranging from energy to taxes. She said, after a man was arrested on Sunday after pointing a rifle through the fence at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf course in Florida as the former president was playing a round: \u8220\'20\'1CI will be clear: I condemn political violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked by a journalist if the rhetoric was all one-sided, Vance said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere are absolutely people on our side who say ridiculous things\u8221\'20\'1D, but he added that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat is one-sided\u8221\'20\'1D is that only one person was being targeted by known gunmen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who\u8217\'20\'19s getting shot at,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, reiterating that Democrats should stop talking in tones of eliminating him as a threat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are going to get someone killed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 vice-presidential nominee, JD Vance, is on the campaign trail talking in Sparta, near Grand Rapids in central Michigan, the vital swing state, right now.\par \par \uc2 The White House daily media briefing, with press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , has been moved back to 2pm, from its previous schedule of 1.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Vance is talking about prices, the cost of food, gas, housing, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe number one thing\u8221\'20\'1D the US has to do to get \u8220\'20\'1Cthis crazy inflation\u8221\'20\'1D under control is to have better energy supply from the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDrill, baby, drill,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. He said the US has \u8220\'20\'1Cabundant American energy\u8221\'20\'1D and natural resources that are the envy of other countries.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e9a6a88f08e43e1272b175#block-66e9a6a88f08e43e1272b175"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later this afternoon}}}\uc2  hold a vote on protecting access to IVF care, as they seek to pressure Republicans over the politically volatile topic that will sure to be on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds when they head to the presidential polls in 49 days. Over in the House, the Republican speaker, Mike Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e993748f086ad2b4929a18#block-66e993748f086ad2b4929a18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  for the chamber to vote tomorrow on a spending bill that will prevent a partial government shutdown but be paired with legislation aimed at cracking down on non-citizen voting, which rarely happens. Democrats have come out against the latter part of the bill, with Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  saying today that Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s proposal will likely meet \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e9a10b8f086ad2b4929b14#block-66e9a10b8f086ad2b4929b14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a dead end}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, though that could increase the possibility of a government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e97df68f085fa2473a2bc8#block-66e97df68f085fa2473a2bc8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws supported by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to blame for the death of a Georgia woman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In an interview with popular Spanish radio host Stephanie \u8220\'20\'1CChiquibaby\u8221\'20\'1D Himonidis, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e999e58f08e43e1272b0a0#block-66e999e58f08e43e1272b0a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies would result in the separation of migrant families at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/17/donald-trump-shooting-assassination-attempt-kamala-harris-us-politics-news-latest-updates?page=with:block-66e94b1d8f08f5de71dc27fd#block-66e94b1d8f08f5de71dc27fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery nice\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  when the president called him after the second assassination attempt against him on Sunday, and asked if he had any suggestions for how to improve his security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Tammy Duckworth, a Democrat who conceived her daughters using IVF and sponsored the bill coming up for a vote today to protect the fertility treatment, accused Trump and Vance of \u8220\'20\'1Clying about their records on IVF, and pretending to champion this cause \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the campaign call, Duckworth said Vance\u8217\'20\'19s decision to campaign instead of returning to Washington to vote for her bill was proof that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen given the chance, they\u8217\'20\'19ll never actually do anything to support IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to sit quietly while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance run on a platform that would threaten access to IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause every American deserves their right to be called mommy or daddy without being treated like a criminal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the call, Democratic lawmakers said Americans should not trust \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when he says he does not support an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and noted that he has bragged about appointing the supreme court justices whose votes were decisive to overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is somebody who has started a complete crisis, healthcare crisis for women in this country, and now he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to scramble and somehow, as he always does, say it\u8217\'20\'19s not his fault,\u8221\'20\'1D Michigan senator \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Even if Republicans fail to muster the 60 votes needed to enact a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, she pointed to the conservative blueprint, Project 2025, which was created by former Trump officials and suggests invoking an archaic law to ban the distribution of the pills used in medical abortions. Trump has sought to distance himself from the lengthy policy document.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything that we have seen so far \u8211\'20\'13 the efforts by states that he has supported \u8211\'20\'13 would indicate to us that that\u8217\'20\'19s very much a part of his toolbox,\u8221\'20\'1D Stabenow said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains Harris\u8217\'20\'19s strongest issue, on which she holds a 15-percentage-point advantage over Trump, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/09/08/us/politics/times-siena-poll-toplines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national poll of likely voters by the New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  found. Yet there were some signs Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mixed signals over his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had muddied the waters. According to the survey, nearly half of independent voters say they did not think the former president would sign into law a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has responded with a swing state ad buy highlighting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments bragging about his role overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is to blame for, you know, what we are seeing across this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, the Harris-Walz campaign manager, said on the call.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2 , a Michigan Democrat, said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cscrambling\u8221\'20\'1D to rewrite his position on reproductive rights amid a political backlash and fears that a Republican administration would curtail access to IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no way in the world that I believe that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is serious about this,\u8221\'20\'1D Staebnow said. The former president last month announced plans, without offering any detail, to require the federal government or health insurance companies to cover the cost of fertility treatments, which can be tens of thousands of dollars.\par \par \uc2 Stabenow, on a call organized by the Harris campaign, said Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote was all the more important after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that he is a \u8220\'20\'1Cleader on IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBe great if he was,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the way to find out if he\u8217\'20\'19s serious? Was he on the phone last night, calling our colleagues, urging them to vote yes, just like he was on the phone last weekend, urging the US House to shut the government down, just like he was on the phone telling people to vote against the effective border bill. If he was on the phone last night urging people to vote yes, then I\u8217\'20\'19ll take him seriously.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans are expected to block the procedural measure to open debate on the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 bill to protect IVF. JD Vance, the Ohio senator who voted against the bill earlier this year, is campaigning in the midwest and will miss the vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats are holding a press conference on the st eps of the Capitol, where they are pushing Republicans to allow passage of legislation protecting access to IVF care nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The party holds a majority of 51 seats in the chamber, but most legislation needs at least 60 votes to overcome filibusters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re asking our Republican friends: do you support American families\u8217\'20\'19 access to in vitro fertilization or not?\u8221\'20\'1D the majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said, as he was flanked by lawmakers holding up pictures of families who had children through IVF.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor many Americans, starting a family is one of the greatest joys there is. Yet millions of Americans struggle with the defeating battle of infertility every single year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He accused the GOP of being insincere about protecting access to the care:\par \par \uc2 In Alabama this year, we saw just how vulnerable IVF has become as the next target of ultra conservatives. Since then, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen Republicans tie themselves in knots over their support for IVF, claiming they support access to IVF, support insurance paying for IVF treatments, support helping families pay for IVF. And then when the rubber hits the road, they vote no, because here\u8217\'20\'19s the secret, Republicans want people to think they support IVF because they know how unpopular that position is. They want to keep their true agenda hidden from the public.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats plan vote on bill to protect IVF access, again\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic majority will today try once again to pass legislation protecting access to IVF care nationwide, but Republicans are likely to block its passage.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have seized on the issue every since Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court earlier this year handed down a ruling that cut off most access to the treatment used to start families, until its Republican-controlled legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/alabama-ivf-protection-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a law}}}\uc2  that restored access.\par \par \uc2 In remarks today on the Senate floor, the Democratic majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , warned that IVF remained under threat, and federal legislation was necessary to guarantee access across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, access to IVF can no longer be taken from granted. From the moment the Maga supreme court eliminated Roe, the hard-right made clear that they would keep going. As we saw earlier this year in Alabama, IVF has become the next target of ultra-conservatives, and access to this incredible treatment is more vulnerable than ever,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 He tied the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the bill to Project 2025, the rightwing blueprint to remake the \uc2 US government\uc2  authored by conservatives with ties to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Senate Republicans vote no today, and strike IVF protections down yet again, it will be further proof that Project 2025 is alive and well,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf people want to see how strong Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s grip is on the GOP, the outcome of today\u8217\'20\'19s IVF vote will be very, very revealing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In June, Senate Republicans blocked the Right to IVF act, which Schumer is moving to reconsider today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/right-to-ivf-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans block bill that establishes right to IVF across the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senate leader Schumer says House GOP funding vote will run 'into a dead end'\par \par \uc2 Responding to Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s plan to tomorrow hold a vote on a six-month government funding bill paired with a new federal law against non-citizen voting, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , implied that the proposal would go nowhere in his chamber.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpeaker Johnson is reportedly going to hold a vote on his six-month CR tomorrow, but the only thing that will accomplish is make clear that he\u8217\'20\'19s running into a dead end \u8211\'20\'13 we must have a bipartisan \u8211\'20\'13 a bipartisan \u8211\'20\'13 plan instead,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 The majority leader said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cheartened\u8221\'20\'1D that Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s spending proposal did not contain sweeping budget cuts, but said it was otherwise not acceptable to Democrats. The party opposes the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (Save) Act, which requires people to show proof of citizenship when they register to vote, though Schumer did not name the bill in his remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope it\u8217\'20\'19s a sign that the speaker realizes that these bipartisan funding levels must be part of any solution moving forward. But beyond that, the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s CR [continuing resolution] is too unworkable,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI urge him to drop his current plan, and to work together to reach a bipartisan agreement with the other leaders \u8211\'20\'13 Leader McConnell, Leader Jeffries, and myself, as well as the White House. We do not have time to spare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview Stephanie \u8220\'20\'1CChiquibaby\u8221\'20\'1D Himonidis\u8217\'20\'19s show Nueva Network, the vice-president said Latino voters \u8220\'20\'1Chave the power to determine the outcome of the election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone silence you or tell you your vote doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, a nod to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/latino-voters-are-a-target-for-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressive misinformation campaigns}}}\uc2  targeting Spanish speakers in the United States.\par \par \uc2 She also touted her economic agenda, saying she would expand the child tax credit and called growing small businesses \u8220\'20\'1Cone of my passions\u8221\'20\'1D. She noted the explosion of Latino and Latina-owned small businesses.\par \par \uc2 Harris also emphasized her personal biography as the daughter of immigrants, raised by a working mother. She said her mother \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Ca five-foot tall woman with an accent\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 arrived in the US alone at 19. She raised two daughters while working as a breast cancer researcher.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  answered questions about the economy and immigration on Chiquibaby\u8217\'20\'19s radio show, telling the popular Spanish radio host about the work the Biden administration has done to secure the border but also support immigrants already in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to run on the problem instead of fixing the problem,\u8221\'20\'1D she said about Trump during the interview, which was translated from English into Spanish.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis policies would separate families,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CI have already stood, and will always stand, with the belief that we have to keep families together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson announces vote on government funding bill paired with non-citizen voting ban\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, announced that he would tomorrow hold a vote on legislation to head off a partial government shutdown that would begin 1 October, and ban non-citizens from voting.\par \par \uc2 The proposal is unlikely to become law, since Senate Democrats and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have both said they are opposed to the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (Save) Act, which requires people to show proof of citizenship when they register to vote. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and many Republican lawmakers have nonetheless made the legislation a priority, raising the possibility of a standoff that could bring the government to the brink of a shutdown just weeks before the 5 November presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Johnson said about tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s vote:\par \par \uc2 Congress has an immediate obligation to do two things: responsibly fund the federal government and ensure the security of our elections. Because we owe this to our constituents, we will move forward on Wednesday with a vote on the six-month CR with the Save Act attached. I urge all of my colleagues to do what the overwhelming majority of the people of this country rightfully demand and deserve \u8211\'20\'13 prevent non-American citizens from voting in American elections.\par \par \uc2 The speaker\u8217\'20\'19s announcement is something of an about-face, since just last week, he scrapped a vote on the bill after several Republicans objected:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/republicans-government-spending-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson scraps vote on funding bill after Republicans signal opposition}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her interview with Hispanic radio host Stephanie \u8220\'20\'1CChiquibaby\u8221\'20\'1D Himonidis thus far, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has discussed her background and time as a prosecutor, and her plan to lower inflation.\par \par \uc2 Himonidis posed the questions to the vice-president in Spanish, and she is responding in English, with a Spanish translation of her responses playing on the broadcast simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris sits for interview with Hispanic radio host\par \par \uc2 We expect to hear from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  soon, when an interview conducted yesterday with Hispanic radio host Stephanie \u8220\'20\'1CChiquibaby\u8221\'20\'1D Himonidis airs at 10am.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s second interview this year with Himonidis, and first since she became the Democratic nominee for the president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Also dodging questions about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is JD Vance, his running mate.\par \par \uc2 He has previously said that the former president would not sign such legislation, but in an interview with NBC News over the weekend, Vance\u8217\'20\'19s response to the question amounts to one big \u8220\'20\'1Cno comment\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance claims on Meet the Press that he hasn't actually talked about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Trump and dodges questions about whether Trump would sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UnzeyYaZTh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UnzeyYaZTh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1835321357082456420?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Whether or not he would sign a federal law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one of several questions \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did not directly answer at his debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWould you veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban?\u8221\'20\'1D ABC News moderator Linsey Davis asked Trump.\par \par \uc2 The former president equivocated, saying that such a ban would never pass Congress and implying he preferred the issue be decided by states individually \u8211\'20\'13 which is the case after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not going to get the vote. She can\u8217\'20\'19t get the vote. She won\u8217\'20\'19t even come close to it. So it\u8217\'20\'19s just talk,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is that for years, they wanted to get it out of Congress and out of the federal government, and we did something that everybody said couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be done, and now you have a vote of the people on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Trump's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies to blame for death of mother in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said the policies of her opponent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to blame for the death of a 28-year-old mother in Georgia who was denied lifesaving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care under the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the consequences of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s actions,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement responding to the shocking report in ProPublica.}}}\par \par \uc2 A state medical review committee deemed Thruman\u8217\'20\'19s death \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D, and determined that there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood chance\u8221\'20\'1D she would have survived had she been provided a D&C \u8211\'20\'13 a procedure to remove fetal tissue from inside the uterus \u8211\'20\'13 earlier, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . As reported, Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s last words to her mother before she died were: \u8220\'20\'1CPromise me you\u8217\'20\'19ll take care of my son.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis young mother should be alive, raising her son, and pursuing her dream of attending nursing school,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris, who has made protecting what\u8217\'20\'19s left of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access a prominent feature of her presidential campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly what we feared when Roe was struck down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are bleeding out in parking lots, turned away from emergency rooms, losing their ability to ever have children again. Survivors of rape and incest are being told they cannot make decisions about what happens next to their bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now women are dying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris warned Americans not to trust Trump as he tries to recast himself as a moderate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As president, he appointed three conservative supreme court justices who were decisive in overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 As a candidate, Trump has alternately bragged about his role delivering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes the biggest political victory in a half-century, and complaining that Republican extremism on the issue could cost them the election. He has said he would not sign a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but his position has shifted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gets the chance, he will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and these horrific realities will multiply,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must pass a law to restore reproductive freedom. When I am President of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law. Lives depend on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/09/16/donald-trump-assassination-attempt-mar-a-lago-secret-service/?pwapi_token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..xxJHniVOEWZoHs-uJFfLpYEenAbmnxGsmGl09Jw4Gok&stream=top&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  conservative columnist Marc Thiessen, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reflected on being targeted by two assassins in just under two months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI try not to think about it,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president replied. \u8220\'20\'1CBut people ask me that question a lot, and I try not to think about it. This was different from the first one, but this one in a certain way was, I mean, the gun was even more violent. And the bullets were from Secret Service, and they caught him. They caught him before anything happened. But it would have happened. I mean, he\u8217\'20\'19s somebody that it would have happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then attempted to steer blame for the attempts on his life to the Democrats, who have called Trump a threat to democracy. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s opponents have used that language because of his continued insistence, without evidence, that he won the 2020 election, and his vows to take revenge on his political opponents if returned to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/30/trump-interview-jail-political-opponents-glenn-beck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump vows to lock up political enemies if he returns to White House}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has one public event on his schedule today: a briefing on wildfires at 11.15am ET, which are right now burning swaths of land around southern California.\par \par \uc2 He will later in the day meet behind closed doors with \uc2 World Bank\uc2  president Ajay Banga, and White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will take questions from reporters at 1.30pm. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the fires that continue to burn in the mountains not far from Los Angeles:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/california-wildfires-cooler-weather"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles hit by double whammy of wildfires and earthquake}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2 , a businessman and friend of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who was on the golf course on Sunday when Secret Service agents opened fire on suspected gunman Ryan Wesley Routh, has told NBC News more about what he witnessed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/trumps-golf-partner-recalls-moment-secret-service-dived-assassination-rcna171414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He told}}}\uc2  the network\u8217\'20\'19s Today show:\par \par \uc2 [Trump has] a guy who follows him right behind him, but there\u8217\'20\'19s also people perched next to him. The entire team converged on top of him, except for the snipers. The snipers separated and they came within three yards of me, put the tripods down, and they were aiming right at the spot where the shots had come from.\par \par \uc2 He said he had recognised the \u8220\'20\'1Cpop\u8221\'20\'1D sound as shots right away, and that after the incident Trump checked whether everybody was OK. Witkoff says Trump values the protection officers around him, but added that \u8220\'20\'1Cmistakes could have been made, and in this case, lives could be lost because of such, because of a mistake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Later today \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will participate in a Philadelphia forum organized by the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 . The event has been scheduled after the vice-president did not attend the group\u8217\'20\'19s convention held in Chicago during the summer.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did appear at that event in July \u8211\'20\'13 with a typically contentious performance during which he repeated lies and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity}}}\uc2 . Some journalists were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/nabj-trump-panel-black-journalists-respond"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critical of the organisation for inviting him}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that, as Trump did, Harris will face a panel of three journalists in the session. The location is also significant \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania is often regarded as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmust win\u8221\'20\'1D swing state in order to take the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39am BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Rachel Leingang has this report on misinformation and conspiracy theories that have sprung up in the wake of the apparent attempt to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while he was playing golf at the weekend:\par \par \uc2 As details of his passion for Ukraine have emerged, some on the far right have claimed Routh may have ties within the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US military}}}\uc2 , with some going even further to say the arrested suspect could have been part of a larger plot. There is no evidence to suggest either \u8211\'20\'13 and none of those spreading the rumors have put forth any proof.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are the odds that this shooter, who spent months fighting in Ukraine, has zero links to anyone in US military or intelligence circles?\u8221\'20\'1D Charlie Kirk, founder of Turning Point USA, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/charliekirk11/status/1835452637409620345"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CFind them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Questions surrounding how Routh knew Trump would be golfing that day, given that the round wasn\u8217\'20\'19t on a public schedule, led some to suggest that those tasked with protecting the president could be in on the attempt. The former president praised the Secret Service in the aftermath of the apparent thwarted shooting.\par \par \uc2 Another conspiracy theory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/ryan-routh-donald-trump-assassination-attempt-blackrock-ad-1954344"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  Routh appeared in a video for the investment firm \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 . The video footage circulated along with the claim shows him at a protest in Ukraine, though the video is unaffiliated with the firm, the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BlackRock/status/1835703936226926967"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , adding that Routh \u8220\'20\'1Chas never been an employee of \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  nor has he appeared in any \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  ads\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The theory attempted to tie Routh to Thomas Crooks, the shooter in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first assassination attempt}}}\uc2  against Trump in July, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/thomas-matthew-crooks-blackrock-ad-pulled/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did appear}}}\uc2  in a \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  commercial when he was a student at Bethel Park high school in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/trump-assassination-attempt-conspiracy-theories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Far-right conspiracies abound after second apparent Trump assassination attempt}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/trump-assassination-attempt-conspiracy-theories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Far-right conspiracies abound after second apparent Trump assassination attempt}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris focuses on youth voter turnout on National Voter Registration Day\par \par \uc2 As far as the election campaign is concerned, this week the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  team has its focus on youth turnout to coincide with today\u8217\'20\'19s National Voter Registration Day.\par \par \uc2 In a statement campaign manager Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr \u237\'00\'EDguez said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes this November couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be higher, and vice-president Harris knows our democracy is stronger when we all vote. We are focused on meeting young Americans where they are to drive home the stakes of this election on the issues they care most about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the week Harris\u8217\'20\'19s VP pick \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and Pennsylvania governor Josh Shapiro will be among those campaigning on campus in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Recent polling has shown that Harris has a significant lead over Trump in those all important swing states \u8211\'20\'13 provided people come out to vote. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we vote, we win,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56am BST\par \par \uc2 The charges facing Ryan Wesley Routh after his apparent attempt to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the weekend are possession of a firearm by a convicted felon and possession of a firearm with an obliterated serial number. Yesterday Ronald Rowe Jr, acting director of the Secret Service, confirmed that Routh did not fire any shots, and that he did not have the former president in his line of sight when a Secret Service agent opened fire at him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54am BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has spoken to Beth Celestini, a former Secret Service agent who previously protected President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . She said she had concerns about \u8220\'20\'1Creports that the suspect allegedly was in the bushes for 11 hours,\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Secret Service has protocols where if enacted, this suspect should have been discovered before the incident.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another retired security agent, Ronald Layton, said to the paper that the question for the agency was: \u8220\'20\'1CWas this just luck that you caught this guy, or did you have the appropriate mechanisms in place for these kinds of things on the threat spectrum?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump calls Biden 'very nice' after president's remarks on apparent assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 During his appearance on a social media channel to promote a new cryptocurrency venture, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had some conciliatory words about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s response to an apparent second assassination attempt on Trump in the space of a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Trump said:\par \par \uc2 He was very nice today, he called up to make sure I was OK, to make sure, [and ask] do I have any suggestions. We do need more people on my detail, because we have 50,000, 60,000 people showing up to events, and, you know, other people don\u8217\'20\'19t have that, but he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been nicer.\par \par \uc2 It was in marked contrast to the inflammatory words earlier on Fox News Digital, where he had described Biden and his election opponent \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D. On that occasion Trump said:\par \par \uc2 Their rhetoric is causing me to be shot at, when I am the one who is going to save the country and they are the ones that are destroying the country \u8211\'20\'13 both from the inside and out. These are people that want to destroy our country. It is called the enemy from within. They are the real threat.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Suspicious packages sent to election officials in at least six states on Monday\par \par \uc2 Suspicious packages were sent to election officials in at least six states on Monday, Associated Press reports, but there was no indication that any of the packages ultimately contained hazardous material.\par \par \uc2 Powder-containing packages were sent to secretaries of state and state election offices in Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska, Tennessee, Wyoming and Oklahoma, officials in those states confirmed. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  and \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  were investigating. It marked the second time in the past year that suspicious packages were mailed to election officials in multiple state offices.\par \par \uc2 The packages forced an evacuation in Iowa. A state office building in Topeka, Kansas, was also evacuated due to suspicious mail sent to both the secretary of state and attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Suspicious letters were sent to election offices and government buildings in at least six states last November, including the same building in Kansas that received suspicious mail on Monday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20am BST\par \par \uc2 In his press conference on Monday, the acting director of the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  proposed that the agency needs a radical overhaul in order to meet the challenge of protecting presidents in the current climate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CComing out of Butler [where Trump was shot at in Pennsylvania], I have ordered a paradigm shift. The Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s protective methodologies work and they are sound, and we saw that yesterday. [But] we need to get out of a reactive model, and get to a readiness model,\u8221\'20\'1D Ronald Rowe Jr said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  is among those calling for tighter security around former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . In an editorial overnight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/09/16/trump-secret-service-ryan-routh-shooter-protection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the paper wrote}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Trump is not receiving the level of protection he did when he was president. This needs to change. Fifty days before a neck-and-neck election, after what are now two attempts on his life, Trump ought to get presidential-level coverage. Protecting Trump as he campaigns is as essential a part of ensuring political stability and continuity of government as one could imagine.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in its reporting, the paper says that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s penchant for golf has long been a concern of the security services. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/16/trump-golf-courses-secret-service-protection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Trump aides and Secret Service agents have long worried about his possible exposure while golfing. The issue, they say, is twofold. He selects locations to golf \u8211\'20\'13 his own clubs \u8211\'20\'13 that are particularly difficult to secure. And then he follows a highly predictable routine on any given weekend.\par \par \uc2 Bill Gage, a former Secret Service agent, said the armed man probably didn\u8217\'20\'19t need to do \u8220\'20\'1Cvery sophisticated surveillance\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHe just had to sit and wait for Trump to arrive,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to do a lot of guessing to know where he is going to be, and that gives a bad guy time to prepare,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11am BST\par \par \uc2 During his call on social media yesterday evening, the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also had praise for the witness who led to the identification of suspected gunman Ryan Wesley Routh, who was subsequently arrested on I-95.\par \par \uc2 While promoting a new cryptocurrency business venture, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 The civilian did a phenomenal job. A woman. I mean, who would think \u8230\'20\'26 how many people would have the brainpower to follow him and take pictures of the back of his truck so that they end up getting, and the key was the license. So they got the license, and after they had the license, you know, there\u8217\'20\'19s all sorts of technology where they can literally pinpoint where this truck is. I never knew something like that existed. And they pinpointed him on the highway.\par \par \uc2 It was quite something, but it worked out well and Secret Service did an excellent job, and they have the man behind bars, and hopefully he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be there for a long time. Dangerous person, very, very dangerous person.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recounts events of shooting attempt\par \par \uc2 Here is how the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recounted the events of the weekend while speaking on social media on Monday. He told listeners:\par \par \uc2 I was playing golf with some of my friends, it was on a Sunday morning and very peaceful, very beautiful weather, everything was beautiful, it\u8217\'20\'19s a nice place to be. And all of a sudden we heard shots being fired in the air, and I guess probably four or five, and it sounded like bullets. But what do I know about that? But Secret Service knew immediately it was bullets, and they grabbed me.\par \par \uc2 Everybody just, we got into the carts, and we moved along pretty, pretty good. I was with an agent, and the agent did a fantastic job. There was no question that we were off that course. I would have loved to have sank that last putt, but we decided, let\u8217\'20\'19s get out of here.\par \par \uc2 He started shooting at the barrel, started shooting in the bushes. Could only see the barrel. How good is that? Right? Could only see the barrel. Based on that, he started shooting and ran toward the target and was shooting a lot, I mean, those were the shots we heard. The other one never got a shot off.\par \par \uc2 The acting head of the Secret Service, Ronald Rowe Jr, has confirmed that the suspected gunman, 58-year-old Ryan Wesley Routh, did not fire any shots.\par \par \uc2 Trump was speaking as he launched a new cryptocurrency business, having previous derided cryptocurrencies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/business-57392734"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying in 2021}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin, it just seems like a scam.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Welcome and opening summary \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our rolling coverage of US politics, as the country comes to terms with a second attempted assasination bid aimed at one of the presidential election candidates in the space of a few weeks. Here are the headlines \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The suspect in the second apparent assassination attempt of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in as many months was charged in federal court on Monday morning with two gun-related crimes, as urgent investigations began into how he was able to get so close to the former US president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cellphone records showed Ryan Wesley Routh camped out near the golf course for about 12 hours, with food, before being confronted by a Secret Service agent. Ronald Rowe Jr, the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  acting director, said Routh did not fire any shots.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump added to the already tense atmosphere around the US election campaign by making highly inflammatory remarks, explicitly blaming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for inciting the attack and calling them \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden told reporters on Monday that he did not yet have a full report of the Sunday incident at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida golf course, and was thankful Trump was \u8220\'20\'1COK\u8221\'20\'1D. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no place for political violence or for any violence ever in our country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said the state was launching its own investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240917ek9h00109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
