\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 California Teamsters endorse Harris after national union declines to back any candidate \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Lois Beckett ,Chris Stein, Anna Betts and Amy Sedghi (earlier) \par \uc2 13,896 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par 00:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed. You can find the latest election coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closed, thanks for following along. You can find the latest election coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of today\u8217\'20\'19s key developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reservecut US interest rates for the first time in four years, news that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  greeted as an important positive sign, though Harris said in a statement that prices were still too high.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Several polls today showed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  performing better than Harris. Majorities of Americans view both candidates unfavorably, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3#block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup found}}}\uc2 . The Atlanta Journal-Constitution{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1#block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Trump has a narrow edge with voters in Georgia, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won four years ago. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s weakness in Georgia may be due to lackluster support among both Democratic faithful and Black voters, the Journal-Constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739#block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris announced she will travel to Georgia on Friday, with a focus on the effect of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies on women\u8217\'20\'19s lives. She has cited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica investigation}}}\uc2  that named Georgia resident Anna Nicole Thurman, 28, as the first woman officially confirmed to have died a \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable death\u8221\'20\'1D in the wake of the supreme court overturning the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Georgia lawmakers had made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the simple procedure}}}\uc2  that would have saved Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s life into a felony.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  declined to join other unions in endorsing Harris, releasing internal polling data they said showed a majority of their members supported Trump, but saying they would not endorse either presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Harris has gained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967#block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the endorsement}}}\uc2  of more than 100 Republican former national security officials and lawmakers, who say she is a better choice to manage foreign policy and America\u8217\'20\'19s relationships with its allies and enemies than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual leadership conference in Washington DC, where she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419#block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for mass deportations, and said better border security and sorting out the problem of Dreamers are not mutually exclusive.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reported that, according to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and other federal agencies, Iranian hackers sought to interest President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in information stolen from rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, sending unsolicited emails to people connected to the Democratic president in an effort to interfere in the 2024 election. There is no evidence that any of the recipients responded, officials said, preventing the hacked information from surfacing in the final months of the closely contested election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump responded to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cuts, saying the size of the cut suggested the economy may be in trouble. \u8220\'20\'1CTo cut it by that much, assuming they\u8217\'20\'19re not just playing politics, the economy would be very bad,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters. Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , who was appointed by Trump to lead the Fed, said was meant to show policymakers\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to sustaining a low unemployment rate now that inflation has eased. Powell said the economy remained strong, with many job market indicators like unemployment claims and even the current 4.2% unemployment rate not at worrying levels.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump held an election rally in New York state where he claimed that the planet \u8211\'20\'13 which last year saw the hottest year on record and is likely to do so again this year after the hottest summer on record, is cooling. He also announced that he would turn the 9/11 memorial and museum into a national monument.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump just said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe want a landslide that is very simply too big to rig\u8221\'20\'1D. He has repeatedly, falsely, claimed that his legitimate loss to Biden in 2020 was the result of a rigged process.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  306-232 in the Electoral College in 2020 and had a 4-point margin in the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 Trump is played off to the Opera song Nessun dorma \u8211\'20\'13 yesterday it was gay anthem YMCA \u8211\'20\'13 with its famous words Vincer\u242\'00\'F2. (Think: Vinceeeeeeeeeer\u242\'00\'F2\u242\'00\'F2\u242\'00\'F2\u242\'00\'F2), which means \u8220\'20\'1CI will win\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He has used the very famous, and emotional, aria {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/2016/10/18/let-no-one-sleep/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump just claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe planet\u8217\'20\'19s actually getting cooler\u8221\'20\'1D. It is not.\par \par \uc2 The year is not yet done, but this year already saw the hottest summer on record, and it will more than likely lead to warmest year ever measured, according to experts. Last year was the hottest year on record:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/sep/06/hottest-summer-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hottest summer on record could lead to warmest year ever measured}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump admitted during this rally that he has not read his wife Melania\u8217\'20\'19s memoir.\par \par \uc2 Here is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Arwa Mahdawi on the subject:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/17/melania-trump-memoir-coming-out-acting-pretty-strangely"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania Trump has a memoir coming out \u8211\'20\'13 and she's acting pretty strangely | Arwa Mahdawi}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 In a new Fox news poll, Harris leads Trump by 50%:\par \par \uc2 enltrA new national poll, from Fox News:\par \par \uc2 Harris leads 50% to 48% among both registered and likely voters.\par \par \uc2 Fox\u8217\'20\'19s last poll was in August, & had Trump up 1%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/N74uqY4b56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/N74uqY4b56}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taniel (@Taniel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Taniel/status/1836533440637714754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has just announced that he will turn Ground Zero into a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational monument.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The site of the 11 September attacks is currently a called the \u8220\'20\'1CNational September 11 Memorial & Museum\u8221\'20\'1D. I\u8217\'20\'19m not totally sure what the difference is between that and a national monument, but will find out.\par \par \uc2 In other words, it is unclear if there\u8217\'20\'19s a distinction between what it currently is and what he said he\u8217\'20\'19d turn it into.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will officially make the ground zero site at the world trade centre a national monument so that hallowed ground and the memory of those who perished there will be preserved forever,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, to loud cheers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd has given Trump lively cheers, though at first, when Trump talked disparagingly about immigration, they were more muted.\par \par \uc2 37% of people in New York city were born outside of the United States, and almost half speak a language other than English at home, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nyc.gov/site/internationalbusiness/why-nyc/a-diverse-global-city.page"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NYC.gov}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Immigrants make up more than a fifth of New York state\u8217\'20\'19s population and more than 27% of its work force.\par \par \uc2 Now, however, Trump is getting loud cheers when he makes false and offensive claims about immigrants and their impact on the US and New York. It is almost as though they have become more comfortable booing immigration.\par \par \uc2 Half of New York adults identify as Democrats or Democrat-leaning, 26% as Republicans or Republican-leaning while 18% lean neither way, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religious-landscape-study/database/metro-area/new-york-city-metro-area/party-affiliation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Pew}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is talking about immigration and the border again, again making a series of false and outlandish claims. He again claims that he won more votes in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  306-232 in the Electoral College in 2020 and had a 4-point margin in the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  won the Electoral College with 304 votes compared to 227 votes for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , and Trump lost the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 There are more than 14,000 people seated in the stands at this event, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports, with more on the floor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is complaining about the subway in New York.\par \par \uc2 He has appealed to the audience to vote for him saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat do you have to lose\u8221\'20\'1D and repeating the idea that he is a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump continues his racist rhetoric, saying if Harris wins, \u8220\'20\'1CNew York State will be like a third world country, if it isn\u8217\'20\'19t already. I think it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is talking about the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  now. He says he \u8220\'20\'1Cloves them\u8221\'20\'1D and that they have refused to endorse the democrat candidate \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the first time in many, many decades\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday was the first time the teamsters have not make any election endorsement for the first time since 1996. The union has endorsed every Democratic candidate for president since 2000. Earlier on Wednesday, the union said it would not back a candidate, but that internal polling showed a majority of its members supported Trump.\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  President Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien spoke at the Republican National Convention in July, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecoming the first labor leader to do so and sending shock waves through Democratic circles\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is speaking now in Uniondale, New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo as you know three days ago there was yet another assassination attempt on my life,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, and repeats his false claim that both of the alleged gunmen were \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ryan Wesley Routh, the man suspected of carrying out a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/16/trump-golf-club-shooting-what-we-know-so-far-about-apparent-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second assassination attempt}}}\uc2  on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , has undergone shifting political convictions that elude partisan definition.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/16/ryan-wesley-routh-trump-golf-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Muddled politics and multiple arrests: who is alleged Trump would-be assassin?}}}\par \par \uc2 Although records show the 58-year-old former roofing contractor making small financial donations to Democratic candidates in recent years, Routh has acknowledged voting for Trump in his 2016 election before subsequently embarking on a ideological odyssey the aims of which appear incoherent and confused.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks was killed after firing shots at Trump. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-shooting-suspect-home-town-motive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 His motivation remains unclear}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in New York is now starting at 7.15 PM EDT \u8211\'20\'13 in ten minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time \u8211\'20\'13 according to \uc2 C-Span\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has meanwhile sent out an email noting which of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have endorsed the Democratic candidate, after the national union declined to back a candidate. The Harris campaign said:\par \par \uc2 Today, local \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  unions in the key battleground states of Michigan, Nevada and Wisconsin announced their support for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They join nearly a dozen \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  locals including \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  237 which is the largest in the country, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=7afd4c0372&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Black Caucus of the International Brotherhood of Teamsters}}}\uc2  and several Teamster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.us13.list-manage.com/track/click?u=db6b693f24f8d92d026e0c2d2&id=3e5b055c5f&e=2949ec8050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retirees}}}\uc2 . Collectively, these members represent hundreds of thousands of \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  in critical swing states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  announcing that Iranian hackers sought to interest President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in information stolen from rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, sending unsolicited emails to people connected to the Democratic president in an effort to interfere in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is further proof the Iranians are actively interfering in the election to help \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because they know President Trump will restore his tough sanctions and stand against their reign of terror,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump press secretary Karoline Leavitt said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence that any of the recipients responded, officials said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  called the move a \u8220\'20\'1Crecalibration\u8221\'20\'1D to account for the sharp decline in inflation since last year, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 He noted that the economy remained strong but the central bank wanted to stay ahead of and stave off any weakening in the job market; analysts saw a nod to what has been an overarching aim of his to avoid unnecessarily trading higher unemployment to reach the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s 2% inflation target.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA soft landing is within reach, which would seal his legacy as Fed Chairman,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Diane Swonk\uc2 , the chief economist at \uc2 KPMG\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump responds to interest rate cuts\par \par \uc2 Trump has responded to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cuts, saying the size of the cut suggested the economy may be in trouble.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo cut it by that much, assuming they\u8217\'20\'19re not just playing politics, the economy would be very bad,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , who was appointed by Trump to lead the Fed, said was meant to show policymakers\u8217\'20\'19 commitment to sustaining a low unemployment rate now that inflation has eased.\par \par \uc2 Powell said the economy remained strong, with many job market indicators like unemployment claims and even the current 4.2% unemployment rate not at worrying levels.\par \par \uc2 But he nodded to the same issues economists and analysts raise with inflation: That it takes time for changes in monetary policy to have an impact and that, between anecdotal information from companies and slowed hiring rates, officials felt they needed to preempt further labor market weakness just as others have argued for fast action to preempt inflation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is thinking that the time to support the labor market is when it is strong, and not when you begin to see layoffs,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iranian hackers sought to interest Biden campaign in stolen information, no evidence any recipients responded\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that, according to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and other federal agencies, Iranian hackers sought to interest President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in information stolen from rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, sending unsolicited emails to people connected to the Democratic president in an effort to interfere in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence that any of the recipients responded, officials said, preventing the hacked information from surfacing in the final months of the closely contested election.\par \par \uc2 The hackers sent emails in late June and early July to people who were associated with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign before he dropped out. The emails \u8220\'20\'1Ccontained an excerpt taken from stolen, non-public material from former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as text in the emails,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a \uc2 US government\uc2  statement.\par \par \uc2 The announcement is the latest effort to call out what officials say is Iran\u8217\'20\'19s brazen, ongoing work to interfere in the 2024 election, including a hack-and-leak campaign that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and other federal agencies linked last month to Tehran. The Justice Department has been preparing charges in that breach, The Associated Press has reported.\par \par \uc2 In August, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  researchers said that Iran government-tied hackers tried breaking into the account of a \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-ranking official\u8221\'20\'1D on the US presidential campaign in June, weeks after breaching the account of a county-level US official:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/09/microsoft-reports-iran-hackers-presidential-campaign-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran hackers target US officials to influence election, Microsoft says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump will be at a rally in New York in 45 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time. We will bring you any news from that as it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an updated summary of the day in US politics so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reservecut US interest rates for the first time in four years, news that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  greeted as an important positive sign, though Harris said in a statement that prices were still too high.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Several polls today showed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  performing better than Harris. Majorities of Americans view both candidates unfavorably, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3#block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup found}}}\uc2 . The Atlanta Journal-Constitution{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1#block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Trump has a narrow edge with voters in Georgia, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won four years ago. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s weakness in Georgia may be due to lackluster support among both Democratic faithful and Black voters, the Journal-Constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739#block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris announced she will travel to Georgia on Friday, with a focus on the effect of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies on women\u8217\'20\'19s lives. She has cited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica investigation}}}\uc2  that named Georgia resident Anna Nicole Thurman, 28, as the first woman officially confirmed to have died a \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable death\u8221\'20\'1D in the wake of the supreme court overturning the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Georgia lawmakers had made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the simple procedure}}}\uc2  that would have saved Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s life into a felony.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  declined to join other unions in endorsing Harris, releasing internal polling data they said showed a majority of their members supported Trump, but saying they would not endorse either presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Harris has gained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967#block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the endorsement}}}\uc2  of more than 100 Republican former national security officials and lawmakers, who say she is a better choice to manage foreign policy and America\u8217\'20\'19s relationships with its allies and enemies than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual leadership conference in Washington DC, where she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419#block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for mass deportations, and said better border security and sorting out the problem of Dreamers are not mutually exclusive.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pod Save America host competes on new season of Survivor\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been another very long week (yes, it\u8217\'20\'19s Wednesday) and for the crossover of political podcast lovers and Survivor fans, here\u8217\'20\'19s a tiny bit of fun news: Pod Save America\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jon Lovett\uc2  will be appearing on the forthcoming season of Survivor.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/09/18/us/trump-harris-election#survivor-season-47-jon-lovett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ew.com/jeff-probst-jon-lovett-one-of-greatest-survivor-storytellers-ever-8708378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Entertainment Weekly}}}\uc2  both have previews of Lovett\u8217\'20\'19s participation in the beloved reality TV show. Survivor showrunner Jeff Probst had praise for Lovett, calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the greatest storytellers that we will ever have on Survivor \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lovett\u8217\'20\'19s ability to narrate his own experience \u8220\'20\'1Cis just this beautiful gift to us, because no matter what the situation or how you pose a question, he will give you a compelling answer\u8221\'20\'1D, Probst added.\par \par \uc2 enltr'Survivor' host Jeff Probst says \uc2 Jon Lovett\uc2  is one of the show's greatest storytellers ever, and weighs in on what happens if the podcaster is recognized on the island. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6f5Yehnm5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6f5Yehnm5d}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Entertainment Weekly (@EW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EW/status/1836163264192934076?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 How long Lovett actually survives Survivor, of course, is a different question.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 WSJ: Vance\u8217\'20\'19s team knew on day one \u8216\'20\'18cats and dogs\u8217\'20\'19 story attacking Haitians was false\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal published an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in-depth investigation}}}\uc2  into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance \u8217\'20\'19s baseless slurs about Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 A Springfield city manager told the WSJ that a Vance staffer had called his office to fact-check a claim about Haitian immigrants eating pets the same morning that Vance had tweeted about it. He said he told the staffer, very clearly, that the rumors were not true. But Vance just doubled and tripled down on the story and Trump repeated the lurid claim that night at a presidential debate, sparking ongoing harassment and racist rhetoric, fear among Haitians in Ohio for their personal safety, and eventually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/bomb-threats-springfield-schools-highway-patrol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bomb threats targeting schools, hospitals and government buildings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1C.. He asked point-blank, \u8216\'20\'18Are the rumors true of pets being taken and eaten?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D recalled Heck. \u8220\'20\'1CI told him no... I told them these claims were baseless.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy then, Vance had already posted about the rumors to his 1.9 million followers..\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WSJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ohio?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ohio}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vNdrubYnCu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vNdrubYnCu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Zx7p7FuH7a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Zx7p7FuH7a}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carl Quintanilla (@carlquintanilla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/carlquintanilla/status/1836362499911811393?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The WSJ also dug into the sources of the grotesque rumor targeting immigrants and found that locals who had shared these kinds of claims had already apologized for doing so.\par \par \uc2 enltrA Vance spokesperson provided the WSJ with a police report in which a resident claimed her pet might have been taken by her Haitian neighbors.\par \par \uc2 The cat was later found safe in the resident's own basement. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/f8YFLS83aF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/f8YFLS83aF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lvIBW1QYqy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lvIBW1QYqy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 philip lewis (@Phil_Lewis_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Lewis_/status/1836406434562523582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Vance himself has not apologized, either for spreading the baseless story in the first place or for the story\u8217\'20\'19s frightening and destabilizing consequences for people in Springfield.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I have to create stories so the American media actually pays attention to the suffering of the American people, than that\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told CNN anchor Dana Bash earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Axios summarized Vance\u8217\'20\'19s response as embracing a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/18/jd-vance-pet-eating-ohio-debunked?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiospm&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 zero-shame strategy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fact checking Trump and Vance\u8217\'20\'19s claims about that $35 insulin co-payment cap\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/09/18/us/trump-harris-election/fbdd430e-f3aa-5caf-8bb2-5aa64acb7052?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  that at a campaign rally today, JD Vance once again repeated the \u8220\'20\'1Cmisleading claim\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was responsible for capping insulin Medicare co-payments at $35. In fact, the Times reported, Vance is attempting to campaign on an achievement of the Biden administration, which capped Medicare insulin payments at $35 as part of the 2022 Inflation Reduction Act.\par \par \uc2 Under the Trump administration, some Medicare plans voluntarily participated in a program that capped insulin co-payments at $35, but it was the Biden administration which instituted the cost cap more broadly.\par \par \uc2 Confused? KFF Health News, an independent non-profit that covers US health policy, has a very helpful explainer, including their estimate that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/policy-watch/the-facts-about-the-35-insulin-copay-cap-in-medicare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 800,000 Americans}}}\uc2  had access to the $35 cost cap under the Trump policy, but more than 3.3 million had access under the broader Biden policy.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs both the Trump and Biden campaigns claim credit for capping insulin copayments at $35, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KFFHealthNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KFFHealthNews}}}\uc2  has a very helpful explainer of who *actually* did what: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A4w4BJQUvx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/A4w4BJQUvx}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FWtEnk6VGQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FWtEnk6VGQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lois Beckett (@loisbeckett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/loisbeckett/status/1836504927260364934?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The bigger context is also crucial: KFF Health News notes that senate Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/policy-watch/the-facts-about-the-35-insulin-copay-cap-in-medicare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed a full repeal }}}\uc2  of the Inflation Reduction Act, which would roll back the $35 insulin co-pay cap for those millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Biden and the Democratic party have proposed extending the $35 co-pay cap to all people who need insulin, including those with commercial insurance. This would result in cost savings for the vast majority of Americans who need insulin, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/policy-watch/the-facts-about-the-35-insulin-copay-cap-in-medicare/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KFF\u8217\'20\'19s analysis}}}\uc2 . Democrats tried to include that broader co-pay cap in the Inflation Reduction Act, the news organization reported, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut that provision was stripped from the final legislation after the vast majority of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/republicans-block-cap-insulin-costs-many-americans-democratic-deal-rcna41913"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans voted}}}\uc2  to remove it \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 California Teamsters endorse Harris\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 general executive board announced earlier today that the union, which represents over 1.3 million workers, would make no endorsement in the presidential race, they also released polling data that they said showed that a majority of their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/election-teamsters-endorsement-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union members favored Donald Trump.}}}\par \par \uc2 But other organizations of \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have said they will endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , including the California Teamsters.\par \par \uc2 enltrCalifornia \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are proud to endorse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Tim_Walz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zZGC3kmSxu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zZGC3kmSxu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 California Teamsters Public Affairs Council (@CalTeamstersPAC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CalTeamstersPAC/status/1836487069855592760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More on the political divisions within the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  from Guardian labor reporter Michael Sainato:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/election-teamsters-endorsement-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters decline to endorse election candidate \u8211\'20\'13 but claim majority backs Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will address Fed\u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cut on Thursday\par \par \uc2 This is Lois Beckett, picking up our live US politics coverage from Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tweeted that he will address Americans on Thursday on the state of the economy, in the wake of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it was cutting interest rates for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe just reached an important moment: Inflation and interest rates are falling while the economy remains strong.\par \par \uc2 The critics said it couldn\u8217\'20\'19t happen \u8211\'20\'13 but our policies are lowering costs and creating jobs.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll speak tomorrow about what this means for Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1836487370562052371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also put out a statement in response to the announcement, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcome news\u8221\'20\'1D for Americans, but saying more work was needed to bring prices down, which she called an important focus of her presidential campaign:\par \par \uc2 While this announcement is welcome news for Americans who have borne the brunt of high prices, my focus is on the work ahead to keep bringing prices down. I know prices are still too high for many middle class and working families, and my top priority as president will be to lower the costs of everyday needs like health care, housing, and groceries. That is why I am proposing plans to cut taxes for more than 100 million working and middle-class Americans, pass the first-ever federal ban on corporate price gouging on food and groceries, and make housing more affordable by building 3 million new homes and giving more Americans down payment assistance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris announces Georgia visit amid furor over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related death\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will travel to Georgia on Friday to highlight the importance of keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accessible, her campaign announced, after a report emerged earlier this week of a pregnant woman who died after being denied timely medical care due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Cwill speak about reproductive freedom and how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, which has led to Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country, including in Georgia,\u8221\'20\'1D according to her campaign.\par \par \uc2 It cited \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reporting on Amber Nicole Thurman, a Georgia medical assistant who died in 2022 in what the outlet described as the first \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related death since Roe v Wade as overturned that year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president will highlight the stark contrast between her commitment to fight for reproductive freedom and the devastating and deadly consequences of Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bans,\u8221\'20\'1D her campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Harris will also hold a previously scheduled campaign event in Madison, Wisconsin on Friday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris blames Trump for Georgia \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related death: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s what we feared\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  is one of the few major labor unions not to back \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After taking over from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 presidential candidate in July, Harris quickly picked up endorsements from labor organizations, including the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  and the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 . But despite endorsing Biden in 2020, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  held out, and their just-announced decision to stay out of the race robs the vice-president of support that could have helped her gain the edge in what polls currently show is a very close contest against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the wave of enthusiasm from organized labor that greeted Harris in July, when she threw her hat into the ring:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/labor-unions-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unions rally round Harris as Trump makes populist appeal to workers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  made no endorsement in the presidential race, the Trump campaign is nonetheless claiming victory because the polls of the union\u8217\'20\'19s rank and file show that the ex-president is their preferred candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the executive board of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  is making no formal endorsement, the vast majority of rank-and-file working men and women in this important organization want President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D his campaign said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Left unsaid is the fact that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who struggled to overtake Trump in public polling throughout the entirety of his aborted bid for a second term, was the pick of \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  members when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eb20698f08c4c724a40534#block-66eb20698f08c4c724a40534"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the survey was first conducted}}}\uc2  earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  say they will not make endorsement in presidential election\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  leadership says they will not endorse a candidate in the presidential election, after backing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 and being courted by both \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 The union, America\u8217\'20\'19s largest, said its general executive board determined neither candidate would address the issues its members care about.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  thank all candidates for meeting with members face-to-face during our unprecedented roundtables,\u8221\'20\'1D president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, neither major candidate was able to make serious commitments to our union to ensure the interests of working people are always put before Big Business. We sought commitments from both Trump and Harris not to interfere in critical union campaigns or core \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  industries - and to honor our members\u8217\'20\'19 right to strike - but were unable to secure those pledges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union noted that its own polling of members found \u8220\'20\'1Cno majority support for vice-president Harris and no universal support among the membership for president Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  polling data shows rank and file support Trump ahead of endorsement announcement\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  released polling data of its members this afternoon that showed its members supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by a large margin over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and said the union\u8217\'20\'19s leaders will announce its endorsement for president later today:\par \par \uc2 enltrTEAMSTERS RELEASE PRESIDENTIAL ENDORSEMENT POLLING DATA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the past year, the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2  has pledged to conduct the most inclusive, democratic, and transparent Presidential endorsement process in the history of our 121-year-old organization\u8212\'20\'14and today we are delivering on\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CnFNN9uosx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CnFNN9uosx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  (@Teamsters) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Teamsters/status/1836463348269092918?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Organized labor, including the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , have typically backed Democrats, but this year, the union, which is the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest, has held off endorsing a presidential candidate. President Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien spoke at the Republican national convention in July, infuriating some members of the rank-and-file, while the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/16/us/politics/teamsters-harris.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier this week that Harris had met with O\u8217\'20\'19Brien in what was described as a meeting that grew tense over how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had handled a potential railway strike and a dispute between the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and UPS.\par \par \uc2 While the Teamster\u8217\'20\'19s straw poll shows Harris is unpopular with its members, Biden was preferred over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when the survey was taken earlier this year. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the tensions within the union over O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\u8217\'20\'19s overtures to Trump:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/teamsters-sean-obrien-rnc-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters social media attacks leader over Republican convention speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is scheduled to join a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://events.democrats.org/event/698345/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtual organizing call }}}\uc2  on Wednesday afternoon, intended to rally young voters.\par \par \uc2 The event will feature Harris, as well as Tennessee state representative Justin J Pearson and actor and producer Chlo\u235\'00\'EB Grace Moretz.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 During a campaign event for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday, the Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  took a swipe at vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for not having biological children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo my kids keep me humble,\u8221\'20\'1D Huckabee Sanders said, adding \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything keeping her humble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSarah Huckabee Sanders starts the Trump town hall by taking a shot at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for not having biological children.\par \par \uc2 "So, my kids keep me humble. Unfortunately, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn't have anything keeping her humble." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/URV9FZBqhv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/URV9FZBqhv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 American Bridge 21st Century (@American_Bridge) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/American_Bridge/status/1836179313789476937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Though Harris does not have biological children, she has two stepchildren through her marriage to her husband, Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 In response to Huckabee Sanders\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on Tuesday, Kerstin Emhoff, who is the ex-wife of the second gentlemen, reposted the video of Huckabee Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/keprettybird/status/1836197526653014297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on X,}}}\uc2  and added the caption: \u8220\'20\'1CCole and Ella keep us inspired to make the world a better place. I do it through storytelling. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has spent her entire career working for the people, ALL families. That keeps you pretty humble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/ajc-poll-finds-kamala-harris-and-donald-trump-are-locked-in-a-tight-race-in-georgia/C5CQ6742V5AHVIDUVQ77LQ7YMY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll }}}\uc2  conducted by the Atlanta Journal-Constitution and released on Wednesday shows a tight race in the state of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The results show that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  received 47% of the support among registered voters in Georgia, compared with 44% for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrAJC POLL: Presidential election\par \par \uc2 The race has tightened since the AJC\u8217\'20\'19s June poll, when Trump held a 5-point lead over President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , with 8% of voters undecided. More: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TvFl6t2isu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/TvFl6t2isu}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3MdLotTstG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3MdLotTstG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Atlanta Journal-Constitution (@ajc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ajc/status/1836403394719654330?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday afternoon, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/harris-to-promote-abortion-rights-in-atlanta-friday-after-reports-of-2-deaths-linked-to-state-abortion-limits/5XWO3DHUGFHDXBFFICKAFC42Z4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal-Constitution}}}\uc2  also reported a Harris campaign official has said that the Democratic nominee will be traveling to Atlanta, Georgia on Friday in an appearance focusing on reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  cuts interest rates by half a point\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has announced it is cutting rates by a half point, bringing them down to between 4.75% and 5%.\par \par \uc2 This marks the first time in four years that the Fed has cut interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The Fed chair \uc2 Jay Powell\uc2  is expected to hold a press conference about the rate cut at 2.30pm ET.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/09/archive-zip/giv-134251DUDecQpxJQK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/sep/18/us-interest-rate-decision-federal-reserve-uk-infation-cost-of-living-bank-of-england-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fed cuts US interest rates by half a percentage point \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders of Vermont announced on Wednesday that he is preparing to file resolutions that would block the sale of offensive US weaponry to Israel. This comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/israel-gaza-20-billion-weapons-us-aid-b6a99129c88a5dcc4a4753e20b5e19ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last month}}}\uc2  the Biden administration approved $20bn in arms sales to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Sanders said in a statement that after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacked Israel on 7 October, killing around 1,200 people and kidnapping 250 others, Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cof course, had the right to defend itself against \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt did not, however, have the right to wage an all-out war against the Palestinian people, which is what prime minister Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s extremist government has done\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 Since October of last year, more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/17/gaza-publishes-identities-of-34344-palestinians-killed-in-war-with-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 41,000 Palestinians }}}\uc2  have been killed by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing attacks in Gaza, according to the Gaza health ministry.\par \par \uc2 Sanders continued:\par \par \uc2 Sadly, and illegally, much of the carnage in Gaza has been carried out with U.S.-provided military equipment. Providing more offensive weapons to continue this disastrous war would violate U.S. and international law.\par \par \uc2 The sales would reward Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s extremist government, even as it continues to cause massive destruction in Gaza, undermine the prospects of a ceasefire deal that would secure the release of the hostages, and advance its effort to illegally annex the West Bank.\par \par \uc2 Congress must act to save lives, uphold U.S. and international law, and stand up for U.S. interests. We must end our complicity in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s illegal and indiscriminate military campaign, which has caused mass civilian death and suffering.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 New poll shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pennsylvania and Michigan, close race in Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3905"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  released by \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in two key battleground states and just slightly ahead of Trump in Wisconsin, another battleground state.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, the poll states that 51% of likely voters said they supported Harris, compared with 45% for Trump, a six-point difference. In Michigan, Harris leads Trump by five points in this poll, and in Wisconsin Harris leads Trump by just one percentage point.\par \par \uc2 The new poll was published on Wednesday, just over a week after the 2024 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-presidential-debate-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential debate}}}\uc2 , and with less than 50 days to go until the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has gained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967#block-66ead71c8f085fa2473a3967"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the endorsement}}}\uc2  of more than 100 Republican former national security officials and lawmakers, who say she is a better choice to manage foreign policy and America\u8217\'20\'19s relationships with its allies and enemies than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But several new polls show voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t quite so sure about the two candidates. Majorities of Americans view both candidates unfavorably, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3#block-66eacd578f086ad2b492a5c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup found}}}\uc2 , while in Georgia, the Atlanta Journal-Constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1#block-66eaddec8f086ad2b492a6d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Trump has a narrow edge with voters in the swing state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won four years ago. Harris just finished speaking at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual leadership conference in Washington DC, where she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419#block-66eb07d28f08c4c724a40419"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for mass deportations, and said better border security and sorting out the problem of Dreamers are not mutually exclusive.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s weakness in Georgia may be due to lackluster support among both Democratic faithful and Black voters, the Journal-Constitution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739#block-66eae24d8f086ad2b492a739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House will vote today on a government funding bill that also cracks down on non-citizens casting ballots, but the legislation is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eaf1888f0860cc21944c74#block-66eaf1888f0860cc21944c74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not expected}}}\uc2  to pass.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/18/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66eaf9978f08893ca2b39def#block-66eaf9978f08893ca2b39def"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  the GOP for blocking legislation to protect IVF access nationwide, and linked their opposition to Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris just wrapped up her speech, but before she did, she made the case that restoring reproductive freedom was a concern of Hispanic voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, 40% of Latinas in America live in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 She then described how difficult it could be for a pregnant woman to travel out-of-state to seek care:\par \par \uc2 So, imagine if she is a working woman \u8211\'20\'13 understand that the majority of women who seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care are mothers, understand what that means for her. So, she\u8217\'20\'19s got to now travel to another state. God help her that she has some extra money to pay for that plane ticket. She\u8217\'20\'19s got to figure out what to do with her kids. God help her if she has affordable childcare. Imagine what that means. She has to leave her home to go to a airport, stand in a TSA line.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Go through the details. So, she\u8217\'20\'19s got to stand in the TSA line to get on a plane, sitting next to a perfect stranger, going to a city where she\u8217\'20\'19s never been to go and receive a medical procedure. She\u8217\'20\'19s going to have to get right back to the airport, because she got to get back to those kids, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not like her best friend can go with her, because the best friend is probably taking care of the kids, all because these people have decided they\u8217\'20\'19re in a better position to tell her what\u8217\'20\'19s in her best interest than she is to know.\par \par \uc2 Harris then argued that support for reproductive freedom does not necessarily clash with religious beliefs against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just simply wrong, and I think we all know one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do if she chooses. If she chooses, she will talk with her priest, her pastor, her rabbi, her imam, but not the government telling her what to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris condemns Trump over plans for mass deportations\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has shifted to immigration, hitting out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his promise to carry out mass deportations if elected, while insisting that border security and sorting out the status of undocumented people brought to the country as children are not mutually exclusive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we fight to move our nation forward to a brighter future, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his extremist allies will keep trying to pull us backward,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe all remember what they did to tear families apart, and now they have pledged to carry out the largest deportation, a mass deportation, in American history. Imagine what that would look like and what that would be. How\u8217\'20\'19s that going to happen? Massive raids, massive detention camps. What are they talking about?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris also mentioned Dreamers, as undocumented people who grew up in the United States are known, and improving border security, which an increasing number of Democrats are demanding:\par \par \uc2 We must also reform our broken immigration system and protect our Dreamers. And, understand, we can do both \u8211\'20\'13 create an earned pathway to citizenship and ensure our border is secure. We can do both, and we must do both.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris began her remarks with a staple of her stump speeches: her background as a prosecutor in the Bay Area of northern California, which she said was informed by her mother\u8217\'20\'19s quest to cure breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 Shyamala Gopalan Harris, a biomedical scientist, \u8220\'20\'1Chad two goals in her life, to raise her two daughters, my sister, Maya and me, and to end breast cancer,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was a breast cancer researcher, and growing up, our mother taught us certain fundamental values, the importance of hard work, the power of community, and the responsibility that we have to not complain about anything, much less injustice, right? Because, why are you complaining about it? She would say, do something about it,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 Harris continued:\par \par \uc2 Part of the background on why I became a prosecutor was actually when I was in high school, I learned that my best friend was being abused, being molested by her stepfather, and when I learned about it, I told her she had to come live with us. And I called my mother, and my mother said, of course she does, and she did.\par \par \uc2 And so I decided I wanted to start a career and do the work of \u8230\'20\'26 making sure that we protect the most vulnerable. And so I started my career as a courtroom prosecutor and took on those who would be predators against the most vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now giving remarks at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual leadership conference in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s about 30 minutes late to starting the event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 This evening, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will rally in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Long Island, a state home to several House districts that will determine whether the GOP retains control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this morning, a social media account reported that police securing the Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum in Uniondale, where Trump will speak, had found an explosive device. But the county police department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NassauCountyPD/status/1836424612214636876"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on X}}}\uc2  that report is not correct, though it had detained for questioning one person \u8220\'20\'1Cwho may have been training a bomb detection dog near the site\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to speak at Latino leadership institute conference\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to soon deliver remarks at the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual leadership conference in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 She will undoubtedly mark Hispanic Heritage Month, which began on Sunday, and make the case for why Latino voters should support her in the November election.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the vice-president has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democratic leader Schumer hits GOP for again blocking bill to protect IVF access\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Senate Democrats tried for the second time to pass legislation protecting access to IVF care nationwide, in reaction to an Alabama supreme court ruling earlier this year that temporarily cut off access to the procedure in the state.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans stood in the bill\u8217\'20\'19s way, voting almost unanimously to keep it from clearing the 60-vote threshold needed for passage.\par \par \uc2 In remarks on the Senate floor today, the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s votes were a harbinger of what would come if Project 2025, the rightwing blueprint to remake the \uc2 US government\uc2  authored by conservatives connected to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was implemented. Pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups fear the plan\u8217\'20\'19s proposals to curb access to the procedure could also be used against IVF:\par \par \uc2 Yesterday was a sad day in the Senate as Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 for the second time this year \u8211\'20\'13 blocked legislation to protect families\u8217\'20\'19 access to IVF.\par \par \uc2 By voting against IVF, Republicans confirmed many Americans\u8217\'20\'19 worst fear: Project 2025 is alive and well when it comes to reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have spent months tying themselves into knots claiming that of course they are in favor of protecting IVF.\par \par \uc2 But when it mattered most \u8211\'20\'13 when it came time to actually vote \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans showed their true colors and voted no.\par \par \uc2 And what made yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s vote even worse was that was the second time they\u8217\'20\'19ve blocked IVF protections, even though it\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly clear many Americans are worried about access.\par \par \uc2 Both times, without hesitation, Senate Republicans caved to the extremists on their right flank.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the effort by Democrats to protect IVF access:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/senate-vote-ivf-bill-democrats-republicans-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans block bill to ensure IVF access for second time}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over in the Senate, Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  continued to press House Republicans to approve spending legislation, known as a continuing resolution (CR) that has the support of both parties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the last two weeks, Speaker Johnson and House Republican leaders have wasted precious time on a proposal that everyone knows can\u8217\'20\'19t become law. His own Republican Conference cannot unite around his proposal. Today, the House is expected to vote on the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s CR, and it is expected to fail,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said, in remarks on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that once the Speaker\u8217\'20\'19s CR fails he moves on to a strategy that will actually work: bipartisan cooperation. It\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing that has kept the government open every time we have faced a funding deadline. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the only thing that works this time too. Bipartisan, bicameral cooperation. That\u8217\'20\'19s what works. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re willing and happy to do. And the clock is ticking. If Republicans keep squabbling and careen us into a shutdown, the consequences will reverberate across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are expected to vote against the government funding bill that is paired with legislation intended to keep non-citizens from voting.\par \par \uc2 Even if the legislation does pass, the White House said it \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly opposes\u8221\'20\'1D the Save act, which requires people to prove citizenship when registering to vote.\par \par \uc2 But a perhaps more significant question is whether Republican House speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s push even has the requisite support of his own party. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/91824-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Punchbowl News suggests}}}\uc2  it does not:\par \par \uc2 The House is set to vote today on a short-term funding bill that won\u8217\'20\'19t pass. GOP lawmakers are grumbling about messaging, strategy and yearning to get back home to run for reelection. And Speaker Mike Johnson is being publicly and privately cagey about his next move, frustrating the entire House Republican Conference, which is looking for guidance about the leadership\u8217\'20\'19s plans.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the GOP leadership is even in the dark at most times as to what Johnson is thinking and planning.\par \par \uc2 Johnson is putting a bill on the floor that his entire leadership team \u8212\'20\'14 Majority Leader Steve Scalise of Louisiana and \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  of Minnesota \u8212\'20\'14 knows is going to fail. One House Republican lawmaker entered a meeting of GOP whips Tuesday and told us that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to see how well they\u8217\'20\'19re polishing this turd.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In theory, the impending failure of the six-month stopgap funding bill coupled with the SAVE Act will lead House Republicans toward accepting a clean CR. Johnson can then tell hardline conservatives that he has no other option.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19ll fail, then we\u8217\'20\'19ll go back and do something that\u8217\'20\'19s to the end of the year clean,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rep. Mark Amodei (R-Nev.), a senior House appropriator. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s just reality. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been through this drill enough times to know that nobody\u8217\'20\'19s come up with a silver bullet to put somebody in a chokehold \u8216\'20\'18till they scream, \u8216\'20\'18Uncle.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson vows to press on with spending bill tied to non-citizen voting ban\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker of the House of Representatives, this morning elaborated on his plan to hold a vote on a government funding bill linked to legislation that would require people to prove their citizenship before registering to vote.\par \par \uc2 Congress is scrambling to authorize new spending to ward off a partial government shutdown that could begin 1 October, but Johnson has insisted on pairing a funding bill with the legislation intended to crack down on non-citizens casting ballots, even though that rarely happens.\par \par \uc2 Johnson has scheduled for today a vote in the House on the controversial package, told Fox News this about his intentions in an interview this morning:\par \par \uc2 Listen, Congress has an immediate obligation to do two very important things. We have to keep the government funded, and we need to make sure that our elections are secure. And we have a vehicle today to do both things, because we owe that to the American people and because they demand it. We\u8217\'20\'19re moving legislation today to have a continuing resolution to keep the government going for six months and to make sure that illegals cannot vote, noncitizens cannot vote in the upcoming election. It\u8217\'20\'19s a number one issue around the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just Georgia where Black voters have grown skeptical of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Polls taken throughout this year showed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  struggling with the group, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has made winning their support a priority. In a conversation organized by the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  yesterday, the vice-president was asked about her strategy, specifically as it pertained to men. She replied:\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very important to not operate from the assumption that Black men are in anybody\u8217\'20\'19s pocket. Black men are like any other voting group \u8211\'20\'13 you gotta earn the vote. So I am working to earn the vote, and not assuming I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have it because I am Black, but because the policies and perspectives I have understand what we must do to recognize the needs for all communities.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 One reason why \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  may be trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Georgia? Weakness with Black voters.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/ajc-poll-finds-kamala-harris-and-donald-trump-are-locked-in-a-tight-race-in-georgia/C5CQ6742V5AHVIDUVQ77LQ7YMY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal-Constitution poll}}}\uc2  of the state finds that the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s support among the group \u8211\'20\'13 a key part of the Democratic constituency \u8211\'20\'13 is not where it should be, and that Harris also has not rallied enough of her party\u8217\'20\'19s voters overall.\par \par \uc2 Harris has the support of 86% of Democrats, and 77% of Black voters, which the Journal-Constitution said is 10 percentage points below her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s goals. If there\u8217\'20\'19s a silver lining here for Harris, it\u8217\'20\'19s that about 12% of Black voters say they have not made up their minds.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump leads Harris in swing state Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 poll\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a lead over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in swing state Georgia, a new poll finds, raising questions about the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s ability to repeat the victory \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pulled off there four years ago.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s triumph in 2020 was the first time since 1992 that Georgia had supported a Democratic presidential candidate, but prior to his departure from the presidential race in July, polls of the state had generally shown Trump with the advantage in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 That trend continues under Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/ajc-poll-finds-kamala-harris-and-donald-trump-are-locked-in-a-tight-race-in-georgia/C5CQ6742V5AHVIDUVQ77LQ7YMY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution found}}}\uc2  in its data released this morning, although the gap between Trump and Harris is not as big as it was with Biden on the ballot. Trump leads with 47% support, compared to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 44%. In June, Trump had a five-percentage-point lead against Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 100 Republican former national security officials, congressional lawmakers endorse Harris\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rbmralumni4harris.substack.com/p/over-100-republican-national-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an open letter}}}\uc2 , a group of more than 100 Republican former national security officials and House and Senate lawmakers have endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  cannot be trusted to manage threats and the United State\u8217\'20\'19s relationships with allies and adversaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect to disagree with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on many domestic and foreign policy issues, but we believe that she possesses the essential qualities to serve as president and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not. We therefore support her election to be president,\u8221\'20\'1D the group writes, adding that, \u8220\'20\'1CWe firmly oppose the election of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They write that the former president \u8220\'20\'1Cpromoted daily chaos in government, praised our enemies and undermined our allies, politicized the military and disparaged our veterans, prioritized his personal interest above American interests, and betrayed our values, democracy, and this country\u8217\'20\'19s founding documents.\u8221\'20\'1D They also say Trump has shown he is susceptible to manipulation by foreign rivals like Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and China\u8217\'20\'19s Xi Jinping.\par \par \uc2 The letter continues:\par \par \uc2 We appreciate that many Republicans prefer \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , for a variety of reasons. We recognize and do not disparage their potential concerns, including about some of the positions advocated by the left wing of the Democratic party. But any potential concerns pale in comparison to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s demonstrated chaotic and unethical behavior and disregard for our Republic\u8217\'20\'19s time-tested principles of constitutional governance. His unpredictable nature is not the negotiating virtue he extols. To the contrary, in matters of national security, his demeanor invites equally erratic behavior from our adversaries, which irresponsibly threatens reckless and dangerous global consequences.\par \par \uc2 The signatories stretch from recent government veterans all the way back to officials who served under \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . The group includes former congressman and January 6 committee member \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  and \uc2 Chuck Hagel\uc2 , a former senator who served as defense secretary under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 John Negroponte, a director of national intelligence for \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , signed, as did Eliot A Cohen, a co-founder of the neoconservative Project for the New American Century, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2003/feb/23/usa.iraq1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was influential}}}\uc2  in laying the groundwork for Bush\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Iraq. Also on the letter is Chester Crocker, who served as assistant secretary of state for African affairs under Reagan, and was a key figure in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with South Africa and its neighbors during the volatile years that preceded the end of Apartheid.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to read that \uc2 Chuck Hagel\uc2  served under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another poll released today showed a majority of Americans would support mass deportations of undocumented immigrants, something \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has suggested doing in a second term.\par \par \uc2 Vows to crack down on undocumented migrants are a major plank of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, and at the Republican national convention in Wisconsin two months ago, attendees at one point were given signs reading, \u8220\'20\'1CMass deportation now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ewscripps.brightspotcdn.com/76/25/c50efe0b45bf80f50cbbb6ed38a7/scripps-news-ipsos-poll.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scripps News/Ipsos survey}}}\uc2  released today finds that 54% of those polled would support mass deportations, while 42% would be opposed to it.\par \par \uc2 However, the poll found that 68% of those surveyed would be ok with creating a pathway to citizenship for undocumented people brought to the United States as children. Enacting such a policy has eluded Congress for years:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/04/dreamers-daca-program-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I can\u8217\'20\'19t plan ahead\u8217\'20\'19: Dreamers speak out as US program faces new threat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Majorities of Americans hold unfavorable views of Trump and Harris \u8211\'20\'13 poll\par \par \uc2 With all this talk of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , one would think that they are popular with Americans. A new survey indicates otherwise.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/650774/favorable-ratings-harris-trump-remain.aspx?utm_source=alert&utm_medium=email&utm_content=morelink&utm_campaign=syndication"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup released data}}}\uc2  this morning showing that more people view both the Democratic vice-president and Republican former president unfavorably than favorably.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unfavorability rating is 53%, seven points higher than his favorability rating. Harris has seen a jump in her popularity with voters since becoming the Democratic nominee last month, but even with that, 54% of voters view her unfavorably, and 44% favorably \u8211\'20\'13 a gap of 10 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re looking for a clue as to how this data, gathered from 3 to 15 September, could affect the election, you\u8217\'20\'19ll find it among the perceptions of independent voters, who might make a difference in deciding the winner of battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Trump has the edge with that group, with 44% viewing him favorably, as opposed to 35% feeling the same about Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance have campaign events today, though only one is in a battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Vance will rally in North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s capital city, Raleigh, at 3pm. Polls have recently shown \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  coming within striking distance of winning the Tar Heel state, which has not voted for a Democratic presidential candidate since 2008. Vance wants to keep that streak going.\par \par \uc2 Trump will be hold a rally at 7pm in a coliseum in Uniondale, in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Long Island suburbs. The state is not considered winnable by Republicans this year, but is home to several heavily contested House districts that the GOP is vying for. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said he will zero in on crimes involving undocumented people on Long Island \u8211\'20\'13 even though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://siepr.stanford.edu/news/mythical-tie-between-immigration-and-crime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nij.ojp.gov/topics/articles/undocumented-immigrant-offending-rate-lower-us-born-citizen-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  has shown that group offends at comparatively lower rates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 National Hispanic Heritage Month began on Sunday, and will be a focus of both \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will address the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus Institute\uc2  annual conference at 12.15pm ET, then hold a virtual campaign event at 3.45pm.\par \par \uc2 At the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host a reception in honor of Hispanic Heritage Month at 5pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 America Pac, one of the largest and the most ambitious of the groups supporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, is replacing its voter turnout operations in the crucial battleground states of Arizona and Nevada, according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The political action committee, backed by billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has ended its contract with the September Group and will hire a new company to knock on doors with fewer than 50 days left until the election.\par \par \uc2 America Pac used non-performance as the stated reason to back out of the contract in the past few days, claiming the September Group was not hitting its door-knocking targets, one of people said.\par \par \uc2 The shake-up comes at a crunch moment for the Trump campaign, which has outsourced virtually its entire ground game operation to a number of political action committees in this presidential cycle. America Pac is seen as the most ambitious, with a presence in every swing state.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the shake-up, America Pac has not canvassed any neighbourhoods in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  and Nevada on behalf of the Trump campaign for the past few days as it resets its operations in the two states.\par \par \uc2 America Pac hopes the roughly 300 canvassers employed by the September Group will be rehired by its successor but whether that occurs remains uncertain.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/trump-american-pac-voter-turnout-operation-arizona-nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-allied Pac fires canvassing vendor in crucial states weeks before election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 US still unprepared for Russian election interference, \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 The US is still not prepared for inevitable Russian attacks on its elections, the former special counsel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-mueller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Mueller}}}\uc2  , who investigated Russian interference in 2016 and links between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Moscow, warns in a new book.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is \u8230\'20\'26 evident that Americans have not learned the lessons of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attack on our democracy in 2016,\u8221\'20\'1D Mueller writes in a preface to Interference: The Inside Story of Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  and the Mueller Investigation by Aaron Zebley, James Quarles and Andrew Goldstein, prosecutors who worked for Mueller from 2017 to 2019.\par \par \uc2 Mueller continues:\par \par \uc2 As we detailed in our report, the evidence was clear that the Russian government engaged in multiple, systematic attacks designed to undermine our democracy and favor one candidate over the other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That candidate was Trump, the Republican who beat the Democrat, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , for the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were not prepared then,\u8221\'20\'1D Mueller writes, \u8220\'20\'1Cand, despite many efforts of dedicated people across the government, we are not prepared now. This threat deserves the attention of every American. Russia attacked us before and will do so again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Interference will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uk.bookshop.org/p/books/untitled-s-s-nf-if-to-be-confirmed-simon-schuster/7709017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  in the US next week. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Zebley, Quarles and Goldstein tell the story of the Mueller investigation, from its beginnings in May 2017 after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/may/09/james-comey-fbi-fired-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired the FBI director}}}\uc2 , \uc2 James Comey\uc2 , to its conclusion in March 2019 with moves by William Barr, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second attorney general, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/mar/24/mueller-report-donald-trump-william-barr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obscure and dismiss}}}\uc2  Mueller\u8217\'20\'19s findings.\par \par \uc2 Mueller did not establish collusion between Trump and Moscow but did initiate criminal proceedings against three Russian entities and 34 people, with those convicted including a Trump campaign manager, \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2 , who was jailed. Mueller also laid out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-ap-top-news-elections-james-comey-north-america-e0d125d737be4a21a81bec3d9f1dffd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 instances}}}\uc2  of possible obstruction of justice by Trump. Though he did not indict Trump, citing justice department policy regarding sitting presidents, Mueller {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/mueller-i-did-not-clear-trump-of-obstruction-of-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he was not clearing him either.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/russia-election-interference-robert-mueller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US still unprepared for Russian election interference, Robert Mueller says }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Poland's Duda may meet in battleground state of Pennsylvania, sources say\par \par \uc2 Polish president \uc2 Andrzej Duda\uc2  might hold talks on Sunday with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the US election battleground state of Pennsylvania, a senior Polish official said on Wednesday, confirming an earlier Reuters report that the two men may meet.\par \par \uc2 Any such meeting would mark a rare instance of a foreign leader appearing alongside a US presidential candidate on the campaign trail. Pennsylvania, which is home to a sizeable Polish US population, is one of several key battleground states in a tight race for the 5 Novermber US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Duda, a nationalist who forged close ties with Trump when he was US president in 2017-21, will attend the unveiling of a Solidarity monument, the senior Polish official said, adding that Trump had also been invited to the event. However, it was not yet known whether Trump would attend, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf President Trump comes, then of course there will definitely be an opportunity to exchange a few words and talk about the most important topics,\u8221\'20\'1D the Polish official told Reuters, speaking on condition of anonymity. These topics would include Polish-US relations, Poland\u8217\'20\'19s security and the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Neither the Trump campaign nor the organisers of the event in Pennsylvania responded immediately to Reuter\u8217\'20\'19s requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Two sources, also speaking on condition of anonymity, had earlier told Reuters that Trump planned to appear with Duda in Pennsylvania on Sunday, though they stressed that the joint appearance had not yet been finalised.\par \par \uc2 One of those sources said Trump and Duda were expected to appear at a Polish-US Catholic shrine in the suburbs north of Philadelphia. News of the visit was first reported by LevittownNow.com, a local outlet in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The chief of Duda\u8217\'20\'19s chancellery, Malgorzata Paprocka, later clarified that both Duda and Trump had been invited by organisers to the same event. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether President Trump will be there, I do not have one hundred percent confirmation at this moment. We, as the president\u8217\'20\'19s office, are not organisers of this meeting,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Duda, whose term in office expires in 2025, have described themselves as friends. The two men last met in New York in April.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 American politics often has wild deviations from the norms of other major democracies and one of the most striking differences is set to be on display in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election \u8211\'20\'13 the performance of its domestic Green party.\par \par \uc2 There are elected Greens at the national level in the UK, Canada, Mexico, France, Germany and Australia, sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/sep/05/green-party-leaders-carla-denyer-adrian-ramsay-labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helping form governments}}}\uc2 , and yet the US Green party has only ever had a handful of state-level representatives (it currently has none) and has never had a federal election winner.\par \par \uc2 Of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poliengine.com/blog/how-many-politicians-are-there-in-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about}}}\uc2  500,000 elected positions in the US, from school boards and township supervisors to the presidency, the Green party holds just 149. There\u8217\'20\'19s little indication there will be an influx of left-leaning Greens in November\u8217\'20\'19s elections, which will include local and state polls, as well as the headline presidential race in which Jill Stein is the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for a third time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a story of complete failure,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , a political scientist at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2  who argued the most consequential Green party impact has been as \u8220\'20\'1Cspoilers\u8221\'20\'1D helping Republicans in close elections, such as \uc2 Ralph Nader\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in 2000 and Stein\u8217\'20\'19s in 2016. There\u8217\'20\'19s a small chance such a scenario could play out again in this year\u8217\'20\'19s tight contest between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . One poll this month had Stein leading Harris among Muslim-American voters in three key swing states of Michigan, Arizona and Wisconsin, Middle East Eye {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/harris-and-stein-neck-and-neck-among-muslim-american-voters-survey-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNormally the Greens aren\u8217\'20\'19t important but they were in 2016, they cost Hillary Clinton a couple of blue wall states, and they were in 2000,\u8221\'20\'1D Sabato said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy vote for them when Democrats are also concerned about climate change? All you\u8217\'20\'19re doing is helping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 . Without them we might not have had the Iraq invasion, we might not have had \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others are more sympathetic, pointing to the winner-takes-all nature of US politics and the well-funded machinery of the two-party system that makes it hard for third parties, including the Green party and the Libertarian party, to break through. Notably, however, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Green party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/jul/07/well-push-the-government-to-be-bolder-carla-denyer-on-election-success-for-the-greens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did win four seats}}}\uc2  in first-past-the-post Westminster elections in July.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/green-party-jill-stein-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC calls the US Green party \u8216\'20\'18not serious\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 can it be more than a \u8216\'20\'18spoiler\u8217\'20\'19 in the election?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49am BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House}}}\uc2  will vote Wednesday on a government funding bill that appears doomed to fail, with less than two weeks left to prevent a partial shutdown starting 1 October.\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson}}}\uc2  , announced Tuesday that the chamber would move forward with the vote, despite vocal opposition from members of his own conference. The announcement came one week after that opposition forced Johnson to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/republicans-government-spending-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delay}}}\uc2  a planned vote on his bill, and the speaker has only faced more resistance in the days since.\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s proposed bill combines a six-month stopgap funding measure, known as a continuing resolution, with the Safeguard American Voter Eligibility {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/11/save-act-voting-bill-passes-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (Save) Act}}}\uc2 , a controversial proposal that would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/10/us-house-save-act-citizenship-proof-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 require}}}\uc2  people to show proof of citizenship when they register to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress has an immediate obligation to do two things: responsibly fund the federal government, and ensure the security of our elections,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1836049986707996808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI urge all of my colleagues to do what the overwhelming majority of the people of this county rightfully demand and deserve \u8211\'20\'13 prevent non-American citizens from voting in American elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Critics of the Save Act note that it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/11/trump-mike-johnson-migrant-voting-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already illegal}}}\uc2  for non-citizens to vote, and they fear such a law would hinder legitimate voters\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to cast their ballots. House Democrats remain overwhelmingly opposed to the proposal, and only a few of them are expected to support Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s bill on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Given Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 narrow House majority and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 widespread opposition to the bill, Johnson can only afford a handful of defections within his conference on Wednesday. But a number of hard-right {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  have already indicated they will vote against the bill, as many of them have rejected any kind of continuing resolution amid demands for more budget cuts.\par \par \uc2 Hard-right Republicans worry that, once the vote fails on Wednesday, Johnson will turn his attention to passing a more straightforward continuing resolution without the Save Act attached, although the speaker has dismissed those concerns.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/speaker-johnson-funding-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House will vote on doomed funding bill as shutdown deadline nears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  to meet on Wednesday to consider potential US presidential endorsement\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  executive board is meeting on Wednesday in Washington as the 1.3 million-member union decides who to endorse in the 2024 US presidential election, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 endorsement could be a factor in a handful of battleground states that will decide the 5 November election, including Michigan, Nevada and Pennsylvania, where union membership is strong.\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said on Monday the union could make its pick as early as Wednesday after union representatives met with vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They met her Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t kick this can down the road,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest unions, represents truck drivers and a wide range of other workers including airline pilots and zookeepers.\par \par \uc2 The union endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, as well as Democrats Hillary Clinton in 2016 and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2008 and 2012. It picked Republicans in some earlier elections.\par \par \uc2 Most major unions have endorsed Harris, including the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 . The \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , which represents 60 unions and 12.5 million workers, endorsed Harris in July.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien spoke to the Republican National Convention in July, but also criticised Trump for suggesting that workers who go on strike could be fired.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that the union will present the results of polling of its members to the executive board on Wednesday, which is one factor in its decision making.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the union could opt not to make an endorsement, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said:\par \par \uc2 We are going to look at any and all options \u8230\'20\'26 We need to make sure we make the right decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am BST\par \par \uc2 A 22-year-old woman who became an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocate after she was raped by her stepfather as a child tells her story in a new campaign ad for Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 Hadley Duvall says in voiceover that she has never slept a full night in her life \u8211\'20\'13 her stepfather first started abusing her when she was five years old, and impregnated her when she was 12. As she speaks, images of Duvall as a child flash on the screen. The soundtrack of the ad is a song by Billie Eilish, who endorsed the vice-president on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just remember thinking I have to get out of my skin. I can\u8217\'20\'19t be me right now. Like, this can\u8217\'20\'19t be it,\u8221\'20\'1D Duvall says. \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what to do. I was a child. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what it meant to be pregnant, at all. But I had options.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ad is part of a continued push by the Harris campaign to highlight the growing consequences of the fall of Roe, including that some states have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions with no exceptions for rape or incest. The AP reports that women in some states are suffering increasingly perilous medical care and the first reported instance of a woman dying from delayed reproductive care surfaced this week. Harris lays the blame squarely on Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appointed three of the conservatives to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  who helped overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The AP reports that Duvall blames Trump, too. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade, girls and women all over the country have lost the right to choose, even for rape or incest,\u8221\'20\'1D she says in the ad. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this. He took away our freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHer name is Hadley Duvall, and you need to hear her story. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ub5Kmhi5pD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ub5Kmhi5pD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr. Jill Biden (@DrBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrBiden/status/1813598818299990300?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 During the presidential debate on 10 September, Trump repeatedly took credit for appointing the three supreme court justices and leaned heavily on his catchall response to questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, saying the issue should be left up to the states. He said he would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not signing a ban,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is no reason to sign the ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he also repeatedly declined to say whether he would veto such a ban if he were elected again \u8211\'20\'13 a question that has lingered as the Republican nominee has shifted his stances on the crucial election issue.\par \par \uc2 Duvall of Owensboro, Kentucky, first told her story publicly last autumn in a campaign ad for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in her home state supporting Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 . Duvall\u8217\'20\'19s stepfather was convicted of rape and is in prison; she miscarried.\par \par \uc2 Beshear won reelection, and Democrats have said Duvall\u8217\'20\'19s ad was a strong motivator, particularly for rural, male voters who had previously voted for Trump, reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 Duvall is also touring the country to campaign for Harris along with other women who have been telling their personal stories since the fall of Roe, joining Pennsylvania governor Josh Shapiro last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls Ohio bomb threats \u8216\'20\'18crying shame\u8217\'20\'19 in talk with Black journalists\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  was interviewed by a panel of three \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) members, during which the vice-president talked about the anti-immigrant sentiment toward Haitians in Springfield, Ohio; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza}}}\uc2  ; domestic economic issues; gun violence; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . The conversation was one of the few interviews Harris has done since becoming the Democratic nominee, and it served as an opportunity for her to reaffirm policies.\par \par \uc2 When asked about \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere [she] sees the line in terms of aggression and defense\u8221\'20\'1D in regards to the war, she said that she supported the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s one-time pause on the delivery of 2,000lb bombs to Israel as \u8220\'20\'1Cleverage\u8221\'20\'1D that they \u8220\'20\'1Chave had and used\u8221\'20\'1D, but that achieving a deal was the real means to ending the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to agree that not only must we end this war, but we have to have a goal of a two-state solution because there must be stability and peace in that region,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cinasmuch as our goal must be to ensure that Israelis have security and Palestinians in equal measure have security, self determination, dignity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked what mechanisms the US has to support Palestinian self-determination, and whether or not it was even possible, as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ally, to support such a goal, Harris responded saying that she believed that it was. She described meetings with Israeli and Arab leaders to \u8220\'20\'1Ctalk about how we can construct a day-after scenario\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She said that her \u8220\'20\'1Cgoals\u8221\'20\'1D are that there be no reoccupation of Gaza, no changing of the territorial lines in Gaza and \u8220\'20\'1Can ability to have security in the region for all concerned in a way that we create stability\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris was also asked about the false and racist tropes that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance have espoused about Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, which has resulted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/more-bomb-threats-hit-springfield-ohio-after-trump-elevates-false-claims-about-haitians"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bomb threats and lockdowns}}}\uc2  in the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a crying shame. I mean, my heart breaks for this community,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were children, elementary schoolchildren, [for whom] it was school photo day. Do you remember what that\u8217\'20\'19s like, going to school on picture day? Dressed up in their best, got all ready, knew what they were going to wear the night before. And had to be evacuated. Children. Children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-nabj-panel-ohio-bomb-threats-gaza-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris calls Ohio bomb threats \u8216\'20\'18crying shame\u8217\'20\'19 in talk with Black journalists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump rejects 'rambling' label and mocks climate change\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  touched on a range of topics during his town hall with \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , that included \u8211\'20\'13 according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4885493-5-takeaways-from-trumps-town-hall-with-sarah-huckabee-sanders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the fate of the US auto industry, climate change (which he mocked) and a rejection of the \u8216\'20\'18rambling\u8217\'20\'19 label he\u8217\'20\'19s been given by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Hill reports that, after giving a long and winding answer on Tuesday during which Trump spoke about the withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan, appeared to confuse Bagram airbase with an oil reserve in Alaska and threatened to impose a 200% tariff on cars imported from Mexico, the Republican presidental nominee argued his words were more \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive\u8221\'20\'1D than what Harris says on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fake news likes to say, \u8216\'20\'18Oh he was rambling.\u8217\'20\'19 No, no. That\u8217\'20\'19s not rambling. That\u8217\'20\'19s genius,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of his own comments. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you can connect the dots. Now, Sarah, if you couldn\u8217\'20\'19t connect the dots, you got a problem. But every dot was connected. And many stories were told in that little paragraph.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also mocked climate change. According to The Hill, Trump said that the biggest threat to the public was not climate change but nuclear warfare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot that the ocean is going to rise in 400 years an eighth of an inch, and you\u8217\'20\'19ll have more seafront property if that happens,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI said, \u8216\'20\'18Is that good or bad?\u8217\'20\'19 I said, isn\u8217\'20\'19t that a good thing if I have a little property on the ocean? I have a little bit more property, I have a little bit more ocean.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held his first campaign event on Tuesday since the thwarted assassination attempt over the weekend, telling a packed 6,000-seat arena in Flint, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  that the assassin \u8220\'20\'1Ccouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even get a shot off\u8221\'20\'1D while describing the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D response to the threat.\par \par \uc2 During a town hall moderated by former White House press secretary \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , Trump took audience questions about manufacturing and the economy, among other issues. Like his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/trump-vance-michigan-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first appearance}}}\uc2  after the attempt on his life in July \u8211\'20\'13 also a rally in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 Trump appeared ready to return to business as usual on the campaign trail, and his supporters were eager to see him in action.\par \par \uc2 Susan Moore and Christopher Moore, who came to the rally from Mundy Township, Michigan, got in line at 9.30am for a chance to get inside their first Trump event, where doors didn\u8217\'20\'19t open until 3pm. \u8220\'20\'1CThe atmosphere is just electric,\u8221\'20\'1D Susan Moore said.\par \par \uc2 Clark Grognan, a career auto worker from Whiteford, Michigan, said \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible\u8221\'20\'1D presidency convinced him to vote Republican, and that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cexciting\u8221\'20\'1D to meet so many like-minded people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod is not done with President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Huckabee Sanders said as she opened the event, calling Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat our country desperately needs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Auto workers were among the most common attendees. Several people wore \u8220\'20\'1CUnions for Trump\u8221\'20\'1D merchandise, and some had UAW T-shirts.\par \par \uc2 Flint, like much of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s east side, has been a bastion of the US auto industry. Trump began the night by lamenting the rise of Mexican car manufacturing. He championed new tariffs, saying about Mexico: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to let them sell one car in the USA.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/trump-town-hall-flint-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump praises Secret Service in first event since thwarted assassination plot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03am BST\par \par \uc2 'Only consequential presidents get shot,' says Trump, at first public event after assassination bid\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our coverage of the run-up to the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The fallout from Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s apparent assassination attempt on Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is continuing. Last night the former president made his first public appearance since the incident, which occurred while he was playing golf in Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a great experience,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican presidential nominee said in an evening town hall in Flint, Michigan, about holding events with thousands of supporters. But he also went on to call running for president \u8220\'20\'1Ca dangerous business\u8221\'20\'1D akin to car racing or bull riding.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly consequential presidents get shot at,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chanted \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfight, fight, fight\u8221\'20\'1D as \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  agents surrounded the stage to protect him.\par \par \uc2 Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s incident, for which a suspect has been charged with possession of a firearm as a felon, comes two months after Trump was lightly injured when a gunman opened fire on him at a Pennsylvania rally.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  was interviewed by a panel of three \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) members, during which the vice-president talked about the anti-immigrant sentiment toward Haitians in Springfield, Ohio; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza}}}\uc2  ; domestic economic issues; gun violence; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . The conversation was one of the few interviews Harris has done since becoming the Democratic nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance defended his comments about Haitian immigrants eating pets during a Tuesday rally, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe media has a responsibility to factcheck\u8221\'20\'1D stories \u8211\'20\'13 not him. The rally in Eau Claire, Wisconsin, came two days after the Ohio senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/15/jd-vance-lies-haitian-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN host Dana Bash}}}\uc2  it was OK \u8220\'20\'1Cto create stories\u8221\'20\'1D to draw attention to issues his constituents care about, regarding inflammatory and unfounded claims that Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, had eaten residents\u8217\'20\'19 pets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the \uc2 US Postal Inspection Service\uc2  on Tuesday were investigating the origin of suspicious packages that have been sent to or received by elections officials in more than 15 states, but there were no immediate reports of injuries or that any of the packages contained hazardous material. The latest packages were sent to elections officials in Alaska, Colorado, Georgia, Indiana, Kentucky, Massachusetts, Missouri, New York and Rhode Island.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is planning to appear with Polish President \uc2 Andrzej Duda\uc2  in the battleground state of Pennsylvania on Sunday, according to two sources familiar with the plan, reports Reuters. The dual appearance is not yet finalised, said one of the sources, who requested anonymity to discuss plans that are still private. But if the dual appearance goes forward, it would mark a rare instance of a foreign leader appearing alongside a US presidential candidate on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A false claim circulating on social media that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  was involved in an alleged hit-and-run in San Francisco in 2011 is the work of a covert Russian disinformation operation, according to new research by \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . The Russian group responsible, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/microsoft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Microsoft}}}\uc2  dubs Storm-1516, is described as a Kremlin-aligned troll farm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 America Pac, one of the largest and the most ambitious of the groups supporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, is replacing its voter turnout operations in the crucial battleground states of Arizona and Nevada, according to two people familiar with the matter. The political action committee, backed by billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has ended its contract with the September Group and will hire a new company to knock on doors with fewer than 50 days left until the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240918ek9i0018s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
