\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s powerful  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  stance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fact-checks: key takeaways from the debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon \par \uc2 1,356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2024\par 09:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Presidential candidates face off in fiery debate displaying diverging visions of the country\par \par \uc2 The presidential hopefuls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  went head to head on Tuesday night in their first \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially only \u8211\'20\'13 debate before voters head to the polls on 5 November. The candidates went into the event virtually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied in the polls}}}\uc2  with just weeks to convince a small but mighty minority of unsure voters on how to cast their ballot.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of arguments over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/04/kamala-harris-donald-trump-debate-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 format and rules}}}\uc2 , the debate aired live on ABC from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, a key swing state, with no audience in attendance and each candidate\u8217\'20\'19s microphone muted while their opponent spoke.\par \par \uc2 This was the second presidential debate this year for Trump, who also went up against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in June. The latter\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating performance}}}\uc2  triggered an upheaval within the Democratic party that would ultimately push Biden to step down and position Harris to head the ticket, an outcome Trump both takes credit for and complains about at his rallies.\par \par \uc2 With just 55 days until votes are tallied, Harris strived to highlight that she has a plan, and clearly responded to criticisms that she hasn\u8217\'20\'19t shared enough details with voters about her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/kamala-harris-policy-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 platform and priorities}}}\uc2 . With focused rhetoric on planning for the future, building the middle class and reframing her record on everything from immigration to climate, Harris was able to show voters how she hopes to lead.\par \par \uc2 Analysts, meanwhile, were watching Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demeanor and clarity. The former president repeated frequent rhetoric from his rallies \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely disputed claims}}}\uc2  about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , crime and his belief that he won the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 but shared little about how he would address key problems Americans are facing.\par \par \uc2 Beyond their differences in policy positions, the candidates also displayed diverging visions of the country. Trump promised his base to restore what he sees as the glory of the past, and Harris heralded the hope of a brighter future.\par \par \uc2 Here are the highlights:\par \par \uc2 Trump repeatedly spewed misinformation\par \par \uc2 Throughout the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump spread misinformation}}}\uc2  to make his points, repeating already debunked rhetoric on everything from the results of the 2020 election to his involvement in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/paul-dans-project-2025-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a conservative-backed plan to change the \uc2 US government\uc2  from the inside out. The former president distanced himself from the January 6 attack on the Capitol, saying he was there only to make a speech, and blamed the then House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , for not beefing up security. He also incorrectly said crime rates had risen in the US when they have in fact fallen.\par \par \uc2 ... and was frequently fact-checked by the moderators\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-abc-moderators"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s moderators}}}\uc2 , David Muir and Linsey Davis, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/themoneycoach/status/1833683477272609221"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/beccalew/status/1833695055963623908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  for delivering a strong performance. They effectively rerouted discussions back to the questions they had asked on key topics including the economy, immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the peaceful transfer of power, and made important clarifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact-check statements}}}\uc2  when they were warranted.\par \par \uc2 Muir and Davis are veteran journalists who have collectively spent decades helping the American public navigate presidential positions. Feedback for their performance stands in contrast to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-cnn-presidential-debate-reaction-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN debate in June}}}\uc2 , when moderators frequently missed opportunities to fact-check Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris defended Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 position on reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 When challenged on his changing take on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, Trump made some alarming \u8211\'20\'13 and easily refuted \u8211\'20\'13 claims that Democrats supported executing babies after they are born. He also took credit for overturning of Roe v Wade, a decision made by the supreme court after he appointed three members to make a 6-3 conservative majority, that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unpopular with the majority of Americans}}}\uc2 . Trump did clarify his position, though, that he believes in exceptions for rape, incest and threats to the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 Harris called his stances \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulting to the women of America\u8221\'20\'1D, and countered his statements that he delivered on a promise to bring the issue back to the states by saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe people of American have voted for freedom\u8221\'20\'1D. She highlighted the difficult realities faced by women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and would-be mothers who would struggle to access IVF care.\par \par \uc2 The candidates both touted their work to improve the economy\par \par \uc2 Harris was quick to tout her \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opportunity economy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a plan that includes tax reductions for those starting small businesses, relief for new parents and first-time homebuyers, and a crackdown on corporate price-gouging. \u8220\'20\'1CI am the only person on this stage that is about lifting up the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, noting her upbringing in a middle-class household.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, claimed that he oversaw the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest economy\u8221\'20\'1D, even with the downturn caused by the Covid pandemic, and accused his opponent of increasing costs on American families. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople can\u8217\'20\'19t go out and buy cereal, or bacon, or anything else,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation did spike under the Biden-Harris administration, but it has fallen just as quickly. As of August, the US inflation rate settled at 2.9%.\par \par \uc2 Trump also touted his stance on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-economy-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariffs}}}\uc2 , which he plans to prioritize if he regains the White House.\par \par \uc2 Trump spouted sometimes racist claims about immigrants\par \par \uc2 Throughout the debate, Trump pivoted his talking points to immigration, spouting claims about criminals being welcomed into the country and towns where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pets are eaten by incoming immigrants.}}}\par \par \uc2 While debate moderators attempted to counter the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2 , challenging Trump on the validity and also on how he would execute the deportation of millions as he\u8217\'20\'19s promised to do, Harris took the offensive. Highlighting her record as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only person on the stage who has prosecuted transnational organizations\u8221\'20\'1D, she also accused her opponent of calling on the GOP to oppose legislation to bolster the border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe preferred to run on a problem rather than fixing a problem,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The candidates sparred over Ukraine and how they would handle the war\par \par \uc2 Harris said that if Trump were currently in office, the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , would have taken Kyiv, saying Putin would \u8220\'20\'1Ceat you for lunch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the reason that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  says that this war would be over within 24 hours is because he would just give it up,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris also said.\par \par \uc2 When Trump was asked by Muir how he would end the war \u8211\'20\'13 and specifically if he wanted Ukraine to win \u8211\'20\'13 the former president didnot offer a clear answer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop. I want to save lives that are being lost uselessly. People being killed by the millions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. When pressed again on if it was in the US best interest for Ukraine to win he doubled down. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s the US best interest to get this war finished and just get it done, all right, negotiate a deal, because we have to stop all of these human lives from being destroyed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris baited Trump by attacking him where it hurts\par \par \uc2 As moderators pushed Harris to respond to criticisms she and Biden have faced over border policy, the vice-president expertly derailed her opponent\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on what is perhaps his favorite issue to discuss by deriding his performances at rallies.\par \par \uc2 She invited voters to view the speeches for themselves, saying that attenders can be seen leaving out of exhaustion and boredom, and characterized the events as a platform for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s complaints and not plans that put the American people first.\par \par \uc2 The jab landed well. An offended and flustered Trump jumped on the chance to defend attendance at his rallies, claiming Harris pays attenders at her own campaign events, and then pivoted to insults that failed to hit their mark. He accused Harris of planning to turn the country into \u8220\'20\'1CVenezuela on steroids\u8221\'20\'1D, and called the US a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing nation\u8221\'20\'1D, before resurfacing false claims that immigrants were eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 Read more about the 2024 US election:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fact checking the presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift endorses Harris in post signed \u8216\'20\'18childless cat lady\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Maga mad libs\u8217\'20\'19: How the debate played out on social media}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Presidential poll tracker}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2024/sep/11/rally-sizes-abortion-and-eating-cats-the-trump-and-harris-debate-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rally sizes, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and eating cats: the Trump and Harris debate \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240911ek9b000p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
