\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris blames Trump for Georgia  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 -related death: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s what we feared\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 1,142 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2024\par 15:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Harris points to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies in what was reported as a rare \u8216\'20\'18preventable\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked death\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  blamed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies and condemned state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on Tuesday after it was reported that a woman in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  died after being denied timely medical care due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s comments came on the heels of an investigation published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2  on Monday, recounting the circumstances surrounding the 2022 death of Amber Nicole Thurman, a medical assistant from Georgia. The outlet called the case the first \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related death to be confirmed, and said it would name a second in coming days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the consequences of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s actions,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in a statement. Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/24/georgia-abortion-ban-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  went into effect shortly after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Thurman died after she developed a rare complication from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Days after taking the pills, she was taken to an emergency room with heavy bleeding, as she had not yet expelled all of the fetal tissue from her body. Doctors waffled on her treatment, according to the report, waiting 20 hours to perform a routine procedure. Thurman, who was 28 years old and the mother of a six-year-old boy, died in emergency surgery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis young mother should be alive, raising her son, and pursuing her dream of attending nursing school,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/kamala-harris-abortion-rights-healthcare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  a prominent feature of her presidential campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly what we feared when Roe was struck down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Georgia, performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy is a felony. While the law allows for exceptions to save a pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s life, doctors say its wording is too vague to be workable in practice.\par \par \uc2 Since 2022, more than 20 states have enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions.\par \par \uc2 After Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s death, a state medical review committee deemed that her death was \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D, and that there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood chance\u8221\'20\'1D she would have survived if she had received the procedure earlier, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported that Thurman became pregnant shortly after Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban took effect and that her pregnancy had just passed that mark.\par \par \uc2 Thurman scheduled a procedure known as dilation and curettage, or D&C, in North Carolina for 13 August and journeyed there with her best friend, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported, after finding a babysitter and scheduling a day off work.\par \par \uc2 However, they encountered heavy traffic on the drive, her best friend told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 , and the clinic could not hold Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s spot longer than 15 minutes.\par \par \uc2 As a result, Thurman was given a two-pill medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen approved by the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2 , which included mifepristone and misoprostol, as her pregnancy was well within the standard of care for that treatment.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using medication is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/72/ss/ss7209a1.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most common way}}}\uc2  to end a pregnancy in the US, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/health/abortion-pill-safety-dg/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deaths from complications are extremely rare}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported that at the clinic in North Carolina, Thurman received instructions on how to safely take the pills and was told to go to the emergency room if complications developed.\par \par \uc2 She took the first pill at the clinic and drove home before any symptoms started and took the second pill the next day, as directed.\par \par \uc2 Initially, she only experienced cramping, but her condition worsened over several days with vomiting and heavy bleeding.\par \par \uc2 If she had lived near the North Carolina clinic, she would have received a D&C for free as soon as she followed up, the executive director there told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . But Thurman was about four hours away.\par \par \uc2 Thurman passed out and was taken to a hospital in suburban Atlanta with a severe infection. Thurman needed a D&C, but the operation was delayed for around 20 hours as her blood pressure sank and her organs started to fail, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report states that she was diagnosed with \u8220\'20\'1Cacute severe sepsis\u8221\'20\'1D the following morning. However, even then, a D&C was not performed.\par \par \uc2 Around 20 hours after she arrived at the hospital, the doctor conducted the D&C and discovered that a hysterectomy was also necessary. Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s heart stopped during the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The maternal mortality review committee in Georgia determined that there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood chance\u8221\'20\'1D that Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s death could likely have been prevented if the D&C had been provided earlier.\par \par \uc2 Before her death, Thurman had been planning to enroll in nursing school, her friend told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . She and her child had recently moved out of her family\u8217\'20\'19s place and into their own apartment.\par \par \uc2 Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s last words to her mother before she died were: \u8220\'20\'1CPromise me you\u8217\'20\'19ll take care of my son,\u8221\'20\'1D the outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 Studies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3913899"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have shown}}}\uc2  that the availability of the D&C procedure for abortions and miscarriage care in the year after Roe v Wade was passed in 1973 reduced the rate of maternal deaths for women of color by up to 40%.\par \par \uc2 But since more than 20 states enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions in the last two years, women in with medical complications have been repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/19/pregnant-women-denied-care-us-hospitals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned away from emergency rooms}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are bleeding out in parking lots, turned away from emergency rooms, losing their ability to ever have children again,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris statement said. \u8220\'20\'1CSurvivors of rape and incest are being told they cannot make decisions about what happens next to their bodies. And now women are dying.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As president, Trump appointed three conservative supreme court justices who were decisive in overturning Roe. And as a candidate, he has alternately bragged about his role in overturning Roe v Wade, and also complained that Republican extremism on the issue could cost them the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gets the chance, he will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and these horrific realities will multiply,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must pass a law to restore reproductive freedom. When I am president of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law. Lives depend on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2  , the president of Naral Pro-Choice America, said in a press call on Monday that Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s death \u8220\'20\'1C substantiated proof of something we already knew \u8211\'20\'13 that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans kill people and it cannot go on\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Regina Davis Moss, the CEO of In Our Own Voice: National Black Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Justice Agenda, said in a statement that what happened to Thurman was \u8220\'20\'1Centirely preventable\u8221\'20\'1D adding that this is the \u8220\'20\'1Cpost-Dobbs reality for many Black women, girls, gender expansive people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moss also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nationalpartnership.org/report/state-abortion-bans-threaten-black-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted a study}}}\uc2  that estimated that if abortions ban were in every state, there could be a \u8220\'20\'1Cstaggering\u8221\'20\'1D 39% increase in maternal deaths for Black women.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Gambino contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240917ek9h0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
