\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Killing a baby \u8216\'20\'18after birth\u8217\'20\'19 is homicide and legal nowhere. What is Trump on about?\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2024\par 14:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The ex-president repeated the rightwing talking point during the debate with Harris, and now even Fox News is validating it\par \par \uc2 Can doctors kill babies after they\u8217\'20\'19re born?\par \par \uc2 Excuse me for a moment while I state the bleeding obvious: there is no state in the US where it is \u8220\'20\'1COK\u8221\'20\'1D to kill a baby after it is born. That is homicide and there are one or two laws that frown on that sort of thing. Unless you\u8217\'20\'19ve just suffered some sort of traumatic head injury, then there\u8217\'20\'19s really no excuse for confusion when it comes to this.\par \par \uc2 Yet, here we are, in the year of our lord 2024, still arguing over this very issue. You may have missed it among all the other unhinged things \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but the former president repeated the longstanding rightwing talking point that Democrats love executing babies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Harris\u8217\'20\'19s] vice-presidential pick \u8230\'20\'26 says that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month is absolutely fine,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1C[\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ] also says: \u8216\'20\'18Execution after birth\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 execution, no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the baby is born \u8211\'20\'13 is OK.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both these false claims were fact-checked live by ABC News moderator Linsey Davis during the debate, but that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped the usual suspects from doubling down and insisting Trump was right. On Wednesday, for example, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/right-wing-media-spread-falsehoods-about-minnesotas-abortion-law-after-trumps-poor-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 Brian Kilmeade falsely claimed}}}\uc2  Minnesota (where Walz is governor) loves itself a little infanticide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[At first] I thought the moderators were fair but then it soon turned to the fact-checking on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when it come [sic] to \u8216\'20\'18there\u8217\'20\'19s no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the ninth month\u8217\'20\'19, when, in fact, under Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , it happened at least five times in Minnesota,\u8221\'20\'1D Kilmeade said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a moderator \u8230\'20\'26 fact-checks you and the moderator is wrong, that\u8217\'20\'19s tough on a candidate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kilmeade, I\u8217\'20\'19d just like to remind everyone, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/03/15/cable-news-salaries-fox-cnn-msnbc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likely paid seven figures}}}\uc2  for saying this sort of unsubstantiated and unintelligible nonsense on national TV. While it\u8217\'20\'19s not entirely clear what he\u8217\'20\'19s going on about, I presume what Kilmeade is referring to is an amendment to a Minnesota law that Walz signed in May 2023. You can see the amendment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.revisor.mn.gov/laws/2023/0/70/laws.4.56.0#laws.4.56.0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . The law originally stated that medical personnel must \u8220\'20\'1Cpreserve the life and health of the born alive infant\u8221\'20\'1D. The amendment reworded this to say \u8220\'20\'1Ccare for the infant who is born alive\u8221\'20\'1D. No change was made to the earlier part of the sentence which says that: \u8220\'20\'1CAll reasonable measures consistent with good medical practice\u8221\'20\'1D must be taken.\par \par \uc2 That amendment has been under the spotlight ever since Walz was chosen as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate. The right has interpreted the change of wording from \u8220\'20\'1Cpreserve the life\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Ccare for\u8221\'20\'1D to argue that it\u8217\'20\'19s now OK for doctors to let healthy babies die. Sadly, it\u8217\'20\'19s not just the likes of Fox News pushing this dangerous and false idea. In August, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/08/30/tim-walz-half-truths-record/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a piece}}}\uc2  by Pulitzer prize-winning columnist Kathleen Parker that said much the same thing. In a piece arguing that Walz is a dangerous liar, Parker states: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Walz-approved law says only that doctors \u8216\'20\'18care for the infant who is born alive.\u8217\'20\'19 So \u8216\'20\'18care\u8217\'20\'19 can mean \u8216\'20\'18let die,\u8217\'20\'19 if one\u8217\'20\'19s conscience permits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Technically that sentence is correct, but it\u8217\'20\'19s missing some rather crucial context. If a baby is born with a condition that means it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to survive more than a few hours, for example, the former wording would have forced doctors to keep that baby alive as long as possible, even if it was suffering. The amendment allows healthcare professionals and the baby\u8217\'20\'19s parents to decide if they\u8217\'20\'19d prefer to offer palliative care and ensure the baby is as comfortable as possible in its last moments.\par \par \uc2 In other words: the amendment is not cruel, it\u8217\'20\'19s compassionate. Critics are \u8220\'20\'1Cnot wrapping their head around what some of these situations are like\u8221\'20\'1D, Sara Pentlicky, a gynecologist and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, explains. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one\u8217\'20\'19s sitting there saying: \u8216\'20\'18We should let this baby die.\u8217\'20\'19 Everyone is making really hard decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D The former wording of the Minnesota law might have forced medical professionals to take extensive measures that would have prolonged the baby\u8217\'20\'19s life in a way that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t meaningful in order to ensure nobody got in legal trouble. The amendment, meanwhile, \u8220\'20\'1Cis intended to give people the space to actually care for the baby, which in some cases might be something like hospice or palliative care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Those five instances of babies dying after birth in Minnesota that Kilmeade references are cases in point. Kilmeade seems to have been referencing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.health.state.mn.us/data/mchs/pubs/abrpt/docs/2021abrpt.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2022 Minnesota department of health}}}\uc2  report that states that in 2021 \u8220\'20\'1C5 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures resulting in a born-alive infant were reported\u8221\'20\'1D. Go take a look at page 30 of that for yourself. Nobody was letting a healthy baby starve to death because the mother suddenly decided she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to be a parent. The babies weren\u8217\'20\'19t going to survive and so they were kept as comfortable as possible in the meantime. Once again, when you drill down into it, what the right really has a problem with is compassion.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  offers to give Taylor Swift a baby\par \par \uc2 After Swift finally endorsed Harris on Tuesday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s BFF Elon responded by tweeting: \u8220\'20\'1CFine Taylor, you win \u8230\'20\'26 I will give you a child and guard your cats with my life.\u8221\'20\'1D It\u8217\'20\'19s wild that the richest man in the world is just routinely creepy towards women and it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to hurt his businesses at all. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jezebel.com/bumping-the-sexual-harassment-allegations-against-elon-musk-for-no-particular-reason"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Jezebel reports}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CSwift is actually just the latest woman Musk has nonconsensually solicited to make babies with him. In June, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/business/elon-musk-spacex-employee-relationships-8bca2806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on the disturbing case of at least one of Musk\u8217\'20\'19s employees recounting how, in 2013, he repeatedly asked her to have children with him.\u8221\'20\'1D And that\u8217\'20\'19s just the tip of the iceberg when it comes to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting behaviour regarding women.\par \par \uc2 Laura Loomer tweets that \u8216\'20\'18the White House will smell like curry\u8217\'20\'19 if Harris wins\par \par \uc2 The far-right activist is not just some random extremist; she\u8217\'20\'19s been travelling with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/laura-loomer-trump-pet-eating-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump a lot recently}}}\uc2 , including to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/yashar/status/1833642166482292923"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear just how much she\u8217\'20\'19s advising him but she\u8217\'20\'19s certainly in his inner circle. Meanwhile, she\u8217\'20\'19s so incredibly racist that even far-right {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/marjorie-taylor-greene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  has told Loomer to tone it down. On Thursday, Greene, who has a long history of unhinged and bigoted comments, said Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crhetoric and hateful tone\u8221\'20\'1D are concerning and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/12/politics/marjorie-taylor-greene-laura-loomer-rhetoric-maga/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t represent Maga as a whole}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. I rather think it does.\par \par \uc2 Why Afghan women have risked their lives to attend a summit in Albania\par \par \uc2 The Guardian notes that the summit comes as the world\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/jun/21/shutting-afghan-women-out-of-key-un-conference-to-appease-taliban-a-betrayal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diplomatic relations with the Taliban}}}\uc2  begin to be normalized, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/sep/13/we-will-never-stop-fighting-why-afghan-women-have-risked-their-lives-to-attend-a-summit-in-tirana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with women\u8217\'20\'19s voices largely absent from the conversation}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gallup analysis finds young women in the US are more liberal than they\u8217\'20\'19ve been in decades\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to an analysis of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/649826/exploring-young-women-leftward-expansion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 20 years of polling data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Florida lawmaker celebrates killing of Turkish American human rights activist Aysenur Ezgi Eygi\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C#FireAway,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-cair-fl-call-for-censure-of-florida-lawmaker-who-celebrated-israels-murder-of-american/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted Randy Fine}}}\uc2 . One imagines he will face zero consequences for this tweet. It\u8217\'20\'19s certainly not the only outrageous comment made by a US lawmaker about the death of the 26-year-old, who was shot in the head by Israeli forces while protesting settlements in the West Bank. Joe Biden told reporters that the killing was just a sad accident due to \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessary escalation\u8221\'20\'1D and the result of a bullet ricochet. There is zero evidence that this is the case; that\u8217\'20\'19s just the \uc2 IDF\uc2  story, which Biden chose to parrot. Eyewitness reports and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/12/israeli-forces-mischaracterised-events-leading-fatal-shooting-aysenur-ezgi-eygi-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post investigation}}}\uc2 , meanwhile, refute this account.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Friedland uses her platform to condemn \u8216\'20\'18genocide\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Jewish American director {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/program/newsfeed/2024/9/8/jewish-director-at-venice-film-festival-speaks-in-solidarity-with-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used her acceptance speech}}}\uc2  at the Venice film festival for her debut film, Familiar Touch, to voice support for Palestinians facing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe 336th day of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s genocide in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D. It feels like the horrors happening in Gaza have been disturbingly normalized now \u8211\'20\'13 so it is even more important that people continue to speak up.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Regular readers will know that this section normally hosts a lighthearted story about dogs or cats. Unfortunately, all the pet-related stories this week focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/09/11/nx-s1-5108401/donald-trump-debate-eating-dogs-cats-immigrants-false-stereotype"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist rumours}}}\uc2  about immigrants eating them. So, instead, please enjoy this story about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/sep/12/ig-nobel-prize-goes-to-team-who-found-mammals-can-breathe-through-anuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 researchers winning an Ig Nobel prize}}}\uc2  (always my most-anticipated award) for discovering mammals can breathe through their anuses. Rumour also has it that Trump talks through his.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240914ek9e001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
