\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump repeats false claims about Ohio cities after Biden says \u8216\'20\'18no place in America\u8217\'20\'19 for attacks on Haitian immigrants \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Anna Betts and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 4,917 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par 21:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on Trump, read our full report:Trump repeats racist, anti-immigrant lies\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/springfield-ohio-bomb-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said }}}\uc2  the hostile attacks on Haitian immigrants in the US \u8220\'20\'1C[have] to stop\u8221\'20\'1D after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeated a false and derogatory claim about a Haitian community in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/trump-repeats-lies-haitian-immigrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  racist claims about Haitian migrants in Springfield, Ohio, on Friday, doubling down on anti-immigrant rhetoric as residents in the town have faced bomb threats and have detailed their fears amid harassment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Some schools in Springfield were reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e44a478f08c69019f64da9#block-66e44a478f08c69019f64da9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  closed}}}\uc2  by administrators for a second day in a row as Trump and his allies spread unproven stories of pet-eating by Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Haitians have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e468128f082b0bb978b682#block-66e468128f082b0bb978b682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  been intimidated and had their cars vandalized in Springfield since the campaign against them began. People {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e45df28f08c69019f64ed0#block-66e45df28f08c69019f64ed0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanted}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not eating cats\u8221\'20\'1D at a rally held by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , in Michigan yesterday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e47fd58f082b0bb978b805#block-66e47fd58f082b0bb978b805"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended }}}\uc2  his association with Laura Loomer, a conspiracy theorist whose penchant for public displays of racism has unnerved even some of his most extreme allies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is participating in a taped interview with a local station in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, to air later on Friday. Harris will also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e4956f8f082dce7ae333b0#block-66e4956f8f082dce7ae333b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 host }}}\uc2  a virtual livestream rally together with Oprah Winfrey next week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/13/pope-trump-kamala-harris-immigration-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized }}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his plan to deport millions of immigrants and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over her stance supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/harris-trump-second-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepped up}}}\uc2  its mockery of \u8220\'20\'1Cchicken\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for ducking out of another presidential debate, with the Democratic nominee telling her Republican rival he owes it to voters to face her again.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , the UK prime minister, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e4a6428f082b0bb978b94b#block-66e4a6428f082b0bb978b94b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  meeting}}}\uc2  at the White House where they are expected to discuss a loosening of restrictions on Ukraine to launch long-range strikes into Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e493228f082dce7ae3338f#block-66e493228f082dce7ae3338f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning}}}\uc2  a trip to Angola in the coming weeks. This would make Biden the first US head of state to visit sub-Saharan Africa since then president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2015, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with the UK\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , at the White House.\par \par \uc2 The pair are expected to discuss \u8211\'20\'13 though not necessarily announce \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/13/ukraine-must-defend-itself-washington-leaders-dismiss-putins-war-talk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a loosening of restrictions on Ukraine}}}\uc2  to launch long-range strikes into Russia.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Starmer took photos inside the Oval Office before sitting down for talks in the Blue Room alongside UK and US officials, per pool report.\par \par \uc2 Before talks began, Biden said the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , will not prevail in the war with Ukraine. He said he and Starmer would talk about Ukraine, the Middle East and the need for a hostage and ceasefire deal, as well as the Indo-Pacific region.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , said political leaders should not be \u8220\'20\'1Cattacking vulnerable communities\u8221\'20\'1D as she criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for spreading false and racist theories targeting Haitians in Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported Jean-Pierre, whose parents immigrated from Haiti to New York, telling reporters today:\par \par \uc2 Political leaders should not be attacking vulnerable communities. That\u8217\'20\'19s not who we should be. And if they\u8217\'20\'19re going to fall for conspiracy theories online, maybe they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be our leaders.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis has criticized both \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for their policies on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and immigration, claiming both candidates are \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The pope was speaking to journalists on Friday when he was asked about the US presidential election. He replied:\par \par \uc2 Both are against life, be it the one who kicks out migrants, or be it the one who kills babies.\par \par \uc2 He went on to say that not welcoming migrants is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave\u8221\'20\'1D sin and compared undergoing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an assassination, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Catholics would have to \u8220\'20\'1Cchoose the lesser evil\u8221\'20\'1D when they vote in November, he said, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 Who is the lesser evil? That lady, or that gentleman? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Everyone, in conscience, (has to) think and do this.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot voting is ugly,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not good. You must vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is participating in a taped interview with Brian Taff for Action News 6 ABC, a local station in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The interview will air on the station\u8217\'20\'19s 6pm broadcast.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will host a virtual livestream rally together next week.\par \par \uc2 The event, titled Unite for America, will take place on Thursday 19 September, at 8pm ET.\par \par \uc2 This comes as Winfrey, who said she was a registered independent, made a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/oprah-winfrey-democratic-national-convention-speech-trump-harris-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise appearance }}}\uc2  at the Democratic national convention last month and endorsed Harris for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to make first Africa visit in coming weeks - report\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is planning a trip to Angola in the coming weeks, Reuters is reporting, citing several sources familiar with the plans.\par \par \uc2 The trip, Reuters reports, is likely to occur after the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly meeting in September and before the presidential election in November, according to a source.\par \par \uc2 This would make Biden the first US head of state to visit sub-Saharan Africa since then president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2015, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Biden had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-africa-antony-blinken-gina-raimondo-e61f9758da2fac08aa11d1068478ffe1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously said}}}\uc2  he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-africa-climate-change-2024-9cf0bcf783050bfad71a521cf1c05ca7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit Africa}}}\uc2  during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 MoveOn, a progressive public policy advocacy group, is partnering with ice-cream company Ben & Jerry\u8217\'20\'19s to create a special limited edition \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  -inspired ice-cream flavor, titled Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s Coconut Jubilee, as part of a get-out-the-vote initiative.\par \par \uc2 MoveOn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://front.moveon.org/new-moveon-launches-ice-cream-truck-tour-to-give-away-free-ice-cream-and-gotv-for-harris-and-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on Friday}}}\uc2  that it will also be traveling to battleground states with an ice-cream truck, where it will hand out free ice-cream, and raffle off free, limited-edition, autographed pints of Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s Coconut Jubilee \u8211\'20\'13 which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://campaigns.moveon.org/scoop-2024/?_gl=1%2A13qr7xd%2A_gcl_au%2AMTA5MDIzMTAuMTcyNjI1NDQ3Mw..%2A_ga%2ANTEyOTM0MzE1LjE3MjYyNTQ0NzM.%2A_ga_75F6DH82Y3%2AMTcyNjI1NDUwMy4xLjEuMTcyNjI1NTU4OC4wLjAuMA.."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  as a coconut ice-cream with a caramel ripple and confetti stars.\par \par \uc2 enltrTo kick off our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ScoopTheVote?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ScoopTheVote}}}\uc2  campaign, we're raffling off free, limited-edition pints of Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s Coconut Jubilee, a coconut ice cream with a caramel ripple and confetti stars, made by \uc2 Ben Cohen\uc2  & \uc2 Jerry Greenfield\uc2 !\par \par \uc2 Enter here for your chance to win: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eKnQlI4Mvh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eKnQlI4Mvh}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tu29tb7DOO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tu29tb7DOO}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BAjgZTtuOw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BAjgZTtuOw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MoveOn (@MoveOn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MoveOn/status/1834336803014541496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Scoop the Vote tour begins on 16 September in Philadelphia with the founders of \uc2 Ben & Jerry\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Ben Cohen\uc2  and \uc2 Jerry Greenfield\uc2 , the organization said.\par \par \uc2 In addition to free ice-cream and other goodies, the tour will feature elected officials, activists and other special guests, MoveOn said.\par \par \uc2 And on top of the coconut ice-cream, MoveOn will also serve a variety of electorally themed ice-cream flavors, they said, that include: Unburdened by What Has Vanilla Bean, Inauguration Celebration Birthday Cake, Fight for Our Rights Sorbet and MoveOn Mobilizer Milk Chocolate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Despite the efforts of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e454d28f08c69019f64e56#block-66e454d28f08c69019f64e56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 local}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e44fbf8f08c69019f64dfd#block-66e44fbf8f08c69019f64dfd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaders}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has continued to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e47bb48f08c69019f6511b#block-66e47bb48f08c69019f6511b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demonize}}}\uc2  the Haitian community of Springfield, Ohio, vowing at a press conference to carry out \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e480f88f082b0bb978b819#block-66e480f88f082b0bb978b819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large deportations}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in the town if returned to the White House. He also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e47fd58f082b0bb978b805#block-66e47fd58f082b0bb978b805"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended his association}}}\uc2  with Laura Loomer, a conspiracy theorist whose penchant for public displays of racism has unnerved even some of his most extreme allies. At a White House event celebrating Black excellence, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the attacks on Haitians have \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e46dcd8f082b0bb978b6da#block-66e46dcd8f082b0bb978b6da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no place in America}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was on her way to Pennsylvania for more campaign events {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e42f578f08c69019f64bc1#block-66e42f578f08c69019f64bc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this evening}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Some schools in Springfield {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e44a478f08c69019f64da9#block-66e44a478f08c69019f64da9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were reportedly closed}}}\uc2  by administrators for a second day in a row as Trump and his allies spread unproven stories of pet-eating by Haitian migrants.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 People{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e45df28f08c69019f64ed0#block-66e45df28f08c69019f64ed0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanted}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not eating cats\u8221\'20\'1D at a rally held by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , in Michigan yesterday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Haitians have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e468128f082b0bb978b682#block-66e468128f082b0bb978b682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  been intimidated and had their cars vandalized in Springfield since the campaign against them began.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press conference has concluded, but before he wrapped up, the former president was prompted to talk about what he might do for California if he wins the election.\par \par \uc2 Trump turned it into a campaign pitch to Golden State voters, who haven\u8217\'20\'19t backed a Republican presidential candidate since \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2  was on the ballot in 1988:\par \par \uc2 Vote for me, California. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to give you safety. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to give you a great border, and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to give you more water than almost anybody has.\par \par \uc2 Notice the reference to water, an all-important issue in the western state, which is also the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most populous:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/california-water-drought-farm-ground-sinking-tulare-lake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California cracks down on water pumping: \u8216\'20\'18The ground is collapsing\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked again about his association with Laura Loomer, and what he thinks she brings to his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Loomer has pedaled conspiracy theories about the 9/11 attacks, and made racist posts on social media. Nonetheless, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 She brings a spirit to us that a lot of people have. We have very spirited people. And, in all fairness to her, she hates seeing what\u8217\'20\'19s happened to the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump vows 'large deportations' from Ohio town if elected\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  went on to threaten \u8220\'20\'1Clarge deportations\u8221\'20\'1D in Springfield, Ohio, which is home to a large Haitian community that he and his allies have vilified in recent days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can say this: we will do large deportations from Springfield, Ohio, large deportations. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get these people out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Haitians are currently shielded from deportation under the homeland security department\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscis.gov/humanitarian/temporary-protected-status/temporary-protected-status-designated-country-haiti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Temporary Protected Status}}}\uc2  through 3 February 2026, due to their home country\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/aug/02/haiti-gang-wars-un-deployment-foreign-security-forces-quash-violence-rape"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubles}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he has no control over conspiracy theorist Loomer amid criticism of association\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked about his association with Laura Loomer, the rightwing conspiracy theorist who has recently been spotted with him on the campaign trail, prompting complaints from some Republicans who see her as a bad influence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLaura\u8217\'20\'19s been a supporter, just like a lot of people are supporters, and she\u8217\'20\'19s been a supporter of mine. She speaks very positively of the campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t control Laura. Laura has to say what she wants. She\u8217\'20\'19s a she\u8217\'20\'19s a free spirit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the outcry over Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s involvement with the Trump campaign:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/laura-loomer-trump-pet-eating-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans point finger at Laura Loomer for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pet-eating rant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 After talking for nearly an hour, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken his first question.\par \par \uc2 It was hard to hear what was asked, but it seemed to be about criticism from Republicans of his debate performance.\par \par \uc2 Trump insisted that he had done fine: \u8220\'20\'1CMost of my Republican allies had said I was great in the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 While he did not repeat his baseless claim of pet-eating, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a point of attacking the Haitian community in Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpringfield, Ohio, 20,000 illegal Haitian migrants have descended upon a town of 58,000 people, destroying the way of life,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, neglecting to mention that Haitians are protected from deportation and allowed to apply for work permits under a government policy that applies to migrants from unstable countries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople don\u8217\'20\'19t like to talk about it, because even the town doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like to talk about it, it sounds so bad for the town. They live there. They\u8217\'20\'19re proud. They love the town. For years, it was a great place, safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , a Republican who backs Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/13/trump-harris-us-election?page=with:block-66e454d28f08c69019f64e56#block-66e454d28f08c69019f64e56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  the migrants have filled jobs that were looking for workers, and he\u8217\'20\'19s heard positive things about them from employers.\par \par \uc2 This \u8220\'20\'1Cpress conference\u8221\'20\'1D has been going on for well over half an hour now, and Trump has yet to take a question.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign billed this as a press conference, but he has yet to take a question from the reporters who are there.\par \par \uc2 For the past 15 minutes, he\u8217\'20\'19s been attacking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , whom he dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CComrade Kamala\u8221\'20\'1D for her record as San Francisco district attorney, a job she held from 2004 to 2011.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is speaking slowly and clearly, but without as much enthusiasm as he has been known to bring, also unsurprisingly claimed victory in his Tuesday debate with the vice-president, and criticized the moderators from ABC News.\par \par \uc2 From 2019, here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s stints as San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s top prosecutor and attorney general of California:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jan/19/kamala-harris-2020-election-top-cop-prosecutor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris: can a \u8216\'20\'18top cop\u8217\'20\'19 win over progressives in 2020?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 After lengthy delay, Trump begins press conference\par \par \uc2 Following a delay of about 90 minutes, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has started his press conference in Rancho Palos Verdes, California.\par \par \uc2 Before he started speaking, he yielded to Mayor \uc2 John Cruikshank\uc2 , who talked about the struggles of the community, where Trump has a golf course, including landslides.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/california-power-outages-landslide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Gigantic\u8217\'20\'19 landslides hit California coastal town: \u8216\'20\'18Watching their homes crumble\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden also used the term \u8220\'20\'1CBlack jobs\u8221\'20\'1D, seemingly by accident, when addressing attendees at a White House event to celebrate achievements by African Americans.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  first used {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the offensive term}}}\uc2  in his June debate against Biden, where the president performed so poorly he eventually ended his bid for a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn just three and a half years we\u8217\'20\'19ve created just over 2m new Black jobs for Black Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, drawing halting laughter from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, seeming to recover, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next Black job to be filled is as president of the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D The crowd cheered heartily at that.\par \par \uc2 Biden has made similar verbal slips throughout his presidency:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/05/joe-biden-verbal-decline-warning-signs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Warning signs: a history of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s verbal slips}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says attacks on Haitian immigrants have 'no place in America'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hosted a celebration of Black excellence at this White House his afternoon, where he made a point to condemn attacks on Haitian immigrants in Ohio made by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies.\par \par \uc2 The president described Haitian Americans as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity that\u8217\'20\'19s under attack in our country right now\u8221\'20\'1D which he said was \u8220\'20\'1Csimply wrong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no place in America. This has to stop, what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing. It has to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, without mentioning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name.\par \par \uc2 The former president and his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , have claimed that Haitians in the town of Springfield have been eating pets, which local officials say is not true.\par \par \uc2 Vance has also blamed the entire community for the death of a child killed in a car accident involving a Haitian driver, prompting the boy\u8217\'20\'19s father to publicly ask that the tragedy not be used for \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical gain\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/trump-vance-ohio-aiden-clark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Father of Ohio boy, 11, tells Trump and Vance to stop using son\u8217\'20\'19s death for \u8216\'20\'18political gain\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 For the Haitian community in Springfield, Ohio, the unproven claims of pet-eating directed at them by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have had serious consequences, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://haitiantimes.com/2024/09/11/haitian-immigrants-in-ohio-under-racist-attacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Haitian Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The New York-based publication, which focuses on covering the Caribbean nation and its diaspora in the United States, reported that Haitians in Springfield have had their cars vandalized and experienced intimidation since Trump and his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , accused them of eating pets, as part of their campaign to convince voters that immigrants are dangerous. Local officials in Springfield have said that the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 claims are not true.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Haitian Times:\par \par \uc2 The morning after former President \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://haitiantimes.com/2024/09/11/2024-ohio-haitians-featured-in-us-presidential-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated racist claims about Haitians}}}\uc2  in Springfield, Ohio, some Haitian families are keeping their children home from school for their safety, according to an area activist. Those who allowed their children did so, but with heavy hearts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe [my niece] was scared, but I told her to go, that God would protect,\u8221\'20\'1D said one Haitian resident, who asked that she not be identified publicly for fear of reprisal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re all victims this morning,\u8221\'20\'1D said the woman, who moved to Springfield six years ago. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re attacking us in every way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Aside from the anxiety caused by Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, the woman also said her cars have been vandalized twice in the middle of the night. She woke up one morning to broken windows and another to acid thrown on the vehicle. She has added cameras to her driveway and tried to report the incidents to the police to no avail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to have to move because this area is no longer good for me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t even leave my house to go to \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19m anxious and scared.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Haitian families\u8217\'20\'19 accounts, shared with The Haitian Times under condition of confidentiality, are the latest tales of intimidation, bullying and assaults as anti-Haitian sentiment has gone viral.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press conference appears to have been delayed.\par \par \uc2 Broadcast networks now indicate he will speak at 12.45pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to hold first press conference since debate with Harris\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to give a press conference for the first time since his debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19ll speak to reporters at his golf course in Rancho Palos Verdes, California, a wealthy community near Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Expect him to declare that he won his first debate against the vice-president, and perhaps elaborate as to why he has declined her invitation for a second face-off. It\u8217\'20\'19ll also be interesting to see if he mentions the unproven pet-eating allegations he has spread in recent days, or avoids the topic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The apparently bogus story of pet-eating by migrants in Ohio seems to have caught on among Democrats as well, with chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not eating cats\u8221\'20\'1D breaking out at vice-presidential candidate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Michigan yesterday.\par \par \uc2 As captured by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrMore chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not eating cats\u8221\'20\'1D at Walz\u8217\'20\'19s Grand Rapids rally. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PmLrxDQx5X"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PmLrxDQx5X}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dylan Wells (@dylanewells) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dylanewells/status/1834372283785175099?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The crowd is clearly making light of the latest attempt by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to demonize immigrants. Yet though many political analysts see the embrace of the story as a political boondoggle that Trump should avoid, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s allies continue to defend it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s conservative activist Charlie Kirk, who says the chants at Walz\u8217\'20\'19s rally are proof that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19ve broken them\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrDemocrats are now chanting \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not eating cats!\u8221\'20\'1D at their rallies.\par \par \uc2 I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve broken them. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gVC2gZyGWe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gVC2gZyGWe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Charlie Kirk (@charliekirk11) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/charliekirk11/status/1834386274217853156?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, claims he heard the stories of pet-eating migrants in Springfield, Ohio, from his constituents, even though local officials say they are not true. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports that several Republicans believe the true source of the tale is Laura Loomer, a conspiracy theorist with a history of making racist statements:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  are blaming the influence of Laura Loomer, a rightwing conspiracy theorist, for this week\u8217\'20\'19s botched debate performance by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , which included the former president repeating a bizarre and unfounded claim that pet cats and dogs were being eaten by Haitian immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Loomer flew with Trump on his private plane to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate in Philadelphia and has been identified as a key promoter of the pets rumour, which has been dismissed as false by authorities in Springfield, Ohio, where the practice was alleged to have been taking place.\par \par \uc2 However, Trump amplified it in a moment that has become emblematic of his erratic showing in the debate with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , the Democratic nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs, the people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed during a debate segment}}}\uc2  on immigration. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there, and this is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in our country, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the ABC debate moderator David Muir informed him that the story had been debunked, Trump stood by the claim, saying he had seen it \u8220\'20\'1Con television\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The rumour had also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/09/10/nx-s1-5107320/jd-vance-springfield-ohio-haitians-pets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disseminated}}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, who in the aftermath of the debate justified doing so.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, following the event scrutiny has turned to the supposed role of Loomer. The Semafor website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/09/11/2024/republicans-fear-laura-loomer-is-influencing-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  an unnamed source close to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as saying they were \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D concerned about Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s sway over the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/laura-loomer-trump-pet-eating-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans point finger at Laura Loomer for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pet-eating rant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , told CBS News yesterday that he believes Springfield, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, who has said members of the Haitian immigrant community are not eating pets.\par \par \uc2 DeWine also praised the community\u8217\'20\'19s work ethic. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment:\par \par \uc2 enltrOhio Gov. \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , a Republican, says Springfield, Ohio officials "have no evidence" of Haitian migrants eating pets there, a claim amplified by former President Trump during Tuesday night's debate, saying, "I think we go with what the mayor says, he knows his city."\par \par \uc2 "The\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YWRQgSLhh1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YWRQgSLhh1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1833992475905491083?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The governor is nonetheless supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, the Ohio senator who says he learned about the alleged pet-eating from his constituents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the second time in as many days that schools in Springfield have been evacuated, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies press on with their unfounded claims of pet-eating by migrants in the Ohio city.\par \par \uc2 The cause of the evacuations yesterday, which also included city hall, was a bomb threat that turned out to be unfounded, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc6onyourside.com/news/local/springfield-mayor-on-politicians-after-bomb-threat-it-was-their-words-that-did-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  Columbus\u8217\'20\'19s ABC 6.\par \par \uc2 The broadcaster also heard from the town\u8217\'20\'19s Republican mayor, Rob Rue, who said no one\u8217\'20\'19s pets were being eaten in Springfield, and criticized the politicians who spread the story, without naming Trump:\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s just not happening in our community. Pets are safe in our community, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate that there was a spotlight put on a story that was validated that was not true at all \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 When a federal politician has the stage, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t take the opportunity to build up the community instead of inadvertently not understand what their words are, what they\u8217\'20\'19re going to do to the community, it can really hurt the community like it\u8217\'20\'19s hurting ours. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been punched in a way we should not have been punched.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schools evacuated in Ohio town targeted by Trump's baseless pet-eating claims - report\par \par \uc2 Two elementary schools and a middle school have been evacuated or are closed in Springfield, Ohio, the town that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his campaign have baselessly claimed is being menaced by immigrants who eat pets, a Spectrum News affiliate reports.\par \par \uc2 Spectrum reports that the school disruptions were caused by unspecified information received by the police department:\par \par \uc2 enltrContinued threats in Springfield, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpectrumNews1OH?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpectrumNews1OH}}}\uc2  newsroom just received this statement from Springfield City School District saying several school buildings have been evacuated or are closed today "based on information received from the Springfield Police Division." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8uhGXWQmJk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8uhGXWQmJk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taylor Popielarz (@TaylorPopielarz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TaylorPopielarz/status/1834592984832045173?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump and his running mate, JD Vance, who represents Ohio in the Senate, have in recent days accused people from Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s Haitian immigrant community of eating pets, despite denials from city officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  this morning announced it had bought video billboards on the Las Vegas strip and New York\u8217\'20\'19s Times Square to promote \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 Only the former is located in a swing states, but DNC communications director Rosemary Boeglin says the idea is to build on momentum from the debate and turn out voters: \u8220\'20\'1CAs we drive the contrast between Vice-President Harris\u8217\'20\'19s New Way Forward and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 agenda, which would rip away reproductive rights and rig the economy against working families, we\u8217\'20\'19re reminding voters that it is critical to speak now to dump Trump and enter our Kamala era by visiting IWillVote.com and doing their research on how, where and when to vote in this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the Times Square billboard will show:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 To be clear: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  continues to want a second debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice-president is clear she believes there should be another debate and we do not consider this to be the last word from him,\u8221\'20\'1D Brian Fallon, a spokesman for Harris, told Politico. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is just working through his feelings after losing very badly Tuesday night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would do no such thing in a Truth Social post yesterday that involved a lot of capital letters:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/harris-election-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris touts strong debate performance as Trump says he won\u8217\'20\'19t face her again}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign slams Trump for dodging questions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ukraine\par \par \uc2 In a memo released this morning, Harris campaign spokesman Ian Sams said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should be held accountable for his refusal to answer questions dealing with some of the thorniest issues the president faces at Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 Sams cited direct questions to Trump from the moderators about whether he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, or if he wanted Ukraine to win its war against Russia \u8211\'20\'13 both queries to which the former president did not directly respond. Trump also restated his debunked belief that he won the 2020 election, and said that he would seek to repeal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/10/obamacare-supreme-court-aca-what-is-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Affordable Care Act}}}\uc2 , despite only having \u8220\'20\'1Cconcepts\u8221\'20\'1D of a plan to replace it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe debate was a mess for Trump, yes. But these answers are simply toxic. In almost any other circumstance, any one of these answers might drive days of a media crisis for the candidate. Taken together, they are an unmitigated disaster,\u8221\'20\'1D Sams wrote, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump should have to answer for these positions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Perhaps he will, at his press conference set to take place at 12pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris seeks to drive home debate advantage after Trump declines to face off again\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  may have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/harris-election-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put the kibosh on}}}\uc2  another debate against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  yesterday, but the vice-president isn\u8217\'20\'19t letting the matter rest. Yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/kamala-harris-north-carolina-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris told a crowd in North Carolina}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1CI believe we owe it to the voters to have another debate\u8221\'20\'1D, and this morning, her campaign released a memo blasting Trump for the \u8220\'20\'1Ctoxic positions\u8221\'20\'1D he took during their encounter, and saying he should respond to them \u8211\'20\'13 implicitly in the form of another debate against the vice-president. The Harris campaign has said it would be happy to participate in such an event next month, but that would require Trump to reverse his position. Expect the former president to elaborate on the subject around 12pm ET, when he holds a press conference in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris campaigns at 6.35pm ET in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, the swing state that some believe will be the most important in deciding the outcome of this election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, is campaigning in the two other Great Lake swing states, Michigan and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  welcomes the UK prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/keir-starmer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer}}}\uc2 , to the White House at 4.30pm, for his first visit since taking office in July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240913ek9d001uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
