\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Competing  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  measures can appear on November\u8217\'20\'19s ballot, Nebraska supreme court says\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par 17:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 One measure would enshrine the state\u8217\'20\'19s current 12-week ban, while the other would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 24 weeks\par \par \uc2 Nebraska residents will vote this November on two competing ballot measures to expand or limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the state supreme court ruled on Friday.\par \par \uc2 One of the measures that will be put to voters would enshrine Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s current \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which outlaws the procedure past 12 weeks of pregnancy, into the state constitution. The other would amend the state constitution to add the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until fetal viability, or at about 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the Nevada supreme court heard arguments in lawsuits that tried to kick one or both of the measures off the ballot. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters and opponents had tussled in court over whether the measures violated state law that requires ballot measures to address only a single subject, but the supreme court rejected that argument on Friday and found that neither measure broke the law.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska legislators passed the 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in 2023, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/05/20/1177304503/nebraska-12-week-abortion-ban-restrictions-gender-affirming-care"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failing to pass a bill}}}\uc2  that would have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past about six weeks of pregnancy. Without the viability standard, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers could try to get an even stricter ban through the legislature, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates warned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPatients with pregnancy complications after 12 weeks are being delayed and restricted care, or must leave the state to get the help they need \u8211\'20\'13 putting their lives, fertility, and physical and mental health at risk,\u8221\'20\'1D Protect Our Rights, the organization behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measure, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ketv.com/article/nebraska-supreme-court-decisions-abortion-ballot-initiative-challenges/62187055"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Nebraska ruling, which had to be issued by Friday in order to finalize the ballot, tees up an unusually direct showdown in the nationwide fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022, more than a dozen states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned almost all abortions}}}\uc2 . In response, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have started adding pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures to state ballots.\par \par \uc2 So far, they have an unbroken winning streak. States such as Michigan and Ohio have passed ballot measures enshrining the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state constitutions, while voters in states such as Kansas and Kentucky have rejected measures that could curtail the right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 However, no state has overturned a post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban through a ballot measure , and no state has put such dueling measures in front of voters at the same time.\par \par \uc2 Voters in 10 states, including Nebraska, will have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measures on their ballots this year. Democrats are hoping that the measures will drive turnout in key battleground states such as Arizona and Nevada, and Kamala Harris has made support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a key plank in her policy platform.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240913ek9d002e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
