\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says he won\u8217\'20\'19t debate Harris again as candidates hold dueling swing state rallies \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Livingstone (now); Maanvi Singh, Chris Stein, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Lily Bayer (earlier) \par \uc2 7,734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par 09:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump repeats claims he won the matchup to Arizona crowd; Harris says in North Carolina that Americans should see another debate. This blog is now closed.Harris heads to North Carolina as Trump says \u8216\'20\'18there will be no third debate\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing soon, thanks for joining us. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s main developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced he would not participate in a second debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying she has turned down previous opportunities to meet and alleging she lost their Tuesday night face-off. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e325e78f082b0bb978a986#block-66e325e78f082b0bb978a986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A new Reuters/Ipsos poll}}}\uc2  found Harris the overall winner of the Tuesday evening face-off, and slightly improving her lead nationally.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e332868f082dce7ae32553#block-66e332868f082dce7ae32553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed the influence of Laura Loomer}}}\uc2 , a rightwing conspiracy theorist, for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s botched debate performance on Tuesday. The Semafor website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/09/11/2024/republicans-fear-laura-loomer-is-influencing-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  an unnamed source close to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as saying they were \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D concerned about Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s sway over the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Springfield, Ohio, said a bomb threat that forced the evacuation of the city hall and other buildings on Thursday, had used \u8220\'20\'1Chateful language\u8221\'20\'1D towards Haitians and other immigrants. Springfield was thrust into the spotlight this week after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other Republicans including JD Vance promoted the false rumour that immigrants in the city are eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e3432a8f082b0bb978aa69#block-66e3432a8f082b0bb978aa69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had two counts tossed from his criminal case}}}\uc2  in Georgia over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election, after the presiding judge decided on Thursday they fell under the supremacy clause in the US constitution that bars state prosecutors from charging federal crimes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e317148f0841a3e811dd87#block-66e317148f0841a3e811dd87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed in his latest attempt}}}\uc2  to lift the limited gag order imposed on him by Juan Merchan, the judge who presided over the trial in which the former president was convicted of 34 felony counts of falsifying business records to conceal hush-money payments. New York\u8217\'20\'19s appeals court declined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request today \u8220\'20\'1Cupon the ground that no substantial constitutional question is directly involved\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A North Dakota judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e31c548f082dce7ae323fe#block-66e31c548f082dce7ae323fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down its near-total ban on abortions}}}\uc2 , saying the state constitution protects some access to the procedure, and the law as written is vague, the Associated Press reports. District judge Bruce Romanick\u8217\'20\'19s decision comes in a lawsuit filed by North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s sole \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, which has moved to neighboring Minnesota since the ban was signed by Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The joint session of Congress scheduled for 6 January 2025 to count and certify electoral votes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e30ca58f080c42b80d1130#block-66e30ca58f080c42b80d1130"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be considered}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational special security event\u8221\'20\'1D by the homeland security department, all because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/23/jan-6-panel-final-report-trump-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what happened last time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alberto Gonzales, a Republican who served as attorney general under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e2e4af8f087250b15aa0c1#block-66e2e4af8f087250b15aa0c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  he will vote for Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CAs the United States approaches a critical election, I can\u8217\'20\'19t sit quietly as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps the most serious threat to the rule of law in a generation \u8211\'20\'13 eyes a return to the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a column for Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 The mayor of Springfield, Ohio, has said a bomb threat that led to the evacuation of City Hall and numerous buildings on Thursday \u8220\'20\'1Cused hateful language towards immigrants and Haitians in our community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpringfield is a community that needs help,\u8221\'20\'1D mayor Rob Rue told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/12/bomb-threat-springfield-ohio-haitian-immigrants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 . The mayor added that national leaders should provide that help and not \u8220\'20\'1Churt a community like, unfortunately, we have seen over the last couple of days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Springfield was thrust into the spotlight this week after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other Republicans including vice presidential candidate JD Vance promoted the false rumour that immigrants in the city are eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the stage in Greensboro, North Carolina, and immediately brought up this week\u8217\'20\'19s debate and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision not to take part in another.\par \par \uc2 We \u8220\'20\'1Cowe it to the voters\u8221\'20\'1D to have another, she said, to big applause from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 She also talked more about her past as a prosecutor and her plans for new home-owners and small businesses: \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the courtroom to the White House, my client have been the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will always put the middle-class and working-class families first, I know where I came from,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m clear about that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has rebuked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his association with far-right conspiracy theorist Laura Loomer, who has been traveling with him this week and who has been identified as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/laura-loomer-trump-pet-eating-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key promoter of the false rumour}}}\uc2  that immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, have been eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 Before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday, Loomer made racist comments about Harris, who is of Indian descent, saying that if she won the 5 November election, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe White House will smell like curry & White House speeches will be facilitated via a call center\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is repugnant, these types of comments, it is un-American to say these types of things, exactly the kind of hateful and divisive rhetoric that we should denounce,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House spokesperson, said on Thursday, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo leader should ever associate with someone who spreads this kind of ugliness, this kind of racist poison,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Tucson rally, Trump also promised to eliminate taxes on overtime pay.\par \par \uc2 But it is unclear how such a policy would work. It is also worth noting that Project 2025, the platform devised for a second Trump term, seeks to make overtime \u8211\'20\'13 also known as time-and-a-half pay \u8211\'20\'13 more confusing for workers to navigate and would likely reduce the number of workers eligible for overtime.\par \par \uc2 From PolitiFact:\par \par \uc2 The plan doesn\u8217\'20\'19t call for banning overtime wages. It recommends changes to some \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2 , or \uc2 OSHA\uc2 , regulations and to overtime rules. Some changes, if enacted, could result in some people losing overtime protections, experts told us.\par \par \uc2 The document proposes that the Labor Department maintain an overtime threshold \u8220\'20\'1Cthat does not punish businesses in lower-cost regions (e.g., the southeast United States).\u8221\'20\'1D This threshold is the amount of money executive, administrative or professional employees need to make for an employer to exempt them from overtime pay under the Fair Labor Standards Act.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert Reich, the former US labor secretary, responded to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s incendiary claims about immigrants by noting that immigrants make up about a fifth of the country\u8217\'20\'19s essential workforce.\par \par \uc2 A 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fwd.us/news/immigrant-essential-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the bipartisan immigration and criminal justice reform group Fwd.us estimated that one in five essential workers were immigrants, including in the medical, agriculture and food service industries. The group also estimated that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than two-thirds of all undocumented immigrant workers serve in frontline jobs in essential industries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrAmerica is prosperous largely BECAUSE of immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 23 million immigrants are considered essential workers \u8212\'20\'14 that's 1 in 5 individuals in the total U.S. essential workforce.\par \par \uc2 They should be lauded for their importance and commitment to our country, not demonized. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Fog9ip5ytx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Fog9ip5ytx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Reich (@RBReich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RBReich/status/1834347504424357954?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 At his event in Tucson, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is repeating many of his rote lines about the US-Mexico border, accusing arrivals at the southern border of \u8220\'20\'1Cstealing\u8221\'20\'1D jobs and falsely accusing immigrants overall of driving up crime rates.\par \par \uc2 In a city that is not far from the border, Trump doubled down on his racist denigration of immigrants and asylum seekers.\par \par \uc2 He also repeated misinformation about immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, \u8220\'20\'1Cwalking off\u8221\'20\'1D with geese in the town\u8217\'20\'19s public parks and with residents\u8217\'20\'19 pets. The hoax can be traced back to a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post that has been debunked. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assertion during the debate that immigrants \u8220\'20\'1Care eating the dogs \u8230\'20\'26 they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats\u8221\'20\'1D has been widely ridiculed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Markwayne Mullin, the US senator from Oklahoma, would not say whether he would accept a peaceful transfer of power if Trump were to lose and every state certified the result.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Pamela Brown, Mullin repeated election misinformation and made vague references to \u8220\'20\'1Cirregularities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI asked Sen. Markwayne Mullin if he would vote to certify November's election results once every state has certified them.\par \par \uc2 His response: "It's hard to say." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SLHHIfTohR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SLHHIfTohR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pamela Brown (@PamelaBrownCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PamelaBrownCNN/status/1834335275897815165?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks in Tucson at first post-debate rally\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now in Tucson, Arizona, for a rally \u8211\'20\'13 his first since his debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Arizona is a key swing state that both candidates will want to secure. Tucson, however, leans heavily Democratic. Second gentleman Doug Emhoff also scheduled a visit to the city today on behalf of the Harris-Walz campaign.\par \par \uc2 The former president, who is widely judged as having fumbled his debate against Harris, began by airing his frustrations on stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolls clearly show that I won the debate against Comrade Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. Early or flash polls after the debate found that, in fact, viewers largely thought that Harris had won the debate. Trump also called moderators David Muir and Linsey Davis \u8220\'20\'1Clowlives\u8221\'20\'1D for fact-checking him during the debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Steve Sadow has released a statement on the ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump and his legal team in Georgia have prevailed once again. The trial court has decided that counts 15 and 27 in the indictment must be quashed/dismissed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Two of the charges brought against Trump by \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney, for allegedly trying to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 elections were dropped.\par \par \uc2 The dropped charges dealt with filing false documents in federal court. But the judge in the case allowed eight other allegations against the former president to stand.\par \par \uc2 Correction: A previous version of this post quoted Sadow saying that counts 15 and 17 were dismissed. Sadow corrected the quote and we updated this post to reflect that the counts were actually 15 and 27.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is important that the vice-president continues to define and expose Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Bernie Sanders wrote in an op-ed for the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1C But it may not be enough to secure a victory. Voters are hungry for a candidate that will deliver meaningful, material change to their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator writes:\par \par \uc2 I applaud Harris for laying out the fundamentals of her economic vision: she promised to cap the cost of prescription drugs for all Americans at $2,000, address the severe housing crisis we face by building 3m units of affordable housing, eliminate medical debt, and take on corporate price gouging that has made it impossible for working families to afford groceries and other basic necessities.\par \par \uc2 The American people want change, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what Harris must deliver\par \par \uc2 These are valuable policies. I believe, however, that her chances of winning improve if she expands that agenda to include popular solutions to the most important economic and political realities facing this country.\par \par \uc2 The American people want change, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what she must deliver.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/12/kamala-harris-debate-bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris was great in the debate. Will that be enough to win? | Bernie Sanders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , riding high off \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s poor debate performance, has honed in on one line from her opponent:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris: "He said! He said! Concepts of a plan!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pMTCNU1Rf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pMTCNU1Rf5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1834321855592706170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 During the debate this week, moderator Linsey Davis asked Trump to detail his new approach to healthcare \u8211\'20\'13 which he had repeatedly promised to deliver in his previous two presidential runs.\par \par \uc2 When Trump equivocated, Davis doubled down: \u8220\'20\'1CSo just a yes or no,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou still do not have a plan?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have concepts of a plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 The fumble was especially unfortunate given that surrogates and advisers talked up the president\u8217\'20\'19s dedication to talk policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says 'we owe it to the voters to have another' debate with Trump\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just took the stage at a rally in Charlotte, North Carolina, where she continued to push \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to debate again, despite his announcement that he would not do so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo nights ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I had our first debate, And I believe we owe it to the voters to have another debate, because this election and what is at stake could not be more important,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said to applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia judge dismisses some charges against Trump in election meddling case\par \par \uc2 An Atlanta-area judge dismissed two of the charges brought against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney, for allegedly trying to overturn Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 elections, but allowed the rest of the case to proceed, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The charges dismissed by judge Scott McAfee deal with filing false documents in federal court. McAfee allowed eight other allegations against the former president to stand.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will not debate Harris again\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced he will not participate in a second debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying she has turned down previous opportunities to meet and alleging she lost their Tuesday night face-off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a prizefighter loses a fight, the first words out of his mouth are, \u8216\'20\'18I WANT A REMATCH.\u8217\'20\'19 Polls clearly show that I won the Debate against Comrade \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Radical Left Candidate, on Tuesday night, and she immediately called for a Second Debate,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113126153368079486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Truth Social}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump restated his much-repeated claim that Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroyed our Country\u8221\'20\'1D, then said:\par \par \uc2 Everyone knows this, and all of the other problems caused by Kamala and Joe - It was discussed in great detail during the First Debate with Joe, and the Second Debate with Comrade Harris. She was a no-show at the Fox Debate, and refused to do NBC & CBS. KAMALA SHOULD FOCUS ON WHAT SHE SHOULD HAVE DONE DURING THE LAST ALMOST FOUR YEAR PERIOD. THERE WILL BE NO THIRD DEBATE!\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has previously said she would be willing to debate Trump again sometime in October. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance remains scheduled to debate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential nominee, on 1 October in New York.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign says support is increasing in swing states following debate\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pollsters say support for the former president has increased in swing states since his debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.donaldjtrump.com/news/4c4bdd07-0a56-4451-a726-fc20c352e5bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a memo}}}\uc2 , Tony Fabrizio and Travis Tunis write that the candidates were tied before the debate, but after surveying 1,893 likely voters in seven swing states, Trump now leads Harris 48% to 46% when third-party candidates are included, and 50% to 47% in a head-to-head matchup.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, target state voters were not impressed by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 empty platitudes and while the media would have people believe she is cruising to victory, this couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be farther from the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D the pollsters write.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A bomb threat prompted the evacuation and closure of the city hall in Springfield, Ohio, which has been thrust into national focus after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed false and unsubstantiated claims}}}\uc2  of Haitian immigrants in the city eating pets and local wildlife.\par \par \uc2 The bomb threat \u8220\'20\'1Cwas issued to multiple facilities throughout Springfield\u8221\'20\'1D, the city said.\par \par \uc2 We ask the community to avoid the area surrounding City Hall vicinity while the investigation is ongoing and to report any suspicious activity to the Springfield Police Division.\par \par \uc2 The city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Rob Rue, indicated that the threat included complaints about Haitian immigrants in the city, according to NBC News.\par \par \uc2 Local police and officials have said there were no credible reports of Haitian immigrants stealing pets to eat them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans are blaming the influence of Laura Loomer, a rightwing conspiracy theorist, for this week\u8217\'20\'19s botched debate performance by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which included the former president repeating a bizarre and unfounded claim that pet cats and dogs were being eaten by Haitian immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Loomer flew with Trump on his private plane to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate in Philadelphia and has been identified as a key promoter of the pets rumour, which has been dismissed as false by authorities in Springfield, Ohio, where the practice was alleged to have been taking place.\par \par \uc2 The Semafor website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/09/11/2024/republicans-fear-laura-loomer-is-influencing-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted}}}\uc2  an unnamed source close to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as saying they were \u8220\'20\'1C100%\u8221\'20\'1D concerned about Loomer\u8217\'20\'19s sway over the Republican nominee. \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of any guardrails the Trump campaign has put on her, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s working,\u8221\'20\'1D the source said.\par \par \uc2 Trump this year proposed giving Loomer an official role on his campaign, but the idea was resisted by staffers. Loomer, who styles herself as an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestigative journalist\u8221\'20\'1D, last year promoted a conspiracy theory alleging that 9/11 was an \u8220\'20\'1Cinside job\u8221\'20\'1D. On Wednesday she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LauraLoomer/status/1833723601800855732"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  an unfounded allegation that Harris had worn earphones disguised as earrings during the debate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/laura-loomer-trump-pet-eating-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans point finger at Laura Loomer for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pet-eating rant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  following the debate on Tuesday drove hundreds of thousands of people to voter-registration resources, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 Swift\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post included a link to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vote.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vote.gov}}}\uc2 , the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s voting registration site. According to the \uc2 General Services Administration\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 There were a total of 405,999 visitors referred to vote.gov from the custom URL created and shared by Ms Swift during the 24 hour period the post was live.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-harris-endorsement-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s Harris endorsement has thrilled fans \u8211\'20\'13 but will it move the election needle?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e2af788f08e370bfa989f5#block-66e2af788f08e370bfa989f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back to the campaign trail}}}\uc2  for both \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , two days after their first and perhaps only debate. The vice-president has two events planned for this afternoon in North Carolina, while Trump will be in Arizona. Speaking of the debate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e325e78f082b0bb978a986#block-66e325e78f082b0bb978a986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new Reuters/Ipsos poll}}}\uc2  finds Harris the overall winner of the Tuesday evening face-off, and slightly improving her lead nationally. In the legal arena, a New York appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e317148f0841a3e811dd87#block-66e317148f0841a3e811dd87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just rejected}}}\uc2  another attempt by Trump to get the gag order imposed on him in his hush-money case lifted.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Dakota \u8217\'20\'19s strict ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e31c548f082dce7ae323fe#block-66e31c548f082dce7ae323fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was tossed out}}}\uc2  by a judge who said it ran afoul of the state constitution and was vague.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The joint session of Congress scheduled for 6 January 2025 to count and certify electoral votes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e30ca58f080c42b80d1130#block-66e30ca58f080c42b80d1130"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be considered}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational special security event\u8221\'20\'1D by the homeland security department, all because of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/23/jan-6-panel-final-report-trump-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what happened last time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alberto Gonzales, a Republican who served as attorney general under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/12/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-election-debate-news-updates?page=with:block-66e2e4af8f087250b15aa0c1#block-66e2e4af8f087250b15aa0c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  he will vote for Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polls finds Harris victorious in debate, building lead over Trump nationally\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/harris-builds-lead-over-trump-voters-see-her-debate-winner-reutersipsos-poll-2024-09-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters}}}\uc2  is out with one of the first polls since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  debated on Tuesday evening, and found voters view the vice-president as the winner in the debate, where Trump came off as the less sharp candidate.\par \par \uc2 Harris is also building her lead among registered voters nationally to 47% over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 42%, a slight jump from previous weeks, according to the survey, which was conducted with \uc2 Ipsos\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about it:\par \par \uc2 The two-day poll showed Harris with a five percentage point lead among registered voters, just above the four-point advantage she had over Trump in an Aug 21-28 Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 Among voters who said they had heard at least something about Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate, 53% said Harris won and 24% said Trump won. Some 52% of respondents said that Trump stumbled and didn\u8217\'20\'19t appear sharp, while 21% said that of Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris, 59, put Trump, 78, on the defensive with a stream of attacks on his fitness for office and his myriad legal woes.\par \par \uc2 The poll surveyed 1,690 US adults nationwide, including 1,405 registered voters. It had a margin of error of around three percentage points for registered voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  traveled to Shanksville, Pennsylvania, yesterday on somber business: laying a wreath at the site where Flight 93, one of the planes hijacked on 9/11, crashed.\par \par \uc2 He then traveled to the local fire station, where the mood lightened considerably when the 81-year-old president met a similarly mature resident, who was wearing a Trump cap.\par \par \uc2 Biden offered the man, whose name reporters did not catch, a hat with the presidential seal on it, prompting the old-timer to ask the president for an autograph.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou remember your name?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked the president. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t remember my name, I\u8217\'20\'19m slow,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden replied. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re an old fart!\u8221\'20\'1D the resident told him. \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I know, man, I\u8217\'20\'19m an old guy,\u8221\'20\'1D the president gamely replied.\par \par \uc2 After more banter, the pair traded hats, with Biden putting a red Trump cap over one he was already wearing, before advising the room not to eat dogs or cats (cuisine that is not so bad, the elderly resident advised him).\par \par \uc2 Watch the exchange here:\par \par \uc2 A White House spokesperson later said Biden had put on the hat in a show of \u8220\'20\'1Cbipartisan unity\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrAt the Shanksville Fire Station, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  spoke about the country's bipartisan unity after 9/11 and said we needed to get back to that.\par \par \uc2 As a gesture, he gave a hat to a Trump supporter who then said that in the same spirit, POTUS should put on his Trump cap. He briefly wore it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7VKZnkVMY7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7VKZnkVMY7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Bates (@AndrewJBates46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewJBates46/status/1833949159730073638?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge strikes down North Dakota's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 A North Dakota judge struck down its near-total ban on abortions, saying the state constitution protects some access to the procedure, and the law as written is vague, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 District judge Bruce Romanick \u8217\'20\'19s decision comes in a lawsuit filed by North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s sole \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, which has moved to neighboring Minnesota since the ban was signed by Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  in 2022. Burgum made a failed run for the Republican presidential nomination this year, and has since become a top surrogate to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Appeals court rejects Trump's attempt to lift gag order in hush-money case\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has failed in his latest attempt to lift the limited gag order imposed on him by Juan Merchan, the judge who presided over the trial in which the former president was convicted of 34 felony counts of falsifying business records to conceal hush-money payments.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s appeals court declined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request today \u8220\'20\'1Cupon the ground that no substantial constitutional question is directly involved\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly complained about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/25/trump-partial-gag-order-lift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the gag order}}}\uc2 , which prevents him from making public statements about the case\u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors, court staff and their families.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The top House Democrat, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , said the homeland security department\u8217\'20\'19s designation of the upcoming January 6 joint session of Congress as a \u8220\'20\'1C national special security event\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessary \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He cited \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of fraud in his 2020 election loss, and the possibility he may make the same allegations if he loses in November:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJeffries?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepJeffries}}}\uc2  on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DHSgov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DHSgov}}}\uc2  designating January 6th Election Certification as a National Special Security Event: "Yes. I think evaluating the facts...that this designation by national security professionals seems to have been necessary." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4HY9rg7HHc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4HY9rg7HHc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1834238134592078307?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Homeland security gives Congress top protection for upcoming 6 January 2025 joint session\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.secretservice.gov/newsroom/releases/2024/09/2025-counting-and-certification-electoral-votes-designated-national"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced yesterday}}}\uc2  that the joint session of Congress scheduled for 6 January 2025 to certify the winner of the November election will be given high-level protection as a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational special security event\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The January event be the first gathering of senators and House representatives to count electoral votes since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters attacked the Capitol on the same day in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The designation puts the Secret Service in charge of security for the day and allows \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant resources from the federal government, as well as from state and local partners\u8221\'20\'1D, to be deployed, the homeland security department said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNational special security events are events of the highest national significance,\u8221\'20\'1D the special agent in charge of the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s dignitary protective division, Eric Ranaghan, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 , in collaboration with our federal, state and local partners, are committed to developing and implementing a comprehensive and integrated security plan to ensure the safety and security of this event and its participants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officers battled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters throughout the building in 2021, and had this to say about the designation:\par \par \uc2 This national special security event (NSSE) designation will help us build on the plans that we have already put into place to protect the members of Congress and the constitutional process on January 6. Our department has made more than 100 improvements during the last few years to prepare for anything. We are working closely with our law enforcement partners, as we do during other NSSEs such as the State of the Union, to ensure the legislative process goes smoothly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the most important viewers of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  were voters living in the swing states expected to decide the election.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-obordo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Obordo}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nyima-jobe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nyima Jobe}}}\uc2  heard from several about who they thought came out on top. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what they had to say:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/swing-state-voters-debate-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Swing state voters respond to the presidential debate: \u8216\'20\'18Trump couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even look at her!\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The occupant of the White House is not all that voters will decide in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Thirty-four Senate elections will be held in states nationwide, which will determine if Democrats hold on to their 51-seat majority in the chamber. It has long been viewed as a difficult task for the party, since they are believed to have slim chances of picking up a seat, and are almost certain to lose one thanks to Democrat Joe Manchin \u8217\'20\'19s retirement in deep-red West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/senate/montana-senate/montana-senate-moves-lean-republican-gop-increasingly-favored-win?check_logged_in=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today forecast}}}\uc2  that the Senate is likely to flip to GOP control, thanks to polling that shows Republican \uc2 Tim Sheehy\uc2  overtaking \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , the Democrat running for a fourth term in red state Montana:\par \par \uc2 But today we are making a major shift \u8211\'20\'13 moving the Montana Senate race from Toss Up to Lean Republican. This means that Republicans are now an even heavier favorite to win back control of the Senate, regardless of the result at the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 Montana Sen \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  has been a political unicorn for nearly two decades, but in a presidential year with an even more polarized electorate, he is now the underdog heading into the final stretch of the race to his Republican opponent, former Navy SEAL \uc2 Tim Sheehy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, Sen \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  has consistently led in public polling over his GOP challenger, Bernie Moreno, but it\u8217\'20\'19s within the margin of error. While Sheehy appears to have consolidated enough Republican and Trump voters behind him \u8211\'20\'13 an easier lift given the state\u8217\'20\'19s far deeper red hue \u8211\'20\'13 there is still work for Moreno to do in the final weeks. And the key difference may be that Sheehy has been doing work to hone his positive image with voters while Moreno has left many attacks on his character and business record unanswered.\par \par \uc2 A loss in only Montana would give Republicans an outright majority of 51 seats, and their ranks could possibly climb as high as 54. The range of possible pickups is now between one and four for Republicans. At this point, a GOP gain of two to three seats is the likeliest scenario, but this could change in the coming weeks once polls tighten and candidates solidify their bases and woo undecided voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is also planning to sit for media interviews with local news outlets across the battleground states, the memo said. Next week she will participate in an interview with the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Harris was unable to attend the group\u8217\'20\'19s convention in July, which took place just days after she became the Democratic nominee. Trump participated, however, and shocked the room of \uc2 NABJ\uc2  reporters by attacking Harris\u8217\'20\'19s biracial identity and insulting the hosts.\par \par \uc2 During the debate on Tuesday, Trump was asked about his comments, in which he suggested Harris had \u8220\'20\'1Cturned Black\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump replied that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t care how Harris identified, then repeated his claim that the vice-president, the daughter of a Jamaican economist who graduated from one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most prestigious Black colleges, hadn\u8217\'20\'19t identified as Black until recently.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who is Black and south Asian, did not engage with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false assertions about her identity. Instead she called it a \u8220\'20\'1Ctragedy\u8221\'20\'1D that he sought to use \u8220\'20\'1Crace to divide the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris sets 'aggressive' campaign schedule after debate\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign is embarking on an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive\u8221\'20\'1D new phase, building off of the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s commanding performance in Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to a memo released this morning, the campaign is launching a \u8220\'20\'1CNew Way Forward\u8221\'20\'1D tour that begins on Thursday with two stops in North Carolina, a Republican-leaning state where Harris has shown strength. On Friday, Harris will return to Pennsylvania for events in Johnstown and Wilkes-Barre.\par \par \uc2 The stepped-up battleground state travel will be paired with a series of new TV and digital advertisements featuring moments from the debate, the first of which, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g8Dt_UJLjlY&themeRefresh=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leadership,}}}\uc2  aired on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 It features moments from the debate, including the vice-president saying Americans are seeing \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo very different visions for the country: one that is focused on the future, one that is focused on the past\u8221\'20\'1D. The ad then cuts to Trump saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re a failing nation. A nation that is dying. We\u8217\'20\'19re a nation that\u8217\'20\'19s in serious decline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The campaign, newly energized after Harris\u8217\'20\'19s performance, said it spent hours on Wednesday reviewing footage of the debate, culling what it believes are revealing exchanges that show Trump on the defensive and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s offering a vision for the future.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is spending today in North Carolina, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll hold campaign events in Charlotte and Greensboro.\par \par \uc2 The first appearance begins at 3.40pm ET, and the second at 5.40pm.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is at the White House, and will hold an event to mark the 30th anniversary of the Violence Against Women Act at 5.45pm. The press briefing is scheduled for 2.30pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tens of millions of Americans watched Tuesday evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and so, too, did European diplomats looking for an idea of which direction the country might take under whoever wins, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/patrickwintour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Wintour}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The TV debate between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was as keenly watched by European diplomats and politicians as by US voters, eager to see who may be next in the White House and \u8211\'20\'13 crucially \u8211\'20\'13 the direction that a vital ally may next take.\par \par \uc2 One diplomat said they empathised when Harris adopted a series of poses that ranged from pity, bemusement and genuine curiosity about what craziness would emerge from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mouth next as she listened to his conspiracy-laden theories. However, the diplomat said they still did not underestimate Trump and the hold he had over one part of a divided America, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CNever write him off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another European observer judged Harris to have been the victor in the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CObjectively on any count she won. She showed her teeth, broke with [Joe] Biden and showed she is a leader, and that is something Americans love,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 In Germany, Michael Roth, the Social Democratic party chair of the Bundestag foreign affairs committee, said Harris had succeeded in making Trump seem \u8220\'20\'1Clike an ageing incumbent, old, angry and confused\u8221\'20\'1D, despite having been in government herself for much of the past four years. \u8220\'20\'1CHarris has dismantled Trump on the open stage and positioned herself as a candidate of change. She deliberately provoked Trump, and he fell into the trap,\u8221\'20\'1D Roth said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-debate-europe-diplomats-us-ukraine-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe watches Harris-Trump debate for clues on direction US may take}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative billionaire \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  announces push to 'crush liberal dominance' in US\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/0b38aaed-ec58-40cd-9047-0c7b7b83164a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 , \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the conservative activist who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/aug/09/leonard-leo-federalist-society-manipulates-free-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 involved in the effort}}}\uc2  to build the current rightwing supermajority on the supreme court, says he will spend $1b to fight liberal cultural influence in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to crush liberal dominance where it\u8217\'20\'19s most insidious, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll direct resources to build talent and capital formation pipelines in the areas of news and entertainment, where leftwing extremism is most evident,\u8221\'20\'1D Leo told the FT in a rare interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExpect us to increase support for organisations that call out companies and financial institutions that bend to the woke mind virus spread by regulators and NGOs, so that they have to pay a price for putting extreme leftwing ideology ahead of consumers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/25121805/grant_review_letter_final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter obtained by Axios}}}\uc2 , Leo writes that his 85 Fund will review its support of rightwing groups, saying it wants to prioritize efforts to \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponize the conservative vision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 85 Fund intends to gap-fill by placing much, much greater emphasis on projects and leaders that operationalize or weaponize ideas and policies, much in the same way the Left has,\u8221\'20\'1D Leo wrote.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have attempted to get Leo to testify about his activities, but he has so far frustrated them:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/12/billionaire-leonard-leo-rejects-senate-subpoena-supreme-court-gifts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Billionaire Leonard Leo rejects Senate subpoena over supreme court gifts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican former attorney general Gonzales says he will vote for Harris\par \par \uc2 Alberto Gonzales, the attorney general under Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , says he will vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gonzales made the announcement with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2024/09/12/alberto-gonzales-kamala-harris-endorsement-00178746?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a column in Politico}}}\uc2 , where he wrote:\par \par \uc2 As the United States approaches a critical election, I can\u8217\'20\'19t sit quietly as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps the most serious threat to the rule of law in a generation \u8211\'20\'13 eyes a return to the White House. For that reason, though I\u8217\'20\'19m a Republican, I\u8217\'20\'19ve decided to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 His reasons center less on support for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s policies than disgust with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s actions, including his involvement in January 6:\par \par \uc2 Trump failed to do his duty and exercise his presidential power to protect members of Congress, law enforcement and the Capitol from the attacks that day. He failed to deploy executive branch personnel to save lives and property and preserve democracy. He just watched on television and chose not to do anything because that would have been contrary to his interests. Trump still describes that day as beautiful. And as for those subsequently convicted of committing crimes, he describes them as hostages.\par \par \uc2 His felony convictions:\par \par \uc2 Any discussion about fidelity to the rule of law has to include Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 34 state felony convictions, his state civil financial judgment of libel based on sexual abuse, as well as the pending federal elections interference case, not to mention the recently dismissed federal documents case that Special Counsel Jack Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/08/26/jack-smith-appeal-trump-classified-documents-case-00176380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is continuing to pursue}}}\uc2 . Standing alone, these charges, convictions and judgments show that Trump is someone who fails to act, time and time again, in accordance with the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 And the fact that so many of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s senior officials have turned against him:\par \par \uc2 To be fair, I have spoken with Trump only once. I do not really know him. It is telling, however, that several senior officials who worked for him in the White House now refuse to support him, including his vice president, chief of staff, defense secretary and national security adviser. Their unwillingness to endorse their former boss is an indictment of his character at a level equal to his many, many criminal indictments.\par \par \uc2 Gonzales, interestingly, also says he thinks the supreme court should adopt \u8220\'20\'1Ca tougher ethics code of disclosure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the ongoing controversy over the justices\u8217\'20\'19 ethics:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/biden-supreme-court-reforms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to reportedly push for supreme court term limits and new ethics code}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Axios has obtained a letter from the White House News Photographers Association to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top aides, complaining about a lack of access to the vice-president as she campaigns for the White House:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: In an Aug. 28 letter obtained by Axios, the WH News Photographers Association said Harris' team was engaging in an "unprecedented reduction in access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The VP\u8217\'20\'19s team didn\u8217\'20\'19t respond until last night after we asked about the letter\par \par \uc2 W/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarafischer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @sarafischer}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OOch8LDqWX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OOch8LDqWX}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qkl5MaStBr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qkl5MaStBr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Thompson (@AlexThomp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexThomp/status/1834181718435139786?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJessica Koscielniak, the president of the WHNPA, wrote to Harris' top aides last month protesting that "the four independent news photographer seats have been downgraded to one."\par \par \uc2 She proposed either adding a "chaser plane" for additional media or the WHCA reorganizing who gets a\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OZL99bKHwy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OZL99bKHwy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Thompson (@AlexThomp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexThomp/status/1834182559317508538?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The complaints are reminiscent of those made by reporters at the Democratic national convention in Chicago last month, where there were fewer accommodations for the press in the venue than at July\u8217\'20\'19s Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first ballots of the presidential race were mailed to voters yesterday in Alabama, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-2024-first-ballots-voting-alabama-mail-1ef4f9694cc5edbb07fd3d641d6d248e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 North Carolina was expected to be the first state to mail out its ballots, but \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s successful court challenge to remove his name caused a delay.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Young women are more liberal than they have been in decades, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Over the past few years, about 4 in 10 young women between the ages of 18 and 29 have described their political views as liberal, compared with two decades ago when about 3 in 10 identified that way, according to a Gallup analysis of polling data.\par \par \uc2 The share of young women who hold liberal views on the environment, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , race relations and gun laws has also jumped by double digits, Gallup found.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46am BST\par \par \uc2 X\u8217\'20\'19s AI chatbot spread voter misinformation \u8211\'20\'13 and election officials fought back\par \par \uc2 Soon after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced he was ending his bid for re-election, misinformation started spreading online about whether a new candidate could take the president\u8217\'20\'19s place.\par \par \uc2 Screenshots that claimed a new candidate could not be added to ballots in nine states moved quickly around \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2 , racking up millions of views. The Minnesota secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office began getting requests for fact-checks of these posts, which were flat-out wrong \u8211\'20\'13 ballot deadlines had not passed, giving \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  plenty of time to have her name added to ballots.\par \par \uc2 The source of the misinformation: \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chatbot, Grok. When users asked the artificial intelligence tool whether a new candidate still had time to be added to ballots, Grok gave the incorrect answer.\par \par \uc2 Finding the source \u8211\'20\'13 and working to correct it \u8211\'20\'13 served as a test case of how election officials and artificial intelligence companies will interact during the 2024 presidential election in the US amid fears that AI could mislead or distract voters. And it showed the role Grok, specifically, could play in the election, as a chatbot with fewer guardrails to prevent the generating of more inflammatory content.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/twitter-ai-bot-grok-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a de facto Russian asset, \uc2 FBI\uc2  official he fired suggests\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can be seen as a Russian asset, though not in the traditional sense of an active agent or a recruited resource, an ex-\uc2 FBI\uc2  deputy director who worked under the former US president said.\par \par \uc2 Asked on a podcast if he thought it possible Trump was a Russian asset, \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/mar/16/andrew-mccabe-former-fbi-director-fired-russia-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump fired as FBI deputy director}}}\uc2  in 2018, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI do, I do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that I would characterize it as [an] active, recruited, knowing asset in the way that people in the intelligence community think of that term. But I do think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has given us many reasons to question his approach to the Russia problem in the United States, and I think his approach to interacting with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , be it phone calls, face-to-face meetings, the things that he has said in public about Putin, all raise significant questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McCabe was speaking to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.onedecision.com/podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One Decision podcast}}}\uc2 , co-hosted by Sir \uc2 Richard Dearlove\uc2 , a former head of MI6, the British intelligence service.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/trump-russia-putin-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign publicly claims debate win but aides privately express doubts\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign publicly claimed victory in the debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday night, but at least some of his aides privately conceded it was unlikely that he persuaded any undecided voters to break for him, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill tonight benefit us? No, it will not,\u8221\'20\'1D one Trump aide said.\par \par \uc2 The sentiment summed up the predicament for the Trump campaign that with 55 days until the election, Trump is still casting around for a moment that could allow his attack lines against Harris to break through and overwrite her gains in key battleground state polls.\par \par \uc2 And it was an acknowledgment that despite their hopes of getting Happy Trump on stage, they got Angry Trump, who seemingly could not shake his fury at being taunted over his supporters leaving his rallies early and being repeatedly fact-checked by the moderators.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-advisers-debate-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump to campaign in battleground states after debate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are focusing on swing states today.\par \par \uc2 Harris is scheduled to hold rallies in North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 in Charlotte and Greensboro, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump is heading west to Tucson, Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the candidates marked the anniversary of the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks.\par \par \uc2 At a fire station in Shanksville, Pennsylvania, close to where United Airlines Flight 93 crashed, Trump posed for photos with children who wore campaign shirts. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Harris visited the same fire station earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris-Trump debate watched by 67m people, beating pivotal Biden showdown\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome back to our rolling US political coverage.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 67.1 million people watched the presidential debate between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a 31% increase from the June debate between Trump and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that eventually led to the president dropping out of the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 The debate was run by ABC News but shown on 17 different networks, the Nielsen company said. The Trump-Biden debate in June was seen by 51.3 million people.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s count was short of the record viewership for a presidential debate, when 84 million people saw Trump\u8217\'20\'19s and Hillary Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s first face-off in 2016. The first debate between Biden and Trump in 2020 reached 73.1 million people.\par \par \uc2 There was a marked increase in younger and middle-aged viewers, with 53% more adults aged 18-49 tuning in to see Harris debate Trump than watched Biden do the same, according to Nielsen data.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/us-presidential-debate-tv-ratings-harris-trump-abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240912ek9c0015x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
