\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris-Trump debate watched by 15m more than Biden clash \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh ,Chris Stein, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Tom Bryant, Martin Belam and Amy Sedghi (earlier) \par \uc2 11,995 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par 23:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read the latest at the links below: Trump campaign claims debate win amid private skepticismWill Swift endorsement make a difference to election outcome?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. Here is our latest on the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to that debate:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-advisers-debate-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump campaign publicly claims debate win but aides privately express doubts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Election Day is less than two months away. The first mail ballots of the general election were sent out Wednesday, the day after the first debate between Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Early in-person voting will start as soon as 20 September in some states.\par \par \uc2 The first batch of ballots typically sent out are ones to military and overseas voters. Under federal law, that must happen at least 45 days before an election \u8212\'20\'14 which this year is 21 September.\par \par \uc2 Election offices in North Carolina had been scheduled to begin sending mail ballots to all voters who requested them on 6 September. But that has been delayed because presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  successfully sued to have his name removed from the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot after he suspended his campaign and endorsed Trump. That allowed Alabama to become the first state to send out absentee ballots for the presidential election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Voter registration deadlines vary by state, with most falling between eight and 30 days before the election, according to the National Conference of State Legislatures. The deadline is 7 October in Georgia, one of this year\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent presidential battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 Nearly all states offer some version of in-person voting, though the rules and dates vary considerably.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 While we haven\u8217\'20\'19t yet seen data that shows the uptick in the number of voters who registered after Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, hundreds of thousands visited the voter registration website vote.gov after Swift shared the link.\par \par \uc2 More than 306,000 people have visited the website since Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement:\par \par \uc2 enltrSince \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president, more than 306,000 people have visited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GXzFzvCkvp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GXzFzvCkvp}}}\uc2  using the voter registration link that she shared. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dVM2J7uZhF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dVM2J7uZhF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Axios (@axios) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/axios/status/1833957799199440950?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The father of an 11-year-old boy who was killed last year when a minivan driven by an immigrant from Haiti collided with his school bus has asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  to stop using his son\u8217\'20\'19s name for \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical gain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During a city commission meeting on Tuesday in Springfield, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , Nathan Clark, the father of Aiden Clark, addressed the forum alongside his wife, Danielle. Speaking at the meeting, Clark said: \u8220\'20\'1CI wish that my son, Aiden Clark, was killed by a 60-year-old white man. I bet you never thought anyone would say something so blunt, but if that guy killed my 11-year-old son, the incessant group of hate-spewing people would leave us alone,\u8221\'20\'1D the Springfield News-Sun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/news/aiden-clarks-dad-begs-springfield-politicians-stop-using-son-to-hate-haitians/QEZC7DVPKVC5JDPLNH7H2YSRPU/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clark went on to list politicians including Trump and Vance, who he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/keithboykin/status/1833881010271858987"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  have been using his son\u8217\'20\'19s name for \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical gain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/trump-vance-ohio-aiden-clark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Father of Ohio boy, 11, tells Trump and Vance to stop using son\u8217\'20\'19s death for \u8216\'20\'18political gain\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 About 67m people watch debate, roughly 15m more than Trump-Biden clash\par \par \uc2 An estimated 67.1 million people watched the presidential debate between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a sharp increase from the June debate that eventually led to President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropping out of the race.\par \par \uc2 The debate was run by ABC News but shown on 17 different networks, the Nielsen company said. The Trump-Biden debate in June was seen by 51.3 million people.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s count was short of the record viewership for a presidential debate, when 84 million people saw Trump\u8217\'20\'19s and Hillary Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s first face-off in 2016. The first debate between Biden and Trump in 2020 reached 73.1 million people.\par \par \uc2 With Harris widely perceived to have outperformed Trump on Tuesday night, the former president and his supporters are sharply criticising ABC moderators David Muir and Linsey Davis. The journalists waded into on-the-fly fact checks during the debate, correcting four statements by Trump.\par \par \uc2 enltrNielsen: 67.1 million viewers tuned in for last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate across 17 television networks\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jesse Rodriguez (@JesseRodriguez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JesseRodriguez/status/1833988498799366311?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 No other debates are currently scheduled between the two presidential candidates, although there\u8217\'20\'19s been some talk about it and Fox News Channel has publicly offered alternatives. \uc2 CBS\uc2  will host a vice presidential debate between \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate stakes were high to begin with, not only because of the impending election itself but because the last presidential debate uncorked a series of events that ended several weeks later with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from the race after his performance was widely panned.\par \par \uc2 Opinions on how ABC handled the latest debate Tuesday were, in a large sense, a Rorschach test on how supporters of both sides felt about how it went. MSNBC commentator Chris Hayes sent a message on X that the ABC moderators were doing an \u8220\'20\'1Cexcellent\u8221\'20\'1D job \u8212\'20\'14 only to be answered by conservative commentator \uc2 Ben Shapiro\uc2 , who said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is how you know they\u8217\'20\'19re complete s\u8212\'20\'14-.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While CNN chose not to correct any misstatements by the candidates during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s debate with Biden in June, ABC instead challenged statements that Trump made about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration, the 2020 election and violent crime.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US elections coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stridently backed new fracking and expanded US gas production in comments that raised eyebrows among some environmentalists as, yet again, the unfolding climate crisis was largely overlooked during a set piece presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Harris, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a televised debate with Donald Trump}}}\uc2  on Tuesday night in Philadelphia, rebuffed the former president\u8217\'20\'19s claim that she will end fracking \u8220\'20\'1Con day one\u8221\'20\'1D if elected by touting booming levels of drilling during her term as vice-president, in which US oil and gas production {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/jul/24/fossil-fuel-liquified-natural-gas-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has hit record highs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not ban fracking,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-fracking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissing a past campaign promise to do so}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, I was the tie-breaking vote on the Inflation Reduction Act, which opened new leases for fracking. My position is that we have got to invest in diverse sources of energy so we reduce our reliance on foreign oil.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris pointed to \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased domestic gas production to historic levels\u8221\'20\'1D and said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have had the largest increase in domestic oil production in history because of an approach that recognizes that we cannot over-rely on foreign oil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of the calculations of winning over moderate US voters in battleground states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/apr/04/its-over-for-fossil-fuels-ipcc-spells-out-whats-needed-to-avert-climate-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scientists are clear}}}\uc2  that the use of fossil fuels, including oil and gas obtained through hydraulic fracturing, or fracking, needs to be drastically cut if the world is to avoid the worst impacts of climate change.\par \par \uc2 The US, along with countries around the world, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2020/dec/08/the-paris-agreement-five-years-on-is-it-strong-enough-to-avert-climate-catastrophe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committed}}}\uc2  to not breaching a global temperature increase of 1.5C (2.7F) above pre-industrial times, a threshold that is likely to be breached within a decade amid ongoing record-breaking temperatures.\par \par \uc2 Some green groups, many of which have enthusiastically endorsed Harris as the Democratic nominee, were left disappointed by her strong embrace of fracking, which was similar in tone to the \u8220\'20\'1Call of the above\u8221\'20\'1D energy rhetoric common during \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, since which alarm has mounted over climate breakdown.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/climate-harris-trump-debate-fracking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Climate experts lament Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vow to keep fracking in debate with \u8216\'20\'18walking oil spill\u8217\'20\'19 Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The afternoon so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaigns continue to look for an advantage over the other after last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, which may be the only such event before the election. While Harris\u8217\'20\'19s team says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e195f98f086d5a40e67ef0#block-66e195f98f086d5a40e67ef0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she would be happy}}}\uc2  to duke it out with the former president again, Trump said he would be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e18d488f086d5a40e67e83#block-66e18d488f086d5a40e67e83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less inclined}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to do so. Surprisingly, the candidates today crossed paths at a ceremony in New York City to commemorate 9/11, where they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb#block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shook hands}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1caee8f08e370bfa98324#block-66e1caee8f08e370bfa98324"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surrogates}}}\uc2  are being asked about their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1bea98f086d5a40e6814d#block-66e1bea98f086d5a40e6814d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unproven}}}\uc2  claims that Haitian immigrants are eating pets in an Ohio town, which his running mate JD Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1c7278f087250b15a9675#block-66e1c7278f087250b15a9675"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insists}}}\uc2  is true. Separately, a father from the town, whose son\u8217\'20\'19s death in a bus crash has been seized on by conservatives to argue that immigrants are dangerous, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1b8a88f086d5a40e680c7#block-66e1b8a88f086d5a40e680c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for them}}}\uc2  to stop using the tragedy for \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical gain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Frank Luntz, a pollster known for his work with Republican campaigns, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1d5a88f087250b15a9798#block-66e1d5a88f087250b15a9798"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Trump \u8220\'20\'1Clost\u8221\'20\'1D last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate by focusing on topics irrelevant to voters \u8211\'20\'13 like unproven allegations of immigrants eating pets \u8211\'20\'13 rather than more important topics like inflation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1df2f8f08e370bfa98478#block-66e1df2f8f08e370bfa98478"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent the day}}}\uc2  commemorating 9/11 alongside Harris, and at one point {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1f8648f08e370bfa98540#block-66e1f8648f08e370bfa98540"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donned a Trump cap}}}\uc2  handed to him in Pennsylvania, which the White House described as a show of \u8220\'20\'1Cbipartisan unity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1c2258f087250b15a9619#block-66e1c2258f087250b15a9619"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have paid for}}}\uc2  a billboard in Phoenix that attempts to win over voters by referencing the pet-eating claim.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Inflation was a major topic at last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1a4578f08e370bfa98091#block-66e1a4578f08e370bfa98091"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest government data}}}\uc2  shows price growth slowing to levels last seen at the start of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1776f8f085827d9ecd31b#block-66e1776f8f085827d9ecd31b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  pop superstar \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cpay the price\u8221\'20\'1D for endorsing Harris after the debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail and at last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has repeatedly alleged that crime is down in Venezuela \u8211\'20\'13 proof, he says, that immigrants from the troubled South American country who enter the United States are criminals.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/trump-stephen-miller-anti-white-racism-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an architect}}}\uc2  of the hardline immigration policies Trump enacted as president, made the assertion to reporters in Philadelphia after the debate. But Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Del Pino of Colombia\u8217\'20\'19s NTN24 wanted to know where Miller was getting his data on crime in Venezuela, and asked specifically whether he was relying on figures released by the president, Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro, whom the United States has repeatedly accused of fraudulently holding on to power, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/11/venezuela-election-maduro-gonzalez-exiled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in July\u8217\'20\'19s elections}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Miller, who may return to the White House if Trump wins the November elections, grew angry as Del Pino pressed him for the source of his numbers, which Miller wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t provide. The full exchange is worth watching:\par \par \uc2 esltrLe pregunt\u233\'00\'E9 a \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , uno de los principales asesores de \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , cu\u225\'00\'E1l es la evidencia para se\u241\'00\'F1alar que Caracas y Venezuela son m\u225\'00\'E1s seguras que Estados Unidos. Comenz\u243\'00\'F3 respondiendo que son las cifras del gobierno. Le pregunt\u233\'00\'E9, \u191\'00\'BFentonces conf\u237\'00\'EDa en los n\u250\'00\'FAmeros de\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1eH4Fh5d0K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1eH4Fh5d0K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Del Pino (@josemdelpino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/josemdelpino/status/1833912161594478665?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just laid a wreath at the Pentagon, concluding a day spent commemorating the three sites of the 9/11 attack.\par \par \uc2 During the ceremony, they were joined by the defense secretary, Lloyd Austin, and the chair of the joint chiefs of staff Charles Q Brown Jr :\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 State officials warn 'trust in the election process' at risk over postal service struggles\par \par \uc2 With just weeks remaining until the 5 November election, groups representing state-level poll administrators have warned that the US postal system is not ready to handle the flood of ballots that will be sent by mail.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to \uc2 Louis DeJoy\uc2 , a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointee who has remained as the US postal service postmaster general under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the groups warn that USPS employees are \u8220\'20\'1Cuninformed\u8221\'20\'1D about how to handle election mail, creating misdeliveries of ballots that leave \u8220\'20\'1Cvoters disenfranchised\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The officials, who include the leaders of the National Association of State Election Directors, the National Association of Secretaries of State, and the heads of 29 election official associations, add that ballots are taking much longer than expected to be delivered, and that too many ballots are being returned as undeliverable \u8211\'20\'13 raising the possibility that voters will have their registrations canceled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CState and local officials need a committed partner in USPS. We implore you to take immediate and tangible corrective action to address the ongoing performance issues with USPS election mail service. Failure to do so will risk limiting voter participation and trust in the electoral process,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/usps-mail-election-ballots-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Postal Service delays threaten to disrupt election voting, officials say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says Biden donned Trump hat in show of 'bipartisan unity'\par \par \uc2 During his visit to the rural Pennsylvania village where one of the planes hijacked on 9/11 crashed, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  put on a Trump cap, in what a White House spokesperson said was an attempt to encourage a return to the \u8220\'20\'1Cbipartisan unity\u8221\'20\'1D the country felt following the attacks 23 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign was quick to put out a photo of the Democratic president wearing one of the iconic red hats:\par \par \uc2 enltrThanks for the support, Joe! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GeNDXWEHVi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GeNDXWEHVi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1833946499035570613?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s senior deputy press secretary Andrew Bates confirmed that the moment happened, and explained how the president came to be wearing the cap:\par \par \uc2 enltrAt the Shanksville Fire Station, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  spoke about the country's bipartisan unity after 9/11 and said we needed to get back to that.\par \par \uc2 As a gesture, he gave a hat to a Trump supporter who then said that in the same spirit, POTUS should put on his Trump cap. He briefly wore it. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7VKZnkVMY7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7VKZnkVMY7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Bates (@AndrewJBates46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewJBates46/status/1833949159730073638?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made many assertions on the debate stage last night, including that Germany tried and failed to implement decarbonization policies that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  supports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou believe in things like, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to frack, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to take fossil fuel, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to do things that are going to make this country strong. Whether you like it or not, Germany tried that, and, within one year, they were back to building normal energy plants,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said to Harris in his closing statement.\par \par \uc2 Berlin apparently did not like what it heard on the debate stage last night, and tweeted the below this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltrLike it or not: Germany\u8217\'20\'19s energy system is fully operational, with more than 50% renewables. And we are shutting down \u8211\'20\'13 not building \u8211\'20\'13 coal & nuclear plants. Coal will be off the grid by 2038 at the latest. PS: We also don\u8217\'20\'19t eat cats and dogs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Debate2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Debate2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PiDO98Vxfo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PiDO98Vxfo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 GermanForeignOffice (@GermanyDiplo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GermanyDiplo/status/1833808396618764327?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to note that Germany\u8217\'20\'19s tweet appears to reference Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about its decarbonization, not the \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2  pipeline.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also attended the 9/11 memorial ceremony in Shanksville, Pennsylvania, where CBS News reports he repeated to the press his uncertainty over whether he will accept \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invitation for a second debate:\par \par \uc2 enltrTRUMP: "Are we going to do a rematch? I just don't know. We'll think about it," he tells reporters about the prospects for a second Harris-Trump debate as he leaves Shankville, Pa. 9/11 commemoration events.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed O'Keefe (@edokeefe) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe/status/1833948483285647869?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether he crossed paths with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who also visited the site today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 300,000 people visit voter registration site from Taylor Swift post\par \par \uc2 The Vote.org website has recorded more than 300,000 visitors referred from \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post last night in which she endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , according to \uc2 NPR\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Elena Moore.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: A \uc2 General Services Administration\uc2  spox tells \uc2 NPR\uc2  that as of 11 a.m. ET today there have been 306,422 visitors to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WXfQ7iuhYq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WXfQ7iuhYq}}}\uc2  referred from Taylor Swifts\u8217\'20\'19s URL she shared on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  last night\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elena Moore (@ElenaMMoore) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElenaMMoore/status/1833936170301960507?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 After Swift encouraged her fans to vote in 2023, Vote.org recorded more than 35,000 registrations in a single day.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-harris-endorsement-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s Harris endorsement has thrilled fans \u8211\'20\'13 but will it move the election needle?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Accompanying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance at an event today commemorating the anniversary of 9/11 was a far-right conspiracy theorist who has previously claimed that the attacks were an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/lauraloomer/status/1672642483958710274?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inside job}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Laura Loomer, who once described herself as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/08/19/politics/laura-loomer-donald-trump-florida/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proud Islamophobe}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and who has also spread conspiracy theories about mass shootings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1df2f8f08e370bfa98478#block-66e1df2f8f08e370bfa98478"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traveled with}}}\uc2  Trump to Shanksville, Pennsylvania, on Wednesday after accompanying him to Philadelphia yesterday for the presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Trump has praised Loomer as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/laura-loomer-trump-praise-white-supremacist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terrific}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvery special\u8221\'20\'1D and endorsed her failed Florida House primary run in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign was in damage control mode on Wednesday amid widespread dismay among supporters over a presidential debate performance that saw \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  repeatedly goad him into going wildly off-message and missing apparent opportunities to tackle her on policy.\par \par \uc2 Even with Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Channel4News/status/1833753161665773805"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisting}}}\uc2  to have won the debate \u8220\'20\'1Cby a lot\u8221\'20\'1D, Republicans were virtually unanimous that Trump had come off second best in a series of exchanges that saw the vice-president deliberately bait him on his weak points while he responded with visible anger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s make no mistake. Trump had a bad night,\u8221\'20\'1D the Fox News analyst Brit Hume said immediately after the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just heard so many of the old grievances that we all know aren\u8217\'20\'19t winners politically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was exquisitely well-prepared, she laid traps and he chased every rabbit down every hole instead of talking about the things that he should have been talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former Republican governor of New Jersey who helped Trump prepare for his 2016 debates with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , told ABC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was unfocused and poorly prepared,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/guypbenson/status/1833698983992291677"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed}}}\uc2  Guy Benson, editor of the conservative website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://townhall.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Townhall}}}\uc2  on X. \u8220\'20\'1C[Harris] basically accomplished exactly what she wanted to here. I suspect the polls about the debate will show that she won it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congressional Republicans voiced disappointment over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inability to discipline himself and press home key policy issues. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just sad,\u8221\'20\'1D one House Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4873509-trump-harris-debate-house-republicans/?email=ad2a11c281e64942732657414f9b1bbaf87e9ad8&emaila=b8b88509b42b638f27f41c0f891843f1&emailb=c87b91852013b3237ae7cbc122f432f1538d7ec1795d620264ed9c234e8cf439&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=9.11.24%20CJ%20Morning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CShe knew exactly where to cut to get under his skin. Just overall disappointing that he isn\u8217\'20\'19t being more composed like the first debate. The road just got very narrow. This is not good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-republican-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans dismayed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18bad\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18unprepared\u8217\'20\'19 debate performance}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier this afternoon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  attended a wreath-laying ceremony at the Flight 93 memorial near Shanksville, Pennsylvania, to mark the 23rd anniversary of 9/11.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris also visited Shanksville\u8217\'20\'19s volunteer fire department to meet with firefighters and the families and friends of Flight 93 victims.\par \par \uc2 More than an hour later, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also paid a visit to the site.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb#block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2 , Trump and Harris \u8211\'20\'13 who met in person for the first time during last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate \u8211\'20\'13 shook hands as they attended a memorial service in New York City.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the conservatives amplifying the unproven story of immigrants eating pets in Ohio is \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the billionaire \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO who endorsed Trump weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Reacting to pop superstar (and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/apr/02/world-gains-141-new-billionaires-in-amazing-year-for-rich-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fellow billionaire}}}\uc2  ) \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  yesterday, Musk said:\par \par \uc2 enltrFine Taylor \u8230\'20\'26 you win \u8230\'20\'26 I will give you a child and guard your cats with my life\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1833728804579111268?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Musk has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/aug/09/elon-musks-journey-from-humanitarian-to-poster-of-rightwing-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 12 children}}}\uc2 , including one from whom he is estranged. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jun/21/elon-musk-daughter-legal-name-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s daughter legally changes name and cuts ties with her father}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican pollster Frank Luntz said Trump 'lost' debate by focusing on issues unimportant to voters\par \par \uc2 Frank Luntz, a veteran pollster who has worked for Republican campaigns, told CNBC \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was in a good position at the start of last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, but the former president effectively \u8220\'20\'1Clost\u8221\'20\'1D by focusing on topics voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t interested in \u8211\'20\'13 like the unproven story of migrants eating pets in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Luntz argued that Trump missed opportunities to sway voters by talking about the issues where he\u8217\'20\'19s strongest, such as inflation, though he also did not believe \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  won the face-off.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full interview:\par \par \uc2 Luntz also said Harris appeared more presidential in the debate. He criticized both candidates for \u8220\'20\'1Cslim\u8221\'20\'1D details on their economic policies, suggesting voters were \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointed\u8221\'20\'1D about lack of information.\par \par \uc2 Luntz accused Trump of \u8220\'20\'1Cmissing a golden opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D to get across his message, saying the former president failed to convince undecided voters to lend him their vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaigns continue to look for an advantage over the other after last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, which may be the only such event before the election. While Harris\u8217\'20\'19s team says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e195f98f086d5a40e67ef0#block-66e195f98f086d5a40e67ef0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she would be happy}}}\uc2  to duke it out with the former president again, Trump said he would be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e18d488f086d5a40e67e83#block-66e18d488f086d5a40e67e83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less inclined}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to do so. Surprisingly, the candidates crossed paths at a ceremony in New York City to commemorate 9/11, where they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb#block-66e194888f08e370bfa97fcb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shook hands}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1caee8f08e370bfa98324#block-66e1caee8f08e370bfa98324"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surrogates}}}\uc2  are being asked about their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1bea98f086d5a40e6814d#block-66e1bea98f086d5a40e6814d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unproven}}}\uc2  claims that Haitian immigrants are eating pets in an Ohio town, with his running mate JD Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1c7278f087250b15a9675#block-66e1c7278f087250b15a9675"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisting}}}\uc2  that the story is true. Separately, a father from the town whose son\u8217\'20\'19s death in a car crash has been seized on by conservatives to argue that immigrants are dangerous has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1b8a88f086d5a40e680c7#block-66e1b8a88f086d5a40e680c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for them}}}\uc2  to stop using the tragedy for \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical gain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1c2258f087250b15a9619#block-66e1c2258f087250b15a9619"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have paid for}}}\uc2  a billboard in Phoenix that attempts to win over voters by referencing the pet eating claim.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Inflation was a major topic at last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1a4578f08e370bfa98091#block-66e1a4578f08e370bfa98091"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest government data}}}\uc2  shows price growth slowing to levels last seen at the start of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates?page=with:block-66e1776f8f085827d9ecd31b#block-66e1776f8f085827d9ecd31b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  pop superstar \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cpay the price\u8221\'20\'1D for endorsing Harris after the debate last night.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN earlier today, top \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign advis er \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2  gave a different answer than Vance, when asked about the former president mentioning on the debate stage allegations of migrants eating pets in an Ohio town.\par \par \uc2 Miller said the story stemmed from reporting by the Federalist, which he described as both a \u8220\'20\'1Cnews outlet\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca very well-respected research organization\u8221\'20\'1D. He neglected to mention that the Federalist is thoroughly rightwing, and promoted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims of fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Responding to a question about whether it was a good strategy for Trump to promote the story at the debate, Miller claimed that the moderators were biased, then said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis issue of illegal immigration that there is many of as 20 million illegals been brought in the country, many of them airlifted to the middle of America, making every community a border community, that that was the issue that we should have been talking about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance doubles down on claim of migrants eating pets in Ohio city\par \par \uc2 After the debate last night, NBC News asked JD Vance, the Ohio senator who is running alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , why he kept insisting that Haitian immigrants were eating pets in an Ohio town, despite local officials\u8217\'20\'19 insistence to the contrary.\par \par \uc2 In response, the senator said he had heard from his constituents that the story was true, and cast doubt on the Springfield, Ohio, town manager\u8217\'20\'19s refutation of the claim. Here\u8217\'20\'19s that moment, from NBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy Q to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JDVance}}}\uc2  last night in Philly: What do you say to Haitian Americans and Haitian immigrants who say spreading false claims about them puts their lives at risk?\par \par \uc2 Our full exchange on video. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S0NG02Ci2S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S0NG02Ci2S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yamiche Alcindor (@Yamiche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1833836021349302733?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona GOP amplifies false claims about migrants with 'Eat less kittens' billboard\par \par \uc2 Republicans nationwide are leaning into the baseless claim that Haitian migrants in an Ohio town are eating pets, with Arizona GOP buying a billboard in Phoenix that references the conspiracy theory:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? NEW AZGOP BILLBOARD ALERT! ??\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEAT LESS KITTENS \u8211\'20\'13 Vote Republican!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This campaign highlights just how horrific things have become under the failed policies of \u8216\'20\'18Border Czar\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 President Trump is committed to securing our borders and ensuring that what we\u8217\'20\'19ve\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NM3jlN2oau"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NM3jlN2oau}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republican Party of Arizona (@AZGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AZGOP/status/1833521842058863047?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  on the campaign by conservatives to demonize Springfield, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s Haitian community, which was amplified by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the debate stage last night:\par \par \uc2 Prominent Republicans including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  campaign and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  are sharing false and unsubstantiated claims that Haitian migrants in an Ohio city are eating pets and local wildlife.\par \par \uc2 The salacious and often racist social media posts claim, without evidence, that migrants from Haiti to Springfield, Ohio, are stealing pets and local wildlife such as ducks and geese and are butchering them for food. Many of the posts, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1833154509222129884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one shared by the X account}}}\uc2  for the Republicans on the House judiciary committee, use images generated by artificial intelligence to show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  holding and protecting cats and ducks, casting him as a savior to the town. \uc2 Ted Cruz\uc2 , the Republican senator from Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/tedcruz/status/1833174142591365185"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared a meme}}}\uc2  of two cats hugging one another that said, \u8220\'20\'1CPlease vote for Trump so Haitian immigrants don\u8217\'20\'19t eat us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Springfield News-Sun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/news/springfield-police-say-no-reports-of-pets-stolen-after-viral-social-media-post/3WSIZQNHQVE4NP4TS5BVHBB2PY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Monday that police have \u8220\'20\'1Creceived no reports related to pets being stolen and eaten\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The claims appear to have originated from a commenter at a local city meeting, who said migrants were grabbing ducks from the park to kill and eat, and from local crime-watch \uc2 Facebook\uc2  groups. They were then shared on other social media platforms and made it into a headline in the Daily Mail.\par \par \uc2 The misinformation about migrants in Springfield comes as the Trump campaign has sought to make immigration a key issue, tying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the towns unprepared for migrants arriving via the southern border. Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Rob Rue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/ohio-city-plunged-housing-crisis-15000-migrants-arrive-setting-us-up-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on Fox}}}\uc2  to say the Biden administration was to blame for \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing cities like ours and taxing us beyond our limit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans spread baseless slurs about \u8216\'20\'18cat-eating migrants\u8217\'20\'19 in Ohio city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Father of child killed in crash involving Haitian driver asks Republicans to stop using tragedy 'political gain' - report\par \par \uc2 Over the past few days, conservatives have fixated on the town of Springfield, Ohio, which is home to a large number of Haitian migrants who they have baselessly claimed pose a danger to the community.\par \par \uc2 Immigration is a major topic of this election, but in this case, the claims have veered into the outlandish, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his running mate JD Vance, alleging that the Haitians have been eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 Town authorities have said there is no proof of that happening, but a tragedy did occur in the town last year, involving a Haitian driver who caused a car accident that killed an 11-year-old boy, Aiden Clark. Republicans have used his death to bolster their claims against the immigrant community, something his father, Nathan Clark, condemned publicly at a city commission meeting yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/news/aiden-clarks-dad-begs-springfield-politicians-stop-using-son-to-hate-haitians/QEZC7DVPKVC5JDPLNH7H2YSRPU/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Springfield News-Sun reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish that my son, Aiden Clark, was killed by a 60-year-old white man. I bet you never thought anyone would say something so blunt, but if that guy killed my 11-year-old son, the incessant group of hate-spewing people would leave us alone,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark said during an open forum at the meeting.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Nathan Clark denounced multiple Republican politicians, including vice presidential candidate and U.S. Sen. \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  candidate Bernie Moreno for statements that Clark said \u8220\'20\'1Cused his death for political gain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis needs to stop now. They can vomit all the hate they want about illegal immigrants, the border crisis and even untrue claims about fluffy pets being ravaged and eaten by community members,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark said. \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, they are not allowed nor have they ever been allowed, to mention Aiden Clark from Springfield, Ohio. I will listen to them one more time to hear their apologies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are an estimated 12,000 to 15,000 Haitian immigrants living in Springfield now according to data from the Clark County Combined Health District and other partners, Springfield Mayor Rob Rue said at a press conference earlier Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Clark said Aiden was not murdered but killed by accident. He said the community is still deeply affected by the accident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis tragedy is still all over this community, the state and even the nation, but don\u8217\'20\'19t spin this towards hate,\u8221\'20\'1D Clark said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to live like Aiden, you need to accept everyone, choose to shine, make the difference, lead the way and be the inspiration. What many people in this community and state and nation are doing is the opposite of what we should be doing. Sure we have our problems here in Springfield and in the U.S., but does Aiden Clark have anything to do with that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alyssa Farah Griffin, a former press secretary for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who has turned on him, said the following about the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s claim that the moderators of last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate were biased against him:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe moderators are not the problem. The wildly unprepared, undisciplined GOP candidate is the problem.\par \par \uc2 Republicans had a chance to nominate someone who could discuss policy rather than crowd size. But R\u8217\'20\'19s chose this.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alyssa Farah Griffin (@Alyssafarah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Alyssafarah/status/1833696921598201857?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters checked in with 10 undecided voters who watched last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, and asked them which candidate they were leaning towards.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  turned out to be the winner of this very small sample poll, with several voters saying they found \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to be vague when it came to which policies she supported. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/some-undecided-voters-not-convinced-by-harris-after-debate-with-trump-2024-09-11/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was widely seen as dominating Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate against Republican former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but a group of undecided voters remained unconvinced that the Democratic vice-president was the better candidate.\par \par \uc2 Reuters interviewed 10 people who were still unsure how they were going to vote in the 5 November election before they watched the debate. Six said afterward they would now either vote for Trump or were leaning toward backing him. Three said they would now back Harris and one was still unsure how he would vote.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump are in a tight race and the election will probably be decided by just tens of thousands of votes in a handful of battleground states, many of whom are swing voters like the undecided voters who spoke to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Although the sample size was small, the responses suggested Harris might need to provide more detailed policy proposals to win over voters who have yet to make up their minds.\par \par \uc2 Five said they found Harris vague during the more than 90-minute debate on how she would improve the US economy and deal with the high cost of living, a top concern for voters.\par \par \uc2 The encounter was particularly important for Harris, with a weekend New York Times/Siena College opinion poll showing that more than a quarter of likely voters feel they do not know enough about her, in contrast to the well-known Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you're a swing state voter, read this\par \par \uc2 The November presidential election will probably be decided by voters in seven states where polls show a close race between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan, Arizona, Georgia and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 And if you happen to vote in one of those states, we want to hear your thoughts on last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate between the two candidates. Fill out our survey here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/us-swing-state-voters-share-your-reaction-to-the-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US swing state voters: share your reaction to the presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 US inflation continues to decline in weeks before November election\par \par \uc2 At his debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last night, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took pains to mention inflation, which rose to levels not seen since the 1980s as the US economy recovered from the Covid-19 pandemic over the past three years.\par \par \uc2 All signs point to prices for consumer goods being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/us-jobs-figures-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a potent political issue}}}\uc2 , but economically speaking, they\u8217\'20\'19re on the decline \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 US government\uc2  data released this morning shows that the inflation rate has receded to where it was when Biden took office.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/callum-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Callum Jones}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/11/august-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US inflation softens to lowest level since February 2021 as Fed prepares to cut interest rates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Philippe Reines, a former aide to \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  who played \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s debate prep, posted to X an image of him in his costume and makeup.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo do: facial, hair cut, spiritual cleanse,\u8221\'20\'1D Reines wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrto do:\par \par \uc2 facial\par \par \uc2 haircut\par \par \uc2 spiritual cleanse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xpYQW17yg3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xpYQW17yg3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Philippe Reines (@PhilippeReines) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PhilippeReines/status/1833850281613787390?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from last night's debate\par \par \uc2 1. Trump repeatedly spewed misinformation: Throughout the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump spread misinformation}}}\uc2  to make his points, repeating already debunked rhetoric on everything from the results of the 2020 election to his involvement in Project 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 a conservative-backed plan to change the \uc2 US government\uc2  from the inside out.\par \par \uc2 The former president distanced himself from the January 6 attack on the Capitol, saying he was there only to make a speech, and blamed the then House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , for not beefing up security. He also incorrectly said crime rates had risen in the US when they have in fact fallen.\par \par \uc2 2.... and was frequently fact-checked by the moderators: ABC\u8217\'20\'19s moderators, David Muir and Linsey Davis, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/themoneycoach/status/1833683477272609221"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/beccalew/status/1833695055963623908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  for delivering a strong performance. They effectively rerouted discussions back to the questions they had asked on key topics including the economy, immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the peaceful transfer of power, and made important clarifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact-check statements}}}\uc2  when they were warranted.\par \par \uc2 3. Harris defended Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 position on reproductive rights: When challenged on his changing take on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, Trump made some alarming \u8211\'20\'13 and easily refuted \u8211\'20\'13 claims that Democrats supported executing babies after they are born. He also took credit for overturning of Roe v Wade, a decision made by the supreme court after he appointed three members to make a 6-3 conservative majority, that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unpopular with the majority of Americans}}}\uc2 . Trump did clarify his position, though, that he believes in exceptions for rape, incest and threats to the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 Harris called his stances \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulting to the women of America\u8221\'20\'1D, and countered his statements that he delivered on a promise to bring the issue back to the states by saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe people of American have voted for freedom\u8221\'20\'1D. She highlighted the difficult realities faced by women in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and would-be mothers who would struggle to access IVF care.\par \par \uc2 4. The candidates both touted their work to improve the economy: Harris was quick to tout her \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opportunity economy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a plan that includes tax reductions for those starting small businesses, relief for new parents and first-time homebuyers, and a crackdown on corporate price-gouging.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, claimed that he oversaw the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest economy\u8221\'20\'1D, even with the downturn caused by the Covid pandemic, and accused his opponent of increasing costs on American families. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople can\u8217\'20\'19t go out and buy cereal, or bacon, or anything else,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Inflation did spike under the Biden-Harris administration, but it has fallen just as quickly. As of August, the US inflation rate settled at 2.9%.\par \par \uc2 5. Trump spouted salacious and sometimes racist claims about immigrants: Throughout the debate, Trump pivoted his talking points to immigration, spouting salacious claims about criminals being welcomed into the country and towns where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pets are eaten by incoming immigrants.}}}\par \par \uc2 While debate moderators attempted to counter the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2 , challenging Trump on the validity and also on how he would execute the deportation of millions as he\u8217\'20\'19s promised to do, Harris took the offensive. Highlighting her record as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only person on the stage who has prosecuted transnational organizations\u8221\'20\'1D, she also accused her opponent of calling on the GOP to oppose legislation to bolster the border. \u8220\'20\'1CHe preferred to run on a problem rather than fixing a problem,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 6. The candidates sparred over Ukraine and how they would handle the war: Harris said that if Trump were currently in office, the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , would have taken Kyiv, saying Putin would \u8220\'20\'1Ceat you for lunch\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the reason that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says that this war would be over within 24 hours is because he would just give it up,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris also said.\par \par \uc2 When Trump was asked by Muir how he would end the war \u8211\'20\'13 and specifically if he wanted Ukraine to win \u8211\'20\'13 the former president did not offer a clear answer. \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop. I want to save lives that are being lost uselessly. People being killed by the millions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 7. Harris baited Trump by attacking him where it hurts: As moderators pushed Harris to respond to criticisms she and Biden have faced over border policy, the vice-president expertly derailed her opponent\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on what is perhaps his favorite issue to discuss by deriding his performances at rallies.\par \par \uc2 She invited voters to view the speeches for themselves, saying that attenders can be seen leaving out of exhaustion and boredom, and characterized the events as a platform for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s complaints and not plans that put the American people first.\par \par \uc2 The jab landed well. An offended and flustered Trump jumped on the chance to defend attendance at his rallies, claiming Harris pays attenders at her own campaign events, and then pivoted to insults that failed to hit their mark. He accused Harris of planning to turn the country into \u8220\'20\'1CVenezuela on steroids\u8221\'20\'1D, and called the US a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing nation\u8221\'20\'1D, before resurfacing false claims that immigrants were eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A top Harris campaign official said \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was open to a second debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in October.\par \par \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s deputy campaign manager, told CNN this morning:\par \par \uc2 I think that both campaigns are going to have to agree to a time but I think the vice-president is open to a debate in October.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether the vice-president would agree to a 25 September debate on NBC, Fulks declined to commit, adding that the \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo campaigns are going to have to agree on a date.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A senior Trump campaign adviser, also speaking to CNN, refused to definitely say whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would take part in an NBC debate on 25 September. \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 , the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s senior adviser, said:\par \par \uc2 I thought this was a bit perplexing because President Trump has already said that he is going to do three debates. We had the September 4 debate, which was going to be on Fox, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was a no-show. We had last night. And President Trump already said that on September 25, we would do a debate on NBC.\par \par \uc2 Miller continued:\par \par \uc2 But now \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  seems to have memory holed that and rather than just saying, we\u8217\'20\'19ll see you on September 25 on NBC, is now throwing out some fictional day in October.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo very clearly, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to go back to the drawing board,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump shake hands at 9/11 memorial service\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shook hands as they attended a memorial service to commemorate the 23rd anniversary of 9/11 in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2 , the former New York mayor, appeared to facilitate the handshake between Harris and Trump, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just hours after meeting in person for the first time, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have crossed paths again as they attend commemoration events marking the 23rd anniversary of the September 11 attacks.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Harris, Trump and his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , attended the traditional memorial service in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Memorial Plaza at Ground Zero.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris are then expected to travel to Shanksville, Pennsylvania, to participate in a wreath-laying ceremony at the Flight 93 memorial. They are then expected to travel to the Pentagon in Arlington, Virginia, for another wreath-laying ceremony.\par \par \uc2 Trump will also travel to Shanksville today, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he is 'less inclined' to participate in another debate\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking to Fox and Friends, said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know if he wanted to debate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  again, claiming he \u8220\'20\'1Cwon the debate\u8221\'20\'1D last night.\par \par \uc2 Well, I\u8217\'20\'19d be less inclined to because we had a great night. We won the debate.\par \par \uc2 Trump had previously agreed to participate in a debate hosted by Fox News, moderated by Martha MacCallum and Bret Baier. But this morning, he said:\par \par \uc2 I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t want to have Martha and Bret. I\u8217\'20\'19d love to have somebody else other than Martha and Bret.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked on Fox & Friends this morning why he believed the country would be safer under him. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I deal with foreign policy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 The former president repeated his attacks blaming the Biden administration on the chaotic Afghanistan withdrawal, claiming that the former chair of the joint chiefs of staff, \uc2 Gen Mark Milley\uc2 , was \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetent\u8221\'20\'1D and should have been \u8220\'20\'1Cfired and reprimanded like you\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Fox and Friends \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said that today he will be attending memorial events for 9/11 in New York and in Pennyslvania with his VP pick JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 It was put to him that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would also be there, and he was asked \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are going to be at the site together. Are you going to say anything to them?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1COh I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure. It\u8217\'20\'19s, you know, look, everybody should be very angry at how badly they\u8217\'20\'19ve run this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former president then launched into a familiar diatribe about immigration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  expressed frustration that factcheckers corrected him more in last night\u8217\'20\'19s TV debate than they corrected \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a call to Fox & Friends this morning, the former president cited his use of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cbloodbath\u8221\'20\'1D, his comments after the murder of Heather Danielle Heyer in the Charlottesville car attack and his position on IVF treatment as areas where he claims he was wrongly corrected by moderators.\par \par \uc2 Trump maintained his use of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cbloodbath\u8221\'20\'1D solely pertained to the economy, saying:\par \par \uc2 Bloodbath was referring to the economy. Everybody loved the term, because as soon as they heard the word, it\u8217\'20\'19s sort of a vicious word, but referring to the economy. They have created an economy [sic]. Bloodbath was the word that I used, and it was fine in that context. They were trying to make it sound like it was a riot or something.\par \par \uc2 On IVF, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 IVF. I was a leader on IEF [sic]. The IVF. The IVF, which is fertilization. I was a total leader on that, when I first heard about it, like right from the beginning, I was one of the leaders on it, and the Republican party has been a leader on it.\par \par \uc2 He then complained he had been corrected six times in his statements about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the debate, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe whole thing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . What he said, I mean, it was incredible. I think he corrected me six times, and each time I was right. I believe each time I was right. Didn\u8217\'20\'19t correct her at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also unexpectedly cited Laura Ingraham while defending his comments about Charlottesville, saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cshe said that in fact it makes it [sic] angry. She makes \u8230\'20\'26 she gets angry when people hear about Charlottesville.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said it was wrong to say he did not condemn neo-Nazis in Charlottesville because people do not refer to the full quote.\par \par \uc2 Trump said at the time: \u8220\'20\'1CYou had some very bad people in that group, but you also had people that were very fine people, on both sides,\u8221\'20\'1D and then later said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re changing history. You\u8217\'20\'19re changing culture. And you had people \u8211\'20\'13 and I\u8217\'20\'19m not talking about the neo-Nazis and the white nationalists \u8211\'20\'13 because they should be condemned totally. But you had many people in that group other than neo-Nazis and white nationalists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has called for ABC to lose their broadcasting license after the way the network moderated last night\u8217\'20\'19s TV debate. Saying the network took \u8220\'20\'1Ca big hit last night\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump said \u8220\'20\'1CThey have to be licensed to do it. They ought to take away their license for the way they did that. I think they lost a lot of credibility.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He told viewers of Fox & Friends that he had polls showing he had won the debate \u8220\'20\'1Cby 80-20, 90, we we have one here, 92 to seven. And I sort of believe that\u8217\'20\'19s right.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump did not name the polls.\par \par \uc2 He continued his attack on ABC, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the standpoint of ABC, they\u8217\'20\'19re the most dishonest, in my opinion, the most dishonest news organization, and that\u8217\'20\'19s saying a lot, because they\u8217\'20\'19re all essentially really dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also managed to aim a jibe at his hosts this morning, insisting that he would not want to do a debate on Fox if Bret Baier and Martha MacCallum were the moderators, and he said that Fox\u8217\'20\'19s Harold Ford Jr must have been watching a different debate, and was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust as dishonest as ABC in my opinion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims he won presidential debate \u8216\'20\'18by a lot\u8217\'20\'19 and that \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2  will \u8216\'20\'18pay the price\u8217\'20\'19 for endorsing Harris\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is currently being interviewed on Fox & Friends. We will have more detail on that interview soon. But he has told the show that it was his \u8220\'20\'1Cbest ever\u8221\'20\'1D debate, and that he won it by \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He attacked the ABC news network and claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cthey kept correcting me\u8221\'20\'1D, saying that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  told \u8220\'20\'1Coutright lies\u8221\'20\'1D and was not corrected. In a familiar diatribe, he claimed the debate was \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally rigged\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo many things I said were debunked, like totally debunked,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the news programme. \u8220\'20\'1CBut she could say anything she wanted. My stuff was right, but they would correct you.\u8221\'20\'1D He accused ABC, without evidence, of being the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost dishonest news organization\u8221\'20\'1D and that the debate was stacked against him.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Responding to Taylor Swift }}}\uc2  announcing she would vote for the Harris campaign, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a very liberal person, she always seems to endorse a Democrat and she will probably pay the price for that in the market.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 During the debate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeated an unsubstantiated claim that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigrants are eating pets in an Ohio town}}}\uc2 , forcing the moderator to tell him that there is no proof of that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Springfield, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs, the people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump during the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Alice Herman reports }}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims about immigrants allegedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing and eating the pets}}}\uc2  of US citizens originated, apparently, with a viral video of a resident of Springfield, Ohio, claiming before the town\u8217\'20\'19s council that immigrants in the community had killed ducks from a local park for food. The unsubstantiated and inflammatory video was shared widely on rightwing accounts, evolving quickly into a viral meme featuring AI-generated images of Trump surrounded by cats and dogs, appearing to protect them.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As our Fact Check makes clear}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The story of migrants allegedly eating pets has circulated in rightwing media in recent days and been repeated by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 . These are false and unsubstantiated claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou bring up Springfield, Ohio, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC}}}\uc2  News did reach out to the city manager there. He told us there have been no credible reports of specific claims of pets being harmed, injured or abused by individuals within the immigrant community,\u8221\'20\'1D moderator David Muir told Trump.\par \par \uc2 The Springfield News-Sun {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.springfieldnewssun.com/news/springfield-police-say-no-reports-of-pets-stolen-after-viral-social-media-post/3WSIZQNHQVE4NP4TS5BVHBB2PY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Monday that police have \u8220\'20\'1Creceived no reports related to pets being stolen and eaten\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz campaign quickly capitalised on \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support after she endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for president in a post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Quickly available on the Harris-Walz campaign site were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://store.kamalaharris.com/harris-walz-friendship-bracelets/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift-inspired friendship bracelets}}}\uc2 . Swift fans are famous for swapping friendship bracelets during concerts, tours and events inspired by her song You\u8217\'20\'19re on Your Own, Kid, which includes the lyrics \u8220\'20\'1Cso make the friendship bracelets, take the moment and taste it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a voter, I make sure to watch and read everything I can,\u8221\'20\'1D Swift wrote on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  to her 283 million followers late on Tuesday, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI will be casting my vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in the 2024 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think she is a steady-handed, gifted leader and I believe we can accomplish so much more in this country if we are led by calm and not chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07am BST\par \par \uc2 'It's just sad': Republicans express dismay at Trump performance as polling suggests Harris won debate\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have expressed dismay at former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , as snap polling suggested she was widely seen by the public to have won last night\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election TV debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just sad,\u8221\'20\'1D one House Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4873509-trump-harris-debate-house-republicans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told website The Hill}}}\uc2 , adding \u8220\'20\'1CShe knew exactly where to cut to get under his skin\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump allowed himself to get distracted from key talking points as Harris got him to talk about the size of the crowds at his rallies, or make false claims about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[It is] just overall disappointing that he isn\u8217\'20\'19t being more composed like the first debate,\u8221\'20\'1D the anonymous House Republican told the Hill, adding \u8220\'20\'1CThe road just got very narrow. This is not good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/09/11/politics/election-poll-trump-harris-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN flash poll}}}\uc2  after the debate suggested that two-thirds of the watching public believed that Harris had out-performed Trump, with the news network reporting that \u8220\'20\'1C96% of Harris supporters who tuned in said that their chosen candidate had done a better job, while a smaller 69% majority of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters credited him with having a better night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another House Republican source speaking anonymously told the Hill website \u8220\'20\'1CShe talks to us like toddlers but is doing a good job provoking him. Many are disappointed he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t stay focused or land a punch. Not sure much changes but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a good performance,\u8221\'20\'1D while a third said \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not devastating \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s not good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conservative Fox News political analyst Brit Hume also contended that Harris had won, telling viewers \u8220\'20\'1CShe baited him, successfully. She came out ahead in this, in my opinion. No doubt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CNN polling margin \u8211\'20\'13 63% for Harris, 37% for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 marks a sharp reverse of the numbers Trump achieved when debating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  earlier in the year, which led to the sitting president pulling out of the race, and comes as megastar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift announced she was endorsing Harris}}}\uc2 , signing her message as from a \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat lady\u8221\'20\'1D, a dig at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s VP pick JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-debate-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s powerful \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  stance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fact-checks: key takeaways from the debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Russia has accused both presidential candidates of using \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name as part of a domestic political fights, saying: \u8220\'20\'1Cwe really, really don\u8217\'20\'19t like it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov said on Wednesday that the US was hostile and negative towards Russia, Reuters reports, and the Kremlin hoped that candidates would drop such references to Putin.\par \par \uc2 Last week the White House said Putin should stop commenting on the US election after he said in an apparently teasing comment that he favoured Harris over Trump and that her \u8220\'20\'1Cinfectious\u8221\'20\'1D laugh was one of the reasons why.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump Media & Technology Group\uc2  shares fell 17% in premarket trading on Wednesday following the combative presidential debate between the former president and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the debate, pricing for a Trump victory slipped by 6 cents to 47 cents on online betting site PredictIt, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s odds climbed to 57 cents from 53 cents.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy also received a boost after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pop star Taylor Swift said she will vote for the Democratic candidate}}}\uc2  to her 280m on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump is the biggest shareholder in \uc2 Trump Media & Technology Group\uc2  (TMTG), the parent of Truth Social app, which is popular among retail traders and is often sensitive to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning the 2024 US election, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Majority of those watching debate say Harris outperformed Trump - CNN poll\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/09/11/politics/election-poll-trump-harris-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flash poll by CNN}}}\uc2 , registered voters who watched Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate broadly agreed that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  outperformed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is based on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/25117207/cnn-flash-poll-majority-of-debate-watchers-say-harris-outperformed-trump-onstage.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN poll of debate watchers conducted by SSRS}}}\uc2 , that also found that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Coutpaced both debate watchers\u8217\'20\'19 expectations for her and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/27/politics/takeaways-biden-trump-debate/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s onstage performance}}}\uc2  against the former president earlier this year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The CNN snap poll found:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Watchers said, by 63% to 37%, that Harris turned in a better performance onstage in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 96% of Harris supporters who watched said that their chosen candidate had done a better job\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A smaller 69% of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters thought he had done a better job\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters who watched the debate found their views of Harris were improved\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump was seen to have an advantage on the economy, immigration and being commander in chief. Harris was more trusted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protecting democracy\par \par \uc2 However, the vast majority who tuned in said the debate had no effect on who they were going to vote for in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Following the debate between Trump and Biden in June, watchers said, 67% to 33%, that Trump outperformed the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended at 11.48 BST. The CNN poll found that 63% of watchers thought that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  had a better performance, not 67% as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54am BST\par \par \uc2 And finally, the fifth key exchange of the night was on the Biden legacy, writes Bland:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : Where is our president? We don\u8217\'20\'19t even know if he\u8217\'20\'19s a president.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : You\u8217\'20\'19re not running against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , you\u8217\'20\'19re running against me.\par \par \uc2 This line from Harris, clearly scripted, was nonetheless a useful shorthand for the way she wants the race to be framed: as a chance to move on from the political division that has exhausted Americans for the last eight years, with her as a candidate who is not wedded to every aspect of the Biden record. In her closing statement, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve heard tonight two very different visions for our country: one that is focused on the future and the other that is focused on the past, and an attempt to take us backward. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not going back.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his own closing statement, Trump finally did what his team would have wanted him to do throughout \u8211\'20\'13 blame Harris relentlessly for everything voters dislike about Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s been there for three and a half years,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve had three and a half years to fix the border. They\u8217\'20\'19ve had three and a half years to create jobs and all the things we talked about. Why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t she done it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But by then, it felt like the narrative of the night was irreversibly set. And when Trump rambled into the claim that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re going to end up in a third world war, and it will be a war like no other because of nuclear weapons, the power of weaponry,\u8221\'20\'1D it merely seemed like normal service had been resumed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49am BST\par \par \uc2 The third key exchange, writes Bland, is on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Namely, the last night\u8217\'20\'19s factcheck on a wild claim that Democrats will execute babies after birth.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : Her vice-presidential pick says \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month is absolutely fine. He also says execution after birth \u8230\'20\'26 and that\u8217\'20\'19s not OK with me.\par \par \uc2 Moderator Linsey Davis : There is no state in this country where it is legal to kill a baby after it\u8217\'20\'19s born.\par \par \uc2 While it\u8217\'20\'19s not exactly a Woodward and Bernstein moment to observe that murdering babies is illegal in America, it was significant that Trump was much more thoroughly factchecked by the debate moderators than he was when he faced Biden. And it was part of a section on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, up there with the economy as one of the key issues driving this election, which did him few favours.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, if you had \u8220\'20\'1Cbaby killers\u8221\'20\'1D on your bingo card, you may nonetheless have been caught unawares by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other truly wild lie of the night: his reference to false claims that Haitian immigrants in Ohio are eating their neighbours\u8217\'20\'19 pets. \u8220\'20\'1CIn Springfield, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe people that came in. They\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats. They\u8217\'20\'19re eating -- they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there.\u8221\'20\'1D Harris turned to a visual shorthand she used repeatedly over the course of the debate (above) \u8211\'20\'13 cocking her head and looking at Trump with a bemused look on her face and her chin resting on her hand. You will certainly see this memed endlessly in the days ahead.\par \par \uc2 The Spingfield city manager said that there have been no such reports, moderator David Muir noted. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the people on television say their dog was eaten,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied. After the debate, Trump and his supporters characterised this kind of exchange as evidence of a \u8220\'20\'1Cthree-on-one\u8221\'20\'1D debate, which you can make your own mind up about. Harris, for her part, responded by saying \u8220\'20\'1Ctalk about extreme\u8221\'20\'1D and immediately pivoting to her own attack lines \u8211\'20\'13 the inverse of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s approach.\par \par \uc2 The fourth key exchange was on healthcare:\par \par \uc2 Linsey Davis: So just a yes or no, you still do not have a plan?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : I have concepts of a plan.\par \par \uc2 By coincidence, this is exactly what I told my editor when she asked how close I was to filing about an hour ago. It is also the kind of wafty answer on a matter of substance that is likely to be clipped up and used in Harris attack ads repeatedly over the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Trumps \u8220\'20\'1Cconcepts of a plan\u8221\'20\'1D refer to how he would replace the Affordable Care Act, the popular Obama era law that mandated the availability of health insurance to low-income families. There were other evasions, too, like his complicated language on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and on whether he had any regrets about January 6. On Ukraine, Trump would not say that he wanted Kyiv to win, instead saying \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop\u8221\'20\'1D and claiming that he would end it before even taking office by making \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  talk to each other.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/archie-bland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Archie Bland}}}\uc2  writes that there are five key exchanges that are likely to dominate the campaign in the days ahead. The first is on the economy, as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  promised to lift up the middle class while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  blamed her for high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Moderator David Muir : When it comes to the economy, do you believe Americans are better off than they were four years ago?\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : So, I was raised as a middle-class kid. And I am actually the only person on this stage who has a plan that is about lifting up the middle class and working people of America.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : We have inflation like very few people have ever seen before. Probably the worst in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 The debate kicked off with a section on the economy, arguably the toughest section of the night for Harris, who must contend with the fact that many voters blame the Biden administration for years of high inflation. While Harris set out more details of her own agenda, from a $6,000 child tax credit to a tax deduction for small businesses, her point that she and Biden were dealing with the Trump legacy of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst unemployment since the Great Depression\u8221\'20\'1D did not really make an affirmative case for the record of the last four years.\par \par \uc2 Trump did land his points about inflation and the dubious claim that he created \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the greatest economies in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D in his first term. But he also got distracted: by Harris calling his plan to raise tariffs a \u8220\'20\'1CTrump sales tax\u8221\'20\'1D, and by his own digression into a claim that \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of people [are] pouring into our country from prisons and jails, from mental institutions and insane asylums\u8221\'20\'1D. That was a hint of what was to come.\par \par \uc2 Second, writes Bland, is Harris tempting Trump into going off topic:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : You will see during the course of his rallies he talks about fictional characters like Hannibal Lecter. He will talk about \u8220\'20\'1Cwindmills cause cancer\u8221\'20\'1D. And what you will also notice is that people start leaving his rallies early out of exhaustion and boredom. And I will tell you the one thing you will not hear him talk about is you.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : People don\u8217\'20\'19t leave my rallies. We have the biggest rallies, the most incredible rallies in the history of politics. That\u8217\'20\'19s because people want to take their country back.\par \par \uc2 Can it really be this easy to wind him up? Again and again, Harris chose lines that keyed into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal preoccupations \u8211\'20\'13 and managed to goad him into responding to them at length instead of focusing on the kinds of issues that matter to voters. This exchange about crowd sizes, during a section of the debate that was supposed to be about immigration, meant that he had less time to talk a subject that is one of the areas where voters have the most doubts about Harris.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, during a section about Harris\u8217\'20\'19 changing position on fracking, he allowed himself to be sidetracked by her claim that he was given $400m by his father. Then there was the sales tax thing; the controversial conservative roadmap for a second Trump term, Project 2025; and the way he let a discussion about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Afghanistan withdrawal turn into one about his invitation to \uc2 Taliban\uc2  leaders to come to Camp David for talks.\par \par \uc2 None of these subjects would have been on his campaign managers\u8217\'20\'19 list of the talking points they would have wanted him to hit \u8211\'20\'13 and none of them mean very much to swing voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28am BST\par \par \uc2 After a period of undoubted momentum for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president came into this debate having stalled somewhat. Recent polls suggest that the race is effectively tied, both nationally and in most of the battleground states that will likely decide the outcome. Because the way voters are distributed gives Republicans an advantage in the electoral college, and because you would usually expect to see Harris\u8217\'20\'19 post-convention bump fade somewhat, polling experts like Nate Silver have recently seen \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR-u75l6i1nQO4VMmVf_el1RR7gSwg2lAV5ERkQU3rUGODvhFdq40Z9guVqlTdyNFJlro0ZyhBvp6HgqoMmU-weGpMpVz8XVB9bAT0laAZKg8_rXBTMGPxvAL7hHb9uAx2L4w4a4TES4NLEYVZhVv9fVEM_wVWbHnQxcrrhAgwJe1rGj6D611-LIGst0621COMir-ZriwVKudAjXkX_kJ8Eh4Pzk7sXaSPorcWwtUrpPYLjEJA9BBo0hY7NzCyROgZQ/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h39/h001.8VWoh_lSBTvL4Dbknu0LyCb3gQOzrephZMZ0xFNA-Us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the favourite to prevail}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many presidential candidates have \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8221\'20\'1D debates and ultimately lost the race \u8211\'20\'13 but there is little doubt that Harris had a good enough night to change those odds in her favour. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team wanted him to hang the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s unpopular policies around her neck, but instead he repeatedly lapsed into rambling and extreme Maga talking points that seem likely to have left many voters nonplussed.\par \par \uc2 The problem is not so much that he revealed himself as an erratic character, which any swing voter surely already knows: the problem is that he gifted Harris, who appeared supremely well-prepared, the chance to present him as the exhausting candidate of the all-too-familiar past \u8211\'20\'13 and herself as the optimist with a vision for the future.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17am BST\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s First Edition newsletter, Archie Bland writes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiuYhNFd-RqPBdryBPCDzfO0sy2Mr12UP4se8692qw16DyZvBDkV4nVNpnn6DtlGUyxGm_Ejb7j9uJ3AkTYRamYSa6thJeItsvT6gPDf7Ol9SGCBvd8Ar_KZs0eQowOa8fAkQYuDp8VU_XYV36JJIMKTV1zYmJnRDG6ebjIzfDITAnJgsWIIwhsGu5oYEErMOVq66qS462L3ulNXx0rEdo_QB3poa8AfJ2o_sI7IcK7-1Lm/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h30/h001.Go5ux-g0JJ7dafgcOO3yJX03Q9MBK9hwRW89zHb8rQk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even Fox News said }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiuYhNFd-RqPBdryBPCDzfO0sy2Mr12UP4se8692qw16DyZvBDkV4nVNpnn6DtlGUyxGm_Ejb7j9uJ3AkTYRamYSa6thJeItsvT6gPDf7Ol9SGCBvd8Ar_KZs0eQowOa8fAkQYuDp8VU_XYV36JJIMKTV1zYmJnRDG6ebjIzfDITAnJgsWIIwhsGu5oYEErMOVq66qS462L3ulNXx0rEdo_QB3poa8AfJ2o_sI7IcK7-1Lm/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h30/h001.Go5ux-g0JJ7dafgcOO3yJX03Q9MBK9hwRW89zHb8rQk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiuYhNFd-RqPBdryBPCDzfO0sy2Mr12UP4se8692qw16DyZvBDkV4nVNpnn6DtlGUyxGm_Ejb7j9uJ3AkTYRamYSa6thJeItsvT6gPDf7Ol9SGCBvd8Ar_KZs0eQowOa8fAkQYuDp8VU_XYV36JJIMKTV1zYmJnRDG6ebjIzfDITAnJgsWIIwhsGu5oYEErMOVq66qS462L3ulNXx0rEdo_QB3poa8AfJ2o_sI7IcK7-1Lm/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h30/h001.Go5ux-g0JJ7dafgcOO3yJX03Q9MBK9hwRW89zHb8rQk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  won}}}\uc2  last night\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate. Bland writes:\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 moods can only have been improved by the news, a few minutes after it ended, that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEB3Khvg1OizrO-5VCH71GGvDr8PWZqJ653EaFsfnXyQDomWvmiyN2UotzPvBxyrIHUR2BmjuRjIY3o4mEmZG_aI4ORtNCRm4HaT9u3MaaMa1A7CersWs7fcY4gZ14-U7DEALFEdnYWbRU8D8faoFYUGtF2YtbxK2b5kXoP1D8jhXeQaqHyeYYmCPPUEI1T5_Zq7bBQS-NHrwJAQXjQlCTGjkRwutSODA0xE4DdI7acCBZKzDMM5ahQwfGE-98IajRDMpEeKEKLcGVEWTlqTItt-vGo37MgcK8LC9bGdNqcrJQ/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h31/h001.-sE1u5UGycn-OdJ4HcEV404q1Y2REfSvYGPBwRP_v1Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift had endorsed Harris}}}\uc2 , and signed her post \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat lady\u8221\'20\'1D. And CNN\u8217\'20\'19s snap poll suggested that voters thought Harris won by a margin of 63% to 37% \u8211\'20\'13 nearly as big a margin as Trump achieved over Biden last time around. Key to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 success was baiting her opponent into rants on marginal topics, instead of talking about the issues that voters are interested in.\par \par \uc2 But while millions watched, Harris and Trump will reach millions more through the clips that will now be distributed through news and social media. For further reading on the debate, take a look at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDDGAS1e6MmybtSgiM4w2qa6yXT35cKg_TcyUD85CxQeSldi0JxFQwGoW_OiRQN_ee03WVLneLu6HsEZV0V9T3iwhSCt2Ss1wfPP8JVXPx4aPlcSJQ_gNQPTxgFjNQ0OtaRqU4OYcJdR4_KDAEGczbnlvTXRU-Uq93iYN9nul-bL7u1UPuEZIJwEuqkKiSCPtsq-THriHF-JALkRRIqYOiH9SdM7h-Jyjqw9jpbdUX8Sasc-2ztUxlI4iRc8qg7iq0/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h32/h001.6R4J2aH40H32EEH83h0oL_n0QnNm-SSUOtg3mN8MbF8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gabrielle Canon\u8217\'20\'19s key takeaways}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDDGAS1e6MmybtSgiM4w2qa9zr7owczksGVei__Q61SveFjNY36k-uMa0X3B1kxoQKB4dtt_H0SJ0Ad1QcG3rgwH6XXuMT3p1yq4Ti4rpP37vToNBXpNhrBqTAvLCZD_6Eb2EK_HAtw2Vnon1OK2tiaohanlmXajSQDignvyeSxF2Eey5_b-fkalTP4G_2tdzljpcWYfzj4bXzLHOwXxZ4wvYcE8Tsz-jQvTCNeLj3Q-lTTu4FcQz8I3v-rymj256SK6lkl8DGRWdNb0y4S3iSA/49o/5T-9ekQkRj-mHJPtEuW1uw/h33/h001.a4nWDL3R5k_Sq7xErsz76CabdPZ9MZYkJ0-mpxXxupg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this factcheck on both candidates}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Investors were watching for any market impact from the debate between the US presidential candidates, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Agence France-Presse (AFP) reports that the yen hit a nine-month high after a \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  official hinted at more monetary tightening. But, the news agency reports, the Japanese unit was also boosted by bets on a Harris presidency after she was considered to have come out on top in the US presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 According to AFP, The chances of Trump losing also weighed on bitcoin after he had previously vowed to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-bitcoin president\u8221\'20\'1D if elected in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  puts \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the defensive in head to head debate\par \par \uc2 US presidential hopefuls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  went head to head on Tuesday night in their first \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially only \u8211\'20\'13 debate before voters head to the polls on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 Democratic candidate Harris put her Republican rival Trump on the defensive with a stream of attacks on his fitness for office, his support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and his myriad legal woes.\par \par \uc2 A former prosecutor, Harris, 59, controlled the debate from the start, getting under her rival\u8217\'20\'19s skin repeatedly and prompting a visibly angry Trump, 78, to deliver a series of falsehood-filled retorts.\par \par \uc2 At one point, she goaded the former president by saying that people often leave his campaign rallies early \u8220\'20\'1Cout of exhaustion and boredom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has been frustrated by the size of Harris\u8217\'20\'19 own crowds, said, \u8220\'20\'1CMy rallies, we have the biggest rallies, the most incredible rallies in the history of politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then pivoted to a false claim about immigrants eating pets in Springfield, Ohio, that has circulated on social media and was amplified by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential candidate, Senator JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 The debate ended with Harris vowing to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca president for all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D while Trump attacked her as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst vice-president in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D. It was a fitting end for two candidates who offered starkly different visions for the nation in what might be their only presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-debate-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s powerful \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  stance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fact-checks: key takeaways from the debate}}}\par \par \uc2 No other presidential debate has yet been officially scheduled, so the face-off on Tuesday may represent the last time that Harris and Trump meet before election day. The days ahead will determine whether the debate made a lasting impression on the undecided voters who will decide what appears to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/latest-poll-kamala-harris-donald-trump-2024-us-election-presidential-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 neck-and-neck race.}}}\par \par \uc2 More on that in a moment, but first here are some other key updates:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift has endorsed Kamala Harris for president}}}\uc2 , in a post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  published minutes after the US presidential debate, saying the Democratic candidate would be the \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior\u8221\'20\'1D to fight for the rights and causes she believes in. Swift signed off \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C_wtAOKOW1z/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Childless cat lady}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D a reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/jd-vance-childless-cat-ladies-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments made by Republican vice-presidential candidate JD Vance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a sign of confidence in the debate\u8217\'20\'19s outcome, Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign challenged Trump to a second round in October, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sidestepped a direct question at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tuesday evening\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate}}}\uc2  on whether he wanted Ukraine to win in its war against Russia, underlining concerns that a second Trump administration could suspend military support for Kyiv. Asked directly by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-abc-moderators"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s David Muir}}}\uc2  on whether or not he wants Ukraine to win the war, he did not answer the question and said simply: \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240911ek9b00106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
