\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris targets Trump for falsehoods on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and immigration in fiery debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve \par \uc2 1,107 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par 13:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Presidential candidates meet for first time in contentious face-off as moderators fact-check Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statementsUS politics live \u8211\'20\'13 follow the latestHarris-Trump debate: key takeaways\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  sparred on Tuesday in a contentious presidential debate that repeatedly went off the rails, as the former president pursued bizarre and often falsehood-ridden tangents about crowd sizes, immigration policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The Philadelphia debate marked arguably the most significant opportunity for both Harris and Trump since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden withdrew}}}\uc2  from the presidential race in July, and the event began cordially enough. Harris crossed over to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s podium to shake his hand and introduce herself, an acknowledgement that the two presidential nominees had never met face to face before Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 But the cordiality did not last long. After delivering some boilerplate attack lines about the high inflation seen earlier in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, Trump pivoted to mocking Harris as a \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D and peddling baseless claims that Democrats want to \u8220\'20\'1Cexecute the baby\u8221\'20\'1D by allowing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions}}}\uc2  in the ninth month of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 That false claim was corrected by both Harris and the ABC News anchor Linsey Davis, who joined her fellow moderator David Muir in fact-checking some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements throughout the evening. Harris then segued into a stinging rebuke of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , criticizing him for nominating three of the supreme court justices who ruled to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly should not be telling a woman what to do with her body,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I pledge to you, when Congress passes a bill to put back in place the protections of Roe v Wade, as president of the United States, I will proudly sign it in to law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite broad public support for Roe v Wade, Trump boasted about his role in reversing it and applauded the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat courage\u8221\'20\'1D in issuing its ruling, while he dodged repeated questions about whether he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president.\par \par \uc2 Trump seemed to trip over himself even when moderators offered questions on his strongest issues, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2 . When asked about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the US-Mexico border, Harris pivoted to discussing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rallies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to invite you to attend one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rallies because it\u8217\'20\'19s a really interesting thing to watch,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou will see during the course of his rallies, he talks about fictional characters like Hannibal Lecter. He will talk about [how] windmills cause cancer. And what you will also notice is that people start leaving his rallies early out of exhaustion and boredom. And I will tell you, the one thing you will not hear him talk about is you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The tangent appeared to be a blatant attempt by Harris to bait Trump into squabbling over attendance at his rallies instead of discussing immigration policy \u8211\'20\'13 and it worked. Trump began attacking Harris with baseless accusations that her campaign was paying people to attend her rallies while celebrating his own events as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most incredible rallies in the history of politics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Then, rather than highlighting his immigration proposals, Trump chose to spread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debunked}}}\uc2  claims that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haitian migrants in an Ohio}}}\uc2  city have started capturing and eating their neighbors\u8217\'20\'19 pets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs. The people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there. And this is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in our country, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The outburst instantly became a source of mockery on social media, as Democrats celebrated Trump for \u8220\'20\'1Cdoubling down on the crazy uncle vibe\u8221\'20\'1D, in the words of the transportation secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PeteButtigieg/status/1833685626895442431"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Buttigieg.}}}\par \par \uc2 Even as moments of the debate bordered on absurdity, other exchanges regarding foreign policy and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 insurrection}}}\uc2  felt heavy with meaning. Pressed on his false claims regarding widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election, Trump again refused to acknowledge his defeat, prompting a stark warning from Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was fired by 81 million people, so, let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear about that. And, clearly, he is having a very difficult time processing that,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we cannot afford to have a president of the United States who attempts, as he did in the past, to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On foreign policy, Harris fielded difficult questions on the war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , as she expressed her support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cright to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D while calling for \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity, self determination and the dignity they so rightly deserve\u8221\'20\'1D for Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 Asked about his own stance on the war, Trump reiterated his bombastic claims that his presence in the White House would have prevented the wars in both Gaza and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were president, it would have never started,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were president, Russia would have never, ever. I know Putin very well. He would have never \u8211\'20\'13 and there was no threat of it either, by the way, for four years \u8211\'20\'13 have gone into Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And yet, when asked directly whether he wanted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  to win its war against Russia, Trump deflected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s the US\u8217\'20\'19s best interest to get this war finished and just get it done, all right? Negotiate a deal because we have to stop all of these human lives from being destroyed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The debate ended with Harris vowing to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca president for all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D while Trump attacked her as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst vice-president in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D. It was a fitting end for two candidates who offered starkly different visions for the nation in what might be their only presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 No other presidential debate has yet been officially scheduled, so the face-off on Tuesday may represent the last time that Harris and Trump meet before election day. The days ahead will determine whether the debate made a lasting impression on the undecided voters who will decide what appears to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/latest-poll-kamala-harris-donald-trump-2024-us-election-presidential-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 neck-and-neck race.}}}\par \par \uc2 Read more about the 2024 US election:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fact-checking the presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris slams Trump for falsehoods in fiery debate}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par 