\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris warns of \u8216\'20\'18what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake\u8217\'20\'19 for US as vice-president appears to win debate with Trump \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein, Maanvi Singh, Helen Sullivan and Kirsty McEwen \par \uc2 14,923 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par 08:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Candidates clashed on January 6, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration, Gaza and Ukraine. This live blog is closed. Follow the latest hereFull report: Harris slams Trump\u8217\'20\'19s flurry of liesTaylor Swift endorses Kamala HarrisFact checking the presidential debate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52am BST\par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closing. Please follow our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new US politics live blog here}}}\uc2 , which will cover all the reaction and fallout from the head to head debate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris puts Donald Trump on defensive in fiery debate \u8211\'20\'13 live US election updates}}}\par \par \uc2 Further reading:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris targets Trump for falsehoods on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and immigration in fiery debate}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fact-checking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s debate claims: from \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  to Project 2025}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-debate-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris-Trump debate: key takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats\u8217\'20\'19: Trump rambles falsely about immigrants in debate}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moira Donegan: The bar was low but Trump still didn\u8217\'20\'19t clear it}}}\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2024/sep/11/rally-sizes-abortion-and-eating-cats-the-trump-and-harris-debate-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rally sizes, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and eating cats: the Trump and Harris debate \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Freedland and Nikki McCann Ramirez of \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2  discuss the debate and what happened in our podcast, which you can listen to here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2024/sep/11/rally-sizes-abortion-and-eating-cats-the-trump-and-harris-debate-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rally sizes, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and eating cats: the Trump and Harris debate \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the video highlights:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48am BST\par \par \uc2 And in other news you should know if you\u8217\'20\'19re just tuning in: Taylor Swift has endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for president, in a post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  published minutes after the US presidential debate, saying the Democratic candidate would be the \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior\u8221\'20\'1D to fight for the rights and causes she believes in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a voter, I make sure to watch and read everything I can,\u8221\'20\'1D Swift wrote on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  to her 283 million followers late on Tuesday, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI will be casting my vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in the 2024 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think she is a steady-handed, gifted leader and I believe we can accomplish so much more in this country if we are led by calm and not chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In her statement, Swift encouraged her fans to register to vote.\par \par \uc2 Swift also addressed AI-generated images shared by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in late August that falsely depicted Swift and her fans endorsing his campaign for president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift endorses Kamala Harris for president in post signed \u8216\'20\'18childless cat lady\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from the debate\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just tuning in: presidential hopefuls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  went head to head on Tuesday night in their first \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially only \u8211\'20\'13 debate before voters head to the polls on 5 November. The candidates went into the event virtually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied in the polls}}}\uc2  with just weeks to convince a small but mighty minority of unsure voters on how to cast their ballot.\par \par \uc2 After weeks of arguments over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/04/kamala-harris-donald-trump-debate-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 format and rules}}}\uc2 , the debate aired live on ABC from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, a key swing state, with no audience in attendance and each candidate\u8217\'20\'19s microphone muted while their opponent spoke.\par \par \uc2 This was the second presidential debate this year for Trump, who also went up against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in June. The latter\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating performance}}}\uc2  triggered an upheaval within the Democratic party that would ultimately push Biden to step down and position Harris to head the ticket, an outcome Trump both takes credit for and complains about at his rallies.\par \par \uc2 With just 55 days until votes are tallied, Harris strived to highlight that she has a plan, and clearly responded to criticisms that she hasn\u8217\'20\'19t shared enough details with voters about her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/kamala-harris-policy-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 platform and priorities}}}\uc2 . With focused rhetoric on planning for the future, building the middle class, and reframing her record on everything from immigration to climate, Harris was able to show voters how she hopes to lead.\par \par \uc2 Analysts, meanwhile, were watching Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demeanor and clarity. The former president repeated frequent rhetoric from his rallies \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely disputed claims}}}\uc2  about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , crime, and his belief that he won the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 but shared little about how he would address key problems Americans are facing.\par \par \uc2 Beyond their differences in policy positions, the candidates also displayed diverging visions of the country. Trump promised his base to restore what he sees as the glory of the past, and Harris heralded the hope of a brighter future.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Gabrielle Canon has rounded up the key takeaways:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-debate-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s powerful \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  stance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fact-checks: key takeaways from the debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22am BST\par \par \uc2 You may be wondering what happened on the debate stage during the commercial breaks.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CBS\uc2  press pooler Sara Cook, during the second break, Harris made notes while Trump left the stage:\par \par \uc2 The second the stage hand said they were clear for a 4 minute break, Trump turned towards the exit, gave a big sigh through closed lips, and walked off stage without looking at Harris.\par \par \uc2 From the time the moderators announced they were going to break, Harris began writing on her notepad. She wrote continuously for the entire first two minutes of the break, occasionally bringing one hand to her chin or brushing hair behind her ear.\par \par \uc2 She then reviewed what she wrote for the next minute, making a few tweaks, before putting the pen down and looking out around the room with her hands folded in front of her. She took a sip of water from a glass placed under the lectern.\par \par \uc2 Trump walked back onstage 30 seconds before the end of break. He did not look at Harris, she did not look at him. Harris made small adjustments to her collar. Both candidates looked straight ahead until the program restarted.\par \par \uc2 Again, no words were spoken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump refused to say whether he wants Ukraine to win war against Russia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sidestepped a direct question at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/harris-trump-debate-fact-check-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tuesday evening\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate}}}\uc2  on whether he wanted Ukraine to win in its war against Russia, underlining concerns that a second Trump administration could suspend military support for Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Asked directly by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-abc-moderators"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s David Muir}}}\uc2  on whether or not he wants Ukraine to win the war, he did not answer the question and said simply: \u8220\'20\'1CI want the war to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D He focused on the war\u8217\'20\'19s human toll by saying that people were being killed \u8220\'20\'1Cby the millions,\u8221\'20\'1D a number that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been confirmed by any country or international organisation.\par \par \uc2 He went on to say that if elected he would negotiate a deal even before becoming president and suggested the United States was \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying with World War three.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  quickly pounced on his remarks, saying that if Trump had been president during the invasion, then \u8220\'20\'1CPutin would be sitting in Kyiv with his eyes on the rest of Europe\u8221\'20\'1D, and that in such a scenario the Russian president would move on to Poland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy don\u8217\'20\'19t you tell the 800,000 Polish Americans right here in Pennsylvania how quickly you would give up for the sake of favour and what you think is a friendship with what is known to be a dictator who would eat you for lunch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks will renew concerns in Kyiv that he will cut off military and economic aid toward the country if he is reelected at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/02/negotiated-outcome-now-seen-as-most-likely-result-of-russia-ukraine-war-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crucial moment in the war}}}\uc2 , when Kyiv is desperate for troops, financial support and for military hardware, much of it supplied by the United States and its Nato allies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/us-presidential-debate-donald-trump-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump refuses to say whether he wants Ukraine to win war against Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Back to the map shared earlier of \uc2 Google\uc2  trends during the debate. The only state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not the top search term was Ohio where the top term was \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moderator David Muir had asked about immigration \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favourite topic \u8211\'20\'13 but when Harris wrapped her remark with a jab about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crowd sizes, the former president could not help but take the bait. First, Trump claimed without evidence that Harris paid people to attend her rallies. Clearly wound up, he began to ramble \u8211\'20\'13 about immigrants eating people\u8217\'20\'19s pets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Springfield, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs, the people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims about immigrants allegedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing and eating the pets}}}\uc2  of US citizens originated, apparently, with a viral video of a resident of Springfield, Ohio, claiming before the town\u8217\'20\'19s council that immigrants in the community had killed ducks from a local park for food. The unsubstantiated and inflammatory video was shared widely on rightwing accounts, evolving quickly into a viral meme featuring AI-generated images of Trump surrounded by cats and dogs, appearing to protect them.\par \par \uc2 Here is that graphic again:\par \par \uc2 enltrBefore, and during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ndPir04XgM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ndPir04XgM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NickdMiller ? (@NickdMiller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NickdMiller/status/1833717247996760563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52am BST\par \par \uc2 In his response on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Trump made extremely erroneous claims, including that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe plan is, as you know, the vote is, they have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month. They even have, and you can look at the governor of West Virginia, the previous governor of West Virginia, not the current governor, who\u8217\'20\'19s doing an excellent job, but the governor before. He said the baby will be born and we will decide what to do with the baby. In other words, we\u8217\'20\'19ll execute the baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump was resurfacing a claim he made in October 2020, based on comments made in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Here is Reuters\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/world/fact-check-virginia-governors-2019-comments-about-abortion-bill-are-missing-co-idUSKBN27D2GS/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact check}}}\uc2  from the time:\par \par \uc2 A meme shared by over 70,766 on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  misrepresents comments made by Virginia Governor Ralph Northam in 2019 when he was asked about a bill that, among other things, aimed to ease restrictions for third trimester abortions in the state. The meme falsely suggests that Northam is in favor of legalizing infanticide by leaving out some key contextual references in his remarks.\par \par \uc2 Northam was referring to \u8220\'20\'1Cthird-trimester abortions\u8221\'20\'1D that are done in cases \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere there may be severe deformities. There may be a fetus that\u8217\'20\'19s non viable\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf a mother is in labor, I can tell you exactly what would happen. The infant would be delivered. The infant would be kept comfortable. The infant would be resuscitated if that\u8217\'20\'19s what the mother and the family desired, and then a discussion would ensue between the physicians and the mother,\u8221\'20\'1D Northam stated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Nick Miller has taken a look at how google searches by US state changed during the debate \u8211\'20\'13 almost universally, the top search turned to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the candidates spoke:\par \par \uc2 enltrBefore, and during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ndPir04XgM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ndPir04XgM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NickdMiller ? (@NickdMiller) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NickdMiller/status/1833717247996760563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris appears to win debate\par \par \uc2 Statistician Nate Silver has written on his blog that there is \u8220\'20\'1Ca strong consensus that Harris won the night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He notes that Bitcoin prices are down, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich also implies a loss for Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He adds:\par \par \uc2 Even the Fox News panel that I caught at the tail end of the evening seemed to concede that it was a win for Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris won the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mkraju/status/1833718682435870989"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN snap poll of debate-watchers}}}\uc2  63-37. You can find polling on past debates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/24781959/cnn-flash-poll.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . On average, the winner of the debate has led in this poll by 18 points, so Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 26-point win is toward the higher end of the range.\par \par \uc2 The majority of voters participating in a CNN focus group at \uc2 Mercyhurst University\uc2  in Erie, Pennsylvania, also said they thought Harris has won.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe group was made up of 13 voters who had not yet made a decision on who to vote for before the debate. When CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Phil Mattingly asked the group who won the debate, eight of the voters said Harris won the showdown. Mattingly noted that Erie is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe swingiest county\u8221\'20\'1D in the battleground state,\u8221\'20\'1D CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 Some conservatives, including Chris Rufo and Rod Drehrer conceded \u8211\'20\'13 with caveats \u8211\'20\'13a win for Harris, too, posting on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X:\par \par \uc2 enltrI think she's winning this. She comes across as normal , clear, and strong. Trump can't land a blow -- he is blustering and unfocused. Yeah, ABC's moderators are biased, but you can't blame them for Trump's vanity and lack of precision.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rod Dreher (@roddreher) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/roddreher/status/1833692175768383737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHarris wins slightly on points. This shouldn't change the race significantly either way, but she was able to de-risk this event and now the Right has lost the narrative that Harris is refusing media or engagement. Will be interesting to see if she goes silent again.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christopher F. Rufo ?? (@realchrisrufo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realchrisrufo/status/1833697047423398177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris appeared to address 'hero voters'\par \par \uc2 Harris also appeared to address what British political strategists termed \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/sep/07/us-hero-voters-key-to-harris-win-say-ex-aides-who-plotted-labour-uk-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hero voters}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, or voters who once voted Democrat but have since switched to the Republicans, or who might be lured from a party that they feel has veered too far to the right.\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former pollster, Deborah Mattinson, is to meet \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign team in Washington this week to share details of how Labour pulled off its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/jul/05/time-for-us-to-deliver-says-starmer-as-labour-heads-for-landslide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stunning election win}}}\uc2  by targeting key groups of \u8220\'20\'1Csqueezed working-class voters who wanted change\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Writing in the Observer, Mattinson said many of the concerns of crucial undecided voters will be similar on both of sides of the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese voters \u8211\'20\'13 often past Labour voters \u8211\'20\'13 had rejected the party because they believed that it had rejected them. Often Tory voters in 2019, they made up nearly 20% of the electorate. Labour\u8217\'20\'19s focus on economic concerns, from affordable housing to job security, won them back.\par \par \uc2 During the debate, in response to Trump stating, falsely, that Harris wanted to take guns away, Harris said that both she and Walz were gun owners.\par \par \uc2 Harris said in 2019 that she owned a gun for personal safety reasons. At the time, CNN reported that an aide has said she kept the handgun safely locked up.\par \par \uc2 Toward the end of the debate, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t ask if you\u8217\'20\'19re a democrat, I ask if you\u8217\'20\'19re ok.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier, she said:\par \par \uc2 So for everyone watching who remembers what January 6th was, I say we don\u8217\'20\'19t have to go back. Let\u8217\'20\'19s not go back. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going back. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to turn the page. And if that was a bridge too far for you, well, there is a place in our campaign for you. To stand for country. To stand for our democracy. To stand for rule of law. And to end the chaos. And to end the approach that is about attacking the foundations of our democracy \u8216\'20\'18cause you don\u8217\'20\'19t like the outcome.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Fox news proposes second debate in October\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Fox News said it proposed to hold a second presidential debate in October, adding it sent letters to the campaigns for both Democratic Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 campaign said on Tuesday night that Harris and her Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should do a second debate in October.\par \par \uc2 In the spin room shortly after the debate, Trump wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t commit to the rematch the Harris campaign has already offered, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI have to think about it\u8221\'20\'1D and that he might do it \u8220\'20\'1Cif it was on a fair network.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason you do a second debate is if you lose, and they lost,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19ll think about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Appearing nervous at first, Harris gained momentum when she was asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump, who appeared calm at first, grew more irate as he again and again turned questions back onto the topic of immigration.\par \par \uc2 Here is Harris on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a topic on which she has been notably strong. Much of her response was delivered while looking into the camera, as she did often during the debate, so that it appeared that she was speaking directly to voters:\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s understand how we got here. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hand-selected three members of the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe V. Wade. And they did exactly as he intended. And now in over 20 states there are Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans which make it criminal for a doctor or nurse to provide health care. In one state it provides prison for life. Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that make no exception even for rape and incest. Which understand what that means. A survivor of a crime, a violation to their body, does not have the right to make a decision about what happens to their body next. That is immoral. And one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly, should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I have talked with women around our country. You want to talk about this is what people wanted? Pregnant women who want to carry a pregnancy to term suffering from a miscarriage, being denied care in an emergency room because the health care providers are afraid they might go to jail and she\u8217\'20\'19s bleeding out in a car in the parking lot? She didn\u8217\'20\'19t want that. Her husband didn\u8217\'20\'19t want that. A 12 or 13-year-old survivor of incest being forced to carry a pregnancy to term? They don\u8217\'20\'19t want that. And I pledge to you when Congress passes a bill to put back in place the protections of Roe V. Wade as president of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law. But understand, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to be re-elected, he will sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Understand in his project 2025 there would be a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Understand in his project 2025 there would be a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- a monitor that would be monitoring your pregnancies, your miscarriages. I think the American people believe that certain freedoms, in particular the freedom to make decisions about one\u8217\'20\'19s own body, should not be made by the government.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Back to the debate. Harris and Trump debated for 90 minutes on a sombrely blue-lit stage at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2  in Philadelphia. Their mics were muted between responses, and they were given two minutes to respond to questions from ABC moderators Linsey Davis and David Muir.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate was the first time that Harris and Trump had met. As the two candidates took to the stage, she walked over to Trump and shook his hand before returning to the podium.\par \par \uc2 The first question asked of Harris was whether the American people were better off now than they were four years ago, and she failed to answer it directly. Instead, she talked about the future, and what she calls the \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That said, her answer sought instead to explain some of her policies for the future \u8211\'20\'13 something voters have been saying they want more of. A New York Times/Siena poll found that 28% of likely voters \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt they needed to know more about Ms. Harris, while only 9% said they needed to know more about Mr. Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo-thirds of those who want to know more said they were eager to learn about her policies, specifically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Do celebrity endorsements matter?\par \par \uc2 In 2012, researchers at \uc2 Northwestern University\uc2  and the University of Maryland tried to establish the correlation, if any, between celebrity {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insight.kellogg.northwestern.edu/article/the_oprah_effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsements and votes}}}\uc2 . They used \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/barack-obama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}\uc2  ahead of the 2008 Democrat primary to examine whether it had any effect on the polls.\par \par \uc2 The researchers concluded that \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement was worth about a million votes for Obama, who beat his main primary challenger, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , by about 270,000 votes in the states used in the sample.\par \par \uc2 Swift is a popular figure nationwide; especially among Democrats. An October 2023 Fox News poll found that 55% of voters overall, including 68% of Democrats, said they had a favourable view of Swift. Republicans were divided, with 43% having a favourable opinion and 45% an unfavourable one.\par \par \uc2 Cayce Myers, a professor of public relations at \uc2 Virginia Tech\uc2  said, Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement \u8220\'20\'1Cmay have an impact on the election because it may encourage younger Gen. Z fans to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Celebrity endorsements do not necessarily translate into meaningful turnout,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement was going out to particularly large fan base, was focussed on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, an issue that favours Democrats, and that the post, \u8220\'20\'1Chas the potential to raise awareness among younger voters who might be paying less attention to the presidential election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54am BST\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US elections coverage after the first debate between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you analysis, news, responses to that celebrity endorsement (Taylor\u8217\'20\'19s version) for the next while.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris tells supporters: 'We have a lot of work to do'\par \par \uc2 Speaking to supporters after the debate, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appeared to be in her stride.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we have a lot of work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd tonight I think highlighted for the American people what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHarris, addressing supporters now, clearly has swag and knows she won the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6c0vigKy6U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6c0vigKy6U}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1833709668335558859?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38am BST\par \par \uc2 California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  called Harris\u8217\'20\'19s performance a \u8220\'20\'1Cmasterclass\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s daylight and darkness, competency versus chaos, right versus wrong, illiberal versus liberal,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans meanwhile offered qualified praise, and bashed the moderators for fact-checking Trump.\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a Republican presidential hopeful turned Trump surrogate and harsh Harris critic, conceded that the vice-president had had a good night, perhaps even a better night. But he insisted that Trump won on the policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe heard a lot of words better delivered than usual, I will admit, from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but actions speak louder than words,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before mustering a very qualified assessment of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s performance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sad truth is, we only had a portion of this debate that was focused on policy, but for the portion of the debate that was focused on policy, which is the most important part of a presidential debate, I think in that area of it, I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to make an overall claim with respect to the policy aspect of this debate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won hands-down,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  welcomes 'eloquent' Swift endorsement 'as a fellow cat owner'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  reacted to Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement in the middle of an interview with MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Walz learns about Taylor Swift's endorsement of Harris in real time on MSNBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KVsyH9v87d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KVsyH9v87d}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1833708267597386157?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor said her post on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Celoquent\u8221\'20\'1D and called on Swifties, as her fans are known, to get on board with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump cheers debate performance, but says: 'I don't know if we're going to do another one'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made a surprise appearance in the spin room at the debate venue in Philadelphia, where he told reporters he felt good about his performance against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but might not debate her again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was my best debate ever, I think,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt showed how weak they are, how pathetic they are, and what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing to destroy our country, on the border, with foreign trade, with everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t good enough to do again, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CNow she wants to do another one, because she got beaten tonight, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do another one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Harris, even \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the far-right Florida representative, knew better than to attack the pop star.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love her songs, but I want to live in a world where liberals make my art and conservatives make my laws and policies,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris 'ready for a second debate', campaign team says\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cready for a second debate\u8221\'20\'1D in October, her campaign said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the bright lights, the American people got to see the choice they will face this fall at the ballot box: between moving forward with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , or going backwards with Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris-Walz campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what they saw tonight and what they should see at a second debate in October. Vice-president Harris is ready for a second debate. Is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This second debate would come in addition to an October face-off between vice-presidential candidates \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20am BST\par \par \uc2 In her post announcing her support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Taylor Swift said that she had been spurred to act after the Trump campaign implied that she supported him, and also was not pleased with a certain remark made by his running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRecently I was made aware that AI of \u8216\'20\'18me\u8217\'20\'19 falsely endorsing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential run was posted to his site. It really conjured up my fears around AI, and the dangers of spreading misinformation. It brought me to the conclusion that I need to be very transparent about my actual plans for this election as a voter. The simplest way to combat misinformation is with the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D Swift wrote.\par \par \uc2 She signed her post, in which she posed with a long-haired cat, \u8220\'20\'1CChildless Cat Lady\u8221\'20\'1D. That\u8217\'20\'19s something Vance once said, and which is not going away:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/jd-vance-childless-cat-ladies-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance pleads sarcasm in latest effort to clean up \u8216\'20\'18childless cat ladies\u8217\'20\'19 remark}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: 2020 election lawsuits\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeated misinformation about the result of lawsuits contesting the 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 The former president said that \u8220\'20\'1Cno judge looked at\u8221\'20\'1D lawsuits he and allies filed about irregularities in the election. \u8220\'20\'1CThey said we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have standing. A technicality. Can you imagine a system where a person in an election doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have standing? The president of the United States doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have standing. That\u8217\'20\'19s how we lost,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s misleading \u8211\'20\'13 some lawsuits were dismissed due to a lack of standing, meaning that those who brought the lawsuits didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a stake in the results. Others were decided on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://campaignlegal.org/results-lawsuits-regarding-2020-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merit}}}\uc2 . Judges found in some cases that evidence provided was speculative, or failed to show fraud.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Taylor Swift says she will vote for Harris\par \par \uc2 Taylor Swift, the world-famous pop superstar, just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C_wtAOKOW1z/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on Instagram}}}\uc2  that she will vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , giving the vice-president perhaps her biggest celebrity endorsement yet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will be casting my vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in the 2024 Presidential Election. I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/kamalaharris/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kamalaharris}}}\uc2  because she fights for the rights and causes I believe need a warrior to champion them. I think she is a steady-handed, gifted leader and I believe we can accomplish so much more in this country if we are led by calm and not chaos. I was so heartened and impressed by her selection of running mate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/timwalz/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @timwalz}}}\uc2 , who has been standing up for LGBTQ+ rights, IVF, and a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to her own body for decades,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance clears up Trump's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position and says Harris focused on 'echoing platitude after platitude'\par \par \uc2 ABC News then heard from JD Vance, the Ohio senator who is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, and asked him for clarity on whether the former president supported national restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The debate\u8217\'20\'19s moderators tried to get an answer out of Trump, but he instead talked about how he was proud that states were deciding the issue, while falsely claiming that Democrats supported infanticide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the president\u8217\'20\'19s been very clear that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. I think in some ways he finds the question a little bit ridiculous, because why are we asking him about legislation that\u8217\'20\'19s never going to actually happen, and why he would veto it or not veto it, when he says very explicitly that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t support a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and he wants these policies to be made by the states,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He then criticized Harris for debate rhetoric he described as empty, saying:\par \par \uc2 You had \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  effectively echoing platitude after platitude after platitude. The American people can\u8217\'20\'19t pay their grocery bills on platitudes. They can\u8217\'20\'19t put their kids in a house on platitudes. And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  had a lot to say but very little actual substance behind it for how she\u8217\'20\'19s going to lower grocery prices, secure the border and make housing more affordable in this country.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s been the vice-president for three-and-a-half years. She can\u8217\'20\'19t run on a record, and she apparently can\u8217\'20\'19t run on much of her plans either, because it\u8217\'20\'19s just a lot of slogans and not a whole lot of substance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says Trump's performance reminds him of 'an old man yelling at the clouds'\par \par \uc2 In an interview with ABC News after the debate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for vice-president, said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came off as unhinged.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have to tell you, if it weren\u8217\'20\'19t so dangerous, it reminds you of an old man yelling at the clouds. That was his thing: \u8216\'20\'18Get off my yard,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Walz, the governor of Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, I think country can see what happened tonight. We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep pushing forward. That\u8217\'20\'19s the way that the country wants to see our politics be \u8211\'20\'13 she laid it out clearly. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  brought nothing tonight but anger, resentment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Women were chipping in for Harris during the debate.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said that during the first hour of the debate, 71% of their grassroots donors were women. The campaign has not yet provided an overall tally for her fundraising figures.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 In a conversation about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity, the vice-president said Trump had a long history of stoking racial division.\par \par \uc2 She recalled that he had placed a full-page ad in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  that called for the death penalty for the Central Park Five, a group of Black and Latino teenagers who were wrongly accused of raping a white woman.\par \par \uc2 It appears the reference was intentional.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign announced that Yusef Salaam, one of the five exonerated men who is now a New York councilmember, will be in the spin room as a surrogate for the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump hits back at Harris's promises, asking: 'Why hasn't she done it?'\par \par \uc2 While Harris held off on attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in her closing statement, the former president did not do the same, instead seizing on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s years in the vice-presidency to argue she would be an ineffective leader.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, she just started by saying she\u8217\'20\'19s going to do this, she\u8217\'20\'19s going to do that. She\u8217\'20\'19s going to do all these wonderful things. Why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t she done it?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump asked.\par \par \uc2 He went on:\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s been there for three-and-a-half years. They\u8217\'20\'19ve had three-and-a-half years to fix the border. They\u8217\'20\'19ve had three-and-a-half years to create jobs and all the things we talked about. Why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t she done it? She should leave right now, go down to that beautiful White House, go to the Capitol, get everyone together and do the things you want to do, but you haven\u8217\'20\'19t done it and you won\u8217\'20\'19t do it because you believe in things that the American people don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in.\par \par \uc2 Trump restated his downbeat view of the state of the country, which is a major part of his pitch to voters:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re a failing nation. We\u8217\'20\'19re a nation that\u8217\'20\'19s in serious decline. We\u8217\'20\'19re being laughed at all over the world. All over the world, they laughed. I know the leaders very well, they\u8217\'20\'19re coming to see me. They call me. We\u8217\'20\'19re laughed at all over the world. They don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what happened to us as a nation.\par \par \uc2 He concluded by calling Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst vice-president in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And with that, the debate concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 In her closing statement, Harris vows to 'protect our fundamental rights and freedoms'\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now at the closing statements of the debate, with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  up first.\par \par \uc2 Casting herself as a unifier, she argues her background as a prosecutor made her the right person to lead the country:\par \par \uc2 I will be a president that will protect our fundamental rights and freedoms, including the right of a woman to make decisions about her own body and not have her government tell her what to do. I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you, I started my career as a prosecutor. I was the DA, I was an attorney general, United States senator and now vice-president. I only have one client: the people.\par \par \uc2 And I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you, as a prosecutor, I never asked a victim or a witness, are you a Republican or a Democrat? The only thing I ever asked them, are you OK? And that\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of president we need right now, someone who cares about you and is not putting themselves first. I intend to be a president for all Americans and focus on what we can do over the next 10 and 20 years to build back up our country by investing right now in you, the American people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: the Central Park Five\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doubled down on his claims that the Central Park Five, a group of Black teenagers who were arrested in connection with the rape and assault of a white female jogger in 1989 and convicted based on police-coerced confessions.\par \par \uc2 Back then, Trump called for the execution of these five children. When \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  brought up Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance, he dug in: \u8220\'20\'1CThey pled guilty \u8230\'20\'26 They badly hurt a person, they killed a person, ultimately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 All of them were exonerated after a convicted murderer confessed to the crime in 2002. In 2014, they were awarded a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/06/nyregion/41-million-settlement-for-5-convicted-in-jogger-case-is-approved.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $41m settlement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 1989, before any of the boys had faced trial, Trump paid a reported $85,000 to take out advertising space in four of the city\u8217\'20\'19s newspapers, including the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , calling for their execution. The headline read: \u8220\'20\'1CBring Back The Death Penalty. Bring Back Our Police!\u8221\'20\'1D and above his signature, Trump wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to hate these muggers and murderers. They should be forced to suffer and, when they kill, they should be executed for their crimes. They must serve as examples so that others will think long and hard before committing a crime or an act of violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Oliver Laughland reported back in 2016, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s charge against the Central Park Five was a precursor to his divisive populism:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/17/central-park-five-donald-trump-jogger-rape-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump and the Central Park Five: the racially charged rise of a demagogue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  could have been a mess of layered talking, unchallenged claims and wild veers off-topic.\par \par \uc2 Instead, ABC\u8217\'20\'19s moderators, David Muir and Linsey Davis, kept the candidates on point.\par \par \uc2 Muir and Davis took on the first matchup between the two virtually tied presidential candidates, seeking to \u8220\'20\'1Cenforce timing agreements and ensure a civilized discussion\u8221\'20\'1D, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc.com/news/5e38600c-4732-4cd2-a99c-3dedfa81beb0/category/1138628"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate rules}}}\uc2  from ABC that took weeks to negotiate, and it was no easy task.\par \par \uc2 The two effectively rerouted discussions back to the questions they had asked, on key topics including the economy, immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the peaceful transfer of power, and made important clarifying fact-check statements when they were warranted.\par \par \uc2 When Trump made the outlandish claim that Democrats supported \u8220\'20\'1Cthe execution\u8221\'20\'1D of babies after they were born and accused \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, of supporting abortions in the ninth month, Davis laid out the facts. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no state in this country where it is legal to kill a baby after it is born,\u8221\'20\'1D Davis told viewers.\par \par \uc2 Muir also pushed Trump on his connection to the 6 January attack on the US Capitol, and his belief that he won the election, despite all evidence to the contrary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris rebuts Trump gun claims, saying she and Walz 'are both gun owners'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may have been a transformational force in the GOP, but he\u8217\'20\'19s followed in the footsteps of many Republicans who came before him by saying his Democratic opponent wants to take away guns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe has a plan to confiscate everybody\u8217\'20\'19s gun,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump alleged at one point in the debate.\par \par \uc2 A few minutes later, Harris mentioned that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2019/04/11/politics/kamala-harris-gun-owner/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she is a gun owner}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 something she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t bring up often.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis business about taking everyone\u8217\'20\'19s guns away \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and I are both gun owners. We\u8217\'20\'19re not taking anybody\u8217\'20\'19s guns away. So stop with the continuous lying about this stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Snap analysis: where the candidates stand\par \par \uc2 As the debate winds into its final stretch, both candidates have stayed true to form.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has doubled down on his tried-and-true talking points \u8211\'20\'13 including a barrage of misinformation about immigration and immigrants, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and election security.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appears to have rattled him in several moments, including when she made light of his tendency to reference fictional characters like Hannibal Lecter, or to set off on difficult-to-follow tangents about windmills.\par \par \uc2 Though the candidates were muted while the other was speaking, Harris also made good use of her side of the screen \u8211\'20\'13 putting out a range of expressions to show skepticism, concern and dismissal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris accuses Trump of using 'race to divide the American people'\par \par \uc2 Days after Harris launched her campaign, Trump alleged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/kamala-harris-texas-rally-donald-trump-racial-identity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 something that was shocking}}}\uc2 , even by his standards: that the vice-president, who is of South Asian and Black Jamaican heritage, was not actually African American.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do you believe it\u8217\'20\'19s appropriate to weigh in on the racial identity of your opponent?\u8221\'20\'1D moderator David Muir asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t care. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care what she is. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care. You make a big deal out of something, I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t care less, whatever she wants to be is OK with me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 Muir then asked Harris for her thoughts. She replied:\par \par \uc2 Honestly, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a tragedy that we have someone who wants to be president who has consistently, over the course of his career, attempted to use race to divide the American people. You know, I do believe that the vast majority of us know that we have so much more in common than what separates us, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t want this kind of approach that is just constantly trying to divide us, and especially by race.\par \par \uc2 She made a point to bring up Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in pushing for the prosecution of the Central Park Five. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/17/central-park-five-donald-trump-jogger-rape-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump and the Central Park Five: the racially charged rise of a demagogue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now getting into a perilous topic for Harris: the US pullout from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings dropped after the chaotic departure of American troops, during which a terrorist attack killed 13 US soldiers, and Republicans have hammered his administration over the withdrawal ever since. Harris says she approved of the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to end US involvement in the war, then pivoted to, once again, attacking Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI agreed with President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pull out of Afghanistan. Four presidents said they would, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did. And as a result, America\u8217\'20\'19s taxpayers are not paying the $300m a day we were paying for that endless war. And as of today, there is not one member of the United States military who is in active duty in a combat zone, in any war zone around the world, the first time this century,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 Then, on to Trump:\par \par \uc2 But let\u8217\'20\'19s understand how we got to where we are. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , when he was president, negotiated one of the weakest deals you can imagine. He calls himself a dealmaker. Even his national security adviser said it was a weak, terrible deal, and here\u8217\'20\'19s how it went down: he bypassed the Afghan government. He negotiated directly with a terrorist organization called the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . The negotiation involved the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  getting 5,000 terrorists, \uc2 Taliban\uc2  terrorists released.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris, no surprise, strongly defended Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support for Ukraine, then again attacked Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the reason that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says that this war would be over within 24 hours is because he would just give it up,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said. \u8220\'20\'1CThrough the work that I and others did, we brought 50 countries together to support Ukraine in its righteous defense, and because of our support, because of the air defense, the ammunition, the artillery, the javelins, the Abrams tanks that we have provided, Ukraine stands as an independent and free country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were president, Putin would be sitting in Kyiv right now, and understand what that would mean, because Putin\u8217\'20\'19s agenda is not just about Ukraine. Understand why the European allies and our Nato allies are so thankful that you are no longer president, and that we understand the importance of the greatest military alliance the world has ever known, which is Nato, and what we have done to preserve the ability of Zelenskiy and the Ukrainians to fight for their independence. Otherwise, Putin would be sitting in Kyiv with his eyes on the rest of Europe, starting with Poland.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump declines to say whether he wants Ukraine to win against Russia\par \par \uc2 The debate just resumed after a short break, and the first question, to Trump, was about Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have said you would solve this war in 24 hours. You said so just before the break tonight. How exactly would you do that? And I want to ask you a very simple question tonight: do you want Ukraine to win this war?\u8221\'20\'1D moderator David Muir asked.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s response wasn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly a yes:\par \par \uc2 I want the war to stop. I want to save lives that are being uselessly. People being killed by the millions. It\u8217\'20\'19s the millions. It\u8217\'20\'19s so much worse than the numbers that you\u8217\'20\'19re getting, which are fake numbers.\par \par \uc2 Muir pressed: \u8220\'20\'1CJust to clarify the question, do you believe it\u8217\'20\'19s in the US best interest for Ukraine to win this war?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s the US best interest to get this war finished and just get it done, all right, negotiate a deal, because we have to stop all of these human lives from being destroyed,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: crime\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  claimed that crime is way up in the US \u8211\'20\'13 and he\u8217\'20\'19s wrong.\par \par \uc2 Crime is actually down. Data from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found that violent crime decreased during the Trump administration, spiking in 2020 during the pandemic, and continuing to trend downward afterwards.\par \par \uc2 Preliminary data from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found that violent crime was down 6% in 2023, and 15% in the first quarter of 2024.\par \par \uc2 Violent crime decreased throughout most of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cde.ucr.cjis.gov/LATEST/webapp/#/pages/explorer/crime/crime-trend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to FBI data}}}\uc2  that uses information provided by law enforcement agencies. However, it spiked in 2020 during the Covid-19 pandemic. It has trended downward since 2020 across the US, nearing pre-pandemic levels in 2022. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/crime-fbi-violence-murder-8f47df4e8cf1917e6d8032e19dc1b4c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Preliminary FBI data for 2023}}}\uc2  shows that violent crime overall was down another 6% that year.\par \par \uc2 Though the data is preliminary, it includes numbers from 80% of the law enforcement agencies in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump got the same question, and didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much new to say, instead insisting that both the 7 October attack and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine would not have happened if he had been president \u8211\'20\'13 a line from previous speeches and debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were president, it would have never started. If I were president, Russia would have never, ever, I know Putin very well. He would have never. There was no threat of it either,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris dodges when asked how she would resolve stalemate over Gaza ceasefire\par \par \uc2 The debate has now shifted into foreign policy territory, and the first question, to Harris, was how she would convince Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to agree to a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president didn\u8217\'20\'19t quite answer the question, instead vowing to defend Israel, while acknowledging the toll taken on civilians by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza:\par \par \uc2 Now, Israel has a right to defend itself \u8230\'20\'26 and how it does so matters. Because it is also true, far too many innocent Palestinians have been killed, children, mothers. What we know is that this war must end \u8230\'20\'26 And the way it will end is we need a ceasefire deal, and we need the hostages out, and so we will continue to work around the clock on that. Work around the clock, also understanding that we must chart a course for a two-state solution, and in that solution, there must be security for the Israeli people and Israel, and an equal measure for the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI will always give Israel the ability to defend itself, in particular, as it relates to Iran, and any threat that Iran and its proxies pose to Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Trump 'was fired by 81 million people' after he again refuses to accept 2020 election loss\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued to insist that he won the 2020 election, despite moderator David Muir pointing out that judges across the country had thrown out his claims of fraud.\par \par \uc2 That gave \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  an opening to attack him in terms that the former The Apprentice host would well understand:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was fired by 81 million people, so, let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear about that. And, clearly he is having a very difficult time processing that. But we cannot afford to have a president of the United States who attempts, as he did in the past, to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.\par \par \uc2 And I\u8217\'20\'19m going to tell you that I have traveled the world as vice-president of the United States, and world leaders are laughing at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I talked with military leaders, some of whom work with you, and they say, you\u8217\'20\'19re a disgrace. And when you then talk in this way in a presidential debate and deny \u8230\'20\'26 you have lost because you did, in fact, lose that election, it leads one to believe that perhaps we do not have, in the candidate to my right, the temperament or the ability to not be confused about facts. That\u8217\'20\'19s deeply troubling, and the American people deserve better.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 In her debate against \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  four years ago, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  memorably rebuked him when he interrupted her, by responding: \u8220\'20\'1CMr vice-president, I\u8217\'20\'19m speaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just deployed the line against Harris at their debate. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWait a minute, I\u8217\'20\'19m talking now. If you don\u8217\'20\'19t mind. Please. Does that sound familiar?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  throws \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 famous \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m speaking\u8221\'20\'1D moment back at her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uYjI3UZnlh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uYjI3UZnlh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1833684503455314122?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 A bit more about how Harris\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 quip\uc2  landed in 2020:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/08/kamala-harris-mike-pence-vice-presidential-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Looks speak louder than words as Harris makes quotable case against Pence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attack\par \par \uc2 Trump repeated one of his usual falsehoods: that abortions are taking place in the ninth month of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In fact, fewer than 1% of abortions are performed past 21 weeks of pregnancy; when these abortions do take place, they often occur in medical emergencies or cases of fetal anomalies.\par \par \uc2 Trump also suggested, at multiple points, that abortions take place after birth. That would be infanticide, and it is illegal in all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims Harris's verbal attacks led to assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is still not sure why a young man opened fire at a Trump rally in Pennsylvania in July, wounding the former president and killing an attendee. But at the debate, the former president has said that Harris and other Democrats calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat to democracy\u8221\'20\'1D sparked the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI probably took a bullet to the head because of the things that they say about me. They talk about democracy, I\u8217\'20\'19m a threat to democracy, they\u8217\'20\'19re the threat to democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, before bringing up the investigation into Russian influence that bedeviled him during his first term.\par \par \uc2 Moderator David Muir then cut him off, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot to get to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: immigrants\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spouted off a number of false claims about immigration and immigrants.\par \par \uc2 To start, he said immigrants are \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking over the towns \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re going in violently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s false. Although some US cities have seen an influx of immigrants, most have arrived legally, with work permits or with authorization to stay while their cases are worked out in the courts.\par \par \uc2 There has been no widespread violence in these cities and overall, immigrants are less likely to commit crimes than the US-born according to multiple, extensive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w31440/w31440.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 studies}}}\uc2 , including from the conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cato.org/sites/cato.org/files/2020-10/working-paper-60.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cato Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump also referenced immigrants \u8220\'20\'1Ceating the dogs\u8221\'20\'1D in Springfield, Ohio, which was live fact-checked by the debate moderators. Republicans have sometimes substituted dogs for cats when repeating this misinformation. Here\u8217\'20\'19s some reporting from the Guardian looking into the salacious, and completely false claim:\par \par \uc2 The misinformation about migrants in Springfield comes as the Trump campaign has sought to make immigration a key issue, tying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the towns unprepared for migrants arriving via the southern border. Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Rob Rue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/ohio-city-plunged-housing-crisis-15000-migrants-arrive-setting-us-up-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on Fox}}}\uc2  to say the Biden administration was to blame for \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing cities like ours and taxing us beyond our limit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The city has seen a large number of migrants from Haiti, which has both helped the economy there with staffing concerns while also stretching the capacity of some services like clinics and schools, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/03/us/springfield-ohio-school-bus-crash-haiti-immigrants.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times reported}}}\uc2 . A Biden administration policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/investigations/biden-admin-gives-protected-status-309000-haitians-rcna159438?utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=240909-kamala_migrants_ravage_ohio_city_and_its_coming_to_your_city_next&utm_content=ncl-rugWmD7K9C&_nlid=rugWmD7K9C&_nhids=rXWVHwR8gA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided}}}\uc2  temporary protected status to hundreds of thousands of Haitian migrants, who have left their home country because of ongoing violence. Some estimates say as many as 20,000 people from Haiti have come to the city, the Times said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans spread baseless slurs about \u8216\'20\'18cat-eating migrants\u8217\'20\'19 in Ohio city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Harris took Trump to task for spending his rallies making strange statements, rather than talking about how he would solve Americans\u8217\'20\'19 problems:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to actually do something really unusual, and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to invite you to attend one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rallies, because it\u8217\'20\'19s a really interesting thing to watch. You will see during the course of his rallies, he talks about fictional characters like Hannibal Lecter. He will talk about, windmills cause cancer. And what you will also notice is that people start leaving his rallies early out of exhaustion and boredom. And I will tell you, the one thing you will not hear him talk about is you. You will not hear him talk about your needs, your dreams and your needs and your desires. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you I believe you deserve a president who actually puts you first. And I pledge to you that I will.\par \par \uc2 The former president replied by defending the size of his events:\par \par \uc2 People don\u8217\'20\'19t leave my rallies. We have the biggest rallies, the most incredible rallies in the history of politics. That\u8217\'20\'19s because people want to take their country back.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump falsely claims immigrants are 'eating the pets' in Ohio town\par \par \uc2 In perhaps the most bizarre moment of this debate so far, Trump repeated an unsubstantiated claim that immigrants are eating pets in an Ohio town, forcing the moderator to tell him that there is no proof of that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Springfield, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the dogs, the people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats \u8230\'20\'26 they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the pets of the people that live there. And this is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in our country, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said.\par \par \uc2 The story of immigrants allegedly eating pets has circulated in rightwing media in recent days, and been repeated by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou bring up Springfield, Ohio, and ABC News did reach out to the city manager there. He told us there have been no credible reports of specific claims of pets being harmed, injured or abused by individuals within the immigrant community,\u8221\'20\'1D moderator David Muir told Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on this most strange story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans spread baseless slurs about \u8216\'20\'18cat-eating migrants\u8217\'20\'19 in Ohio city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris got into a back and forth, after the former president demanded that she answer whether she supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the third trimester.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill she allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the eighth month, ninth month, seventh month?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump demanded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCome on,\u8221\'20\'1D an annoyed Harris replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump's economy\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as he always does, boasted that the US experienced its \u8220\'20\'1Cbest\u8221\'20\'1D economy under his administration, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  noted that Trump left the US with \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst unemployment since the Great Depression\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re both wrong \u8211\'20\'13 Trump by a lot, and Harris by a shade.\par \par \uc2 Though unemployment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/virus-outbreak-financial-markets-us-news-ap-top-news-unemployment-623da121a91a4951b3bcde201a46120d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spiked to its worst levels}}}\uc2  since the Great Depression in the immediate aftermath of the pandemic, it had dipped back by the time Trump left office.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbest economy\u8221\'20\'1D line has been the bane of fact-checkers since he was in office. \u8220\'20\'1CBest\u8221\'20\'1D is a very vague term \u8211\'20\'13 but by several measures, including GDP, unemployment and the trade deficit \u8211\'20\'13 the economy was far from its peak.\par \par \uc2 Here are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some final numbers}}}\uc2  from his term, compiled by FactCheck.org:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The economy lost 2.7m jobs. The unemployment rate increased by 1.7 percentage points to 6.4%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Paychecks grew faster than inflation. Average weekly earnings for all workers were up 8.4% after inflation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 After-tax corporate profits went up, and the stock market set new records. The S&P 500 index rose 67.8%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The international trade deficit Trump promised to reduce went up. The US trade deficit in goods and services in 2020 was the highest since 2008 and increased 36.3% from 2016.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The number of people lacking health insurance rose by 3 million.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The federal debt held by the public went up, from $14.4tn to $21.6tn.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Home prices rose 27.5%, and the homeownership rate increased 2.1 percentage points to 65.8%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump 'should not be telling a woman what to do with her body', Harris says\par \par \uc2 Harris then explained her support for reinstating Roe v Wade, in much clearer terms than Trump used:\par \par \uc2 Now, in over 20 states, there are Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, which make it criminal for a doctor or nurse to provide healthcare. In one state, it provides prison for life. Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that make no exception, even for rape and incest, which, understand what that means, a survivor of a crime of violation to their body does not have the right to make a decision about what happens to their body.\par \par \uc2 Next, that is immoral, and one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.\par \par \uc2 She vowed to sign legislation restoring the overturned precedent, if Congress approves it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says supreme court showed 'great courage' in overturning Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Linsey Davis, a moderator of the debate, pressed Trump to explain his policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting that he has changed his views repeatedly.\par \par \uc2 Trump responded by going through how various states have handled the issue, and claiming, falsely, that in some states, babies are killed after they are born (which is murder, and illegal everywhere).\par \par \uc2 Then, he thanked the supreme court justices who voted to overturn Roe v Wade, though misstated the number \u8211\'20\'13 five voted to do away with the precedent, not six. Trump said:\par \par \uc2 Each individual state is voting. It\u8217\'20\'19s the vote of the people. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s not tied up in the federal government. I did a great service in doing it. It took courage to do it, and the supreme court had great courage in doing it, and I give tremendous credit to those six justices.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris just made something of a new attack on Trump, by accusing him of being deferential to Chinese president Xi Jinping despite lingering questions over what his government knows about the origins of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did, let\u8217\'20\'19s talk about this with Covid, is, he actually thanked President Xi for what he did during Covid. Look at his tweet: \u8216\'20\'18Thank you, President Xi. Exclamation point\u8217\'20\'19, when we know that Xi was responsible for lacking and not giving us transparency about the origins of Covid,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump and Project 2025\par \par \uc2 As expected, Trump denied knowledge of Project 2025, a 900-page plan for the aggressive rightwing reform of nearly every aspect of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Though Trump has tried repeatedly to distance himself from the platform, which seeks to strip away reproductive rights, LGBTQ+ rights and voting rights, his policies align heavily with Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  reported: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump well knows \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and has spoken at their events, and [Kevin] Roberts, Heritage\u8217\'20\'19s leader, has previously said he and Trump have talked several times. Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s authors and supporters contain a ton of former Trump administration officials.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is Project 2025 and what is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 As Trump is talking, Harris appears to be looking at him and lightly shaking her head.\par \par \uc2 And whenever it\u8217\'20\'19s Harris\u8217\'20\'19s turn to talk, Trump has been looking straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he has 'nothing to do with Project 2025'\par \par \uc2 As the two candidates squabbled over the economy, Harris quickly brought up Project 2025, the rightwing blueprint to remake the \uc2 US government\uc2  authored by former Trump officials and people connected to him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to tell you all on this debate tonight, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear from the same old, tired book, a bunch of lies, grievances and name-calling. What you\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear tonight is a detailed and dangerous plan called Project 2025 that the former president intends on implementing if he were elected to again,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 Trump replied by saying he has no involvement with the document:\par \par \uc2 I have nothing to do with Project 2025. That\u8217\'20\'19s out there. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t read it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to read it, purposely. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to read it. This was a group of people that got together. They came up with some ideas, I guess, some good, some bad. But it makes no difference. I have nothing to do. Everybody knows I\u8217\'20\'19m an open book. Everybody knows what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do, cut taxes very substantially and create a great economy like I did. Before, we had the greatest economy, we got hit with a pandemic, and the pandemic was, not since 1917 where 100 million people died, has there been anything like it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 In his rebuttal, Trump zeroed in on what his campaign believes are two of his strongest issues: inflation and undocumented people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, we\u8217\'20\'19ve had a terrible economy because inflation has, which it\u8217\'20\'19s really known as a country buster. It breaks up countries. We have inflation like very few people have ever seen before, probably the worst in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. That isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite true \u8211\'20\'13 inflation had been worse in the past than the bout experienced over the last three years.\par \par \uc2 Then, Trump raised the issue of illegal immigration:\par \par \uc2 On top of that, we have millions of people pouring into our country from prisons and jails, from mental institutions and insane asylums, and they\u8217\'20\'19re coming in, and they\u8217\'20\'19re taking jobs that are occupied right now by African Americans and Hispanics and also unions. Unions are going to be affected very soon. And you see what\u8217\'20\'19s happening. You see what\u8217\'20\'19s happening with towns throughout the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris asked whether Americans are better off than they were four years ago\par \par \uc2 The first question, for Harris, was: \u8220\'20\'1CDo you believe Americans are better off than they were four years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was raised as a middle-class kid, and I am actually the only person on this stage who has a plan that is about lifting up the middle class and working people of America. I believe in the ambition, the aspirations, the dreams of the American people, and that is why I imagine and have actually a plan to build what I call an opportunity economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also made a point to attack Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax policy:\par \par \uc2 My opponent, on the other hand, his plan is to do what he has done before, which is to provide a tax cut for billionaires and big corporations, which will result in $5tn to America\u8217\'20\'19s deficit. My opponent has a plan that I call the Trump sales tax, which would be a 20% tax on everyday goods that you rely on to get through the month. Economists have said that that Trump sales tax would actually result for middle-class families in about $4,000 more a year because of his policies and his ideas about what should be the backs of middle-class people paying for tax cuts for billionaires.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris walks to Trump to shake hands as both take stage at presidential debate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have just taken the stage at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2  in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s their first time ever meeting, and they did shake hands after Harris approached Trump\u8217\'20\'19s podium. The debate has begun.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The candidates\u8217\'20\'19 top messengers are floating through the spin room to \u8220\'20\'1Cspin\u8221\'20\'1D us ahead of the debate.\par \par \uc2 So far, we\u8217\'20\'19ve heard Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  pre-emptively accuse the media of downplaying a good performance.\par \par \uc2 Asked about House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 report on the Afghanistan withdrawal, Senator Chris Murphy quipped that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t typically read \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican campaign documents\u8221\'20\'1D. The reporter didn\u8217\'20\'19t get the joke and tried again, clarifying that he meant the \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial\u8221\'20\'1D report. Murphy repeated the joke.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr, who recently bowed out of the race and endorsed Trump, barreled through the room, drawing a large audience as he spoke to a handful of conservative outlets.\par \par \uc2 California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , one of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 best messengers, held court, lacing into Trump and touting his fellow Californian. Surrogates from both Dakotas turned out for Trump: South Dakota governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  and theNorth Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I also dropped into a revealing gaggle with Florida Representative Byron Donalds, another Trump surrogate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a cigar guy. I\u8217\'20\'19m a tequila guy. You know, I work out when I can. I hit the weights. I like movies,\u8221\'20\'1D he told a reporter.\par \par \uc2 Another cut in to ask whether he\u8217\'20\'19d tried Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s new whiskey, SirDavis. (He has not but appeared genuinely excited to do so.)\par \par \uc2 enltrapropos of nothing, I walked in late to a spin room gaggle with Fl. Rep. Byron Donalds as he was being asked whether he's tried Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9's new whiskey. "She got a whiskey? I'm gonna have to sample some of that."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1833662686803923050?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the governor of California, told reporters in the debate spin room that he is confident about how Harris will perform on the biggest night of the election campaign so far.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not nervous about her debate skills,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I\u8217\'20\'19m \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I\u8217\'20\'19d be nervous. That said, he has more options because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t play by the same sets of rules and so he\u8217\'20\'19s a very challenging person to debate in that respect. If he feels he\u8217\'20\'19s losing, this will get very interesting and you will feel that very quickly. My sense is we\u8217\'20\'19re going to feel that right out of the gate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump will find it especially difficult to debate a woman, Newsom continued, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHe has a hard time with women generally. He sure as hell has a hard time with critique, criticism. He\u8217\'20\'19s the most easily manipulated human being I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met in my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom said he has met 30 world leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cand literally every conversation begins with, what the hell is going on in the United States of America? They\u8217\'20\'19re laughing behind his back. At the same time they said if he does come back, he\u8217\'20\'19s pretty easily manipulated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe can easily get under his skin by just asserting herself competently and prosecuting the case against the guy who\u8217\'20\'19s quite literally a convicted felon. He\u8217\'20\'19s a fraudster and he\u8217\'20\'19s boring, not just boorish. He\u8217\'20\'19s become boring and that is showing up more and more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked by the Guardian whether Harris should attempt to fact-check Harris during the debate, Newsom replied: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to fact-check a serial liar. There\u8217\'20\'19s no capacity to do that unless an AI bot is doing the debate. But there are some outlandish and outrageous things that we certainly need to push back.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do think that\u8217\'20\'19s the role of the moderator for those outlandish and absurd things but it\u8217\'20\'19s also the role of the candidate - both candidates. I expect with that ample opportunity \u8211\'20\'13 two minutes, a minute to respond and an opportunity for follow up \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19ll be a lot more give-and-take in that respect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 The rules of the Trump-Harris debate\par \par \uc2 Here are the rules of this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate, according to the host, ABC News:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The debate will be 90 minutes with two commercial breaks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The two seated moderators, David Muir and Linsey Davis, will be the only people asking questions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A coin flip was held virtually on Tuesday, 3 September, to determine podium placement and order of closing statements; former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the coin toss and chose to select the order of statements. The former president will offer the last closing statement, and Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  selected the right podium position on screen (stage left).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates will be introduced by the moderators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The candidates will enter upon introduction from opposite sides of the stage; the incumbent party will be introduced first.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There will be no opening statements; closing statements will be two minutes per candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates will stand behind podiums for the duration of the debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Props or pre-written notes are not allowed on stage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No topics or questions will be shared in advance with campaigns or candidates.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates will be given a pen, a pad of paper and a bottle of water.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates will be given two minutes to answer questions, two minutes for rebuttals, and one extra minute for follow-ups, clarifications or responses.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates\u8217\'20\'19 microphones will be live only for the candidate whose turn it is to speak and muted when the time belongs to another candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Candidates will not be permitted to ask questions of each other.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Campaign staff may not interact with candidates during commercial breaks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moderators will seek to enforce timing agreements and ensure a civilized discussion.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There will be no audience in the room.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what we can expect when Trump and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  take the stage in just a few minutes:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-watch-time-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What time is the Trump-Harris debate \u8211\'20\'13 and what are the rules? Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Gaza solidarity protesters have taken to the streets today near the venue where the two candidates are having their debate:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris arrives at debate venue\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s motorcade has arrived at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2  in Philadelphia, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll debate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in about 12 minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 So, too, did \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, who had several high-profile Democrats giving interviews at the debate:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign had a host of surrogates talking with reporters before the debate:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the Democratic governor of California, has urged \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to communicate a vision of hope and inclusion to millions of viewers watching tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s got to show the American people tonight that she\u8217\'20\'19s not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . She sure as hell is not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom told reporters in the debate spin room. \u8220\'20\'1CShe is a new generation of leader and that\u8217\'20\'19s her opportunity. She shows up on stage. You see that. You feel that. And now she\u8217\'20\'19s got to express it in a way that communicates a vision where people feel hope and included.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s got to talk to the extent that she is specifically talking to the people watching \u8211\'20\'13 they feel that she\u8217\'20\'19s talking about them. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in contrast \u8211\'20\'13 we know, you know \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19ll be talking about himself. That is a powerful, powerful contrast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom, who was seen as a potential replacement for Biden before the party consolidated around Harris, added: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s not the status quo. She\u8217\'20\'19s not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s her own person. She\u8217\'20\'19s always been her own person. Trust me, I\u8217\'20\'19ve known \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for 30 years. She is her own person. She has unique skill sets that are unique and distinctive from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Doug Emhoff, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s husband, is with \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, riling up supporters outside the debate venue.\par \par \uc2 enltrA great way to start debate day in Philly with my friend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GavinNewsom}}}\uc2  and this group of amazing supporters. They are fired up for tonight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V8YViL3Q55"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/V8YViL3Q55}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Doug Emhoff (@DouglasEmhoff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DouglasEmhoff/status/1833616082566775204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , who recently endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after abandoning his independent run for president, was in the debate spin room with the Trump campaign.\par \par \uc2 enltrRFK Jr. leaves the spin room after conducting a handful of interviews with conservative media outlets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vJcKCPzssn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vJcKCPzssn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1833657427880759533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has done the most prep sessions before the ABC presidential debate tonight of any of his prior seven debates, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The former president has been practicing primarily with his pal \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , a Republican representative, and \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic representative.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, ABC News released a photo of the debate stage where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are to meet:\par \par \uc2 One imagines they\u8217\'20\'19ll turn the lights up when the candidates are on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign seeks to undermine debate before it starts\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign is already playing the refs and suggesting that, if the moderators fail to sufficiently challenge \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on her record, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can throw the whole debate out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the governor of North Dakota and a Trump surrogate, told reporters in the debate spin room that ABC News\u8217\'20\'19s moderators have \u8220\'20\'1Ca responsibility to the American people, and part of their responsibility is to actually ask Vice-President Harris real questions and tough questions. This is historic. She\u8217\'20\'19s a historic candidate but for a different reason.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s historic because she\u8217\'20\'19s 55 days away from the election and she\u8217\'20\'19s done one short interview and has never done a debate and this may be the only one. I think America is going to be outraged if we find out a few hours from tonight that she got through a debate and nobody asked her tough questions about her past positions and why her anonymous aides are saying no, she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe in all this anymore on issues that are critical, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s energy policy, the border, whether fentanyl should be legal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burgum, who was on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shortlist for running mate until senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  got the nod, added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just about plastic straws that she supported. She needs to be asked tough questions tonight, and that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the things that I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be looking for. If the moderators don\u8217\'20\'19t come through, then you can throw the whole debate out because it was a three-on-one tilted playing field from the start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Burgum called for close scrutiny of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s past record, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a dangerously progressive liberal from California, and people should understand that when they\u8217\'20\'19re voting. Is that a direction she wants to take the country? Because the last time I checked, California\u8217\'20\'19s losing population. One of the states where people are leaving, voting with their feet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump seen arriving in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrived in Philadelphia earlier today for his debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Photographers captured him and his entourage deplaning:\par \par \uc2 The debate takes place at Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s National Constitution Center. Here are some scenes from the area:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign will be fact-checking the debate in real time, on X.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is going to lie tonight. A lot.\par \par \uc2 So we are going to fact check him in real time.\par \par \uc2 Follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHQ}}}\uc2  and tap the bell icon to help amplify the truth.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1833647043430039784?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 ABC, meanwhile, has said that the debate moderators will facilitate the debate but not fact-check. Rick Klein, ABC News\u8217\'20\'19 political director, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not making a commitment to fact-check everything, or fact-check nothing, in either direction. We\u8217\'20\'19re there to keep a conversation going, and to facilitate a good solid debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For truly unbiased fact-checking of both candidates, follow along here on the Guardian US liveblog!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters in Philadelphia, \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , the Republican senator from Florida, said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been \u8220\'20\'1Cvery clear\u8221\'20\'1D about his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the former president sought to moderate on an issue he fears will hurt Republicans in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Trump recently suggested he would support a Florida ballot initiative enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, only to say the following day, amid blowback from conservative Christians, that he would vote against it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court made a decision. It\u8217\'20\'19s a state issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott told reporters in the spin room, summarizing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s view on the matter. He said Trump would have an opportunity to turn the issue on Democrats, whom he falsely claimed support laws allowing people to get abortions after the baby is born. This is untrue: infanticide is criminalized in all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 During the debate, Scott predicted that Trump would seek to tie \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s record, and expected her to face sharp criticism from the former president over the administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 He also sought to set expectations, pre-emptively accusing the press of not giving the president a fair shake.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, first off, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to have a big win tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow the question will be, will the mainstream media say he\u8217\'20\'19s had a big win?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz campaign will be putting on a drone show over the \uc2 Philadelphia Museum of Art\uc2  prior to the debate.\par \par \uc2 Per the campaign, \u8220\'20\'1Cthis drone show will serve as a perfect opener as eyes turn to the debate stage, where Vice President Harris will make her case for her popular New Way Forward agenda\u8221\'20\'1D. The show \u8220\'20\'1Cwill echo some of the popular messaging this campaign and grassroots supporters have latched onto\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a campaign statement. It is unclear how the drones will be spelling out or interpreting Harris\u8217\'20\'19s newly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/kamala-harris-policy-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  policy platform, but do watch the skies over Philly and let us know!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump official warns over ex-president's threats to jail opponents\par \par \uc2 Now from \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2 , a former homeland security and counter-terrorism adviser to \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the vice-president under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Troye is holding a press conference as a surrogate of the Harris campaign before the debate, and was asked whether she fears retribution from the former president because of her staunch opposition to him.\par \par \uc2 Troye highlighted a social media post by Trump on Saturday threatening to jail \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D election officials if he wins. The former president wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThose involved in unscrupulous behavior will be sought out, caught, and prosecuted at levels, unfortunately, never seen before in our Country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Troye told reporters in Philadelphia: \u8220\'20\'1CJust this weekend, he threatened to throw election workers in jail. Actually wanted law enforcement to go after them. Think about that. Take a step back and think about what that means for our elections right now, when you have a former president of the United States who seeks the Oval Office again and he\u8217\'20\'19s advocating attacks on our election officials.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, they\u8217\'20\'19ve already suffered from threats \u8211\'20\'13 we saw that in Georgia especially. Even some of the threats to Governor Kemp who just simply held the line and told the truth and stood by the 2020 election, which was a free and fair election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you have someone that\u8217\'20\'19s speaking in that way, I think, yes, he has said there\u8217\'20\'19ll be retribution. I have no doubt there\u8217\'20\'19ll be retribution against myself and others who don\u8217\'20\'19t fall in line with exactly his type of cult.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Young voter groups have criticized the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s gun store debate watch party, calling Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D and the former president \u8220\'20\'1Cout of touch\u8221\'20\'1D for hosting the event so close to a mass school shooting site.\par \par \uc2 The groups, which include Voters of Tomorrow, College Democrats of America, Leaders We Deserve, College Democrats of Georgia, Georgia High School Democrats, Young Democrats of Georgia, Path to Progress and Blue Future issued a joint statement condemning the committee\u8217\'20\'19s decision:\par \par \uc2 Just days after students and teachers were murdered in Apalachee High School, Republicans are hosting a debate watch party an hour away at the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest gun store. The Trump team is evil for disrespecting the victims like this \u8211\'20\'13 and by continually refusing to support life-saving gun violence prevention policies.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is out-of-touch with the vast majority of Americans on gun violence prevention. He continues to suck up to the gun lobby and insult victims, as shown by today\u8217\'20\'19s event. As young organizers in Georgia and across the country, and members of a generation that has been defined by mass shootings, we know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s flagrant disregard for young Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives will cost him this election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://app.trumpforce47.com/event/trump-force-47-debate-watch-party-3887"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has scheduled}}}\uc2  a watch party for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate at a gun store in Georgia just miles away from Apalachee high school, where two teachers and two students were killed by a 14-year-old shooter last week.\par \par \uc2 Gun-control advocacy group Moms Demand Action condemned the event on X:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhile Georgians continue to mourn the students and educators who were shot and killed at Apalachee High School last week, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  is hosting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Debate2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Debate2024}}}\uc2  watch party at the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest gun store tonight\u8212\'20\'14less than 50 miles from Apalachee High School.\par \par \uc2 INSENSITIVE. GROSS.\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KCna31bLQl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KCna31bLQl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Moms Demand Action (@MomsDemand) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MomsDemand/status/1833560496546713951?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Adventure Outdoors, which proudly proclaims itself as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Greatest Store on Earth\u8221\'20\'1D, carries more than 15,000 guns and has a 17-lane shooting range. The store has hosted debate watch parties before, including last June when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  debated \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The event, which includes dinner and refreshments, is sponsored by a slew of conservative groups, including Tea Party Patriots Action, the Fulton county Republican party and Pac Turning Point Action.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump, Harris may be tied in presidential race\par \par \uc2 Earlier, we described this race as \u8220\'20\'1Cneck and neck\u8221\'20\'1D. We mean that literally \u8211\'20\'13 our polling average shows the two candidates tied nationally, at 47.3% support each.\par \par \uc2 Of course, America\u8217\'20\'19s use of the electoral college means that seven swing states \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona, Nevada, Georgia, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 are expected to decide this election.\par \par \uc2 For an idea of how Trump and Harris are faring in each, check out our poll tracker:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 How to watch the Harris-Trump debate\par \par \uc2 Whether you\u8217\'20\'19re in the United States or abroad, we have a handy guide that\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you how to tune in to this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and that covers its ground rules.\par \par \uc2 Read it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-debate-watch-time-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What time is the Trump-Harris debate \u8211\'20\'13 and what are the rules? All you need to know}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump to debate as polls show dead heat in presidential race\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as we cover tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which we expect to be a milestone in what has already been a historically tumultuous presidential race. The two contenders will square off for 90 minutes at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2  in Philadelphia, with ABC News hosting and their anchors David Muir and Linsey Davis moderating. The Democratic and Republican candidates are meeting as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls indicate}}}\uc2  a neck-and-neck race between them, particularly in the seven swing states expected to decide the winner.\par \par \uc2 This will be the first debate between Harris and Trump. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Trump faced off in June, but the president put in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such a poor showing}}}\uc2  that it sparked a plunge in his poll numbers and a Democratic pressure campaign that contributed to his decision to end his bid for a second term. Though Harris has been vice-president since 2021, she has done only one formal interview since launching her presidential campaign, and polls have indicated that voters are looking to find out more about her plans, if elected. This debate could present her with the opportunity to do that \u8211\'20\'13 while, for Trump, he\u8217\'20\'19ll be given the chance to make the case for his return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching out for:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will either candidate deliver a knockout blow to the other? Biden certainly received one when he encountered Trump just over two months ago, though he was far from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/famous-us-presidential-debate-moments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the only candidate}}}\uc2  to emerge from a debate with their campaign hanging by a thread.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will Trump say something insensitive about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity? Just days after she launched her campaign, the former president claimed that the vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/kamala-harris-texas-rally-donald-trump-racial-identity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was not really Black}}}\uc2 , sparking outrage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will Harris say about her policies? She inherited a campaign from Biden, but has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/kamala-harris-policy-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowly deviated}}}\uc2  from some of his proposals. Look out for anything she has to say about US support for Israel, and her previous stances on immigration \u8211\'20\'13 a subject Trump is sure to bring up.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240910ek9a003pg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
