\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US election live: former Trump officials to join Harris campaign at debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Anna Betts (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 4,180 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2024\par 17:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Anthony Scaramucci\uc2  and \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2  will speak out against their former boss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ahead of the debate, Harris campaign saysHarris and Trump make final preparations for crucial debate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  posted a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1833495327040803288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1833495327040803288%7Ctwgr%5E255557e821587104e9cc78a10fd21007711bfc95%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fd-2486477438338553807.ampproject.net%2F2406131415000%2Fframe.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video on X }}}\uc2  on Tuesday, urging his followers not to vote for his name on the ballot, but to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This comes one day after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/rfk-jr-michigan-ballot-lawsuit-4aa84852759b5f3fe9ac7e5790af54d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan supreme court ruled that}}}\uc2  that Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s name will remain on the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot despite his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrawal from the race}}}\uc2  several weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter what state you live in, you should be voting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said in the video. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the only way we can get me and everything I stand for into Washington DC and fulfil the mission that motivated my campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBottom line: No matter what state you live in, VOTE TRUMP. A Trump victory is a Kennedy victory. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GBn2p2RLnX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GBn2p2RLnX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr\uc2  (@RobertKennedyJr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1833495327040803288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 ex-director accuses Trump campaign advisers of \u8216\'20\'18malpractice\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The former head o f Project 2025, a rightwing blueprint for remaking the \uc2 US government\uc2  that was created by many of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former officials, has urged the former president to replace his two campaign managers if he wants to win November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Paul Dans, who stepped down as the project\u8217\'20\'19s director in July after Trump dissociated himself from it, turned his fire on Susie Wiles and Chris LaCivita, blaming the advisers for a series of errors that he claims have jeopardised the Republican nominee\u8217\'20\'19s chances of beating \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/09/us/politics/project-2025-trump-dans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused them}}}\uc2  of being guilty of overconfidence and of failing to adequately prepare Trump for the possibility that Harris would replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the Democratic nominee. That development changed the race, which polls suggested Trump had previously been leading. Dans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/09/us/politics/project-2025-trump-dans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Trump should be running like Secretariat at the Belmont, but instead it\u8217\'20\'19s a race to the wire.\par \par \uc2 He also accused Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign advisers of \u8220\'20\'1Cmalpractice\u8221\'20\'1D, and said their misjudgments led to an embarrassing public about-face, in which Trump finally claimed to disown the Project 2025 document.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/paul-dans-project-2025-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 ex-director accuses Trump campaign advisers of \u8216\'20\'18malpractice\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two former Trump White House officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e04f068f089d7307cf7e63#block-66e04f068f089d7307cf7e63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will join}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign as surrogates for Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate. \uc2 Anthony Scaramucci\uc2 , a former White House communications director for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2 , who was homeland security adviser to \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , will speak out against Trump and for Harris ahead of the debate, the campaign said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House described {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 false claims}}}\uc2  being shared by prominent Republicans including the Trump campaign and JD Vance about Haitian migrants in an Ohio city eating pets and local wildlife as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e070728f08960bb04d2013#block-66e070728f08960bb04d2013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  misinformation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A new Harris-Walz campaign ad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e05ca48f08766de018b282#block-66e05ca48f08766de018b282"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  features}}}\uc2 Barack Obama mocking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his \u8220\'20\'1Cweird obsession\u8221\'20\'1D with crowd sizes during his speech at the Democratic national convention last month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump, the former first lady, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e06b0d8f08766de018b343#block-66e06b0d8f08766de018b343"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned }}}\uc2  the official account of the attempted assassination of her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in a bizarre new video posted to X to promote her new memoir.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the hard-right Republican governor of Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e061368f089d7307cf7f88#block-66e061368f089d7307cf7f88"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  the signature collection process for the state\u8217\'20\'19s amendment on November\u8217\'20\'19s ballot to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was fraudulent, and is reportedly sending his election police force to voters\u8217\'20\'19 homes to try to gather evidence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e070728f08960bb04d2013#block-66e070728f08960bb04d2013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  misinformation about migrants in Springfield, Ohio}}}\uc2 , comes as the Trump campaign has sought to make immigration a key issue, tying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the towns unprepared for migrants arriving via the southern border.\par \par \uc2 The city has seen a large number of migrants from Haiti, which has both helped the economy there with staffing concerns while also stretching the capacity of some services like clinics and schools, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/03/us/springfield-ohio-school-bus-crash-haiti-immigrants.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Biden administration policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/investigations/biden-admin-gives-protected-status-309000-haitians-rcna159438?utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=240909-kamala_migrants_ravage_ohio_city_and_its_coming_to_your_city_next&utm_content=ncl-rugWmD7K9C&_nlid=rugWmD7K9C&_nhids=rXWVHwR8gA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided}}}\uc2  temporary protected status to hundreds of thousands of Haitian migrants, who have left their home country because of ongoing violence. Some estimates say as many as 20,000 people from Haiti have come to the city, the Times said.\par \par \uc2 Last year, a migrant driving a van outside Springfield crashed into a school bus, killing one child, which added fuel to the concerns some residents have had with migration. Housing costs have also increased, which has led to fewer options for low-income residents of all backgrounds, the paper reported.\par \par \uc2 Springfield\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Rob Rue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/ohio-city-plunged-housing-crisis-15000-migrants-arrive-setting-us-up-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on Fox}}}\uc2  to say the Biden administration was to blame for \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing cities like ours and taxing us beyond our limit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Residents at recent council meetings have appealed to their elected officials to better manage the new stream of residents. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-13828455/Woman-forced-home-45-years-Haitian-Immigrants-Springfield-Ohio-squatters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now viral testimony}}}\uc2 , one woman said she and her husband might need to move from their home because of ongoing problems with \u8220\'20\'1Cmen that cannot speak English in my front yard screaming at me\u8221\'20\'1D and throwing items in her yard.\par \par \uc2 Some have also tried to tie a woman who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2024/08/22/ohio-woman-ate-cat/74902749007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged recently}}}\uc2  in Canton, Ohio, for allegedly killing and then eating a cat to the influx of migrants in Springfield, a different city more than 150 miles (241km) away. She does not appear to be a Haitian migrant.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance appeared to backtrack on the false claim he promoted on Monday saying that Haitian migrants in an Ohio city were eating pets and local wildlife.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Ohio senator and vice-presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance/status/1833505359513661762"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  his office had received \u8220\'20\'1Cmany inquiries\u8221\'20\'1D about the false claims, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s possible, of course, that all of these rumors will turn out to be false.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Police in Springfield, Ohio on Monday said they had received no credible reports of immigrants harming pets.\par \par \uc2 The false claims appear to have originated from a commenter at a local city meeting, who said migrants were grabbing ducks from the park to kill and eat, and from local crime-watch \uc2 Facebook\uc2  groups. They were then shared on other social media platforms and made it into a headline in the Daily Mail.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans spread baseless slurs about \u8216\'20\'18cat-eating migrants\u8217\'20\'19 in Ohio city}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says JD Vance false conspiracy about Haitian \u8216\'20\'18cat-eating migrants\u8217\'20\'19 is racist and 'dangerous'\par \par \uc2 The White House described {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/republicans-haitian-migrants-pets-wildlife-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  false claims being shared}}}\uc2  by prominent Republicans including the Trump campaign and JD Vance about Haitian migrants in an Ohio city eating pets and local wildlife as \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D misinformation.\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s national security adviser John Kirby told reporters on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 This kind of misinformation is dangerous. Because there will be people that believe it, no matter how ludicrous and stupid it is. And they might act on that kind of misinformation and act on it in a way where somebody can get hurt so it needs to stop.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s deeply concerning to us is you\u8217\'20\'19ve got now elected officials in the Republican Party pushing yet another conspiracy theory that\u8217\'20\'19s just seeking to divide people based on lies and \u8211\'20\'13 let\u8217\'20\'19s be honest \u8211\'20\'13 based on an element of racism.\par \par \uc2 Social media posts have claimed, without evidence, that migrants from Haiti to Springfield, Ohio, are stealing pets and local wildlife such as ducks and geese and are butchering them for food.\par \par \uc2 Many of the posts, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1833154509222129884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one shared by the X account}}}\uc2  for the Republicans on the House judiciary committee, use images generated by artificial intelligence to show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  holding and protecting cats and ducks, casting him as a savior to the town.\par \par \uc2 enltrProtect our ducks and kittens in Ohio! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YnTZStPnsg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YnTZStPnsg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Judiciary GOP ???????????? (@JudiciaryGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1833154509222129884?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Ted Cruz\uc2 , the Republican senator from Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/tedcruz/status/1833174142591365185"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared a meme}}}\uc2  of two cats hugging one another that said, \u8220\'20\'1CPlease vote for Trump so Haitian immigrants don\u8217\'20\'19t eat us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 qmeltr?????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/96vvZhvuSv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/96vvZhvuSv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ted Cruz\uc2  (@tedcruz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tedcruz/status/1833174142591365185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sexual abuse accuser Jessica Leeds says she ruefully \u8220\'20\'1Claughed out loud\u8221\'20\'1D when the former president recently disputed her sworn testimony that he grabbed her, tried to kiss her and ran his hand up her skirt on a plane in the 1970s by insisting \u8220\'20\'1Cshe would not have been the chosen one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe assaulted me 50 years ago and continues to attack me today,\u8221\'20\'1D Leeds said alongside her attorneys during a press conference in New York on Monday.\par \par \uc2 It was like he had 47 arms \u8211\'20\'13 like an octopus, but not a sound was spoken.\par \par \uc2 Her remarks came after Trump appeared at an appeal hearing on the sexual abuse case brought by E Jean Carroll, which resulted in a jury finding Trump liable of sexually abusing and defaming Carroll.\par \par \uc2 Leeds, 82, came forward in 2016 and later testified in the Carroll trial, which centered on Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s testimony that the Republican nominee in November\u8217\'20\'19s election had assaulted her at a department store in the 1990s.\par \par \uc2 Leeds has accused Trump of groping her in the first-class section of an airplane. She said she fought him off and moved to the back of the plane. At her press conference, she said she later ran into him, prompting him to exclaim, \u8220\'20\'1CI remember you,\u8221\'20\'1D before calling her a derogatory word.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/donald-trump-accuser-jessica-leeds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Like an octopus\u8217\'20\'19: Trump accuser rebuts ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s denial that he groped her}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump claims there is 'definitely more' to assassination attempt against husband\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump, the former first lady, questioned the official account of the attempted assassination of her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in a bizarre new video posted to X to promote her new memoir.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe attempt to end my husband\u8217\'20\'19s life was a horrible, distressing experience,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Now, the silence around it feels heavy. I can\u8217\'20\'19t help but wonder: Why didn\u8217\'20\'19t law enforcement officials arrest the shooter before the speech?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is definitely more to this story, and we need to uncover the truth, she added.\par \par \uc2 The video ends with an image of her new book, \u8220\'20\'1CMelania\u8221\'20\'1D, due to be released on 8 October.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZCTwZSqZND"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZCTwZSqZND}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KKA6anTEYC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KKA6anTEYC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MELANIA TRUMP (@MELANIATRUMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MELANIATRUMP/status/1833476085998063741?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The dispatching of election police to voters\u8217\'20\'19 homes is not the only beef \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  critics have with the Republican Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to upend the amendment 4 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measure.\par \par \uc2 The official \uc2 Florida health department\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s website is urging voters to reject it, an unlawful use of taxpayers\u8217\'20\'19 money for what amounts to political advertising, according to the ACLU of Florida.\par \par \uc2 Bacardi Jackson, executive director of the ACLU of Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclufl.org/en/press-releases/aclu-florida-denounces-state-agencys-unprecedented-move-undermine-citizen-initiated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 To our knowledge, it is unprecedented for the state to expressly advocate against a citizen-led initiative.\par \par \uc2 enltrDystopian behavior by GOP politicians who are so desperate to keep Florida\u8217\'20\'19s near total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place that they will spend YOUR public money on political ads while come to your door with police to intimidate you on your petition signature. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7ghWdii2qR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7ghWdii2qR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Anna V. Eskamani, PhD ?? (@AnnaForFlorida) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnaForFlorida/status/1833176658162933884?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 This kind of propaganda, using taxpayer money and operating outside of the political process, sets a dangerous precedent. This is what we would expect to see from an authoritarian regime.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s illegal act to undermine amendment 4 is nothing more than an abuse of power, aimed at preventing voters from rejecting the cruel and extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has railed against amendment 4, which would nix the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he signed into law}}}\uc2  in April last year, and allow abortions until viability of the fetus.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a new squabble in Florida over an amendment on November\u8217\'20\'19s ballot to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Having failed to persuade the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court from blocking the measure going before voters in the first place, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s hard-right Republican governor, now claims the signature collection process for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridiansprotectingfreedom.com/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amendment 4}}}\uc2  was fraudulent, and is reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/elections/2024/09/06/florida-abortion-amendment-petition-signature-fraud-voters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending his election police force to voters\u8217\'20\'19 homes}}}\uc2  to try to gather evidence.\par \par \uc2 The Tampa Bay Times spoke to voters who said uniformed officers from the Florida department of law enforcement showed up at their door. One told the newspaper that the officer had a 10-page dossier on him, including a printout of his driver\u8217\'20\'19s license and a copy of his signature.\par \par \uc2 After the voter confirmed he had indeed signed the petition, the officer left.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis set up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/25/ron-desantis-florida-governor-bill-police-voter-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own election fraud unit}}}\uc2  in 2022 and has been busy scouring thousands of the almost one million signatures that put the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure on the ballot for authenticity.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are calling foul. State representative \uc2 Anna Eskamani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sun-sentinel.com/2024/09/09/desantis-claims-state-is-finding-fraud-in-amendment-4-petitions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Orlando Sentinel}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 These tactics set a very dangerous precedent for the future of our elections where [an] election police force can be sent in to intimidate, to try to re-evaluate history and to take away our votes and to take away our voices.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference Monday, DeSantis defended his tactics. His investigators, he said, found signatures that \u8220\'20\'1Cappeared\u8221\'20\'1D not to be authentic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt may be\u8230\'20\'26 that voter will say, \u8216\'20\'18No, I actually did do that,\u8217\'20\'19 maybe they signed their name. That is absolutely possible,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis conceded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked to explain her shifts on certain policy issues over the years {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during a CNN interview}}}\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 Pressed on her reversals on fracking and decriminalizing illegal border crossings, Harris insisted that her \u8220\'20\'1Cvalues had not changed\u8221\'20\'1D. She said:\par \par \uc2 I think the most important and most significant aspect of my policy perspective and decisions is my values have not changed.\par \par \uc2 On fracking, she said she made clear in the 2020 debate that she no longer supports a ban, and that as president she would not ban fracking.\par \par \uc2 On immigration, Harris said she thought laws on illegal border crossing should be followed and enforced on immigration. She pointed to her record as California attorney general, when she prosecuted gangs accused of cross border trafficking, as an indication of her values on immigration.\par \par \uc2 My values have not changed. So that is the reality of it. And four years of being vice president, I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you, one of the aspects, to your point, is traveling the country extensively. I believe it is important to build consensus, and it is important to find a common place of understanding of where we can actually solve problems.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he is feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate and that his biggest challenge facing off against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is that she has changed her positions on so many issues over the years.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/donald-trump-biggest-challenge-debating-kamala-harris-rcna170388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  NBC News this morning:\par \par \uc2 You don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to expect. She\u8217\'20\'19s changed all of her policies over the years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt makes it much easier. She\u8217\'20\'19s no longer believable,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s debate preparations have been far less extensive and structured than Harris\u8217\'20\'19s, but he participated in intensive sessions over the past two days, the outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 Sources told NBC that Trump has been nervous or disengaged with debate preparation in the past few weeks, but that he has been more focused as debate day neared.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama mocks Trump's 'weird obsession' with 'crowd sizes' in new Harris campaign ad\par \par \uc2 A new Harris-Walz campaign ad features Barack Obama mocking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his \u8220\'20\'1Cweird obsession\u8221\'20\'1D with crowd sizes during his speech at the Democratic national convention last month.\par \par \uc2 The ad, titled Crowd Size, features footage from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks the convention in Milwaukee where he decries Trump for \u8220\'20\'1Cwhining about his problems\u8221\'20\'1D such as his \u8220\'20\'1Cweird obsession with crowd sizes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis weird obsession with crowd sizes... it just goes on, and on, and on,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama says, making a suggestive hand gesture that drew laughter from the audience.\par \par \uc2 The ad launched this morning and will air nationally and in markets that appear intentionally targeted at Trump, including on Fox News and in West Palm Beach, Florida, as well as Philadelphia, where tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate is taking place.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will arrive in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, on Tuesday for their first (and potentially only) presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 The event will mark the first time that Harris and Trump have ever met face to face, and it comes less than two months after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  withdrew from the presidential race following his own fateful debate performance in June.\par \par \uc2 The change at the top of the Democratic ticket appears to have unnerved Trump and his campaign advisers, who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/09/trump-harris-election-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled to land attacks}}}\uc2  against Harris. The debate will present Trump with his most significant opportunity yet to negatively define Harris in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds, as polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  a neck-and-neck race in key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 For Harris, the debate could allow her to deliver on her oft-repeated promise to voters: that she will prosecute the case against Trump. Her political history \u8211\'20\'13 both on the debate stage and in Senate hearings \u8211\'20\'13 suggest she is well-positioned to make that case. But Harris is not without her vulnerabilities either.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are five key moments from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s career that could offer a preview of her debate strategy.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How will Harris debate Trump? Six key moments offer insight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign noted that the two former Trump White House officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/10/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest?page=with:block-66e04f068f089d7307cf7e63#block-66e04f068f089d7307cf7e63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  joining them as surrogates tonight,}}}\uc2 Anthony Scaramucci\uc2  and \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2 , are not the only former Trump aids and officials speaking out against him.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign also released a new TV ad, titled The Best People, to coincide with tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate featuring former top officials in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration, including his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , secretary of defense, \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2 , national security adviser, \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , and chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, \uc2 Gen Mark Milley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2016 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would choose only the best people to work in his White House,\u8221\'20\'1D a narrator in the ad says.\par \par \uc2 Now those people have a warning for America: Trump is not fit to be president again.\par \par \uc2 enltrTake it from the people who worked for him: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a danger to our troops, our security, and our democracy.\par \par \uc2 He should never again stand behind the seal of the President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Watch our new ad: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LWiyK1sfnm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LWiyK1sfnm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1833112474893082878?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump officials to join Harris campaign at debate\par \par \uc2 Two former Trump White House officials will join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign in Philadelphia as surrogates for Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate, the Harris campaign announced.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Scaramucci\uc2 , who served as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House communications director, and \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2 , who was homeland security adviser to \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and a top aide on the Trump White House\u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus task force, will speak out against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and for Harris ahead of the debate, the campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Announcing the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s plans to bring Scaramucci and Troye to the debate, the Harris-Walz campaign\u8217\'20\'19s communications director Michael Tyler said:\par \par \uc2 Listen, don\u8217\'20\'19t take it from us: Take it from the ones who know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the best and who are telling the American people exactly how unfit Trump is to serve as president. They saw firsthand the abject failure of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White Stripes \u8217\'20\'19 Jack White and Meg White have filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for what they allege is the \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrant misappropriation\u8221\'20\'1D of a recording of their hit song Seven Nation Army in a campaign video.\par \par \uc2 The video that spurred the legal action was posted by Trump staffer Margo McAtee Martin on X on 29 August, but has since been deleted. It shows the Republican presidential nominee boarding a plane with the opening riff of Seven Nation Army playing in the background.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/reel/C_Q6is_SO4z/?igsh=ZG04MmNwZjVsaXE2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Responding via Instagram}}}\uc2  at the time, Jack White wrote:\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t even think about using my music you fascists. Law suit coming from my lawyers about this (to add to your 5 thousand others).\par \par \uc2 The singer has made good on the threat, filing a copyright infringement suit, alongside Meg White, as the White Stripes, seeking \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant monetary damages\u8221\'20\'1D, and listing Trump, his campaign and Martin as defendants.\par \par \uc2 The suit alleges that the campaign did not seek or obtain permission from the band to use the song, and did not respond to pre-litigation efforts to resolve the issue.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/09/white-stripes-trump-lawsuit-seven-nation-army"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White Stripes sue Trump over \u8216\'20\'18flagrant misappropriation\u8217\'20\'19 of hit song}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will rally supporters in critical battleground states following tonight\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign will kick off a \u8220\'20\'1CNew Way Forward\u8221\'20\'1D tour involving a four-day campaign trip through major swing states, a new television spot, rallies, canvassing events and programs designed to target important voting groups, it said.\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to attend 9/11 memorial ceremonies on Wednesday, and will embark on her tour on Thursday. Harris will visit North Carolina on Thursday and Pennsylvania on Friday. Walz will be in Nevada on Tuesday, Michigan on Thursday and Wisconsin on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris v Trump: How to watch tonight's debate\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  meet tonight for their only scheduled debate, here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know:\par \par \uc2 What time is the debate?\par \par \uc2 The debate will start at 9pm Eastern Time (1am GMT) and is expected to last 90 minutes with two commercial breaks.\par \par \uc2 Where is the debate?\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate will take place at the \uc2 National Constitution Center\uc2  in Philadelphia, a key election battleground state. As with the previous debate between Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , there will be no audience present.\par \par \uc2 World News Tonight anchor David Muir and ABC News Live Prime anchor Linsey Davis will moderate the debate.\par \par \uc2 How can I watch the debate?\par \par \uc2 ABC News will carry the debate live on its broadcast network as well as its streaming platform ABC News Live, \uc2 Disney\uc2 + and \uc2 Hulu\uc2 . Several networks have also agreed to carry the event live.\par \par \uc2 When is the next debate?\par \par \uc2 As of now, there is only one debate scheduled before the election. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance are due to face off at a vice-presidential debate on 1 October in New York City.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump to face off in presidential debate\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics }}}\uc2  readers. It was the debate that was never meant to happen. Tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet for the first time ever when they take the stage at Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s national constitution center for the presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 With just eight weeks until election day and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/latest-poll-kamala-harris-donald-trump-2024-us-election-presidential-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent polls showing the candidates neck-and-neck}}}\uc2 , the stakes couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be higher for both Harris and Trump. Today\u8217\'20\'19s debate, which will start at 9pm ET and is expected to last 90 minutes, may well be the only chance the American public have to see their Democratic and Republican presidential candidates face off against each other on what voters say are their key issues, including the economy, immigration and reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 We will be covering the debate tonight on our live blog. In the meantime, here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz campaign unveiled a new ad for debate day, entitled \u8220\'20\'1CCrowd Size\u8221\'20\'1D, that features Barack Obama ridiculing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insecurities about his crowd size.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Paul Dans, the former director of Project 2025, sharply criticized the Trump campaign, revealing discontent on the right about what some see as a pivot to the center.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voters in Delaware, New Hampshire and Rhode Island will cast their ballots in a slate of primary races today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , the former New York governor, appears before the House select subcommittee on the coronavirus pandemic this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , the secretary of state, is in the UK for a US-UK strategic dialogue and will meet with the UK prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240910ek9a0020j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
