\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris warns Trump will \u8216\'20\'18speak a lot of untruths\u8217\'20\'19 during TV debate \u8211\'20\'13 US elections live updates\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 4,180 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2024\par 16:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president says Republican nominee likely to launch personal attacks; 10 former top military officials who call Trump a \u8216\'20\'18danger to national security\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Six key moments that could offer insight into Harris's debate strategy against Trump\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will arrive in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, on Tuesday for their first (and potentially only) presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 The event will mark the first time that Harris and Trump have ever met face to face, and it comes less than two months after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  withdrew from the presidential race following his own fateful debate performance in June.\par \par \uc2 The change at the top of the Democratic ticket appears to have unnerved Trump and his campaign advisers, who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/09/trump-harris-election-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled to land attacks}}}\uc2  against Harris. The debate will present Trump with his most significant opportunity yet to negatively define Harris in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds, as polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  a neck-and-neck race in key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 For Harris, the debate could allow her to deliver on her oft-repeated promise to voters: that she will prosecute the case against Trump. Her political history \u8211\'20\'13 both on the debate stage and in Senate hearings \u8211\'20\'13 suggest she is well-positioned to make that case. But Harris is not without her vulnerabilities either.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are five key moments from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s career that could offer a preview of her debate strategy.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/harris-trump-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How will Harris debate Trump? Six key moments offer insight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican officials are raising the alarm that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has invested far fewer resources for its voter turnout operation in battleground states than previous presidential election races, and attempts to bridge the gap with political action committees have come too late.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) once envisioned an extensive field operation for the 2024 election, including having about 90 staffers in the must-win state of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 But the Trump campaign scrapped those plans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/11/new-rnc-leadership-trump-loyals-purge-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when it took over the RNC in March}}}\uc2 , redirecting the focus on field operations to combating supposed voter fraud and pursuing a twin voter turnout strategy of relying on several political action committees and ardent Trump volunteers.\par \par \uc2 The result has been that the Trump campaign has put fewer resources into its ground game in battleground states, according to people familiar with the matter \u8211\'20\'13 and Republican officials have derisively said the Trump operation is more comparable in size to a midterm cycle than a presidential.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/trump-campaign-rnc-ground-game-pacs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s voter turnout operation in swing states is too small, GOP worries}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  an \u8220\'20\'1Cunrecoverable catastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D on Sunday and urged fellow Republicans to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Cheney said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/cheney-trump-unrecoverable-catastrophe-call-gop-vote-harris/story?id=113486970"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  on ABC News This Week, a show on the network that is hosting Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate between Trump and Harris:\par \par \uc2 We see it on a daily basis \u8211\'20\'13 somebody who was willing to use violence in order to attempt to seize power, to stay in power, someone who represents unrecoverable catastrophe, frankly, in my view, and we have to do everything possible to ensure that he\u8217\'20\'19s not re-elected.\par \par \uc2 enltrLiz Cheney: \u8220\'20\'1CWe now have a Republican Party that is embracing isolationism, that is embracing Putin, that we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen\u8230\'20\'26the Republican vice presidential nominee\u8230\'20\'26willing to be interviewed by \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 who is platforming pro-Nazis\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/spLieyoqHF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/spLieyoqHF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republicans against Trump (@RpsAgainstTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RpsAgainstTrump/status/1832991569915342869?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Cheney also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4868127-liz-cheney-donald-trump-kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reaffirmed}}}\uc2  her endorsement of Harris and urged other prominent Republicans who have stated they plan on writing in a third option rather than vote for Trump to cast their ballots for the Democrat instead.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether she was still a Republican, Cheney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ThisWeekABC/status/1832788335141540293"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  she was still a conservative. She said she hoped to \u8220\'20\'1Crebuild\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican party after the 5 November presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/liz-cheney-trump-catastrophe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney calls Trump a \u8216\'20\'18catastrophe\u8217\'20\'19 and urges Republicans to vote for Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marc Elias, a prominent Democratic election lawyer, responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/09/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66df1afa8f086598f6766007#block-66df1afa8f086598f6766007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threat to imprison anyone \u8220\'20\'1Cinvolved in unscrupulous behavior\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  this election by saying:\par \par \uc2 We won\u8217\'20\'19t let \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intimidate us. We won\u8217\'20\'19t let him suppress the vote. We won\u8217\'20\'19t let him subvert the election. We won\u8217\'20\'19t let him cheat. We will fight and we will WIN.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump is desperate because he is going to lose this election. Let me be clear:\par \par \uc2 We won't let \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intimidate us.\par \par \uc2 We won't let him suppress the vote.\par \par \uc2 We won't let him subvert the election.\par \par \uc2 We won't let him cheat.\par \par \uc2 We will fight and we will WIN.??????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xErsYG4mpw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xErsYG4mpw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marc E. Elias (@marceelias) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marceelias/status/1832575927827497273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump threatens to jail lawyers, election officials for \u8216\'20\'18unscrupulous behavior\u8217\'20\'19 if he wins\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  threatened in a Truth Social post over the weekend that he would jail those \u8220\'20\'1Cinvolved in unscrupulous behavior\u8221\'20\'1D during this year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 In an attempt to sow doubt about the integrity of November\u8217\'20\'19s election, Trump wrote:\par \par \uc2 WHEN I WIN, those people that CHEATED will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the Law, which will include long term prison sentences so that this Depravity of Justice does not happen again.\par \par \uc2 He indicated that lawyers, political operatives, donors, voters and election officials could all be targeted with prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Those involved in unscrupulous behavior will be sought out, caught, and prosecuted at levels, unfortunately, never seen before in our Country.\par \par \uc2 Trump later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1832589096029450360"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  the message to X.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is most concerned going into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=debate+harris+trump+the+guardian&oq=debate+harris+trump+the+guardian&gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUyBggAEEUYOTIQCAEQABiDARixAxjHAxiABDIQCAIQABiDARixAxjHAxiABDIHCAMQABiABDIHCAQQABiABDIKCAUQABjHAxiABDIGCAYQRRg8MgYIBxBFGDzSAQgzNjg4ajBqN6gCALACAA&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s mood, afraid that the mercurial Trump could engage in the kind of self-sabotage that turned off voters in the 2020 presidential election, according to people familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 The campaign\u8217\'20\'19s internal refrain is whether they get \u8220\'20\'1Chappy Trump\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cangry Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, the people said, as they count down the days to perhaps the final presidential debate this cycle.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s televised debate is widely seen as a crux moment in the rebooted 2024 campaign. Since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped out of the race after a campaign-killing debate performance crystalized fears over his age and mental acuity, Harris has turned the race on its head.\par \par \uc2 But Harris\u8217\'20\'19s upward trajectory appears to have crested and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers have been looking at the debate as their best chance to retake the momentum after weeks of being humped out of the news cycle. Their hope, the people said, is to get the Trump who was fast on his feet during the debate against Biden.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/trump-debate-campaign-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/trump-debate-campaign-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Advisers worry whether \u8216\'20\'18happy Trump\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18angry Trump\u8217\'20\'19 will show up to debate}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/trump-debate-campaign-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Advisers worry whether \u8216\'20\'18happy Trump\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18angry Trump\u8217\'20\'19 will show up to debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The leaders of two major left-leaning women\u8217\'20\'19s organizations said the issue of reproductive rights would offer the \u8220\'20\'1Cstarkest possible contrast\u8221\'20\'1D between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 On a Monday call with reporters, Fatima Goss Graves, president of the National Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center Action Fund and Jessica Mackler, president of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, argued that Harris was the party\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful messenger on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has the track record as a prosecutor, senator and vice-president to press the case on the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 The issue is likely to be raised in the debate on ABC News. They said viewers should expect Harris to challenge Trump on the \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse notion\u8221\'20\'1D that he would not move to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reproductive rights. Mackler said:\par \par \uc2 He continues to lie to voters and distract from his record.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed the three supreme court justices who were decisive in overturning Roe v Wade. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said he would not sign a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban but had previously entertained the idea of a 15-week ban.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s strongest issue, but there are signs Trump\u8217\'20\'19s waffling on his position has muddied the waters.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/09/08/us/politics/times-siena-poll-toplines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national poll of likely voters by The New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  found that nearly half of independent voters say they did not think the former president would sign into law a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe one who got us into this mess\u8221\'20\'1D, Mackler said, adding that Harris was the only candidate who will \u8220\'20\'1Cget us out of it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/democrats-republicans-abortion-rights-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats unite to center reproductive rights as Republicans flail on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , in an interview with Rickey Smiley that aired this morning, also discussed her vision for small business growth.\par \par \uc2 Harris said that if elected, she would aim to reach 25m new small business applications by the end of her first term by reducing government bureaucracy and simplifying the process for obtaining occupational licenses across state lines.\par \par \uc2 She also pledged to introduce a \u8220\'20\'1Cstandard deduction\u8221\'20\'1D for small businesses and support investments in rural areas through an \u8220\'20\'1Cexpansion fund\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrIf elected as the next President of the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  has several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/economicproposals?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #economicproposals}}}\uc2  she hopes to enact. Listen to what she told me last week about her plans to help the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/smallbusinesses?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #smallbusinesses}}}\uc2  and people in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/middleclass?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #middleclass}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RickeySmiley?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RickeySmiley}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/KamalaHarris?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #KamalaHarris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Interview?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Interview}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DORwMo5Ahb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DORwMo5Ahb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rickey Smiley (@RickeySmiley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RickeySmiley/status/1833130811421323371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Trump will 'speak a lot of untruths' during debate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably going to speak a lot of untruths\u8221\'20\'1D during their debate tomorrow night, and that her Republican opponent will likely revert to personal attacks, pointing to the \u8220\'20\'1Cplaybook\u8221\'20\'1D he used with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no floor for him in terms of how low he will go,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in an interview with Rickey Smiley that aired this morning.\par \par \uc2 We should be prepared for that. We should be prepared for the fact that he is not burdened by telling the truth. And we should be prepared for the fact that he is probably going to speak a lot of untruths.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to lie,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris added.\par \par \uc2 He has a playbook that he has used in the past, be it, you know, his attacks on President Obama or \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . So we should expect that some of that might come out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/09/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66df0b398f080b4351299997#block-66df0b398f080b4351299997"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the House foreign affairs committee released today castigating the Biden administration for the chaotic Afghanistan withdrawal mentions \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s name 251 times.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, a 115-page interim report issued by the committee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican chairman, Michael McCaul, on the committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation in 2022 name-checked Harris just twice.\par \par \uc2 Democrats seized on the contrast, accusing McCaul of inflating Harris\u8217\'20\'19s part in the incident simply because she had replaced Biden as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 Democrats accused the Republicans of trying to exploit the withdrawal for election purposes while overlooking the fact that the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , took the original {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/06/white-house-blames-trump-afghanistan-troop-withdrawal-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  to withdraw US troops from Afghanistan when he was president. \uc2 Gregory Meeks\uc2 , the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 ranking member on the committee wrote in a 59-page rebuttal to McCaul\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 Republicans now claim [Harris] was the architect of the US withdrawal though she is referenced only three times in 3,288 pages of the Committee\u8217\'20\'19s interview transcripts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 House clashes over Harris\u8217\'20\'19s role in 2021 Afghanistan troop withdrawal\par \par \uc2 Partisan divisions over the chaotic 2021 pullout of western forces from Afghanistan have burst into the open ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate in Philadelphia after a Republican-led congressional report attempted to implicate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the episode.\par \par \uc2 A 250-page report from the House of Representatives\u8217\'20\'19 foreign affairs committee castigated the Biden administration for failing to anticipate the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rapid takeover and neglecting to prepare for the orderly departure of non-combatant personnel.\par \par \uc2 The report, written by the committee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican chairman, Michael McCaul, zeroes in on the supposed role played by the vice-president, although no evidence has emerged that she was directly involved in the decisions leading to one of the most damaging foreign policy chapters of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency. The report states:\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was the last person in the room when President Biden made the decision to withdraw all US forces from Afghanistan; a fact she boasted about shortly after President Biden issued his go-to-zero order.\par \par \uc2 The report\u8217\'20\'19s front page carries a picture of Harris prominently displayed below that of Biden, and above an image of Jake Sullivan, the national security adviser, who played a more prominent role in the withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/kamala-harris-afghanistan-withdrawal-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House clashes over Harris\u8217\'20\'19s role in 2021 Afghanistan troop withdrawal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The statement of support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by a group of retired top military officials comes a day before the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, and the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , will host a congressional gold medal ceremony honoring the 13 service members killed in the chaotic 2021 Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his fellow Republicans have tried to blame Harris for the Afghanistan pullout, including in a report by House GOP lawmakers today.\par \par \uc2 The report claims that in the months before the Afghanistan withdrawal, Biden administration officials \u8220\'20\'1Cwatered down\u8221\'20\'1D warnings about crumbling security and failed to launch an emergency evacuation of Americans and Afghan allies until it was too late, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/investigations/biden-officials-warnings-crumbling-security-afghan-withdrawal-rcna170121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to NBC News.\par \par \uc2 The Texas representative Michael McCaul, chair of the House foreign affairs committee, said:\par \par \uc2 Our investigation reveals the Biden-Harris administration had the information and opportunity to take necessary steps to plan for the inevitable collapse of the Afghan government. At each step of the way, however, the administration picked optics over security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25106804-nsl4a-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  letter }}}\uc2  by National Security Leaders for America also sought to defend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attacks over the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic 2021 Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly fails to take responsibility for his own role in putting service members in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way\u8221\'20\'1D, the retired US military officials wrote.\par \par \uc2 Without involving the Afghan government, he and his administration negotiated a deal with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  that freed 5,000 \uc2 Taliban\uc2  fighters and allowed them to return to the battlefield.\par \par \uc2 The Republican former president then left \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cwith no plans to execute a withdrawal, and with little time to do so\u8221\'20\'1D, they said.\par \par \uc2 This chaotic approach severely hindered the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s ability to execute the most orderly withdrawal possible and put our service members and our allies at risk.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ten former top military officials endorse Harris, call Trump 'a danger to our national security'\par \par \uc2 Ten retired top US military officials have announced their endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in a letter warning that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Ca danger to our national security and democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25106804-nsl4a-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  by the bipartisan group National Security Leaders for America, first obtained by Axios, is signed by retired Adm Steve Abbot, who served as deputy homeland security adviser to \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , \uc2 Gen Lloyd W Newton\uc2  and Gen Larry R Ellis, who has never previously endorsed a political candidate.\par \par \uc2 Harris is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best \u8211\'20\'13 and only \u8211\'20\'13 presidential candidate in this race who is fit to serve as our commander-in-chief\u8221\'20\'1D, the letter says, adding that the Democratic vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Chas demonstrated her ability to take on the most difficult national security challenges in the Situation Room and on the international stage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not understand selfless service and sacrifice, and he should never be allowed to again serve as commander-in-chief of the greatest fighting force in the world\u8221\'20\'1D, the group writes.\par \par \uc2 The release of the letter coincides with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/09/trump-harris-presidential-debate-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66dee4e88f08a07a6f4ced08#block-66dee4e88f08a07a6f4ced08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 release of a new Harris campaign ad}}}\uc2  featuring former Trump officials warning of the threat a second Trump presidency could pose to the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will vote yes on Florida amendment to legalize marijuana\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has confirmed he will vote in support of a ballot measure in Florida that would legalize recreational marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe it is time to end needless arrests and incarcerations of adults for small amounts of marijuana for personal use,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113105431683796730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  posted}}}\uc2  to Truth Social on Sunday night.\par \par \uc2 As a Floridian, I will be voting YES on Amendment 3 this November.\par \par \uc2 He added that as president, he would support the passage of similar laws in other states \u8220\'20\'1Cthat work so well for their citizens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, as a resident Floridian, will be able to cast a vote on the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/19/florida-legalize-marijuana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amendment 3}}}\uc2  in November, which would allow adults over 21 to legally buy and use marijuana without a medical card.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support contrasts with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor and fellow Republican, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/ron-desantis-freedom-fund-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vocal opponent }}}\uc2  of the ballot measure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential nominee, has postponed a rally he was scheduled to speak at this evening in Reno, Nevada due to wildfires in the region, his campaign said.\par \par \uc2 The Davis Fire in northern Nevada has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rgj.com/story/news/2024/09/09/davis-fire-monday-updates-what-we-know-about-the-fire-as-schools-close-homes-still-threatened/75140844007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so far scorched}}}\uc2  more than 6,500 acres and triggered evacuations since starting on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 enltrNevada Army National Guard Staff Sgt. Audrey Williams, a soldier with the 2/238th Aviation unit, captured footage of a UH-60 Black Hawk helicopter executing a crucial water bucket drop to combat the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DavisFire?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DavisFire}}}\uc2  Washoe Valley, Nevada. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4MD4UiZMlL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4MD4UiZMlL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nevada Guard (@NVNationalGuard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NVNationalGuard/status/1832948714228634083?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Walz is still expected to visit Reno today for other political engagements, the campaign said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepare to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/kamala-harris-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meet on the debate stage}}}\uc2  in Philadelphia, the battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has vaulted to the center of the 2024 presidential election campaign, the first since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/presidential-polling-analysis-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bitterly contested race for the White House}}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a glaring vulnerability for the Republican nominee. \uc2 Celinda Lake\uc2 , a veteran Democratic pollster, said:\par \par \uc2 You know it\u8217\'20\'19s an important issue because Trump is trying to change his position.\par \par \uc2 As a candidate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/03/donald-trump-abortion-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump has held conflicting positions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , alternately boasting}}}\uc2  that he appointed three of the nine supreme court justices whose votes were decisive in overturning Roe, while complaining that Republican extremism on the issue has cost his party at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 ?He recently appeared to endorse a ballot measure to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in his adopted home state of Florida, only to announce one day later \u8211\'20\'13 after sparking backlash among prominent conservative groups \u8211\'20\'13 that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would vote against it}}}\uc2 . He has also previously hinted at support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 15-week federal ban}}}\uc2  only to insist that the issue should be left to the states. His campaign has said Trump would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/democrats-republicans-abortion-rights-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats unite to center reproductive rights as Republicans flail on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris releases ads targeting Trump on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, the Harris campaign also released thee new TV ads targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate that includes comments from the Republican nominee claiming credit for helping overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The 30-second ad has includes a clip of Trump saying in 2016 that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere has to be some form of punishment\u8221\'20\'1D for women who seek abortions. It then has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/donald-trump-abortion-election-republicans-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clip of him earlier this year}}}\uc2  saying: \u8220\'20\'1CFor 54 years they were trying to get Roe v Wade terminated and I did it and I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have done it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to go further, with plans to restrict birth control, ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, even monitor women\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancies\u8221\'20\'1D, the narrator says.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Harris-Walz campaign is launching a new ad campaign ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate on reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 The three ads feature Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own words saying he is \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D to have overturned Roe, as well as two women who have been directly affected by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/390JrfXbLi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/390JrfXbLi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Hitt (@LaurenHitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaurenHitt/status/1832383854243447206?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The ad will appear on broadcast and cable networks in seven swing states \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 and in Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s competitive second congressional district, according to the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 Another ad discusses the impact of the Alabama supreme court \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/20/alabama-supreme-court-frozen-embryos-children-ruling-ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling that frozen embryos are \u8220\'20\'1Cchildren\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  on a woman\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to conceive.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign said the new ad would run as part of their $370m digital and television buy.\par \par \uc2 A statement by Harris-Walz principal deputy campaign manager \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2  reads:\par \par \uc2 This ad will remind Fox News viewers, perhaps even a certain defeated former president himself, about how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own national security team can\u8217\'20\'19t stomach him anymore because of how he\u8217\'20\'19d put the country at risk. To every American who understands the threat that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  poses, who cares about upholding the constitution, who believes in the rule of law, and who knows America is stronger when it leads, there\u8217\'20\'19s a home for you in Vice-President Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2016, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would choose only the best people to work in his White House.,\u8221\'20\'1D the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s new ad reads.\par \par \uc2 Now, those people have a warning for America: Trump is not fit to be president again.\par \par \uc2 The ad includes clips from the former Republican vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  saying that he would not be endorsing Trump in 2024, and from the former defense secretary \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2  warning that another Trump presidency \u8220\'20\'1Cplaces our service members at risk, places our nation\u8217\'20\'19s security at risk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pence, Esper and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former national security adviser \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , who is also featured in the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s ad, have said they will not vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/interactive/2024/trump-cabinet-endorsements/?itid=lk_inline_manual_15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , just over of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former cabinet supports his comeback campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris goads Trump with ad of former officials warning of a second Trump term ahead of debate\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. The Harris campaign is set to air a new TV ad featuring former officials in Donald\u8217\'20\'19s Trump administration warning about the threat he poses to the country, in what looks like an attempt to goad the former president ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/kamala-harris-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s debate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The minute-long spot, entitled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Best People\u8221\'20\'1D, will run on Fox News as well as in West Palm Beach, Florida, and Philadelphia on Tuesday to coincide with the presidential debate between Trump and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . It will continue to play throughout the week, according to the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 The ad features Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former defense secretary \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2 , former national security adviser \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  and retired \uc2 Gen Mark Milley\uc2 , former chairman of the joint chiefs of staff. The ad reads:\par \par \uc2 Take it from the people who knew him best: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a danger to our troops and our democracy. We can\u8217\'20\'19t let him lead our country again.\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign ad.\par \par \uc2 The ad came after endorsements by some high-profile Republicans for Harris last week, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  former vice-president }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dick Cheney}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  and}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his daughter }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney,}}}\uc2  a former representative of Wyoming, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/mccain-trump-arlington-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jim McCain, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/mccain-trump-arlington-democrat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the son of the late senator and 2008 presidential nominee John McCain.}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/09/latest-poll-kamala-harris-donald-trump-2024-us-election-presidential-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  is in Pittsburgh preparing for her debate tomorrow. She is expected to travel to Philadelphia in the late afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congress is back. The House rules committee is set to take up Speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s six-month stopgap funding bill, which would extend government funding through 28 March.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be in New York, Pennsylvania and the Pentagon for 9/11 events this week. He will welcome the UK prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , to the White House on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240909ek99001mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
