\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats unite to center reproductive rights as Republicans flail on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2024\par 16:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Harris campaign seeks to press advantage on powerful motivator, especially in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepare to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/kamala-harris-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meet on the debate stage}}}\uc2  in Philadelphia, the battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has vaulted to the center of the 2024 presidential election campaign, the first since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 At the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention last month, Democrats spotlighted the harrowing stories of women placed in medical peril as a result of post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in their states. Last week, the Harris campaign launched a 50-stop \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D bus tour across several battleground states, kicking off in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cback yard\u8221\'20\'1D, miles from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence in south Florida.\par \par \uc2 And this weekend, days before the first \u8211\'20\'13 and perhaps only \u8211\'20\'13 primetime presidential debate, where the issue is likely to be raised, the Harris campaign debuted three new TV ads reminding voters that Trump has repeatedly taking credit for his role in ending the 50-year-old constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The message is blunt: because of Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/06/23/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-highlights-commitment-to-defending-reproductive-rights-and-actions-to-protect-access-to-reproductive-health-care-one-year-after-overturning-of-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one in three }}}\uc2  women of reproductive age now live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned or significantly restricted. And it could get worse, they warn, if Trump is given a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a fundamental threat to reproductive freedom \u8211\'20\'13 and you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to take our word for it \u8211\'20\'13 Trump said it himself,\u8221\'20\'1D Lauren Hitt, a spokesperson for the Harris-Walz campaign, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CVice-President Harris and Governor Walz are fighting to restore reproductive freedom in all 50 states because they trust women to make the right decisions for their families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/presidential-polling-analysis-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bitterly contested race for the White House}}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a glaring vulnerability for the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know it\u8217\'20\'19s an important issue because Trump is trying to change his position,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Celinda Lake\uc2 , a veteran Democratic pollster.\par \par \uc2 As a candidate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/03/donald-trump-abortion-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump has held conflicting positions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , alternately boasting}}}\uc2  that he appointed three of the nine supreme court justices whose votes were decisive in overturning Roe, while complaining that Republican extremism on the issue has cost his party at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 ?He recently appeared to endorse a ballot measure to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in his adopted home state of Florida, only to announce one day later \u8211\'20\'13 after sparking backlash among prominent conservative groups \u8211\'20\'13 that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would vote against it}}}\uc2 . He has also previously hinted at support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 15-week federal ban}}}\uc2  only to insist that the issue should be left to the states. His campaign has said Trump would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as president.\par \par \uc2 While the economy remains the top election issue for voters this November, a New York Times/Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/08/10/us/elections/times-siena-poll-registered-voter-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  released in August showed that a growing share of battleground state voters, particularly women, say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/31/us/elections/abortion-polls-women-trump-harris.html?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be central to their decision}}}\uc2 . Among women younger than 45, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eclipsed the economy as their single most important issue.\par \par \uc2 In the final months of the campaign, Democrats are aiming to harness the unabated anger over the loss of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, especially among women and young people, and unifying around a platform that seeks to protect what remains of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and the availability of reproductive healthcare, including contraception and fertility treatments such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/jd-vance-trump-ivf-abortion-heritage-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in vitro fertilization}}}\uc2  (IVF).\par \par \uc2 In polling and focus groups, Lake said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights remains an especially salient issue for women and the issue was helping to fuel a widening gender gap between Harris and Trump. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vocal support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has not only energized young voters, a core Democratic constituency, but is also helping to persuade independent women and, as Lake put it, \u8220\'20\'1Colder women who remember when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal, and don\u8217\'20\'19t think the idea of jailing doctors, investigating miscarriages, [and] eliminating birth control and IVF is a good idea\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Trump, who has long worried that Republican-led efforts to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and restrict access to reproductive care could imperil his White House bid, has sought recast his approach to the issue. During a town hall even in battleground Wisconsin, he endorsed a plan to make the government or insurance companies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  cover the cost of IVF}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a type of fertility assistance that can cost tens of thousands of dollars and that some in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement want to see limited.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe wanna produce babies in this country, right?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats assailed the proposal as insincere, pointing to the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s record and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/jd-vance-trump-ivf-abortion-heritage-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 positions of his running mate}}}\uc2 , JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Trump has had \u8220\'20\'1Cmore positions on reproductive rights than he has had wives\u8221\'20\'1D, Ana Navarro, a TV personality and anti-Trump Republican, said last week, at the Florida launch of the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s bus tour.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have leveraged the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to secure key victories in the 2022 midterms, when mobilization efforts around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights drove strong turnout and enthusiasm, helping the party keep control of the Senate and limiting Republican gains in the House. In Michigan, Democrats secured a governing trifecta as voters in the state overwhelmingly turned out to back a ballot initiative enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBringing the message to the people, talking with women and healthcare providers and our families, that\u8217\'20\'19s how we had such a historic outcome in our \u8217\'20\'1922 election here in Michigan,\u8221\'20\'1D the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , a co-chair of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, said in an MSNBC interview this week. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s important, even for Michiganders and New Yorkers and Floridians, to know what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake if we have a second Trump presidency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans have argued that the potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would wane in a noisy presidential election. But Lake believes the opposite could be true.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a priority for young voters who are more likely to turn out in a presidential election year. Constitutional amendments seeking to guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are on the ballot in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2023/12/abortion-states-election-2024-ballot-measures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 states this fall}}}\uc2 , including battleground states like Arizona and Nevada as well as Florida, once a presidential bellwether that has trended Republican in recent cycles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the belly of the beast here in the state of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , the chair of the Florida Democratic party. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the state that has drastically moved on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from two years ago having full access to now being one of the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Florida Democrats are hopeful the ballot initiative will help boost the former representative \uc2 Debbie Mucarsel-Powell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s underdog campaign against the Republican incumbent senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 . Elsewhere in the battle for control of the Senate, vulnerable Democratic incumbents \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  of Montana and \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  of Nevada will appear on the ballot alongside measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Fried, who joined the Harris campaign kick-off in Palm Beach county last week, said the referendum had helped draw attention to the state \u8211\'20\'13 and was mobilizing voters of all political stripes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they can take away access to reproductive healthcare, what else is next?\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat other types of rights have we moved the needle on that would be going backwards if Trump is re-elected?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s referendum would overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s unpopular six-week ban, guaranteeing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbefore viability\u8221\'20\'1D, usually around 24 weeks of pregnancy. A poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/4829471-florida-abortion-poll-amendment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released in mid-August}}}\uc2  found that 56% of Sunshine state voters support the proposed amendment, just shy of the 60% threshold needed to become law. Yet it drew more support than Trump, who led Harris 51% to 47% in the state, according to the survey.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains Harris\u8217\'20\'19s strongest issue. She holds a 15-percentage-point advantage over Trump in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/09/08/us/politics/times-siena-poll-toplines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national poll of likely voters by The New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2 . Yet there were also signs that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mixed signals have muddied the waters on the issue. According to the survey, released Sunday, nearly half of independent voters say they did not think the former president would sign into law a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Republican nominee must contend with his base, particularly evangelicals and other conservative Christians, who expect Trump to further restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as president.\par \par \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of the prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life of America, recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/30/trump-ivf-anti-abortion-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  that young conservatives were \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked and saddened to see someone who they thought was pro-life, or who had always reaffirmed pro-life values, walking back on that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate in Philadelphia offers one of the highest-profile opportunities for Harris to draw a sharp contrast with Trump on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reproductive rights supporters anticipate Harris will challenge the former president over his attempts to shift positions on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that Vice-President Harris makes it crystal clear for the tens of millions of people who are watching that leaving it to the states is not a moderate position \u8211\'20\'13 that it is extreme,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rob Davidson, a Michigan-based emergency physician and executive director of the Committee to Protect Health Care, a left-leaning coalition of physicians and medical professionals that recently endorsed Harris.\par \par \uc2 Davidson said voters will also want to hear Harris articulate her vision for expanding access to reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what Trump did,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat are we going to do going forward?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240908ek98001p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
