\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge rules Missouri ballot measure to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights is invalid\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 493 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2024\par 18:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling, which may be reviewed by appellate court, could strike reproductive rights measure off November ballot\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2  judge has ruled that a ballot measure asking voters whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights should be enshrined in the state constitution is invalid, potentially jeopardizing an election scheduled for November.\par \par \uc2 In a ruling issued on Friday, Cole county circuit judge Christopher Limbaugh said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2  petition \u8211\'20\'13 also known as amendment 3 \u8211\'20\'13 led by Missourians for Constitutional Freedom did not comply with state law.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists are hopeful an appellate court could reverse Limbaugh\u8217\'20\'19s decision, but for now it remains unclear whether voters will be able to decide the issue as scheduled on 5 November, the same day as the presidential election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courts.mo.gov/fv/c/JUDGMENT.PDF?courtCode=19&di=3287306"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  Limbaugh, his decision came as a result of the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfailure to include any statute or provision that will be repealed, especially when many of these statues are apparent\u8221\'20\'1D. He went on to add: \u8220\'20\'1CThe court must conclude that the defendant-intervenors\u8217\'20\'19 initiative petition was insufficient.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Limbaugh, however, also said he \u8220\'20\'1Crecognizes the gravity of the unique issues involved in this case and the lack of direct precedent on point\u8221\'20\'1D. He ruled that he would wait until Tuesday for the amendment to be removed from the ballot, giving an appellate court time to decide whether or not to uphold his ruling.\par \par \uc2 Under amendment 3, Missourians would be granted the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until fetal viability, in addition to protections surrounding other reproductive healthcare needs such as birth control and in vitro fertilization. The amendment would also provide protections against criminal prosecution for individuals who assist with abortions.\par \par \uc2 Missouri was the first state to officially outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  eliminated the federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that had previously been established by the Roe v Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 A total of 14 states have now enacted near-total bans on the procedure, though a clear majority of Americans generally favor legalizing access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost completely banned in the state with very limited exceptions, Missouri is among the most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/missouri/abortion-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictive}}}\uc2  when it comes to reproductive freedoms.\par \par \uc2 In response to Limbaugh\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Rachel Sweet, the campaign manager for Missourians for Constitutional Freedom, said that the group\u8217\'20\'19s effort \u8220\'20\'1Cremains unwavering in our mission to ensure Missourians have the right to vote on reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, the Kansas City Star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article292074825.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to block Amendment 3 from appearing on the ballot is a profound injustice to the initiative petition process and undermines the rights of the 380,000 Missourians who signed our petition demanding a voice on this critical issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Sweet added.\par \par \uc2 Sweet also vowed to appeal the decision, saying that she hopes for a \u8220\'20\'1Cswift resolution so that Missourians can vote on November 5 to protect reproductive freedom, including access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , birth control and miscarriage care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240907ek9700231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
