\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court allows US to withhold Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s family planning fund\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton \par \uc2 419 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2024\par 11:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State refused to comply with health and human services department\u8217\'20\'19s order to give \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers\u8217\'20\'19 information\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  will allow the Biden administration to withhold millions of dollars in grant money from the state of Oklahoma over its refusal to provide information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to patients who seek it. In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/orders/courtorders/090324zr1_bqm2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 order released}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, the nine-member court said an injunction filed by the state had been denied in a 6-3 decision. Justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  were the three who would have granted Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s application for relief.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s order reaffirms two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.justia.com/cases/federal/appellate-courts/ca10/24-6063/24-6063-2024-07-15.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous lower-court decisions}}}\uc2  in which judges determined a lawsuit filed against the Biden administration by the state of Oklahoma over the taking back of the funds was unlikely to succeed.\par \par \uc2 The grant at the center of the legal battle \u8211\'20\'13 Title X family planning program \u8211\'20\'13 is distributed by the US Department of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ). In 2021, \uc2 HHS\uc2  created a new rule for grant recipients that required them to offer \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-directive\u8221\'20\'1D, neutral information about health and family planning options, including on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and to offer people referrals to medical providers, including those who offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 The following year, \uc2 HHS\uc2  approved a grant to Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s health department, but reminded the state it had to comply with the new rule, a point that \uc2 HHS\uc2  reiterated after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitutioncenter.org/the-constitution/supreme-court-case-library/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the landmark 2022 Dobbs decision}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which overturned the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 came down, according to court records. That same year, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s governor signed one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, but the \uc2 HHS\uc2  determined that state law did not preclude them from meeting the requirement for neutral information on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and referrals to providers upon request.\par \par \uc2 In March last year, Oklahoma accepted another Title X grant from the \uc2 HHS\uc2 . To satisfy the 2021 rule, the state promised to provide patients with a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational call-in\u8221\'20\'1D phone number that would provide them with neutral information. But by May, Oklahoma officials had removed the phone number, prompting \uc2 HHS\uc2  to give the state 30 days to come into compliance, which Oklahoma refused to do.\par \par \uc2 In September, \uc2 HHS\uc2  redirected the $4.5m in grant funding away from the state, and gave it to Missouri-based organizations. Oklahoma appealed the move, and in November the state attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oklahoma.gov/oag/news/newsroom/2023/november/drummond-sues-biden-administration-over-title-x-abortion-overrea.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the Biden administration}}}\uc2 , arguing that Biden officials had \u8220\'20\'1Coverreached\u8221\'20\'1D by taking the funds away.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240904ek940005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
