\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump says he will vote against Florida  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights ballot amendment \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon and Chris Stein \par \uc2 7,161 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 23:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our latest story hereAnalysis: Harris\u8217\'20\'19s much-hyped interview was... radically normalKey takeaways from Harris and Walz\u8217\'20\'19s first interview\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hit his favorite talking points in a rally held in Pennsylvania Friday afternoon, as he scolded the media, reiterated his call for death sentences for drug dealers, and spouted derogatory nicknames he\u8217\'20\'19s assigned to opponents. The event was one of two on his schedule this afternoon as the former president heads back to Washington DC to speak at the national summit of Moms for Liberty, a conservative organization pushing for the removal of LGBTQ+ mentions and structural racism from schools.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is looking to keep her momentum with voters going, after yesterday conducting the first interview of her presidential bid with CNN, alongside her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . Her campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1b9b08f08e2612479478b#block-66d1b9b08f08e2612479478b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused bus tour that will crisscross swing states, while Georgia is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1d93e8f08e261247949c5#block-66d1d93e8f08e261247949c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  seeing a surge in registrations by new voters, particularly among the groups most likely to vote for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s statement yesterday that he would support requiring the government or private insurances to back IVF care by saying he \u8216\'20\'18lies as much if not more than he breathes\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump addressed the recent altercation at Arlington cemetery, claiming he only posed for pictures because families asked him to. Arlington officials said in a statement that members of his campaign staff were reported for their behavior during a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrass\u8221\'20\'1D photo opportunity for the Republican candidate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/arlington-cemetery-altercation-trump-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US army confirms Arlington cemetery worker \u8216\'20\'18pushed aside\u8217\'20\'19 by Trump staff}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 After receiving backlash for breaking with his base this week after he criticized Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Trump clarified he will vote against an amendment that would strike it down.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for tuning in! Have a good night.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Defend Democracy Project, an organization formed to combat misinformation about the results of the 2020 election, condemned the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/trump-hush-money-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to move his election interference case from Manhattan to federal court}}}\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 After being convicted on 34 felony counts for falsifying business records in relation to hush-money he paid to adult film star Stormy Daniels during the 2020 election, Trump was scheduled to be sentenced next month in state court. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have been pushing to delay sentencing until after the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump already tried to move this case to federal court under the exact same statute in 2023 and was denied. This time, he is trying to use the Supreme Court decision on presidential immunity to bolster his argument,\u8221\'20\'1D Ambassador Norman Eisen, who served as special counsel to the \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  majority during the first impeachment and trial of President Trump and Michael Podhorzer, the chair of the Defend Democracy Project said in a joint statement issued Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump knows this argument is a dead-end on the merits, but he\u8217\'20\'19s clearly hoping to quickly force this up the ladder to the complicit MAGA justices on the Supreme Court to once again save him from facing accountability for his repeated attempts to interfere in our elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/trump-hush-money-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump tries to move hush-money case to federal court to avoid sentencing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 A man was tackled to the ground by officers at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pennsylvania rally today, after he tried to climb over a fence and into the press area and then onto another piece of infrastructure at the event. Additional security has been added since the assassination attempt last month.\par \par \uc2 Videos taken by reporters of the altercation and posted online show several officers pulling the man down before pushing him to the ground, handcuffing him, and leading him out of the event, as Trump talks about the shooting incident in the background.\par \par \uc2 enltrVideo of the incident. Security in the press pen grabbed him first before he was taken down by law enforcement. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xdw1CZ9dE0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Xdw1CZ9dE0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taurean Small (@taureansmall) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/taureansmall/status/1829636618233287111?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump defends himself from rambling accusations with wordy explanation\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has defended himself from accusations that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/24/donald-trump-mental-fitness-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rambles nonsensically}}}\uc2  at his rallies by claiming that he is in fact weaving together complex thoughts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, I do the weave. You know what the weave is? I\u8217\'20\'19ll talk about like nine different things, that they all come back brilliantly together. And it\u8217\'20\'19s like friends of mine that are like English professors, they say\u8221\'20\'1D \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s the most brilliant thing I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D he told a rally in Johnstown, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut the fake news, you know what they say: \u8216\'20\'18He rambled\u8217\'20\'19. It\u8217\'20\'19s not rambling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her first solo campaign event, Gwen Walz, the wife of vice presidential candidate Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , said she didn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Ctake kindly\u8221\'20\'1D to remarks from JD Vance about family planning.\par \par \uc2 Vance has recently said childless citizens have less of a stake in the future of the US, but Walz responded to resurfaced remarks he made back in 2021 about childless teachers:\par \par \uc2 JD Vance said he was \u8216\'20\'18really disturbed\u8217\'20\'19 by teachers who don\u8217\'20\'19t have biological children. For a long time, Tim and I were teachers who struggled with infertility. We were only able to start a family because of fertility treatments. We do not take kindly to folks like JD Vance telling us when or how to start our families. So let me use my teacher voice. Mr. Vance, how about you mind your own business?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GwenWalz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GwenWalz}}}\uc2  : JD Vance said he was 'really disturbed' by teachers who don't have biological children. For a long time, Tim and I were teachers who struggled with infertility. We were only able to start a family because of fertility treatments. We do not take kindly to folks like JD\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XrrepJRAOX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XrrepJRAOX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1829561289191899255?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump tells Fox News he will vote against Florida's six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment\par \par \uc2 On Friday, in comments to Fox News, Trump also clarified his position on a Florida amendment that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and overturn the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, saying he would vote against it. The Republican candidate had previously told NBC News that the six-week window is \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo short\u8221\'20\'1D, sparking confusion about his stance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think six weeks, you need more time than six weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said Friday, but added: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, the Democrats are radical because the nine months is just a ridiculous situation where you can do an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month \u8230\'20\'26 So I\u8217\'20\'19ll be voting no for that reason.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The amendment would ensure access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care before fetal viability around the 24th week, and add exceptions when the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health is in danger.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says he will vote to uphold Florida\u8217\'20\'19s 6-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zf4RbhvN4B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zf4RbhvN4B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1829635594403578062?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says gold star families asked him for picture at Arlington as he again addresses controversy\par \par \uc2 Trump addressed the recent controversy at Arlington cemetery, when members of his campaign staff were reported for their behavior during a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrass\u8221\'20\'1D photo opportunity for the Republican candidate. Trump was there participating in a wreath-laying ceremony for 13 US service personnel killed in a 2021 suicide bomb attack in Afghanistan, and he told supporters at his rally that he was asked by families there to take photos.\par \par \uc2 Blaming Biden and Harris (whose name mispronounces frequently) for the deaths of these soldiers, Trump said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful ceremony\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter the ceremony they said, could you come to the graves?\u8221\'20\'1D he said, insisting he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want any publicity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am the only guy who would hire a public relations agency to get less publicity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, but added he wanted to do so for these families. \u8220\'20\'1CI am so happy they took pictures of me and them and the tombstone and their lovely son or daughter \u8211\'20\'13 there was a daughter too, an incredible daughter, frankly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But as Richard Luscombe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/trump-arlington-cemetery-visit-altercation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Arlington acknowledged one of its representatives became involved in the altercation with two Trump staffers, telling them that only cemetery representatives were allowed to take video and photographs in section 60, an area where recent US casualties, mostly from Iraq and Afghanistan, are buried.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFederal law prohibits political campaign or election-related activities within Army National Military Cemeteries, to include photographers, content creators or any other persons attending for purposes, or in direct support of a partisan political candidate\u8217\'20\'19s campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Ca report was filed\u8221\'20\'1D over the incident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArlington National Cemetery reinforced and widely shared this law and its prohibitions with all participants,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 The staffers \u8220\'20\'1Cverbally abused and pushed the official aside\u8221\'20\'1D as the person attempted to prevent them from accompanying Trump into the section, according to NPR, which first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/27/nx-s1-5091154/trump-arlington-cemetery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published the allegation}}}\uc2  on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest pictures from the Trump rally in Johnstown, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters wave placards at rally. Photograph: Roberto Schmidt/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump hits favorite talking points of immigration and media attacks\par \par \uc2 Trump has already hit many of his favorite talking points in this speech, opening by scolding journalists present at the event, using derogatory nicknames for his opponents, and talking about his patriotism. He claimed he would push for prison time for anyone who burns an American flag, even though the action is protected by the constitution, and that he agrees with death sentences for drug dealers. He also repeated claims about immigration.\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has attacked foreign governments for allegedly emptying their prisons and shipping criminals to the US illegally. But then said that if he was in charge of the same countries he would be more effective at the same thing.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If I was running one of those countries, I\u8217\'20\'19d be doing better than them at getting them out,\u8217\'20\'19 he told a rally in Johnstown, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Trump was hitting a favoured theme even though he has yet to produce evidence for his claim. But he did make reference to the release of video of Venezuelan gangs operating in Aurora, Colorado including shootouts. Trump has previously alleged that the Venezuelan government is one of those sending known criminals across the Mexican border.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump holds rally in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters have gathered and are waiting for him to speak in Johnstown, Pennsylvania. The former president is expected to take the stage at about 4.45pm ET, before heading to a national summit in Washington of Moms for Liberty, a conservative organization pushing for the removal of LGBTQ+ mentions and structural racism from schools.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Responding to Trump's IVF policy, Harris campaign says former president 'lies as much if not more than he breathes'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s statement yesterday that he would support requiring the government or private insurances to back IVF care:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur statement on Trump lying about IVF {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IVd6Tl3XOk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IVd6Tl3XOk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1829302031183425943?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that Democrats in the Senate have proposed legislation that would protect access to IVF, in response to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision}}}\uc2  earlier this year that essentially banned the care in the state.\par \par \uc2 However, Republican lawmakers have stopped that bill from passing:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/right-to-ivf-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans block bill that establishes right to IVF across the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re wondering why you haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard much about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  these past few days \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s because the president has been on vacation ever since giving the keynote speech on the first night of last week\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic convention. Photographers saw him on Rehoboth Beach, Delaware on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at his speech to the Democratic convention, where he made good on his pledge to pass the torch to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/joe-biden-democratic-convention-chicago-gaza-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden speaks at first night of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gwen Walz says Trump 'put access to IVF at risk' after former president tries to pitch himself as IVF champion\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign clearly wants to keep reproductive rights at the top of voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds in the weeks that remain before the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Gwen Walz, the wife of vice-presidential nominee \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , in Virginia:\par \par \uc2 enltr"\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the one who took down Roe and put access to IVF at risk. That's a fact."\par \par \uc2 Gwen Walz slams Trump on reproductive rights at campaign event. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B2KOcT0iBr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B2KOcT0iBr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1829557406621192271?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1c6788f0871b94295bab1#block-66d1c6788f0871b94295bab1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would support}}}\uc2  requiring the government or private insurances to pay for IVF care.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick T Brown, a fellow at the conservative Ethics and Public Policy Center who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement of support for a Florida ballot measure that would expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access \u8220\'20\'1Canother middle finger towards pro-lifers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though Trump played a major role in overturning Roe v Wade by appointing three of the conservative justices who approved the ruling, Brown\u8217\'20\'19s piece underscore how uneasy his relationship is with advocates for limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ptbwrites.substack.com/p/another-trump-middle-finger-to-pro?utm_source=post-email-title&publication_id=2781825&post_id=148187733&utm_campaign=email-post-title&isFreemail=true&r=35gftk&triedRedirect=true&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Brown\u8217\'20\'19s Substack}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Florida is faced with a ballot amendment that would wipe nearly all restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  off the books this fall. It needs 60% of votes to pass, so pro-lifers had been modestly hopefully they could keep the \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D vote under the threshold. But their cause will not be helped by Trump suggesting that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to be voting that we need more than six weeks\u8221\'20\'1D (though his campaign later \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/reesejgorman/status/1829321109369712749"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarified}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D that he \u8220\'20\'1Chas not yet said how he will vote on the ballot initiative.\u8221\'20\'1D) This, of course, comes after Trump has repeatedly stressed how \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone\u8221\'20\'1D should be happy that the Dobbs returns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation to the states. Apparently his version of federalism only goes one direction, as his sandbagging of the efforts of Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and other pro-life Florida Republicans could push the \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D side over the finish line in November - a catastrophe for the pro-life cause in the Sunshine State and nationwide.\par \par \uc2 But wait - there\u8217\'20\'19s more. At a rally that night, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/08/29/trump-ivf-proposals-costs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined a proposal}}}\uc2  for covering IVF either through an Obamacare insurance mandate or paying for it with public money. According to the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , the cost per successful IVF outcome ranges somewhere around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/about/news/2024/03/13/fact-sheet-in-vitro-fertilization-ivf-use-across-united-states.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $61,000}}}\uc2 , and over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asrm.org/news-and-events/asrm-news/press-releasesbulletins/ivf-assisted-pregnancies-constitute/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 90,000 babies}}}\uc2  were born via IVF in 2022 (2.5% of all births nationwide.) That\u8217\'20\'19s a static estimate of $50 billion over a ten-year budget window, putting aside what universally available free IVF would do to increase demand. For those who remember the contraceptive mandate fight of 2012, this would be that \u8212\'20\'14 on steroids.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to a question during her CNN interview last night about her views on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza was not well received by the Uncommitted movement, which has called for the Democratic party to stop supporting the incursion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael has a right to defend itself \u8211\'20\'13 we would,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, while adding, \u8220\'20\'1CHow it does so matters,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CFar too many innocent Palestinians have been killed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She reiterated her support for the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s long-running efforts to secure a ceasefire in the enclave, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have got to get a deal done. This war must end.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, the Uncommitted National Movement\u8217\'20\'19s co-founders, Layla Elabed and Abbas Alawieh, said:\par \par \uc2 The Vice President\u8217\'20\'19s statement was morally indefensible and politically shortsighted as the lack of American consequences for Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s horrific assault on Palestinian civilians in Gaza has emboldened Israel to now invade the West Bank. Vice President Harris must turn the page from one of the most glaring foreign policy failures of our time by aligning with the American majority that opposes sending weapons to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s assault on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The controversy over the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Arlington does not appear to be going away \u8211\'20\'13 and some Democrats are weighing in on what they see as the latest example of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lack of respect for fallen soldiers and active servicemen and women.\par \par \uc2 New Jersey congresswoman and former Navy pilot Mikie Sherill wrote on X earlier this week: \u8220\'20\'1CArlington National Cemetery isn\u8217\'20\'19t a place for campaign photo-ops. It\u8217\'20\'19s a sacred resting place for American patriots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , disrespecting military veterans is just par for the course. It\u8217\'20\'19s an absolute disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrArlington National Cemetery isn't a place for campaign photo-ops. It's a sacred resting place for American patriots.\par \par \uc2 But for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , disrespecting military veterans is just par for the course.\par \par \uc2 It's an absolute disgrace.\par \par \uc2 We're not going back. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MRgU95xx0u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/MRgU95xx0u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mikie Sherrill\uc2  (@MikieSherrill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikieSherrill/status/1828617840846307367?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/defense/4854751-democrats-attack-donald-trump-arlington/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill }}}\uc2  reports Virginia congressman \uc2 Gerry Connolly\uc2  and Maine representative Jared Golden \u8211\'20\'13 a former Marine \u8211\'20\'13 also criticized Trump\u8217\'20\'19s use of the military cemetery for campaign purposes.\par \par \uc2 Connolly said it was \u8220\'20\'1Csad but all too expected that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would desecrate this hallowed ground and put campaign politics ahead of honoring our heroes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Golden reportedly said \u8220\'20\'1Call visitors should take the time to learn the rules of decorum that ensure the proper respect is given to the fallen and their families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her interview with CNN, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made herself out to be a centrist leader who was not interested in discussing how her election would break longstanding racial and gender barriers in US politics, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/gabrielle-canon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gabrielle Canon}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In a primetime spot on CNN Thursday evening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  sat for their first interview together as the Democratic ticket, taking questions from the anchor Dana Bash on a range of important issues, including their plans for day one if they win the race, the approach to the war in Gaza, and how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  passed the baton.\par \par \uc2 With just over two months until voters will head to the polls on 5 November \u8211\'20\'13 and even less time before some will mail in their ballots \u8211\'20\'13 the Democratic candidates for president and vice-president made good on a promise to speak more candidly about how they will tackle the US\u8217\'20\'19s most pressing problems.\par \par \uc2 But this interview was about more than just policies and priorities.\par \par \uc2 For weeks, Republicans and members of the media have called for the nominees to open themselves up to questions, especially the vice-president, who has for the most part sidestepped unscripted moments in the six weeks since the president ended his bid for re-election and endorsed her. Analysts and opponents were watching Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s interview closely for new insights into how a Harris administration would approach the presidency, how the candidates interact with one another, and how she would respond in more candid moments.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we learned:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Next question, please\u8217\'20\'19 and Gaza war: key takeaways from Harris and Walz\u8217\'20\'19s first interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  finally sat down for an interview yesterday, alongside her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . The encounter with CNN quelled weeks of growing pressure for her to interact with the press, though expect it to amp back up again if she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t keep the outreach going. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what the vice-president had to say, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Democrats lauded it as the perfect pitch; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  dismissed it as \u8220\'20\'1Cboring\u8221\'20\'1D, while fellow Republicans invoked derogatory terms like \u8220\'20\'1Cgobbledygook\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Between the two extremes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  appeared to have achieved what she wanted from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s groundbreaking CNN interview}}}\uc2 , given along with her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 her first since become the Democratic presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 Under fierce scrutiny after nearly six weeks of interview radio silence, the vice-president earned lavish praise from the Democratic base while denying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  a clear line of attack simply by avoiding major missteps of the type that undid \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s candidacy in June\u8217\'20\'19s climactic debate.\par \par \uc2 The performance is also unlikely to shake up a race that has reversed itself since Harris entered it and replaced Biden, flipping a narrow but solid Trump lead into a contest in which she is now firmly ahead.\par \par \uc2 A commentator with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://azcentral.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AZCentral.com}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a news site in the key swing state of Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/entertainment/media/2024/08/29/harris-walz-interview-cnn/74973222007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performance}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo sane to be great TV\u8221\'20\'1D, an implicit comparison with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s frequently ostentatious media appearances.\par \par \uc2 Commenting on her championing of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s record in office, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/29/us/politics/harris-walz-interview-cnn-takeaways.html?searchResultPosition=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cit turns out, Ms Harris is a better salesperson for Mr Biden\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments and defender of his record than he ever was\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the highest praise came from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s party supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis interview with Dana Bash is a moment to recognize that it is absolutely under-appreciated that Vice President Harris is running a perfect campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D Bill Burton, a former deputy press secretary in \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/billburton/status/1829333096510234912"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  on X.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/kamala-harris-interview-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s interview: Democrats swoon while Republicans grimace}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s niece, his political ascension has been so devastating that it pushed her to seek ketamine treatment, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In a new memoir, Mary L Trump, niece of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , writes of being pushed to despair, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/apr/11/ketamine-clinics-us-business-safety-mental-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ketamine}}}\uc2  therapy, by her uncle\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2016 presidential election}}}\uc2 , his chaotic, far-right administration and his refusal to leave national politics despite his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because five years ago, I lost control of my life,\u8221\'20\'1D Mary Trump writes, describing ketamine treatment undertaken in December 2021. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because the world has fallen away and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to find my way back.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is my uncle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her doctor, she says, answered: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry. That must be very difficult for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now 59, Mary Trump is a trained psychologist and bestselling author. Her new book, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Who-Could-Ever-Love-You/dp/1250278473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who Could Ever Love You: A Family Memoir}}}\uc2 , will be published in the US on 10 September. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/article/2024/aug/30/donald-trump-ketamine-therapy-niece-mary-new-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump pushed me to ketamine therapy, niece Mary says in new book}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is looking to keep her momentum with voters going, after yesterday conducting the first interview of her presidential bid with CNN, alongside her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . Her campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1b9b08f08e2612479478b#block-66d1b9b08f08e2612479478b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced plans}}}\uc2  for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused bus tour that will crisscross swing states, while Georgia is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1d93e8f08e261247949c5#block-66d1d93e8f08e261247949c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  seeing a surge in registrations by new voters, particularly among the groups most likely to vote for Democrats. Speaking of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday said he supported a ballot initiative to overturn Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on the procedure, but both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1e2478f08e26124794a5a#block-66d1e2478f08e26124794a5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his campaign}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1e7138f0871b94295bcee#block-66d1e7138f0871b94295bcee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running mate }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1e7138f0871b94295bcee#block-66d1e7138f0871b94295bcee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  are trying to walk back the comment, underscoring the perils of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s position on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1c6788f0871b94295bab1#block-66d1c6788f0871b94295bab1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also broke}}}\uc2  with years of Republican orthodoxy by saying he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t move to block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Washington DC, and told supporters he wanted the government or private insurance to pay for IVF care.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Spencer Cox\uc2 , the Republican governor of Utah, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1eac28f08e26124794af8#block-66d1eac28f08e26124794af8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apologized}}}\uc2  after his campaign used images of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Arlington national cemetery this week \u8211\'20\'13 which the former president has refused to do.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/30/election-trump-harris-abortion-updates?page=with:block-66d1f3c08f08e26124794b6f#block-66d1f3c08f08e26124794b6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will travel}}}\uc2  to southern California for a judiciary committee hearing that will likely be aimed at Harris and her stance on undocumented migration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans, who have spent much of their nearly two years in control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber investigating the Biden administration with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/28/biden-impeachment-inquiry-republicans-evidence-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mixed}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/dismiss-impeachment-charges-mayorkas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 results}}}\uc2 , will next week hold a judiciary committee hearing on the effects of undocumented migrants in California.\par \par \uc2 That is, of course, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s home state, which she represented in the Senate from 2017 to 2021. The hearing, titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden-Harris Border Crisis: California Perspectives\u8221\'20\'1D will take place next Friday in Santee, California, a San Diego suburb in a Republican-leaning House district.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have campaigned on cracking down on undocumented migrants, and have accused Harris of changing her answers over whether or not she supports building a wall along the border with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s stated policy on the matter is a little more complicated than they make it out to be:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/27/harris-border-wall-policy-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans accuse Kamala Harris of flip-flopping on border wall policy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again tries to play down Arlington controversy and claims he knew nothing of the rules\par \par \uc2 NBC News asked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s decision to use images of his visit to Arlington national cemetery in communications to supporters, including on TikTok.\par \par \uc2 He downplayed the controversial decision, saying, essentially, that they were just pictures and that he did not know \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat the rules and regulations are\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump claims without evidence that his Arlington National Cemetery photo-op controversy \u8220\'20\'1Cwas a setup by the people in the administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll I do is, I stood there and I said, if you'd like to have a picture, we can have a picture.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/duK4yO3oyj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/duK4yO3oyj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1829527414164111794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Utah governor who joined Trump at Arlington says visit was not meant to be campaign event\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, outrage continues over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Arlington national cemetery on Monday, during which one of his staffers pushed aside a cemetery employee who tried to prevent them from shooting pictures and video in an area where doing so was prohibited.\par \par \uc2 While the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has forcefully rejected criticism of their conduct, their indignation was not shared by Utah governor \uc2 Spencer Cox\uc2 , who joined Trump during the visit.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, he apologized for using images of the cemetery, where American war dead are buried, in a campaign email:\par \par \uc2 enltrYou are correct Alan. This was not a campaign event and was never intended to be used by the campaign. It did not go through the proper channels and should not have been sent. My campaign will be sending out an apology.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Spencer Cox\uc2  (@SpencerJCox) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpencerJCox/status/1828850554711474253?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance was asked about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s stated opposition to Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator also tried to clean Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks up:\par \par \uc2 The president is simply saying he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like six weeks. He obviously has said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and I think he will make an announcement on what he actually wants to do on the Florida law in particular. But again, President Trump has been extremely consistent that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to make this decision as a citizen of Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump speaks out against Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions - then campaign walks it back\par \par \uc2 In further evidence that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite sure how to balance his party\u8217\'20\'19s longstanding opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with concerns that many voters favor continued access to the procedure, the former president yesterday spoke out against Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, leaving his campaign to clean up his comments.\par \par \uc2 Florida, where Trump lives, bans abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, and voters in November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will decide}}}\uc2  whether to pass a measure guaranteeing a right to the procedure until fetal viability, which is usually around 24 weeks of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News yesterday}}}\uc2  asked Trump how he\u8217\'20\'19d vote on the measure. He replied:\par \par \uc2 I am going to be voting that we need more than six weeks.\par \par \uc2 That didn\u8217\'20\'19t sit well with his campaign, who quickly moved to walk back the former president\u8217\'20\'19s comments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-michigan-wisconsin-harris-battleground-campaign-0583faabae5e36000baa18c7b2bea752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign spokeswoman Karoline Leavitt said in a statement after the rally Thursday that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas not yet said how he will vote on the ballot initiative in Florida\u8221\'20\'1D known as Amendment 4 and that he \u8220\'20\'1Csimply reiterated that he believes six weeks is too short.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His comments nonetheless drew immediate reaction from those who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including Marjorie Dannenfelser, the president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, who said she had spoken with Trump after his speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has not committed to how he will vote on Amendment 4. President Trump has consistently opposed abortions after five months of pregnancy. Amendment 4 would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past this point. Voting for Amendment 4 completely undermines his position,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that, \u8220\'20\'1Canyone who believes in drawing a different line\u8221\'20\'1D still \u8220\'20\'1Cmust vote against Amendment 4, unless they don\u8217\'20\'19t want a line at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spent the last two days in Georgia on a bus tour (her campaign seems to like bus tours) that culminated with a rally in Savannah yesterday evening. From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/justin-glawe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Glawe}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s what the vice-president told supporters, as she hopes for a repeat of the luck \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had in the state four years ago:\par \par \uc2 After two days on a bus tour through south-east Georgia with her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  arrived at an arena in Savannah to a boisterous crowd and told them that despite the state being a stretch, it is still winnable in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t pay attention to polls \u8211\'20\'13 we are underdogs,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said, telling the roughly 9,500 attendees that they had \u8220\'20\'1Cwork to do\u8221\'20\'1D in order to secure victory. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t mind hard work. Hard work is for workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thousands waited outside for hours as a spitting rain became a steady drizzle, which turned into an outright downpour, on a hot and characteristically humid Savannah afternoon. Inside, thousands of supporters filled out an arena usually reserved for minor league hockey games and concerts \u8211\'20\'13 taking up every last seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back in Savannah,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, jumping right into a stump speech that, while familiar, nonetheless kept the crowd\u8217\'20\'19s attention for the entirety of her remarks.\par \par \uc2 Recent polling has Harris and \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolling.com/polls/president/general/2024/georgia/trump-vs-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly tied}}}\uc2  in Georgia, an indication of how close the race is likely to be in the state that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won in 2020 by just 11,779 votes.\par \par \uc2 During her brief remarks that lasted just under 20 minutes, Harris contrasted her campaign with that of Trump, who she criticized with her regular campaign line of moving the country backward, not forward. She touted policy plans such as affordable childcare and healthcare, paid family leave, expanding Medicaid and other aspects of what she called \u8220\'20\'1Can opportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D focused on \u8220\'20\'1Cbuilding inter-generational wealth\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/kamala-harris-savannah-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are the underdogs\u8217\'20\'19: Harris tells Georgia voters \u8216\'20\'18hard work\u8217\'20\'19 can win critical swing state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 New voter registrations surged in swing state Georgia after Harris launched campaign - report\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s been a sharp increase in people registering to vote in Georgia in the weeks since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  launched her campaign, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/harris-presidential-run-shakes-up-voter-registration-trends-in-georgia/ZSHZQD7XXJA7RCUP7WPXWXV5LU/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports}}}\uc2 , with groups that tend to back Democrats making up a large part of the new registrants.\par \par \uc2 It could be a good sign for the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in a state where Democrats reversed years of election losses in 2020, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won its electoral votes and the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidates captured both of its Senate seats.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Journal-Constitution on the registration trends:\par \par \uc2 Black women led the surge, with a 75% jump in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/sharp-growth-in-georgia-voters-alters-landscape-for-2022-elections/HEZQQJR75NAP5CHY56SKB4TS54/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 registrations}}}\uc2  compared with the same 3 1/2 week period in 2020, according to the most recent voter registration data available from the Georgia secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office, stretching from July 21 to Aug. 13.\par \par \uc2 Sign-ups by Hispanic voters grew by an even larger percentage, 114% over the 2020 period, though the raw number of new registrations was lower than other racial groups because there are fewer Hispanic voters overall in the state.\par \par \uc2 And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/democrats-and-republicans-in-georgia-are-working-to-reach-young-voters/R7IYWUANJVAL7IP4QGD6Z2EFHA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new voters}}}\uc2  under 30 years old spiked by 76%. Overall, 50% more voters have registered since July 21 than in the same period four years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s shocking. I did not expect to see something of this scope,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2 , a Democratic strategist and CEO of the data company TARA Group. \u8220\'20\'1CThis has the potential to be a game changer in terms of the presidential race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bonier\u8217\'20\'19s research also found similar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/tbonier/status/1828457890228629534"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaps in 13 other states}}}\uc2  since Harris joined the race, and he said Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s growth in registrations reinforces an emerging national trend.\par \par \uc2 More than 46,000 people have registered since July 21, bringing Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s total number of voters to 8.1 million. So far this year, 226,000 new voters have registered.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s climb in recent polls has been driven by a surge in enthusiasm among Democratic voters, and the traditional bounce in support seen after party conventions, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s entry into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential race}}}\uc2  has given a shot in the arm to Democratic voters, who are now expressing near-record enthusiasm levels, fresh polling data shows.\par \par \uc2 While the figures from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/649397/democrats-drive-surge-election-enthusiasm.aspxhttps://x.com/%3E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup}}}\uc2  indicate rising enthusiasm among all voters \u8211\'20\'13 including Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 over the past five months, comparative figures show a much steeper increase among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 indicating that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s replacement of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as presidential candidate is the likely driving factor.\par \par \uc2 The surging enthusiasm coincides with an improved general polling performance from Harris compared with Biden, who dropped out of the race last month after a poor debate performance that threatened to further depress his already stagnant numbers in survey match-ups against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A fresh Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll released on Thursday showed Harris leading Trump nationwide by 45% to 41% \u8211\'20\'13 a margin consistent with other surveys since last week\u8217\'20\'19s boisterous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic national convention}}}\uc2  in Chicago that confirmed the US vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s status as the nominee.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s figures since then have generally enhanced the small leads that she had accrued since her elevation to the top of the Democratic ticket in July, suggesting that her standing has been further boosted by the traditional post-convention bounce that presidential candidates customarily receive.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/2024-us-presidential-polls-harris-enthusiasm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls: Harris taps into near-record levels of enthusiasm}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz campaign\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CFighting for Reproductive Freedom\u8221\'20\'1D bus tour will begin on Tuesday in Palm Beach, Florida \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s backyard.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota senator Amy Klobuchar, TV personality Ana Navarro, who had a prominent spot at the Democratic convention and campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez will be among those onboard for what is expected to be 50 stops in swing states. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s husband Doug Emhoff and Gwen Walz, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s wife, will also make appearances along the way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about freedom \u8211\'20\'13 and the American people want and deserve the freedom to make their own health care decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Chavez Rodriguez said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur campaign is hitting the road to meet voters in their communities, underscore the stakes of this election for reproductive freedom, and present them with the Harris-Walz ticket\u8217\'20\'19s vision to move our country forward, which stands in stark contrast to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to drag us back. As we crisscross the country, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be driving that contrast home to red and blue voters and independents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued his attempted pivot on reproductive rights yesterday while campaigning in Wisconsin alongside former Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , who recounted her experience with IVF. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  was there, and has this report:\par \par \uc2 At a town hall event in La Crosse, Wisconsin, on Thursday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and the former Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , now a Trump campaign surrogate, attempted to pitch themselves to the crowd as supporters of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard, who moderated the event after endorsing the former president earlier this week, opened the town hall with emotional remarks about her experience with in vitro fertilization. The comments came shortly after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804?cid=eml_nbn_20240829&user_email=44c11d5d46c3757ec95f4420aa14bc672186d4206f29a3824bba58589834f455&utm_campaign=breakingnews&%243p=e_sailthru&_branch_match_id=1308400092925361144&utm_medium=Email%20Sailthru&_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAAzVP7WrDMAx8muyf28QfqTMoYzD2GkGxnVQ0VoztNOztpwwGAulOukP3qDWV9%2BuVJkfhKBdI6bIiPa8qfTRSq3QPYwFc6yPvb0xsGRckWMc9r%2FfHKW7UZyO%2FuY7juPzbuC0yk7YVK7rCo99Y5EXNe0wM%2F7oo8FPEAVSLiPAMAl8zXwSoMZxcAvRi2V4h00kIpLJnIBcE2ycgFNkRdL21rW7Ut0PfqK8Q15EmGmUrdWvl0Mh%2BLyGPIXIK3mvtus4br3unbuYW3GBmrWUL0OnJ9TfZ2d4z7mc5gLJSTxMYa%2BxglZ61MadfjaMD%2FgAXYseJP34iLWfwXzF7KTJPAQAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in an NBC interview}}}\uc2  that he would make the government or insurance companies pay for IVF if he is elected, although it is unclear how he would accomplish that or if he is serious about the proposal given the pivotal role he played in overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were not successful in trying to get pregnant. For us, IVF seemed to be the only option and the last resort,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gabbard, who described to a quiet audience the costly and at times painful fertility treatment process she said she underwent 10 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Following Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s comments on IVF, Trump reiterated his promise from earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe wanna produce babies in this country, right?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 By stating his support for IVF and claiming that he would leave \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to the states if elected, Trump is hoping to retain the support of women who count reproductive rights as a top issue \u8211\'20\'13 but risks alienating his supporters on the religious right.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We wanna produce babies\u8217\'20\'19: Trump tries to pitch himself as IVF supporter after Roe fall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump indicates support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Washington DC, IVF care in attempt to pivot on vulnerable issues\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights has been a major vulnerability for Republicans nationwide ever since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade two years ago and allowed states to ban the procedure. As the president who appointed three of the justices who supported that ruling, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been no exception, and he\u8217\'20\'19s lately tried to execute something of a pivot on the issue.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2024/08/30/trump-dc-abortion-ban-column-00176791?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that the former president has signaled support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Washington DC, going against years of attempts by the GOP to use Congress\u8217\'20\'19s unique oversight of the capital to restrict the procedure in its city limits.\par \par \uc2 And, yesterday, he told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804?cid=eml_nbn_20240829&user_email=44c11d5d46c3757ec95f4420aa14bc672186d4206f29a3824bba58589834f455&utm_campaign=breakingnews&%243p=e_sailthru&_branch_match_id=1308400092925361144&utm_medium=Email%20Sailthru&_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAAzVP7WrDMAx8muyf28QfqTMoYzD2GkGxnVQ0VoztNOztpwwGAulOukP3qDWV9%2BuVJkfhKBdI6bIiPa8qfTRSq3QPYwFc6yPvb0xsGRckWMc9r%2FfHKW7UZyO%2FuY7juPzbuC0yk7YVK7rCo99Y5EXNe0wM%2F7oo8FPEAVSLiPAMAl8zXwSoMZxcAvRi2V4h00kIpLJnIBcE2ycgFNkRdL21rW7Ut0PfqK8Q15EmGmUrdWvl0Mh%2BLyGPIXIK3mvtus4br3unbuYW3GBmrWUL0OnJ9TfZ2d4z7mc5gLJSTxMYa%2BxglZ61MadfjaMD%2FgAXYseJP34iLWfwXzF7KTJPAQAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  that he would support requiring the government or private insurers to pay for IVF for families. He also said that he would not back restrictions on the care \u8211\'20\'13 which Democrats have accused the GOP of wanting to do, after Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/university-alabama-ivf-embryo-care-paused-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this year}}}\uc2  handed down a ruling that cut off access.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what Trump said, from NBC:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be, under the Trump administration, we are going to be paying for that treatment,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said before adding, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to be mandating that the insurance company pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked to clarify whether the government would pay for IVF services or whether insurance companies would do so, Trump reiterated that one option would be to have insurance companies pay \u8220\'20\'1Cunder a mandate, yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and IVF have been political liabilities for the GOP this year. Democrats have blasted Republicans over IVF in recent months, saying GOP-led restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lead to restrictions on IVF, as well.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Sarafina Chitika, a spokesperson for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 campaign, said that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own platform could effectively ban IVF and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause Trump overturned Roe v. Wade, IVF is already under attack and women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms have been ripped away in states across the country. There is only one candidate in this race who trusts women and will protect our freedom to make our own health care decisions: Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign launches \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused bus tour as polls continue to indicate momentum against Trump\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  yesterday sat for their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first joint interview}}}\uc2  since launching their campaign, and outlined some of the policies they\u8217\'20\'19d bring to the White House, if elected. Now, they\u8217\'20\'19re looking to press the advantage over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and JD Vance that polls continue to indicate they may have, particularly on issues of reproductive health. Their campaign this morning announced a bus tour through swing states that will focus on promoting her policies towards IVF access and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and feature prominent surrogates including Minnesota senator Amy Klobuchar and campaign manager Julie Chavez Rodriguez.\par \par \uc2 We continue to see signs that Harris and Walz are posing a much stiffer challenge to Trump than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-08-29/election-2024-poll-harris-leads-or-ties-with-trump-in-swing-states?accessToken=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzb3VyY2UiOiJTdWJzY3JpYmVyR2lmdGVkQXJ0aWNsZSIsImlhdCI6MTcyNDk2NzM4OSwiZXhwIjoxNzI1NTcyMTg5LCJhcnRpY2xlSWQiOiJTSjAxMENUMEFGQjQwMCIsImJjb25uZWN0SWQiOiIxMzlDREUxRTMxNzc0RTM0QjVBQ0MxNDMwQzNCNjlENyJ9.54w3OwHMdvc-mhpuowBGnx9Ni2rLx-8mNe2Brpgf-zg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News/Morning Consult poll}}}\uc2  published yesterday shows Harris with the advantage in all seven swing states it surveyed, even North Carolina, which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t supported a Democrat since 2008. That said, it\u8217\'20\'19s only one poll, and others have shown her in a weaker position with voters in these states, most notably Pennsylvania, which is viewed as perhaps the deciding state this election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite his role in the overturning of Roe v Wade and his party\u8217\'20\'19s pursuit of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions nationwide, Trump tried to remake himself into a supporter of reproductive rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a rally yesterday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 We will hear more from Trump today, who will campaign in Johnstown, Pennsylvania at 4.30pm ET, and speak at a conference of conservative group Moms for Liberty at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris is back in Washington DC, and has no public events scheduled today. Expect speculation to grow in the coming days over when she will sit for her next interview.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240830ek8u001s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
