\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups warn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s row back on position risks losing votes\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,182 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 23:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican candidate\u8217\'20\'19s comments seen by Democrats as hypocritical \u8216\'20\'18sadden\u8217\'20\'19 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists\par \par \uc2 Over the last two weeks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has publicly backed away from multiple anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions \u8211\'20\'13 a move that Democrats see as hypocritical and that, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists warn, risks alienating voters who have long stood by him.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Trump said that, if elected, he would make the government or insurance companies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cover in vitro fertilization}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a type of fertility assistancethat some in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement want to see curtailed. Trump also seemed to indicate that he planned to vote in favor of a ballot measure to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Florida, which currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CI am going to be voting that we need more than six weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump told NBC News in an interview}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign quickly rushed to walk back his remarks on the ballot measure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/29/g-s1-20187/trump-ivf-funding-abortion-reproductive-rights-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling NPR}}}\uc2  that Trump simply meant that six weeks is too early in pregnancy to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump has not yet said how he will vote on the ballot initiative in Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D his press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, in comments to Fox News, Trump also clarified his position on a Florida amendment that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and overturn the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, saying he would vote against it. The Republican candidate had previously told NBC News that the six-week window is \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo short\u8221\'20\'1D, sparking confusion about his stance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think six weeks, you need more time than six weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said Friday, but added: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, the Democrats are radical because the nine months is just a ridiculous situation where you can do an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month \u8230\'20\'26 So I\u8217\'20\'19ll be voting no for that reason.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, in a decision backed by three justices that the former president appointed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/03/donald-trump-abortion-republicans-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has alternately bragged}}}\uc2  about toppling Roe and complained that outrage over its fall will cost Republicans elections. But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments on Thursday mark his latest attempt to apparently clarify and soften his stance on the controversial procedure. Last week, Trump also suggested that he would not use a 19th century anti-vice law to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, while his running mate, JD Vance, said the Republican presidential nominee would not sign a national ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it tells us necessarily what Trump is or isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to do, because he\u8217\'20\'19s still been leaving himself wiggle room on a lot of critical questions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  school of law who studies the legal history of reproduction. But, she continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat had been a strategy of \u8216\'20\'18be ambiguous and then hopefully be everything to everyone\u8217\'20\'19 has tilted more in the direction of Trump trying to assure voters that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new strategy comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , a far more effective champion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , has taken over as the Democratic nominee for president, and as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/2024-us-presidential-polls-harris-enthusiasm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls show}}}\uc2  the two candidates are neck and neck. But this strategy may leave anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters feeling less energized to vote for him, warned \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of the prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life of America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe pro-life movement didn\u8217\'20\'19t always have a firm place in the Republican party. For many years, we were at the little kids\u8217\'20\'19 table,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe young people that we work with, they don\u8217\'20\'19t remember that. And so they\u8217\'20\'19re absolutely shocked and saddened to see someone who they thought was pro-life, or who had always reaffirmed pro-life values, walking back on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement was a critical component of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s success in the 2016 presidential election, Republicans have tried to back away from it in the years since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have repeatedly won ballot measures even in red states. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sixty per cent of American adults}}}\uc2  believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/05/13/americans-overwhelmingly-say-access-to-ivf-is-a-good-thing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70% say}}}\uc2  access to IVF is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood thing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tresa Undem, who has polled people on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than 20 years, does not think that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments will necessarily win him the support of uncertain or independent voters who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Instead, he may be trying to reassure the segment of his base that also supports access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA third of his voters are pro-choice,\u8221\'20\'1D Undem said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn a recent survey we did, 16% of 2020 Trump voters say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a top five issue. So when you have an election that is probably going to be determined based on 1% of people, 16% of Trump voters saying their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is top in their mind \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s a problem for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats have cast Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new strategy, particularly his comments on IVF, as a sham. In a Friday press call organized by the Harris campaign, the Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren, a Democrat, repeatedly pointed out that Vance had voted against a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/right-to-ivf-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate bill to create federal protections for IVF}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump that thinks women are stupid and that we can be gaslighted,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe seems to believe he can do one thing when he talks to his extremist base and then turn around and smile at the overwhelming majority of Americans who want to see access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and IVF protected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the DNC is rolling out billboards in Pennsylvania, a critical battleground state, that slam Trump over IVF, according to a strategy shared exclusively with the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump overturned Roe, threatening the future of IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D one billboard reads. Another says: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 Undermines Reproductive Care and Threatens IVF.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, a playbook of conservative policies drawn up by the influential Heritage Foundation, contains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a long list of anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  proposals}}}\uc2 . Trump has tried to distance himself from it over the last several weeks.\par \par \uc2 At least one prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist, \uc2 Lila Rose\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2024/08/29/lila-rose-abortion-trump-interview-00176619"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly declared}}}\uc2  she currently does not plan to vote for Trump, given his recent turn away from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions. But Hawkins is still committed to getting people to vote for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 not because of Trump himself, but because she fears how a Harris presidency would strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t like it. It\u8217\'20\'19s not where I think we should be as a nation, but I think that we\u8217\'20\'19ve had to do this at times within the pro-life movement,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CFolks are asked: if you can\u8217\'20\'19t vote for a candidate, vote against the worst one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What Hawkins is less sure of is whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments will affect Students for Life\u8217\'20\'19s get out the vote program for the 2024 election. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it remains to be seen whether or not we\u8217\'20\'19re also talking about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the doors,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240830ek8u002jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
