\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinic offers \u8216\'20\'18hopeful\u8217\'20\'19 sanctuary for US south\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Petersburg, Virginia \par \uc2 1,522 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 15:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As a need for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics grows and laws toughen up, Virginia may be the last southern state left for providers\par \par \uc2 With her blond hair pulled into a braided ponytail, a small gold cross slung around her neck and decked out in teal scrubs covered in cartoon frogs, Brenda Morgan was polite but firm as she doled out instructions to her clinic employees.\par \par \uc2 People rarely pick up their phone if they don\u8217\'20\'19t recognize the number, so you\u8217\'20\'19ll probably have to leave a voicemail, Morgan advised a trio of staffers. When you leave that voicemail, she continued, never say you\u8217\'20\'19re calling from Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health. Instead, Morgan suggested they say something vague, like: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is Brenda from your doctor\u8217\'20\'19s office. Please give me a call back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The last thing they want is for the wrong person to hear the voicemail and realize an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is calling.\par \par \uc2 The staffers eyed the phones on the desk. Protecting a patient\u8217\'20\'19s privacy was paramount, but they had little time to perfect their voicemail technique. Less than 24 hours later, that clinic, the latest addition to the Whole Woman Health\u8217\'20\'19s network of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, would welcome its first patient.\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and allowed more than a dozen states to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban almost all abortions}}}\uc2 , more than 100 facilities have stopped providing abortions. New clinics have sprung up in states that still allow the procedure, but there are nowhere near enough to make up for those that shuttered. Many of those clinics are also in solidly liberal, northern states.\par \par \uc2 We opened this clinic because we know how many people are traveling from the region\par \par \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health founder\par \par \uc2 By contrast, Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health newest clinic \u8211\'20\'13 which quietly opened last week \u8211\'20\'13 is located in Petersburg, Virginia, within a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/31/virginia-abortion-rights-ban-south-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purplish state}}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/virginia-election-voting-results-house-delegates-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuked a GOP campaign}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/01/republicans-abortion-ads-virginia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  past 15 weeks}}}\uc2  in the 2023 elections but remains ruled by a Republican governor. In opening in Petersburg, a small city perhaps best known for being home to some of the American civil war\u8217\'20\'19s final battles, Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health is declaring a new front in a war that has again divided the US north from south: the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Virginia is likely the last southern state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can hope to open new clinics \u8211\'20\'13 and the need for southern, or southern-adjacent, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics has recently metastasized. On 1 May, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-takes-effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida banned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, decimating the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last southern stronghold of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 . Women from Florida and its neighboring states must now travel hundreds of miles for abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t open this only because of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , founder of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health. \u8220\'20\'1CWe opened this clinic because we know how many people are traveling from the region.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Probably should have given up earlier\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 For years, Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health was the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , where it ran a handful of clinics. In 2016, the organization {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/case/whole-womans-health-v-hellerstedt/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  case that toppled several Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions; at the time, the decision seemed to be a sign that the war over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was turning in their favor.\par \par \uc2 Eight years later, Roe is gone and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/08/texas-abortion-high-risk-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas has banned almost all abortions}}}\uc2 . Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health has closed its Texas clinics, as well as another clinic in Indiana, which has also outlawed the procedure.\par \par \uc2 It was devastating \u8211\'20\'13 emotionally and financially. It took more than a year for Hagstrom Miller to sell buildings where her clinics had operated. ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/11/04/texas-abortion-clinic-pregnancy-crisis-center/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  group later bought}}}\uc2  one of the buildings.) Getting out of one lease, she said, cost tens of thousands of dollars.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose operational things are real. They can take down \u8211\'20\'13 I mean, they almost did take down \u8211\'20\'13 one of the most stable, independent providers in the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hagstrom Miller, who likes to dress as loud as her politics. The day before the Petersburg clinic opened, she wore a chartreuse suit and a necklace that read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. The underside of her silvery hair was dyed a searing purple \u8211\'20\'13 a signature shade of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, whose walls are usually painted in mauve hues.\par \par \uc2 Hagstrom Miller continued: \u8220\'20\'1CI had to spend our organization\u8217\'20\'19s reserves to do all that stuff, which kept me from being able to open something in Kansas or figure out how to help people in southern Illinois.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I am absolutely terrified for Trump to get re-elected. I have to plan for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\par \par \uc2 Over the last several months, Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health has tried to start multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. One, in New Mexico, successfully opened. But Hagstrom Miller purchased a building in Oklahoma \u8211\'20\'13 right before the state banned the procedure. \u8220\'20\'1CI still have that building,\u8221\'20\'1D Hagstrom Miller said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been playing a mortgage on that building for \u8211\'20\'13 I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even tell you how long it\u8217\'20\'19s been.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also bought a practice from a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/10/abortion-ban-north-carolina-decrease#:~:text=Abortions%20in%20North%20Carolina%20drop,data%20shows%20%7C%20Abortion%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  provider but spent a year battling state regulations before having to concede that the clinic would never open.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProbably should have given up earlier,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CNot so good at that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A few weeks later, North Carolina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/north-carolina-abortion-ban-veto-override"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Morgan was part of these efforts. For the last two years, she has hopscotched across the country, closing and setting up clinics as the director of growth and acquisitions for Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health. During a tour of the clinic, Morgan pointed out pieces of equipment that had been repurposed from former Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health locations: black chairs in the waiting room, blush-colored surgical trays, a chair where patients get their blood drawn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it could talk, it would tell you many, many stories,\u8221\'20\'1D Morgan said of an exam bed from San Antonio, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Hanging in the waiting room, greeting patients as they walk in the door, is a royal purple sign bearing the \u8220\'20\'1CMISSION STATEMENT\u8221\'20\'1D of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, which reads, in part: \u8220\'20\'1CWe honor women\u8217\'20\'19s hopes, dreams and intentions in all of the care that we provide.\u8221\'20\'1D Morgan stroked a finger down the sign, noting where the purple paint had faded away to reveal white underneath. The sign originally hung in a Texas clinic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love the fact that it has some dings in it, because it\u8217\'20\'19s just like us,\u8221\'20\'1D Morgan said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s stood the duration of time, but it also has taken its little nicks and bruises, as we have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I have to plan\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s first day of operation, one woman flew in from Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was so sweet and so grateful,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Meera Shah, the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s medical director. \u8220\'20\'1CIt made me angry that she had to even do that, that she had to leave Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In her other job, as the chief medical officer of a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  affiliate in New York state, Shah said she has treated numerous patients fleeing southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws \u8211\'20\'13 including one Florida woman who had an ectopic pregnancy, a nonviable pregnancy where the embryo implants outside of the uterus. If left untreated, ectopic pregnancies can rupture women\u8217\'20\'19s fallopian tubes, leading them to hemorrhage and even die.\par \par \uc2 Theoretically, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans should not apply to ectopic pregnancies. But the woman had been turned away from a Florida emergency room because, Shah said, a doctor found the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws \u8220\'20\'1Cconfusing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, she could have ruptured,\u8221\'20\'1D Shah said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe zip code in which you live really determines the type of healthcare that you\u8217\'20\'19ll receive. And it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By the weekend, the Petersburg clinic had helped another another three people \u8211\'20\'13 from Florida, Georgia and Alabama \u8211\'20\'13 get abortions. Eventually, Morgan expects the clinic to serve about 30 to 50 patients a week.\par \par \uc2 The upcoming 2024 elections, however, may scramble these plans, especially as southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are still in flux. Floridians will vote on a ballot measure that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/florida-abortion-democrats-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restore \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 , but it needs 60% of the vote to pass. In North Carolina, a Republican who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/17/politics/kfile-mark-robinson-abortion-ban-no-exceptions/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D is now running for governor. He has tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wunc.org/2024-08-21/mark-robinsons-softening-abortion-stance-splits-some-in-his-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soften his position on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  recently but if he wins, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s state government could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely.\par \par \uc2 The same week the Petersburg clinic opened, Donald Trump pledged not to use a 19th-century anti-vice law to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, while his running mate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/elizabeth-warren-jd-vance-nationwide-abortion-ban-veto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance said}}}\uc2  Trump would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. But Project 2025, an influential blueprint for a conservative presidential administration, has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long list of anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  proposals}}}\uc2 . Trump could also renege on his promise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling much more engaged and hopeful than I have felt in a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D Hagstrom Miller said. \u8220\'20\'1CI also am absolutely terrified for Trump to get re-elected and I have to plan for that contingency. I have to plan for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240830ek8u001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
