\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris defends stance on Israel-Gaza, US border and fracking in interview \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 5,690 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 04:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full story on the Harris-Walz interview on CNN here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thank you for following. You can read our full story on the interview at the link below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris defends policy stances and shares plan for office in first major interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has responded to that interview on Truth Social, posting one word as the interview ended: \u8220\'20\'1CBORING!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: Harris says her values have not changed\par \par \uc2 In a primetime spot on CNN Thursday evening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  sat for their first interview together as the Democratic ticket, taking questions from anchor Dana Bash on a range of important issues, including their plans for day 1 if they win the race, the approach to the war in Gaza, and how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  passed the baton.\par \par \uc2 Bash pushed Harris on how voters should view some key shifts on important policy positions over the years, including on immigration and the climate crisis. Harris responded resolutely saying her \u8220\'20\'1Cvalues have not changed\u8221\'20\'1D but explained that experience has provided some new insights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs president I will not ban fracking,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, reversing a position she expressed during her first bid for the presidency. Explaining that she now believes a \u8220\'20\'1Cthriving clean energy economy\u8221\'20\'1D can be built without a ban, Harris highlighted achievements from the Biden administration, including the US\u8217\'20\'19s landmark climate bill, the Inflation Reduction Act, that have helped set the course. \u8220\'20\'1CThe climate crisis is real, it is an urgent matter,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am very clear about where I stand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also spoke about her work on the border and how she plans to address the immigration crisis. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe we have laws that have to be followed and enforced,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that she is the only person in the race who has prosecuted transnational criminal organizations, work she did as California\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Next question, please\u8217\'20\'19 and Gaza war: key takeaways from Harris and Walz\u8217\'20\'19s first interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  sat for her first interview as the Democratic presidential nominee with CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash alongside her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , on Thursday, and defended her shifts on certain policy issues over the years and her support for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the interview, which was taped from Savannah, Georgia, earlier Thursday, the vice-president said her highest priority upon taking office would be to \u8220\'20\'1Csupport and strengthen the middle class\u8221\'20\'1D through policies including increasing the child tax credit, curtailing price gouging on everyday goods and increasing access to affordable housing \u8211\'20\'13 all policies that she has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  since she started campaigning for the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Harris also shared how the president shared with her his decision not to continue running for re-election, a first public retelling of that moment. She said she was making breakfast with her family, including her nieces, and was just sitting down to do a puzzle when the phone rang, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI asked him, are you sure? And he said yes. And that\u8217\'20\'19s how I learned about it.\u8221\'20\'1D As far as whether she asked for his endorsement or he offered it, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe was very clear that he was going to support me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy first thought was not about me, to be honest with you, my first thought was about him,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that history will remember Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency as transformative.\par \par \uc2 Harris defended Biden, saying she had no regrets about supporting his re-election before his decision to leave the race, despite concerns over his age and acuity. She said serving as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president has been \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the greatest honors\u8221\'20\'1D of her career and that Biden has the \u8220\'20\'1Cintelligence, commitment, judgement and disposition that the American people deserve in their president\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the former president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Chas none of that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m the best person to do this job\u8217\'20\'19: Harris gives first major interview of campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am BST\par \par \uc2 At a town hall event in La Crosse, Wisconsin, on Thursday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and former Democratic congressperson \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , now a Trump campaign surrogate, attempted to pitch themselves to the crowd as supporters of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard, who moderated the event after endorsing the former president earlier this week, opened the town hall with emotional remarks about her experience with in vitro fertilization. The comments came shortly after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804?cid=eml_nbn_20240829&user_email=44c11d5d46c3757ec95f4420aa14bc672186d4206f29a3824bba58589834f455&utm_campaign=breakingnews&%243p=e_sailthru&_branch_match_id=1308400092925361144&utm_medium=Email%20Sailthru&_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAAzVP7WrDMAx8muyf28QfqTMoYzD2GkGxnVQ0VoztNOztpwwGAulOukP3qDWV9%2BuVJkfhKBdI6bIiPa8qfTRSq3QPYwFc6yPvb0xsGRckWMc9r%2FfHKW7UZyO%2FuY7juPzbuC0yk7YVK7rCo99Y5EXNe0wM%2F7oo8FPEAVSLiPAMAl8zXwSoMZxcAvRi2V4h00kIpLJnIBcE2ycgFNkRdL21rW7Ut0PfqK8Q15EmGmUrdWvl0Mh%2BLyGPIXIK3mvtus4br3unbuYW3GBmrWUL0OnJ9TfZ2d4z7mc5gLJSTxMYa%2BxglZ61MadfjaMD%2FgAXYseJP34iLWfwXzF7KTJPAQAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in an NBC interview}}}\uc2  that he would make the government or insurance companies pay for IVF if he\u8217\'20\'19s elected, although it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how he would accomplish that or if he\u8217\'20\'19s serious about the proposal given the pivotal role he played in overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Alice Herman reports:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/trump-ivf-tulsi-gabbard-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We wanna produce babies\u8217\'20\'19: Trump tries to pitch himself as IVF supporter after Roe fall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from Harris-Walz interview\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the key lines from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s CNN interview, their first since Harris became the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked what she would do on day one in the White House if she was elected, Harris said that she would focus on her\u8220\'20\'1Copportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D plan to bring down the cost of everyday goods.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she would not ban fracking if she became president. Asked why she had changed her previous position on fracking, Harris said \u8220\'20\'1Cmy values have not changed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked why the Biden administration did not act sooner to cut down on border crossings, Harris side-stepped the question and instead blamed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for telling his allies to kill a bipartisan border bill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she believes \u8220\'20\'1Cthere should be consequence\u8221\'20\'1D to illegal border crossings, a change in her position from 2020 when she agreed with a statement that illegal border crossings should be decriminalized.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she would name a Republican to her cabinet if she was elected to the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insulting claim that she \u8220\'20\'1Cturned Black\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris replied: \u8220\'20\'1C Same old, tired playbook. Next question, please.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris did not express any policy differences from Biden on the issue of the US\u8217\'20\'19s position on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. Harris said she is \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocal and unwavering in my commitment to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defense and its ability to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not going to change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Walz clarified previous statements he made about his military service and the infertility treatment his wife underwent in becoming pregnant with their children.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she was sitting down to do a puzzle with her nieces when she found out that Biden was stepping aside. \u8220\'20\'1CThe phone rang. And it was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And \u8211\'20\'13 and he told me what he had decided to do. And \u8211\'20\'13 I asked him, \u8216\'20\'18Are you sure?\u8217\'20\'19 And he said, \u8216\'20\'18Yes.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , at a town hall event in La Crosse, Wisconsin, repeated his usual talking points on immigration and the economy.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question about job opportunities for young people, Trump blamed immigrants, saying there had been \u8220\'20\'1Cno job creation\u8221\'20\'1D from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/17/politics/fact-check-donald-trump-jobs-biden-immigration/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsely claiming}}}\uc2  that all new jobs \u8220\'20\'1Cwere filled by illegal immigrants\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , a former Democratic congressperson turned Trump campaign surrogate, denounced \u8220\'20\'1Cwarmongers\u8221\'20\'1D and set up Trump to riff on the topic of foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 As he frequently does, Trump praised \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian prime minister, and told the audience that Orb\u225\'00\'E1n \u8220\'20\'1Csaid you have to bring Trump back as president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump promised later in the evening to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring back that level of respect\u8221\'20\'1D from foreign adversaries, which he claimed he enjoyed during his first term.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 At a town hall event in La Crosse, Wisconsin, on Thursday night, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and former Democratic congressperson \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , now a Trump campaign surrogate, attempted to pitch themselves to the crowd as supporters of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard, who moderated the event after endorsing the former president earlier this week, opened the town hall with emotional remarks about her experience with in vitro fertilization. The comments came shortly after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-says-wants-make-ivf-treatments-paid-government-insurance-compani-rcna168804?cid=eml_nbn_20240829&user_email=44c11d5d46c3757ec95f4420aa14bc672186d4206f29a3824bba58589834f455&utm_campaign=breakingnews&%243p=e_sailthru&_branch_match_id=1308400092925361144&utm_medium=Email%20Sailthru&_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAAzVP7WrDMAx8muyf28QfqTMoYzD2GkGxnVQ0VoztNOztpwwGAulOukP3qDWV9%2BuVJkfhKBdI6bIiPa8qfTRSq3QPYwFc6yPvb0xsGRckWMc9r%2FfHKW7UZyO%2FuY7juPzbuC0yk7YVK7rCo99Y5EXNe0wM%2F7oo8FPEAVSLiPAMAl8zXwSoMZxcAvRi2V4h00kIpLJnIBcE2ycgFNkRdL21rW7Ut0PfqK8Q15EmGmUrdWvl0Mh%2BLyGPIXIK3mvtus4br3unbuYW3GBmrWUL0OnJ9TfZ2d4z7mc5gLJSTxMYa%2BxglZ61MadfjaMD%2FgAXYseJP34iLWfwXzF7KTJPAQAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in an NBC interview}}}\uc2  that he would make the government or insurance companies pay for IVF if he\u8217\'20\'19s elected, although it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how he would accomplish that or if he\u8217\'20\'19s serious about the proposal given the pivotal role he played in overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were not successful in trying to get pregnant. For us, IVF seemed to be the only option and the last resort,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gabbard, who described to a quiet audience the costly and at times painful fertility treatment process she said she underwent 10 years ago.\par \par \uc2 Following Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s comments on IVF, Trump reiterated his promise from earlier in the day. Trump said:\par \par \uc2 We wanna produce babies in this country, right?\par \par \uc2 By stating his support for IVF and claiming that he would leave \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to the states if elected, Trump is hoping to retain the support of women who count reproductive rights as a top issue \u8211\'20\'13 but risks alienating his supporters on the religious right.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/29/politics/harris-walz-interview-read-transcript/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  a full transcript of its interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The interview was Harris\u8217\'20\'19s first since ascending to the top of the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump asks federal court to take over hush-money criminal case\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  filed a petition seeking a federal court to intervene in his New York hush-money criminal case, in an attempt to overturn his felony conviction and indefinitely delay his sentencing scheduled for next month.\par \par \uc2 In a petition filed late on Thursday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued that the prosecution violated the former president\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rights and ran afoul of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s recent ruling on presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 If the case is moved to federal court, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers wrote, they will then seek to have the verdict overturned and the case dismissed.\par \par \uc2 If the case remains in state court, with sentencing proceeding as scheduled, it could amount to election interference, they said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has never met or spoken with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in person, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash noted in the interview.\par \par \uc2 Aside from attending Trump\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union addresses during his time as president, Harris has never been in the same room as him, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had just one thing to say about his opponents\u8217\'20\'19 CNN interview:\par \par \uc2 enltrOne viewer\u8217\'20\'19s feedback: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kwtyab3ldB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Kwtyab3ldB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Wingrove (@josh_wingrove) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/josh_wingrove/status/1829337437409042890?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says he is 'so proud' of son Gus when asked about emotional moment at convention\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is asked about the moment during the Democratic national convention when his son, Gus, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/tim-walz-son-gus-crying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was seen tearing up and saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s my dad.\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\par \par \uc2 Walz says it was important to have his son \u8220\'20\'1Cfeel a sense of pride\u8221\'20\'1D that he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to do the right thing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You try to protect your kids, you know it brings notoriety and things but it was such a visceral emotional moment. I\u8217\'20\'19m grateful I got to experience and I\u8217\'20\'19m so proud of him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris recounts moment \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told her he was dropping out of race\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked to discuss the moment she learned \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was stepping aside from the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Harris says she was with her family at the time, including her baby nieces and had just had pancakes and bacon. She says:\par \par \uc2 The phone rang and it was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and he told me what he had decided to do and I asked him, \u8216\'20\'18Are you sure?\u8217\'20\'19 And he said \u8216\'20\'18yes\u8217\'20\'19 and that\u8217\'20\'19s how I learned about it.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether she asked for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Harris says the president \u8220\'20\'1Cwas very clear that he was going to support me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She says that when Biden called her, her first thought \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not about me\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CMy first thought was about him, to be honest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she has no regrets defending Biden's ability to serve\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked if she has any regrets about previously telling the American people about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s capacity to serve another four years as president.\par \par \uc2 Harris says \u8220\'20\'1Cnot at all\u8221\'20\'1D, and that serving with Biden has been \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the greatest honors of my career\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Ccares so deeply about the American people\u8221\'20\'1D, and is \u8220\'20\'1Cso smart and loyal\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris says.\par \par \uc2 He has the intelligence, the commitment, judgment and disposition that I think the American people rightly deserve in their president. By contrast, the former president has none of that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  says that Republicans are either attacking him for his children \u8220\'20\'1Cfor showing love\u8221\'20\'1D or it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Can attack on my dog\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Walz is also asked to clarify earlier statements he made about his family\u8217\'20\'19s experiences using in vitro fertilization to conceive a child.\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Gwen Walz, earlier this month said that she did not use in vitro fertilization to conceive, but rather a different fertility treatment called intrauterine insemination (IUI).\par \par \uc2 Walz tells CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash that he spoke about his and his wife\u8217\'20\'19s infertility issues \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it\u8217\'20\'19s hell, and families know this\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I spoke about the treatments that were available to us \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s quite a contrast in folks that are trying to take those rights away from us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says his military record 'speaks for itself'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is asked to clarify previous comments he and his campaign has made about his time serving in the army national guard.\par \par \uc2 In a 2018 video clip, Walz spoke out about against gun violence and said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe can make sure that those weapons of war, that I carried in war, is the only place where those weapons are at.\u8221\'20\'1D He subsequently apologized and said it was a misstatement.\par \par \uc2 Walz was in the army national guard for 24 years, in infantry and artillery, deploying in response to natural disasters on US soil and to Europe in support of operations in Afghanistan. He retired in 2005, to run for Congress, shortly before his unit deployed to Iraq.\par \par \uc2 Walz says he is \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly proud\u8221\'20\'1D of the 24 years he served wearing the uniform of this country and that his record \u8220\'20\'1Cspeaks for itself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He tells CNN that he speaks \u8220\'20\'1Ccandidly\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he wears his \u8220\'20\'1Cemotions on my sleeves\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CMy record has been out there for over 40 years,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked about a previous policy position from 2019, when she agreed with a statement that illegal border crossings should be decriminalized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe there should be consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D she told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash.\par \par \uc2 We have laws that have to be followed and enforced that address and deal with people across our border illegally, and there should be consequences.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris reiterates commitment to Israel's right to defend itself and push for Gaza ceasefire\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked if she would do anything differently than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the US\u8217\'20\'19s position on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Harris says she is \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocal and unwavering\u8221\'20\'1D in her \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitment to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defense and its ability to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not gonna change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She says \u8220\'20\'1Cfar too many innocent Palestinians have been killed\u8221\'20\'1D, and that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have got to get a deal done\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This war must end, and we must get a deal that is about getting the hostages out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Trump's comments on her racial identity are 'same old tired playbook'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s questioning of her racial identity, to which she responds that it is part of the \u8220\'20\'1Csame old tired playbook\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During a panel hosted by the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) last month, Trump questioned Harris\u8217\'20\'19s race, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe was always of Indian heritage, and she was only promoting Indian heritage. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know she was Black until a number of years ago, when she happened to turn Black.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she would appoint a Republican in her cabinet\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expressed openness to appointing a Republican into her cabinet. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got 68 days to go with this election, so I\u8217\'20\'19m not putting the cart before the horse,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told CNN.\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s really important. I have spent my career inviting diversity of opinion. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s important to have people at the table when some of the most important decisions are being made that have different views, different experiences. And I think it would be to the benefit of the American public to have a member of my cabinet who was a Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris accuses Trump of killing bipartisan border bill for political gain\par \par \uc2 On the subject of immigration, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of killing a bipartisan border bill earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked why the Biden administration waited more than three years to implement sweeping asylum instructions. Harris side-stepped the question, and said:\par \par \uc2 Trump got word of this bill that would have contributed to securing our border and because he believed it would not have helped him politically, he told his folks in Congress, \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t put it forward.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  acknowledged that \u8220\'20\'1Cprices, in particular for groceries, are still too high\u8221\'20\'1D as she pointed to the progress that she and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made on the economy.\par \par \uc2 The economy had crashed \u8211\'20\'13 in large part all of that because of mismanagement by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of that crisis. When we came in, our highest priority was to do what we could to rescue America.\par \par \uc2 Harris noted her proposal for the first-ever federal ban on price gouging on food and groceries, as well as her plan to provide up to $25,000 in down payment assistance for first-time homeowners.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says her values 'have not changed' despite policy reversals\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is asked to explain why her positions have changed on policies such as fracking and decriminalizing illegal border crossings.\par \par \uc2 Harris says \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear \u8211\'20\'13 my values have not changed\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 I think the most important and most significant aspect of my policy perspective and decisions is my values have not changed. You mentioned the Green New Deal. I have always believed \u8211\'20\'13 and I have worked on it \u8211\'20\'13 that the climate crisis is real, that it is an urgent matter to which we should apply metrics that include holding ourselves to deadlines around time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she will not ban fracking\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash says fracking is an important issue in the key battleground state of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 She points to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s previous statements where she said she was in favor of banning fracking. Does Harris still want to ban fracking? Harris says:\par \par \uc2 No, and I made that clear on the debate stage in 2020 that I would not ban fracking. As vice-president, I did not ban fracking. As president, I will not ban fracking.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  says he is \u8220\'20\'1Cexcited\u8221\'20\'1D about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda about implementing an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Walz says he shares many of the same values as Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she would bring 'down the cost of everyday goods'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says that on day one of being in the White House, she would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cimplementing my plan for what I call an opportunity economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She says she has already laid out a number of proposals in that regard, including what she will do to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring down the cost of everyday goods\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cto invest in America\u8217\'20\'19s small businesses\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Cto invest in families\u8221\'20\'1D, including extending the child tax credit to $6,000 for families for the first year of their child\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 Harris pledges to focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cinvesting in the American family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash tells \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that she has less time to make her case to voters than any candidate in modern American history.\par \par \uc2 Harris is asked what she would do on day one in the White House if she wins the November election.\par \par \uc2 Harris says \u8220\'20\'1Ca number of things\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 First and foremost, one of my highest priorities, is to do what we can to support and strengthen the middle class.\par \par \uc2 Harris says the American people \u8220\'20\'1Care ready for a new way forward\u8221\'20\'1D and to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz appear on CNN\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , are now appearing on CNN in their first joint interview since becoming the Democratic presidential and vice-presidential nominees.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz spoke to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash at Kim\u8217\'20\'19s Cafe in Savannah, Georgia, in an interview that was taped earlier today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  addressed a boisterous crowd during a campaign rally in Savannah, Georgia, earlier today and told them that despite the state being a stretch, it is still winnable in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t pay attention to polls \u8211\'20\'13 we are underdogs,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, telling the roughly 9,500 attendees that they had \u8220\'20\'1Cwork to do\u8221\'20\'1D in order to secure victory.\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t mind hard work. Hard work is for workers.\par \par \uc2 Thousands waited outside for hours as a spitting rain became a steady drizzle, which turned into an outright downpour, on a hot and characteristically humid Savannah afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Inside, thousands of supporters filled out an arena usually reserved for minor league hockey games and concerts \u8211\'20\'13 taking up every last seat.\par \par \uc2 Harris, speaking after two days on a bus tour through south-east Georgia with her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back in Savannah,\u8221\'20\'1D before jumping right into a stump speech that, while familiar, nonetheless kept the crowd\u8217\'20\'19s attention for the entirety of her remarks.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/kamala-harris-savannah-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris tells Georgia crowd she will put \u8216\'20\'18working class families first\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has clarified that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chas not yet said how he will vote\u8221\'20\'1D on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment on the ballot in Florida this November.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in an interview with NBC News earlier today, was asked whether he would vote to repeal his home state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was signed into law by the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , last year. Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 I think the six week is too short, there has to be more time \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19ve told them I want more weeks.\par \par \uc2 enltr"I think the six week is too short, there has to be more time," former President Trump says how he'll vote on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment in Florida. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rQAdPtW9i0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rQAdPtW9i0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC Politics (@NBCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCPolitics/status/1829264988269101277?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 According to a statement by Karoline Leavitt, the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary:\par \par \uc2 President Trump has not yet said how he will vote on the ballot initiative in Florida, he simply reiterated that he believes six weeks is too short.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is clearly still not over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/aug/06/tim-walz-on-calling-donald-trump-weird-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being called \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , instead accusing the Minnesota governor and Democratic vice-presidential nominee, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , of the same label.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a weird guy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump tells supporters at the town hall event in La Crosse, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Trump says his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , is also \u8220\'20\'1Cnot weird\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s not weird and I\u8217\'20\'19m not weird. I mean, we\u8217\'20\'19re a lot of things, but that guy [Walz] is weird.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cown platform could effectively ban [in vitro fertilization] and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D, a spokesperson for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest IVF comments.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign statement continued:\par \par \uc2 Because Trump overturned Roe v. Wade, IVF is already under attack and women\u8217\'20\'19s freedoms have been ripped away in states across the country. There is only one candidate in this race who trusts women and will protect our freedom to make our own health care decisions: Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Alabama state supreme court ruled earlier this year that embryos created via IVF were to be considered people. As a result, the state\u8217\'20\'19s three major IVF providers paused services, as patients in Alabama reported that upcoming embryo transfers had been abruptly cancelled and their paths to parenthood put in doubt.\par \par \uc2 Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , then signed into law legislation that would shield IVF providers from the fallout of the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 The head of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, a group dedicated to electing Democratic candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, mocked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66d1110d8f08f4abbe22c682#block-66d1110d8f08f4abbe22c682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/29/cnn-harris-walz-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66d1110d8f08f4abbe22c682#block-66d1110d8f08f4abbe22c682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 s comments}}}\uc2  that he wanted to make the government or insurance companies pay for in vitro fertilization treatments.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Mackler, the president of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, said in a statement shared by NBC News:\par \par \uc2 Congratulations to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for realizing that his position and his record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are wildly unpopular, particularly with women who will decide this election.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 But rather than give him credit for a disingenuous and unserious proposal that contradicts his own GOP platform, we\u8217\'20\'19ll credit him for something he actually did: overturning Roe v Wade, ending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for millions of women across the country, and jeopardizing reproductive freedom for all of us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic congresswoman for Hawaii, starts off the town hall event by discussing her struggle to conceive a child through in vitro fertilization (IVF).\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tells Gabbard that her situation sounds like \u8220\'20\'1Ctough stuff\u8221\'20\'1D and that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery much for\u8221\'20\'1D IVF.\par \par \uc2 At a campaign event in Potterville, Michigan, earlier this evening, Trump said he would require the government or insurance companies to pay for IVF fertility treatments if he is elected in November.\par \par \uc2 In remarks likely aimed at appealing to women and suburban voters, Trump told supporters in Michigan:\par \par \uc2 Your government will pay for or your insurance company will be mandated to pay for all costs associated with IVF treatment fertilization for women.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on stage at Wisconsin town hall event\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is on stage, enjoying a prolonged standing ovation.\par \par \uc2 The former president will hear questions during a town hall event here in La Crosse, Wisconsin, which former Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , will moderate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-Democrat \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  introduces Trump at town hall event\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has taken the stage in La Crosse, Wisconsin, where she will moderate a town hall event with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tonight, to wild applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo former Democratic candidates have endorsed \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  to be president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gabbard, referring to herself and \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , who both endorsed Trump this week.\par \par \uc2 I am so excited about the opportunity that we have before us to stand together not as Democrats or Republicans, but as proud Americans who love this great country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters lined up for blocks to see the Republican presidential nominee at a town hall in La Crosse, Wisconsin, even as he was speaking at a campaign event in Michigan earlier.\par \par \uc2 I spoke with Michelle Thiessen, a 56-year-old nurse from the La Crosse area who said that her top issue is keeping the US out of foreign conflicts, and sees Trump as the candidate most likely to do that.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said, would be his toughest issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLots of women are flipping because of that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thiessen, who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and said she does not believe Trump will allow for a nationwide ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris pledges to appoint a Republican to her cabinet\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  promised to name a Republican to serve in her cabinet if elected.\par \par \uc2 In her first major interview since becoming the Democratic nominee, the vice-president told CNN journalist Dana Bash that she had spent her career \u8220\'20\'1Cinviting diversity of opinion\u8221\'20\'1D. Harris said:\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s important to have people at the table when some of the most important decisions are being made that have different views, different experiences. And I think it would be to the benefit of the American public to have a member of my Cabinet who was a Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, CNN released a first clip of the interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , in which the vice-president said that her values have not changed.\par \par \uc2 CNN journalist Dana Bash asked Harris what voters should make of the changes to some of her policy positions. Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Dana, I think the most important and most significant aspect of my policy perspective and decisions is my values have not changed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou mentioned the Green New Deal. I have always believed that the climate crisis is real, that it is an urgent matter to which we should apply metrics that include holding ourselves to deadlines around time,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe did that with the Inflation Reduction Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 My value around what we need to do to secure our border \u8211\'20\'13 that value has not changed. I spent two terms as the attorney general of California prosecuting transnational criminal organizations, violations of American laws regarding the illegal passage of guns, drugs and human beings across our border. My values have not changed.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn an exclusive interview, CNN's Dana Bash presses Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on why her policies have changed over the years. The full interview will air at 9 p.m. ET Thursday on CNN's "The First Interview: Harris & Walz, A CNN Exclusive."\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JYgHvcXZMd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JYgHvcXZMd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CNN (@CNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1829261939333120477?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to answer questions in Wisconsin town hall event\par \par \uc2 There aren\u8217\'20\'19t many open seats at the La Crosse Center, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to answer questions at a town hall event moderated by former Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  later this evening.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard, who announced her support for Trump this week, could earn Trump support from voters such as Melissa Nelson, an attendee sitting near me at the event in a \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  for President T-shirt.\par \par \uc2 Nelson told me she voted for \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  in the 2016 primary, supported Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s run in 2020, and is reluctantly throwing her support behind Trump this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democratic Party is going downhill,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nelson, who cited healthcare and disability benefits as her top issues. Gabbard\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Nelson said, \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of pushed me over the edge, for sure, that I was gonna vote for Trump. Otherwise I would have voted for Jill Stein.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to give first major TV interview since nomination\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will give her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/kamala-harris-walz-cnn-interview-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first major interview}}}\uc2  since becoming the Democratic presidential nominee in a few hours \u8211\'20\'13 in what is being seen as a key test of her credibility after a prolonged honeymoon during which she surged ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 She and her running mate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  , will face CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Dana Bash in a pre-recorded interview due to be aired at 9pm ET. It was scheduled following some criticism of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s reluctance to expose herself to media scrutiny following her ascent to the top of the Democratic ticket last month in place of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  , who withdrew from the race on 21 July.\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president, who has had a variable performance in past televised one-on-ones, had previously pledged to hold a major interview before the end of August.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering the interview and bring you all the latest updates and reaction. So stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/kamala-harris-walz-cnn-interview-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How to watch the Harris-Walz interview with CNN}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240830ek8u0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
