\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Vance attacks Biden-Harris economic record in Wisconsin rally \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Dani Anguiano ,Chris Stein and Anna Betts (earlier) \par \uc2 7,383 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 August 2024\par 00:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can find all of our US elections coverage here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for today\u8217\'20\'19s live politics coverage. This blog is closing \u8211\'20\'13 you can find the full Arlington cemetery story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/trump-arlington-cemetery-visit-altercation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump staffers reported over altercation at Arlington cemetery during photo op}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says that Harris has \u8220\'20\'1Cfake hope\u8221\'20\'1D. He urges people to vote and bring people who can\u8217\'20\'19t make it in person on their own to the polls. There is a short cheer as he leaves the stage. People wave signs for a moment, then check their phones, chat amongst each other, and start to leave.\par \par \uc2 It is a very different energy from the Harris and Walz campaign events.\par \par \uc2 Here is what building materials manufacturer Amerilux International, where Vance spoke, looked less than a minute after he finished:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance is asked by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  about Arlington national cemetery.\par \par \uc2 Officials at Arlington national cemetery have filed a report over the behavior of members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign staff who reportedly shoved and verbally abused an employee during a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrass\u8221\'20\'1D photo opportunity for the Republican presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Following the wreath-laying, photographs from his visit showed Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NoLieWithBTC/status/1828580120023511467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grinning and flashing a thumbs-up sign}}}\uc2  as he stood at the graves of several of the fallen military members, imagery that drew swift rebuke.\par \par \uc2 The journalist at the Vance event in Wisconsin points out that the Trump campaign said it had permission to film, but that there is a federal ban on doing so at cemeteries like Arlington. The journalist asks whether Vance thinks presidents should have to obey laws.\par \par \uc2 Vance says the media acts like Trump wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cfilm an ad at a gravesite\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vance essentially says that the people whose loved ones are buried there wanted Trump to film there.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Arlington acknowledged one of its representatives became involved in the altercation with two Trump staffers, telling them that only cemetery representatives were allowed to take video and photographs in Section 60, an area where recent US casualties mostly from Iraq and Afghanistan are buried.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFederal law prohibits political campaign or election-related activities within Army National Military Cemeteries, to include photographers, content creators or any other persons attending for purposes, or in direct support of a partisan political candidate\u8217\'20\'19s campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Ca report was filed\u8221\'20\'1D over the incident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArlington National Cemetery reinforced and widely shared this law and its prohibitions with all participants,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/trump-arlington-cemetery-visit-altercation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump staffers reported over altercation at Arlington cemetery during photo op}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 On those comments about RFK Jr, via the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Patrick Marley:\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance blames \u8220\'20\'1Cbureaucrats\u8221\'20\'1D for keeping RFK Jr. on the ballot in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The election commission\u8217\'20\'19s vote to keep him on the ballot was 5-1, with two Republicans in favor, including one who was appointed to the commission by the speaker of the state Assembly. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yi5S4Uo0G4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yi5S4Uo0G4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patrick Marley (@patrickdmarley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/patrickdmarley/status/1828938541524480341?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance is asked what he wants when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He says it is up to states to decide, and quickly pivots to fentanyl and the border.\par \par \uc2 He then says that Harris wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cforce her radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies down the throats of the American people\u8221\'20\'1D. He gets one of the loudest cheers of the night, and decides to continue.\par \par \uc2 He says that Harris is \u8220\'20\'1Canti-family\u8221\'20\'1D. He says, \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to start a family if you can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to buy a home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s have a pro-family country, let\u8217\'20\'19s make it easy to bring new life into this world, and let\u8217\'20\'19s make a pro-family America, that\u8217\'20\'19s our vision and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to fight for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Project 2025 document says it aims to \u8220\'20\'1Cdelete the term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D along with other terms, end federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate central promotion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  health services,\u8221\'20\'1D and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication including the Plan B pill.\par \par \uc2 Trump and his campaign have worked to distance the candidate from the project, which was put together by the conservative thinktank \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . But many of the authors and groups behind the project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have Trump ties}}}\uc2 , and the policy goals often align with things Trump has said he intends to do if he wins again.\par \par \uc2 Here is some other actual text from Project 2025:\par \par \uc2 The Life Agenda.\par \par \uc2 The Office of the Secretary should eliminate the \uc2 HHS\uc2  Reproductive Healthcare Access Task Force and install a pro-life task force to ensure that all of the department\u8217\'20\'19s divisions seek to use their authority to promote the life and health of women and their unborn children. Additionally, \uc2 HHS\uc2  should return to being known as the Department of Life by explicitly rejecting the notion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is health care and by restoring its mission statement under the Strategic Plan and elsewhere to include furthering the health and well-being of all Americans \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom conception to natural death.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance is asked about claims made by Democrats that Trump has wealthy Americans\u8217\'20\'19 interests at hard \u8211\'20\'13 something borne out by his tax cuts for the super rich \u8211\'20\'13 and starts to talk about how he grew up in poverty.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe if you work hard and play by the rules \u8230\'20\'26 you ought to be able to turn your heater on in winter,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He says that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s energy policies will mean the \u8220\'20\'1Clittle guy\u8221\'20\'1D can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to heat their homes. He accuses her of being the \u8220\'20\'1Cpresident of a corrupt leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Karl Winter has asked about RFK Jr. not being allowed to remove his name from the ballot in Wisconsin, where third-party candidates could potentially have a large influence in a swing state with tight margins.\par \par \uc2 Vance says that he thinks it is \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Ca bunch of bureaucrats\u8221\'20\'1D are not going to take RFK Jr.\u8217\'20\'19s name off the ballot, because they want to hurt Trump. He says he thinks they\u8217\'20\'19ll win anyway.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance has finished his speech and is now taking questions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that is broken about this country is our failed leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 From what I can tell, this event is a small one (Vance has during his speech already made claims that people were leaving Harris\u8217\'20\'19s events while she spoke, following on from false claims made by Trump about AI-generated crowd sizes).\par \par \uc2 NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Karl Winter is at the event, where earlier he counted 180 chairs. It is unclear how many of them are occupied now.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe venue of today\u8217\'20\'19s Sen. JD Vance campaign event at Amerilux International in De Pere, Wisconsin \u8212\'20\'14 plus a peek at the playlist.\par \par \uc2 I count 180 white chairs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DQbnWX2QHD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DQbnWX2QHD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karl Winter (@KarlWinterTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KarlWinterTV/status/1828900424931475589?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance claims that Harris is using tax dollars to subsidise products made by the \u8220\'20\'1CCommunist Chinese\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He is repeating false claims about Harris and electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Biden in May announced a quadrupling of tariffs on Chinese electric vehicles to 100%.\par \par \uc2 China has vowed retaliation against the \u8220\'20\'1Cbullying\u8221\'20\'1D tariff hikes and Foreign Minister Wang Yi said they showed that some in the US may be \u8220\'20\'1Closing their minds\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Biden-Harris administration is expected to announce final implementation plans for steep tariff increases on certain Chinese imports this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Obama has just marked the tenth anniversary of his tan suit with a side-by-side picture of Harris in hers at the DNC:\par \par \uc2 enltrHow it started. How it's going.\par \par \uc2 Ten years later, and it's still a good look! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NKXRGNgJPv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NKXRGNgJPv}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KeI1gn7HSg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KeI1gn7HSg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1828933458460389523?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More on this important subject:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/kamala-harris-wore-a-tan-suit-to-day-one-of-the-dnc-what-does-it-mean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris wore a tan suit to day one of the DNC \u8211\'20\'13 what does it mean?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance turns to Harris, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CShe does this thing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe stands before crowds like this and she\u8217\'20\'19ll say without a hint of irony, without a hint of shame that on Day one she\u8217\'20\'19ll tackle the affordability crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDay One was 1300 days ago, what the hell have you been doing all that time,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance is speaking now. He has welcomed his wife Usha Vance, said she always gets a little embarrassed, and added, \u8220\'20\'1CBut why not embarrass your wife? Take the opportunity, I\u8217\'20\'19ll deal with the consequences later.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance and his wife, Usha Vance, are taking to the stage in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Harris and Walz, dropped in on a high school band practice Wednesday as part of a two-day bus tour through southeast Georgia campaigning for the critical battleground state, as the students performed their school fight song for the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re so proud of you and we\u8217\'20\'19re counting on you,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the young crowd at Liberty County High School, some shrieking with excitement at the sight of the vice president. \u8220\'20\'1CYour generation \u8230\'20\'26 is what is going to propel our country into the next era of what we can do and what we can be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The trip culminates Thursday with a rally in Savannah, the Associated Press reports. Campaign officials believe that in order to win the state over Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November they must make inroads in GOP strongholds. They need more than Atlanta and the suburbs that delivered for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign communications director Michael Tyler said bus tours offer an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity to get to places we don\u8217\'20\'19t usually go (and) make sure we\u8217\'20\'19re competing in all communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The campaign wants the events to motivate voters in GOP-leaning areas who don\u8217\'20\'19t traditionally see the candidates, and hopes that the engagements drive viral moments that cut through crowded media coverage to reach voters across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, is expected to speak in Wisconsin in ten minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time, at 7pm ET, according to the Hill. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the main developments from that live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The gunman in the assassination attempt of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  searched online for events of both the former president and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and saw the Pennsylvania {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign rally}}}\uc2  where he opened fire last month as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget of opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D, a senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  official said on Wednesday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-shooting-suspect-home-town-motive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks}}}\uc2 , who shot at Trump from a nearby roof before being killed by a Secret Service counter-sniper, did extensive research for an attack before the shooting and had looked at any number of events or targets, including the current and former president, said Kevin Rojek, the special agent in charge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh field office.\par \par \uc2 The new details were disclosed as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  officials, in the latest in a series of briefings about the investigation, revealed that they had yet to uncover a motive for the 13 July attack in Butler, Pennsylvania, despite conducting nearly 1,000 interviews.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a clear idea of mindset, but we are not ready to make any conclusive statements regarding motive at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Rojek said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/trump-shooting-gunman-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gunman at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally saw it as \u8216\'20\'18target of opportunity\u8217\'20\'19, FBI official says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  decided on Wednesday that it will not reinstate the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s multibillion-dollar student loan repayment plan, Save, which aims to lower monthly payments for millions of borrowers.\par \par \uc2 The plan was blocked by a federal appeals court earlier this summer as a result of a legal challenge led by several Republican states.\par \par \uc2 In an unsigned order with no noted dissents, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/orders/courtorders/082824zr_8mj9.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that it \u8220\'20\'1Cexpects that the court of appeals will render its decision with appropriate dispatch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision has no immediate impact on the 8 million borrowers currently enrolled in the program.\par \par \uc2 In June, US district judge John Ross in St Louis blocked the Biden administration on a preliminary basis from implementing the provision of the Save plan that would have granted loan forgiveness to certain borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/biden-student-loan-debt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court will not reinstate Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student loan repayment plan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance said at a rally that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  can \u8220\'20\'1Cgo to hell\u8221\'20\'1D as he criticized the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  won a new trial in her libel lawsuit against the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  after an appeals court ruled that a judge who oversaw the 2022 trial in the case made several errors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance said the Trump campaign was given permission to have a photographer present during his visit this week to a section of Arlington national cemetery where photography is not allowed. His remarks were in response to a report from NPR that Trump staffers had been involved in an altercation with a cemetery official.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  denied a request from the Biden administration to allow a plan that would lower or pause federal student debt payments for borrowers to take effect.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The gunman who tried to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, viewed the event as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget of opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D and had spent months researching potential events and targets, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his remarks in Erie, JD Vance again argued that the altercation at Arlington national cemetery was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe media creating a story\u8221\'20\'1D and instead used a question from a reporter about the incident to condemn \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NPR reported on Tuesday that two Trump campaign staffers had been involved in an altercation with a cemetery official for filming and taking pictures in a section that is reserved for recent US military casualties. The Trump campaign was given permission to have a photographer in attendance while Trump was visiting the cemetery, Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what I think our veterans care a lot more about, that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s VP nominee lied about his military experience,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Republicans have repeatedly attacked Walz\u8217\'20\'19s military record in recent weeks by spreading falsehoods and distortions about his service.\par \par \uc2 Vance also argued that 13 Americans died in Afghanistan because Harris \u8220\'20\'1Crefused to do her job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is so asleep at the wheel that she won\u8217\'20\'19t even do an investigation into what happened and she wants to yell at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because he showed up. She can go to hell!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says Harris can 'go to hell' in critical remarks on Afghanistan withdrawal\par \par \uc2 JD Vance said at a rally that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can \u8220\'20\'1Cgo to hell\u8221\'20\'1D as he heavily criticized the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Afghanistan withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 The Republican vice-presidential candidate was speaking at a campaign rally in Erie, Pennsylvania. Republicans have long sought to use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/afghanistan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Afghanistan}}}\uc2  pullout to attack \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and are now using the same line of criticism against Harris in hopes of defeating the Democrat in November.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JDVance}}}\uc2  : "\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is so asleep at the wheel that she won't even do an investigation into what happened and she wants to give \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because he showed up, she can go to hell!" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hoUO0DRhQm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hoUO0DRhQm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1828885507218247938?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  won a new trial in her libel lawsuit against the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A jury in 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/15/sarah-palin-new-york-times-lawsuit-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  the former Alaska governor\u8217\'20\'19s claims of defamation. Palin had argued that the newspaper damaged her reputation by linking her campaign rhetoric to the 2011 Arizona shooting that wounded US representative \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2  and left six others dead.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, a federal appeals court ruled that she should receive a new trial, and found that the judge in the original proceedings made several errors, including wrongly excluding evidence.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the Times called Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointing\u8221\'20\'1D while Palin\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ca significant step forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressman says relatives approved Trump campaign taking photos at Arlington cemetery\par \par \uc2 Mike Waltz, a Republican congressman, shared a statement from the families of US soldiers killed and injured during the 2021 withdrawal from Afghanistan, who said they approved of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign staff taking photos and videos during his visit to Arlington national cemetery on Monday:\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom the Abbey Gate Gold Star families and Purple Heart recipients who were at Arlington National Cemetery on Monday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u1YfJlZe2i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u1YfJlZe2i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Mike Waltz (@michaelgwaltz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michaelgwaltz/status/1828818588259787058?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209#block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to NPR}}}\uc2 , an Arlington official got into an altercation with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign staff because the former president\u8217\'20\'19s entourage had been visiting a section of the grounds where only cemetery employees can take photos.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether Trump having the permission of some of the families of those buried there is relevant to the cemetery\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that the former president is gearing up to continue his legal challenge against special counsel Jack Smith, who yesterday unveiled a new indictment against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is expected to? continue to battle against criminal charges of trying to overturn the 2020 election by challenging further parts of the revised indictment that removed allegations? the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  found were subject to immunity?.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/27/trump-jan-6-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 superseding indictment ?filed on Tuesday}}}\uc2  by special counsel prosecutors mainly removed allegations about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to use the? justice department to ?obstruct the peaceful transfer of power and reframed the narrative to say Trump was being charged in his capacity as a candidate?.\par \par \uc2 The document retains the same four criminal ?conspiracy statutes against Trump that were originally filed last summer. But portions of the new indictment have been rewritten to emphasize that Trump was not acting in his official capacity during his efforts to try? to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers see the changes as minimal and will seek to pare back the charges further, ?according to people familiar with the matter, because they consider large parts of what remains in the updated indictment to be presumptively immune conduct that the judge needs to resolve?.\par \par \uc2 In that sense, there are no immediate consequences of the ?special ?counsel Jack Smith getting a superseding indictment in the case. Trump still ?plans to initiate new litigation, ?which will be appealed to the US court of appeals for the DC circuit?, and any trial would not happen before the November election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/trump-lawyers-new-indictment-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump plans to keep challenging January 6 charges after new indictment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says Trump campaign 'was allowed' to have photographer at Arlington national cemetery\par \par \uc2 JD Vance said the Trump campaign was given permission to have a photographer present during his visit this week to a section of Arlington national cemetery where photography is not allowed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is verifiable evidence that the campaign was allowed to have a photographer there \u8230\'20\'26 they were invited to have a photographer there,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said during a campaign rally in Erie, Pennsylvania.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209#block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR has reported}}}\uc2  that two Trump campaign staffers got in an altercation with a Arlington official for filming and taking pictures in a section of the cemetery reserved for recent US military casualties, and where only staff members are allowed to use cameras.\par \par \uc2 Addressing reports of a scuffle, Vance said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe altercation at Arlington cemetery is the media creating a story where I really don\u8217\'20\'19t think that there is one,\u8221\'20\'1D and, \u8220\'20\'1CApparently somebody at Arlington cemetery, some staff member, had a little disagreement with somebody, and they have turned the media has turned this into a national news story.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 During an appearance in Erie, Pennsylvania, this afternoon, JD Vance trotted out a new attack line against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , accusing her of running a \u8220\'20\'1Ccopycat campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator, who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  selected as his running mate last month, said, without offering evidence, that the Democratic nominee had adopted the same policies as his campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at her campaign the past week and a half, she pretends that she agrees with Donald J Trump on every issue. She is running a copycat campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 There are wide differences between the two campaigns \u8211\'20\'13 something Vance well knows, considering that he spent much of his speech attacking Harris for her support of efforts to encourage electric vehicle usage.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Ccopycat campaign\u8221\'20\'1D line may be a reference to one of the few areas where the two candidates align, which is on taxing tips. Trump has said he\u8217\'20\'19d like to remove taxes on gratuities, and Harris recently said she would support that as well. The policy is generally seen as a way to woo votes in Nevada, a swing states with a large number of workers dependent on tips:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/harris-no-tax-on-tips-nevada-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No tax on tips fires up Nevada hospitality workers: \u8216\'20\'18I want that!\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court maintains hold on latest Biden student debt relief plan\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has declined a request from the Biden administration to allow a plan that would lower or pause federal student debt payments for borrowers to take effect, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-biden-student-loans-f566c623ccb3f322523d7e0a2f88b0c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  proposed the plan, known as Save, after a previous attempt to cancel billions of dollars in federal student loans was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/30/student-loan-forgiveness-supreme-court-ruling-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority}}}\uc2 . Republican-led states sued over the Save plan, and have won rulings against it at the appeals level.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision from the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court will allow those rulings to stand while litigation plays out.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The justices rejected an administration request to put most of it back into effect. It was blocked by 8th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals.\par \par \uc2 In an unsigned order, the court said it expects the appeals court to issue a fuller decision on the plan \u8220\'20\'1Cwith appropriate dispatch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Education Department is seeking to provide a faster path to loan cancellation, and reduce monthly income-based repayments from 10% to 5% of a borrower\u8217\'20\'19s discretionary income. The plan also wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t require borrowers to make payments if they earn less than 225% of the federal poverty line \u8212\'20\'14 $32,800 a year for a single person.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/student-loan-forgiveness-supreme-court-653c2e9c085863bdbf81f125f87669fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  an earlier plan that would have wiped away more than $400 billion in student loan debt.\par \par \uc2 Cost estimates of the new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/student-loans-forgiveness-save-plan-debt-borrowers-313afd73cadc3cfc8ab3a6ee684fc3e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAVE plan}}}\uc2  vary. The Republican-led states challenging the plan peg the cost at $475 billion over 10 years. The administration cites a \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  estimate of $276 billion.\par \par \uc2 Two separate legal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/politics/joe-biden-000001904d5edaf5afd4df5f13b00000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenges}}}\uc2  to the SAVE plan have been making their way through federal courts. In June, judges in Kansas and Missouri issued separate rulings that blocked much of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s plan. Debt that already had been forgiven under the plan was unaffected.\par \par \uc2 The 10th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/student-loan-repayment-save-plan-b39342e0dce69dce2c5582ffba1cfcb7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  that allowed the department to proceed with a provision allowing for lower monthly payments. Republican-led states had asked the high court to undo that ruling.\par \par \uc2 But after the 8th Circuit blocked the entire plan, the states had no need for the Supreme Court to intervene, the justices noted in a separate order issued Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Failed Trump assassin viewed rally as 'target of opportunity'\par \par \uc2 The gunman who tried to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, viewed the event as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctarget of opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  revealed today, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fbi-trump-assassination-attempt-919bc3a7bba02f6e340fed321b20dfdd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The special agent in charge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh office, Kevin Rojek, told reporters that Thomas Crooks, who opened fire on Trump, searched on the internet for: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere will Trump speak from at Butler Farm Show?\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CButler Farm Show podium\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CButler Farm Show photos\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s rally in July.\par \par \uc2 However, Rojek said that Crooks\u8217\'20\'19s motive remains a mystery: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a clear idea of mindset, but we are not ready to make any conclusive statements regarding motive at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  say Trump gunman spent months researching events and seeking a target before settling on Trump's Pennsylvania rally\par \par \uc2 The gunman who tried to assassinate former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a rally in Pennsylvania in July searched more than 60 times for information about Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , before registering for the Trump rally, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/fbi-says-trump-gunman-spent-months-looking-target-before-settling-trump-2024-08-28/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters}}}\uc2  report that cites \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials.\par \par \uc2 Reuters also reported that Kevin Rojek, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top official in western Pennsylvania, said that the 20-year-old gunman, Thomas Crooks, mounted a \u8220\'20\'1Csustained, detailed effort to plan an attack on some events, meaning he looked at any number of events or targets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Crooks then became \u8220\'20\'1Chyper focused\u8221\'20\'1D on the Trump rally after it was announced, Rojek said.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2024/08/28/fbi-new-details-trump-assassination-attempt/74982956007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  USA Today}}}\uc2 , Rojek said that Crooks researched the Trump and Biden campaigns between April and July 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new poll released today by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.activote.net/harris-and-trump-essentially-tied-in-michigan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ActiVote}}}\uc2  shows the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cessentially tied\u8221\'20\'1D in the battleground state of Michigan, with Harris leading Trump by just 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 The new Michigan presidential poll was conducted between 28 July and 28 August and was among 400 likely voters. The poll has an \u8220\'20\'1Caverage expected error of 4.9%\u8221\'20\'1D, the company said.\par \par \uc2 According to the data, Harris leads among such as urban voters, women, low income voters, young voters in Michigan, where Trump leads among rural and suburban voters, men, and those 50 to 64 years old, ActiVote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.activote.net/harris-and-trump-essentially-tied-in-michigan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new survey released by Gallup suggests that a majority of Americans continue to approve of labor unions.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/12751/labor-unions.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  survey}}}\uc2 , 70% of respondents said that they approve of labor unions, up from 67% last year. This year\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating is the second highest recorded by Gallup since 1965, per the data, with the 2022 being the highest with 71% approval rating of labor unions.\par \par \uc2 The recent survey, which was conducted in August of this year, also states that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/12751/labor-unions.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23%}}}\uc2  of respondents said that they disapproved of labor unions and 7% had no opinion.\par \par \uc2 enltrSince 1936, Gallup has measured how Americans feel about labor unions.\par \par \uc2 In 2024, 70% of Americans approve of labor unions, which has been generally trending higher since hitting a low point in 2009. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g4IunmgAPh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/g4IunmgAPh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gallup (@Gallup) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Gallup/status/1828793176754409957?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The new data comes as \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential candidate and governor of Minnesota, spoke to unionized firefighters this morning at the \uc2 International Association of Fire Fighters\uc2  convention in Boston.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Controversy brews over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209#block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a report}}}\uc2  that campaign staffers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were involved in a physical altercation with an official from Arlington national cemetery, which he visited earlier this week. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former defense secretary \uc2 Mark Esper{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf42628f08f4abbe22b367#block-66cf42628f08f4abbe22b367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  he was waiting to hear the outcome of an investigation into the scuffle, while saying the cemetery should never be used for \u8220\'20\'1Cpartisan political purposes\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s communications director {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf47c58f08b036ea3f443c#block-66cf47c58f08b036ea3f443c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  that her campaign and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s were still not on the same page about the rules for their 10 September debate, with the sticking point being whether the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 microphones would be live when it was not their turn to talk. Trump seems to want them switched off, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s people want them on.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor who is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, invited unionized firefighters to tune into the debate, saying: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf36ee8f083d0558af62ea#block-66cf36ee8f083d0558af62ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be good}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Clips of JD Vance attacking people who do not have children {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf390f8f083d0558af6313#block-66cf390f8f083d0558af6313"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep emerging}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf4e988f08b036ea3f44ac#block-66cf4e988f08b036ea3f44ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued}}}\uc2  to rail against the gag order imposed on him in his hush money case, saying it is preventing him from talking about the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost important and corrupt aspects\u8221\'20\'1D of his prosecution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles are clearly on his mind today, if his recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social posts}}}\uc2  are any indication.\par \par \uc2 The special counsel Jack Smith yesterday unveiled a new indictment of the former president for his attempt to overturn the 2020 election. While it does not dramatically alter the facts of the case, and appears mostly a response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s immunity decision handed down last month, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis}}}\uc2  reports in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/trump-on-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump on Trial newsletter}}}\uc2  that it may be a sign the former president\u8217\'20\'19s luck in the courts has run out:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/27/trump-on-trial-new-indictment-jack-smith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lucky streak with his criminal cases may have ended}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is meanwhile busy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2 , posting about various things on his mind, including the gag order he remains under in his New York hush -money case.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/trump-gag-order-remains-hush-money-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The order}}}\uc2  prevents him from making statements about prosecutors, court staff and their families, at least until his 18 September sentencing date. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fairly small group of people, but Trump is nonetheless very upset about it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113040485793876843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as he wrote}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 When asked about the lawless Manhattan D.A. Hoax, I am not allowed to talk about the most important and corrupt aspects of it, because of the completely unConstitutional Gag Order. I am the first Candidate in American History who is not allowed to freely speak about a major Witch Hunt being perpetrated against him. I must be immediately released from the Gag Order, so I can continue to expose the Weaponization of our Justice System by the Radical Democrats. The GOOD NEWS is that the American People see through these Witch Hunts, and will bring us a dominant Victory on November 5th. MAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign spokesman says question of live microphones in debate with Trump still undecided\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday said he had agreed on the rules for his 10 September debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but a spokesman for the vice-president indicates they still are not on the same page over whether the microphones will be on or off when it is not a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s turn to speak.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113035417108806850"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday said}}}\uc2  he had agreed to the same rules that governed his June debate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . In that case, microphones were muted when it was not time for him or the president to talk.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN today, the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s communications director Michael Tyler implied that Trump had agreed that microphones would be on throughout \u8211\'20\'13 something the former president has not explicitly said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a 90-minute debate. Both candidates have said that they are comfortable with live, unmuted microphones for the duration of the debate that allows for the free flow and exchange of ideas between the two candidates. I understand that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team of handlers is now attempting to overrule him. But as insofar as the candidates themselves, we\u8217\'20\'19re in total alignment that this should be a 90-minute debate with live microphones. And so that\u8217\'20\'19s what we look forward to,\u8221\'20\'1D Tyler said.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Harris would attend the debate, hosted by ABC News, if microphones are not always on, Tyler replied:\par \par \uc2 We fully intend to debate. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be there. The question is, will \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  commit to the terms that he\u8217\'20\'19s publicly agreed to? Or will he let his team overrule him? So I guess we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if when he shows up on September 10, which decision he has made.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump defense secretary says Arlington cemetery should never be used for 'partisan political purposes' after report of Trump altercation\par \par \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2 , a former defense secretary under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , told CNN that he hoped the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/28/trump-harris-georgia-campaign-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209#block-66cf2c708f08f4abbe22b209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported altercation}}}\uc2  between the former president\u8217\'20\'19s staff and an official at Arlington national cemetery was investigated, while saying that the grounds should never be used for \u8220\'20\'1Cpartisan political purposes\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump SecDef Esper tells me he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Canxious\u8221\'20\'1D to see what comes of Arlington investigation- \u8220\'20\'1CBottom line: The principle is that no person or party, either side, should ever use Arlington National Cemetery \u8211\'20\'13 or any of our cemeteries or battlefields \u8211\'20\'13 for partisan political purposes.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zazLTDGPUQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zazLTDGPUQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Acosta (@Acosta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acosta/status/1828817074254172215?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Esper served under Trump from 2019 until shortly after the 2020 election, when Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/09/mark-esper-fired-defence-pentagon-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired him}}}\uc2 . The former defense chief has since decried Trump as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RpsAgainstTrump/status/1772874892339241470"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threat to democracy}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/28/jd-vance-attack-childless-teachers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newly resurfaced remarks}}}\uc2  from 2021, JD Vance, the Republican vice-presiden tial candidate, attacked teachers and Democratic leaders who do not have children.\par \par \uc2 In the clip, Vance, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LrBGXUIhdog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was speaking at a forum}}}\uc2  held by the Center for Christian Virtue can be heard saying:\par \par \uc2 So many of the leaders of the left, and I hate to be so personal about this, but they\u8217\'20\'19re people without kids trying to brainwash the minds of our children, that really disorients me and disturbs me.\par \par \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s the head of the most powerful teachers\u8217\'20\'19 union in the country, she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a single child. If she wants to brainwash and destroy the minds of children, she should have some of her own and leave ours the hell alone.\par \par \uc2 In a post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/rweingarten/status/1828552792664838264"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2 , Weingarten responded to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s resurfaced comments, calling them \u8220\'20\'1Cgross\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csad and insulting to millions of modern families, and school teachers including Catholic nuns, none of whom should be targeted for their family decisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This comes just weeks after Vance came under fire after a clip of him in 2021 calling leading Democrats \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/jd-vance-childless-cat-ladies-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bunch of childless cat ladies}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D resurfaced.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz also referenced his past as a football coach to argue that, despite the former president\u8217\'20\'19s protestations, Trump plans to implement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  if elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the goals of their Project 2025 is to screw the middle class, making it harder for workers to collectively bargain, allowing employers to drastically cut overtime or eliminate it, slash taxes for the ultra wealthy by imposing a national sales tax on the rest of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I\u8217\'20\'19ve said this, I\u8217\'20\'19m an old-time football coach. If you draw up a playbook, you plan on using it. Project 2025 is a plan to reshape what America looks like \u8211\'20\'13 moving away from the middle class and putting it right back on the oligarchs and the wealthy at the top.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says Harris's debate with Trump is 'going to be good'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  encouraged unionized firefighters to watch \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 10 September debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she\u8217\'20\'19s ready to hold him accountable on the debate stage,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said of Trump. He continued:\par \par \uc2 Tell me you\u8217\'20\'19re not looking forward to that. Look, I know you\u8217\'20\'19re busy. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to be watching Monday Night Football or something, but it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be good. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be good because again, as I said, this is going to impact you. The things that are said on that debate stage are going to impact your retirement. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to impact your kids, education, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to impact infrastructure. These are things that matter to us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz addresses firefighter union convention in Boston\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is now onstage at the \uc2 International Association of Fire Fighters\uc2  convention in Boston, where he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s policies towards labor unions.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the Minnesota governor has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will rally supporters tomorrow in Savannah, Georgia, at the conclusion of her bus tour through the state.\par \par \uc2 Based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_post%E2%80%932016_election_Donald_Trump_rallies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this list}}}\uc2 , it does not appear that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ever held a rally in the coastal city, but he nonetheless knows where his supporters (or at least three of them) can be found \u8211\'20\'13 at Waffle House:\par \par \uc2 enltrTHANK YOU\u8212\'20\'14WAFFLE HOUSE IN SAVANNAH, GEORGIA... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZgOytm0EGd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZgOytm0EGd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump on ?? (@trump_repost) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/trump_repost/status/1828790892637151320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign staff had 'verbal and physical altercation' with Arlington cemetery officials over taking pictures - report\par \par \uc2 Two staffers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign had a \u8220\'20\'1Cverbal and physical altercation\u8221\'20\'1D with an official at Arlington national cemetery over filming and taking photos in a section reserved for recent US casualties of war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/27/nx-s1-5091154/trump-arlington-cemetery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has denied the episode, which it blamed on an \u8220\'20\'1Cunnamed individual\u8221\'20\'1D who was \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly suffering from a mental health episode\u8221\'20\'1D. The national cemetery told NPR that it had filed a report over the incident.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 A source with knowledge of the incident said the cemetery official tried to prevent Trump staffers from filming and photographing in a section where recent US casualties are buried. The source said Arlington officials had made clear that only cemetery staff members would be authorized to take photographs or film in the area, known as Section 60.\par \par \uc2 When the cemetery official tried to prevent Trump campaign staff from entering Section 60, campaign staff verbally abused and pushed the official aside, according to the source.\par \par \uc2 Trump participated in an event to mark the third anniversary of a deadly attack on US troops in Afghanistan as US forces withdrew from the country; 13 US service members were killed in the attack. The Trump campaign has blamed President Biden and Vice President Harris, now the Democratic presidential nominee, for the chaotic withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to NPR, \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2 , the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman, strongly rejected the notion of a physical altercation, adding: \u8216\'20\'18We are prepared to release footage if such defamatory claims are made.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The fact is that a private photographer was permitted on the premises and for whatever reason an unnamed individual, clearly suffering from a mental health episode, decided to physically block members of President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team during a very solemn ceremony,\u8217\'20\'19 Cheung said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign declined to make that footage immediately available.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to NPR, Arlington National Cemetery said it \u8216\'20\'18can confirm there was an incident, and a report was filed.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why are \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  heading to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s rural south?\par \par \uc2 Democrats have suffered in rural areas in recent election cycles nationwide, instead drawing support from cities and their suburbs.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 swing through the Georgia hinterlands is part of a strategy \u8211\'20\'13 which they plan to replicate in other swing states \u8211\'20\'13 of trying to limit their losses in rural areas, while also turning out support in urban areas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to really stave down margins and go places even when you don\u8217\'20\'19t think you can win it outright,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris-Walz principal deputy campaign manager \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2  told Politico. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know you\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose that county, but just showing up there can sometimes be the difference between 5 to 10 percentage points, or sometimes just putting an office there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz set for first joint interview with CNN on Thursday\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has not done a single sit-down interview since embarking on her presidential campaign, but that will change on Thursday at 9pm ET when CNN airs a joint interview with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/27/politics/kamala-harris-cnn-interview/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The network says}}}\uc2  the candidates will talk about their swing through Georgia, and we can expect the vice-president to also be asked for her thoughts on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ending his bid for a second term and clearing the way for her to become the Democratic nominee.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just one interview, though, and is unlikely to quiet the attacks from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his running mate JD Vance and other Republicans who claim that Harris and Walz can\u8217\'20\'19t handle scrutiny from the press. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if the pair schedule more encounters with the media in the weeks to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz kick off bus tour of Georgia to build momentum in swing state\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. There are seven swing states whose voters are expected to decide the November presidential election: Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Nevada, North Carolina, Arizona and Georgia. It\u8217\'20\'19s that last state which will be getting special attention from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  over the next two days, as they look to preserve inroads made by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four years ago, when he became the first Democrat to win its electoral votes since 1992. The pair is kicking off a bus tour of the state\u8217\'20\'19s southern counties on Wednesday that will culminate on Thursday with Harris holding a rally in Savannah.\par \par \uc2 Their campaign says that Harris and Walz are aiming to build off their momentum from last week\u8217\'20\'19s convention, when they accepted the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination amid enthusiasm from Democrats. They\u8217\'20\'19re also aiming to win a state that may be the toughest to hold in November \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls generally show}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with the advantage among Georgia voters, though the gap has grown narrower since Harris entered the race. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see what the vice-president and Minnesota governor encounter as they traverse the state today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump earlier this week visited Arlington national cemetery, and his campaign staff had an altercation with an official who tried to prevent them from taking pictures in area where only employees are allowed to do so, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/27/nx-s1-5091154/trump-arlington-cemetery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR reports}}}\uc2 . The Trump campaign has rejected their description of events.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Cook Political Report, the closely watched forecaster, now views North Carolina as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss up\u8221\'20\'1D in the presidential election. The state hasn\u8217\'20\'19t voted for a Democratic candidate since 2008.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate GOP campaign arm is buying ads for incumbent \uc2 Ted Cruz\uc2 , in a sign that polls of his re-election race against Democrat \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  in the Republican bastion may be too close for comfort.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240828ek8s001s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
