\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Special counsel appeals dismissal of Trump classified documents case; Harris endorsed by former Republican staffers \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now) with L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 7,657 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2024\par 22:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on the 2024 US election, you can read our full coverage here.Special counsel appeals Trump classified documents case dismissal\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it for today\u8217\'20\'19s live US elections and politics coverage. You can find our latest stories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and the full story on \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/tulsi-gabbard-endorses-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Democrat Tulsi Gabbard endorses Donald Trump in 2024 presidential race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House national security communications adviser John Kirby has spoken to journalists about the ongoing talks in in Cairo. He was asked how long the talks might take, what was being negotiated, and whether the Israeli air strokes on southern Lebanon, and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s drone and rocket attacks on nrothern Israel on the weekend have impacted the talks.\par \par \uc2 He said the exchange of hostilities had not had an impact on the talks in Cairo. He could not say how long the negotiations will take, but he did say that one of the issues beign discussed is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe exchange of hostages and prisoners that Israel is holding\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kirby: So, the working groups are meeting now in Cairo. \uc2 Brett McGurk\uc2  stayed in Cairo an extra day to get them kicked off, and he\u8217\'20\'19s there now, but he\u8217\'20\'19ll probably depart relatively soon and leave the discussion and the work to the working group members. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a list of names of all the people that are going to be represented there, but all parties will be represented, including \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , in those working group discussions.\par \par \uc2 And as for how long they\u8217\'20\'19ll take, I think that remains to be seen. We expect that these working group discussions will at least take place over the next few days. But whether it goes longer or, you know, could end sooner, I think really is going to be up to those in the room and what they\u8217\'20\'19re able to accomplish.\par \par \uc2 And then that gets to your other question about, well, what are they working on. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say that the issues they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be talking about are of a much more detailed, specific nature than we\u8217\'20\'19ve typically been able to talk about.\par \par \uc2 For instance \u8211\'20\'13 and I want to be careful, obviously \u8211\'20\'13 but for instance, one issue that will be for the working groups to flesh out is the exchange of hostages and prisoners that Israel is holding. What that exchange looks like, how many, you know, some of the details of exactly who will be released on either side and at what pace, those kinds of things, that\u8217\'20\'19s a good example of some of the things that they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to flesh out now. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s best if I don\u8217\'20\'19t go into more detail than that, though, right now.\par \par \uc2 And on the attacks over the weekend: No, there was not an impact on the talks in Cairo, and we\u8217\'20\'19re certainly glad to see that. Obviously, as I said earlier, the working groups are now meeting and talking, and so there continues to be progress, and our team on the ground continues to describe the talks as constructive.\par \par \uc2 So, despite the rocket and drone attack by \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  over the course of the weekend, which Israel did a terrific job defending against, it has not affected the actual work on the ground by the teams trying to get this ceasefire deal in place.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , a former Democratic congresswoman, endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the presidential election. Gabbard has become a fixture at conservative conferences and in rightwing media and has been helping Trump prepare for next month\u8217\'20\'19s televised presidential debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 200 former Republican staffers who worked for former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , and senators \uc2 John McCain\uc2  and \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , signed a letter endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith urged an appeals court to reinstate his office\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after it was dismissed by a judge last month. The US district judge Aileen Cannon threw out the case last month after concluding that Smith\u8217\'20\'19s appointment was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Police Association announced its endorsement of Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  in the state\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race, despite backing Republican Kari Lake in her gubernatorial bid last cycle. The group publicly threw its support behind Trump just days ago during a rally in Glendale.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  expressed doubt that he will participate in a 10 September televised debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  next month, hurling a trademark \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D slur at the network that had agreed to host it. Trump appeared to undercut his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s position over the conditions of next month\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled debate by declaring he would prefer to have participants\u8217\'20\'19 microphones when it was not their turn to speak.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said it has now raised $540m for its election battle against Trump. The campaign said it saw a surge of donations during last week\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic national convention in Chicago where Harris and her vice-presidential running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , accepted their nominations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  issued statements on Monday marking the third anniversary of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited Arlington national cemetery in Virginia on Monday to take part in a wreath laying ceremony as he seeks to tie Harris to the chaotic US pullout and attack at Kabul airport\u8217\'20\'19s Abbey Gate that killed 13 US soldiers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing the Arizona \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D case involving a scheme by Republican allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to overturn his loss in the state during the 2020 presidential election set a trial date of 5 January 2026.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/26/trump-harris-election-debate-updates?page=with:block-66ccdadb8f0855397f4b0746#block-66ccdadb8f0855397f4b0746"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  court filing}}}\uc2  on Monday, urged a federal appeals court to revive the criminal case accusing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of retaining classified documents after it was dismissed by US district court judge Aileen Cannon last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress has bestowed on the Attorney General, like the heads of many Executive Departments, broad authority to structure the agency he leads to carry out the responsibilities imposed on him by law,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team wrote.\par \par \uc2 The district court\u8217\'20\'19s contrary view conflicts with an otherwise unbroken course of decisions, including by the Supreme Court, that the Attorney General has such authority, and it is at odds with widespread and longstanding appointment practices in the Department of Justice and across the government.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , the Michigan congresswoman and leading progressive Democrat, criticized the Democratic national convention for denying a speaking slot for a Palestinian American on the main stage last week.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib, who is the sole Palestinian American member of Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://zeteo.com/p/jon-stewart-gets-it-right-again-plus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Zeteo in a statement:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s hard not to feel invisible as a Palestinian-American. Our trauma and pain feel unseen and ignored by both parties. One party uses our identity as a slur, and the other refuses to hear from us. Where is the shared humanity? Ignoring us won\u8217\'20\'19t stop the genocide.\par \par \uc2 The uncommitted national movement, who represent hundreds of thousands of anti-war protest votes from the primary season, staged a multi-day sit-in protest outside the United Center in Chicago where the Democratic convention was being held, after the convention told the group it would not get a speaker on the main stage.\par \par \uc2 The family of the Israeli American hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, who was kidnapped by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  on 7 October, spoke on the convention stage on Wednesday, which the uncommitted movement supported.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib, who did not attend the convention, said the lineup showed that the convention \u8220\'20\'1Cmade it clear with their speakers that they value Israeli children more than Palestinian children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic congresswoman who endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Monday, served in the military in Iraq and ran for president in the Democratic primary in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard quit the Democratic party two years later and has become a fixture at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/tulsi-gabbard-republican-speech-cpac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative conferences}}}\uc2  and in rightwing media.\par \par \uc2 Addressing a National Guard Association conference in Detroit, Michigan, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?537982-1/president-trump-addresses-national-guard-association"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president was speaking}}}\uc2 , Gabbard, who represented Hawaii in Congress and is a former vice-chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , accused \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of retaliating against political opponents, undermining civil liberties and weaponising the US\u8217\'20\'19s institutions against both Trump and herself.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Democratic Rep. \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  endorses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a National Guard event.\par \par \uc2 "[Trump] exercised the courage that we expect from our commander in chief.... This [Biden-Harris] administration has us... closer to the brink of nuclear war than we ever have been before." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nsQuOy5u2w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nsQuOy5u2w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1828140341368857030?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Recently Gabbard has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/17/tulsi-gabbard-trump-kamala-harris-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been helping Trump}}}\uc2  prepare for next month\u8217\'20\'19s televised presidential debate against Harris. In 2020 she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s6CFS4tHf4w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took Harris to task}}}\uc2  on the debate stage over her record as a prosecutor \u8211\'20\'13 a clip that still circulates in rightwing media.\par \par \uc2 Her announcement comes a day after \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , scion of a Democratic dynasty, suspended his own White House bid and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw his weight behind Trump}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who describes himself as \u8220\'20\'1Chistorically a moderate Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D, is also backing Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing the Arizona \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D case involving a scheme by Republican allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to overturn his loss in the state during the 2020 presidential election has set a trial date of 5 January 2026.\par \par \uc2 Trump allies including the former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and former Trump attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  will stand trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/26/arizona-trump-fake-electors-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on charges}}}\uc2  they conspired to subvert Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election results.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you type in NeverWalz.com in your browser, the page that appears probably doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look like what you expected from a webpage donning a slogan against \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the governor of Minnesota and the current vice-presidential candidate for the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is a convicted felon. Let\u8217\'20\'19s vote for adults,\u8221\'20\'1D the webpage reads. \u8220\'20\'1CTry being joyful instead of an asshole.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After just a few seconds on the webpage, users are automatically redirected to KamalaHarris.com, the official website for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 The slogan \u8220\'20\'1CNever Walz\u8221\'20\'1D is indeed anti-Walz, and was seen recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/search?q=%22neverwalz%22&src=typed_query&f=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plastered on a booth}}}\uc2  set up by an group against Walzt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/action_liberty/status/1826350988133105763"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Action 4 Liberty}}}\uc2 , at the Minnesota state fair. The group was seen handing out fliers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://action4libertymn.myshopify.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 selling merchandise}}}\uc2  that criticizes Walz.\par \par \uc2 enltrFairgoers line up at the Never Walz booth to spin the wheel. Each person who spins receives a \u8220\'20\'1Cnever Walz\u8221\'20\'1D fan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ni1XayKttD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ni1XayKttD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sydney Kashiwagi (@SydneyKashiwagi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SydneyKashiwagi/status/1826679495899959346?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 But, it appears that the group did not secure a website domain for the \u8220\'20\'1CNever Walz\u8221\'20\'1D slogan, leaving it available for someone else to buy and use.\par \par \uc2 As of Monday, the website domain NeverWalz.com is being used to criticize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and then quickly redirects viewers to the Harris campaign website.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/never-walz-website-trolls-trump-supporters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anti-Walz slogan website used to troll Trump supporters: \u8216\'20\'18Let\u8217\'20\'19s vote for adults\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona police association endorses Democratic Senate candidate \uc2 Ruben Gallego\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Police Association (APA) announced its endorsement of Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  in the state\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race, despite backing Republican Kari Lake in her gubernatorial bid last cycle.\par \par \uc2 Gallego \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstands the complexities of modern policing in American society today\u8221\'20\'1D, the group\u8217\'20\'19s president Justin Harris said in a statement posted to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X.\par \par \uc2 The APA does not take our endorsements lightly; we recognize the importance of having a U.S. senator that can bring people together to improve society for all. We believe congressman Gallego will be that U.S. Senator.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS\par \par \uc2 The Arizona Police Association, which has endorsed former President Trump, has announced they\u8217\'20\'19re endorsing Congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  for Senate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EuDqtDAbOZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EuDqtDAbOZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yashar Ali ?? (@yashar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/yashar/status/1828138076713165069?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The group publicly threw its support behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just days ago during a rally in Glendale.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 A messy Michigan Republican party gathering this weekend to nominate candidates for office illustrated the diminished sway of two high-profile Michigan election deniers and highlighted longstanding divisions within the party.\par \par \uc2 Matthew DePerno, who faces charges for allegedly assisting in a scheme to improperly access voting machines in the wake of the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/08/24/matt-deperno-withdraws-candidacy-michigan-supreme-court/74933884007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew from the race}}}\uc2  for Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s top court hours before the state party convention. In a statement, DePerno said that instead of running for state supreme court, he would \u8220\'20\'1Cuse my knowledge about how elections work to get Republicans elected\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DePerno, a rightwing attorney from Kalamazoo, Michigan, was a vocal proponent of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s false claims of a stolen election in Michigan after Trump lost in 2020 to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , appearing on rightwing media to promote the claims of widespread fraud and helping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/the-original-election-fraud-grifter-matthew-deperno-is-back-to-claim-his-kraken-crownand-his-money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fund}}}\uc2  Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s sham election audit. DePerno ran for Michigan attorney general in 2022 but lost decisively to Dana Nessel \u8211\'20\'13 whose office has charged him for his role in allegedly tampering with voting machines.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, he lost his bid to chair the state party to Kristina Karamo \u8211\'20\'13 an outspoken elections conspiracy theorist who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/rnc-kristina-karamo-michigan-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ousted}}}\uc2  from her role earlier this year amid accusations that she had mismanaged the party\u8217\'20\'19s already dwindling finances.\par \par \uc2 During the convention, Karamo faced a more dramatic setback of her own when she was escorted from the venue by police officers. Karamo reportedly entered with an all-access pass, which was revoked during the convention.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/michigan-republican-party-convention-kristina-karamo-matthew-deperno"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Republican convention removes chair amid party tensions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US district judge Aileen Cannon threw out the classified documents case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last month after concluding that Jack Smith\u8217\'20\'19s appointment was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team appealed to the 11th US circuit court of appeals, arguing that Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s decision was \u8220\'20\'1Cat odds with widespread and longstanding appointment practices in the Department of Justice and across the government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how long the appeals court\u8217\'20\'19s decision could take, but even if it overturns Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal there is no chance of a trial before the November presidential election, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 If elected, Trump could then appoint an attorney general who would dismiss the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel appeals dismissal of Trump classified documents case\par \par \uc2 The special counsel Jack Smith has urged an appeals court to reinstate his office\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after it was dismissed by a judge last month.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW \u8212\'20\'14 Special Counsel Jack Smith appeals dismissal of the Trump classified docs case without asking for Judge Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s removal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V2II9qx2Zt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/V2II9qx2Zt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1828153705243517078?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least five Secret Service agents have been placed on leave after the failed assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in July.\par \par \uc2 The action is reportedly the latest consequence of the security failings surrounding the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 July shooting}}}\uc2 , when a 20-year-old gunman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/thomas-matthew-crooks-drone-trump-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks}}}\uc2 , opened fire on Trump as he spoke at a campaign rally in Butler, Pennsylvania. Trump was wounded after a bullet grazed his right ear. One rally-goer, Corey Comperatore, was killed in the shooting while two others were seriously injured. Crooks was later shot dead by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  sniper.\par \par \uc2 The agents who were placed on leave work at the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh field office, which was responsible for coordinating security at the rally along with local law enforcement, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/articles/2024/08/22/secret_service_agents_placed_leave_after_trump_assassination_attempt__151502.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Real Clear Politics}}}\uc2 , which broke the story. They include the head of the Pittsburgh office.\par \par \uc2 The officers concerned are believed to have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/secret-service-agents-on-leave-trump-shooting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put on administrative leave}}}\uc2 , which usually involves being taken off operational duties while still receiving a full salary. They are expected to report to the office and may be given paperwork duties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in his remarks to \uc2 the National Guard Association of the United States\uc2 , made reference to \u8220\'20\'1Cif there is a debate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a Truth Social post last night, Trump cast doubt on whether he would participate in a scheduled debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  next month, claiming that the network that had agreed to host it was \u8220\'20\'1Cbiased\u8221\'20\'1D against him.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/trump-harris-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump threatens to pull out of 10 September presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking to \uc2 the National Guard Association of the United States\uc2 , pledged to create a \u8220\'20\'1CSpace National Guard\u8221\'20\'1D if he is elected back to the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/21/donald-trump-officially-launches-us-space-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launching space force}}}\uc2  in 2019 was one of his proudest achievements in his first term, adding:\par \par \uc2 The time has come to create a Space National Guard as the primary combat reserve of the US space force.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 200 former Republican staffers endorse Harris\par \par \uc2 More than 200 former Republican staffers who worked for former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , and senators \uc2 John McCain\uc2  and \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , have signed a letter endorsing vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25071901-bush-mccain-and-romney-alumni-for-harris-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2 , obtained and published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/08/26/bush-mccain-romney-trump-harris-2024/74947380007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA Today }}}\uc2  reads in part:\par \par \uc2 Of course, we have plenty of honest, ideological disagreements with Vice President Harris and Gov. Walz. That\u8217\'20\'19s to be expected. The alternative, however, is simply untenable.\par \par \uc2 At home, another four years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chaotic leadership, this time focused on advancing the dangerous goals of Project 2025, will hurt real, everyday people and weaken our sacred institutions.\par \par \uc2 Abroad, democratic movements will be irreparably jeopardized as Trump and his acolyte JD Vance kowtow to dictators like \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  while turning their backs on our allies.\par \par \uc2 We can\u8217\'20\'19t let that happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 When endorsing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president, \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic Hawaii congresswoman who is also an Iraq war veteran, told the crowd at the National Guard Association\u8217\'20\'19s conference that she believes that Trump has a better understanding of the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D that a president bears \u8220\'20\'1Cfor every single one of our lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gabbard praised the former president and said that during his first term, Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cexercised the courage that we expect from our Commander in Chief,\u8221\'20\'1D and exhausted \u8220\'20\'1Call measures of diplomacy, having the courage to meet with adversaries, dictators, allies and partners alike in the pursuit of peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  endorses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has just formally endorsed former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard left the Democratic party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/11/tulsi-gabbard-quits-democratic-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2022}}}\uc2 , after her 2020 run for president and it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/17/tulsi-gabbard-trump-kamala-harris-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently reported}}}\uc2  that she has been helping Trump prepare for next month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic Hawaii congresswoman, has just been introduced on stage by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the National Guard Association of the United States Conference in Detroit, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a special person\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Gabbard. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s got great common sense, great spirit, she loves our country and she loves the people in this room.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to speak in Detroit at National Guard Association conference\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about to appear at the National Guard Association of the United States Conference in Detroit, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic Hawaii congresswoman, is expected to formally endorse Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid at the event, CNN reported earlier today, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appeared to undercut his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s position on a scheduled televised debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by declaring he would prefer to have the microphones on when it was not their turn to speak.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told reporters on Monday that he\u8217\'20\'19d \u8220\'20\'1Crather have it probably on, but the agreement was that it would be the same as it was last time. In that case, it was muted" amid a reported impasse between the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Trump campaigns over the conditions of next month\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump, in a Truth Social post on Sunday, threatened to pull out of the 10 September debate with Harris, hurling a trademark \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D slur at ABC News.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said it has now raised $540m for its election battle against Trump. The campaign said it saw a surge of donations during last week\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic National Convention in Chicago where Harris and her vice-presidential running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , accepted their nominations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren said on Sunday that \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican women are not stupid\u8221\'20\'1D enough to believe JD Vance \u8217\'20\'19s promise that Trump would veto any nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed by Congress if Trump is elected again to the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kerry Kennedy, the sister of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , said on Sunday she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusted\u8221\'20\'1D by his decision to drop out and endorse Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid. Max Kennedy, her brother, also condemned his sibling\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  issued statements on Monday marking the third anniversary of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited Arlington national cemetery in Virginia on Monday to take part in a wreath laying ceremony as he seeks to tie Harris to the chaotic US pullout and attack at Kabul airport\u8217\'20\'19s Abbey Gate that killed 13 American soldiers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic Hawaii congresswoman, is expected to formally endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid today at his event in Detroit, Michigan, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge in Arizona will hear arguments on Monday in the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D case involving a scheme by Republican allies of Trump to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win in the state during the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/26/trump-harris-election-debate-updates?page=with:block-66ccb5598f089e7649977251#block-66ccb5598f089e7649977251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments}}}\uc2  came in response to separate Meet the Press interview with JD Vance in which he was asked whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if elected again to the Oval Office, would use the presidency\u8217\'20\'19s veto powers overrule a congressional federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he would,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe said \u8230\'20\'26 explicitly that he would.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if he could commit to Trump not imposing a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Vance said:\par \par \uc2 I can absolutely commit that. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s view is that we want the individual states and their individual cultures and their unique political sensibilities to make these decisions because we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to have a nonstop federal conflict over this issue.\par \par \uc2 He insisted that Trump would veto such legislation if it were passed by Congress:\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re not supporting it as the president of the United States, you fundamentally have to veto it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Women aren\u8217\'20\'19t stupid\u8217\'20\'19 enough to believe Trump would veto federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, says Warren\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren said \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican women are not stupid\u8221\'20\'1D enough to believe JD Vance \u8217\'20\'19s promise that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would veto any nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed by Congress if the Republican presidential ticket wins November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Warren said on Sunday on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press:\par \par \uc2 American women are not stupid, and we are not going to trust the futures of our daughters and granddaughters to two men who have openly bragged about blocking access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for women all across this country.\par \par \uc2 enltrAmerican women are not stupid\u8212\'20\'14and we are not going to trust the futures of our daughters and granddaughters to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, who have openly bragged about blocking access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rFYAC9iukk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rFYAC9iukk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@ewarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1827747323897663997?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 She added that she suspects conservative activists could use the Comstock Act, a 19th-century anti-obscenity law which bans mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials, to enforce a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the former president clinches a second presidency with Vance as his running mate. She said it would not be all that \u8220\'20\'1Chard to accomplish\u8221\'20\'1D with \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right person [in] the Department of Justice and one of their extremist judges out in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstand this: today 30% of all women live in states that effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said, referring to how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 US states}}}\uc2  have enacted near-total bans on the procedure since the 2022 \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling that eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance in the White House \u8211\'20\'13 it won\u8217\'20\'19t be 30%. It\u8217\'20\'19ll be 100%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , at a campaign event in northern Virginia, was asked he would consider appointing \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  to the post of health and human services secretary if he were re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Trump said they had not talked about it but said Kennedy \u8220\'20\'1Cknows a lot about the subject,\u8221\'20\'1D and that he had made a good impression within the Republican party, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Max Kennedy, the brother of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , also condemned his sibling\u8217\'20\'19s decision to suspend his independent presidential campaign and endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/opinion/story/2024-08-25/robert-kennedy-donald-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  on Sunday, Max Kennedy said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was exactly the kind of arrogant, entitled bully\u8221\'20\'1D that his father, the former US senator and attorney general Robert F Kennedy, stood against before he was assassinated in 1968 as he pursued the Democratic presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Max Kennedy predicted his father would have admired \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  because she was a former prosecutor as well. \u8220\'20\'1CHer career, like his, has been all about decency, dignity, equality, democracy and justice for all,\u8221\'20\'1D Max Kennedy wrote.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m heartbroken over my brother Bobby\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s life was dedicated to promoting the safety, security and happiness of the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/25/rfk-jr-brother-heartbroken-trump-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\u8217\'20\'19s brother \u8216\'20\'18heartbroken\u8217\'20\'19 over Trump endorsement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kerry Kennedy, the sister of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusted\u8221\'20\'1D by his decision to drop out and endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to MSNBC on Sunday, Kerry Kennedy said she planned to \u8220\'20\'1Cseparate and dissociate myself from \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr.\uc2  in this flagrant and inexplicable effort to desecrate and trample and set fire to my father\u8217\'20\'19s memory,\u8221\'20\'1D adding:\par \par \uc2 I think if my dad were alive today, the real Robert Kennedy would have detested almost everything \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  represents.\par \par \uc2 enltrKerry Kennedy: I am disgusted by my brother\u8217\'20\'19s obscene embrace of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And I completely disavow and dissociate myself from \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr.\uc2  and his flagrant efforts to desecrate my father's memory. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iW8pmRQRdn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iW8pmRQRdn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1827753489176637570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Larry Sabato\uc2 , the director of the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s center for politics and editor in chief the election forecaster the Crystal Ball, said he believes \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to drop out of the presidential race will not have a substantial effect on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  his independent presidential campaign and endorsed Trump. His running mate, Nicole Shanahan, said he was considering dropping out \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause we draw votes from Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But \u8220\'20\'1Cfew people will vote for another candidate just because their candidate drops out and endorses someone else,\u8221\'20\'1D Sabato said.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re going to split, some for the Democrat, some for the Republican, some are going to vote for one of the other independents, and others will just sit on the couch. They won\u8217\'20\'19t vote at all.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brian Fallon, a senior adviser for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/26/trump-harris-election-debate-updates?page=with:block-66cca07c8f089e7649977103#block-66cca07c8f089e7649977103"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest comments }}}\uc2  saying that whether or not the microphones are unmuted in the presidential debate \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter\u8221\'20\'1D to him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this resolved, everything is now set for Sept 10th,\u8221\'20\'1D Fallon posted to X.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump said unmuting the mics \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter to me.\u8221\'20\'1D Always suspected it was something his staff wanted, not him personally.\par \par \uc2 With this resolved, everything is now set for Sept 10th. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l98QiTD9lh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/l98QiTD9lh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Fallon (@brianefallon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianefallon/status/1828089108734054572?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he would rather have microphones unmuted during debate with Harris\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would rather keep microphones on during a scheduled televised debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  next month, despite his campaign team pushing to keep the same rules as in a previous debate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , when participants\u8217\'20\'19 microphones were turned off when it was not their turn to speak.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would want the microphone unmuted between exchanges, Trump said it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter to me\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d rather have it probably on, but the agreement was that it would be the same as it was last time. In that case, it was muted. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t like it the last time, but it worked out fine.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jake__traylor?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jake__traylor}}}\uc2  : "Would you want the microphones muted in the debate whenever you're not speaking?"\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : "We agreed to the same rules. I don't know, doesn't matter to me.... The agreement was that it would be the same as it was last time. In that case, it was muted." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l7d7Odd7cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l7d7Odd7cb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC Politics (@NBCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCPolitics/status/1828085210996424722?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 According to a Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/08/26/kamala-harris-donald-trump-debate-abc-microphones-00176294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  report, }}}\uc2  negotiations between the Trump and Harris campaigns over the 10 September ABC News debate broke down over the turning off of the participants\u8217\'20\'19 microphones when it was not their turn to speak.\par \par \uc2 The report said that the Harris campaign is demanding that the microphones be left \u8220\'20\'1Chot\u8221\'20\'1D at all times, while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has insisted Harris was reneging on terms agreed for the debate by the Biden campaign when it accepted the 10 September date.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  expected to endorse Trump at Detroit event, reports say\par \par \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , the former Democratic Hawaii congresswoman, is expected to formally endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid today at his event in Detroit, Michigan, CNN is reporting, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard, an Iraq war veteran, had been floated as a potential Trump vice-presidential pick. The former Democrat fell out with her party after standing in the 2020 presidential primaries after being smeared by Hillary Clinton as a \u8220\'20\'1CRussian asset\u8221\'20\'1D. That generated a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=0000016f-cdbf-df03-a1ff-fdbffaf00000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  in which Gabbard alleged that Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion she was the Democratic candidate favored by Russia was \u8220\'20\'1Cretribution\u8221\'20\'1D for Gabbard backing Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s rival Bernie Sanders in the 2016 primary.\par \par \uc2 Gabbard has been helping Trump prepare for next month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , although Trump has since threatened to pull out of the 10 September debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Actor Billy Baldwin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/rfk-jr-trump-billy-baldwin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as a former friend on Sunday while accusing him of betraying his values and selling his political soul after the independent presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended his campaign and endorsed }}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were friends,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin wrote in a lengthy post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BillyBaldwin/status/1827838134849077671?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1827838134849077671%7Ctwgr%5E3e37b582d1bf718470c722aee4b224950b0ff703%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Farticle%2F2024%2Faug%2F26%2Frfk-jr-trump-billy-baldwin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I loved his politics. His speeches inspired me. We were neighbors. Our kids were friends. We carpooled the kids to school for a few years.\par \par \uc2 But now the actor said he has \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely\u8221\'20\'1D disavowed and dissociated from Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 Baldwin described Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Cnot only a betrayal of the values and traditions of the Kennedy family\u8221\'20\'1D but also an act of \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical cowardice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI have known Bobby Kennedy Jr. for decades.\par \par \uc2 We were friends.\par \par \uc2 I loved his politics.\par \par \uc2 His speeches inspired me.\par \par \uc2 We were neighbors.\par \par \uc2 Our kids were friends.\par \par \uc2 We carpooled the kids to school for a few years.\par \par \uc2 Bobby Kennedy\uc2  has had presidential ambitions his entire adult life.\par \par \uc2 In 2006,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Be6JGWn5i2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Be6JGWn5i2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Billy Baldwin (@BillyBaldwin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BillyBaldwin/status/1827838134849077671?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The rebuke from Baldwin adds to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/25/rfk-jr-brother-heartbroken-trump-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of blowback}}}\uc2  against Kennedy for his support of the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/26/trump-harris-election-debate-updates?page=with:block-66cc8fa38f089e7649976ff0#block-66cc8fa38f089e7649976ff0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit}}}\uc2  to the Arlington national cemetery in Virginia today comes after comments earlier this month that the Presidential Medal of Freedom \u8211\'20\'13 a civilian award \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than the Medal of Honor given to service members.\par \par \uc2 Trump was talking about giving Miriam Adelson, a wealthy Republican donor, the Medal of Freedom, which he said was \u8220\'20\'1Cactually much better\u8221\'20\'1D than the Medal of Honor \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause everyone (who) gets the congressional medal of honor, that\u8217\'20\'19s soldiers,\u8221\'20\'1D adding:\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re either in very bad shape because they\u8217\'20\'19ve been hit so many times by bullets, or they\u8217\'20\'19re dead.\par \par \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff and a retired Marine General, later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/08/19/politics/john-kelly-donald-trump-medal-of-honor/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected }}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments and said the two honors are \u8220\'20\'1CNot even close. No equivalency of any kind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 A judge in Arizona will hear arguments today in the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D case involving a scheme by Republican allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win in the state during the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and Christina Bobb, who serves as the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top lawyer on election integrity, are among the 18 defendants in the case.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/22/trump-fake-elector-scheme-case-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of seven states}}}\uc2  where Trump and his allies sought to install \u8220\'20\'1Calternate\u8221\'20\'1D electors who claimed Trump won in their states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris mark Afghanistan withdrawal anniversary\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  issued statements today marking the third anniversary of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 In her statement, Harris said she mourns the 13 American service members who were killed in the bombing outside the Kabul airport, in which more than 100 Afghans were also killed. Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Today and everyday, I mourn and honor them. My prayers are with their families and loved ones. My heart breaks for their pain and their loss. These 13 devoted patriots represent the best of America, putting our beloved nation and their fellow Americans above themselves and deploying into danger to keep their fellow citizens safe.\par \par \uc2 She added that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cmade the courageous and right decision to end America\u8217\'20\'19s longest war\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that she will \u8220\'20\'1Cnever hesitate to take whatever action necessary to counter terrorist threats and protect the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement paid tribute to the 13 Americans who died as \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriots in the highest sense\u8221\'20\'1D who \u8220\'20\'1Cembodied the very best of who we are as a nation: brave, committed, selfless\u8221\'20\'1D. He added:\par \par \uc2 Today, our longest war is over. But our commitment to preventing attacks on our homeland \u8212\'20\'14 or our people \u8212\'20\'14 never will be. We will continue to disrupt terrorist activity, wherever we find it. We will continue to deliver justice to terrorists who plot against America \u8212\'20\'14 just as we have over the last three years with the leader of al-Qaeda and the global leader of \uc2 ISIS\uc2 . And we will do so without deploying thousands of American troops to ground wars overseas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited Arlington national cemetery in Virginia on Monday to take part in a wreath laying ceremony to mark the third anniversary of the US withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential nominee has regularly attacked the Biden administration over the chaotic pullout and attack at Kabul airport\u8217\'20\'19s Abbey Gate that killed 13 American soldiers, and will be seeking to tie his Democratic opponent, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to those events.\par \par \uc2 Trump is then scheduled to visit Michigan to address \uc2 the National Guard Association of the United States\uc2  conference.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign remains jittery about the prospect of a power struggle inside the inner circle that could become a major distraction just months until the 2024 election, even if? the jockeying for influence by top officials has ended with a truce, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/15/trump-campaign-new-advisers-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 momentary power play among the senior advisers}}}\uc2  is widely seen to be over, for now, after the 2016 campaign chief, \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , distanced himself from suggestions he was returning to the fold to run the campaign and the current leadership remained in their roles. (Lewandowski was brought on the current campaign as an adviser.)\par \par \uc2 But there has been trepidation that if the Trump campaign hits more rough patches in the race against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , any disagreements for instance on strategy between Lewandowski and the current chiefs, Susie Wiles and Chris LaCivita, could cause a blow-up, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/trump-campaign-palace-intrigue-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears within Trump campaign that palace intrigue could cause distraction}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 It is not the first time that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/kamala-harris-takes-7-point-lead-over-donald-trump-national-poll-1943901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trails }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/kamala-harris-takes-7-point-lead-over-donald-trump-national-poll-1943901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/kamala-harris-takes-7-point-lead-over-donald-trump-national-poll-1943901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  by seven points nationally}}}\uc2  in a new \uc2 Fairleigh Dickinson University\uc2  poll published at the weekend, has sowed doubt over his debate appearance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now I say, why should I do a debate? I\u8217\'20\'19m leading in the polls. And, everybody knows her, everybody knows me,\u8221\'20\'1D he told \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2  on \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  earlier this month after Harris replaced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the top of the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 He stated he had pledged instead to take part in a 4 September debate on Fox News, to which the Harris campaign did not agree, saying he would see Harris there \u8220\'20\'1Cor not at all\u8221\'20\'1D, before changing his mind again.\par \par \uc2 Harris, meanwhile, seized on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wavering commitment before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-atlanta-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lively crowd}}}\uc2  at a rally in Atlanta, Georgia, last month. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you got something to say, say it to my face,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign says it has now raised $540m for its election battle against Republican nominee and former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The campaign has had no problems getting supporters to open their wallets since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced on July 21 he was ending his campaign and quickly endorsed Harris, The Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The campaign said it saw a surge of donations during last week\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic National Convention in Chicago where Harris and her vice presidential running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , accepted their nominations.\par \par \uc2 Just before Vice President Harris\u8217\'20\'19 acceptance speech Thursday night, we officially crossed the $500 million mark. Immediately after her speech, we saw our best fundraising hour since launch day,\u8221\'20\'1D campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  wrote in a memo released by the campaign yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also proven to be a formidable fundraiser, but appears to be outpaced in her month-old campaign. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and its related affiliates announced earlier this month that they had raised $138.7m in July \u8212\'20\'14 less than what Harris took in during her White House bid\u8217\'20\'19s opening week. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign reported $327m in cash on hand at the start of August.\par \par \uc2 The Harris fundraising totals were raised by Harris for President, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , and joint fundraising committees.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  raising doubts about his participation in his first debate with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  , scheduled for September 10, there is also an argument about the rules for the set piece.\par \par \uc2 In the debate between Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  on June 27, which went {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-withdraw-democrat-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so badly}}}\uc2  for Biden that it precipitated his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropping out}}}\uc2  of his re-election race, the agreed rule was that while one candidate was taking his turn to speak, the other\u8217\'20\'19s microphone would be muted.\par \par \uc2 That was the expected rule {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/kamala-harris-trump-debate-abc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for September 10}}}\uc2 . Trump and Biden had been due to debate again then, on ABC, but now Harris is the Democratic nominee. She wants it to go ahead, had insisted that it should go ahead when Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/donald-trump-agrees-debate-kamala-harris-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initially bridled}}}\uc2  after she took over the Democratic ticket, but now wants to tweak the rule.\par \par \uc2 Brian Fallon, the senior adviser for communications at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s election campaign, issued a statement, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have told ABC and other networks seeking to host a possible October debate that we believe both candidates\u8217\'20\'19 mics should be live throughout the full broadcast,\u8221\'20\'1D Brian Fallon, the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s senior adviser for communications, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team is protesting, as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 election}}}\uc2  moves into high gear.\par \par \uc2 Rick Wilson, the co-founder of the Republican anti-Trump organization the Lincoln Project, wasn\u8217\'20\'19t mincing words on X.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonnie Chickenshit is afraid to debate Harris. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6AHjQj0SV9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6AHjQj0SV9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rick Wilson (@TheRickWilson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheRickWilson/status/1827909984556106106?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More of that Harris statement:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Harris campaign is arguing the mics should NOT be muted at the upcoming debates.\par \par \uc2 Senior comms advisor Brian Fallon:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Vice President is ready to deal with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s constant lies\u8230\'20\'26 Trump should stop hiding behind the mute button."\par \par \uc2 h/t {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @edokeefe}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zf5HYAKJme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zf5HYAKJme}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 aaron navarro (@aaronlarnavarro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aaronlarnavarro/status/1828044117462438270?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 First Trump-Harris debate in jeopardy as campaigns spar\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  threw into question last night his intended participation in the presidential debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on September 10, to be hosted by the ABC News TV network.\par \par \uc2 The former US president and now, once again, the Republican nominee for the White House, has kicked off a fresh fuss, beginning last night when he posted on his social media platform that he thinks the network is biased against him.\par \par \uc2 He asked in a Truth Social post just after 10pm on the US east coast: \u8220\'20\'1CWhy would I do the debate against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on that network?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a classic, Trumpian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113025866788629314"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  he called ABC, one of the three largest mainstream terrestrial TV networks, \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D, said its chief Washington correspondent, \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  (deliberately misspelled), conducted a \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous and biased\u8221\'20\'1D interview with a Republican congressman, Tom Cotton, and a \u8220\'20\'1Cso-called panel of Trump haters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He called out Democratic strategist Donna Brazile (also misspelled) and called veteran ABC anchor and political operator George Stephanopoulos \u8220\'20\'1CLiddle George Slopodopolus\u8221\'20\'1D. Politico was first to report the news, also saying that, according to sources \u8220\'20\'1Cthe two campaigns hit an impasse over the rules of the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D More on that next.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris argue over first debate\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers, there\u8217\'20\'19s no slowing down after the Democratic National Convention in Chicago last week, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/harris-convention-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/harris-convention-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  was officially anointed as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee}}}\uc2 , with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate. This week, they and their Republican opponents, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance are on a campaign blitz: Democrats heading south, GOP heading north. And, kicking off Monday morning, there\u8217\'20\'19s a loud argument under way about a different matter.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s in store:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now protesting about the first debate with his Democratic opponent for the White House, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , being on ABC News, according to fresh reports. He\u8217\'20\'19s arguing that the TV news network is too biased against him and he\u8217\'20\'19s questioning whether he will go ahead with it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election campaign team, meanwhile, is now asking that the debate rules allow \u8220\'20\'1Chot mics\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 ie that each candidate\u8217\'20\'19s microphone is on all the time, and therefore that interjections will be audible, rather than the rules agreed prior to her replacing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the top of the ticket, that if it\u8217\'20\'19s not your turn to speak your mic will be muted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign is waiting to see if their nominee and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post-convention bump in the polls}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Team Harris announced a post-DNC fundraising bump, saying that straight after Harris\u8217\'20\'19s convention speech on Thursday, Harris-Walz saw its best hour of fundraising since it launched just a few weeks ago, with $540m raised in total since Biden announced he was dropping out of his re-election race on 21 July.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Campaign swing stateblitzes are in store this week from both parties\u8217\'20\'19 candidates. Trump and his running mate, JD Vance, between them are planning three stops in Michigan and, at current billing, one in Wisconsin and one in Pennsylvania; Harris and Walz are embarking on a bus tour of southern Georgia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In just 11 days the first mail-in ballots will be sent to voters to begin defining their choices for president, Congress and measures up and down the ballot, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in some states, in this pivotal 2024 election. In-person voting begins in less than a month, on September 20.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign remains jittery about the prospect of a power struggle inside the inner circle that could become a major distraction just months until the 2024 election, even if? the jockeying for influence by top officials has ended with a truce, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/trump-campaign-palace-intrigue-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears within Trump campaign that palace intrigue could cause distraction}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240826ek8q0020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
