\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Trump campaign fears grow over possible internal discord\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,100 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2024\par 11:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Return of 2016 chief sparks concerns of tensions distracting voters as election looms. Plus, man taking on taking on TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s gambling influencersDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign remains nervous about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co.uk/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/trump-campaign-palace-intrigue-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possibility of a power struggle among key figures}}}\uc2  that could dissuade the electorate from voting for him in November, according to sources close to the matter.\par \par \uc2 Its current leadership, Susie Wiles and Chris LaCivita, remain in the top jobs, and potential discord appears to have simmered down after the first manager of the 2016 campaign, \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , played down suggestions that he was returning to run Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 bid for the White House. However, people close to the matter warned there was potential for further tension if the campaign were to hit more rocky periods.\par \par \uc2 If Lewandowski were to disagree with Wiles and LaCivita, there is concern internally that it could form a significant distraction at a time when the Republican and Democratic tickets are roughly level in key swing state polls.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are the battleground states? Georgia, Arizona, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/25/trump-harris-swing-states-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this week will see both campaigns}}}\uc2  focus on Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Women aren\u8217\'20\'19t stupid\u8217\'20\'19 enough to believe Vance\u8217\'20\'19s US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban veto promise, says Warren\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren said women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co.uk/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/elizabeth-warren-jd-vance-nationwide-abortion-ban-veto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not buy JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s pledge that Trump}}}\uc2  would veto any national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed by Congress if elected in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican women are not stupid, and we are not going to trust the futures of our daughters and granddaughters to two men who have openly bragged about blocking access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for women all across this country,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic senator from Massachusetts said on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 With 30% of American women already living in US states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, Warren said this proportion would rise to 100% with Trump and Vance in power. Her comments come after the Ohio senator and Republican nominee for vice-president said Trump would use the presidency\u8217\'20\'19s veto powers to overrule a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 a promise Democrats believe is a lie in light of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How could \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be banned nationwide under Trump? Warren said she believed conservative activists could use the Comstock Act of 1873, which bans mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related information, backed by supportive figures in the Department of Justice and judiciary.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s response to the killing of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  chief in Tehran will be \u8216\'20\'18definite and calculated\u8217\'20\'19, foreign minister says\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Abbas Araghchi\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/aug/26/israel-gaza-war-live-ceasefire-hezbollah-lebanon-iran-middle-east-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66cc2d348f089e7649976c31#block-66cc2d348f089e7649976c31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has reportedly said Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s response}}}\uc2  to the killing of the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  political chief in the Iranian capital would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinite and calculated\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Iran blames Israel for the assassination of \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2  on 31 July. In a phone call with his Italian counterpart, \uc2 Antonio Tajani\uc2 , Araghchi was quoted by Iran\u8217\'20\'19s state media as calling it \u8220\'20\'1Can unforgivable violation of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s security and sovereignty\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Israel\u8217\'20\'19s government officially refused to comment on Haniyeh\u8217\'20\'19s death, the strike has been widely seen as an Israeli operation. \u8220\'20\'1CIran does not seek to increase tensions. However, it is not afraid of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Araghchi told Tajani. He added that Iran\u8217\'20\'19s response would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinite, calculated and accurate\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the statement.\par \par \uc2 The statement came after Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , vowed that Israeli airstrikes targeting Iran-backed \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rockets in southern Lebanon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/25/netanyahu-says-attacks-on-hezbollah-in-lebanon-not-the-end-of-the-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot the end of the story\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , following the heaviest trading of fire between the two sides since the Gaza war started more than 10 months ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the mood in the region? \uc2 Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson, Sufain Qudah, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/aug/26/israel-gaza-war-live-ceasefire-hezbollah-lebanon-iran-middle-east-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66cbc2268f089e76499769cd#block-66cbc2268f089e76499769cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said that}}}\uc2  escalating tensions between Israel and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  could trigger a \u8220\'20\'1Cregional war\u8221\'20\'1D, mirroring earlier comments made by Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s president, Abdel Fatah al-Sisi.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The body of a 33-year-old woman has been found three days after she was carried away by a flash flood\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/25/grand-canyon-colorado-river-flash-flood-arizona-woman-missing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near the Grand Canyon}}}\uc2  in Arizona, officials have said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Macklemore has cancelled\par \par \uc2 his October show in Dubai in protest against the United Arab Emirates\u8217\'20\'19 role in the Sudan civil war,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/aug/26/macklemore-cancels-dubai-show-to-protest-uae-role-in-sudan-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where thousands of people have}}}\uc2  been killed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 1,600 people have been detained in Venezuela for protesting against Nicol\par \par \uc2 \u225\'00\'E1s Maduro\u8217\'20\'19s widely doubted claim to have won\par \par \uc2 the country\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election last month,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/26/nicolas-maduro-intent-third-term-1600-opponents-venezuela"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with many facing charges}}}\uc2  that could lead to decades in jail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Australian workers now have \u8220\'20\'1Cright to disconnect\u8221\'20\'1D after new laws came into force,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/aug/26/right-to-disconnect-laws-australia-boss-employer-work-calls-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meaning they can refuse}}}\uc2  to monitor work messages outside contracted hours, unless doing so is unreasonable.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Women may only make up a quarter of the top EU roles\par \par \uc2 Women might only make up between 22% and 26% of the next \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , which is expected to take office in December, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/26/von-der-leyen-set-to-miss-gender-balance-target-for-eu-top-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after EU governments ignored the commission president\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  request to propose two candidates, a man and a woman. This worst-case scenario would amount to a far worse gender imbalance than the previous commission, which took office in 2019 with 44% female representation.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Taking on TikTok\u8217\'20\'19s gambling influencers\par \par \uc2 When Rob Minnick was 23, he traveled 3,700 miles from New Jersey to Paris to explore the French capital. But when he got there, he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop excusing himself to get a quick hit of online gambling. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.co.uk/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/tiktok-gambling-addiction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now uses TikTok to raise awareness}}}\uc2  of problem gambling, which he believes the platform is helping to normalize among young people, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, it\u8217\'20\'19s David v Goliath.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check: \uc2 UN\uc2  chief to push for more climate action at Pacific leaders\u8217\'20\'19 summit\par \par \uc2 The general secretary of the \uc2 UN\uc2 , \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/24/pacific-leaders-summit-tonga-antonio-guterres-un-secretary-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will call for more climate action}}}\uc2  at an annual summit of Pacific leaders this week in Tonga. Pacific island nations are among the most vulnerable to rising sea levels and temperature increases. Regional leaders will be hoping for more financial support for their climate and disaster initiatives.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: What do the Trump campaign and being stuck next to a screaming child on a plane have in common?\par \par \uc2 With 70 days to go until the election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/picture/2024/aug/26/edith-pritchett-week-in-venn-diagrams-cartoon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edith Pritchett compares}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign to what she characterizes as a similarly trying ordeal.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240826ek8q001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
