\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris urges America to choose \u8216\'20\'18freedom and fairness\u8217\'20\'19 over Trump extremism \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Chris Stein in Chicago and Sam Levin(earlier) \par \uc2 11,718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2024\par 06:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find all of our US elections coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. Here is Joan E Greve\u8217\'20\'19s piece on the last night of the DNC:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-nomination-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris pledges to \u8216\'20\'18chart a new way forward\u8217\'20\'19 as she accepts nomination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Harris makes forceful speech \u8211\'20\'13 and skewers the menace from Mar-a-Lago\par \par \uc2 It was not a political address for the ages. It was not even the best of the convention (no one can compete with the Obamas). But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  did enough in her speech accepting the Democratic presidential nomination on Thursday to put an exclamation mark on one of the most dramatic turnarounds in modern political history.\par \par \uc2 And she made you reflect that you would not want to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  facing her in next month\u8217\'20\'19s televised debate. A speech that was short on policy and poetry was nevertheless devastating in skewering the menace from Mar-a-Lago. Trump can expect the same kind of interrogation when the two go head to head that would make most mortals tremble.\par \par \uc2 Just over a month after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  exited the race and passed her the baton, this was the most important speech of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s career as she sought to build on the momentum of huge crowds, record fundraising and viral phenomena on social media. Long in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s shadow as vice-president, the primary objective was to make the American public comfortable with the notion of a President Harris regularly appearing on their screens.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/harris-convention-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris makes forceful speech \u8211\'20\'13 and skewers the menace from Mar-a-Lago}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  accepted the Democratic presidential nomination Thursday with a sweeping, pointed speech in which she vowed to prosecute the case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and carry the country to a brighter and fairer future.\par \par \uc2 In an address that balanced optimism with scathing criticism of her opponent, Harris acknowledged her \u8220\'20\'1Cunlikely\u8221\'20\'1D path to the nomination and extended her hand to voters of all political ideologies who believe in America\u8217\'20\'19s promise. Harris would make history if elected \u8211\'20\'13 as the first woman, first Black woman and first Asian American woman to serve as president \u8211\'20\'13 but she instead focused on the history that the country could change in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation, with this election, has a precious, fleeting opportunity to move past the bitterness, cynicism and divisive battles of the past, a chance to chart a new way forward \u8211\'20\'13 not as members of any one party or faction, but as Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told thousands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 She then said to roaring applause: \u8220\'20\'1COn behalf of everyone whose story could only be written in the greatest nation on Earth, I accept your nomination for president of the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The speech came just one month after Harris launched her campaign, following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from the presidential race. With the president\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Harris was able to quickly consolidate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 support and secure the nomination. Harris has enjoyed a wave of enthusiasm since entering the race, as most polls now show her pulling slightly ahead of Trump in the key battleground states that will determine the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-nomination-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris pledges to \u8216\'20\'18chart a new way forward\u8217\'20\'19 as she accepts nomination}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36am BST\par \par \uc2 This photograph is of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 great-niece, Amara, watching Harris make her speech. It was taken by Kevin Wurm, for Reuters:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Civil rights leader the Rev \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  brought out four of the exonerated Central Park Five, including Yusef Salaam, who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently elected}}}\uc2  to the New York City council. The survivors of wrongful incarceration spoke about the impact of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vicious attacks, which included his calls for execution of the group of innocent young men.\par \par \uc2 Salaam said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwanted us un-alive. He wanted us dead. Today we are exonerated because the actual perpetrator confessed and DNA proved it.\u8221\'20\'1D He noted that the former president refuses to recant his accusations against them, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHe dismisses the scientific evidence rather than admit he was wrong \u8230\'20\'26 He has never changed, and he never will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18am BST\par \par \uc2 In one of the most emotional moments of the four-day convention, survivors of gun violence took the stage to call for gun safety. The Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2 , who lost her son to gun violence, led the group, saying: \u8220\'20\'1COur losses do not weaken us. They strengthen our resolve. We will secure safer futures \u8230\'20\'26 We will organize. We will advocate. We will run for office.\u8221\'20\'1D Kim Rubio, the mother of 10-year-old Lexi, who was killed in Uvalde, Texas, talked about her child she \u8220\'20\'1Cwill never hold again\u8221\'20\'1D. And Abbey Clements, a teacher and survivor of the Sandy Hook elementary school shooting, recounted in detail the terror of the shooting, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI carry that horrific day with me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former congresswoman \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2  recounted her recovery from the assassination attempt she survived, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CKamala will be a great president. She is tough. She has grit. Kamala can beat the gun lobby. She can fight gun trafficking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-convention-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s big moment, and a message of hope: key takeaways from the Democratic convention\u8217\'20\'19s final night}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06am BST\par \par \uc2 After days of sustained pro-Palestinian protests calling for an arms embargo on Israel, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s final address offered both a defense of Israel and a call for Palestinian self-determination. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CI will always stand up for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself, and I will always ensure Israel has the ability to defend itself, because the people of Israel must never again face the horror \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  caused on October 7.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat has happened in Gaza over the past 10 months is devastating. So many innocent lives lost, desperate, hungry people fleeing for safety, over and over again, the scale of suffering is heartbreaking,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris continued. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden and I are working to end this war such that Israel is secure, the hostages are released, the suffering in Gaza ends, and the Palestinian people realize their right to dignity, security, freedom and self-determination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-convention-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s big moment, and a message of hope: key takeaways from the Democratic convention\u8217\'20\'19s final night}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56am BST\par \par \uc2 And the story you\u8217\'20\'19ve all been waiting for:\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  prepared to deliver the biggest speech of her career, one of the year\u8217\'20\'19s biggest rumours snowballed online and in the media about a potential surprise guest.\par \par \uc2 In an election campaign in which anything has seemed possible, a Democratic National Convention appearance by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/beyonce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9}}}\uc2 , whose song Freedom is the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s official song, seemed for a brief moment like it could be on the cards.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, TMZ published a story with the headline \u8220\'20\'1CBeyonc\u233\'00\'E9 Performing at DNC final night!!!\u8221\'20\'1D, reporting \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple sources in the know\u8221\'20\'1D had said she would \u8220\'20\'1Cbe the big surprise performer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Hill posted a story headlined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4843083-beyonce-performs-dnc-vice-presidential/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 to perform at Democratic convention: Sources}}}\uc2  and also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/blogs/in-the-know/4842936-beyonce-dnc-democratic-convention/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Nick Hutchins, who works for the progressive firm Swing Left, had posted on social media saying he heard a band at the convention rehearsing Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 songs, including \u8220\'20\'1CCuff It\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Florida Representative Frentrice Driskell also posted video of the band performing a Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 song.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/aug/23/democratic-national-convention-dnc-beyonce-performance-rumour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From buzz to fizzle as rumours of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 performance at DNC fly, then fade }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44am BST\par \par \uc2 The convention ended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/uncommitted-movement-deadline-delegates-democratic-convention-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without a Palestinian American speaker}}}\uc2  on the main stage, a key demand of the uncommitted movement. The Harris campaign and Democratic party faced increasing pressure throughout the week to include a Palestinian voice, particularly after parents of a \uc2 Hamas\uc2  hostage were given a speaking slot and delivered emotional testimony on Wednesday. Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and other high-profile Democrats and activists had called on the convention to find a way to accommodate the uncommitted delegates\u8217\'20\'19 request, but officials did not change the schedule.\par \par \uc2 Ruwa Romman, a Georgia state representative who wrote a speech for the convention to consider, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/08/dnc-speech-uncommitted-movement-harris-walz-ruwan-romman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 read her prepared remarks}}}\uc2  to a crowd gathered outside, instead. Abbas Alawieh, a leader of the uncommitted movement, told supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CThe scandal is that there are forces within Democratic party leadership who do not want us to talk about Palestinian human rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32am BST\par \par \uc2 More from a second post-speech gathering gathering, where, per the pool report, the crowd sang \u8220\'20\'1CHappy Anniversary\u8221\'20\'1D to Harris and Emhoff to the tune of Happy Birthday.\par \par \uc2 Harris said the campaign has been \u8220\'20\'1Cgruelling\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cuplifting.\u8221\'20\'1D She said the next days are going to be \u8220\'20\'1Crough and tough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight we\u8217\'20\'19re partying, tomorrow lets get back to work. Please wish me and my husband a happy anniversary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz spoke, and said that he had lost his voice. He thanked the convention staff, saying the \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry saw the best of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The second gentleman\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were almost parallel to his remarks at the first party talking about their first dance 10 years ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us, here is a look at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the DNC:\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s final speech offered a forceful rebuke of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and laid out the stakes of the election: \u8220\'20\'1CConsider not only the chaos and calamity when he was in office, but also the gravity of what has happened since he lost \u8230\'20\'26 Trump tried to throw away your votes. When he failed, he sent an armed mob to the United States Capitol, where they assaulted law enforcement \u8230\'20\'26 For an entirely different set of crimes, he was found guilty of fraud by a jury of everyday Americans and separately, found liable for committing sexual abuse \u8230\'20\'26 Consider the power he will have, especially after the United States supreme court just ruled that he would be immune from criminal prosecution. Just imagine \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with no guardrails.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She ended with a message of hope and optimism that has been a theme all week: \u8220\'20\'1CLet us show each other and the world who we are and what we stand for: freedom, opportunity, compassion, dignity, fairness and endless possibilities. We are the heirs to the greatest democracy in the history of the world and \u8230\'20\'26 we must be worthy of this moment. It is now our turn to do what generations before us have done, guided by optimism and faith, to fight for this country we love, to fight for the ideals we cherish.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-convention-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s big moment, and a message of hope: key takeaways from the Democratic convention\u8217\'20\'19s final night}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and her husband, Doug Emhoff, made brief remarks at a gathering after the DNC closing speech.\par \par \uc2 Today is their tenth wedding anniversary, and Emhoff, the first second gentleman, raised a toast to his wife.\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 So thank you for sharing this important day with us, but truly, thank you all so very much. I know who\u8217\'20\'19s in this room. I know what you do every day and what you have done to support everything that we care about, everything that we believe is possible. We are truly invested in the future of our country. Our fight is truly and deeply worn out. Love country, and I know we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna get this done. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut only if we understand you can party tonight and you need to work for the next 75 days or so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cits been a wonderful convention, and so much of it is about everyone who is here who dedicates so much of your time and love to our country. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna get this done!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then Emhoff spoke, saying:\par \par \uc2 It is hard to imagine, like, literally 10 years ago right now, we had just taken our vows, gotten married, and we\u8217\'20\'19re probably likely no that\u8217\'20\'19s just literally, like probably having our first dance. And then to think about, literally, 10 years later, to the night she gave one of, if not the greatest speeches.\par \par \uc2 But like she said, we haven\u8217\'20\'19t won anything yet, right? So it\u8217\'20\'19s just 70 odd days left. Let\u8217\'20\'19s I think tonight we can\u8217\'20\'19t have some fun. And unlike my great friend, Governor Walz, he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna he said he sleep when he\u8217\'20\'19s dead. That\u8217\'20\'19s extreme. I want to see her be president, so I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna sleep on November 6, celebrating you becoming our next president.\par \par \uc2 So join me in toasting my wife, the love of the love of my life, on our 10th anniversary. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not looking back. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going back. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking into the future with you as our next president. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , we love you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US politics and post-DNC coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01am BST\par \par \uc2 A look back at the conclusion of the Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 The fourth and final night of the Democratic national convention finished after \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7f8358f088d87b0e5dcde#block-66c7f8358f088d87b0e5dcde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Only 74 days remain until the 5 November election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what happened this evening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In her acceptance speech, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7fe3b8f0841a2a14c4da7#block-66c7fe3b8f0841a2a14c4da7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight for this country we love\u8221\'20\'1D, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7f93b8f0841a2a14c4d94#block-66c7f93b8f0841a2a14c4d94"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning}}}\uc2  of the \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely serious\u8221\'20\'1D consequences of electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who she described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunserious man\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris reflected on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7f6f88f088d87b0e5dcd8#block-66c7f6f88f088d87b0e5dcd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the role her mother played}}}\uc2  in influencing her career as a prosecutor, which was also inspired by a friend who was sexually abused.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-president said she would \u8220\'20\'1Calways stand up for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D, but also spoke of Gaza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7fc218f085d577f48753d#block-66c7fc218f085d577f48753d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe scale of suffering is heartbreaking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris described the election as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7f8358f088d87b0e5dcde#block-66c7f8358f088d87b0e5dcde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fleeting opportunity}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to move the country out of what she described as a political rut, while trying to appeal to the moderate and independent voters who could decide swing states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the Michigan governor and rising talent in the Democratic party, was one of the final speakers before Harris, and called her \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66c7eede8f0841a2a14c4d63#block-66c7eede8f0841a2a14c4d63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a total badass}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D who can be trusted in a crisis.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , the former congresswoman and gun safety advocate who suffered a brain injury in a 2011 assassination attempt that left six people dead, told the convention Harris could \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7e73a8f085d577f4874bb#block-66c7e73a8f085d577f4874bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beat the gun lobby}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Uncommittedmovement{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7d70f8f088d87b0e5dc1d#block-66c7d70f8f088d87b0e5dc1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not succeed}}}\uc2  in getting a Palestinian-American to speak from the convention stage, despite holding a sit-in outside the venue. Outside the security perimeter, Gaza solidarity protests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7d74f8f088d87b0e5dc20#block-66c7d74f8f088d87b0e5dc20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite plenty of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7fb908f0841a2a14c4d9d#block-66c7fb908f0841a2a14c4d9d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rumors}}}\uc2 , there was no special musical guest. Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 did not appear, nor did Taylor Swift, though we did see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7e8988f085d577f4874c1#block-66c7e8988f085d577f4874c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pink}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/22/kamala-harris-dnc-night-4?page=with:block-66c7dfff8f085d577f487493#block-66c7dfff8f085d577f487493"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Chicks}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats were \u8220\'20\'1Ceuphoric\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Coverjoyed\u8221\'20\'1D as they left their party\u8217\'20\'19s convention.\par \par \uc2 Charlene Dukes, a delegate from Maryland, said she shed a few tears as she watched \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  accept the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo know that we have the possibility to have the first woman, the first woman of color, who identifies as Black and Asian American \u8230\'20\'26 oh my goodness,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Dukes said she will return to Maryland \u8211\'20\'13 a blue state with a competitive senate race \u8211\'20\'13 with a renewed sense of determination to organize and mobilize voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue telling young people, middle-aged persons and seniors: you have the right to vote, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is our right and that determines the where this country is headed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic national convention concludes\par \par \uc2 And with that, the Democratic national convention has ended.\par \par \uc2 Now we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  can translate the energy in the convention hall into an election win. The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s next big moment in the public spotlight will come on 10 September, when she meets \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a debate in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 The convention hall is only slowly emptying out.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps people believe the rumored special musical guest will still appear, or they\u8217\'20\'19re just having too much fun with the balloons and confetti that continues to fall from on high.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and their entourages have left the stage after about 10 minutes as balloons dropped and confetti filled the air.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now hearing the convention\u8217\'20\'19s closing benediction.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 False Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 rumors spread throughout the night\par \par \uc2 There were widespread rumors that Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 was going to perform as a surprise guest on the final night of the convention, fueled by a TMZ report in the middle of the program, headlined, \u8220\'20\'1CBEYONC\u201\'00\'C9 PERFORMING AT DNC\u8217\'20\'19S FINAL NIGHT!!!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 never showed up. As the event was nearing the end, the star\u8217\'20\'19s representative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/politics-news/beyonce-not-attending-2024-dnc-1235982694/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a statement}}}\uc2  to the Hollywood Reporter, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CBeyonc\u233\'00\'E9 was never scheduled to be there. The report of a performance is untrue.\u8221\'20\'1D There were also rumors that Taylor Swift or another surprise guest would show up, but the night has ended without any celebrity surprises.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Moments after Harris ended her address, Doug Emhoff walked onstage as Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom\u8221\'20\'1D played.\par \par \uc2 Then came her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , and his wife, Gwen. The balloons dropped not longer after that, as the screen behind Harris played videos of supporters in swing states waving signs and dancing.\par \par \uc2 In the United Center, the crowd is waving American flags, and tossing around the red, white and blue balloons that fell from the ceiling.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls for Americans to 'fight for this country we love' as she wraps up convention address\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then wrapped up her address to the Democratic convention by again mentioning the lessons she learned from her mother.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, our opponents in this race are out there every day denigrating America, talking about how terrible everything is. Well, my mother had another lesson. She used to teach. Never let anyone tell you who you are, you show them who you are,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, let us show each other and the world who we are and what we stand for: freedom, opportunity, compassion, dignity, fairness and endless possibilities. We are the heirs to the greatest democracy in history of the world, and on behalf of our children and our grandchildren and all those who sacrificed so dearly for our freedom and liberty, we must be worthy of this moment. It is now our turn to do what generations before us have done, guided by optimism and faith, to fight for this country we love, to fight for the ideals we cherish and to uphold the awesome responsibility that comes with the greatest privilege on Earth, the privilege and pride of being an American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris signals support for ceasefire deal, calls Gaza war 'heartbreaking'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  addressed one of the most divisive issues before Democrats: Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith respect to the war in Gaza. President Biden and I are working around the clock, because now is the time to get a hostage deal and a ceasefire deal done,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She spoke forcefully against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and the October 7 attack, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI will always stand up for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself, and I will always ensure Israel has the ability to defend itself, because the people of Israel must never again face the war that a terrorist organization called \uc2 Hamas\uc2  caused on October 7.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris then turned to the devastation wreaked on Gaza by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion:\par \par \uc2 At the same time, what has happened In Gaza over the past 10 months is devastating. So many innocent lives lost, desperate, hungry people fleeing for safety, over and over again, the scale of suffering is heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 She then brought the crowd to their feet by declaring:\par \par \uc2 President Biden and I are working to end this war such that Israel is secure, the hostages are released, the suffering in Gaza ends, and the Palestinian people realize their right to dignity, security, freedom, and self-determination.\par \par \uc2 As she talked about her policy towards Israel, we could hear shouting in the United Center, but it was not clear what they were saying.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 More applause followed when Harris proclaimed: \u8220\'20\'1CWe trust women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe trust women, and when Congress passes a bill to restore reproductive freedom. As president of the United States, I will proudly sign it into law,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The United Center is filling with the sounds of boos, as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  recounts \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hand in the downfall of Roe v Wade, and the move by Republican-led states to ban access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFriends, I believe America cannot truly be prosperous unless Americans are fully able to make their own decisions about their own lives, especially on matters of heart and home. But tonight, in America, too many women are not able to make those decisions, and let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear about how we got here,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, then continued:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  handpicked members of the United States supreme court to take away reproductive freedom, and now he brags about it in his words, \u8220\'20\'1CI did it, and I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have done it.\u8221\'20\'1D Well, let me tell you, over the past two years, I\u8217\'20\'19ve traveled across our country, and women have told me their stories. Husbands and fathers have shared theirs stories of women miscarrying in a parking lot, developing sepsis, losing the ability to ever again have children, all because doctors are afraid they may go to jail for caring for their patients, couples just trying to grow their family, cut off in the middle of IVF treatments.\par \par \uc2 This is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in our country because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And understand he is not done as a part of his agenda. He and his allies would limit access to birth control, ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and enact a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, with or without Congress. And get this, get this, he plans to create a national anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordinator and force states to report on women\u8217\'20\'19s miscarriages and abortions.\par \par \uc2 After all that booing, Harris drew claps by declaring: \u8220\'20\'1CThey are out of their minds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris got the crowd chanting her campaign staple of \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back!\u8221\'20\'1D after she brought up Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s discussion of ending the department of eduction, as well as early education service Head Start.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back, and we are charting a new way forward, forward to a future with a strong and growing middle class, because we know a strong middle class has always been critical to America\u8217\'20\'19s success, and building that middle class will be a defining goal of my presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 In lengthy denunciation, Harris warns of 'extremely serious' consequences of re-electing Trump\par \par \uc2 Then, it was time to attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  described in a thorough denunciation as a threat to the country\u8217\'20\'19s way of governing and life.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn many ways, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an unserious man. But the consequences of putting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House are extremely serious,\u8221\'20\'1D she began, before laying out what those consequences would be:\par \par \uc2 Consider not only the chaos and calamity when he was in office, but also the gravity of what has happened since he lost the last election. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to throw away your votes. When he failed, he sent an armed mob to the United States Capitol, where they assaulted law enforcement officers. When politicians in his own party begged him to call off the mob and send help, he did the opposite. He fanned the flames, and now, for an entirely different set of crimes, he was found guilty of fraud by a jury of everyday Americans and separately, found liable for committing sexual abuse.\par \par \uc2 Consider what he intends to do if we give him power again. Consider his explicit intent to set free violent extremists who assaulted those law enforcement officers at the Capitol. His explicit intent to jail journalists political opponents, and anyone, he sees as the enemy, his explicit intent to deploy our active duty military against our own citizens.\par \par \uc2 Consider the power he will have, especially after the United States supreme court just ruled that he would be immune from criminal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Just imagine \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with no guardrails.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says November election represents 'fleeting opportunity' to move country forward\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then outlined her view of the stakes of this election, while trying to appeal to the moderate and independent voters who may make the difference in the crucial swing states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation, with this election, has a precious, fleeting opportunity to move past the bitterness, cynicism and divisive battles of the past, a chance to chart a new way forward not as members of any one party or faction, but as Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let me say, I know there are people of various political views, and I want you to know I promise to be a president for all Americans. You can always trust me to put country above party and self, to hold sacred America\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental principles, from the rule of law, to free and fair elections to the peaceful transfer of power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris accepts Democratic presidential nomination\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then accepted the Democratic presidential nomination:\par \par \uc2 So, on behalf of the people, on behalf of every American, regardless of party, race, gender or the language your grandmother speaks, on behalf of my mother and everyone who has ever set out on their own unlikely journey on behalf of Americans, like the people I grew up with, people who work hard, chase their dreams and look out for one another, on behalf of everyone whose story could only be written in the greatest nation on Earth. I accept your nomination for president of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 The room erupted into applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is now telling us about how her mother influenced her career path.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy mother was a brilliant, five-foot-tall brown woman with an accent, and as the eldest child, I saw how the world would sometimes treat her, but my mother never lost her cool,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was tough, courageous, a trailblazer in the fight for women\u8217\'20\'19s health, and she taught Maya and me a lesson that Michelle mentioned the other night. She taught us to never complain about injustice, but do something about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After deciding to be a lawyer, Harris recounted why she wanted to be a prosecutor:\par \par \uc2 When it came time to choose the type of law I would pursue, I reflected on a pivotal moment in my life. You see, when I was in high school, I noticed something about my best friend, Wanda. She was sad at school, and there were times she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to go home. So, one day, I asked if everything was all right, and she confided in me that she was being sexually abused by her stepfather, and I immediately told her she had to come stay with us, and she did.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the reasons I became a prosecutor, to protect people like Wanda, because I believe everyone has a right to safety, to dignity and to justice.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am BST\par \par \uc2 She then talked about her upbringing with her parents who moved around the country for various jobs and would eventually divorce, and the virtues they instilled in her.\par \par \uc2 My early memories of our parents together are very joyful ones, a home filled with laughter and music, Aretha, Coltrane and Miles at the park. My mother would say, stay close. But my father would say, as he smiled, run, Kamala, run. Don\u8217\'20\'19t be afraid. Don\u8217\'20\'19t let anything stop you.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39am BST\par \par \uc2 She began by thanking her husband, Doug Emhoff, and then \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 When I think about the path we have traveled together, Joe, I am filled with gratitude. Your record is inspiring, as history will show, and Doug and I love you, and Jill, and are forever thankful to you both.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 After a very long applause and lots of \u8220\'20\'1Cthank yous\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech is getting under way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COK, let\u8217\'20\'19s get to business,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 When she made a surprise and brief appearance on the convention\u8217\'20\'19s opening day, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wore a tan suit, which people interpreted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/kamala-harris-wore-a-tan-suit-to-day-one-of-the-dnc-what-does-it-mean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in all sorts of ways}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Today, she\u8217\'20\'19s in an all-black suit. Make of that what you will.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on stage to accept Democratic presidential nomination\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now on stage, where she will accept the Democratic presidential nomination in a speech that will be a crucial moment in her campaign to be elected president.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is only the second woman ever nominated for the presidency by a major political party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Roy Cooper represents what is for Democrats, at best, a purple state.\par \par \uc2 His speech has emphasized \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s moderate appeal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if you don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with her on everything, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will fight for you to the very end,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor parents who want better schools for their kids, for workers worried about a secure retirement for themselves, Kamala will fight for you. For any of our allies anywhere in the world wondering if America still has your back, remember this, Kamala will fight for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Now we\u8217\'20\'19re hearing from North Carolina governor Roy Cooper.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the last scheduled speaker before \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long claimed to be the party of patriots \u8211\'20\'13 the party that loves America and its military more.\par \par \uc2 But since Trump stormed on to the political stage, praising despots, mocking service-members, undermining faith in institutions and threatening to turn the military on US citizens, not to mention his role inciting his supporters on January 6, Democrats have attempted to reclaim the word.\par \par \uc2 Woven throughout the convention this week, speakers have encouraged chants of \u8220\'20\'1CU-S-A\u8221\'20\'1D. The line-up has included several members of the armed forces, with a heavy emphasis on Democrats commitment to protecting the constitution and preserving democracy.\par \par \uc2 Former defense secretary \uc2 Leon Panetta\uc2  said the country needed a \u8220\'20\'1Ctough, cool-headed commander-in-chief\u8221\'20\'1D who understood American values and was respected the world-over.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe stand united as veterans, Democrats and patriots,\u8221\'20\'1D congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , a former Marine who is running for Senate in Arizona, said on stage on Thursday night, surrounded by Democrats who have served in the military.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShow some respect,\u8221\'20\'1D he admonished Trump, recalling the former president\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on the late senator \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , a former prisoner of war.\par \par \uc2 The audience waved American flags and chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CU-S-A.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s now a curtain over the door leading to backstage that, if you were seated on far stage right, you could see speakers walking on to the stage.\par \par \uc2 Might it be a sign that the rumored surprise musical guest is up next?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , a Republican former congressman who served on the House committee that investigated the January 6 attack, accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of destroying his party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a Republican for 12 years in Congress, and I still hold on to the label. I never thought I\u8217\'20\'19d be here. But listen, you never thought you\u8217\'20\'19d see me here, did you? But I\u8217\'20\'19ve learned something about the Democratic party, and I want to let my fellow Republicans in on the secret the Democrats are as patriotic as us,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said.\par \par \uc2 He shared his thoughts on what the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s takeover of the GOP means for those who don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in his Maga agenda:\par \par \uc2 He puts on quite a show. But there is no real strength there. As a conservative and a veteran, I believe true strength lies in defending the vulnerable. It\u8217\'20\'19s in protecting your family. It\u8217\'20\'19s in standing up for our constitution and our democracy that that is the soul of being a conservative. It used to be the soul of being a Republican, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has suffocated the soul of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Whitmer calls Harris 'a total badass'\par \par \uc2 In praising \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  adopted a theme that has run through many Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 speeches at the convention thus far: that she would be a steady hand in times of crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, we\u8217\'20\'19ve all lived through a lot of history over the past few years,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know what the next four years will bring, but what we do know is this: through it all, your life won\u8217\'20\'19t stop. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to get to work, pick up the kids and pay your bills, and then one day, when you\u8217\'20\'19re just trying to get everyone out the door, a news alert goes off. Something happened. Something hit the fan. You\u8217\'20\'19ll ask, is my family going to be okay? And then you\u8217\'20\'19ll ask, who the hell is in charge? What if it\u8217\'20\'19s him? What if it\u8217\'20\'19s that man from Mar-a-Lago?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitmer then asked:\par \par \uc2 I know in a crisis, we need someone strong enough to come up with a plan to tell the truth and to bring people together. Right now, before the crisis, is when we get to choose. Why wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t we choose the leader who\u8217\'20\'19s tough, tested, and a total badass?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Eva Longoria: 'The energy is all across the country'\par \par \uc2 Actor and activist Eva Longoria just took the stage and said she\u8217\'20\'19s long known the vice-president:\par \par \uc2 I have known \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for more than a decade, and she comes from a family a lot like mine, and I\u8217\'20\'19m sure a lot like yours. We were both raised knowing that no one was going to hand us anything, especially as women, and we were going to have to touch every rung of the ladder to get ahead. We were going to have to work really hard \u8230\'20\'26 She worked at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , I worked at Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s, and look at us now.\par \par \uc2 The energy tonight isn\u8217\'20\'19t just here in Chicago, it\u8217\'20\'19s all across the country. People are gathered at watch parties everywhere to celebrate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Whitmer does the familiar compare and contrast of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  knows who she\u8217\'20\'19s fighting for, too. She took care of her mom, who also battled cancer. As president, she\u8217\'20\'19ll fight to lower the cost of health care and elder care for every family. She\u8217\'20\'19s lived a life like ours. She knows us,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer said.\par \par \uc2 Then on to Trump:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know you at all. You think he understands that when your car breaks down, you can\u8217\'20\'19t get to work. No, no. His first word was probably chauffeur.\par \par \uc2 You think he\u8217\'20\'19s ever had to take items out of the cart before checking out? Hell, you think he\u8217\'20\'19s ever been to a grocery store? That\u8217\'20\'19s what the chauffeur is for.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . She gets us. She sees us. She is us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  takes Democratic convention stage\par \par \uc2 Rising Democratic star \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, is now on stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Lansing, they call me governor, but in Detroit, they call me Big Gretch,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, then pivoted to the obligatory Trump diss:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called me that woman from Michigan, as an insult. Being a woman from Michigan is a badge of honor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Up now is congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , who is running for Senate in Arizona, a must-win seat if Democrats hope to keep their majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about how \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  have supported military veterans like himself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-president Harris has stood up for our families, always,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Of Walz, Gallego said that \u8220\'20\'1Chis passion for veterans has earned him respect on both sides of the aisle\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Then a group of veterans joined him on stage, who Gallego said, \u8220\'20\'1Cput country over politics. We are proud to wear the uniform.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Leon Panetta\uc2 , former secretary of defense, said Harris can take on tyrants\par \par \uc2 Leon Panetta\uc2 , former US secretary of defense, said \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctough, cool-headed commander-in-chief to defend our democracy from tyrants and terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 She knows a tyrant when she sees one, and our allies know a leader when they see one. On the Senate intelligence committee and as vice president, she worked with more than 150 world leaders. She\u8217\'20\'19s looked our allies in the eye and said, \u8216\'20\'18America has your back\u8217\'20\'19. Trump would abandon our allies and isolate America. We tried that in the 1930s \u8230\'20\'26 It was foolish and dangerous then, and it\u8217\'20\'19s foolish and dangerous now.\par \par \uc2 He continued, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump tells tyrants like Putin, they can do whatever the hell they want. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tells tyrants the hell you can, not on my watch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 : Trump 'sucked up to dictators'\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  just came back on stage alone to talk about foreign policy and security \u8211\'20\'13 topics we have not heard a ton about over the past three nights of the convention.\par \par \uc2 More specifically, he talked about how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be trusted to handle those issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  skipped his intelligence briefings. He was too busy sucking up to dictators and dreaming of becoming one himself,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said.\par \par \uc2 He then gave his view of the stakes of this election \u8211\'20\'13 which, he noted, will be close:\par \par \uc2 The alliances we\u8217\'20\'19ve spent decades building are too critical. That\u8217\'20\'19s whats at stake now. And the choice, the choice isn\u8217\'20\'19t even close. But in Arizona and nationwide, this election will be.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll win the same way we launch rockets into space and land fighter jets on aircraft carriers \u8211\'20\'13 as one team on one mission.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Pink performs with her daughter\par \par \uc2 Pink has just performed with her daughter, Willow, at the DNC:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The White House says he and Jill Biden called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cwish her luck\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of her marquee speech this evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Giffords tells convention: 'Kamala can beat the gun lobby'\par \par \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2  recounted her recovery from the assassination attempt, which left six people dead, and praised both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI learned to walk again, one step at a time. I learned to talk again, one word at a time. So many people helped me as I worked hard to recover, including a decent man for Delaware who always checked in he still does,\u8221\'20\'1D Giffords said, as \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  looked on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , thank you for everything. Joe is a great president. My friend, Kamala will be a great president. She is tough. She has grit. Kamala can beat the gun lobby. She can fight gun trafficking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2  addresses Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , the former congresswoman who survived a mass shooting that left her with injuries to her brain, is now onstage.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chanted \u8220\'20\'1CGabby! Gabby!\u8221\'20\'1D when she came out.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s with her husband, Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , and appears to be reading off a tablet on the podium.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to survivors of horrific mass shootings, we also heard from survivors of lesser-known killings.\par \par \uc2 Edgar Vilchez of Chicago recounted how a classmate of his was killed in school, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of worrying about taking a test, I started worrying about living to take another test.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the shooting left him traumatized, Vilchez added that, \u8220\'20\'1CI learned something new, too: that we can write a new story, if we choose to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 The discussion began with Abbey Clements, a survivor of the 2012 massacre at an elementary school in Newtown, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 She recounted hearing the sounds of the shooting, which left dead 20 children and six adult staff members, then said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey should still be here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now getting into one of the more somber parts of the evening: a discussion of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Lucy McBath\uc2 , whose son was shot dead, is to lead the discussion, which will feature people from communities where mass shootings have happened.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Kerry Washington taught the crowd how to correctly pronounce \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CConfusion is understandable. Disrespect is not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She brought out two of the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s nieces to teach the crowd the lesson.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CConfusion is understandable. Disrespect is not,\u8221\'20\'1D Kerry Washington says of pronouncing Harris\u8217\'20\'19s first name. She then gets help from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s grand-nieces to properly pronounce her name. It\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccomma\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Cla.\u8221\'20\'1D They lead a chant.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1826789209790624178?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of the moment:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden tunes into Democratic convention from vacation in California\par \par \uc2 We haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard much from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  since he departed for vacation in California\u8217\'20\'19s Santa Barbara wine country after delivering the convention\u8217\'20\'19s keynote address on Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 On X, he said he\u8217\'20\'19s looking forward to watching \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech this evening, and tweeted a photo of him and Jill Biden tuned in to the convention:\par \par \uc2 enltrJill and I just spoke to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 we can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to watch her accept this historic nomination.\par \par \uc2 Kamala and Tim will inspire a generation and lead us into the future. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/guKuTevT8F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/guKuTevT8F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1826789597600256189?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 After Kerry Washington exited the stage, the crowd began chanting \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Onstage now is the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s niece Meena Harris, her stepdaughter Ella Emhoff, and her goddaughter Helena Hudlin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s fighting for social justice, health justice, environmental justice and she isn\u8217\'20\'19t alone. We\u8217\'20\'19re all in this together\u8221\'20\'1D, said Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo let\u8217\'20\'19s keep up the fight, let\u8217\'20\'19s keep up the joy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hudlin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let\u8217\'20\'19s elect this extraordinary woman as our next president,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Harris. The trio then hugged and walked off stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Kerry Washington energizes the crowd\par \par \uc2 Actor Kerry Washington has now taken the stage:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I stand here, I know that there are folks on social media already saying, \u8216\'20\'18Go back to your TV show, shut up and act.\u8217\'20\'19 But I am not here tonight as an actor. I am here as a mother, as a daughter, as a proud union member, as the granddaughter of immigrants, as a Black woman descended from enslaved people. I am here tonight because I am an American and because I am a voter, and because we the people are stronger when all our voices are heard.\par \par \uc2 The Scandal actor, a longtime Democratic activist, is joined by Tony Goldwyn, her former co-star and a previous host. She is now having everyone on the crowd film videos of this moment, chanting: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we fight, we win!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The Chicks take the stage\par \par \uc2 The Chicks have just sung the national anthem at the convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 After a daylong sit-in, uncommitted delegates entered the United Center to take their seats among their state delegations on the floor.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference outside, movement leaders said they do not plan to disrupt the evening\u8217\'20\'19s events inside.\par \par \uc2 The movement is calling for Harris or senior members of her team to meet with them in Michigan to talk about a ceasefire and arms embargo. They set a 15 September deadline for a meeting.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe uncommitted delegates have peacefully entered the arena hand in hand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wA5DAcyHKl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wA5DAcyHKl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Uncommitted National Movement ?? (@uncommittedmvmt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/uncommittedmvmt/status/1826780703716982862?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  enters convention hall\par \par \uc2 The convention jumbotron has just shown \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , who is sitting somewhere in the packed United Center.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re in the middle of a musical interlude that\u8217\'20\'19s gone on for a few minutes. Delegates are waving American flags, and Bruce Springsteen \u8217\'20\'19s Born in the USA is playing.\par \par \uc2 There may be more music to come. A single microphone is set up on stage, in place of the podium. Could it be our surprise guest?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Octavia Spencer and Sheryl Lee Ralph in attendance\par \par \uc2 Oscar-winning actor Octavia Spencer was spotted in the crowd at the convention:\par \par \uc2 Emmy winner Sheryl Lee Ralph, from the hit TV show Abbott Elementary, is seating next to her:\par \par \uc2 Actor Kerry Washington, from the TV show Scandal, is due to speak tonight, one of many celebrities who have taken the stage throughout the week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestinian activists march outside the convention\par \par \uc2 Thousands of pro-Palestinian activists have left Union Park in Chicago and are marching past the convention center where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is due to accept the democratic nomination in just hours. Activist delegates are holding a sit-in near the convention center to demand that a Palestinian American be allowed to address the convention before it concludes on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, protestors holding flags and signs calling Harris \u8220\'20\'1CKiller Kamala\u8221\'20\'1D demanded an end to US military aid to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Michael, who said his family was Palestinian and Irish, said that he was marching to \u8220\'20\'1Cdemand that the US stop funding genocide\u8221\'20\'1D and said that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to listen to us and empathize with ordinary Palestinians\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been locked out and exiled,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The protestors chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CIntifada! Revolution! \u8230\'20\'26 End the occupation! \u8230\'20\'26 It is right to rebel! Democrats go to hell! \u8230\'20\'26 Just like 1968! Nothing here to celebrate!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of police officers, some in riot helmets, are lining the protest route near the United Center.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2  star Steph Curry says of Harris: 'The Oval Office suits her well'\par \par \uc2 We just had the first surprise celebrity appearance of the night: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/jul/24/midas-touch-how-to-shoot-like-steph-curry-paris-olympics-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBA star}}}\uc2  Stephen Curry, who likened the unity he has with his teammates on the basketball court to what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would bring, if elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThats why I believe that Kamala as president will bring that unity back and continue to move our country forward,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Oval Office suits her well,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, in the words of \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 : do something! Go vote! Be active!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  is not a surprise guest of the night, the Republican senator said, adding that he thinks it will be Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 or Taylor Swift:\par \par \uc2 enltrContrary to fake news posts, I am not the surprise guest at the DNC tonight. My guess is that it will be Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 or Taylor Swift. So disappointing, I know!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  (@MittRomney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MittRomney/status/1826767490137161906?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Rumors have swirled that in addition to a powerhouse surprise musical guest, there could be a surprise high-profile Republican speaker, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if there\u8217\'20\'19s any validity to that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 In her remarks tonight, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will speak about her late mother, Shyamala Gopalan Harris, a breast cancer researcher who immigrated to the United States from India at the age of 19.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s mother, who died of colon cancer in 2009, is an animating force in her life, a source of inspiration and the person who shaped her values. Harris describes her mother as the embodiment of the American dream, a striver who left her family and her country to pursue an education in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy mother was 19 when she crossed the world alone, traveling from India to California with an unshakeable dream to be the scientist who would cure breast cancer,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris will say.\par \par \uc2 Harris and her sister, Maya, who will also speak on Thursday night, were mostly raised by their mother. The vice-president has written that her mother raised her girls to be \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D Black women, knowing that is how her adopted country would view them. She was active in the civil rights movement, and surrounded herself with Black activists, artists and political thinkers.\par \par \uc2 Across the four days, several speakers have acknowledged the woman Harris had called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most important person in my life.\u8221\'20\'1D In her remarks, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  invoked her and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s mothers, placing in a line of American women who have pushed their daughters toward progress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy friends, the future is here,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish my mother and Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s mother could see us. They would say, \u8216\'20\'18Keep going.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Uncommitted movement's deadline for speaker decision passes without answer from DNC\par \par \uc2 A deadline set by the Uncommitted movement for an answer from the Democratic national convention\u8217\'20\'19s organizers to their request for a Palestinian American to address delegates has passed, with no response from the organizers.\par \par \uc2 Delegates and activists from the movement are continuing their sit in outside the United Center, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth}}}\uc2  report, it now seems clear that the convention will not agree to their demands:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic national convention}}}\uc2  failed to make a 6pm CT deadline that the ceasefire delegates had set for a final decision on allowing a Palestinian American to speak from the main stage.\par \par \uc2 In a press conference outside the convention around 7pm CT, Abbas Alawieh, a leader of the uncommitted movement and an uncommitted delegate from Michigan, denounced the convention\u8217\'20\'19s failure to listen to their demands.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe scandal is that there are forces within Democratic party leadership who do not want us to talk about Palestinian human rights,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re out of step with the majority of the Democratic base, the majority of Democratic voters who believe that Palestinian human rights are a priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ruwa Romman, a Georgia state representative who wrote a speech for the convention to consider, read her speech to the crowd gathered outside. Earlier on Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/08/dnc-speech-uncommitted-movement-harris-walz-ruwan-romman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mother Jones}}}\uc2  published the text, which began: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m honored to be the first Palestinian elected to public office in the great state of Georgia and the first Palestinian to ever speak at the Democratic national convention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group held an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/democratic-national-convention-uncommitted-delegates-protest-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impromptu}}}\uc2  sit-in on Wednesday after weeks of attempts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/uncommitted-gaza-democrats-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to get a speaker on the main stage}}}\uc2  at the convention. The movement had first requested that Dr Tanya Haj-Hassan, a doctor who worked in Gaza, and a Palestinian American leader take the stage, and then streamlined the request to a Palestinian American leader.\par \par \uc2 About a dozen of those in the movement stayed overnight on the pavement outside the United Center, catching whatever sleep they could. The police did not attempt to get them to leave.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/uncommitted-movement-deadline-delegates-democratic-convention-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic convention misses deadline for Palestinian convention speaker call}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 For background on the Central Park Five and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in the racist attacks against the young men, check out our 2016 story and video from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Laughland:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2016/feb/17/donald-trump-central-park-five-jogger-death-penalty-new-york-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Central Park Five member recalls Trump: 'He has not changed'}}}\par \par \uc2 From our story eight years ago:\par \par \uc2 Yusef Salaam was 15 years old when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  demanded his execution for a crime he did not commit.\par \par \uc2 Nearly three decades before the rambunctious billionaire began his run for president \u8211\'20\'13 before he called for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/dec/08/donald-trump-muslim-ban-republican-party-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on Muslims entering the United States}}}\uc2 , for the expulsion of all undocumented migrants, before he branded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/jul/08/donald-trump-latino-vote-mexico-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexicans as \u8220\'20\'1Crapists\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and was accused of mocking the disabled \u8211\'20\'13 Trump called for the reinstatement of the death penalty in New York following a horrific rape case in which five teenagers were wrongly convicted \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was the firestarter,\u8221\'20\'1D Salaam said of Trump, in his first extended interview since Trump announced his run for the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CCommon citizens were being manipulated and swayed into believing that we were guilty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/17/central-park-five-donald-trump-jogger-rape-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump and the Central Park Five: the racially charged rise of a demagogue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to say election is a 'fleeting opportunity' to move past bitterness of Trump\par \par \uc2 When she closes out the Democratic convention this evening with a speech that is to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/dnc-harris-election-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most closely watched of her political career}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will tell Americans that voting for her will turn a fresh page in the country\u8217\'20\'19s politics, and keep an \u8220\'20\'1Cunserious man\u8221\'20\'1D out of the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this election, our nation has a precious, fleeting opportunity to move past the bitterness, cynicism, and divisive battles of the past. A chance to chart a New Way Forward. Not as members of any one party or faction, but as Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris will say, according to excerpts of the speech released by her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Considering that they capitalized \u8220\'20\'1CNew Way Forward\u8221\'20\'1D, one wonders if this is not the debut of a new campaign slogan.\par \par \uc2 Harris will continue:\par \par \uc2 I know there are people of various political views watching tonight. And I want you to know: I promise to be a President for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 I will be a President who unites us around our highest aspirations. A President who leads -- and listens. Who is realistic. Practical. And has common sense. And always fights for the American people. From the courthouse to the White House, that has been my life\u8217\'20\'19s work.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will say this about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the conservative-dominated supreme court:\par \par \uc2 We know what a second Trump term would look like. It\u8217\'20\'19s all laid out in \u8220\'20\'1CProject 2025.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8230\'20\'26 In many ways, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an unserious man. But the consequences of putting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back in the White House are extremely serious \u8230\'20\'26 Consider the power he will have\u8212\'20\'14 especially after the United States supreme court just ruled he would be immune from criminal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Even though \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not speak for another three hours, the United Center already appears to be nearing capacity.\par \par \uc2 Reporters have filled section 320, where I\u8217\'20\'19m typing this, to the point that there does not appear to be a single seat left. The attendants minding the section have had to turn people away because of capacity concerns.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 rumors escalate\par \par \uc2 The rumors that Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 will be the surprise guest at the convention are spreading, with TMZ now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/search?q=beyonce%20tmz&src=typed_query&f=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  it.\par \par \uc2 The White House political director earlier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Phil_Lewis_/status/1826729624924987431"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cbee\u8221\'20\'1D emoji, which some interpreted as further confirmation, although she followed up by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CSorry guys my 6 year old took my phone.\u8221\'20\'1D A Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 song was also playing during soundcheck.\par \par \uc2 Pink and The Chicks are confirmed to be performing tonight. Some have speculated that Taylor Swift could be a surprise guest, but there\u8217\'20\'19s been no confirmation of that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Exonerated Central Park Five member and New York City councilmember says of Trump: 'He wanted us dead'\par \par \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  then brought out four of the exonerated Central Park Five, including Yusef Salaam, who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently elected}}}\uc2  to the New York City council.\par \par \uc2 Referring to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a cheerleader of their prosecution, as \u8220\'20\'1C45\u8221\'20\'1D, Salaam said:\par \par \uc2 45 wanted us un-alive. He wanted us dead. Today we are exonerated because the original perpetrator confessed and DNA proved it.\par \par \uc2 But Salaam noted that Trump refuses to recant his accusations against them, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHe dismisses the scientific evidence rather than admit he was wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has never changed, and he never will,\u8221\'20\'1D Salaam said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  accuses Trump of 'sowing division' as he introduces Central Park Five\par \par \uc2 Civil rights activist the Rev \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  in on stage now to introduce the Central Park Five, the group of Black and Latino boys falsely convicted over the rape of a jogger in New York, whose prosecution \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  promoted.\par \par \uc2 But before they came on stage, Sharpton had a few words for the former president:\par \par \uc2 All \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been consistent about is making himself richer and sowing division to get that done. This man sat right here in Chicago a few weeks ago refusing to apologize for claims that migrants were taking Black jobs. Well, in November, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to show him when Blacks do their jobs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Uncommitted movement leaders denounce the convention\par \par \uc2 Abbas Alawieh, a leader of the uncommitted movement, is holding a press conference outside the convention now, announcing that the Democratic national convention has failed to meet the group\u8217\'20\'19s deadline to allow a Palestinian American to speak on the main stage. There has been growing pressure throughout the final day of the convention for Democratic officials to find a way to feature a Palestinian voice, but the evening programming is well underway, with no announced plans for inclusion. Alawieh told reporters:\par \par \uc2 The scandal is that there are forces within Democratic party leadership who do not want us to talk about Palestinian human rights \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re out of step with the majority of the Democratic base, the majority of Democratic voters who believe that Palestinian human rights are a priority.\par \par \uc2 Georgia state representative Ruwa Romman, who wrote a speech for the convention to consider, is now reading her speech to the crowd gathered outside. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/08/dnc-speech-uncommitted-movement-harris-walz-ruwan-romman/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mother Jones}}}\uc2  earlier published the text. The speech began, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m honored to be the first Palestinian elected to public office in the great state of Georgia and the first Palestinian to ever speak at the Democratic national convention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Now comes Pat Ryan, who represents a New York battleground district in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 He hit out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/trump-presidential-medal-military-honor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported insults}}}\uc2  towards military veterans, then obliquely referenced the newfound optimism Democrats are feeling since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended his bid for a second term:\par \par \uc2 These last few weeks have felt like a new day in America, when we are waking up, rising up, patriots, to demand a president who does not just treat our veterans with respect, but everyone with respect.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Now the convention is hearing from Michigan congresswoman \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  , who is running for the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump wants to take us backwards. He admires dictators a lot. He treats our friends as adversaries and our adversaries as friends,\u8221\'20\'1D said Slotkin, who opened by talking about her background working for the CIA and the defense department.\par \par \uc2 Ending on a similar theme, she said:\par \par \uc2 We do not retreat, we are the United States of America, we lead!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s musical interludes are being provided by Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s own DJ Metro:\par \par \uc2 He was just bumping Kool & the Gang\u8217\'20\'19s Celebration, and the crowd was vibing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Carrying on with the anti-corporate theme, Warren described Harris as someone who \u8220\'20\'1Ccares deep down, and she will take on the giant corporations that are squeezing American families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19ll take on rightwing extremists who think they should decide who has access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or IVF. Kamala will protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, groceries, gas, housing, healthcare, taxes, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued.\par \par \uc2 And then she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/04/jd-vance-critics-trump-vp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went there}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Trust \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance to look out for your family? Shoot \u8230\'20\'26 I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t trust them to move my couch.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Warren is known for her campaigning against corporate influence, and is telling the convention that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is a fellow traveler.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what I love best about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t be bought and she can\u8217\'20\'19t be bossed around,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said.\par \par \uc2 She recounted how they first met in the aftermath of the 2008 financial crisis, when \u8220\'20\'1CKamala was protecting families, as California\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, and Donald was scamming students at Trump University and trying to make money off people losing their homes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren addresses Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts senator and progressive leader Elizabeth Warren is on stage now at the Democratic national convention.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s being greeted with long and loud applause, and appears to be fighting back tears.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Central Park Five and mass shooting survivors to address convention\par \par \uc2 The Democratic National Convention Committee has released the full schedule of the night\u8217\'20\'19s speakers, which shows that, in addition to a host of powerful and prominent lawmakers, delegates will hear from people affected by issues that the party wants to address.\par \par \uc2 The 8pm hour will feature \u8220\'20\'1Ca conversation on gun violence\u8221\'20\'1D with people from Newtown, Connecticut; Uvalde, Texas; Charleston, South Carolina; and Chicago \u8211\'20\'13 all places that have been the site of mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 Representatives of the Central Park Five, the group of Black and Latino boys wrongfully convicted of raping a jogger in New York, will speak at about 7pm CT. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/17/central-park-five-donald-trump-jogger-rape-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cheerleader of their prosecution}}}\uc2 , something they will no doubt bring up.\par \par \uc2 On a lighter note, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be seeing comedian DL Hughley on the convention stage tonight, along with The Chicks, who will perform the national anthem.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 DNC kicks off final night\par \par \uc2 The final night of the Democratic national convention is officially under way, with Congresswoman \uc2 Veronica Escobar\uc2  gaveling in the session.\par \par \uc2 Even though \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not speak for another four hours, the United Center already looks quite crowded.\par \par \uc2 The delegates representing California, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s home state, are clearly fired up about her speech tonight. They were already chanting \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia!\u8221\'20\'1D before the session even began.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe United Center already looks quite crowded, with tonight\u8217\'20\'19s programming about to get underway. Harris won\u8217\'20\'19t address the convention until roughly 10pm CT. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FT98QJpYUW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FT98QJpYUW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1826748733771624556?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chicago has been revelling in its status as host city of the Democratic national convention.\par \par \uc2 Among its pearls is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alincolnbookshop.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abraham Lincoln Book Shop}}}\uc2 , which opened in 1938 and is a treasure trove of autographs, letters, rare books, presidential memorabilia and reproductions of Lincoln and civil war photos.\par \par \uc2 It currently has an exhibition of artifacts from Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s first political nominating convention in 1860 \u8211\'20\'13 the one that set Lincoln on course for the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/02/james-carville-joe-biden-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 James Carville}}}\uc2  popped up for a tour of the bookshop on Thursday and posed for photos while holding a picture of William Sherman, a union army general during the civil war.\par \par \uc2 In a discussion with shop owner Daniel Weinberg and former White House official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sidneyblumenthal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sidney Blumenthal}}}\uc2  , the veteran Democratic strategist observed: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you listen to Fox, Chicago is this giant hellhole: homeless people, streets, they\u8217\'20\'19re shooting everybody. It\u8217\'20\'19s one of nicest goddamn, places I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy only problem with Chicago as a convention site is that the United Centre is too far away. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know there\u8217\'20\'19s much you can do about it. At some point, Chicago should build a downtown arena like that but I think it\u8217\'20\'19s just a marvellous city. You can get in and out of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Weinberg noted Mark Twain \u8217\'20\'19s saying that history rhymes. Carville, who led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Clinton}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s successful 1992 presidential campaign, replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI think it more than rhymes. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot to be learned from European history \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19re not supposed to say that \u8211\'20\'13 but just the power alliances that live with us today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInternal conflicts: the movies that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing, the books that are being written, January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, that\u8217\'20\'19s a little more than rhyming. Forty percent of the people in 10 different states want to secede. History, I can\u8217\'20\'19t say it repeats itself but I think it repeats itself more than it rhymes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blumenthal, a Guardian columnist currently working on the fourth volume of a monumental {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/08/sidney-blumenthal-lincoln-politics-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lincoln biography}}}\uc2 , rejoined: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19ve been saying is the deeper I get into the past, the closer I get to the present.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris set for biggest speech of her political career on final night of Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as we cover the fourth and final night of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic national convention}}}\uc2  in Chicago. This evening\u8217\'20\'19s big event is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech closing out the convention, which will be her most high-profile opportunity yet to make the case that she is a better choice for president than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  . Expect the vice-president to aim to create a signature moment or line that will be repeated by Democratic faithful as they seek to rally the party\u8217\'20\'19s voters in the less than three months that remain before election day, as polls show a tight contest against the Republican former president.\par \par \uc2 Before the vice-president takes the stage, we expect to hear from another batch of party luminaries, including progressive senator Elizabeth Warren, Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , the Arizona senator who was on Harris\u8217\'20\'19 short list to be vice-president, and former congresswoman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jul/13/gabby-giffords-wont-back-down-documentary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting survivor}}}\uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 . We also hear rumors that there will be a surprise musical guest, but there\u8217\'20\'19s no saying who that might be. Keep in mind that the Democratic party does have the power to dazzle \u8211\'20\'13 yesterday, \uc2 Oprah Winfrey{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/oprah-winfrey-democratic-national-convention-speech-trump-harris-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strolled on stage}}}\uc2  without warning, and made a speech calling on independent voters to back Harris.\par \par \uc2 The convention kicks off at 6pm CT, and the White House said to expect Harris to speak at 9.45pm.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what we\u8217\'20\'19ll watching out for this evening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will the Democrats allow a Palestinian-American to speak at the convention? Outside the United Center, activists and delegates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/democratic-national-convention-uncommitted-delegates-protest-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holding a sit-in}}}\uc2  to pressure convention organizers to allow a speaker from the community. Yesterday, the convention heard from the family of a US citizen taken hostage on October 7, but the Uncommitted National Movement, which has 30 delegates at the convention, wants a Palestinian to be able to offer their views, as well.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The two names flying around as potential surprise musical guests are Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and Taylor Swift. Either one could be huge for Democrats as they seek to underscore the breadth of support for Harris.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cornel West, the independent presidential candidate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1826728841517158549"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was spotted}}}\uc2  outside the convention hall. Is he just coming to watch, or might he be here to announce his support for Harris?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 2024-08-22T22:17:25Z 2024-08-23T06:05:32Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/597df334f28cc1ea2d00ed204162c51f90376c18/0_146_4400_2642/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/597df334f28cc1ea2d00ed204162c51f90376c18/0_146_4400_2642/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stands with her husband Doug Emhoff, running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and his wife Gwen after historic convention address.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240822ek8m003h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
