\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Global health charities warn of \u8216\'20\'18huge and terrible\u8217\'20\'19 threat to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights if Trump returns\b0\par\par\uc2 Kat Lay Global health correspondent \par \uc2 987 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2024\par 10:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Global gag rule\u8217\'20\'19 and funding cuts will be \u8216\'20\'18on different scale\u8217\'20\'19 if Republicans win again, family-planning providers say\par \par \uc2 Providers of women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare around the world are preparing for potentially disastrous consequences should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win the US presidential election in November.\par \par \uc2 Policies pursued during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last presidency caused \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D harm in a number of countries, said Beth Schlachter, a senior director at MSI Reproductive Choices in the US. It meant \u8220\'20\'1Cclinics shuttered, health teams closed, women dying \u8230\'20\'26 but a second Trump term will be on a different scale\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Global health charities lost US funding if they refused to agree not to \u8220\'20\'1Cperform or actively promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D under the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/video/2017/jan/18/what-is-the-global-gag-rule-and-why-does-trump-support-it-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global gag rule}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. This frequently meant the closure of facilities offering wider health services, such as family planning.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/28/joe-biden-global-gag-rule-health-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrapped the ban in 2021}}}\uc2  a week after he was inaugurated as US president in a move celebrated by health groups around the world. However, rightwing US strategists have set out detailed plans in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  roadmap for a Republican administration to change the way the \uc2 US government\uc2  operates immediately after a Trump victory.\par \par \uc2 They are pushing for even wider restrictions on the activities of any organisation receiving US funding, the withdrawal of American support from international agencies, and the country\u8217\'20\'19s influence to be used to further restrict access to abortions globally.\par \par \uc2 Schlachter said the sector needed \u8220\'20\'1Cto get our heads around the implications of Trump retaking the White House\u8221\'20\'1D. Efforts by Trump to distance himself from Project 2025 were disingenuous, she suggested. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are his people and they are telling us loud and clear the damage they intend to inflict.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The global gag rule requiring organisations receiving US funding for family-planning services to agree not to perform or actively promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has existed under Republican presidents since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 . The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2017/jul/21/trump-global-death-warrant-women-family-planning-population-reproductive-rights-mexico-city-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration went further}}}\uc2 , however, and made that agreement a condition for organisations to receive US funding for global healthcare in general.\par \par \uc2 The Project 2025 papers suggest the next Republican president should go further still and apply the gag rule \u8220\'20\'1Cto all foreign assistance, including humanitarian aid\u8221\'20\'1D. This would affect about $51bn (\u163\'00\'A340bn) in overseas aid at current levels, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/issue-brief/what-the-election-could-mean-for-the-mexico-city-policy-and-u-s-foreign-aid/?utm_campaign=KFF-Global-Health-Policy&utm_medium=email&_hsenc=p2ANqtz-8VpUYzGSaJKStoKDt0VCEXFAzD1CadfEVars8RwpgJ90EZOjvTofBsDp5oZditSmeUiVzbb1BJ_gVimW0KPx0FYFwZLQ&_hsmi=309498103&utm_content=309498103&utm_source=hs_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health policy analysts suggest}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such an expansion would be \u8220\'20\'1Chuge and terrible\u8221\'20\'1D, said Dr Marleen Temmerman, a professor in obstetrics and gynaecology at the Aga Khan University East Africa and former director of reproductive health at the \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last administration, US funding for research into subjects such as cardiovascular disease and diabetes was imperilled by the provision of abortions for foetal malformation at the university\u8217\'20\'19s hospital, she said.\par \par \uc2 Dr Carole Sekimpi, the senior Africa director for MSI Reproductive Choices, said the 2017 gag rule was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisastrous for women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf anything, it increases the number of abortions \u8211\'20\'13 because you have more and more women with limited access to contraception, limited access to information, and therefore with a higher likelihood of unplanned pregnancies, and therefore the need for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The gag rule had a wider chilling effect, Sekimpi added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt does really embolden the opposition. Those who are anti-rights, anti-choice \u8211\'20\'13 the hate movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Temmerman said organisations would need to work together and potentially hive off work in reproductive healthcare into separate organisations to safeguard their other projects.\par \par \uc2 The US is responsible for almost two-thirds of global funding for sexual and reproductive health and rights promotion, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://donorsdelivering.report/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/DD_Report2024_FINALspreads.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 German Foundation for World Population\uc2  (DSW), a family-planning charity.\par \par \uc2 During the last Trump presidency, MSI saw annual donor income drop by $30m \u8211\'20\'13 or 17% \u8211\'20\'13 because it refused to sign the global gag rule. The charity said that meant 8 million women lost access to family-planning services \u8211\'20\'13 resulting in an estimated 6m unintended pregnancies, 1.8m unsafe abortions and 20,000 maternal deaths.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  published a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw2.nyl.as/t1/212/ak9oeuqgxf00jksz9sfu42eon/0/25d6fee4546edc766f9076cce6a8b17051a0a5df3958be93154d420c32dfbf8c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  looking at the impact in Uganda and Ethiopia, which found the global gag rule \u8220\'20\'1Cstalled and even reversed progress toward expanded access to modern contraception\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In Nepal, MSI had been working with the government to expand family-planning services, training health workers and establishing clinics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything changed after the election of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tushar Niroula, operations director at MSI Nepal. \u8220\'20\'1CThe operation had to be gradually closed down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The proportion of women of reproductive age in Nepal using modern contraceptives had stagnated, he said. \u8220\'20\'1CUnderprivileged populations in hard-to-reach areas are not able to get the access to the services. That\u8217\'20\'19s the effect of the global gag rule.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Partner agencies were afraid to refer women to MSI for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care even in cases of rape, incest or where the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life was at risk, which were all exceptions to the global gag rule, the charity said, adding that desperate women would opt for unsafe methods.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D Niroula said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen a lot of cases where women have opted for traditional methods of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have got complications, and have nearly died.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static.project2025.org/2025_MandateForLeadership_FULL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Documents}}}\uc2  published by Project 2025 suggest membership of international organisations such as the \uc2 UN\uc2  and \uc2 WHO\uc2  should be seen as only \u8220\'20\'1Ca means to attain defined goals\u8221\'20\'1D and stress that withdrawal is an option \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen such institutions act against US interests\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US should work with a coalition of \u8220\'20\'1Clike-minded nations\u8221\'20\'1D to shape the work of international agencies, building on the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/oct/22/us-trump-administration-signs-anti-abortion-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Geneva Consensus Declaration}}}\uc2  signed by the last Trump administration and 33 largely illiberal or authoritarian governments, they suggest. The US rescinded its signature a few months afterwards after Trump left office.\par \par \uc2 Individuals linked to the last Trump administration and to Project 2025 are already working in countries including Guatemala and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JanetMuseveni/status/1755862005108420676"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uganda}}}\uc2  to embed policies based on that declaration, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/resource/protego-operationalizing-the-geneva-consensus-declaration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis by the reproductive rights group Ipas}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240822ek8m002mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
