\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Obama to deliver \u8216\'20\'18forceful affirmation\u8217\'20\'19 for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Chris Stein in Chicago, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Vicky Graham (earlier) \par \uc2 11,499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par 22:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. Please join us for all the latest developments from day two of the DNC in Chicago in our dedicated live blog:Democratic national convention day two \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now closing this blog \u8211\'20\'13 but join us for all the latest speeches, news and reaction from the second day of the Democratic national convention in our dedicated blog:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/20/dnc-barack-michelle-obama-speech-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DNC 2024 live: Barack Obama to headline day two and wife Michelle, Bernie Sanders and Doug Emhoff also to speak}}}\par \par \uc2 Thanks for following along so far. Here is a recap of the key developments of the day so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obamawill deliver a \u8220\'20\'1Cforceful affirmation that [Kamala] Harris is the right leader for the moment\u8221\'20\'1D during his speech on Tuesday night at the Democratic national convention, an adviser to the former president told CNN. A source familiar with Obama\u8217\'20\'19s prepared speech told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  that he will \u8220\'20\'1Caffirm why {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are precisely the leaders the country needs right now, lay out the task in front of Democrats over the next eleven weeks, and bring into focus the values at stake in this election and at the heart of our politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  will address the convention shortly before her husband Barack takes the stage. The couple\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/26/obama-endorses-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement of Harris}}}\uc2  in July was seminal in securing the Democratic presidential nomination for the current vice-president, helping to bypass a potentially ugly internal fight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\uc2  and his running mate, tech lawyer Nicole Shanahan, are considering dropping out of the race and supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Shanahan said. In a interview on the End Tribalism in Politics podcast that aired today, reported by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , Shanahan said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s two options that we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at and one is staying in, forming that new party, but we run the risk of a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Waltz presidency because we draw more votes from Trump. Or we walk away right now and join forces with with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and explain to our base why we\u8217\'20\'19re making this decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  was checking into bomb threats made at \u8220\'20\'1Cvarious locations\u8221\'20\'1D in downtown Chicago where the Democratic national convention is taking place, AP reported. A threat was emailed to the Fox 32 Newsroom which said pipe bombs were placed at four hotels in downtown Chicago, including the Nobu Hotel, the Hotel Chicago West Loop and the Hyatt House Chicago in West Loop and the University District, the outlet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox32chicago.com/news/chicago-hotel-bomb-threat-nobuhttps://www.fox32chicago.com/news/chicago-hotel-bomb-threat-nobu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chicago policesaid there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrief breach\u8221\'20\'1D of security fencing \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin sight and sound of the United Center\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday evening, where the DNC is being held. Some 13 protesters were arrested on charges ranging from criminal trespass and resisting and obstructing an arrest to aggravated battery of police officers. The pro-Palestine demonstrations have brought thousands to the city.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trumpdelivered remarks on Tuesday in Howell, Michigan, a city with historical links to the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  and where white supremacists marched through the streets last month and chanted \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Hitler. We love Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 ,a former White House press secretary under the Trump administration, will speak at the Democratic national convention today to show her support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will attend a campaign rally in Wisconsin today where she is scheduled to deliver remarks at around 8pm Central Time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, meanwhile, will focus his remarks on the US economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBottom line: we need an economy that works for all of us, not just the greed of the billionaire class,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders plans to say, in a preview of his speech that his press office shared with journalists.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 These oligarchs tell us we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t tax the rich; we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t take on price gouging; we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expand Medicare to cover dental, hearing, and vision; and we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t increase Social Security benefits for struggling seniors.\par \par \uc2 Well I\u8217\'20\'19ve got some bad news for them.\par \par \uc2 That is precisely what we are going to do, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this struggle because this is precisely what the American people want from their government.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has also been discussing plans to propose a federal ban on price gouging on food and groceries and lowering the cost of education and childcare. She is no longer promoting Medicare for All, which she initially had co-sponsored with Sanders, as part of a broader shift toward the center. But she has been promoting strengthening Medicare, and expanding other health programs that area already in place.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on her platform:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-opportunity-economy-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris is pitching an \u8216\'20\'18opportunity economy\u8217\'20\'19 to voters. Will it sway them?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Emhoff will share why he sees his wife \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cjoyful warrior\u8221\'20\'1D in his speech tonight, according to excerpts of his speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhenever she\u8217\'20\'19s needed, however she\u8217\'20\'19s needed, Kamala rises to the occasion,\u8221\'20\'1D Emhoff plans to say. \u8220\'20\'1CShe did it for me and our family. Now that the country needs her, she\u8217\'20\'19s showing you what we already know: she\u8217\'20\'19s ready to lead, she brings both joy and toughness to this task, and she will be a great president who we will all be proud of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emhoff has become an important surrogate for Harris on the campaign trail, speaking about reproductive rights, LGBTQ+ rights and antisemitism.\par \par \uc2 The second gentleman, who is a lawyer and visiting professor at Georgetown University Law Center, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/kamala-harris-doug-emhoff-sexist-antisemitic-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced a wave of}}}\uc2  antisemitic, misogynistic attacks since his wife became a presidential candidate. If Harris wins the election, Emhoff would become the first ever first gentleman.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 About 20 million people watched the first night of the convention on TV, according to Nielsen.\par \par \uc2 The viewership surpassed that of the first day of the Republican convention, when about 18.13 million people tuned in to watch.\par \par \uc2 The media statistics organization accounted for viewership of convention coverage across 13 networks including ABC, \uc2 CBS\uc2 , NBC, Scripps News, Univision, CNN, CNNe, Fox Business, Fox News Channel, MSNBC, \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , NewsNation and \uc2 PBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Away from the Democratic convention , RFK Jr is considering ending his campaign for president to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , according to his running mate.\par \par \uc2 The startling disclosure was made by Nicole Shanahan, Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential candidate, who said the pair was considering dropping their campaign over fears it might help elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , the Democratic nominee, as president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lAqVn5lRdes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shanahan\u8217\'20\'19s remarks}}}\uc2 , made on the Impact Theory With Tim Bilyeau podcast, were close to an all-out admission that Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign had more in common with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s than Harris\u8217\'20\'19s. Kennedy was a member of the Democratic party and attempted to run as its nominee before choosing to stand as an independent.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/rfk-jr-dropping-out-help-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr considers dropping out to help Trump, running mate says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Valerie Jarrett , a former senior adviser to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , has warned that Democratic nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , currently riding high in the polls, faces plenty of ups and downs before November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou all remember when President Obama won the Iowa caucuses \u8211\'20\'13 if you are old enough to remember that,\u8221\'20\'1D Jarrett, speaking at Axios House in Chicago, said of Obama\u8217\'20\'19s first primary campaign against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in 2008. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got: \u8216\'20\'18Oh, my goodness!\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18We are going for gold!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then came the New Hampshire primary and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating defeat\u8221\'20\'1D, she added. \u8220\'20\'1CBut out of that, people found out who he was. We came out of that terrible experience. It forced us to have to go to many more states and introduce him to many more people and, in the end, it was actually good for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris is bound to undergo \u8220\'20\'1Ca whole multitude of tests\u8221\'20\'1D, Jarrett said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe is absolutely on a roll right now. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a hands-up enthusiasm. People are just tired of all the negativity, the polarisation, the toxicity. I think what Governor Walz said: she\u8217\'20\'19s full of joy. People want joy. They actually want to like each other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, who has replaced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the top of the Democratic ticket, has embarked on a much shorter campaign than the one Obama fought. Jarrett expressed confidence in Harris and running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and their advisers to deal with obstacles and keep pushing forward.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hot from his primetime appearance at the Democratic convention on Monday night, Shawn Fain, the president of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , has been explaining to reporters why he wore a T-shirt imprinted with the phrase \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is a scab.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been a union member for \uc2 UAW\uc2  for 30 years, and we have a term for people that cross picket lines and don\u8217\'20\'19t respect working-class people. We call them scabs, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fain said that the political leanings of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s more than 1 million active and retired members had remained stable over the years at about 65% Democratic and 30-32% Republican. But he predicted that this time around, the gap would widen as union members gravitate towards \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s an amazing, very strong woman. I think people underestimate her, and that\u8217\'20\'19s a huge mistake. I think she\u8217\'20\'19s going to move a massive mountain come November,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  is preparing to launch in the next week or so what has been billed as the biggest field campaign in its history to persuade its members to turn out to vote.\par \par \uc2 Fain said that in his view, people would lean towards the Democratic ticket because when they look at Harris and her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cthey see themselves. I mean, no one looks at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and says: \u8216\'20\'18I identify with that person.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , Bernie Sanders, Doug Emhoff among main speakers on Democratic convention's second night\par \par \uc2 The Democratic national convention just released the full schedule of its second night, confirming that \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will deliver the evening\u8217\'20\'19s keynote speech, and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , second gentleman Doug Emhoff and independent senator Bernie Sanders are also scheduled to make remarks.\par \par \uc2 The grandsons of \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  and \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  will be among the early speakers at the convention, along with \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House press secretary.\par \par \uc2 As the night goes on, we\u8217\'20\'19ll hear from Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and then Sanders, both of whom will speak at the 8pm CT hour. Emhoff and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  will speak after 9pm, and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is to address delegates starting at 10pm.\par \par \uc2 Do not be surprised if the schedule runs late, as it did last night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lurking in the United Center\u8217\'20\'19s rafters are thousands of balloons that are primed to drop:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RilSe1YC4U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RilSe1YC4U}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1825996479552508239?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Political conventions, both Democratic and Republican, typically end with a cascade of balloons. Expect to see that on Thursday night, after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  ends her keynote address.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  and transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  spoke at the Veterans and Military Families Council at the Democratic national convention today, arguing that concepts of patriotism and freedom are not the monopoly of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFolks come from all over our country, with all kinds of backgrounds to serve,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve all served alongside folks of different political stripes, and some who are not political at all \u8230\'20\'26 Some Republicans want to think that their political party has a monopoly on patriotism. No party does. But it\u8217\'20\'19s clear which political candidate supports military veterans, and which one does not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , Sec. \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , at the DNC. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A6qarGqQsu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A6qarGqQsu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1825989458681876631?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kelly took Trump to task for his recent comments suggesting that the Presidential Medal of Freedom was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter\u8221\'20\'1D award than the Medal of Honor because \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone [who] gets the Congressional Medal of Honor, they\u8217\'20\'19re soldiers. They\u8217\'20\'19re either in very bad shape because they\u8217\'20\'19ve been hit so many times by bullets, or they\u8217\'20\'19re dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe VFW, of which I am a member, called these comments asinine,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelly, a former astronaut and Gulf war veteran. \u8220\'20\'1CI agree.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both Kelly and Buttigieg made oblique references to the attacks made by Republicans on the record of Democratic vice-presidential candidate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can count from the despicable way \u8211\'20\'13 the weird way - that he talks about the service,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a through-line that goes all the way back to the days when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  used his status as a teenage multimillionaire to procure a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s note to pretend that he was unable to serve, so that some working-class man from who knows, maybe the south side of Chicago went to Vietnam in his place. There\u8217\'20\'19s an unbroken pattern right there of not being able to grasp service to others. Veterans understand service to others. Today\u8217\'20\'19s Democrats understand service to others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gwen Walz, wife of the Democratic VP pick, spoke with pride of their service as teachers, and his service as a national guardsman. \u8220\'20\'1CI will put that service up against anyone\u8217\'20\'19s,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are building a future for all of us, each and every one of us that we can be proud of.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s sound check time inside the United Center, where the Democratic national convention is being held, and the few journalists and guests in the venue early are getting a sneak peak of who\u8217\'20\'19s performing tonight.\par \par \uc2 Rapper Common is onstage now, spitting verse that pays tribute to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go, ya\u8217\'20\'19ll! Chitown! DNC!\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to a smattering of applause. There aren\u8217\'20\'19t that many people here, but he will probably get a much louder reception in a few hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 We {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/20/election-dnc-donald-trump-kamala-harris-barack-michelle-obama-updates?page=with:block-66c4df8c8f0893d34d6b418d#block-66c4df8c8f0893d34d6b418d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier }}}\uc2  that the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  was looking into bomb threats made on Tuesday at \u8220\'20\'1Cvarious locations\u8221\'20\'1D in Chicago where the Democratic national convention is taking place.\par \par \uc2 According to a police scanner, 14 bomb threats were made today, mostly at hotels in downtown Chicago.\par \par \uc2 enltrA listing of all reported bomb threats at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DNCChicago?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DNCChicago}}}\uc2  today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ChicagoScanner?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ChicagoScanner}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iuGgBzmnB2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iuGgBzmnB2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 16th & 17th District Chicago Police Scanner (@CPD1617Scanner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CPD1617Scanner/status/1825973385815327111?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been over at the McCormick Place convention center all day again, popping in and out of caucus and council meetings. And I finally had a chance to check out Dempalooza, an expo event with a bunch of vendors \u8211\'20\'13 some selling Democratic and Harris merch, some selling local goods, some selling politics.\par \par \uc2 I saw at least five \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  cardboard cutouts and a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoconut room\u8221\'20\'1D, a nod to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 iconic \u8220\'20\'1Cyou think you just fell out of a coconut tree\u8221\'20\'1D line that social media loves.\par \par \uc2 One of those cutouts had Harris in a superhero outfit, and people came up to take photos alongside it. There is also a display of presidential footwear, with displays cases of old shoes.\par \par \uc2 enltrChecked out the DNC expo area, called \u8220\'20\'1CDem-palooza,\u8221\'20\'1D which wasn\u8217\'20\'19t super active but had a ton of vendor booths with Dem/Harris merch & local goods along some voter orgs and a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoconut room\u8221\'20\'1D and at least five Harris cardboard cutouts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5Vv9OyBPRS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5Vv9OyBPRS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1825980691927928895?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The area wasn\u8217\'20\'19t very busy \u8211\'20\'13 the Democratic convention is spread across McCormick Place and the United Center, and getting from one to the other was a major challenge for some delegates yesterday, so as the day wears on, the McCormick location is getting quiet as folks start to make their way to the United Center for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s speakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Singer-songwriter James Taylor was scheduled to perform on Monday night on the first night of the Democratic national convention in Chicago, but as the evening ran long, organizers skipped elements of the program, meaning that Taylor never took the stage.\par \par \uc2 DNC officials said in a statement that because of the \u8220\'20\'1Craucous applause interrupting speaker after speaker, we ultimately skipped elements of our program to ensure we could get to President Biden as quickly as possible so that he could speak directly to the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcchicago.com/dnc-chicago-2024/will-james-taylor-perform-at-the-dnc-heres-what-we-know-after-singers-set-was-canceled-monday/3526858/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News Chicago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Taylor himself released a statement this afternoon, saying that it \u8220\'20\'1Cbecame clear\u8221\'20\'1D as the evening went on that there \u8220\'20\'1Cwouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be time for our \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19ve Got a Friend\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe the organizers couldn\u8217\'20\'19t anticipate the wild response from the floor of the United Center.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CSorry to disappoint,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 But a great and inspirational, quintessentially American moment. We were honored to be there.\par \par \uc2 enltr"...But it became clear, as the evening unfolded, that there wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be time for our \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve Got a Friend\u8221\'20\'1D with cello and voices. Maybe the organizers couldn\u8217\'20\'19t anticipate the wild response from the floor of the United Center\u8230\'20\'26 " {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/JT?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #JT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/JamesTaylor?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #JamesTaylor}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DNC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DNC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DNC2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DNC2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B6LG7yxXaX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B6LG7yxXaX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 James Taylor (@JamesTaylor_com) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamesTaylor_com/status/1825948811979628660?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in an interview with CBS News that aired last night, said he would accept the election outcome if he believes the election is \u8220\'20\'1Cfree and fair\u8221\'20\'1D. He said:\par \par \uc2 I think if I lose, this country will go into a tailspin, the likes of which it\u8217\'20\'19s never seen before \u8211\'20\'13 the likes of 1929 \u8211\'20\'13 but if I do, and it\u8217\'20\'19s free and fair, absolutely, I will accept the results.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFair\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cmeans that votes are counted,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding:\par \par \uc2 It means that votes are fair. It means that they don\u8217\'20\'19t cheat on the election, they don\u8217\'20\'19t drop ballots, they don\u8217\'20\'19t install new rules and regulations that they don\u8217\'20\'19t have the power to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 If I see that we had a fair and free election, which I hope to be able to say, but if I see that, I will be \u8211\'20\'13 you will never see anybody more honorable than me. I\u8217\'20\'19m an honorable person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 How to watch Obama's speech at the Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Exactly 20 years ago, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was a relatively unknown state legislator when he delivered a keynote address at the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s convention. Obama said that evening:\par \par \uc2 I stand here knowing that my story is part of the larger American story, that I owe a debt to all of those who came before me, and that, in no other country on Earth, is my story even possible.\par \par \uc2 His {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2004/jul/27/uselections2004.usa4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2004 speech}}}\uc2  offers one of the clearest examples of how convention speeches can elevate a rising political star to national prominence. Four years later, he returned to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/aug/29/uselections2008.barackobama1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accept the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination}}}\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 In 2012, he made the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2012/sep/07/barack-obama-pleads-voters-finish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case for his re-election bid}}}\uc2  ; in 2016, he advocated for \uc2 Hillary Clinton{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jul/28/obama-hillary-clinton-convention-speech-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  to succeed him}}}\uc2  in office; and during the 2020 convention, he issued an attack on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and urged Americans to back \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/19/obama-dnc-speech-trump-democracy-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for president}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, his speech will make the case for the Harris-Walz ticket and the need to defeat Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/how-to-watch-obama-speech-dnc-michelle-barack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else to know about Obama\u8217\'20\'19s speech tonight.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/how-to-watch-obama-speech-dnc-michelle-barack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack and Michelle Obama at the Democratic convention: how to watch}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-insults-harris-intelligence-medical-records-tv-exclusive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with CBS News, said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cgladly\u8221\'20\'1D release his medical records and insisted that he is not experiencing any post-traumatic stress disorder or other lasting effects following his assassination attempt last month.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he had recently passed a medical exam with a \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect score\u8221\'20\'1D and that he had \u8220\'20\'1Caced\u8221\'20\'1D two cognitive tests.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he has 'no regrets' about overturning Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cno regrets\u8221\'20\'1D over how his appointment of three conservative supreme court justices led to the reversal of Roe v Wade and ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump, speaking to CBS News on Monday night, said:\par \par \uc2 The federal government should have nothing to do with this issue.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he has "no regrets" over how his appointment of three conservative Supreme Court justices led to the reversal of Roe v. Wade and ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The federal government should have nothing to do with this issue,"\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zSS8ixCZM2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zSS8ixCZM2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1825924115162706229?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro, the governor of Pennsylvania who was a finalist to be \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, will be speaking in a prime time slot on Wednesday night, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Democrats are expected to be in the spotlight during the Democratic national convention this week. The state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, Austin Davis, addressed the convention on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania and its 19 electoral college votes are considered key to both \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chances of victory in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anxious Democratic strategists are quietly trying to douse the euphoria engulfing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign by warning that her surge in popularity masks an election contest that is on a knife-edge and could easily be lost.\par \par \uc2 As the vice-president basks in adulation and optimism at the Democratic national convention in Chicago, key supporters are cautioning that more trying times lie ahead after an extended honeymoon period following her ascent to the top of the ticket in place of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fuelling the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 feelgood mood have been a spate of opinion polls showing Harris with a national lead over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while also leading or newly competitive in battleground states, including southern Sun belt states where Biden had been struggling badly before his withdrawal from the race last month.\par \par \uc2 A recent compilation of national polls by 538, a polling website, showed Harris leading Trump by 46.6% to 43.8%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/democrat-kamala-harris-polls-optimism-complacency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/democrat-kamala-harris-polls-optimism-complacency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats warned to keep euphoria in check as election remains on knife-edge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service looking into bomb threats in downtown Chicago - report\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  was checking into bomb threats made at \u8220\'20\'1Cvarious locations\u8221\'20\'1D in downtown Chicago where the Democratic national convention is taking place, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 A threat was emailed to the Fox 32 Newsroom which said pipe bombs were placed at four hotels in downtown Chicago, including the Nobu Hotel, the Hotel Chicago West Loop and the Hyatt House Chicago in West Loop and the University District, the outlet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox32chicago.com/news/chicago-hotel-bomb-threat-nobuhttps://www.fox32chicago.com/news/chicago-hotel-bomb-threat-nobu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 The threat mentioned the Democratic national convention that is taking place this week, it said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPolice and K9\u8217\'20\'19s at the Nobu Hotel in west loop \u8230\'20\'26 our news desk received an email claiming a pipe bomb threat at this and three other west loop / near west side hotels {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SVwKpE7ouP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SVwKpE7ouP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Paris Schutz (@paschutz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/paschutz/status/1825938496697282975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  received a huge response from the youth council meeting at the Democratic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convention}}}\uc2 , riling up young people by recalling his time as a high school teacher and a football coach.\par \par \uc2 enltrHuge response at the DNC youth council as Gov \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  unexpectedly pops in to speak. He credits his students for getting him involved in politics. \u8220\'20\'1CBe careful, next thing you know, you\u8217\'20\'19re the next vice presidential nominee.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/p3eueTPpsL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/p3eueTPpsL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1825952952152109324?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Once the word \u8220\'20\'1Ccoach\u8221\'20\'1D was uttered by the person announcing Walz, the crowd started moving toward the stage and cheering. Walz, the governor of Minnesota, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, credited his former students with getting him involved in politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBe careful: next thing you know, you\u8217\'20\'19re the next vice presidential nominee,\u8221\'20\'1D he joked.\par \par \uc2 He brought up issues key to young voters, like the cost of college, saying that the generation before him invested in his generation, so the cost of college back then \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t so damn expensive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And he implored the young people to get out and work hard over the next few months to elect Democrats in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , telling them they can sleep when they\u8217\'20\'19re dead. As he left the stage, the crowd chanted \u8220\'20\'1CCoach! Coach!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMy kids keep me humble. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XP9kpIYjgl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XP9kpIYjgl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@Tim_Walz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz/status/1825716274040557631?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has just posted a clip on X from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/dnc-hillary-clinton-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her speech}}}\uc2  at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DNC}}}\uc2  last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will never rest in defense of our freedom and safety. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fell asleep at his own trial,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, prompting gales of laughter around the convention floor.\par \par \uc2 Clinton continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he woke up, he made his own kind of history\u8212\'20\'14as the first person to run for president with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 felony convictions}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D This elicited pantomime boos from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris will never rest in defense of our freedom and safety. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fell asleep at his own trial.\par \par \uc2 When he woke up, he made his own kind of history\u8212\'20\'14as the first person to run for president with 34 felony convictions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VTUm5KcKHJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VTUm5KcKHJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  (@HillaryClinton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1825924948382105953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello US politics blog readers, there is an awful lot going on at the Democratic National Convention ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DNC}}}\uc2  ) in Chicago as well as on the 2024 election campaign trail for both the Democrats and top Republicans. And it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be another huge night on the convention stage, so stick with Guardian US for all the developments as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will deliver a forceful affirmation that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the \u8220\'20\'1Cright leader for the moment\u8221\'20\'1D during his speech on Tuesday night at the DNC, an adviser to the former president told CNN.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chicago police said there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrief breach\u8221\'20\'1D of security fencing \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin sight and sound of the United Center\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday evening, where the DNC is being held. Some 13 protesters were arrested on charges ranging from criminal trespass and resisting and obstructing an arrest to aggravated battery of police officers. The pro-Palestine demonstrations have brought thousands to the city.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will deliver remarks on Tuesday in Howell, Michigan, a city with historical links to the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  and where white supremacists marched through the streets last month and chanted \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Hitler. We love Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump is scheduled to speak this afternoon about \u8220\'20\'1Ccrime and safety\u8221\'20\'1D at Livingston County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s County in Howell, a city of about 10,000 residents northwest of Detroit. It will be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sixth visit to Michigan this year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 , a former White House press secretary under the Trump administration, will speak at the Democratic national convention today to show her support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Grisham worked in a number of different roles for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 as a press aide during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 presidential campaign, as chief of staff and press secretary for then-first lady, Melania Trump, and as White House press secretary and communications director. She resigned in the aftermath of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6 January 2021 attack}}}\uc2  on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will attend a campaign rally in Wisconsin today where she is scheduled to deliver remarks at around 8pm Central Time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doug Emhoff, the second gentleman of the US, is due to address the DNC later today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  and Bernie Sanders are all scheduled to make speeches at the DNC today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the Democratic governor of Kentucky, has insisted that he does not \u8220\'20\'1Cwish harm on anyone\u8221\'20\'1D after the Trump-Vance campaign accused him of calling for a member of Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s family to be raped.\par \par \uc2 Beshear was speaking on MSNBC this morning when he criticized Republicans for \u8220\'20\'1Cfear tactics\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  messaging, noting Vance\u8217\'20\'19s previous comments about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Beshear said:\par \par \uc2 JD Vance calls pregnancy resulting from rape inconvenient. Inconvenience is traffic, I mean, it is, uh, make him go through this.\par \par \uc2 Beshear was referring to a comment Vance made in 2021, while running for Ohio senate, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/vance-abortion-rape/2021/09/24/c3007318-1d32-11ec-8380-5fbadbc43ef8_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said}}}\uc2  he did not support rape and incest exceptions in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The Trump-Vance campaign quickly jumped on Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s comments today, with Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance/status/1825895520880972118"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking }}}\uc2  why the Kentucky governor is \u8220\'20\'1Cwishing that a member of my family would get raped?!?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if that had been his intent, Beshear replied: \u8220\'20\'1COf course not\u8221\'20\'1D and called Vance\u8217\'20\'19s response an example of the party\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdeflection\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 Obviously, I never wish harm on anyone. It just, again, deflection, trying to make himself and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the victims.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 It has been suggested that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  holds \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  partly culpable for his political demise when he stepped down in July. Obama did not encourage the president to end his campaign, but nor did he rally to his side when pressure mounted.\par \par \uc2 That context will make Obama\u8217\'20\'19s keynote speech on Tuesday all the more poignant. It was already imbued with personal significance for Obama.\par \par \uc2 It was the soaring keynote speech that Obama made at the Democratic national convention in Boston, Massachusetts exactly 20 years ago \u8211\'20\'13 in which he talked of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/keynote-address-the-2004-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Caudacity of hope\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Ca skinny kid with a funny name who believes that America has a place for him, too\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that rocket-launched him from his then relatively lowly status as a state senator in Illinois into the presidency just four years later.\par \par \uc2 In his speech on Tuesday night, Obama is expected to set out Harris\u8217\'20\'19s qualifications for the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful job. Earlier this month he commended her on X, saying:\par \par \uc2 She has the vision, the character, and the strength that this critical moment demands, and I know she will deliver.\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom capping the cost of prescription drugs for all to providing first-time homebuyers with financial support to restoring the child tax credit for families, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  just laid out some ways she'll help lower costs for the American people.\par \par \uc2 She has the vision, the\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ulLBup9tZU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ulLBup9tZU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1824560415126257762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama to deliver 'forceful affirmation' for Harris in speech\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will deliver a \u8220\'20\'1Cforceful affirmation that [Kamala] Harris is the right leader for the moment\u8221\'20\'1D during his speech on Tuesday night at the Democratic national convention, an adviser to the former president told CNN.\par \par \uc2 A source familiar with Obama\u8217\'20\'19s prepared speech told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  that he will \u8220\'20\'1Caffirm why \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are precisely the leaders the country needs right now, lay out the task in front of Democrats over the next eleven weeks, and bring into focus the values at stake in this election and at the heart of our politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carrying the flame on the second night of primetime speeches on Tuesday will be the Obamas, with \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  addressing the convention shortly before her husband Barack takes the stage.\par \par \uc2 The couple\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/26/obama-endorses-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement of Harris}}}\uc2  in July was seminal in securing the Democratic presidential nomination for the current vice-president, helping to bypass a potentially ugly internal fight.\par \par \uc2 The Obamas stamped their approval on a Harris bid for the White House on 26 July, five days after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stepped aside, recording a video of their phone conversation which promptly went viral. \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 I can\u8217\'20\'19t have this phone call without saying to my girl Kamala that I am so proud of you \u8211\'20\'13 this is going to be historic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\uc2  and his running mate, tech lawyer Nicole Shanahan, are considering dropping out of the race and supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Shanahan said.\par \par \uc2 In a interview on the End Tribalism in Politics podcast that aired today, reported by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , Shanahan said:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s two options that we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at and one is staying in, forming that new party, but we run the risk of a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Waltz presidency because we draw more votes from Trump.\par \par \uc2 Or we walk away right now and join forces with with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and explain to our base why we\u8217\'20\'19re making this decision.\par \par \uc2 enltrRFK\u8217\'20\'19s VP Nicole Shanahan says they are debating whether to stay in the race or drop out and join forces with Trump:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s two options that we're looking at and one is staying in, forming that new party, but we run the risk of a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Waltz presidency because we\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/O3HrLbbCLO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/O3HrLbbCLO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 End Tribalism in Politics (@EndTribalism) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EndTribalism/status/1825913860412354588?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 13 protesters arrested during first day of convention, says Chicago police\par \par \uc2 Chicago police said there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrief breach\u8221\'20\'1D of security fencing \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin sight and sound of the United Center\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 Some 13 people were arrested on charges ranging from criminal trespass and resisting and obstructing an arrest to aggravated battery of police officers, Chicago police superintendent Larry Snelling said, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 3,500 protesters participated in the march and rally, Snelling told a news conference on Tuesday, adding that just a small group breached the security fence. The vast majority of protesters were peaceful, he said, adding:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to tie that event \u8211\'20\'13 what happened with the breach \u8211\'20\'13 with the entirety of the protest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would not enforce a 150-year-old federal law to restrict the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication by mail.\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked in an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2  whether he would enforce the Comstock Act, a 1873 law that Trump allies have eyed as a way to ban all abortions nationwide under a second Trump administration. He replied:\par \par \uc2 No. We will be discussing specifics of it, but generally speaking, no, I would not.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump, when asked whether he would enforce the Comstock Act of 1873 to restrict sending medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by mail:\par \par \uc2 "No. We will be discussing specifics of it, but generally speaking, no, I would not." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/c9mWM43oPe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/c9mWM43oPe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1825902912708485170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In its 920-page blueprint for a second Trump administration, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 calls for enforcing Comstock\u8217\'20\'19s criminal prohibitions to provide or distribute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Giles, the mayor of Mesa, Arizona, is among the Republicans who will be speaking at the Democratic national convention this week.\par \par \uc2 Giles, who is expected to speak at the convention today, released a statement:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been a Republican all my life. But since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  refused to accept the results of the 2020 election, the Republican Party has spiraled further and further into political extremism.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Giles {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/opinion/op-ed/2024/07/29/mesa-mayor-republican-vote-kamala-harris/74583703007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  an op-ed in the Arizona Republic calling on Republicans to join him in \u8220\'20\'1Cchoosing country over party this election and to vote against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , a former Republican congressman for Illinois, has also confirmed that he will be speaking at the Democratic national convention this week.\par \par \uc2 Kinzinger, posting to X this morning, said that he will be using his speech on Thursday to argue that \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue conservatism has been replaced with a cult\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI can now report that I will be speaking Thursday at the Democratic National Convention.\par \par \uc2 True conservatism has been replaced with a cult. I\u8217\'20\'19ll be making that clear.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Kinzinger (Slava Ukraini) ???????????? (@AdamKinzinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamKinzinger/status/1825887124450676912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Geoff Duncan, a Republican former lieutenant governor of Georgia, will speak at the Democratic convention this week, the Harris campaign has announced.\par \par \uc2 Duncan will have a \u8220\'20\'1Cprominent\u8221\'20\'1D speaking slot on Wednesday night, CNN reported, citing a source familiar with the speech. Duncan\u8217\'20\'19s remarks will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdirected at Republicans who are sick and tired of making excuses for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the source said.\par \par \uc2 In a statement shared by Fox News, Duncan said:\par \par \uc2 As a lifelong conservative Republican, I do not recognize my own party. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not care about America\u8217\'20\'19s working families; he only cares about revenge and retribution. Americans know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s extremist agenda is a threat to our country, and it\u8217\'20\'19s time to move past his incoherence and division.\par \par \uc2 In May, Duncan said he would vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Cdisqualified himself through his conduct and his character.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to campaign in Michigan city a month after white supremacist rally\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will deliver remarks on Tuesday in Howell, Michigan, a city with historical links to the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2  and where white supremacists marched through the streets last month and chanted \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Hitler. We love Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to speak this afternoon about \u8220\'20\'1Ccrime and safety\u8221\'20\'1D at Livingston County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s County in Howell, a city of about 10,000 residents northwest of Detroit. It will be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sixth visit to Michigan this year.\par \par \uc2 In the 1970s, KKK Grand Dragon Robert Miles had a Howell mailing address and held meetings on a nearby farm, Reuters reported. A cross burning on the lawn of a Black couple rocked the city in the 1980s, and it was the site of a KKK rally in the 1990s, CNN reported. Last month, about a dozen white supremacists chanted \u8220\'20\'1CHeil Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D and carried signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CWhite Lives Matter\u8221\'20\'1D during a march through downtown Howell.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has criticized Trump for planning the event in Howell while failing to condemn what it called a \u8220\'20\'1Cblatant display of racism and antisemitism in his name.\u8221\'20\'1D A statement by the Harris campaign said:\par \par \uc2 The racists and white supremacists who marched in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name last month in Howell have all watched him praise Hitler, defend neo-Nazis in Charlottesville, and tell far-right extremists to \u8216\'20\'18stand back and stand by. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions have encouraged them, and Michiganders can expect more of the same when he comes to town.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign spokesperson rejected criticism of the site of the event, promising Trump would speak against \u8220\'20\'1Chate of any form\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump press secretary \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2  to speak at Democratic convention tonight\par \par \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2 , a former White House press secretary under the Trump administration, will speak at the Democratic national convention today to show her support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Grisham worked in a number of different roles for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as a press aide during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 presidential campaign, as chief of staff and press secretary for then-first lady, Melania Trump, and as White House press secretary and communications director. She resigned in the aftermath of the 6 January 2021 attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 In a statement announcing her appearance at the Democratic national convention this week, Grisham said:\par \par \uc2 I never thought I\u8217\'20\'19d be speaking at a Democratic convention. But, after seeing firsthand who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  really is, and the threat he poses to our country, I feel very strongly about speaking out.\par \par \uc2 Grisham, whose attendance at the DNC was first reported by NBC News, added:\par \par \uc2 While I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with Vice President Harris on everything, I am proud to be supporting her because I know she will defend our freedoms and represent our nation with honesty and integrity.\par \par \uc2 enltr????. We\u8217\'20\'19ll, I\u8217\'20\'19m doing a thing tonight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RepublicansForHarris?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RepublicansForHarris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nR2uKyq6yq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nR2uKyq6yq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Stephanie Grisham\uc2  (@OMGrisham) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OMGrisham/status/1825878604808597591?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Roy Cooper, the Democratic governor of North Carolina, said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cthat 2008 feeling\u8221\'20\'1D about the party\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning his state with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 Cooper, speaking at a Bloomberg event at the Democratic national convention on Tuesday reported by AP, acknowledged that he did not have the same optimism about his state just weeks ago, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was at the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 Before Biden dropped out, Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cwere not united, Cooper said, adding that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful\u8221\'20\'1D for the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to step aside \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it brought everybody together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone loves President Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, but added of the decision to drop out:\par \par \uc2 It was the time to do this, it was the time to make history.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic national convention \u8217\'20\'19s programming tonight will begin earlier after how late it ran last night, CNN is reporting, citing DNC organizers.\par \par \uc2 enltrOrganizers say tonight's convention programming will begin earlier after how late last night ran, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/betsy_klein?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @betsy_klein}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1825904221457162739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Doors at the United Center in Chicago are scheduled to open at 4pm CT, with main programming beginning at 6pm CT.\par \par \uc2 The theme for today\u8217\'20\'19s edition of the convention will be \u8220\'20\'1CA Bold Vision for America\u8217\'20\'19s Future\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the presidential election approaches, a recently designated neo-Nazi terrorist group is covertly seeding violent propaganda on to mainstream social media channels \u8211\'20\'13 exposing tens of thousands of unknowing followers to radicalizing messages \u8211\'20\'13 according to background research and a report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/neo-nazi-terrorist-group-steve-bannon-account"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided to the Guardian}}}\uc2  by the Institute for Strategic Dialogue (ISD).\par \par \uc2 One of those channels on Telegram purports to be associated with \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s War Room podcast, with an administrator claiming in group chats discovered by ISD to have had direct contact with the longtime \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/nov/14/steve-bannon-white-house-racism-fear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-known}}}\uc2  for playing footsie with extremists and admitting to fomenting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/01/opinion/steve-bannon-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revolution}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UK government\uc2  listed th e Terrogram collective as an official terrorist entity in April. The move spiked public interest in the shadowy network of violent neo-Nazi propagandists on Telegram that preaches accelerationism, which demands followers hasten the collapse of society through acts of terrorism.\par \par \uc2 Terrorgram has already had success inspiring adherents. The Bratislava shooter who killed two people outside of a gay bar in 2022 cited it in his manifesto. Just last week, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/8/13/turkey-arrests-teenager-for-stabbing-attack-at-mosque"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teenage suspected supporter in Turkey}}}\uc2  carried out a mass stabbing at a mosque. Followers of Terrorgram in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/neo-nazis-arrested/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canada}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/hatewatch/2021/06/16/texas-man-arrested-charges-terroristic-threats-ran-white-power-telegram-channel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the US}}}\uc2  have already been subject to terrorism-related charges in recent years.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/neo-nazi-terrorist-group-steve-bannon-account"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full report here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/neo-nazi-terrorist-group-steve-bannon-account"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neo-Nazi terrorist group using Steve Bannon account to radicalize people}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/neo-nazi-terrorist-group-steve-bannon-account"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Neo-Nazi terrorist group using Steve Bannon account to radicalize people}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Crews are adding fencing to the security perimeter near the United Center ahead of the second day of the Democratic national convention, after protesters breached the outer perimeter fence on Monday.\par \par \uc2 From CBS News\u8217\'20\'19 Darius Johnson:\par \par \uc2 enltrRIGHT NOW: Crews are adding fencing at Washington and Wolcott in the secure perimeter near the United Center where the DNC is being held. This comes after protesters breached the fence yesterday to get closer to the convention. Several were arrested. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cbschicago?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cbschicago}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DNC2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DNC2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LEupxhJl4R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LEupxhJl4R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Darius Johnson (DJ) (@DariusJohnsonTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DariusJohnsonTV/status/1825832728421396916?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Dozens of protesters appeared to break through one security fence near the convention site on Monday and several demonstrators were handcuffed and detained.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/20/election-dnc-donald-trump-kamala-harris-barack-michelle-obama-updates?page=with:block-66c49ff88f08a6f12b17f45c#block-66c49ff88f08a6f12b17f45c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  the Chicago chapter of the \uc2 National Lawyers Guild\uc2  said 12 protesters were arrested on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Chicago police are expected to hold a press conference later this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 The Democratic national convention kicked off Monday in Chicago, just one month after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  withdrew his candidacy and paved the way for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to take over the ticket. Here are key takeaways from the day:\par \par \uc2 1. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden passed the torch}}}\uc2  : \u8216\'20\'18America, I gave my best to you\u8217\'20\'19: Biden revisited some of the darkest chapters of the Trump administration, including the January 6 insurrection, and attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s vision of America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHe says we\u8217\'20\'19re losing. He\u8217\'20\'19s the loser.\u8221\'20\'1D He earned loud applause for his praise of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying selecting her as vice-president was the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest decision I made my whole career\u8221\'20\'1D, and, \u8220\'20\'1CCrime will keep coming down when we put a prosecutor in the office instead of a convicted felon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Ocasio-Cortez energized the crowd and praised Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ceasefire efforts}}}\uc2  : \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  gave one of the most energetic speeches of the night, talking about her roots as a bartender and saying that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstands the urgency of rent checks and groceries and prescriptions. She is as committed to our reproductive and civil rights as she is to taking on corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D The progressive congresswoman and \u8220\'20\'1CSquad\u8221\'20\'1D member also earned loud applause for saying that Harris was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking tirelessly to secure a ceasefire in Gaza and bringing hostages home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 3. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/dnc-hillary-clinton-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton said Kamala Harris will break the \u8216\'20\'18glass ceiling\u8217\'20\'19:}}}\uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the former secretary of state and 2016 presidential candidate, also gave an impassioned speech, outlining the historic nature of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s nomination: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a barrier falls for one of us, it falls and clears the way for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton drew a sharp contrast between Harris, a former prosecutor, and Trump who \u8220\'20\'1Cfell asleep at his own trial, and when he woke up, he made his own kind of history \u8230\'20\'26 the first person to run for president with 34 felony convictions\u8221\'20\'1D. The remark sparked \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D chants, a throwback to the \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D chants Clinton faced in 2016 at Trump rallies.\par \par \uc2 4. Democrats rallied around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and stopping Project 2025: Speakers from red states gave personal accounts of the impacts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Hadley Duvall, from Kentucky, described how she was raped by her stepfather and became pregnant at age 12: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine not having a choice. But today, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reality for many women and girls across the country because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D Speakers also repeatedly tied the Trump and the Republican agenda to Project 2025, the roadmap for a second Trump administration crafted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/project-2025-training-videos-trump-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former Trump officials}}}\uc2 . Mallory McMorrow, a state senator from Michigan, held a copy of the Project 2025 document and assailed the plan to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  into a dictator\u8221\'20\'1D. Congressman \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  called Project 2025 \u8220\'20\'1CJim Crow 2.0\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden noted that the project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/article/2024/jul/04/trump-project-2025-heritage-foundation-education-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls}}}\uc2  for the dismantling of the US department of education.\par \par \uc2 5. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/kamala-harris-surprise-speech-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Kamala Harris gave surprise remarks:}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/kamala-harris-surprise-speech-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a surprise appearance}}}\uc2  at the convention on Monday night to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his service. Harris, who is due to give her formal speech at the end of the week, electrified the crowd when she entered the stage, with Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 \u8217\'20\'19s Freedom playing in the background.\par \par \uc2 6. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/pro-palestinian-protest-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thousands protested outside the DNC:}}}\uc2  Thousands of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered outside the Democratic National Convention, calling for a ceasefire and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/democrat-platform-israel-arms-embargo-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arms embargo}}}\uc2  on Israel. Dozens of protesters appeared to break through one security fence near the convention site and several demonstrators were handcuffed and detained. During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, demonstrators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265#block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfurled}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel\u8221\'20\'1D banner, but the speech continued uninterrupted. There was limited talk of Gaza on the convention floor, though Biden reiterated his efforts to secure a ceasefire and said, \u8220\'20\'1CThose protesters out in the street, they have a point \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of innocent people are being killed, on both sides.\u8221\'20\'1D The Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/democrat-platform-israel-arms-embargo-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 platform}}}\uc2  released before the convention did not include an arms embargo, a key demand by uncommitted delegates.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 A dozen people were arrested during yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s demonstrations outside the United Center in Chicago, where the Democratic national convention took place, according to the Chicago chapter of the \uc2 National Lawyers Guild\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the guild, a total of 14 protesters have been arrested as of Monday night. It said that two people have required hospitalization as a result of their arrests by Chicago police.\par \par \uc2 A statement posted on social media reads:\par \par \uc2 The Chicago chapter of the \uc2 National Lawyers Guild\uc2  (NLG) is condemning the aggressive and, at times, violent response by the \uc2 Chicago Police Department\uc2  (\uc2 CPD\uc2 ) toward protesters at the start of the Democratic National Convention (DNC).\par \par \uc2 Both protesters arrested on Sunday were held for hours before being allowed to speak to a lawyer, and were not allowed to make private phone calls with attorneys at the police station in violation of \uc2 CPD\uc2  policies and procedures and the law.\par \par \uc2 enltrPer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NLGChicago?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NLGChicago}}}\uc2  this morning: "a total of 14 protesters have been arrested as of Monday night, including two on Sunday and 12 on Monday. Two protesters have needed hospitalization as a result of their arrests by \uc2 CPD\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jinx Press (at DNC) (@JinxPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JinxPress/status/1825866042251350139?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his family are vacationing for the rest of the week in Santa Ynez, California in the heart of Santa Barbara wine country.\par \par \uc2 The Bidens arrived early this morning at the ranch of \uc2 Joe Kiani\uc2 , a longtime Democratic donor and the founder of \uc2 Masimo\uc2  and Cercacor Laboratories.\par \par \uc2 Biden has called Kiani \u8220\'20\'1Cone of my closest friends\u8221\'20\'1D and in 2021 appointed him to the President\u8217\'20\'19s council of advisers on science and technology. Kiani has also previously hosted the president\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked if the president was going to California to \u8220\'20\'1Clay low\u8221\'20\'1D for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  during the Democratic national convention, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery much continuing to be the president, the commander in chief\u8221\'20\'1D. She told reporters:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s going to spend time with his family. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s important for any families to do. Presidents are never on vacation.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s a president wherever he is. He\u8217\'20\'19s certainly going to continue to be doing the work, going to be very much focused and getting updates \u8211\'20\'13 for example, what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in the Middle East; foreign policy, more broadly, and also domestic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz to attend rally in battleground Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will attend a campaign rally in Wisconsin today where she is scheduled to deliver remarks at around 8pm CT.\par \par \uc2 Other attendees joining Harris and Walz at the Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee include congresswoman Gwen Moore, Milwaukee mayor Cavalier Johnson, labor leaders, and members of the \uc2 Milwaukee Bucks\uc2  franchise, the Harris Walz campaign said.\par \par \uc2 It marks Harris\u8217\'20\'19s seventh visit to Wisconsin this year and her third since becoming the Democratic presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  delivered a rousing speech at the Democratic national convention on Monday, offering a full-throated endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and outlining a sweeping progressive vision for the next administration. Ocasio-Cortez said:\par \par \uc2 America, when we knock on our neighbor\u8217\'20\'19s door, organize our communities and elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the presidency on 5 November, we will send a loud message that the people of this nation will not go back. We choose a new path and open the door to a new day: one that is for the people and by the people.\par \par \uc2 The New York congresswoman was greeted by the convention crowd in Chicago with loud applause and cheers of \u8220\'20\'1CAOC! AOC!\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez has won praise for her ability to effectively communicate with voters in an accessible way, promised Harris would be a voice for working Americans and issued a stark warning against reelecting Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AOC calls Trump \u8216\'20\'18two-bit union buster\u8217\'20\'19 as she urges US to elect Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , in her speech on Monday, revelled in the chance to turn the tables on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as she drew a parallel between the slights she endured at the hands of the Republican candidate in 2016 and the insults he continues to hurl at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in 2024.\par \par \uc2 It is no surprise that he is lying about Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s record, he is mocking her name and her laugh. Sounds familiar?\par \par \uc2 Clinton compared Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record as a convicted felon with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s as a former prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 As a prosecutor, Kamala locked up murders and drug traffickers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fell asleep at his own trial.\par \par \uc2 At that moment the thousands of Democratic delegates amassed on the DNC floor spontaneously burst into chants of \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up! Lock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D It was an ironic echo of the chant that was repeatedly directed against Clinton by Trump supporters, with his blessing, in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Clinton, with the diplomacy behoving a former secretary of state, made no comment. But the way she nodded her head in synch to the chants spoke volumes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  pins hope on Harris to \u8216\'20\'18break through\u8217\'20\'19 glass ceiling\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  gave one of the most powerful speeches of her career in politics on Monday as she implored American voters finally to crack the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest, hardest glass ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D that had eluded her so bitterly eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 In a rousing 15-minute speech at the Democratic national convention in Chicago, Clinton returned to the theme that she intended to invoke in a victory speech on election night, 8 November 2016. That speech was never delivered, the glass ceiling standing firm in the wake of her shock defeat to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But what she had failed to attain was within the grasp of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , only the second woman to be nominated at the top of a major party presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 And the man who had derided and humiliated Clinton on the campaign trail back in 2016, mocking her as \u8220\'20\'1CCrooked\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLyin\u8217\'20\'19 Hillary\u8221\'20\'1D, was now on the defensive. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have him on the run now,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 Clinton made little effort to hide that for her the hope of pushing Harris into the White House as the first female US president was profoundly personal. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are so close to breaking through once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, conjuring up the image of Harris raising her hand \u8220\'20\'1Con the other side of that glass ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D to take the presidential oath of office.\par \par \uc2 This is our time America. This is when we stand up, this is when we break through.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made a surprise appearance at the Democratic national convention on Monday night, taking the stage to thank \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his service to the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to be a great week, and I want to kick us off by celebrating our incredible president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , who will be speaking later tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Joe, thank you for your historic leadership, for your lifetime of service to our nation, and for all you will continue to do, we are forever grateful to you. Thank you, Joe!\par \par \uc2 Harris, dressed in a tan suit, kept her remarks brief, taking in the enthusiasm from the delegates and convention attenders that were on their feet cheering and chanting. \u8220\'20\'1CLooking out at everyone tonight, I see the beauty of our great nation,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 Harris walked out to Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 \u8217\'20\'19s Freedom, which has become her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/jul/23/beyonce-kamala-harris-campaign-song"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign anthem}}}\uc2 . Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s name has been floated by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/2024/08/19/celebrities-dnc-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 various sources}}}\uc2  as a potential surprise musical performance at the Democratic convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestinian protesters 'have a point', Biden says as thousands join Gaza demonstrations\par \par \uc2 Thousands of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered outside the Democratic national convention on Monday to demand that the US end military aid to Israel for its ongoing war in Gaza. Activists have branded \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CGenocide Joe\u8221\'20\'1D and called for the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to change course.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have been eager to avoid any repeat of their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/17/dnc-democratic-convention-chicago-1968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago convention in 1968}}}\uc2 , when anti-Vietnam war protests and a police riot led to scenes of chaos that stunned the nation and contributed to the party\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in November.\par \par \uc2 The biggest protest group the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marchondnc2024.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coalition to March on the DNC}}}\uc2  planned demonstrations for Monday and Thursday to coincide with Biden and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speeches. Organizers said they expected at least 20,000 activists to demonstrate, including students who protested against the war on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, dozens of protesters appeared to break through one security fence near the convention site and several demonstrators were handcuffed and detained. During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, demonstrators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265#block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfurled}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel\u8221\'20\'1D banner, but the speech continued uninterrupted.\par \par \uc2 There was limited talk of Gaza on the convention floor, though Biden reiterated his efforts to secure a ceasefire and said:\par \par \uc2 Those protesters out in the street, they have a point \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of innocent people are being killed, on both sides.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  described selecting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as his vice-president as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best decision I made my whole career\u8221\'20\'1D, and he drew a sharp contrast between her and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Mocking Trump over his recent conviction on 34 felony counts, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Violent crime has dropped to the lowest level of more than 50 years, and crime will keep coming down when we put a prosecutor in the Oval Office instead of a convicted felon.\par \par \uc2 Biden landed other punches against Trump as well, attacking the Republican nominee for describing America as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailing nation\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden said to loud cheers:\par \par \uc2 When he talks about America being a failing nation, he says, we\u8217\'20\'19re losing. He\u8217\'20\'19s the loser. He\u8217\'20\'19s dead wrong.\par \par \uc2 Still, Biden made a point to credit Harris with helping to deliver change. When discussing his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to lower prescription drug prices, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Guess who cast the tie-breaking vote? Vice-president, soon-to-be-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And when audience members repeatedly broke out in chants of \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Joe,\u8221\'20\'1D the president responded, \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden urges voters to \u8216\'20\'18preserve democracy\u8217\'20\'19 in hopeful DNC speech\par \par \uc2 Just one month after making the historic choice to withdraw from the presidential race, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took the stage at the Democratic national convention on Monday to deliver a reflective and optimistic address, urging the nation to elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to protect American democracy.\par \par \uc2 Looking back on his one and only presidential term, Biden reminded Americans that he took office just two weeks after the January 6 attack on the US Capitol, when the country was still in the early grips of the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYet, I believe then and I believe now, that progress was and is possible. Justice is achievable, and our best days are not behind us. They\u8217\'20\'19re before us,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 With a grateful heart, I stand before you now on this August night to report that democracy has prevailed. Democracy has delivered, and now democracy must be preserved.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech last night:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has some hints about what we can expect from Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speeches later today.\par \par \uc2 According to the news wire\u8217\'20\'19s sources, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will outline what he believes will lift \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to victory while also warning Democrats about the tough task they face over the next 11 weeks taking on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the run-up to polling day.\par \par \uc2 The former first lady is expected to emphasize the need for the country to turn the page on fear and division. In 2016, she offered a memorable catchphrase of \u8220\'20\'1C When they go low, we go high \u8221\'20\'1D in a speech supporting \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign said on Tuesday that it will spotlight \u8220\'20\'1Ctrusted messengers\u8221\'20\'1D from key battleground states over the convention\u8217\'20\'19s three remaining days.\par \par \uc2 They include Sen. \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  of Nevada ; Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , Sen. \uc2 Gary Peters\uc2  and Rep. \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  of Michigan; Sen. Bob Casey of Pennsylvania and Sen. \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  of Wisconsin. From Arizona, Sen. \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  will speak along with John Giles, the Republican mayor of Mesa.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Roy Cooper of North Carolina will be the last speaker before Harris accepts the Democratic nomination on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will travel on Tuesday to Milwaukee for a rally in the swing state of Wisconsin before returning to Chicago late in the evening.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, as Reuters reports, her opponent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will visit a Michigan town on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://michiganadvance.com/2024/07/22/we-love-hitler-we-love-trump-white-supremacists-march-through-howell/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one month after white supremacists rallied there}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The news has sparking renewed criticism from Democrats who accuse his campaign of stirring up racial tensions for political gain.\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to talk about \u8220\'20\'1Ccrime and safety\u8221\'20\'1D at the Livingston County Sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s Office in Howell, a town of some 10,000 people northwest of Detroit.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign spokesperson rejected criticism of the site of the event, promising Trump would speak against \u8220\'20\'1Chate of any form\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 About a dozen white supremacists chanted \u8220\'20\'1CHeil Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D and carried signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CWhite Lives Matter\u8221\'20\'1D during a march through downtown Howell last month. According to local media, another group of demonstrators shouted, \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Hitler, we love Trump\u8221\'20\'1D from a highway overpass just outside Howell.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 After the former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/06/nikki-haley-drops-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped out of the Republican primary}}}\uc2  earlier this year, some conservatives across the US continued to vote for her in subsequent primaries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/nikki-haley-presidential-primary-election-indiana-8b73a23568e054ce33163e2ca23b8fb3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 casting ballots}}}\uc2  that indicated dissent within a party that has otherwise fully embraced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When Haley finally announced that she would be supporting the ex-president in the upcoming election, she said that it was on him to mobilize her loyalists.\par \par \uc2 But it was the Biden campaign, not Trump\u8217\'20\'19s, that actively began engaging Haley voters. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to be clear: There is a place for you in my campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JoeBiden/status/1773731935619059815"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X alongside an ad targeting Haley voters.\par \par \uc2 With the president out of the race now, some of those former Haley voters have organized behind Democratic candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  in a political action group called Haley Voters for Harris.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here about the voters that have made the surprising switch\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/nikki-haley-voters-for-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Nikki Haley voters rally behind Kamala Harris: \u8216\'20\'18I picked the side that had the least issues\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The opening day of the DNC reportedly ran more than an hour behind schedule and forced some planned speakers, including musician James Taylor, to be dropped from the program, which convention organizers attributed to sustained applause for speakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Emhoff, 'the second gentleman', to address DNC on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s husband, Doug Emhoff, is also due to address the DNC later today, Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The second gentleman has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/26/doug-emhoff-kamala-harris-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described being caught by surprise}}}\uc2  by the timing of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he was dropping out of his re-election campaign, saying he was in an exercise class in Los Angeles when he heard the news.\par \par \uc2 Emhoff, 59, said a friend showed him his phone with news notifications and saying: \u8220\'20\'1CUm, you need to look at this.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have my phone, so I ran and ran and got into our car, and of course my phone is just on fire, and it\u8217\'20\'19s basically, \u8216\'20\'18Call Kamala,\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18Call Kamala,\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18Call Kamala,\u8217\'20\'19 from everyone,\u8221\'20\'1D Emhoff continued, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2024-07-25/doug-emhoff-joins-call-for-wifes-black-queer-supporters-tells-of-learning-biden-was-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the LA Times}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd of course, the first thing she said was, \u8216\'20\'18Where the... were you? I need you.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Presumably Emhoff will be better prepared for his address today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The DNC continues today following an electrifying address from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Monday night. As our Washington bureau chief, \uc2 David Smith\uc2 , writes:\par \par \uc2 More than 20,000 stood, applauded, roared and chanted, \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Joe.\u8221\'20\'1D They held tall narrow signs that said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe ?? Joe\u8221\'20\'1D \u8230\'20\'26 It was the culmination of a night that for Biden must have felt either like receiving an honorary Oscar or giving the oration at his own funeral.\par \par \uc2 In the speech, he attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot say you love your country only when you win\u8221\'20\'1D and, as Smith says:\par \par \uc2 He was a man unburdened, liberated, unrecognisable from the doddering June debate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 You can read the full piece here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden at the Democratic convention was unrecognisable from his disastrous debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Obamas to address conference on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our coverage of the Democratic National Convention.\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  and Bernie Sanders are due to address the crowds in Chicago later, following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rapturous reception for }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Obamas\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/26/obama-endorses-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement of Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  in July was seminal in securing the Democratic presidential nomination for the current US vice-president, helping to bypass a potentially ugly internal fight.\par \par \uc2 As Ed Pilkington writes, today\u8217\'20\'19s convention will also see almost 5,000 delegates from all 50 states and US territories gather on the floor of the United Center to hold what is being billed as a \u8220\'20\'1Cceremonial roll call\u8221\'20\'1D symbolically to hand the Democratic nomination to Harris.\par \par \uc2 The event will be purely figurative: Harris was officially elevated into that position two weeks ago through an online vote of delegates.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/barack-michelle-obama-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack and Michelle Obama to speak on second day of Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 Other Monday highlights include a surprise appearance by Harris herself, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/kamala-harris-surprise-speech-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking the stage to thank Biden for his service to the country}}}\uc2 . She will cap the convention with her speech on Thursday. Also on Monday:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thousands of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered outside the Democratic National Convention, calling for a ceasefire and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/democrat-platform-israel-arms-embargo-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arms embargo}}}\uc2  on Israel. Dozens of protesters appeared to break through one security fence near the convention site and several demonstrators were handcuffed and detained. During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, demonstrators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265#block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfurled}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel\u8221\'20\'1D banner.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  told the convention: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica has before us a rare and precious opportunity in \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 She understands the urgency of rent checks and groceries and prescriptions. She is as committed to our reproductive and civil rights as she is to taking on corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  outlined the historic nature of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s nomination: \u8220\'20\'1CI see the freedom to look our children in the eye and say, \u8216\'20\'18In America, you can go as far as your hard work and talent will take you,\u8217\'20\'19 and mean it. And you know what? On the other side of that glass ceiling is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , raising her hand and taking the oath of office as our 47th president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speakers from red states gave personal accounts of the impacts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Hadley Duvall, from Kentucky, described how she was raped by her stepfather and became pregnant at age 12: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine not having a choice. But today, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reality for many women and girls across the country because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240820ek8k001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
