\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Guys go where their buddies are\u8217\'20\'19: the young men recruiting each other to fight for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par 19:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Most American men support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 but activists say too many are sitting on the sidelines. So they\u8217\'20\'19re calling, texting and knocking on doors to build supportRead more from our series on young men and the US election\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, no, no, I think you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to get in contact with my wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s what a man in Florida recently told an activist who knocked on his door to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But the man was wrong. The activist, who represented a group called Men4Choice, was there to talk to him, because the group is dedicated to getting more men who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights involved in the fight for them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have to get off the sidelines,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dewayne Martin, the youth organizing director for Men4Choice, who relayed the activist\u8217\'20\'19s account to the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have to become the foot soldiers of this movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Two years after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade and allowed more than a dozen states to ban almost all abortions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/245618/abortion-trends-gender.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most men}}}\uc2  in the United States support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Within months of the decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/abortion-attitudes-in-a-post-roe-world-findings-from-the-50-state-2022-american-values-atlas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 65% of men}}}\uc2  between the ages of 18 and 29 said they supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being legal in all or most cases. But Men4Choice calls these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/young-men-and-the-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 young men}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cpassively pro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Young women still support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at higher rates than their male peers \u8211\'20\'13 and young men are just not as motivated to take a public stand on the issue. Just 43% of gen Z men say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical issue\u8221\'20\'1D, compared with 68% of gen Z women, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/07/gen-z-voters-political-ideology-gender-gap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political scientist Melissa Deckman found}}}\uc2  in her forthcoming book The Politics of Gen Z. This indifference has consequences: compared with women, men between the ages of 18 and 44 are less likely to say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is motivating them to vote in the 2024 elections, according to polling from the firm PerryUndem. They are also less likely to say that the state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  rights will affect whom they vote for.\par \par \uc2 Men4Choice\u8217\'20\'19s goal is to get these young men to vote, canvass and otherwise act on their beliefs \u8211\'20\'13 instead of leaving the work to women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we think about our organizing strategy, it\u8217\'20\'19s: help men see the harm,\u8221\'20\'1D said Oren Jacobson, a Men4Choice co-founder. \u8220\'20\'1CHelp men understand how this issue is not just a woman\u8217\'20\'19s issue. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s about freedom, it\u8217\'20\'19s about power, it\u8217\'20\'19s about control. It is an issue that impacts all of us, our families, our loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It affects young men\u8217\'20\'19s futures, too. Compared with young men whose partners got pregnant and gave birth, young men whose partners had abortions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6755038/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost four times}}}\uc2  more likely to graduate college. Young men who have been involved in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also more likely to make more money than those whose partners gave birth. Overall, an estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.contraceptionjournal.org/article/S0010-7824(22)00026-9/abstract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one in five men}}}\uc2  has impregnated somebody who has had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats have made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights one of their central issues in the 2024 elections, while Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 wary of how outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall probably lost them a much heralded \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2022 midterms \u8211\'20\'13 have tried to downplay the issue and their own role in overturning Roe. However, as they\u8217\'20\'19ve backed away, rightwing commentators and politicians have become far more adept at discussing masculinity than their leftwing counterparts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/05/young-men-voters-us-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts have told the Guardian}}}\uc2 . These rightwing public figures are not only willing to acknowledge that young men are struggling \u8211\'20\'13 with getting into college, with their finances, with their mental health \u8211\'20\'13 but also to portray these struggles as the result of women\u8217\'20\'19s growing social and political power.\par \par \uc2 This kind of talk \u8211\'20\'13 which is so popular it has essentially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/14/young-men-election-joe-rogan-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spawned a cottage industry}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is believed to be a major reason why, despite their past support for liberal causes, so many young men are now pivoting towards conservatism (and potentially towards supporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels good. It\u8217\'20\'19s telling men: \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re the priority. You\u8217\'20\'19re the superior being,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Davan\u8217\'20\'19te Jennings, a Men4Choice fellow who lives in Georgia. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18You act like this, this is when you get all the cars, the women, the mansion. Grind 24/7. Don\u8217\'20\'19t think about mental health. Depression isn\u8217\'20\'19t real.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Jennings\u8217\'20\'19 view, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/12/trump-maga-divide-son-father"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 such \u8220\'20\'1Ctoxic masculinity\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  is part of the reason why young men don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like they can be openly passionate about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. He hears references to it all the time: when Jennings talks to men through Men4Choice, the men often use phrases like \u8220\'20\'1Cto be a man\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe manly thing to do\u8221\'20\'1D. Expressing emotions \u8211\'20\'13 including caring about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t fit into that mold of masculinity.\par \par \uc2 Men4Choice, then, aims to reframe how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fits into antiquated and restrictive notions of masculinity. \u8220\'20\'1CMasculinity is taking action,\u8221\'20\'1D Martin said. \u8220\'20\'1CMasculinity is caring for the people that you love. Masculinity is ensuring that you are building a pathway towards freedom for you and your people, and realizing that those two things are not separate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christian Shephard, a 26-year-old Men4Choice fellow who serves as an organizer for the group in central Florida, tries to open up conversations about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights with men by discussing how some men treat women, including how they may objectify or sexualize women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt may sound like that has nothing to do with reproductive justice, but it certainly does,\u8221\'20\'1D Shephard said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a clear connection between how people talk about women and how these [anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] laws are being created to deprive them of fundamental rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a recent Men4Choice \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity conversation\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 virtual and in-person discussions where fellows are expected to bring male friends \u8211\'20\'13 one man claimed he didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to take any responsibility for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen should keep their legs closed\u8221\'20\'1D, Jennings recalled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was literally the words he used,\u8221\'20\'1D Jennings said. \u8220\'20\'1CMost of us who are pro-choice on the call are like: \u8216\'20\'18Now we see why it\u8217\'20\'19s important to dismantle that way of thinking.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jacobson launched Men4Choice in 2015, but the group has exploded in the years since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise. The Men4Choice fellowship program, which runs three times a year and is training 70 men between the ages of 18 and 28 this summer, has almost tripled in size since the summer of 2022. Many Men4Choice fellows are based in Florida, Georgia, and North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 all states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Though he was raised in a Democratic area of Miami, Martin, 22, said he hadn\u8217\'20\'19t acted on his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until 2020. He was a high school senior working on organizing around school boards when a friend told him about Men4Choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was in that moment that I realized, despite my being raised by a community of women who have served as my village and have made my life possible in several ways, I\u8217\'20\'19ve never taken a direct action to support them on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D recalled Martin, who became a Men4Choice fellow that year.\par \par \uc2 In the months before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  became the Democratic nominee for president, Men4Choice partnered with Doug Emhoff, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s husband and the second gentleman of the United States, to host events centered on energizing men to fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. (\u8220\'20\'1CThis is an issue of fairness to women. Women are dying,\u8221\'20\'1D Emhoff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/doug-emhoff-pushing-men-advocate-abortion-rights-rcna151328"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC}}}\uc2  in May. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s affecting men\u8217\'20\'19s ability to plan their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D) Now, the group is trying to mobilize male volunteers and funnel them towards partner organizations working on the ground.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuys go where their buddies are,\u8221\'20\'1D Jacobson said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to create an ecosystem of men to get them to show up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Men4Choice is also heavily focusing on Florida, which has banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 before many people even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 and where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/florida-abortion-democrats-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters will decide}}}\uc2  in November whether to amend the state constitution to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights ballot measures previously have succeeded in Republican strongholds, such as Ohio and Kentucky. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2023/exit-polls/ohio/general/issue-1/20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Exit polls}}}\uc2  found that 73% of male voters between the ages of 18 and 29 voted in favor of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio measure}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a significant share of voters, but still less than the 81% of young female voters who supported it.\par \par \uc2 The Florida amendment must garner 60% of the vote to pass. This fall, Men4Choice wants to reach 400,000 voters through phone and text banking, according to Martin. The group also wants to hold 100 community conversations with men.\par \par \uc2 There is, however, a limit to the organization\u8217\'20\'19s activism. Men4Choice focuses on men who already support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights or are at least open to having a discussion about it \u8211\'20\'13 not men who are adamantly opposed to the procedure. \u8220\'20\'1CIf there\u8217\'20\'19s not an understanding or a clear line of wanting to understand,\u8221\'20\'1D Jennings said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand we\u8217\'20\'19re just going to sit here and get into a debate \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s pointless.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240820ek8k001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
