\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says he gave \u8216\'20\'18heart and soul to our nation\u8217\'20\'19 as he passes torch \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Chris Stein, Sam Levin and Maanvi Singh (earlier) \par \uc2 12,096 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par 06:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full report on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04am BST\par \par \uc2 With that important DNC fashion news, this blog is closing. You can read our full story on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech at the link below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urges voters to elect Harris in order to \u8216\'20\'18preserve democracy\u8217\'20\'19 in hopeful speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02am BST\par \par \uc2 It is a truth universally acknowledged that a prominent female politician in possession of a wardrobe will have her outfits divined for clues about who she is and what she thinks. Democratic presidential nominee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , is no exception.\par \par \uc2 But the dissection of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s choice of outfit took on a different tone after her surprise appearance at the Democratic National Convention in Monday evening, with some asking simply: is she trolling us?\par \par \uc2 Harris wore a suit that could be described as tan: a colour that Barack Obama famously favoured during his two terms in office. It was an outfit choice that drove Republicans and right-wing pundits mad. Most famously when Fox News host Lou Dobbs declared that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cshocking to a lot of people\u8221\'20\'1D that Obama wore a tan suit in 2014 to discuss escalating the US response to Islamic State in Syria.\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz ticket is not immune to poking fun at their Republican rivals. Their debut collection of merchandise included an accessory to rival the Maga hat: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/kamala-harris-tim-walz-merch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris Walz hunting cap}}}\uc2  that raised a million dollars for the campaign within hours of its release.\par \par \uc2 And Harris has form when it comes to including references in her clothing and image: for her cover of Vogue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/kamala-harris-and-the-political-power-of-black-sororities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she appeared in front of colours that represent her sorority}}}\uc2 , Alpha Kappa Alpha, and wearing their signature string of pearls. She was also once known for wearing Converse All Stars.\par \par \uc2 Though the Republicans had, hours after Harris\u8217\'20\'19s appearance, resisted taking the alleged tan suit bait, they have not been above sartorial slights. At the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , Republican party co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/30/us/politics/lara-trump-kamala-harris-trash-bag.html?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared Harris to an $1,800 faux trash bag sold by Balenciaga}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/kamala-harris-wore-a-tan-suit-to-day-one-of-the-dnc-what-does-it-mean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris wore a tan suit to day one of the DNC \u8211\'20\'13 what does it mean?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is our full story on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, from Joan E Greve:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-speech-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urges voters to elect Harris to \u8216\'20\'18preserve democracy\u8217\'20\'19 in hopeful speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gave surprise remarks\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/kamala-harris-surprise-speech-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a surprise appearance}}}\uc2  at the convention on Monday night to thank \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his service: \u8220\'20\'1CJoe, thank you for your historic leadership, for your lifetime of service to our nation, and for all you will continue to do, we are forever grateful to you. Thank you, Joe!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, who is due to give her formal speech at the end of the week, electrified the crowd when she entered the stage, with Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom playing in the background. \u8220\'20\'1CLooking out at everyone tonight, I see the beauty of our great nation. People from every corner of our country and every walk of life are here united by our shared vision for the future of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: Thousands protested outside the DNC\par \par \uc2 Thousands of pro-Palestinian protesters gathered outside the Democratic National Convention, calling for a ceasefire and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/democrat-platform-israel-arms-embargo-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arms embargo}}}\uc2  on Israel. Dozens of protesters appeared to break through one security fence near the convention site and several demonstrators were handcuffed and detained. During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech, demonstrators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265#block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfurled}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel\u8221\'20\'1D banner, but the speech continued uninterrupted. There was limited talk of Gaza on the convention floor, though Biden reiterated his efforts to secure a ceasefire and said, \u8220\'20\'1CThose protesters out in the street, they have a point \u8211\'20\'13 a lot of innocent people are being killed, on both sides.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/democrat-platform-israel-arms-embargo-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 platform}}}\uc2  released before the convention did not include an arms embargo, a key demand by uncommitted delegates.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden took questions when he arrived at O\u8217\'20\'19Hare. From the pool report (and for those following, on him and Pelosi):\par \par \uc2 Ask if he\u8217\'20\'19s mad at Pelosi or at spoken to her: \u8216\'20\'18I haven\u8217\'20\'19t spoken to Nancy. No one made the decision but me.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Asked about tearing up: \u8216\'20\'18The reception was pretty overwhelming.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Ask about his comment earlier questioning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stability: \u8216\'20\'18I think he has a problem.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On the cease-fire: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s still in play.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The highlight of the night: \u8216\'20\'18My daughter\u8217\'20\'19s introduction.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: Democrats rallied around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and stopping Project 2025\par \par \uc2 Speakers from red states gave personal accounts of the impacts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Hadley Duvall, from Kentucky, described how she was raped by her stepfather and became pregnant at age 12: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine not having a choice. But today, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reality for many women and girls across the country because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D She noted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous remarks calling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans a \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful thing\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is so beautiful about a child having to carry her parent\u8217\'20\'19s child?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speakers also repeatedly tied the Trump and the Republican agenda to Project 2025, the roadmap for a second Trump administration crafted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/project-2025-training-videos-trump-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former Trump officials}}}\uc2 . Mallory McMorrow, a state senator from Michigan, held a copy of the Project 2025 document and assailed the plan to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  into a dictator\u8221\'20\'1D. Congressman \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  called Project 2025 \u8220\'20\'1CJim Crow 2.0\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden noted that the project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/article/2024/jul/04/trump-project-2025-heritage-foundation-education-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls}}}\uc2  for the dismantling of the US department of education.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will break the \u8216\'20\'18glass ceiling\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the former secretary of state and 2016 presidential candidate, also gave an impassioned speech, outlining the historic nature of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s nomination: \u8220\'20\'1CI see the freedom to look our children in the eye and say, \u8216\'20\'18In America, you can go as far as your hard work and talent will take you,\u8217\'20\'19 and mean it. And you know what? On the other side of that glass ceiling is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , raising her hand and taking the oath of office as our 47th president \u8230\'20\'26 Because when a barrier falls for one of us, it falls and clears the way for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clinton drew a sharp contrast between Harris, a former prosecutor, and Trump who \u8220\'20\'1Cfell asleep at his own trial, and when he woke up, he made his own kind of history \u8230\'20\'26 the first person to run for president with 34 felony convictions\u8221\'20\'1D. The remark sparked \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D chants, a throwback to the \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D chants Clinton faced in 2016 at Trump rallies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: AOC praised Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ceasefire efforts\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  gave one of the most energetic speeches of the night, talking about her roots as a bartender and saying: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica has before us a rare and precious opportunity in \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . We have a chance to elect a president who is for the middle class, because she is from the middle class. She understands the urgency of rent checks and groceries and prescriptions. She is as committed to our reproductive and civil rights as she is to taking on corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The progressive congresswoman and \u8220\'20\'1CSquad\u8221\'20\'1D member also earned loud applause for saying that Harris was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking tirelessly to secure a ceasefire in Gaza and bringing hostages home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  passed the torch\par \par \uc2 As the president took the stage at around 10:30pm CT, the crowd broke out into enthusiastic \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Joe\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Joe\u8221\'20\'1D chants, with drawn-out cheers that repeatedly prevented him from continuing his remarks. Biden revisited some of the darkest chapters of the Trump administration, including the January 6 insurrection, and attacked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vision of America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHe says we\u8217\'20\'19re losing. He\u8217\'20\'19s the loser.\u8221\'20\'1D He earned loud applause for his praise of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying selecting her as vice-president was the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest decision I made my whole career\u8221\'20\'1D, and, \u8220\'20\'1CCrime will keep coming down when we put a prosecutor in the office instead of a convicted felon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speakers throughout the night heaped praise on Biden. Dr Jill Biden, the first lady, praised her husband for withdrawing from the race, saying she watched him \u8220\'20\'1Cdig deep into his soul\u8221\'20\'1D as he weighed the decision. The president said of his decision: \u8220\'20\'1CI love the job, but I love my country more.\u8221\'20\'1D Toward the end of his speech, he said, \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, I gave my best to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/biden-dnc-convention-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden, Hillary Clinton and AOC boost Harris: key takeaways from night one of the Democratic national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi has just tweeted a picture of herself holding a We heart Joe sign. As I pointed out a short while ago, Pelosi has given some harsh criticism of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s skills as a politician recently, but also said she hoped that their friendship could survive the role she played in ending his presidency.\par \par \uc2 qmeltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ThankYouJoe?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ThankYouJoe}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Rclo6KeuDX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Rclo6KeuDX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@TeamPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamPelosi/status/1825766129517679020?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi recently said she had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been that impressed\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical operation\u8221\'20\'1D discussing a judgment that helped her conclude the president could not beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and should step aside.\par \par \uc2 Speaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/nancy-pelosi-biden-election-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the New Yorker}}}\uc2 , she said she hoped her role in ending Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency would not destroy her relationship with Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope so,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI pray so. I cry so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will be speaking tomorrow night at the DNC\par \par \uc2 Speaking in his political hometown of Chicago, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first Black president will honour President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legacy and make the case for Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s poised to be a significant moment as she takes on former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a matchup that features the same cultural and ideological fissures Obama warned against two decades ago,\u8221\'20\'1D AP writes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Obama is still a north star in the party,\u8221\'20\'1D Illinois lieutenant governor Juliana Stratton told AP. She credits Obama with helping her become her state\u8217\'20\'19s first Black woman in the role.\par \par \uc2 Besides Harris on Thursday, Stratton said, no voice this week is more integral to stirring Democrats, reaching independents and cajoling moderate Republicans than Obama.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe knows how to get across the finish line,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12am BST\par \par \uc2 More now on \uc2 Hilary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech: Clinton compared Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record as a convicted felon with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s as a former prosecutor. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a prosecutor, Kamala locked up murders and drug traffickers. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fell asleep at his own trial.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At that moment the thousands of Democratic delegates amassed on the DNC floor spontaneously burst into chants of \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up! Lock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D. It was an ironic echo of the chant that was repeatedly directed against Clinton by Trump supporters, with his blessing, in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Clinton, with the diplomacy behoving a former secretary of state, made no comment. But the way she nodded her head in synch to the chants spoke volumes.\par \par \uc2 Clinton made little effort to hide that for her the hope of pushing Harris into the White House as the first female US president was profoundly personal. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are so close to breaking through once and for all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, conjuring up the image of Harris raising her hand \u8220\'20\'1Con the other side of that glass ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D to take the presidential oath of office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our time America. This is when we stand up, this is when we break through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/dnc-hillary-clinton-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton takes jabs at Trump and pins hope on Harris to \u8216\'20\'18break through\u8217\'20\'19 glass ceiling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The pool report note that speaker emeritus, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cwaved a \u8216\'20\'18we heart Joe\u8217\'20\'19 sign when Potus came out on stage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi recently said she had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been that impressed\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical operation\u8221\'20\'1D discussing a judgment that helped her conclude the president could not beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and should step aside.\par \par \uc2 Speaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/nancy-pelosi-biden-election-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the New Yorker}}}\uc2 , she said she hoped her role in ending Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency would not destroy her relationship with a man three years younger but elected as a senator in 1972, 14 years before Pelosi won her seat in the House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope so,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI pray so. I cry so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is some of the behind the scenes pool report of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech:\par \par \uc2 Flotus watched Posus\u8217\'20\'19 speech from the convention floor with the Biden grandchildren. The family moved backstage toward the end of his remarks.\par \par \uc2 She came out after his remarks to give him a kiss. Then \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Doug Emhoff came out. Hugs were exchanged.\par \par \uc2 The Biden family was next: Hunter and Melissa led out Baby Beau, holding his hands. Finnegan, Maisy, Naomi and Peter, Natalie and Little Hunter, Ashley and Howard were all on stage.\par \par \uc2 Ashley danced around the stage. Harris bent down to talk to Baby Beau. Baby Beau gave lots of waves. Potus then took Baby Beau\u8217\'20\'19s hand to walk with him off stage.\par \par \uc2 Poolers could see Hunter Biden backstage with Potus, standing near the stage door where Potus came out onto stage, while Potus was speaking.\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestinian protesters were removed after unfurling a banner during Potus remarks. It appeared to read \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D They appeared to be near Florida delegation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton}}}\uc2  gave one of the most powerful speeches of her career in politics on Monday as she implored American voters finally to crack the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest, hardest glass ceiling\u8221\'20\'1D that had eluded her so bitterly eight years ago.\par \par \uc2 In a rousing 15-minute speech at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic national convention}}}\uc2  in Chicago, Clinton returned to the theme that she intended to invoke in a victory speech on election night, 8 November 2016. That speech was never delivered, the glass ceiling standing firm in the wake of her shock defeat to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But what she had failed to attain was within the grasp of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/kamala-harris-surprise-speech-democratic-national-convention/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , only the second woman to be nominated at the top of a major party presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 And the man who had derided and humiliated Clinton on the campaign trail back in 2016, mocking her as \u8220\'20\'1CCrooked\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLyin\u8217\'20\'19 Hillary\u8221\'20\'1D, was now on the defensive. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have him on the run now,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 Reveling in the chance to turn the tables on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2 , Clinton drew a parallel between the slights she endured at the hands of the Republican candidate in 2016 and the insults he continues to hurl at Harris in 2024. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is no surprise that he is lying about Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s record, he is mocking her name and her laugh. Sounds familiar?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/dnc-hillary-clinton-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillary Clinton takes jabs at Trump and pins hope on Harris to \u8216\'20\'18break through\u8217\'20\'19 glass ceiling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech was energetic, and welcomed by sustained applause. He was emotional, at one point wiping away tears, and it had the tone \u8211\'20\'13as expected \u8211\'20\'13 of a farewell. It is likely to be one of a handful of major speeches Biden will make during the remainder of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 It is almost a month to the day that he dropped out of the race.\par \par \uc2 He made reference to the decision, and his age, which was a factor behind it, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been too young to be in the Senate, because I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t 30 yet, and too old to stay as president. But I hope you know how grateful I am to all of you. I can honestly say, and I mean this in the bottom, giving my word as a Biden, I can honestly say I\u8217\'20\'19m more optimistic about the future than I was when I was elected as a 29-year-old United States senator.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48am BST\par \par \uc2 When Harris hugged Biden after that speech, she appears to have said \u8220\'20\'1CI love you\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 tlltrKamala Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yae4JeQ0aZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Yae4JeQ0aZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1825751159413584141?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President Harris embraces President Biden at the end of his speech.\par \par \uc2 You can see her say to him, "I love you."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1825750876130095459?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US Politics coverage as the first night of the Democratic National Convention wraps up in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'I gave my all': Democratic national convention's first night recapped\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  passed the torch to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the Democratic national convention ended the first of its four nights in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what happened this evening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c40f938f08dc0eb7d238b4#block-66c40f938f08dc0eb7d238b4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the convention that \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy has prevailed\u8221\'20\'1D and recounted his accomplishments, while also saying that Harris and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c417b28f087ff7c5bde26d#block-66c417b28f087ff7c5bde26d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carry on}}}\uc2  his work.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As he closed his speech, Biden said he had dedicated himself to serving the US, and had never felt more optimistic about the country\u8217\'20\'19s future. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve made a lot of mistakes in my career, but I gave my best to you for 50 years. Like many of you, I gave my heart and soul to our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3ed288f08dc0eb7d237c7#block-66c3ed288f08dc0eb7d237c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly spoke}}}\uc2  from the convention stage, telling attendees it was \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to be a great week\u8221\'20\'1D and thanking Biden for his leadership.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  gave Harris her endorsement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3eb5f8f089110c1d4f506#block-66c3eb5f8f089110c1d4f506"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  the vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Chas the character, experience, and vision to lead us forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestine demonstrations brought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3c94c8f087ff7c5bde0a8#block-66c3c94c8f087ff7c5bde0a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thousands}}}\uc2  to the streets outside the United Center, where the convention was being held. Part of the protest grew violent, with demonstrators breaking through the outer security fencing, but not getting near the convention, Chicago police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3d4ee8f089110c1d4f495#block-66c3d4ee8f089110c1d4f495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3ca168f087ff7c5bde0af#block-66c3ca168f087ff7c5bde0af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two arrests}}}\uc2  were made.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor who is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3ea618f087ff7c5bde14b#block-66c3ea618f087ff7c5bde14b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  in the convention hall, but did not give a speech.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c4161d8f08dc0eb7d238d1#block-66c4161d8f08dc0eb7d238d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  pro-Palestinian protesters \u8220\'20\'1Chad a point\u8221\'20\'1D, while reaffirming his support for a ceasefire in Gaza. Some demonstrators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265#block-66c415398f087ff7c5bde265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interrupted}}}\uc2  his speech, though it was not clear that he noticed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Residents of red states{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c4034a8f087ff7c5bde1ed#block-66c4034a8f087ff7c5bde1ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told of}}}\uc2  the damage done by Republican-supported restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is a key campaign issue for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden came out onstage after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended his address.\par \par \uc2 She was followed by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , her husband Doug Emhoff and the Biden family, including the president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter Ashley Biden, and his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president and vice-president hugged and waved to the crowd, remaining for several minutes before leaving the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says he gave 'my heart and soul to our nation' as he passes torch to Harris\par \par \uc2 As he closed his speech, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he had dedicated himself to serving the United States, and had never felt more optimistic about the country\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve made a lot of mistakes in my career, but I gave my best to you for 50 years. Like many of you, I gave my heart and soul to our nation, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been blessed a million times in return in the support of the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve really been too young to be in the Senate, because I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t 30 yet, and too old to stay as president. But I hope you know how grateful I am to all of you. I can honestly say, and I mean this in the bottom, giving my word as a Biden, I can honestly say I\u8217\'20\'19m more optimistic about the future than I was when I was elected as a 29-year-old United States senator.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls picking Harris as his running mate the 'best decision' of his career\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said making \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  his vice-presidential pick was the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest decision\u8221\'20\'1D of his five-decade-plus political career.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSelecting Kamala was the very first decision I made \u8230\'20\'26 when I became our nominee, and it was the best decision I made my whole career,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'Kamala and Tim' will protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voting rights\par \par \uc2 The passing of the torch continued, with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  telling Democrats that \u8220\'20\'1CKamala and Tim\u8221\'20\'1D would continue his work on priorities such as protecting voting rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, as well as taxing the megarich.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala and Tim are going to make them pay their fair share. They\u8217\'20\'19ll protect Social Security, Medicare. Trump wants to cut Social Security, Medicare. Kamala and Tim will protect your freedom \u8230\'20\'26 your right to vote, protect your civil rights. And you know, Trump will do everything to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. Oh, he will. Kamala and Tim will do everything they possibly can. That\u8217\'20\'19s why you have to elect a Senate and House to restore Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says Gaza war protesters 'have a point', reiterates support for ceasefire to 'end this war'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addressed the war in Gaza, which became one of the most divisive issues of his presidency after he supported Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of the enclave, while pushing for a ceasefire between the warring parties.\par \par \uc2 The president reiterated that he would continue working towards an elusive deal, and showed sympathy with the pro-Palestinian protesters who have accused him of abetting genocide by supplying Israel with military equipment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA few days ago, I put forward a proposal that brought us closer to [a ceasefire] than we\u8217\'20\'19ve been since October 7,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working around the clock, my secretary of state, [to] prevent a wider war, reunite hostages with their families and surge humanitarian, health and food assistance into Gaza now to end the civilian suffering of the Palestinian people and finally, finally, finally, deliver a ceasefire and,\u8221\'20\'1D as he pounded his fist on the podium, \u8220\'20\'1Cend this war!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then addressed the protesters who have denounced him in demonstrations nationwide over the past 10 months, including right outside the convention in Chicago: \u8220\'20\'1CThose protesters out in the street, they have a point. A lot of innocent people are being killed on both sides.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestine protesters interrupt Biden speech\par \par \uc2 A few anti-war protesters unfurled a banner that said \u8220\'20\'1CStop Arming Israel\u8221\'20\'1D when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was speaking.\par \par \uc2 The move did not go over well with Democrats nearby, some of whom hit the demonstrators with their \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Joe\u8221\'20\'1D signs and tried to rip the banner away from them, video of the incident posted by reporters showed:\par \par \uc2 enltrAudience members at the DNC in Chicago unfurl banner that says \u8220\'20\'1CStop arming Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After audience sees the banner, they begin chanting \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Joe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Man tries to rip banner away.\par \par \uc2 Stadium lights over this spot then dimmed and banner was ripped away. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3RfK1aUSV4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3RfK1aUSV4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Prem Thakker (@prem_thakker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/prem_thakker/status/1825739025606390163?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t clear if the president noticed the disruption.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden once again deployed a line that both trumpeted his own achievements and subtly passed the torch to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president was talking about how violent crime has been declining nationally, then segued into complimenting Harris and attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s recent criminal conviction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe murder rate is falling faster than at any time in history,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CViolent crime has dropped to the lowest level of more than 50 years, and crime will keep coming down when we put a prosecutor in the Oval Office instead of a convicted felon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57am BST\par \par \uc2 We can watch the teleprompter from our perch in the United Center, and can see Biden is going off script occasionally.\par \par \uc2 In one case, it was to make light of his age. \u8220\'20\'1CI know more foreign leaders by their first names and know them well than anybody alive, just because I\u8217\'20\'19m so damn old,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden again brands Trump a 'loser'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  again attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Closer\u8221\'20\'1D for characterizing the United States as a nation in decline.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calls America a failing nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he talks about America being a failing nation, he says, we\u8217\'20\'19re losing. He\u8217\'20\'19s the loser. He\u8217\'20\'19s dead wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden appears emotional after daughter Ashley introduces him\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an image of the emotional moment when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took to the stage at the convention after his daughter, Ashley, introduced him:\par \par \uc2 The president gave heartfelt remarks about his children and his wife, Jill Biden, to kick off his speech. He also appeared to get emotional as the crowd repeatedly interrupted his remarks with lengthy \u8220\'20\'1Cwe love Joe\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you, Joe\u8221\'20\'1D chants.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am BST\par \par \uc2 This is a historic speech for Biden, but he\u8217\'20\'19s not necessarily debuting new lines.\par \par \uc2 Rather, he\u8217\'20\'19s using oldies-but-goodies, such as: \u8220\'20\'1CWall Street didn\u8217\'20\'19t build America, the middle class built America, and unions, unions built the middle class.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 'We finally beat Big Pharma': Biden recounts achievements\par \par \uc2 Biden is both recounting the accomplishments of his administration, and noting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had one of the most extraordinary four years of progress ever, period,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CJust think about it. Covid no longer controls our lives. We\u8217\'20\'19ve gone from economic crisis to the strongest economy in the entire world \u8230\'20\'26 record 16m new jobs, record small business growth, record high stock market \u8230\'20\'26 wages up, inflation down, way down, and continuing to go down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then remarked on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/15/biden-policy-medicines-less-expensive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his efforts}}}\uc2  to lower prescription drug prices, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally beat Big Pharma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuess who cast the tie-breaking vote? Vice-president, soon-to-be-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 At one point, the crowd again began chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you Joe!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CThank you Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D the president replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am BST\par \par \uc2 'Democracy has prevailed', Biden tells convention\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  then reminded the Democrats of all that has passed in the three-and-a-half years since he took office in the wake of the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was, I told you then, a winter of peril and possibility \u8230\'20\'26 we were in the grip of a once-in-a-century pandemic, historic joblessness, a call for racial justice, long overdue, clear and present threats to our very democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CYet, I believe then and I believe now, that progress was and is possible. Justice is achievable, and our best days are not behind us. They\u8217\'20\'19re before us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continues with the metaphor:\par \par \uc2 Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s summer. The winter has passed. With a grateful heart, I stand before you now on this August night to report that democracy has prevailed. Democracy has delivered, and now democracy must be preserved.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The president then turned to more somber matters, describing how he was inaugurated just a few weeks after the January 6 insurrection at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNearly four years ago, in winter, on the steps of the Capitol on a cold January day, I raised my right hand and I swore an oath to you and to God to preserve, protect and defend the constitution and to faithfully execute the office of the president United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn front of me was the city, surrounded by the national guard. Behind me a Capitol, just two weeks before, overrun by a violent mob. But I knew then, from the bottom of my heart, that I knew now there is no place in America for political violence, none.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reprising a line he\u8217\'20\'19s used before, which is of course a reference to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the president said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot say you love your country only when you win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am BST\par \par \uc2 As begins his remarks, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has this crowd wrapped around his finger.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, let me ask you: are you ready to vote for freedom?\u8221\'20\'1D he asked. The response from the crowd was a big \u8220\'20\'1Cyes!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre ready to vote for democracy and for America?\u8221\'20\'1D The answer was \u8220\'20\'1Cyes!\u8221\'20\'1D again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me ask you, are you ready to elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D This time, the \u8220\'20\'1Cyes!\u8221\'20\'1D was even louder.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Lots of people have received warm welcomes at this convention, but none quite like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet been able to say anything because of all the cheering.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 The Democrats are very excited to see \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re holding up signs that read \u8220\'20\'1CWe ? Joe\u8221\'20\'1D, and just cheering and cheering. The president is saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you, thank you, thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D and just said, \u8220\'20\'1CI love you!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is likely to be one of the last major speeches Biden makes in his political career.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addresses Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has come onstage at the Democratic national convention.\par \par \uc2 The president jogged out, and is hugging and exchanging words with his daughter, Ashley, who introduced him.\par \par \uc2 At one point, he took out a handkerchief and dabbed his eye.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expected to speak at Democratic convention, as daughter gives introduction\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to, in a few minutes, take the stage at the Democratic national convention, where he will reaffirm his endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as his successor.\par \par \uc2 His daughter, Ashley Biden, is introducing the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou always tell us, but we don\u8217\'20\'19t tell you enough, that you are the love of our lives and the life of our love,\u8221\'20\'1D the first daughter said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden says president dug 'deep into his soul' in deciding to end re-election bid\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision not to seek a second term as president was perhaps the biggest decision of his political career, and one that came only after some serious soul searching, Jill Biden said.\par \par \uc2 There are moments when I fall in love with him all over again,\u8221\'20\'1D the first lady said. Among them:\par \par \uc2 Weeks ago, when I saw him dig deep into his soul and decide to no longer seek re-election and endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . With faith and conviction, Joe knows that our nation\u8217\'20\'19s strength doesn\u8217\'20\'19t come from intimidation or cruelty, it comes from the small acts of kindness that heal deep wounds, from service to the communities that make us who we are, from love of a country that shines with promise and renewal. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  knows that too.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden addresses Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden has walked onstage.\par \par \uc2 She is wearing a sparkly blue dress. The crowd greeted her with green signs that read \u8220\'20\'1CJILL\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to read that the dress is blue, not gray.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am BST\par \par \uc2 We are almost on to the Bidens.\par \par \uc2 Chris Coons, the senator from their home state Delaware, is now onstage. We expect Jill Biden to speak next and then the president, who will be introduced by his daughter, Ashley Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 George senator Warnock calls Trump 'a plague on the American conscience'\par \par \uc2 In one of the more somber attacks made on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  so far tonight, Georgia senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  called the former president \u8220\'20\'1Ca plague on the American conscience\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a clear and present threat to the precious covenant we share with one another,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 Warnock is also a pastor at Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Ebenezer Baptist Church, and deployed that oratory skill in denouncing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/26/trump-selling-bible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement}}}\uc2  of the Bible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I saw him. I saw him holding the Bible, and endorsing a Bible, as if it needed his endorsement. He should try reading it,\u8221\'20\'1D Warnock said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt says, do justice, love kindness and walk humbly with your God. He should try reading it. It says, love your neighbor as yourself. It says, inasmuch as you\u8217\'20\'19ve done it unto the least of these, you have done it also unto me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 : 'Extremism is being soundly rejected'\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governor, emphasized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and reproductive justice in his speech, one of the final remarks before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  takes the stage.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 Trump says people are absolutely thrilled that women have their basic rights eliminated. JD Vance says women should stay in violent marriages and that pregnancies resulting from rape are simply inconvenient. Their policies give rapists more rights than their victims. That\u8217\'20\'19s not inconvenient. It\u8217\'20\'19s just plain wrong \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Thankfully, this extremism is being soundly rejected all over our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Speakers from red states tell of impacts of GOP's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 A married couple and two women from red states just appeared onstage to attack Republicans over their support for laws that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago, my husband and I were expecting our second child. Our daughter, Lauren, couldn\u8217\'20\'19t wait to be a big sister. I was getting ready for her fourth birthday party when something didn\u8217\'20\'19t feel right. Two emergency rooms sent me away because of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. No one would confirm that I was miscarrying. I was in pain, bleeding so much my husband feared for my life. No woman should experience what I endured,\u8221\'20\'1D said Louisiana resident Kaitlyn Joshua.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s Hadley Duvall described how growing up, she \u8220\'20\'1Cwas an all-American Girl. Varsity soccer captain, cheerleading captain, homecoming queen and survivor\u8221\'20\'1D, who was sexually abused and then raped by her stepfather.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt age 12, I took my first pregnancy test, and it was positive. That was the first time I was ever told you have options. I can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine not having a choice. But today, that\u8217\'20\'19s the reality for many women and girls across the country because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin attacks \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  as Trump's 'pet chameleon'\par \par \uc2 Maryland congressman Jamie Raskin spoke of the January 6 insurrection in his remarks and attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance. He pointed out that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , has disavowed Trump due to January 6 and the threats to his life:\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, do you understand why there was a sudden job opening for running mate on the GOP ticket? They tried to kill your predecessor \u8230\'20\'26 They tried to kill him, because he would not follow Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to destroy and nullify the votes of millions of Americans. Your votes, Pennsylvania. Your votes, Michigan, Nevada, Arizona \u8230\'20\'26 Are we going to go back to the days of election suppression and violent insurrection?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Raskin continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the career criminal and incorrigible recidivist conman and his pet chameleon, JD Vance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRaskin: JD Vance, do you understand why there was a sudden job opening for running mate on the GOP ticket? They tried to kill your predecessor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/STrd0wmTea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/STrd0wmTea}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1825720875053887993?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Raskin also called Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Csore loser who does not know how to take no for an answer from American voters, American courts, or American women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Up now is progressive congresswoman Jasmine Crockett , who seems to be responding to criticisms that dogged \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential run of her record as a prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 The backlash from the left to her record on criminal justice played a role in her swift defeat in the Democratic primaries, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ultimately won. Democrats have been nervous that the same issues could crop up again this year, and Crockett is making a point to cast Harris in a compassionate light.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was the first attorney general in the nation to order that her officers wear body cams, and she started the Back on Track program to reduce recidivism,\u8221\'20\'1D Crockett said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe did all these things because she genuinely cares about people. She sees each person as just that, a person, not a statistic. She\u8217\'20\'19s proven that since the first day she stepped into a courtroom and said what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/19/democratic-convention-dnc-biden-harris-updates?page=with:block-66c3f9b28f08dc0eb7d2381e#block-66c3f9b28f08dc0eb7d2381e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 y\u8217\'20\'19all already heard Hillary say}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Kerr and Tony Goldwyn make appearances\par \par \uc2 Actor Tony Goldwyn is now hosting the programming at the Democratic convention. Goldwyn is most known for his role playing the US president on Shonda Rhimes\u8217\'20\'19 Scandal, opposite Kerry Washington. Washington is also due to make an appearance at the convention.\par \par \uc2 Steve Kerr, head coach of the \uc2 Golden State Warriors\uc2  and coach of the USA men\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team, also earned rapturous applause as he took the stage. Kerr has repeatedly made headlines for speaking his mind on politics. He notably gave an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/may/26/steve-kerr-golden-state-warriors-coach-texas-shootings-gun-control-nba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impassioned speech calling for gun restrictions}}}\uc2  after the massacre in Uvalde claimed the lives of 19 children.\par \par \uc2 In his convention remarks, Kerr said: \u8220\'20\'1CI can see the \u8216\'20\'18shut up and whistle\u8217\'20\'19 tweets fired off as we speak. But I also knew as soon as I was asked that it was too important as an American citizen not to speak up in an election of his magnitude.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 'Lock him up' chants as Hillary Clinton attacks Trump's criminal record\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  drew a stark contrast between Trump and Harris, noting that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Clocked up murderers and drug traffickers\u8221\'20\'1D while Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cfell asleep at his own trial, and when he woke up, he made his own kind of history \u8230\'20\'26 the first person to run for president with 34 felony convictions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The remark prompted loud chants of \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up,\u8221\'20\'1D a throwback to the \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D chants at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rallies when he ran against Clinton in 2016. Clinton initially tried to move on from the chants, but then seemed to smirk a bit as the crowd went wild and continued shouting \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDNC crowd chants "Lock Him Up" after Hillary Clinton mentions \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's 34 felony convictions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aSN4OFBNRr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aSN4OFBNRr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 jordan (@JordanUhl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JordanUhl/status/1825715453689475187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived at the United Center, although he\u8217\'20\'19s not visible in the convention hall.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled to deliver the marquee speech of the evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Clinton kept on with the glass ceiling metaphor, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a barrier falls for one of us, it falls and clears the way for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo for the next 78 days, we need to work harder than we ever had,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to beat back the dangers that Trump and his allies pose to the rule of law and our way of life. Don\u8217\'20\'19t get distracted or complacent. Talk to your friends and neighbors. Volunteer, be proud champions for the truth and for the country that we all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She left the stage not long after, to loud and long applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve heard of the glass ceiling \u8211\'20\'13 the metaphorical barrier that keeps women and minorities from advancing. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has some thoughts about it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn America, you can go as far as your hard work and talent will take you and mean it. And you know what? On the other side of that glass ceiling is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , raising her hand and taking the oath of office as our 47th president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Clinton says Democrats have Trump 'on the run'\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  continued her dressing down of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , accusing him of lowbrow attacks on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn her first day in court, Kamala said five words that still guide her: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for the people. That is something that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will never understand,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, it is no surprise, is it, that he is lying about Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s record. He\u8217\'20\'19s mocking her name and her laugh.\u8221\'20\'1D The latter attack, she quipped, \u8220\'20\'1Csounds familiar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we have him on the run now,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 We had not heard much from the Democrats so far about the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a convicted felon \u8211\'20\'13 until \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  took the stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a prosecutor, Kamala locked up murderers and drug traffickers. She will never rest in defense of our freedom and safety,\u8221\'20\'1D the former secretary of state said. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fell asleep at his own trial, and when he woke up, he made his own kind of history, the first person to run for president with 34 felony convictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Clinton continued by recounting milestones by female politicians in the United States.\par \par \uc2 She talked about the ratification of the 19th amendment, which gave women the right to vote, then said: \u8220\'20\'1CSince that day, every generation has carried the torch forward. In 1972, a fearless Black congresswoman named \uc2 Shirley Chisholm\uc2 . She ran for president and her determination let me and millions of others dream bigger, not just because of who she was, but because of who she fought for, working parents, poor children, the last, the least and the lost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then talked about Geraldine Ferraro, the Democratic vice-presidential nominee in the 1984 election, before turning to herself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then there was 2016, when it was the honor of my life to accept our party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for president and nearly 66 million Americans voted for a future where there are no ceilings on our dreams,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said. Referencing her loss to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , she continued: \u8220\'20\'1CAfterwards, we refused to give up on America. Millions marched. Many ran for office. We kept our eyes on the future. Well, my friends, the future is here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 In a nod to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s place as only the second woman ever nominated for president by a major party in the country\u8217\'20\'19s 248-year history, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CSomething is happening in America. You can feel it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was \u8220\'20\'1Csomething we\u8217\'20\'19ve worked for and dreamed of for a long time\u8221\'20\'1D, Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  takes the stage\par \par \uc2 Up next is \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the former secretary of state who was the first female presidential nominee of a major party, but lost in 2016 to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s wearing a trademark pantsuit, in the color beige. The crowd is very happy that she\u8217\'20\'19s here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans love to mock \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s past as a bartender and waitress, but the congresswoman told the convention that she wished her opponents better understood such work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo love this country is to fight for its people, all people, working people, everyday Americans, like bartenders and factory workers and fast food cashiers who punch a clock and are on their feet all day in some of the toughest jobs out there,\u8221\'20\'1D the congresswoman said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEver since I got elected, Republicans have attacked me by saying that I should go back to bartending. But let me tell you, I\u8217\'20\'19m happy to any day of the week, because there is nothing wrong with working for a living. Imagine, imagine having leaders in the White House who understand that, leaders like Kamala and Tim.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before she left the stage, Ocasio-Cortez noted the importance of Democrats maintaining their majority in the Senate, and retaking control of the House:\par \par \uc2 We cannot send Kamala and Tim to the White House alone together. We must also elect strong democratic majorities in the House and in the Senate, so that we can deliver on an ambitious agenda for the people. Because if you are a working parent trying to afford rent and childcare, Kamala is for you. If you are a senior who had to go back to work because your retirement didn\u8217\'20\'19t stretch far enough. Kamala is for you. If you\u8217\'20\'19re an immigrant family just starting your American story, Kamala is for you.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Convention cheers as Ocasio-Cortez notes Harris's commitment to Gaza ceasefire, release of hostages\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel has been one of the most divisive issues Democrats have confronted over the past four years, sparking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/two-more-us-officials-resign-over-biden-administrations-position-on-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resignations}}}\uc2  from his administration, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/pro-palestinian-protest-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  outside the Democratic convention.\par \par \uc2 As she listed her reason for supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  noted that the vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Cis working tirelessly to secure a ceasefire in Gaza and bring the hostages home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The line generated cheers and applause in the convention hall.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  speaks to Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , the New York congresswoman and progressive celebrity, is speaking now.\par \par \uc2 The crowd began chanting \u8220\'20\'1CAOC! AOC!\u8221\'20\'1D when she came onstage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The biggest surprise of the night so far was \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appearance on the convention stage.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president was expected to attend the convention, but not to speak until Thursday, and the crowd grew rapturous when she came on stage for brief remarks kicking off the four-day gathering of Democratic faithful. Here\u8217\'20\'19s that moment:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Fain whips up Democrats by calling Trump a 'scab'\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain proceeded to lay into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , calling him \u8220\'20\'1Ca scab\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which is someone who crosses a picket line and works during a strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election comes down to one question: which side are you on?\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn one side we have \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  who have stood shoulder to shoulder with the working class. On the other side, we have Trump and Vance, two lap dogs for the billionaire class who only serve themselves. So for us in the labor movement, it\u8217\'20\'19s real simple. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is one of us. She\u8217\'20\'19s a fighter for the working class, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a scab.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And at that, the crowd began chanting: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s a scab! Trump\u8217\'20\'19s a scab!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A little bit later, Fain said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s getting hot in here\u8221\'20\'1D, and then took off his jacket to reveal a red T-shirt that read \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is a scab.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Watch the moment here:\par \par \uc2 enltrShawn Fain at the DNC: In the words of the great American poet Nelly, "It's getting hot in here" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AKLXY9ZZFa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AKLXY9ZZFa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 jordan (@JordanUhl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JordanUhl/status/1825707787919438223?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president Shawn Fain addresses Democrats\par \par \uc2 Now onstage is Shawn Fain, president of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last summer, he led the union in its biggest strike in years, and got \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to join their picket line, something no president had done before.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the union boss whose been seen as a leader of organized labor\u8217\'20\'19s future in the United States:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/who-is-shawn-fain-uaw-strike-union-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The UAW leader fighting to defend autoworkers from \u8216\'20\'18corporate greed\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 The musical guests of the Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 The Democratic national convention has featured two musical performances so far.\par \par \uc2 Mickey Guyton, a country singer, first took to the stage to sing her song, All American. Guyton was the Grammys\u8217\'20\'19 first Black solo female {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2021/mar/12/mickey-guyton-the-grammys-first-black-solo-female-country-nominee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 country nominee}}}\uc2  in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Next up was Jason Isbell, another country singer, who is from Alabama. He sang his song, Something More Than Free. Isbell has become a vocal advocate for Democrats. Asked by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  why many southern, white working class voters like him don\u8217\'20\'19t support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and the Democratic party, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/19/us/politics/jason-isbell-dnc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I think the goals and the intentions of the party were sort of obfuscated by the fact that there was this big PR campaign that sort of made religious morals tie in with a conservative political ideology. And I think that\u8217\'20\'19s kind of where we went wrong, and where a lot of people in the South just started voting against their own interests. And a lot of people like me went along with what their family did, and what their churches did, and became the kind of people who would vote for conservatives no matter what.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 I was on the floor of the Democratic convention when, suddenly, Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 \u8217\'20\'19s Freedom started playing and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  walked in.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the scene:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust watched \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  make her first appearance on the DNC floor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7NAOViEpaK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7NAOViEpaK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ankita Rao (@anrao) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/anrao/status/1825702932102201454?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kept her remarks brief, departing the stage shortly after noting the diversity of the Democratic party faithful gathered in the room.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLooking out at everyone tonight, I see the beauty of our great nation. People from every corner of our country and every walk of life are here united by our shared vision for the future of our country, and this November, we will come together and declare with one voice, as one people, we are moving forward,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith optimism, hope and faith, so guided by our love of country, knowing we all have so much more in common than what separates us, let us fight for the ideals we hold dear, and let us always remember when we fight, we win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris tells convention: 'This is going to be a great week'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is giving some introductory remarks to the crowded convention hall, telling them that tonight, they\u8217\'20\'19ll pay tribute to departing president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to be a great week, and I want to kick us off by celebrating our incredible President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who will be speaking later tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CJoe, thank you for your historic leadership, for your lifetime of service to our nation, and for all you will continue to do, we are forever grateful to you. Thank you, Joe!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris arrives at Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just stepped onstage at the Democratic national convention.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s wearing a light brown suit. The crowd is going wild.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  to tell convention: 'Kamala has the character, experience, and vision to lead us forward'\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the former secretary of state and first female presidential nominee of a major party, will defend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s character in her remarks to the Democratic convention tonight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala has the character, experience, and vision to lead us forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton will say, according to excerpts of her speech.\par \par \uc2 She will tell the convention about the background she shares with Harris as \u8220\'20\'1Cyoung lawyers helping children who were abused or neglected. That kind of work changes you. Those kids stay with you. Kamala carries with her the hopes of every child she protected, every family she helped, every community she served.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo as president, she will always have our backs,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton will say. \u8220\'20\'1CShe will fight to lower costs for hard-working families. Open the doors wide for good paying jobs. And, yes, she will restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clinton lost the 2016 election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who she will reserve some choice words for:\par \par \uc2 Just look at the candidates. Kamala cares about kids, families, and America. Donald only cares about himself.\par \par \uc2 On her first day in court, Kamala said five words that guide her still: \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , for the people.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s something \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will never understand.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  arrives at Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Without much fanfare, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , has arrived at the Democratic national convention:\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor is expected to speak on Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi asked about 'bad blood' with Biden\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , congresswoman and former House speaker, was asked on CNN about any \u8220\'20\'1Cbad blood\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cresentment\u8221\'20\'1D remaining between her and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , surrounding her efforts to get the president to withdraw his candidacy.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Anita Dunn, a former senior White House adviser for Biden, said: \u8220\'20\'1CNobody wants to have a fight with \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D When CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper asked Pelosi to respond to that remark, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes you just have to take a punch for the children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi continued: \u8220\'20\'1CHe made the decision for the country. My concern was not about the president, it was about his campaign. He has seen the exuberance, the excitement that has come forth in our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter Jake Tapper asks about the "residual bad blood" between her and Team Biden, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says: "Sometimes you have to take a punch for the children."\par \par \uc2 She then wonders, "Why are we even talking about it?" prompting Tapper to joke that "they're holding my cat hostage." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VzxH1FuwCB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VzxH1FuwCB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Baragona (@justinbaragona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1825695471580377291?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Austin Davis , lieutenant governor of Pennsylvania, a key battleground state, celebrated the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s achievements on infrastructure:\par \par \uc2 President Trump promised us \u8216\'20\'18infrastructure week\u8217\'20\'19 over and over again. He really didn\u8217\'20\'19t care, though, and it never happened. But President Biden and Vice-President Harris are on our side. They brought together Democrats and Republicans to get it done. We got I-95 in Philly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-06-28/resurrection-of-i-95-in-just-two-weeks-is-dubbed-small-miracle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fixed}}}\uc2  in less than two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The lieutenant governors of Wisconsin and California, and the county judge of Harris county, Texas also just spoke, praising the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s achievements and offering personal stories about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support for their efforts in their states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders: 'Trump is the most dangerous candidate' in US history\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders has offered his take on why the Democratic party rallied around \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  so quickly \u8211\'20\'13 and why he did not seek the presidential nomination himself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what most of us \u8211\'20\'13 and I think most of the American people I hope \u8211\'20\'13 believe is that it\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely imperative that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is defeated,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders, 82, said at a CNN Politico Grill event in Chicago. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is the most dangerous candidate, I think, in the history of this country. I think he lies all of the time in just absolutely preposterous ways so I think there is a consensus that he has to be beaten.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders, who ran for president in both 2016 and 2020, added: \u8220\'20\'1CI am happy right now to be a United States senator. I\u8217\'20\'19m running for election to Vermont \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s keeping me busy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think there was a general consensus that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has done a good job as vice-president, that she would be a strong candidate and the alternative is to open up some kind of wild debate which would fracture the party a little bit is probably not a good idea.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CI think she\u8217\'20\'19s a very strong candidate. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be overly confident but I think she is generating a lot of energy among young people. I think many of them would have voted for Biden but I think they\u8217\'20\'19re more energetic about her candidacy and I look forward to her winning the election. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do everything I can to make that possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders lavished praise on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legislative achievements but offered blunt criticism of the president\u8217\'20\'19s unwavering support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. \u8220\'20\'1COn domestic issues Biden has been the most progressive since FDR. I\u8217\'20\'19ve worked with them in so many ways. On this issue he\u8217\'20\'19s wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if Biden and Harris have differences over Gaza, the senator answered: \u8220\'20\'1CMy honest answer is I don\u8217\'20\'19t know any more than I\u8217\'20\'19ve read.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What does he hope Biden will say on Monday night? \u8220\'20\'1CMy one criticism of the Biden administration is I don\u8217\'20\'19t think they have been as articulate as they should be about their accomplishments. They\u8217\'20\'19ve done a lot more than the average American knows. Maybe he\u8217\'20\'19ll review some of those major accomplishments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Check out footage of a gospel choir\u8217\'20\'19s rendition of the US national anthem, which received a standing ovation at the convention:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  leader says election a choice between 'two economic visions'\par \par \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  trade union federation, said Americans would choose between \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo economic visions\u8221\'20\'1D at the ballot box in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about two economic visions, one where families live paycheck to paycheck, where people have no right to join a union \u8211\'20\'13 a CEO\u8217\'20\'19s dream, but a worker\u8217\'20\'19s nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The other choice is \u8220\'20\'1Can opportunity economy where we lower the costs of groceries, prescriptions and housing; where we go after big pharma, corporate landlords and price gougers; where there\u8217\'20\'19s no such thing as a man\u8217\'20\'19s job or a woman\u8217\'20\'19s job, or like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would say, a Black job, just a good union job,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the future our president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has fought for, and that\u8217\'20\'19s the future \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will keep fighting for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some photos from inside the United Center in Chicago as the first night of the Democratic national convention got under way:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 The pool reporter traveling with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reports that she has arrived at the United Center.\par \par \uc2 We have not laid eyes on her yet, and she is not expected to speak tonight. We expect her to enter the convention hall at some point and watch the speakers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The convention just heard from \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s long-serving Democratic senator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is like a bad boss,\u8221\'20\'1D Durbin said. Then he explained:\par \par \uc2 You want time off to take care of your sick parents? Ask \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 denied. In \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s America, there is no paid family leave. Want to have a child, but need IVF, too bad, that\u8217\'20\'19s shut down. You want a pay raise? Too bad, the boss just gave himself one so there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing left for you. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reminds us of a boss we all had, the guy who thinks he\u8217\'20\'19s a very stable genius but is driving the company into the ground.\par \par \uc2 Now, get this. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did make history. Let\u8217\'20\'19s give him credit. He is one of only two presidents in the history of the United States to leave office with fewer Americans working than when he started. Now he wants a chance to make America unemployed again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 On stage now are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iamals.org/stories/sandra-abrevaya-and-brian-wallach/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sandra Abrevaya and her husband, Brian Wallach}}}\uc2 , who suffers from ALS.\par \par \uc2 Wallach cannot speak, but Abrevaya is talking about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to help people suffering from the neurodegenerative disease.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBrian and I are still driven by hope and by faith in what we can do collectively, and that includes the power of our vote. This November, we are voting for our future,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 At their convention last month, the GOP didn\u8217\'20\'19t talk much about the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 But the Democrats clearly see political advantage in doing so, with California congressman Robert Garcia hitting out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his handling of the virus, in a speech to the convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike many of you, I watched in terror and horror as the Covid pandemic consumed our lives. As mayor, I fought for more hospital beds, for more tests and to make masks more accessible. What we needed at that moment was national leadership, but instead, we got \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Garcia, who was mayor of Long Beach, California, when the virus broke out.\par \par \uc2 Like Flanagan, he noted how the virus had affected his own family:\par \par \uc2 While schools closed and dead bodies filled morgues, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  downplayed the virus. He told us to inject bleach into our bodies. He peddled conspiracy theories across the country. We lost hundreds of thousands of Americans, and our economy collapsed.\par \par \uc2 Now, that summer of 2020 my mom and my stepfather both died of the Covid pandemic, and I miss them every single day. So when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Maga extremists like \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  downplay the horror of the pandemic, it should make us all furious.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Peggy Flanagan , the lieutenant-governor of Minnesota who just spoke at the Democratic convention , is on track to make history if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins.\par \par \uc2 Flanagan, who told the convention about being a member of the White Earth Band of Ojibwe, will take over as governor of Minnesota, if \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the current governor, steps down to serve as vice-president. That would make Flanagan the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/peggy-flanagan-minnesota-indigenous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Indigenous woman to serve as a US governor}}}\uc2  and also be the first female governor in the state\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 She is already the highest-ranking Indigenous woman in a state-level executive office. And, if Flanagan becomes governor, Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s senate president, Bobby Joe Champion, would become the state\u8217\'20\'19s first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/heres-what-would-happen-in-minnesota-if-gov-tim-walz-were-to-become-vice-president/600385291"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black lieutenant governor}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democratic convention speakers have been emphasizing the importance of diversity in the party, a sharp contrast to the Republican convention. More on Flanagan here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/peggy-flanagan-minnesota-indigenous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peggy Flanagan in line to be first US female Indigenous governor if Harris and Walz win}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t shying away from discussing the Covid-19 pandemic, with Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor Peggy Flanagan taking the stage to talk about the tragedy the virus brought upon her family, and how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was to blame.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy brother Ron was the second person to die of Covid in the state of Tennessee. We couldn\u8217\'20\'19t see him. We couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have a memorial. And millions of American families went through the same thing. Our communities were suffering, our economy was struggling, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was playing games. Our country was brought to the brink by his failure to respond, but the Biden-Harris administration stepped in with quick and decisive action,\u8221\'20\'1D Flanagan said.\par \par \uc2 Then a video played showing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements about the coronavirus. The convention heard him say \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have it totally under control\u8221\'20\'1D and that it will go away when the weather gets warm. \u8220\'20\'1CThe risk to the American people remains very low \u8230\'20\'26 this the same as the flu. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to disappear one day,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said in the video.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 This appears to be the outer perimeter that protesters knocked over earlier today:\par \par \uc2 As the Chicago police noted, they did not get through the inner perimeter around the United Center, where the convention is taking place.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Chicago police say demonstrators breached one layer of convention security, but 'no threat' to attendees\par \par \uc2 Protesters outside the Democratic national convention breached the outer security perimeter, but made it no further, the Chicago police said, adding that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno threat\u8221\'20\'1D to those attending the gathering:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t0SnSCK0r7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/t0SnSCK0r7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chicago Police Communications & News Affairs (@CPD_Media) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CPD_Media/status/1825668692522446927?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Taking care of party business is one of the functions of conventions, and the Democrats are no exception.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now hearing from Leah Daughtry, the co-chair of the convention\u8217\'20\'19s rules committee, who is asking the convention to support a resolution regarding automatic delegates. The delegates loudly approved it, by a voice vote.\par \par \uc2 The other co-chair of the rules committee is Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  who is, as Daughtry put it, \u8220\'20\'1Ca little occupied this evening\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 After a video that credited his 1984 presidential run with paving the way for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  to become the first Black president 24 years later, civil rights leader \uc2 Jesse Jackson\uc2  has come onstage.\par \par \uc2 He is in a wheelchair and waved at the crowd, without speaking. He is now being wheeled away by a group that includes \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2 , again waving at the crowd as he goes.\par \par \uc2 Jackson in 2017 announced a diagnosis of Parkinson\u8217\'20\'19s Ddisease, and last year retired as head of the Rainbow Push Coalition civil rights group, which is based in Chicago:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/15/jesse-jackson-steps-down-as-head-of-civil-rights-organisation-rainbow-push-coalition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jesse Jackson to step down as head of civil rights organisation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2  , the leader of the \uc2 National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP)\uc2  civil rights group, opened his remarks with a veiled swipe at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood evening. I\u8217\'20\'19m \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m here to do my Black job,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson began to laughs.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D? The remark is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/trump-racism-black-republicans-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several instances}}}\uc2  of Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/aug/02/simone-biles-trump-black-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepping in it}}}\uc2  in his attempts to win the support of African American voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  opens first night of Democratic convention\par \par \uc2 Democratic chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  has officially kicked off the opening night of the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHope and hard work can take you anywhere,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harrison. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the America Democrats believe in, and that\u8217\'20\'19s the America Democrats are fighting for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least two people arrested at protest against Israel-Gaza war\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s George Chidi, who is reporting from Chicago, writes there was a standoff between demonstrators and the police:\par \par \uc2 At least two people have been arrested in a fenced area between a park and the United Center, as protesters began disabling fences in the narrow gap.\par \par \uc2 Riot police lined up and marched protesters together, driving them back through a gap created in the fence. As police repaired one hole in the fence, masked protesters unlatched holes in other parts.\par \par \uc2 The standoff diminished into a quiet vigil around 5.20 CT, with about 200 people on one side of the fence and equal numbers of cops on the other.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outside of the convention, thousands of protest ers have been demonstrating against the US support for Israel amid the bombardment of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of protesters had broken through a fence set up by police near the United Center, where the convention is being held, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to play our part in the belly of the beast to stop the genocide, to end US aid to Israel and stand with Palestine,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hatem Abudayyeh, a spokesperson for the Coalition to March on the DNC, told the AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe and Jill Biden, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  to headline Democratic convention's opening night\par \par \uc2 Hello, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as we cover the first night of the Democratic national convention in Chicago. Just a few weeks ago, we were expecting the four-day event to be all about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his campaign for a second term, but everything changed after the president bowed out of the race and allowed his vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to take over as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee. Now in the final months of both his presidency and his more than 50-year career in politics, Biden remains an important figure among Democrats, and will give the keynote speech at the convention this evening.\par \par \uc2 Before Biden takes the stage ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/bidens-dnc-speech-time-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting at about 10pm CT}}}\uc2  ), we\u8217\'20\'19ll hear from first lady Jill Biden, and luminaries from across the party\u8217\'20\'19s ideological spectrum, including \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s first female nominee for president, and \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , the New York congresswoman and progressive icon.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/18/dnc-when-where-speakers-guide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convention kicked off at 5.15pm CT}}}\uc2  amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/pro-palestinian-protest-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests near the convention center against the war in Gaza}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching out for this evening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s theme is \u8220\'20\'1CFor the People\u8221\'20\'1D, and is intended to showcase how Democrats are, well, \u8220\'20\'1Cfighting for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the convention\u8217\'20\'19s organizing committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is expected to appear this evening, as is her running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . But do not expect either to speak \u8211\'20\'13 Harris will deliver the final address of the convention on Thursday, and Walz will speak to the crowd on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz have both already been formally nominated by the party, but the convention will nonetheless hold a ceremonial nomination of the Minnesota governor this evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speakers this evening will run the gamut, from members of Congress to state leaders, including longtime South Carolina representative and Biden confidante James Clyburn, New York governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  and progressive Texas congresswoman Jasmine Crockett.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Organized labor will be well-represented this evening, with joint remarks from six labor groups scheduled, as well as an address from \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president Shawn Fain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240819ek8j0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
