\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t just vote\u8217\'20\'19: protesters gather in Chicago for Gaza and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights before Democratic convention\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi in Chicago \par \uc2 602 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2024\par 12:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  prepares to be formally nominated, organizers are expecting widespread protests at the Democratic national convention in Chicago\par \par \uc2 As thousands of Democratic delegates, party officials and elected leaders descend on Chicago for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/18/democratic-national-convention-chicago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic National Convention (DNC)}}}\uc2  a smaller, strident group of protesters have taken to Michigan Avenue ahead of a week that promises several demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 A protest of up to 1,000 marchers combining support for the Palestinian cause and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights gathered at the iconic corner of Wacker Drive and Michigan Avenue in Chicago Sunday evening. The protest is the first of several demonstrations, legally permitted and not, planned for the convention.\par \par \uc2 Some protesters at the march, organized by groups like Bodies Against Unjust Laws, have come explicitly to \u8220\'20\'1CDisrupt the DNC\u8221\'20\'1D, arguing that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/dnc-pro-gaza-palestine-protests-uncommitted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American support for Israel in the Gaza war was tantamount to genocide}}}\uc2  and that the Democratic party was indistinguishable from Republicans and equally unworthy of political support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rhetoric that comes out of the mouths of politicians \u8211\'20\'13 and I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that some of it isn\u8217\'20\'19t sincere in the wish to defend reproductive justice, or for trans and queer people, or even for citizens on the ground in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 but rhetoric does not stop the bombs from falling,\u8221\'20\'1D says Linda Loew, a protest leader.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRhetoric does not deliver \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from someone in a state that has a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. What we need is action. We need the end to funding to Israel and the end of delivery of weapons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It didn\u8217\'20\'19t matter to some of these protesters if the nominee was Joe Biden or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no indication that there is much of a difference at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D says Megan Behrent, a college professor in New York, about Biden and Harris, and said she would vote third party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just kind of expect that in the lead up to this kind of election, the kind of focus on the lesser evil always starts dominating politics,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd for good reason. Trump is, you know, a nightmare. But for me, the most important thing is to maintain an independent kind of organizing voice, to continue to raise the issues that matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Andy Thayer, a notable Chicago activist, speaking for Bodies Outside of Unjust Laws and the Coalition for Reproductive Justice, says: \u8220\'20\'1CWe applied for the permit on the first legal day we could, January 2, and the city delayed us for the next eight-plus months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ronnie Mosley, Chicago city alderman was walking along the outskirts of the protest with police officers. He described this protest as an act of free speech, and something the city can handle.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, protesters interspersed calls to free Palestine with \u8220\'20\'1CIntifada, intifada\u8221\'20\'1D, which translates to uprising or rebellion. Intifada was also the name given to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/09/why-israel-palestine-conflict-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 series of deadly outbreaks}}}\uc2  of violence in Israel and the occupied territories in the 1980s and 2000s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the audience [for the protest] is the entire population of American people. I think that those who want to vote in the election should absolutely vote. We fought hard for that right, and we do not want to see that taken away,\u8221\'20\'1D Loews says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we can\u8217\'20\'19t just vote. We have never been able to rely on a single politician of either party to deliver our rights, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s been civil rights or removal of US forces from unpopular wars or the right to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240819ek8j00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
