\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Walz to grill Vance on Project 2025 in first vice-presidential debate\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Tait in Washington \par \uc2 817 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2024\par 22:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic VP nominee pushes back against his rival\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments as they agree to 1 October debate\par \par \uc2 In a possible early preview of their debate in October, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential nominee, has pushed back against an attempt by his Republican rival, JD Vance, to imply that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a \u8220\'20\'1Cnormal\u8221\'20\'1D concern for women voters.\par \par \uc2 Vance was asked by Laura Ingraham on Fox News how he would respond to suburban women who feared a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. \u8220\'20\'1CFirst of all, I don\u8217\'20\'19t buy that Laura,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied. \u8220\'20\'1CI think most suburban women care about the normal things most Americans care about right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz posted the segment on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Tim_Walz/status/1823870234979094530"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pretty normal to respect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make her own damn health care decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz, the governor of Minnesota, and Vance, a senator from Ohio, have both accepted an invitation by \uc2 CBS\uc2  to take part in a one on one televised debate on 1 October.\par \par \uc2 Walz has vowed to use the debate to push Vance on his links to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the controversial rightwing blueprint to overhaul the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSee you on October 1, JD,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz wrote on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Tim_Walz/status/1823824781873176770"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bullish post on X}}}\uc2  after the network issued the invitations.\par \par \uc2 In a later email to fundraisers, Walz signalled his intentions to confront Vance about his connections to Kevin Roberts, the president of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  thinktank that has drawn up Project 2025. The 922-page document foresees \u8211\'20\'13 among other things \u8211\'20\'13 sacking 50,000 civil servants and closing agencies like the Department of Education in the event of a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance shares \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dangerous and backward agenda for this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz wrote in the email. \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, I just agreed to debate JD Vance on October 1. Boy, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got to tell you, I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to debate the guy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHeck, he even wrote the foreword for the architect of the Project 2025 agenda. I am going to do my best to make sure everyone watching our debate knows just that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The latter comment referred to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s penned forward for Roberts\u8217\'20\'19 forthcoming book Dawn\u8217\'20\'19s Early Light, in which the GOP nominee lavishes praise on both Roberts and the thinktank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNever before has a figure with Roberts\u8217\'20\'19s depth and stature within the American Right tried to articulate a genuinely new future for conservatism,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance writes. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t some random outpost on Capitol Hill; it is and has been the most influential engine of ideas for Republicans from \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s foreword has undermined earlier attempts by Trump to disavow links to Project 2025, which also recommends an expansion of presidential powers, an aggressive offensive against \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D ideology and a ban on sales of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 Trump has tried to neutralise Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to draw attention to the project by claiming that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/08/trump-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he did not know the people involved}}}\uc2  and disagreed with its contents.\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also show his intent to put the focus on Vance\u8217\'20\'19s views on that issue. The Republican has previously spoken in favour of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban but has accepted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stricture that the matter should be left to individual states, following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2022 ruling overturning Roe v Wade, the 50-year-old court judgement that guaranteed a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vance has yet to formally accept \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invitation and \u8211\'20\'13 in contrast to Walz\u8217\'20\'19s gung ho approach \u8211\'20\'13 appeared skittish about the prospect in his interview with Ingraham, in which he tried to set out conditions and said he wanted to avoid \u8220\'20\'1Ca fake new garbage debate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just heard about this thing three hours ago so we\u8217\'20\'19re going to talk to them and figure out when we can debate,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to look at the moderators, talk about the rules a little bit. I strongly suspect we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be there on October 1, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to do one of these fake debates where they don\u8217\'20\'19t actually have an audience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to do a real debate, and if \uc2 CBS\uc2  agrees to it, then certainly we\u8217\'20\'19ll do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance said on 7 August that he would debate Harris \u8211\'20\'13 now the Democratic presidential nominee but previously the vice-presidential candidate when Joe Biden was at the top of the ticket \u8211\'20\'13 but refused to commit to debating Walz because he was not certain that the Democratic ticket had been finalised.\par \par \uc2 In fact, Harris and Walz had been officially certified as the Democratic nominees the previous day after a virtual roll call of delegates to next week\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democratic-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national party convention}}}\uc2 , which takes places in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240815ek8f002h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
