\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona court rules voter pamphlet can refer to fetus as \u8216\'20\'18unborn human being\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman and agency \par \uc2 533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par 21:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling on language in document comes as voters to decide in November whether to add right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to state constitution\par \par \uc2 An official informational pamphlet for Arizona voters who will decide in the fall whether to guarantee a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can refer to a fetus as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn human being\u8221\'20\'1D, the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court ruled on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters will get to decide in November whether to add the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The proposed amendment would allow abortions until a fetus could survive outside the womb, typically around 24 weeks, with exceptions to save the pregnant individual\u8217\'20\'19s life or to protect her physical or mental health. It would restrict the state from adopting or enforcing any law that would prohibit access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The justices of the Arizona supreme court, in Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision, sided with Republican lawmakers over proponents of the ballot measure on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 But Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling drew swift criticism from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates who had argued that the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn human being\u8221\'20\'1D is neither impartial nor objective. They also said they were concerned that Arizonans would be subjected to biased and politically charged words.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply disappointed in this ruling, but will not be deterred from doing everything in our power to communicate to voters the truth of the Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Act and why it\u8217\'20\'19s critical to vote yes to restore and protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care this fall,\u8221\'20\'1D the group, Arizona for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The pamphlet, a voter guide produced by the office of the Arizona secretary of state, gives voters information on candidates and ballot measures to help inform their choices. It was unclear, however, whether any specific language contained in the pamphlet would appear on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/13/arizona-abortion-november-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Monday}}}\uc2  that it had certified 577,971 signatures \u8211\'20\'13 far above the required number that the coalition supporting the ballot measure had to submit in order to put the question before voters.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a central message since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 and it is a key part of their efforts in this year\u8217\'20\'19s elections. Arizona is a major battleground state in the presidential election, and Democrats are hoping that enthusiasm for the ballot measure will translate to increased turnout among their base.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the Arizona supreme court ruled to let a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that dated back to 1864 take effect in the state \u8211\'20\'13 a move that unleashed national outrage and ultimately led a handful of Republican state legislators to join Democrats in voting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeal the 1864 ban}}}\uc2 . Arizona currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Seven other states are also set to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures this year, including Nevada, another battleground state. In the two years since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, GOP stronghold states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  and Kansas have all voted to pass ballot measures that preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240814ek8e003h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
