\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  appears at California fundraiser after defending military service \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Chris Stein and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 8,703 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par 00:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed. You can find our latest US politics coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find our latest US politics coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Walz speaks to donors at fundraising event in Newport\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has wrapped up his 30 minute appearance at an event in Newport that donors paid between $1000 and 100,000 to attend.\par \par \uc2 The Orange Country register reports that his speech was \u8220\'20\'1Cpeppered with Midwest jokes and self-deprecating quips\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here is the local news outlet\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ocregister.com/2024/08/13/gov-tim-walz-vp-kamala-harris-running-mate-introduces-himself-to-donors-in-newport-beach/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Standing before a large ballroom at the Balboa Bay Resort, a waterfront hotel in Newport Beach, Walz ran through his resume: governor, congressman, educator, coach \u8212\'20\'14 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won the damn state championship,\u8221\'20\'1D he reminded a cheering audience. He ran through his platform \u8212\'20\'14 supporting gun ownership when balanced with certain regulations, paid family leave and clean air regulations.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They keep talking about these are radical things, and I\u8217\'20\'19m like, go ahead and label me whatever you want because I\u8217\'20\'19ll damn sure guarantee you 80% of people in Minnesota and across the country want those things,\u8217\'20\'19 said Walz to applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You know better than anybody in this state what we\u8217\'20\'19ve got in the vice president,\u8217\'20\'19 Walz said. \u8216\'20\'18She\u8217\'20\'19s found her voice.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 One of the fundraiser\u8217\'20\'19s hosts, attorney Wylie Aitken, said he had never seen so much enthusiasm in all the years he\u8217\'20\'19d been doing this:\par \par \uc2 '\u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s amazing that when everybody was kind of down and out and feeling, legitimately, concern with Biden, etc., then suddenly to have this reversal and to see this incredible enthusiasm that\u8217\'20\'19s energised everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be on ballot in at least eight states in November\par \par \uc2 Missouri voters will decide in November whether to guarantee a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a constitutional amendment that would reverse the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Missouri has become the eighth state to have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot in November.\par \par \uc2 The secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office certified Tuesday that an initiative petition received more than enough signatures from registered voters to qualify for the general election. It will need approval from a majority of voters to become enshrined in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Missouri will join at least seven states voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights during the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state certified an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights measure for the ballot on Monday. Measures also will go before voters in Colorado, Florida, Maryland, Nevada and South Dakota.\par \par \uc2 While not explicitly addressing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a New York ballot measure would bar discrimination based on \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D among other things.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz are planning to hold a rally in Milwaukee while the DNC is happening in Chicago next week, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports \u8211\'20\'13 in the venue where Trump accepted the Republican nomination last month.\par \par \uc2 The rally is planned for Tuesday, according to the report, which cites four people briefed on the discussions.\par \par \uc2 The Fiserv Forum, where the rally will reportedly take place, is 80 miles, or 128km, from the United Center in Chicago, where the DNC is taking place all week.\par \par \uc2 The move is not unusual, but is interesting because it will serve as a direct comparison of crowd size and energy to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s event. Trump has claimed, falsely, that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s crowd sizes are fake.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s military incursion into Russia has \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated a real dilemma\u8221\'20\'1D for Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . He added that US officials are in constant touch with the Ukrainians about the move.\par \par \uc2 About 1,000 Ukrainian troops rammed through the Russian border in the early hours of 6 August, with tanks and armoured vehicles, Reuters reports. A US official said late on Tuesday that the goal of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Kursk incursion appears to be to force Russia to pull troops out of Ukraine to defend Russian territory against the cross-border assault.\par \par \uc2 Answering questions from reporters upon arrival in New Orleans, Biden said he has been briefed every four to five hours for the last six to eight days on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s creating a real dilemma for Putin,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his first substantive comments about the operation, which appeared to have caught the Russians off guard.\par \par \uc2 The US has provided billions of dollars of weaponry to Ukraine intended largely for defensive purposes, as Ukraine tries to repel the Russian invasion launched in February 2022.\par \par \uc2 In May, Biden authorised Kyiv to launch US-supplied weapons at military targets inside Russia that are supporting an offensive against the northeastern Ukrainian city of Kharkiv.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Ukraine did not provide advance notice of its incursion, which took place in the Kursk region of Russia. Russian forces on Tuesday struck back at Ukrainian troops with missiles, drones and airstrikes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 As we await news of Walz\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at a fundraiser in California, here is AP\u8217\'20\'19s look at his first solo appearance since being named the Democratic vice presidential nominee last week:\par \par \uc2 Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  warned cheering union members Tuesday that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would wage war on working people while threatening Medicare and Social Security as he kicked off a five-state fundraising swing.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in a cavernous, dimly lit ballroom to thousands of members of the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 , Walz said he and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  want to spread collective bargaining and other worker protections to \u8220\'20\'1Cevery state in the union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen unions are strong, America is strong,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz, a former school teacher and union member, said.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic campaign chose to kick off Walz\u8217\'20\'19s national swing on the safest of political terrain \u8212\'20\'14 heavily Democratic California, home to Vice President Harris and where registered Democrats outnumber Republicans about 2-1.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though Harris is gaining ground in the polls, Trump is still more popular than he was at this point in 2016 or 2020:\par \par \uc2 enltrPoint 2 has been overlooked for a year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uQpsRi38iS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uQpsRi38iS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1823460141175288233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  due to appear at California fundraiser\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is scheduled to appear at a fundraiser in Newport Beach, California this afternoon. On Wednesday, he will address fundraisers in Denver and Boston, and then wrap up his trip on Thursday in Newport, Rhode Island, and Southampton, New York.\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s focus on fundraising this week comes after he stormed through a series of battleground states with Harris last week to introduce himself to voters nationally. The two held rallies in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Michigan, Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 His speeches so far have been built around key themes for Democrats in 2024: support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, lifting the middle class and characterizing Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 an attack line Walz has been credited with authoring.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic voter registration surges since Biden drops out - report says\par \par \uc2 Democratic voter registration has surged following Biden dropping out \u8211\'20\'13 and Harris stepping in, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 This follows an almost year-long trend of more people registering as Republicans than Democrats in the battleground states of Pennsylvania and North Carolina, including a spike after the Trump assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 But after Biden dropped out, weekly Democratic registrations outnumbered Republican nominations in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania saw the largest Democratic margin for new registrations since late last year.\par \par \uc2 The paper\u8217\'20\'19s chief political analyst, Nate Cohn, points out that the Democrats nonetheless still need to catch up:\par \par \uc2 enltrA bit of a shift in new voter registration in PA/NC since Biden dropped out, though Democrats still have a big deficit to makeup here - from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/fparises?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @fparises}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QArpHqRIEo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QArpHqRIEo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nate Cohn (@Nate_Cohn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nate_Cohn/status/1823480787834167348?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 AP has important apostrophe news:\par \par \uc2 Whatever possessed Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to pick Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate, it probably wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a desire to inflame arguments about apostrophes. But it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take much to get grammar nerds fired up. They\u8217\'20\'19re all over social media debating rules for possessive proper names ending in S. Some agree with The Associated Press, which says just add an apostrophe to Harris to make it possessive. Others agree with \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and other outlets that add an apostrophe S. Timothy Pulju, a senior lecturer in linguistics at \uc2 Dartmouth College\uc2 , says the AP guidance reflects how English was spoken and written centuries ago but a shift is underway. For now, he says both are acceptable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lower the stakes, the bigger the fight,\u8221\'20\'1D Ron Woloshun, a creative director and digital marketer in California told AP.\par \par \uc2 enltrIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t agree on these rules right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a very long eight years:\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s do an S after the apostrophe after Harris, and an S after the apostrophe after Walz.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris\u8217\'20\'19s pick vindicates Walz\u8217\'20\'19s message.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I will not be taking further questions at this time.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The.Ink, from Anand Giridharadas (@AnandWrites) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnandWrites/status/1820836299848196167?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The resident punctuation guru on my desk, Warren Murray, has this rule: you use apostrophe and -s when that is the way you say it. Otherwise, it is an apostrophe. So it is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s, and Walz\u8217\'20\'19s. (At my Anglican high school the rule was that only Jesus got an apostrophe -s).\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s style guide says: The possessive in words and names ending in S normally takes an apostrophe followed by a second S (Jones\u8217\'20\'19s, James\u8217\'20\'19s), but be guided by pronunciation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s Minnesota Democratic primary is the last in a series of heated primaries for the progressive \u8220\'20\'1CSquad\u8221\'20\'1D of House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  who have been vocal in their criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. Fellow Squad members \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  of New York and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  of Missouri were recently defeated by candidates supported by a deluge of pro-Israel spending. But Omar faces a lower-key race.\par \par \uc2 The two-term congresswoman became the first woman of color to represent Minnesota in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  in 2019. While in office, she has allied herself with the left wing of the Democratic party, serving as the deputy chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus and backing key progressive measures such as the Green New Deal and Medicare for All.\par \par \uc2 Even before the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ensuing offensive, Omar had established herself as a vocal critic of Israel. She memorably drew criticism in 2019 for quipping that US politicians\u8217\'20\'19 support for Israel was \u8220\'20\'1Call about the Benjamins\u8221\'20\'1D, in reference to donations from the American Israel Political Affairs Committee (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ). The comment drew accusations of antisemitism and she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/03/07/700901834/minnesota-congresswoman-ignites-debate-on-israel-and-anti-semitism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later apologized}}}\uc2  for it.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the 7 October attacks, and as Israel escalated its retaliatory war, Omar was among the first in Congress to call for a ceasefire. She has spoken out in support of the university encampments in solidarity with Gaza. Her daughter was suspended from Barnard College for taking part.\par \par \uc2 These together would seem to make Omar a natural target of pro-Israel groups, but Samuels, a former Minneapolis city councilman has not drawn support from \uc2 Aipac\uc2  or its affiliated Super Pac, United Democracy Project. In contrast, UDP dropped more than $20m to unseat Bowman and Bush.\par \par \uc2 The lobby groups have not said why they have not gotten involved in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2  primary \u8211\'20\'13 but it is possible that Omar just did not provide them the fodder.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/ilhan-omar-minnesota-primary-rematch-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ilhan Omar is latest \u8216\'20\'18Squad\u8217\'20\'19 member to face House primary challenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US politics coverage. Coming up today, we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to speak at a Harris-Walz campaign reception in Newport Beach, California.\par \par \uc2 And Representative \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  of Minnesota is defending her seat in the state Democratic primary, a rematch against Don Samuels that comes two years after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/ilhan-omar-minnesota-primary-victory-progressives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barely eked out a victory}}}\uc2  against him. Polls close at 8pm Minnesota time \u8211\'20\'13 in about three hours.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll take you through the latest \u8211\'20\'13 stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The evening so far\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is basking in the afterglow of the interview he conducted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last night. The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb6ed28f08cf3dfc945d47#block-66bb6ed28f08cf3dfc945d47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  their conversation had attracted 1bn views and comments, a number that was impossible to verify, while adding he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb69fb8f08cf3dfc945cf5#block-66bb69fb8f08cf3dfc945cf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be willing}}}\uc2  to hold a similar event with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . But a remark the ex-president made during the interview about firing employees who strike has spurred the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca#block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file a federal labor law complaint}}}\uc2  against both Trump and Musk, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb4c618f080fad90fdc8a0#block-66bb4c618f080fad90fdc8a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  last night\u8217\'20\'19s event as a chat between \u8220\'20\'1Cself-obsessed rich guys who will sell out the middle class and who cannot run a live stream in the year 2024\u8221\'20\'1D. The campaign also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bbc1178f08e4bf5d12c4c3#block-66bbc1178f08e4bf5d12c4c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went public}}}\uc2  with news that it had received warning from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  of foreign hackers trying to breach its systems, but does not think they have been successful.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor who is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, made his first solo campaign appearance at a union convention, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bbc5218f08e4bf5d12c4dc#block-66bbc5218f08e4bf5d12c4dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  his military service.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has no public events scheduled today, but her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb86678f08cf3dfc945ebc#block-66bb86678f08cf3dfc945ebc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to face}}}\uc2  questions over why the vice-president hasn\u8217\'20\'19t held a press conference or granted a sit-down interview since announcing her bid for the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Musk has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb81748f08e4bf5d12c214#block-66bb81748f08e4bf5d12c214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a long history}}}\uc2  of opposing unions, including at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , where the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has been trying to encourage workers to organize.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has been flying around to campaign events in a plane once owned by \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb79178f081edd5aa0ed58#block-66bb79178f081edd5aa0ed58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, the progressive senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bbaa538f081edd5aa0efd3#block-66bbaa538f081edd5aa0efd3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Claying the groundwork\u8221\'20\'1D to dispute the November election, if he loses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bbb4938f08cf3dfc9460dd#block-66bbb4938f08cf3dfc9460dd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the further annals}}}\uc2  of Republicans who broke with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returning to the fold, former North Carolina senator \uc2 Richard Burr\uc2  said he will vote for the ex-president in November.\par \par \uc2 Burr, who declined to seek re-election and left the Senate in 2022, was one of seven Republicans who voted to convict Trump after he was impeached by the House of Representatives in response to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The conviction ultimately failed to receive the necessary two-thirds majority in the Senate required to be approved, and North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s GOP censured Burr for his vote.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumlocalnews.com/nc/triangle-sandhills/news/2024/08/13/richard-burr-trump-impeachment?cid=share_twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Spectrum News}}}\uc2 , Burr said:\par \par \uc2 Maybe someone will have a hard time squaring with it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a hard time squaring with it because I firmly understood why I voted for impeachment. And like I said, that\u8217\'20\'19s not a disqualifier as to whether you can serve. It\u8217\'20\'19s a bad choice I thought a president made one time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is facing accusations of racism over this post on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X earlier today:\par \par \uc2 enltrImport the third world\par \par \uc2 Become the third world {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MVawiHQSpm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MVawiHQSpm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1823379465914741234?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It appears to be in line with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s messaging around undocumented people, who he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/trump-rally-georgia-crime-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has baselessly blamed}}}\uc2  for causing crime, and sparked a wave of condemnation from users of X:\par \par \uc2 enltrRacist motherfucking weirdos\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Keith Olbermann (@KeithOlbermann) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KeithOlbermann/status/1823444305018499273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWell, at least you aren't hiding it behind dog whistles any more.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bricki ?????? (@ohbricki) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ohbricki/status/1823400910296424685?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrracist bullshit\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tab - A Lot of Shark (@Tejana_Tab) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tejana_Tab/status/1823387303995424990?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is set to become one of the most prominent Democrats in the country \u8211\'20\'13 at least for the next three months, as he campaigns alongside \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at his record in Minnesota, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  must be having the wildest month of his life.\par \par \uc2 After the Minnesota governor was announced as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for running mate, the progressive congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and independent senator Joe Manchin both put out statements praising him, an indication of his appeal across Democratic constituencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDems in disconcerting levels of array,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AOC/status/1820846151920230812"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joked on X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the week since his name catapulted from relative obscurity \u8211\'20\'13 Walz flew up the shortlist of second-in-command possibles in a matter of two weeks, buoyed by clips of his TV appearances and memes about his dadliness \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/kamala-harris-tim-walz-merch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 camo caps}}}\uc2  with orange writing have flown off the campaign merch shelves, a nod to Walz\u8217\'20\'19s dressed-down midwestern attire.\par \par \uc2 But beyond the appearances, his record in politics shows an evolution \u8211\'20\'13 a shift from a moderate Democrat winning over a Republican-leaning district to a governor who delivered a laundry list of progressive policy wins that has his critics fuming.\par \par \uc2 Is he a progressive darling? Is he a moderate in progressive clothing? A centrist? Is this a bait-and-switch?\par \par \uc2 Well, he\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When you talk to people who know Walz, they all call him real, genuine, authentic, an everyman. There\u8217\'20\'19s no reason to believe he\u8217\'20\'19s putting on an act.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/11/tim-walz-evolution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The evolution of Tim Walz: from high school teacher to VP nominee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz defends military service in first solo campaign appearance\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the Harris campaign, the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s newly minted running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , today made his first solo campaign appearance at a convention of union members.\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor gave a wide-ranging speech in which he attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and cheered the power of organized labor, while also taking time to respond to attacks from the former president and his supporters, who say Walz has exaggerated his military service.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he said in response, at the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual convention:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I am damn proud of my service to this country. And I firmly believe you should never denigrate another person's service record."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Amid GOP attacks, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  defends the timing of his decision to retire from the National Guard in 2005 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zEXTt2cXLA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zEXTt2cXLA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1823450756004901203?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The attacks on Walz\u8217\'20\'19s military service, from Trump allies including his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , have centered on the timing of his decision to retire after 24 years of army national guard service. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/tim-walz-jd-vance-military-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance attacks Tim Walz\u8217\'20\'19s military record as election race heats up}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign says \uc2 FBI\uc2  warned of foreign hacking, but systems were not breached\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said it has received a warning from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that it had been targeted by foreign hackers, but they have not detected any breaches of their systems.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn July, the campaign legal and security teams were notified by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that we were targeted by a foreign actor influence operation. We have robust cybersecurity measures in place, and are not aware of any security breaches of our systems resulting from those efforts. We remain in communication with appropriate law enforcement authorities,\u8221\'20\'1D a campaign official said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said it was investigating a leak of documents from the Trump campaign that is being blamed on hackers tied to Iran. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-hacking-documents-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI investigating Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s complaint it was hacked by Iran}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Arizona received some good news yesterday, when the secretary of state approved a ballot measure that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports. The party hopes the initiative will bring out voters who will also cast ballots for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in a state that could prove decisive to her hopes to winning the White House:\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters will decide this November whether to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their state constitution, a prospect that could turbocharge voter turnout in a critical battleground state in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the Arizona secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office announced that it had validated an estimated 577,971 signatures in support of a ballot measure, the Arizona For {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  Access Act, to establish a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 On X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderTabet/status/1823170565961871540"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the office called}}}\uc2  the measure \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest petition effort in Arizona history\u8221\'20\'1D. The measure will be listed on the ballot as Proposition 139.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is not the only state to face the prospect of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure this November. So far, states including Colorado, Florida and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 another key battleground state \u8211\'20\'13 are also set to hold similar ballot measures. Tuesday also marks the deadline for the state of Missouri to determine whether to add its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measure to its ballots.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, ballot measures that protect or preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have successfully passed even in red states such as Ohio, Kansas and Kentucky. However, they have never been tested during a presidential election. Democrats are hoping that enthusiasm for the measures will boost turnout among their base, especially since the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , one of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effective messengers on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , became the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/13/arizona-abortion-november-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona to vote on enshrining \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in state constitution in November}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican former governor \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  has endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election bid, after he was censured by the state GOP near the end of his term for not being sufficiently loyal to the former president.\par \par \uc2 Ducey cited his support for tougher immigration policies and a continuation of Trump-era tax cuts in his endorsement:\par \par \uc2 enltrMuch is on the line this election year & I\u8217\'20\'19m encouraging all eligible Arizonans to vote & prioritize the issues that most affect our state & nation.\par \par \uc2 I will be voting for Republicans up & down the ballot in November \u8212\'20\'14 and both \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Kari Lake have my endorsement.\par \par \uc2 1/\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  (@DougDucey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougDucey/status/1823426829010747490?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Three years ago, the state Republican party reprimanded Ducey after it was taken over by rightwing officials who retaliated against politicians from the state that had clashed with Trump:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/24/arizona-republicans-censure-mccain-flake-ducey-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republicans censure McCain, Flake and Ducey over Trump split}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is out with a new statement claiming that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  last night \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaks the internet\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It says 25 million users on X have listened to the entire two-hour-plus interview as of noon today, and that the conversation generated 9.6m posts, among other statistics. It also hit out at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for not having done any interviews since launching her campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile weak, failed, and dangerously liberal \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has avoided answering questions for 23 days, President Trump delivered his message directly to the people in a historic, two-hour interview that generated millions of posts and impressions related to President Trump and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unfiltered conversation,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Trump campaign communications director, \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 President Trump will do everything he can to bring his unscripted message directly to the people, something the fake news media refuses to do. While \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  enjoys the luxury of hiding from the press, President Trump accepted Elon\u8217\'20\'19s invitation to have an unfiltered conversation about his America First policies with voters and people around the world. The media can lie, but the numbers don\u8217\'20\'19t: Americans are eager to hear from President Trump and his momentum is only growing as we get closer to November 5.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders warns Trump is 'laying the groundwork' to dispute election loss\par \par \uc2 The prominent progressive senator Bernie Sanders has warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is preparing to once again dispute the results of the 2024 election, should he lose.\par \par \uc2 Trump has never publicly conceded his 2020 election loss to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and engaged in a months-long effort to prevent the Democrat from taking office that culminated in the violent January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 In a just-released statement, Sanders cites the former president\u8217\'20\'19s recent language to argue that he is preparing to do the same this year:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may be crazy, but he\u8217\'20\'19s not stupid. When he claims that \u8220\'20\'1Cnobody\u8221\'20\'1D showed up at a 10,000-person Harris-Walz rally in Michigan that was live-streamed and widely covered by the media, that it was all AI, and that Democrats cheat all of the time, there is a method to his madness. Clearly, and dangerously, what Trump is doing is laying the groundwork for rejecting the election results if he loses. If you can convince your supporters that thousands of people who attended a televised rally do not exist, it will not be hard to convince them that the election returns in Pennsylvania, Michigan, and elsewhere are \u8220\'20\'1Cfake\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudulent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This is what destroying faith in institutions is about. This is what undermining democracy is about. This is what fascism is about.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former Colorado clerk Tina Peters, the first local election official to be charged with a security breach after the 2020 election as unfounded conspiracy theories swirled, was found guilty by a jury on most charges last night.\par \par \uc2 Peters, a one-time hero to those denying that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 presidential election to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , was accused of using someone else\u8217\'20\'19s security badge to give an expert affiliated with the My Pillow chief executive, Mike Lindell, access to the Mesa county election system and deceiving other officials about that person\u8217\'20\'19s identity, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Lindell is a prominent promoter of false claims that voting machines were manipulated to \u8220\'20\'1Csteal\u8221\'20\'1D the election from Trump. His online broadcasting site has been showing a livestream of Peters\u8217\'20\'19 trial.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors said Peters was seeking fame and became \u8220\'20\'1Cfixated\u8221\'20\'1D on voting problems after becoming involved with those who had questioned the accuracy of the 2020 presidential election results.\par \par \uc2 The breach Peters was charged of orchestrating heightened concerns over potential insider threats, in which rogue election workers sympathetic to partisan lies could use their access and knowledge to launch an attack from within.\par \par \uc2 Peters was convicted of three counts of attempting to influence a public servant, one count of conspiracy to commit criminal impersonation, first-degree official misconduct, violation of duty and failing to comply with the secretary of state. She was found not guilty of identity theft, one count of conspiracy to commit criminal impersonation and one count of criminal impersonation.\par \par \uc2 She will be sentenced on 3 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Musk talk on climate labeled 'dumb' by top expert\par \par \uc2 Sea level rise will help create \u8220\'20\'1Cmore oceanfront property\u8221\'20\'1D, carbon pollution is only a problem once it starts causing \u8220\'20\'1Cheadaches and nausea\u8221\'20\'1D and we should be more worried about \u8220\'20\'1Cnuclear warming\u8221\'20\'1D than global warming.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-elon-musk-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conversation}}}\uc2  on X, which Musk owns, last night featured several incoherent and baseless statements on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  , prompting both confusion and derision among environmental advocates.\par \par \uc2 Bill McKibben\uc2 , co-founder of the climate group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://350.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 350.org}}}\uc2 , labeled it the \u8220\'20\'1Cdumbest climate conversation of all time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, the Republican presidential nominee in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , said that rising seas will help create \u8220\'20\'1Cmore oceanfront property\u8221\'20\'1D and complained that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople talk about global warming or they talk about climate change, but they never talk about nuclear warming,\u8221\'20\'1D in reference to potential nuclear war.\par \par \uc2 During the often disjointed exchange, Trump also said it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgrace\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration hadn\u8217\'20\'19t opened up the Arctic to oil drilling and baselessly claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou have farmers that are not allowed to farm anymore and have to get rid of their cattle\u8221\'20\'1D because of climate edicts.\par \par \uc2 Musk, meanwhile, said that he is \u8220\'20\'1Chelping the environment\u8221\'20\'1D by making electric cars via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla}}}\uc2  but said that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want people to \u8220\'20\'1Cvilify\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/oilandgascompanies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oil and gas industry}}}\uc2  that is driving the climate crisis and that the real dangers were, he felt, an increase in CO2 that will cause \u8220\'20\'1Cheadaches and nausea\u8221\'20\'1D and the world potentially running out of oil.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need to rush and we don\u8217\'20\'19t need to like, you know, stop farmers from farming or, you know, prevent people from having steaks or basic stuff like that,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk said about the urgency of climate change. \u8220\'20\'1CLike leave the farmers alone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scientists are clear that the world needs to rapidly move away from fossil fuels to avoid worsening and disastrous climate impacts such as heatwaves, flooding and droughts.\par \par \uc2 The exchange did little to assuage concerns that a second Trump term will only help accelerate dangerous global heating.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign team has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1823404984039322020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted a clip}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, praising her support for workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to strike, in contrast to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lack of such support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2019, GM [\uc2 General Motors\uc2 ] was on strike for 40 days, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was nowhere to be found, didn\u8217\'20\'19t say nothing, didn\u8217\'20\'19t do nothing. Now, let\u8217\'20\'19s look at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 you want to know where she was? On the picket line \u8230\'20\'26 she stood with workers on strike,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said.\par \par \uc2 He praised job retention and creation in the auto and auto parts industry by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his vice-president, Harris, and criticized Trump for promising to save workers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs but then \u8220\'20\'1Cleaving them behind\u8221\'20\'1D as jobs transferred away from factories \u8220\'20\'1Cleft for dead\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1823404984039322020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reposted the post}}}\uc2  on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The United States was not engaged in any aspect of planning or preparation for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s incursion in Russia, the state department deputy spokesperson Vedant Patel told reporters a little earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine blindsided Moscow by pouring thousands of troops into the western Russian region of Kursk last week in a surprise operation that Kyiv says has seen its forces take 1,000 sq km of land, its largest gains since 2022, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 You can read our global coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/13/russian-authorities-scramble-to-quell-ukraines-week-long-kursk-incursion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The fraud trial against the former congressman George Santos, slated to start in a matter of weeks, is coming into focus after a federal judge ruled today that jurors will have their identities kept secret from the public.\par \par \uc2 They won\u8217\'20\'19t, however, be required to fill out a written questionnaire gauging their opinions of Santos when they arrive for jury selection on 9 September, as his lawyers had requested, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Judge Joanna Seybert said during a brief hearing in federal court on Long Island that she agreed with the government\u8217\'20\'19s assessment that a questionnaire would only bog the proceedings down.\par \par \uc2 She said questioning each potential juror in person would allow her and both sides to ask more varied and probing questions to elicit more truthful responses.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors told the judge the trial could last three weeks. Santos has pleaded not guilty to a range of financial crimes, including lying to Congress about his wealth, collecting unemployment benefits while actually working, and using campaign contributions to pay for personal expenses.\par \par \uc2 Santos declined to speak with reporters outside court after the hearing, the last expected before the trial.\par \par \uc2 For all intents and purposes, \uc2 Santos\uc2  has already been found guilty in the court of public opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D read a memo from Santos\u8217\'20\'19s defense team, filed last week.\par \par \uc2 After Santos, a Republican, was ousted from Congress, Democrat \uc2 Tom Suozzi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/14/tom-suozzi-wins-new-york-election-george-santos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the House seat}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wilma Liebman, chair of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) under the former US president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , said that the fact that Elon Mus k chuckled but did not respond to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments about firing strike workers, during their online conversation last night, makes it harder for the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to find the electric vehicle entrepreneur liable for making illegal threats to workers at his companies, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Under federal law, workers cannot be fired for going on strike, and threatening to do so is illegal under the National Labor Relations Act, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  auto workers union said in a statement. Trump called Musk \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest cutter\u8221\'20\'1D for his swathing job losses.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has limited power to punish unlawful labor practices. In cases involving illegal threats, the board can order employers to cease and desist from such conduct and to post notices in the workplace informing workers of their rights. Unions can also use favorable rulings from the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to engage workers they are trying to organize.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s trying to expose more than anything politically what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about in terms of workers, and Musk as well. Everyone knows the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  remedies are toothless to start with, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not so much for the remedy as for sending both a political message and an organizing message,\u8221\'20\'1D Liebman said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca#block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has filed}}}\uc2  separate complaints against Musk and Trump with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Trump is a scab' \u8211\'20\'13 union\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  (\uc2 UAW\uc2 ) leadership is going all in against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition to the statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca#block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from}}}\uc2  the union president, Shawn Fain, the association has posted on X: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s for the billionaires. Not for you. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a scab.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHe's for the billionaires. Not for you.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a scab. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandUpUAW?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandUpUAW}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hj10zDPbzw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hj10zDPbzw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1823343962012123254?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And, with a skeptical inquiring face emoji, the union re-posted a message from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign X account, @KamalaHQ: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump praises billionaire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  for firing workers who were striking for better pay and working conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has endorsed Harris for president, as the presumptive Democratic nominee against Trump, the Republican nominee. It is also trying to unionize workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla}}}\uc2 , Musk\u8217\'20\'19s electric vehicle company.\par \par \uc2 artltr?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dxTzqxYIzF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dxTzqxYIzF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 UAW\uc2  (@UAW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1823195952016248905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is basking in the afterglow of the interview he conducted on X with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last night. The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb6ed28f08cf3dfc945d47#block-66bb6ed28f08cf3dfc945d47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  their conversation had attracted 1bn views and comments, a number that was impossible to verify, while adding he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb69fb8f08cf3dfc945cf5#block-66bb69fb8f08cf3dfc945cf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would be willing}}}\uc2  to hold a similar event with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . But a remark Trump made during the interview about firing employees who strike has spurred the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca#block-66bb7d198f08e4bf5d12c1ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file a federal labor law complaint}}}\uc2  against both the former president and Musk, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb4c618f080fad90fdc8a0#block-66bb4c618f080fad90fdc8a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  last night\u8217\'20\'19s event as a chat between \u8220\'20\'1Cself-obsessed rich guys who will sell out the middle class and who cannot run a live stream in the year 2024\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has no public events scheduled today, but her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb86678f08cf3dfc945ebc#block-66bb86678f08cf3dfc945ebc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to face}}}\uc2  questions over why the vice-president hasn\u8217\'20\'19t held a press conference or granted a sit-down interview since announcing her bid for the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Musk has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb81748f08e4bf5d12c214#block-66bb81748f08e4bf5d12c214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a long history}}}\uc2  of opposing unions, including at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , where the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has been trying to encourage workers to organize.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has been flying around to campaign events in a plane once owned by \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/13/harris-trump-musk-interview-election-updates?page=with:block-66bb79178f081edd5aa0ed58#block-66bb79178f081edd5aa0ed58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , meanwhile, has no public events scheduled today, but continues to face questions over why she won\u8217\'20\'19t talk to reporters.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president has not granted a proper interview or held a press conference since announcing her bid for the White House late last month, a decision her campaign spokeswoman Adrienne Elrod was asked about today, in an interview with CNN.\par \par \uc2 Elrod replied:\par \par \uc2 She has said on the campaign trail that she would be doing an interview at some point. She said that, I think, last week during \u8211\'20\'13 a during a rope line or when she was talking to reporters. But look, what is important here \u8230\'20\'26 is that she is taking her message directly to the American people. She hit a number of battleground states. I think we had 15,000 people in Detroit last week, 12,000 to 13,000 in Nevada. She\u8217\'20\'19s been taking her message to the voters and drawing large crowds. So, she\u8217\'20\'19s actually having those direct conversations.\par \par \uc2 Among those calling for Harris to talk to the press is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s media columnist Margaret Sullivan. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she has to say:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/aug/13/kamala-harris-must-speak-to-press"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris must speak to the press | Margaret Sullivan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  reported earlier this year, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is part of a group of powerful business interests that have turned to the courts to blunt efforts to organize workers nationwide. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 A multi-pronged legal attack under way by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , large corporations, business groups and anti-union litigators threatens to \u8220\'20\'1Craise havoc\u8221\'20\'1D with US labor law and hobble a resurgent labor movement, according to experts.\par \par \uc2 So far efforts to scale back or undermine workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights through the US courts have centered on the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 the US top workplace watchdog and overseer of union elections. But other laws \u8211\'20\'13 including trademark and property rights statutes \u8211\'20\'13 are also being used.\par \par \uc2 Both Musk and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2  are pursuing cases that would undermine the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s company \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/jan/04/spacex-countersues-ceo-elon-musk-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  championed by the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  and other conservative groups against the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  in January. The lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/technology/space/spacex-sues-us-agency-that-accused-it-firing-workers-critical-elon-musk-2024-01-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  the board is unconstitutional because its members can only be removed for cause, not at will, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/spacexs-bid-to-upend-nlrb-follows-signals-from-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  the board violates due process protections. The suit was filed in Texas by Musk\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lawcha.org/2021/02/02/12-facts-about-morgan-lewis-amazons-powerful-anti-union-law-firm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union avoidance law firm Morgan Lewis}}}\uc2  in response to a board complaint that \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  fired workers in retaliation for writing a letter over concerns about Musk\u8217\'20\'19s behavior.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/anti-union-lawsuit-conservative-courts-musk-starbucks-trader-joes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Dark forces\u8217\'20\'19: how US corporations turned to courts in fight against unions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  files labor charge over Trump comments on strikes\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  labor union, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/dec/11/uaw-tesla-elon-musk-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is trying}}}\uc2  to organize workers at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , has filed a federal labor charge over comments \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made last night in his interview with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The union, which has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bid for the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-files-federal-labor-charges-against-donald-trump-and-elon-musk-for-attempting-to-intimidate-and-threaten-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  this comment from Trump to Musk ran afoul of federal law against threatening to fire workers who go on strike: \u8220\'20\'1CYou walk in, you say, You want to quit? They go on strike, I won\u8217\'20\'19t mention the name of the company, but they go on strike and you say, \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s OK, you\u8217\'20\'19re all gone. You\u8217\'20\'19re all gone. So, every one of you is gone.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain :\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will always side against workers standing up for themselves, and he will always side with billionaires like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who is contributing $45m a month to a Super Pac to get him elected. Both Trump and Musk want working-class people to sit down and shut up, and they laugh about it openly. It\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting, illegal and totally predictable from these two clowns.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was also a friend to the late convicted sex offender and New York socialite \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 . \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports that the former president has been using a plane Epstein once owned to travel to campaign events:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  used a plane that was once owned by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2 , the late disgraced financier and convicted sex offender, to fly to several presidential campaign events last weekend, it has been revealed.\par \par \uc2 The former president flew on a Gulfstream G-550 jet whose previous ownership was subsequently traced to Epstein after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own private plane \u8211\'20\'13 a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  757 known colloquially as Trump Force One \u8211\'20\'13 encountered engine troubles.\par \par \uc2 The former Epstein jet was emblazoned with the slogan \u8220\'20\'1CTrump 2024\u8221\'20\'1D for the duration of the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s use.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/article290986070.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami Herald}}}\uc2 , Trump flew from Bozeman, Montana, to Jackson Hole, Wyoming, and then to Aspen, Colorado, before a final trip to Denver on the jet to attend fundraisers as the Republican presidential nominee for November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  campaign said it was unaware of the plane\u8217\'20\'19s previous ownership when it chartered it from Private Jet Services Group, a charter jet vendor it occasionally uses, after the technical problems with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s own aircraft.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/trump-jeffrey-epstein-plane"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump used Jeffrey Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s former jet for campaign appearances }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  yesterday succeeded in getting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to use X, the platform that he wielded as a bully pulpit throughout his presidency, but has generally avoided ever since, even after Musk reversed a ban placed on his account in response to the January 6 insurrection by the company\u8217\'20\'19s then owners.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to X may not last. The former president has not tweeted since his interview with Musk last night, though he has made several posts on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social}}}\uc2 , the X-like platform that he owns, and which has become one of his primary mouthpieces over the past four years. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know if that changes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  also said that his interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  generated 1bn in both views and discussions:\par \par \uc2 enltrCombined views of the conversation with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  and subsequent discussion by other accounts now ~1 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s8x8QmdmnY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/s8x8QmdmnY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1823249070296797515?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It was impossible to verify Musk\u8217\'20\'19s statement, but it\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that Trump, in the interview yesterday, implied that Musk showed him that tens of millions of accounts were listening in, when X\u8217\'20\'19s public count showed that number was closer to 1m.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Musk says he would be willing to interview Harris, too\par \par \uc2 Following his conversation with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last night, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  said he would be willing to host a similar interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy to host Kamala on an ?? Spaces too\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1823217769229566251?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Musk proposed using X\u8217\'20\'19s Spaces feature, which allows live audio broadcasts. Should Harris take him up on the offer, one wonders if he will first fix whatever issue caused the more than 40-minute delay in beginning his interview with Trump last night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 George Santos, the former Republican New York congressman, is appearing in court for a pre-trial hearing today in the federal fraud case against him.\par \par \uc2 Santos has pleaded not guilty to charges of defrauding supporters, illegally receiving benefits and lying to Congress.\par \par \uc2 The trial is set to begin with jury selection on 9 September, and the parties have proposed for opening statements to begin 16 September.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  of Minnesota will defend her seat on Tuesday in the state Democratic primary, a rematch against Don Samuels that comes two years after she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/ilhan-omar-minnesota-primary-victory-progressives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barely eked out a victory}}}\uc2  against him.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s race is the last in a series of heated primaries for the progressive \u8220\'20\'1Csquad\u8221\'20\'1D of House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  who have been vocal in their criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. Her fellow squad members \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  of New York and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  of Missouri were recently defeated by candidates supported by a deluge of pro-Israel spending. But Omar faces a lower-key race.\par \par \uc2 The two-term congresswoman became the first woman of color to represent Minnesota in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  in 2019. While in office, she has allied herself with the left wing of the Democratic party, serving as the deputy chair of the Congressional Progressive caucus and backing key progressive measures like the Green New Deal and Medicare for All.\par \par \uc2 Even before the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ensuing offensive, Omar had established herself as a vocal critic of Israel. She famously drew criticism in 2019 for quipping that US politicians\u8217\'20\'19 support for Israel was \u8220\'20\'1Call about the Benjamins\u8221\'20\'1D, in reference to donations from the American Israel Political Affairs Committee (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ). The comment drew accusations of antisemitism and she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/03/07/700901834/minnesota-congresswoman-ignites-debate-on-israel-and-anti-semitism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later apologized}}}\uc2  for it.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the 7 October attacks, and as Israel escalated its retaliatory war, Omar was among the first in Congress to call for a ceasefire. She has spoken out in support of the university encampments in solidarity with Gaza. Her daughter was suspended from Barnard College for taking part.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/ilhan-omar-minnesota-primary-rematch-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ilhan Omar is latest \u8216\'20\'18squad\u8217\'20\'19 member to face House primary challenge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will address union members in Los Angeles today as part of his first solo campaign stop since he was announced as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 Walz is scheduled to deliver remarks at the convention of \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2  (\uc2 AFSCME\uc2 ), one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest public sector unions, in Los Angeles today at 12.35 pm PT.\par \par \uc2 He is also expected to deliver remarks at a campaign reception in Newport, California, at 2.30pm PT today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oscar Wilde once described the English country gentleman galloping after a fox as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe unspeakable in full pursuit of the uneatable\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  interviewing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  surely qualifies as the incoherent in full pursuit of the unendurable.\par \par \uc2 The men\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-elon-musk-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joint appearance in an audio conversation on X}}}\uc2  on Monday night was, as expected, a display of two planet-sized egos, toxic masculinity and breathtaking mendacity. More surprisingly it was also dull, like sitting with two drunks at a bar trying to set the world to rights over more than two hours.\par \par \uc2 The main message: if Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t win the election, and if Musk doesn\u8217\'20\'19t become the emperor of the universe, you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have a country any more.\par \par \uc2 Musk and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s banal chatter about subjects such as radioactive vegetables and the defeat of Napoleon made you crave a return to what came first: a blissful 40 minutes of wallpaper music. That was because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/aug/12/elon-musk-donald-trump-x-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crippling technical glitches}}}\uc2  left thousands of people unable to join.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/elon-musk-donald-trump-x-interview-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full sketch from our Washington DC bureau chief: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/elon-musk-donald-trump-x-interview-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Musk-Trump X interview: a surprisingly dull meeting of two planet-sized egos}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/elon-musk-donald-trump-x-interview-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Musk-Trump X interview: a surprisingly dull meeting of two planet-sized egos}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to the social media platform that turbocharged his career for a live discussion with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . The former president unleashed familiar rambling, vitriolic talking points to a sympathetic Musk.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-elon-musk-interview-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are key takeaways from the event.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-elon-musk-interview-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Familiar vitriol, and Musk the enabler: key takeaways from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s X interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat down with billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  on Monday for a rambling and vitriolic interview that revisited many of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s most divisive talking points.\par \par \uc2 The interview on X, which is owned by Musk, got off to an inauspicious start, with technical issues that initially prevented many users from watching the conversation. Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1823152153445404990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed}}}\uc2  the delay on a \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive\u8221\'20\'1D cyber-attack, but the cause of the glitch was not entirely clear.\par \par \uc2 After the interview started more than 40 minutes late, Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who at times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DannyKPolitics/status/1823171472954683489"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to have a lisp}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 began the conversation by recounting the failed assassination attempt against him last month at Musk\u8217\'20\'19s request. Although Trump previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/19/trump-rnc-republicans-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would only share the story once at the Republican convention last month, he again discussed in detail his brush with death at a campaign rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, which he said he would visit again in October.\par \par \uc2 Trump told Musk:\par \par \uc2 It was a miracle. If I hadn\u8217\'20\'19t turned my head, I would not be talking to you right now, as much as I like you.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip from the interview:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign condemns Trump's 'extremism and dangerous agenda' after Musk interview\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. On Monday night, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat down with billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for an interview on X that began 45 minutes late, featured the Republican presidential nominee\u8217\'20\'19s greatest hits and biggest lies, in which he denigrated immigrants and attempted to paint \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D leftist, repeatedly mispronounced her name, and called the Democratic presumptive nominee \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the conversation, the two men lavished praise and admiration on each other and at the end, Musk told Trump he was \u8220\'20\'1Con the right path\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/12/trump-elon-musk-interview-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are key takeaways from the event.}}}\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign condemned the interview as an example of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism and dangerous Project 2025 agenda\u8221\'20\'1D. Joseph Costello, a Harris campaign spokesperson, said:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s entire campaign is in service of people like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and himself \u8211\'20\'13 self-obsessed rich guys who will sell out the middle class and who cannot run a live stream in the year 2024.\par \par \uc2 The interview came as Harris has pulled ahead in polls following the launch of her campaign last month. The Decision Desk HQ and the Hill\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections2024.thehill.com/national/harris-trump-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national polling average}}}\uc2  now shows Harris with a 0.3% lead over Trump, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections2024.thehill.com/national/biden-trump-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had}}}\uc2  a 3.3% advantage over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  before the president withdrew from the race.\par \par \uc2 Harris appears to be in an even stronger position in the key battleground states of Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, which will likely determine the outcome of the election in November. According to a recent set of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/10/us/politics/harris-trump-battleground-polls.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surveys}}}\uc2  conducted last week by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College, Harris now leads by four points in those three states, while prior polls showed a virtual tie or a slight Trump advantage in those states.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 12.20pm ET. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the first lady , Jill Biden, will depart the White House en route to New Orleans.\par \par \uc2 3.35pm. Minnesota governor and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will deliver remarks at the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2  Convention in Los Angeles. He will later deliver remarks at a campaign reception in Newport, California.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240813ek8d001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
