\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Arizona to vote on enshrining  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in state constitution in November\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 August 2024\par 17:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats hope listing measure to establish right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on ballot will boost turnout in battleground state\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters will decide this November whether to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into their state constitution, a prospect that could turbocharge voter turnout in a critical battleground state in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the Arizona secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office announced that it had validated an estimated 577,971 signatures in support of a ballot measure, the Arizona For \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Act, to establish a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 On X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderTabet/status/1823170565961871540"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the office called}}}\uc2  the measure \u8220\'20\'1Cthe largest petition effort in Arizona history\u8221\'20\'1D. The measure will be listed on the ballot as Proposition 139.\par \par \uc2 Arizona is not the only state to face the prospect of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure this November. So far, states including Colorado, Florida and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 another key battleground state \u8211\'20\'13 are also set to hold similar ballot measures. Tuesday also marks the deadline for the state of Missouri to determine whether to add its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measure to its ballots.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, ballot measures that protect or preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have successfully passed even in red states such as Ohio, Kansas and Kentucky. However, they have never been tested during a presidential election. Democrats are hoping that enthusiasm for the measures will boost turnout among their base, especially since the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , one of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effective messengers on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , became the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently legal up until 15 weeks in Arizona. Earlier this year, the state supreme court ruled that a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from 1864 \u8211\'20\'13 enacted before Arizona even became a state \u8211\'20\'13 could take effect. That ruling unleashed weeks of nationwide outrage and ultimately led a handful of Republicans to break with their party to vote in favor of a bill to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeal the 1864 ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If passed, Arizona for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Act would establish that Arizonans have \u8220\'20\'1Ca fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. It would protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, which is typically dated to around 24 weeks of pregnancy, and allow for abortions past that point if a medical provider deems them necessary to protect a pregnant individual\u8217\'20\'19s life, physical health or mental health.\par \par \uc2 In May, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scribd.com/document/733845819/cbsnews-20240519-AZ-1-SUN#1fullscreen=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a CBS poll}}}\uc2  found that 66% of Arizona adults want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240813ek8d002mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
