\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Texas women denied abortions for ectopic pregnancies demand federal investigation\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 664 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 August 2024\par 15:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 27\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Two women say hospitals violated emergency care laws by denying treatment for life-threatening condition\par \par \uc2 Two Texas women who were denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for life-threatening ectopic pregnancies have filed complaints with the Biden administration calling for investigations into the hospitals for violating federal law.\par \par \uc2 An ectopic pregnancy is a dangerous condition in which the fertilized egg implants in the fallopian tube instead of the uterus. It has no chance of developing into a healthy pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 One of the complaints details how Kyleigh Thurman, a 25-year-old woman from Burnet, Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Thurman-EMTALA-complaint_2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was turned away}}}\uc2  at Ascension Williamson hospital in February, even though her OB-GYN told the hospital she probably had an ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Days later, she returned, bleeding and in severe pain, but only received treatment after her OB-GYN traveled to the hospital \u8220\'20\'1Cto plead with the medical staff\u8221\'20\'1D to terminate Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 However, the delay caused her ectopic pregnancy to rupture. Thurman nearly bled to death and was forced into emergency surgery to remove her fallopian tube. Her ability to have children is now compromised.\par \par \uc2 According to the second complaint, Kelsie Norris-De La Cruz experienced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Norris-De-La-Cruz-EMTALA-complaint-2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar harrowing ordeal}}}\uc2  at Texas Health Arlington Memorial hospital, outside Dallas. By the time she received treatment, her pregnancy was near rupture. Norris-De La Cruz lost a fallopian tube and most of her right ovary.\par \par \uc2 Ectopic pregnancy is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10071153/#:~:text=The%20current%20standard%20for%20ectopic,protein%20A%20specifically%20showing%20promise."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading cause}}}\uc2  of maternal mortality in the first trimester, comprising up to 10% of all pregnancy-related deaths nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the fact that my life was clearly in danger, the hospital told me that they could not help me. I ended up losing half of my fertility and if I was made to wait any longer, it\u8217\'20\'19s very likely I would have died,\u8221\'20\'1D said Norris-De La Cruz in a press release.\par \par \uc2 Filed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights}}}\uc2 , the two complaints with the US Department of Health and Human Services allege hospitals violated the longstanding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/medicare/regulations-guidance/legislation/emergency-medical-treatment-labor-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act}}}\uc2  (Emtala), which requires hospitals to provide stabilizing care, including abortions, to patients with emergency medical conditions.\par \par \uc2 After the Biden administration issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/about/news/2022/07/11/following-president-bidens-executive-order-protect-access-reproductive-health-care-hhs-announces-guidance-clarify-that-emergency-medical-care-includes-abortion-services.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guidance}}}\uc2  meant to protect hospitals who offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in emergency situations under Emtala, Texas state officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/news/releases/paxton-sues-biden-admin-over-its-efforts-force-abortions-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  the federal health department and secured a block on that guidance in 2022. (Earlier this year, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed a case}}}\uc2  that weighed whether Emtala superseded Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, returning the case to a lower court. Meanwhile, a conservative appellate court have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ca5.uscourts.gov/opinions/pub/23/23-10246-CV0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld}}}\uc2  the block on care in Texas.)\par \par \uc2 While Texas carries one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/08/texas-abortion-high-risk-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strictest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  in the US, treatment for ectopic pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 which can lead to serious complications and even death \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/HS/htm/HS.245.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explicitly allowed}}}\uc2  under state law and thus not considered \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. This was reaffirmed by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2023/08/22/1195115865/texas-abortion-bans-softened-quietly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law passed}}}\uc2  during the state\u8217\'20\'19s last legislative session.\par \par \uc2 The complaint notes that despite that exception, the severe penalties physicians face for violating the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which include $100,000 in fines and up to life in prison, has instilled fear in doctors, jeopardizing their willingness to provide care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many more people will nearly die before we see change? These women are proof that exceptions do not make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans less dangerous, even when they are exceedingly clear,\u8221\'20\'1D said Beth Brinkmann, senior director of US litigation at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to have the best interest of your patient in mind when you\u8217\'20\'19re staring down a life sentence. Texas officials have put doctors in an impossible situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The complaint asks the \uc2 Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services\uc2  to conduct an investigation into the hospitals and enforce Emtala to hold them accountable, including issuing potential penalties.\par \par \uc2 More than 100 pregnant women in medically dire situations who sought help from emergency rooms were turned away or \u8220\'20\'1Cnegligently treated\u8221\'20\'1D since 2022, a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pregnant-women-emergency-room-ectopic-er-edd66276d2f6c412c988051b618fb8f9?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2  analysis found.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240813ek8d001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
