\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Child rape survivors face extraordinary barriers in states with  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Sara Cincurova and Virginia Williams \par \uc2 1,423 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 August 2024\par 13:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since fall of Roe, 14 states have passed near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 most with no exceptions for rape or incest survivors\par \par \uc2 As children in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , A and her sister were raped multiple times by their stepfather and his friends before she found she was pregnant earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe both had STDs because none of them used condoms,\u8221\'20\'1D A said. Their stepfather stopped sexually abusing them when he found out the sisters were treated at a clinic for sexually transmitted diseases. One of his friends did not.\par \par \uc2 The sisters fled to a domestic violence shelter when A found out she was pregnant, and managed from there to find {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills}}}\uc2  through a network of underground activists. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I would have killed myself,\u8221\'20\'1D A said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe man who raped me was a pig, and I did not want to have his baby inside of me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  in 2022, 14 states have passed near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Ten of those states, including Texas, have no exceptions for survivors of rape or incest. A study published earlier this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/25/abortion-after-rape-laws-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  that 65,000 rape-related pregnancies probably occurred in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 While there are no studies on the numbers of rape-related pregnancies in minors since Roe was overturned, young people in states with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  bans face unique barriers, according to doctors and advocates who spoke with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStates that ban abortions, both with and without rape exceptions, do not have carve-outs for minors,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Samuel Dickman, one of the authors of the study on rape-related pregnancies since Roe fell, said via email. \u8220\'20\'1CMany states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care remains legal impose burdensome additional restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for minors, such as parental consent or notification laws. And of course, the logistical and financial burdens on people trying to get abortions out of state are often worse for minors, who may not have access to transportation or the funds needed to travel and pay for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eleven states that have banned or restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Roe v Wade fell have exceptions for rape and incest \u8211\'20\'13 but, as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/policy-watch/rape-incest-exceptions-abortion-bans-restrictions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent analysis}}}\uc2  from KFF shows, they are often unworkable in practice due to a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, requirements that survivors report the crime to police, and strict gestational limits.\par \par \uc2 Elisabeth Smith, director of state policy and advocacy at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , singles out the law enforcement requirement as a particularly onerous barrier. It is well-known that survivors of rape often avoid going to the police out of fear of retribution or inaction; as the KFF study points out, an estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bjs.ojp.gov/document/cv22.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 21% of sexual assaults are reported}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that sexual assault often goes unreported for various reasons; in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned and clinics have shuttered, everyone, including rape and incest survivors, will likely have to travel out of state to get care,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 When a minor child is a survivor of incest, it is often the primary caregiver \u8211\'20\'13 parent, step-parent or grandparent \u8211\'20\'13 that has raped them, Dr Peta-gay Ledbetter, a psychotherapist and former maternity nurse working with low-income populations in Texas, said. That makes it even less likely she or a relative will report the crime to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 The burdens on people trying to get abortions out of state are often worse for minors\par \par \uc2 Dr Samuel Dickman, co-author on post-Roe study\par \par \uc2 Ledbetter said she had seen a 10-year old become pregnant after her mother\u8217\'20\'19s boyfriend sexually assaulted her, with the mother\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge. \u8220\'20\'1CHer little body was unable to carry the pregnancy, and she started to have a uterine rupture before the fetus was at a viable gestation.\u8221\'20\'1D The complications of preterm labor and uterine rupture necessitated a C-section to save the child\u8217\'20\'19s life; the fetus did not survive. \u8220\'20\'1CAn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have saved this 10-year-old child great suffering and trauma for the rest of her life,\u8221\'20\'1D Ledbetter said.\par \par \uc2 M, the activist who helped A get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, says that the minors she comes across seeking help have often resorted to unsafe measures to try to induce their own abortions. In 2023, she was contacted by another 16-year-old from Texas who got pregnant after a stranger raped her. \u8220\'20\'1CLike other girls I have met, she tried to overdose on borrowed medications,\u8221\'20\'1D M said. Forced to carry to term, she quit school and delivered a baby with a heart defect. M says she remains suicidal. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve met at least three other girls who tried everything from drinking bottles of Nyquil and isopropyl alcohol, to taking Fentanyl,\u8221\'20\'1D M added. \u8220\'20\'1COne of my colleagues had to call the suicide hotline and poison control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is a dearth of literature on the mental health effects of pregnancies caused by rape, says Jennifer Toof, a trauma-informed psychologist based in Pennsylvania who is writing a book about the ethical responsibilities of mental health professionals post-Roe. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that rape and incest are significant risk factors for the development of post-traumatic stress disorder and other mental health disorders, particularly for children, so having pre-existing trauma and mental health struggles on top of being forced to carry an unwanted pregnancy to term when someone is still a child themselves is a dangerous combination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A sprawling, underground network of activists is trying to fill the gap by providing women and girls with the means to end their pregnancies safely. According to M, who is not sharing her real name given the nature of her work, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe rely on a network of women who live in blue states to keep us \u8216\'20\'18supplied\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D These activists often provide support beyond the pills themselves \u8211\'20\'13 M told the Guardian that they also provide funds and help minors travel for the care they need.\par \par \uc2 Tightening restrictions\par \par \uc2 The impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on young rape survivors came into national focus in 2022, when a 10-year-old girl from Ohio who was pregnant as the result of a rape {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was forced to travel}}}\uc2  to Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as her home state banned the procedure after six weeks. (\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have since been codified in Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.) The Indiana doctor who performed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Caitlin Bernard, reported the procedure as required by state law, sparking a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/indiana-abortion-ruling-caitlin-bernard-medical-license"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign}}}\uc2  against her by a group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and politicians.\par \par \uc2 In another highly publicized case, in Mississippi, a 13-year-old girl who was raped by a stranger when she was 12 got pregnant and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/aug/14/mississippi-abortion-ban-girl-raped-gives-birth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to carry the baby to term}}}\uc2  because her family didn\u8217\'20\'19t have the money to drive to the nearest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Chicago, or to pay for the procedure. While the child and her mother reported the rape to law enforcement, she was unable to terminate the pregnancy due to a lack of clarity around the exception. Today, she is raising the baby with the help of her family; her rapist was caught and charged.\par \par \uc2 Some lawmakers have tried to introduce carve-outs to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans for minors but have faced pushback in conservative states. In May 2024, a legislative committee in Louisiana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-incest-rape-louisiana-exception-846480b677fbc6fbe60d18ca13572899"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  a bill that would have added cases of rape and incest as exceptions to Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. They also rejected an amendment brought by the Democratic state representative Delisha Boyd, which would have narrowed the bill to apply only to minors under the age of 17.\par \par \uc2 Other states are seeking to make it even harder for children to access care. Laws in Idaho and Tennessee seek to punish any adult who helps a minor cross state lines for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such laws are \u8220\'20\'1Cfalsely presented as \u8216\'20\'18parents\u8217\'20\'19 rights\u8217\'20\'19 measures\u8221\'20\'1D, says Alison Brysk, a political science professor at the \uc2 University of California, Santa Barbara\uc2 , who researches the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis means that the access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a child impregnated by parental abuse could depend upon the permission of the very person who abused them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Information and support for anyone affected by rape or sexual abuse issues is available from the following organisations. In the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rainn.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rainn}}}\uc2  offers support on 800-656-4673. In the UK, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rapecrisis.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rape Crisis}}}\uc2  offers support on 0808 500 2222. In Australia, support is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1800respect.org.au/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1800Respect}}}\uc2  (1800 737 732). Other international helplines can be found at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240813ek8d001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
