\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Walz whip up crowd at packed Phoenix rally \u8211\'20\'13 but \u8216\'20\'18we are the underdog\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell \par \uc2 985 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2024\par 02:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president addresses Gaza after protesters interrupt speech on immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indigenous rights\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  rallied a packed arena outside Phoenix, Arizona, on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 drawing perhaps the largest Democratic crowd of the election cycle this year.\par \par \uc2 The presumptive Democratic presidential nominee, her running mate and the local leaders who joined them on stage whipped up the crowd, discussing immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Indigenous sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 Noting the Indigenous leaders in the room, Harris also said: \u8220\'20\'1CI will always honor tribal sovereignty and respect tribal self-determination.\u8221\'20\'1D Indigenous voters are credited with helping deliver Arizona to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020; the state is home to 22 federally recognized tribes.\par \par \uc2 At one point during her speech, Harris was interrupted by protesters chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cfree, free Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D and other messages in support of Gaza. She stopped her speech to address the protesters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to fight for our democracy, which includes respecting the voices that I think we are hearing from. Let me just speak to that for a moment and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll get back to the business at hand,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have been clear: now is the time to get a ceasefire deal and get the hostage deal done. Now is the time. And the president and I are working around the clock every day to get that ceasefire deal done and bring the hostages home.\u8221\'20\'1D Her statement represented a noticeable change in tone from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/kamala-harris-meets-with-uncommitted-gaza-protesters-after-they-disrupt-rally-in-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her approach to Gaza protesters}}}\uc2  in Detroit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz took the stage at the Desert Diamond Arena, a venue that can hold 20,000 people. Although official estimates are not yet available, the Harris campaign confirmed that more than 15,000 people attended the Phoenix rally. On stage, in front of attendees waving signs that read \u8220\'20\'1CCoach!\u8221\'20\'1D, Walz said the rally \u8220\'20\'1Cmight be the largest political gathering in the history of Arizona\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not as if anybody cares about crowd sizes or anything,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Other Harris campaign events this week that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/first-thing-thousands-rally-for-harris-and-walz-in-wisconsin-and-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawn crowds}}}\uc2  of up to 15,000, invoking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/trump-january-6-lies-kamala-harris-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ire}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who claims to have \u8220\'20\'1Cspoken to the biggest crowds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz rally represents a renewed push to put the Sun belt back on the map for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s still young campaign. Before Friday night, the state appeared to be leaning red, with Trump leading Harris by single digits in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000191-0bfd-d871-af95-affdc1b80000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/july-2024-swing-state-polls-harris-trails-trump-in-arizona-georgia-michigan-pennsylvania-tied-in-wisconsin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2 . But by the evening of the rally, Harris and Trump appeared neck and neck in the state, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling from FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2  showing Harris\u8217\'20\'19 44.4% closely following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 44.8%.\par \par \uc2 Polls on Friday morning showed Harris narrowly leading Trump nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Despite the large crowd, Harris reminded attendees: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the underdog.\u8221\'20\'1D She added that hard work would be required to win the election, in a short period of time. Harris officially became the presumptive Democratic nominee on Monday and announced her running mate on Tuesday, after Biden withdrew from the election on 21 July.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also bring greetings from our incredible president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. Earlier in the day the White House had announced Biden and Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/09/kamala-harris-trump-polls-us-election-tim-walz-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would attend their first joint event}}}\uc2  since the president pulled out of the race.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in a border state where immigration often ranks as a top issue among voters, Harris struck a tough, but progressive, tone \u8211\'20\'13 emphasizing her history as a prosecutor who \u8220\'20\'1Cwent after the trans-national gangs, the drug cartels and the human traffickers\u8221\'20\'1D but also calling for a pathway to citizenship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know our immigration system is broken and we know what it takes to fix it: comprehensive reform. That includes strong border security and an earned pathway to citizenship,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 While border apprehensions have dropped nationwide, they\u8217\'20\'19ve remained high in Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 where voters will decide in November whether to make unlawfully crossing the border a state crime.\par \par \uc2 Her statements echoed a campaign ad published yesterday, saying Harris would \u8220\'20\'1Chire thousands more border agents and crack down on fentanyl and human trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D. Republicans have criticized Harris\u8217\'20\'19 handling of immigration, saying she was Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D, and an ad released by a pro-Trump super Pac last month blamed her for a \u8220\'20\'1Cchaotic mess\u8221\'20\'1D at the border. Harris was tapped by the Biden administration to address the root causes of migration.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been another key issue in Arizona since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. Harris noted that many states, including Arizona, had laws with \u8220\'20\'1Cno exceptions for rape or incest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently restricted after 15 weeks of pregnancy in Arizona, although a high profile state supreme court ruling had temporarily reinstated a near-total ban earlier this year. Voters will evaluate a ballot measure this November that would codify the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 Long a Republican bastion, Arizona swung blue in 2020 when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-donald-trump-arizona-phoenix-elections-9638adedbe826b31b5d172ba3a1c7c3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden defeated Trump}}}\uc2  by fewer than 11,000 votes, thanks to a coalition of Native Americans, Latinos, young people, white suburban voters and moderates who had traditionally voted Republican but were disenchanted by Trump.\par \par \uc2 Democratic strategists had wondered if the Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , who has won two difficult elections, might have helped Harris cement that coalition as her vice-president. This was Harris\u8217\'20\'19 first visit to the state since she announced Walz as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Kelly and his wife, the former US representative \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , spoke before Harris and Walz. Giffords and Walz were freshman members of Congress together in 2007, before Giffords was shot in an attempted assassination in 2011. Giffords joined Walz in Minnesota in 2023 when he signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/09/tim-walz-gun-control-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a package of gun safety measures}}}\uc2  into law.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  also spoke at the beginning of the rally. Gallego is challenging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-kari-lake-arizona-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s disciple Kari Lake}}}\uc2  for Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s open \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat this November.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240810ek8a0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
