\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Walz fire up crowd in first rally as running mates \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Maanvi Singh, Joan E Greve and Lili Bayer (earlier) \par \uc2 13,950 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 August 2024\par 08:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full report on the Philadelphia rally here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing soon. You can read our full report on the Philadelphia rally here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/kamala-harris-running-mate-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris introduces running mate Tim Walz at raucous Philadelphia rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some pictures from the rally:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Gambino was as the rally in Philadelphia. Here is her report:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  introduced her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of vice-president America deserves,\u8221\'20\'1D at a raucous rally in Philadelphia that showcased Democratic unity and enthusiasm for the party\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic presidential ticket ahead of the November election.\par \par \uc2 Casting their campaign as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfight for the future\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris and Walz were repeatedly interrupted by applause and cheering as they addressed thousands of battleground-state voters wearing bracelets that twinkled red white and blue at Temple University\u8217\'20\'19s Liacouras Center \u8211\'20\'13 a crowd her team said was its largest to date.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for bringing back the joy,\u8221\'20\'1D a beaming Walz said to Harris, after she presented him to the crowd, reciting his biography as a teacher, high school football coach, military veteran, legislator and governor. Harris, who has served as vice-president to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for three and a half years, said Walz, the Minnesota governor, would be \u8220\'20\'1Cready on day one\u8221\'20\'1D, and said the race between them and the Republican presidential ticket of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and JD Vance was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmatchup between the varsity team and the JV squad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/kamala-harris-running-mate-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris introduces running mate Tim Walz at raucous Philadelphia rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris hopes Walz will help her shore up her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s standing across the upper Midwest, a critical region in presidential politics that often serves as a buffer for Democrats seeking the White House. The party remains haunted by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wins in Michigan and Wisconsin in 2016. Trump lost those states in 2020 but has zeroed in on them as he aims to return to the presidency this year and is expanding his focus to Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 Since Walz was announced, the team raised more than $20m from grassroots donations, the campaign said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The new rule essentially makes the certification of election results discretionary, said Democratic state representative Sam Park at a press conference outside of the hearing room at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are Maga certification rules, and they\u8217\'20\'19re in direct conflict with Georgia law, which states in multiple places that local elections board officials shall perform their duties, meaning their duties are mandatory, not discretionary,\u8221\'20\'1D Park said.\par \par \uc2 Debate on the rule centered on how much power state law and court precedent grants to the state board of elections to set rules for local boards. Georgia supreme court case law describes the role of elections supervisors as ministerial with little discretion to declare a vote valid or invalid, said Nikhel Sus, deputy chief counsel at Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is contrary to settled Georgia law and would exceed this court\u8217\'20\'19s rule making authority,\u8221\'20\'1D Sus said. The law requires disputes about a vote to be resolved with investigations by district attorneys, courts and other bodies, he said.\par \par \uc2 Board members in support of the rule say that local elections supervisors are required to sign an affidavit declaring that the results of an election are accurate and correct, and that rules should permit elections boards the power to determine the truth of that statement for themselves.\par \par \uc2 The rule is likely to draw an immediate legal challenge so close to an election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/georgia-local-election-boards-allowed-withhold-vote-certification"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Georgia rules let local boards withhold election certification}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 New Georgia rules let local boards withhold election certification\par \par \uc2 Moving away from the rally for a moment to other important election news: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s state board of elections adopted new rules for local election boards that permit them to withhold the certification of a vote in the face of unspecified discrepancies \u8211\'20\'13 a Republican-led move that could cause uncertainty and confusion after future election days.\par \par \uc2 The five-person board passed the measure in a 3-2 vote. The three board members who voted for it \u8211\'20\'13 Dr Janice Johnson, Rick Jeffares and Janelle King \u8211\'20\'13 were praised by name three days ago by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/trump-rally-georgia-crime-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta campaign rally}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/12/georgia-fulton-county-paper-ballots-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rule was proposed}}}\uc2  by Michael Heekin, a Republican appointee to the Fulton election board who refused to certify the presidential primary earlier this year. The rule requires local boards to initiate a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable inquiry\u8221\'20\'1D when discrepancies emerge at a poll, and gives the power to withhold certification until that inquiry is completed. It does not define the term \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable inquiry\u8221\'20\'1D, nor does it establish strict limitations on the breadth of an inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/georgia-local-election-boards-allowed-withhold-vote-certification"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Georgia rules let local boards withhold election certification}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , who spoke before introducing Harris and Walz at Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s rally, affirmed his support of Harris, exclaiming that she is \u8220\'20\'1Cbattle tested and ready to go\u8221\'20\'1D. He spoke of the danger of Trump becoming president again, citing the statement coined by Walz: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a weirdo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris entered the stage shortly afterward. \u8220\'20\'1CTogether with \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , we will win {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said to applause.\par \par \uc2 Cherelle Parker, Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, also spoke in support of Harris at Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s rally. As the first Black female mayor in the city\u8217\'20\'19s history, Parker acknowledged that the event was \u8220\'20\'1Chistory-making\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on the cusp of electing our vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  to be the 47th president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Parker said as the crowd erupted. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let Trump the trickster take our eyes off the prize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 In the eyes of Andrew Cambron, a 34-year-old teacher from Delaware, Walz was the best option for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, since he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of guy who resonates with the center of the country\u8221\'20\'1D. Cambron added that he wanted to see a broader investment in public education and to see Harris get behind universal healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally have a progressive on the Democratic ticket,\u8221\'20\'1D Cambron said about Walz, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich hasn\u8217\'20\'19t really happened since Obama in 2012.\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro would have been a terrible choice, said Cambron, who disagreed with Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s pro-Israel stance and his efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/philadelphia/news/josh-shapiro-university-of-pennsylvania-protests-palestinian-encampment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quash pro-Palestinian}}}\uc2  protests on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 During the presidential primaries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/03/uncommitted-voters-biden-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 700,000 voters cast uncommitted ballots}}}\uc2  or the equivalent to express their dissatisfaction with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza}}}\uc2 . The Uncommitted National Movement has stated that it\u8217\'20\'19s waiting to hear from Harris on her Gaza policies before agreeing to endorse her. But following Harris\u8217\'20\'19s Tuesday announcement about Walz, the group released a statement saying that they hope he will help change course on Gaza policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor Walz has demonstrated a remarkable ability to evolve as a public leader, uniting Democrats diverse coalition to achieve significant milestones for Minnesota families of all backgrounds,\u8221\'20\'1D Elianne Farhat, senior advisor at Uncommitted and executive director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ceasefiretoday.us21.list-manage.com/track/click?u=be15613b4f6eb611805473e0a&id=bf314d76cb&e=7161125ca1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Take Action Minnesota}}}\uc2 , a political advocacy group, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAs Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, it\u8217\'20\'19s crucial he continues this evolution by supporting an arms embargo on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war and occupation against Palestinians in an effort to unite our party to defeat authoritarianism in the fall.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is that couch moment:\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris' face. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ji6WEwsqB6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ji6WEwsqB6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Heather Thomas (@HeatherThomasAF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HeatherThomasAF/status/1820957973403070655?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic running mates have \u8220\'20\'1CHappy Warrior energy\u8221\'20\'1D, per the New York Times\u8217\'20\'19 chief White House correspondent, Peter Baker:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Happy Warrior energy of the Harris-Walz rally just now is something we haven't seen in American politics for a while. Feels reminiscent of Clinton-Gore '92. Doesn't mean they win; plenty of Happy Warriors lose. But it's a vastly different dynamic than just a few weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Peter Baker (@peterbakernyt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/peterbakernyt/status/1820962911067451778?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  columnist James Hohmann points out that Walz has personal experience with the, at times, astronomically expensive US healthcare system:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , access to health care is personal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/f43TMtfF7g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/f43TMtfF7g}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 James Hohmann (@jameshohmann) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jameshohmann/status/1820908371836588327?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of Harris and Walz\u8217\'20\'19s speeches at the rally:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In her first appearance with her newly minted running mate, Harris sought to define him foremost as a teacher and football coach. He was, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of teacher and mentor that every child in America dreams of having\u8221\'20\'1D. She told a story about him agreeing to be faculty adviser to his school\u8217\'20\'19s gay-straight alliance, knowing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe signal it would send to have a football coach get involved\u8221\'20\'1D. He was, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of coach, because he\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of person, who inspires people to dream big\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris also spoke about Walz\u8217\'20\'19s skills as a marksman, and his views on the second amendment: he is in favour, but with caveats for background checks and red flags. Walz was the highest ranking enlisted man to ever serve in \uc2 US congress\uc2  and the top Democrat on the veterans\u8217\'20\'19 committee, she said. He was also known as one of Capitol Hill\u8217\'20\'19s best marksmen. She also used football references, comparing him and Vance to \u8220\'20\'1Ca matchup between the varsity team and the [junior varsity] squad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Walz, who like Harris is known for his smile, started his speech by saying: \u8220\'20\'1C Thank you for the trust you put in me, but more so, thank you for bringing back the joy. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance are irritated that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  smiles and laughs, they\u8217\'20\'19re really going to be irritated by \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Melissa Hortman\uc2 , the Democratic speaker of Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s house of representatives, told the Guardian on Tuesday. He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t ever underestimate teachers.\u8221\'20\'1D Walz\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Gwen, is a teacher, too.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 WhenWalz talked about Trump, he pivoted quickly, and effectively, from talking about Republicans interfering with healthcare, to his own daughter being born thanks to IVF, to children fearing that they will be shot at school. \u8220\'20\'1CIn Minnesota we respect our neighbours for the personal choices they make,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat includes IVF.\u8221\'20\'1D He talked about his daughter Hope, who often appears in videos and photographs with her father, being born through IVF. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have been increasingly pushing for broader measures that would give rights and protections to embryos and fetuses, which could have huge implications for fertility treatments and other areas of healthcare. Walz said \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t by chance that, when we welcomed our daughter into the world, we named her Hope.\u8221\'20\'1D Then he said that when he and Harris talk about freedom, they mean the freedom to make your own choice about your body, and the freedom for children to go to school and not worry about being shot.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He called on people to \u8220\'20\'1Csettle our political differences not with violence, but with votes\u8221\'20\'1D and said of Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t believe him when he plays dumb. He knows exactly what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/project-2025-key-proposals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  will to do restrict our freedoms.\u8221\'20\'1D He added of a second Trump term: \u8220\'20\'1COnly this time it will be much, much worse.\u8221\'20\'1D Walz seasoned his remarks with midwestern dialect, adding a \u8220\'20\'1Cdamn well\u8221\'20\'1D here and a \u8220\'20\'1Ccome on\u8221\'20\'1D there. \u8220\'20\'1CSay it with me! We are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, starting a chant from the audience. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got 91 days. My God, that\u8217\'20\'19s easy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll sleep when we\u8217\'20\'19re dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Walz made a couch reference. Walz said his GOP rival and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Care creepy and yes, they\u8217\'20\'19re weird as hell\u8221\'20\'1D. He added that he \u8220\'20\'1Ccan\u8217\'20\'19t wait to debate the guy\u8221\'20\'1D. Then, to sustained cheers and laughter, he made a reference to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/04/jd-vance-critics-trump-vp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 baseless}}}\uc2 , but much-shared, claim that JD Vance admitted to having sex with a couch in his memoir. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is if he\u8217\'20\'19s willing to get off the couch and show up.\u8221\'20\'1D Stumping earlier today in Pennsylvania, Vance said, \u8220\'20\'1CI absolutely want to debate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D but not until after the Democratic convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Helen Sullivan taking you through the latest US politics news for the next while.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris-Walz campaign kicks off with an energetic start\par \par \uc2 At {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first rally since announcing Minnesota governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  as her running mate, the room at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, was ebullient, filled with thousands of voters cheering and waving Harris-Walz signs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel ecstatic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joseph Alston, a 69-year-old West Norriton Democratic committee member. Last week, he campaigned for Harris by knocking on doors and handing out flyers in the nearby King of Prussia area. People who he spoke to said that they were committed to vote against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want him anywhere near the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D Alston said.\par \par \uc2 Voters at the Tuesday rally were split in their opinions about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pass over \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  governor who was on the shortlist of vice-presidential candidates. Still, they reaffirmed their vow to support Harris and to ensure that Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t elected again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, it was always going to be Harris and whoever her running mate was going to be,\u8221\'20\'1D said Torri Green, a 35-year-old photographer from Philadelphia. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s too much at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Outside of the event, Green had stood in line with thousands of people waiting to enter. If Harris is elected president, Green said she hopes that teachers will get paid more and that reproductive rights will be protected. Casting a vote for Harris in November is a no-brainer for her, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CI appreciate her as a person and the light that she brings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel so good,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patricia Bai about supporting Harris as the Democratic nominee. The caregiver from Liberia will vote in a presidential election for the first time after recently becoming a US citizen. \u8220\'20\'1CIf [Harris] becomes president tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D Bai said, \u8220\'20\'1Cshe will implement policies that would put us in the right place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bill Haggett, a 72-year-old former health executive, said that he appreciated that Walz made school {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fastcompany.com/91168428/how-tim-walz-made-school-meals-free-for-all-minnesota-students#:~:text=In%20March%202023%2C%20Tim%20Walz,free%20school%20meals%20for%20students."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meals free for all Minnesota students}}}\uc2 , and he was curious to see if Walz\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments in Minnesota would be scalable nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/philadelphia-rally-kamala-harris-tim-walz-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel ecstatic\u8217\'20\'19: Philadelphia rally-goers cheer Harris \u8211\'20\'13 and her VP pick, Tim Walz}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s closing message: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got 91 days. My God, that\u8217\'20\'19s easy. We\u8217\'20\'19ll sleep when we\u8217\'20\'19re dead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just gotta fight,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve just gotta fight, because as soon-to-be-president Harris says, \u8216\'20\'18When we fight, we win.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz also appears to be enjoying his role as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s attack dog on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s not fighting for you or your family,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I gotta tell you, his running mate shares his dangerous and backward agenda for this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was especially pointed in his takedown of JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike all regular people I grew up with in the heartland, JD studied at Yale, had his career funded by Silicon Valley billionaires, and then wrote a bestseller trashing that community,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to debate the guy \u8211\'20\'13 that is if he\u8217\'20\'19s willing to get off the couch and show up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The latter is cheeky reference to a completely unsubstantiated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/04/jd-vance-critics-trump-vp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internet joke }}}\uc2  about Vance \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Walz seemed pleased with himself. \u8220\'20\'1CSee what I did there?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 New Walz catch phrase alert: \u8220\'20\'1CMind your own damn business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Minnesota, we respect our neighbors and their personal choices that they make, even if we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t make the same choice for ourselves,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a golden rule, mind your own damn business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A few in the crowd began to chant it after him.\par \par \uc2 Touting the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s intent to restore reproductive rights, Walz referenced his own family\u8217\'20\'19s use of in vitro fertilization (IVF), which some Republican lawmakers have threatened to limit along with access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen my wife and I decided to have children, we spent years going through infertility treatments, and I remember praying every night for a call with good news,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. When we welcomed our daughter into the world, we named her Hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the vice president and I talk about freedom, we mean the freedom to make your own health care decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  also lavished praise on his fellow Democratic governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Shapiro had referenced his close friendship with Walz. Per the Philadelphia Inquirer\u8217\'20\'19s Julia Terruso, the two attended a Bruce Springsteen concert together.\par \par \uc2 enltrLittle background on Shapiro saying Walz is a good friend - sources familiar tell me they once attended a Springsteen concert in Jersey together.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Terruso (@JuliaTerruso) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaTerruso/status/1820937341566922935?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Walz confirmed this reporting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you this, I know this from experience, there is no one you would rather go to a Springsteen concert in Jersey with,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said of Shapiro.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz commends Harris's 'joy' in first speech as part of ticket\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for bringing back the joy,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said as he took the podium from Harris.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign said that it has raised $20m since Walz joined the ticket.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 As Harris spoke, the Democratic party confirmed that Harris and Walz were certified as the nominees for president and vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe announcement follows a transparent and democratic nominating process, during which delegates to the convention took seriously their responsibilities to cast their votes for our party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee \u8211\'20\'13 with 99% of participating delegates supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the virtual roll call,\u8221\'20\'1D the DNC noted in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe virtual roll call ensured that the Harris-Walz ticket has met all ballot access deadlines and every American will have the opportunity to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in the general election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is really into the football references today.\par \par \uc2 Comparing Walz\u8217\'20\'19s resume to that of JD Vance, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CWell some might say it\u8217\'20\'19s like, a matchup between the varsity team and the JV squad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a lengthy introduction, Harris is touting Walz\u8217\'20\'19s many facets \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s a hunter, and a gun owner, who has fought for gun safety laws: \u8220\'20\'1CHe was known as one of Capitol Hill\u8217\'20\'19s best marksmen,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s an advocate for reproductive rights: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Roe was overturned, he was the first governor in the country to sign a new law that enshrined reproductive freedom as a fundamental right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He supports voting rights: \u8220\'20\'1CHe signed the most significant expansion of voting rights in Minnesota in over 50 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Introducing Walz, Harris touts the governor\u8217\'20\'19s many roles: father, coach, congressman and sergeant major.\par \par \uc2 Walz, beaming behind her, seemed especially chuffed by her mention of his work as a football coach. Of course, there are few things as American as football (my apologies to our international readers rankled by this sentence).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder those Friday night lights, Coach Walz motivated his players to believe they could achieve anything, and together, they defied the odds,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris, hyping up her running mate.\par \par \uc2 She noted that Coach Walz was approached by a student who wanted to start a gay-straight alliance club at school, back in the 1990s. \u8220\'20\'1CTim knew the signal that it would send to have a football coach get involved. So he signed up as faculty adviser,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe made the school a safe place for everybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHold on, hold on,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told supporters who began to chant \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up\u8221\'20\'1D, co-opting the Maga rallying cry against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rivals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis campaign, our campaign, is not just a fight against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1COur campaign, this campaign, is a fight for the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris touts her official Democratic nomination and says 'we got some work to do'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who announced to the crowd that she was now the official Democratic nominee, having earned enough votes from Democratic delegates \u8211\'20\'13 began by acknowledging the long journey ahead: \u8220\'20\'1CNow we got some work to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the underdogs in this race, but we have the momentum, and I know exactly what we are up against,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz take the stage\par \par \uc2 The duo were played on by Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom, soaking in the roaring applause of thousands packed into the rally stadium.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re doing this!\u8221\'20\'1D Harris beamed.\par \par \uc2 Walz had a hand on his heart.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am more optimistic than ever before,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said \u8211\'20\'13 capturing a truly dizzying vibe shift among Democrats over the past two weeks.\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia, Shapiro also referenced the city\u8217\'20\'19s history as the birthplace of American independence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Independence Hall, just a couple miles from here, nearly two and a half centuries ago,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said, the founders declared independence from the British crown. \u8220\'20\'1CThey came together to declare our independence from a king and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going back to a king,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 An riled-up crowd is now chanting \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a weirdo\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 referencing \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s now iconic characterizations of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , in his beautiful midwestern plainspoken way, he summed up JD Vance the best. He\u8217\'20\'19s a weirdo,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said, encouraging the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  had referenced the same, effectively pithy insult.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about moving our country forward with Vice-President Harris and Governor Walz. Or a couple of really, really, really, really weird dudes,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CAnd look, I gotta tell you, I work with JD Vance \u8230\'20\'26 and I\u8217\'20\'19m here to confirm that he is a seriously weird dude.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me tell you about my friend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , someone I\u8217\'20\'19ve been friends with for two decades,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe is courtroom tough. She has a big heart and she is battle tested and ready to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shapiro is speaking to a riled-up crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CNot going back! Not going back!\u8221\'20\'1D the crowd chanted, as he brought up \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s record.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was more chaos, fewer jobs and less freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  speaks ahead of Harris and Walz debut\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love you Philly!\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro began. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8220\'20\'1CI love being your governor. You all fill my heart and I love you so much.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shapiro was considered a frontrunner for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, along with Walz.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for the first time on the campaign trail in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 The rally will mark Walz\u8217\'20\'19s first official campaign appearance since Harris selected him as her running mate earlier today, and for Walz will serve as an introduction to the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be prouder to be on this ticket, and to help make \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  the next president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he is expected to say, according to the campaign, which shared excerpts from his prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor will share about his upbringing in Butte, Nebraska \u8211\'20\'13 a small town of 400 \u8211\'20\'13 as well as his experiences as a teacher and an elected official.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Liacouras Center at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  in Philadelphia, crowds are filing in for a packed rally.\par \par \uc2 Sisters Stephanie Ford, 54, and Diane Harris, 59, said they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have believed it if someone told them one month ago they\u8217\'20\'19d be at a rally to support the first Black woman to lead a major party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 Harris \u8211\'20\'13 no relation to the vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 danced excitedly. She hadn\u8217\'20\'19t seen people this excited to vote since \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2008. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hope and change and newness,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Ford, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.phillytrib.com/news/business/local-shop-serves-up-coffee-and-camaraderie/article_191186bb-63e3-5797-a12d-233278af6646.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who runs a coffee shop}}}\uc2 , said she saw some of her customers in line on the way in.\par \par \uc2 Both said they were hoping Harris picked their governor, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , to be her running mate. \u8220\'20\'1CI was hoping it was him,\u8221\'20\'1D Ford said, as her sister nodded. \u8220\'20\'1CBut now we get to keep him for ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Neither had heard much about the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , who Harris announced on Tuesday would be her running mate. But they both said they liked what they were learning about him, especially what he\u8217\'20\'19s done to help children in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI trust her judgement,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a win-win for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Soon, Harris and Walz will appear together at a campaign rally in Philadelphia, which thousands of people are lining up to attend.\par \par \uc2 enltr??Philadelphia, PA\par \par \uc2 This is the line to get into the first Harris-Walz campaign event. There are thousands of people, the line wraps for blocks and blocks. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ASe0mwkZFW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ASe0mwkZFW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nidia (@NidiaCavazosTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NidiaCavazosTV/status/1820898444241764710?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/reel/C-VwcvHR0Ln/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Instagram Live}}}\uc2 , progressive representative \uc2 Alexandra Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said that Walz has helped unify Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really kind of nuts,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am trying to think about the last time Senator Manchin and I, respectfully, were on the same side of an issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDems in disconcerting levels of array {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F6fmqQK8DE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/F6fmqQK8DE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1820846151920230812?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Walz is hardly a leftist. But in Minnesota, progressives who\u8217\'20\'19ve clashed with him on policy issues are nonetheless rooting for him, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  reported:\par \par \uc2 Elianne Farhat, the executive director of TakeAction MN, said she and her organization had disagreed deeply with Walz over the years, but that he was a person who will move and change his position based on feedback. He evolves.\par \par \uc2 She and others pointed to his position on guns. Walz is a gun owner and a hunter who previously received endorsements and donations from the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  and had an A rating from the group. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/01/us/nra-tim-walz-guns.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he shifted}}}\uc2  : he gave donations from the group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/nra-money-tim-walz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to charity}}}\uc2  after the mass shooting in Las Vegas in 2017, and he supported an assault weapons ban after the 2018 school shooting in Parkland, Florida. While governor, he has signed bills into law that restrict guns. He now has an F rating from the \uc2 NRA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re not electing our saviors. We\u8217\'20\'19re not electing perfect people. We\u8217\'20\'19re electing people who we can make hard decisions with, we can negotiate with, and who are serious about getting things done for people. And Governor Walz has shown that pretty strongly the last couple years as governor of Minnesota,\u8217\'20\'19 Farhat said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign said it has raised more than $10m from grassroots supporters since announcing \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 The campaign released a video of Harris calling Walz to ask him to be her running mate.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen I called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Tim_Walz}}}\uc2  this morning to ask him to join our campaign, I shared my deep level of respect for him and the work we've done together.\par \par \uc2 We're going to unify this country and we're going to win.\par \par \uc2 Let's go get this done. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EcqZ497lyk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EcqZ497lyk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1820900959045685361?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here is where this eventful day in US politics stands so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic presidential nominee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , has selected \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate. Walz, the governor of Minnesota, and \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the governor of Pennsylvania, were reportedly the two finalists in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s search for a running mate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Walz will soon appear at a campaign rally in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, marking their first joint event since the running mate announcement. After the Philadelphia rally, Harris and Walz are scheduled to appear at a series of events in battleground states across the country in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she chose Walz because of his \u8220\'20\'1Cconvictions on fighting for middle-class families\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to build a great partnership,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to build a great team. We are going to win this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Walz thanked Harris for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe honor of a lifetime\u8221\'20\'1D by choosing him. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m all in,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said on X. \u8220\'20\'1CVice President Harris is showing us the politics of what\u8217\'20\'19s possible. It reminds me a bit of the first day of school. So, let\u8217\'20\'19s get this done, folks!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans attacked Walz as extreme, while Democrats praised him as a down-to-earth leader who can achieve change. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is a dangerously liberal extremist, and the Harris-Walz California dream is every American\u8217\'20\'19s nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D the Trump campaign said in a statement. But \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former Democratic House speaker, rejected that characterization. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right down the middle,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi told MSNBC. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a heartland-of-America Democrat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will participate in a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor interview\u8221\'20\'1D with billionaire and X owner Elon Musk on Monday, the former president announced in a social media post. The announcement comes one week after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calamitous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  at the annual convention of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 , where he questioned \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s race.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello from the Liacouras Center at \uc2 Temple University\uc2  in Philadelphia, where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will debut the freshly formed Democratic ticket later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The line to enter wrapped around the university for blocks, and supporters braved a downpour and some sticky summer weather to get inside.\par \par \uc2 There was plenty of excitement among the crowd. Spotted on my way in: several students wearing chartreuse-colored \u8220\'20\'1CKamala is Brat\u8221\'20\'1D shirts. Another woman wore a shirt with the play on words \u8220\'20\'1CAbout Madam time\u8221\'20\'1D to celebrate the possibility of sending the first woman to the White House.\par \par \uc2 enltrLong lines and menacing clouds to attend the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  campaign event in Philadelphia this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UBrbpXLHcY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UBrbpXLHcY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1820889629308117108?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst sighting of the Harris-Walz banners on their first stop of a multi-day battleground state tour. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9I1SGtxZa9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9I1SGtxZa9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1820900584926699720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to participate in 'major interview' with Elon Musk\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will participate in a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor interview\u8221\'20\'1D with billionaire and X owner Elon Musk on Monday, the former president announced in a social media post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CON MONDAY NIGHT I\u8217\'20\'19LL BE DOING A MAJOR INTERVIEW WITH ELON MUSK \u8212\'20\'14 Details to follow!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112916482094082129"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post}}}\uc2  shared to Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes one week after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calamitous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  at the annual convention of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 , where he questioned \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 race.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview was initially supposed to be an hour long, but it ended after just 34 minutes, as the audience jeered many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s responses. He will likely face an easier audience with Musk.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate Democratic leader, was having some fun at Republicans \u8217\'20\'19 expense this afternoon, after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  announced \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans have accused Harris of passing over \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the Pennsylvania governor, for the running mate spot because of his Jewish faith. If chosen, Shapiro could have become the first Jewish American to serve as vice president.\par \par \uc2 enltrNews to me {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VYCrhpfcdM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VYCrhpfcdM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1820870134283587624?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The rightwing commentator Erick Erickson said on X, \u8220\'20\'1CNo Jews allowed at the top of the Democratic Party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer, who is the first Jewish American to lead the Senate as majority leader, responded to Erickson by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CNews to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats also note that Harris is married to a Jewish man, Doug Emhoff, who could become the first Jewish spouse of a US president if the party wins the White House in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign releases new Walz video: 'We believe in the promise of America'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has released a new video introducing \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to the country, as most Americans are not yet familiar with the Minnesota governor.\par \par \uc2 The video, which is narrated by Walz, recounts his upbringing in Nebraska and his decision to join the national guard before he became a teacher and eventually a lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 The video, as well as Walz\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled campaign appearances in battleground states over the coming days, will provide many Americans with their first impression of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s new running mate. A recent ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/most-democrats-are-very-enthusiastic-about-kamala-harris-democratic-nominee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  showed that only 13% of Americans knew enough about Walz to register an opinion of him.\par \par \uc2 enltrGrowing up, I learned to be generous toward my neighbors, compromise without compromising my values, and to work for the common good. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  and I both believe in that common good \u8211\'20\'13 in that fundamental promise of America. We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to fight for it. And like she says:\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5SfrDRqx7C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5SfrDRqx7C}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@Tim_Walz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz/status/1820881730946977902?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here is the full transcript of the video:\par \par \uc2 Sometimes life is as much about the lessons you learn as the lessons you teach.\par \par \uc2 Where I grew up, community was a way of life.\par \par \uc2 My high school class was 24 people.\par \par \uc2 I was related to half of them.\par \par \uc2 I learned to be generous toward my neighbors, compromise without compromising my values, and to work for the common good.\par \par \uc2 My dad was in the army, and with his encouragement, I joined the army national guard when I was 17. I served for 24 years.\par \par \uc2 I used my GI benefits to go to college and become a public school teacher.\par \par \uc2 I coached football and taught social studies for 20 years.\par \par \uc2 And I tried to teach my students what small-town Nebraska taught me: respect, compromise and service to country.\par \par \uc2 And so when I went into government, that\u8217\'20\'19s what I carried with me. I worked with Republicans to pass an infrastructure bill. Cut taxes for working families. Signed paid leave into law. I codified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights after Roe got overturned.\par \par \uc2 Because I go to work for the common good.\par \par \uc2 But enough about me.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s talk about you. Because that\u8217\'20\'19s what this election is about.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s about your future. It\u8217\'20\'19s about your family.\par \par \uc2 And Vice-President Harris knows that. She too grew up in a middle-class family. She too goes to work every day, making sure families can not just get by but get ahead.\par \par \uc2 We believe in the promise of America. In those values I learned in Nebraska. And we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to fight for them.\par \par \uc2 Because as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says: when we fight we win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outside \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s residence in St Paul, TV cameras lined the street, with reporters doing live shots to explain how their governor had been tapped as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the morning, some supporters gathered to send off Walz with cheers as a black SUV whisked him off to the vice-presidential campaign trail, the local \uc2 CBS\uc2  outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 Midday, people on their morning walks and bike rides slowed down, trying to figure out what was happening that required so many cameras. Some took photos of the house, with grins on their faces. A car drove by, honking excitedly at the people gathered.\par \par \uc2 Terryann Nash, who lives across the street from the residence, said she saw security details increasing in recent weeks and wondered what was going on. The residence Walz is staying at is not the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, which is under construction, but a mansion that once housed the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president.\par \par \uc2 Nash, a teacher, was excited to see a fellow teacher on the ticket. \u8220\'20\'1CEven as a governor, he\u8217\'20\'19s always come back to the schools. He\u8217\'20\'19s always been in touch with the teachers. I feel like we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a well-represented voice and a very good heart to send us off,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  won plaudits from fellow Democrats for championing a new and surprisingly effective attack line against Republicans: they\u8217\'20\'19re \u8220\'20\'1Cjust weird\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s something wrong with people when they talk about freedom: freedom to be in your bedroom, freedom to be in your exam room, freedom to tell your kids what they can read,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said recently on MSNBC. \u8220\'20\'1CThat stuff is weird. They come across weird. They seem obsessed with this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Harris campaign event before he was named as her running mate, Walz told supporters, \u8220\'20\'1CThe fascists depend on fear. The fascists depend on us going back. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not afraid of weird people. We\u8217\'20\'19re a little bit creeped out, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not afraid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other prominent Democrats, including Harris, have now embraced the attack line. Watch this video showing the many examples of Walz\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D strategy:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, joined other members of his party in condemning \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cprogressive running mate who has voiced support for socialism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo amount of spin from the campaign or the media can distract from the objective facts and the disastrous records of Harris and Walz,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to highlighting the vast differences between the most radical leftwing ticket in American history and the America First agenda that President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  are fighting for every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats have rejected that characterization of Walz, with \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  telling MSNBC this morning: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right down the middle. He\u8217\'20\'19s a heartland-of-America Democrat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz en route to Philadelphia for campaign rally with Harris\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has left his residence in St Paul to make the trip to Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, where he will appear alongside \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a campaign rally this evening.\par \par \uc2 The rally will mark Walz\u8217\'20\'19s first official campaign appearance since Harris selected him as her running mate earlier today. Minnesotans gathered outside his residence to watch their governor depart.\par \par \uc2 After the Philadelphia rally, Harris and Walz are set to appear at a series of events in battleground states across the country \u8211\'20\'13 with stops planned in Wisconsin, Michigan, North Carolina, Georgia, Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the many progressive accomplishments of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor has quite an impressive record on voting rights.\par \par \uc2 Ever since Democrats gained full control of the state legislature in 2022, Walz and his fellow Democrats have enacted virtually every reform championed by voting rights groups. This includes:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Changing Minnesota law to allow people with a felony conviction to vote once they are released from prison (they previously had to complete probation and parole)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Enacting automatic voter registration and allowing 16- and 17-year-olds to pre-register to vote\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Allowing voters in Minnesota to sign up to automatically receive a mail-in ballot for each election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Approving a state-level Voting Rights Act to protect the interests of minority voters\par \par \uc2 Read more about Walz\u8217\'20\'19s record as governor:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/tim-walz-vp-beliefs-policies-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How could Tim Walz\u8217\'20\'19s political record help and hurt Harris?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has picked her running mate, and it is the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D, but will he be able to pull in enough support for Harris?\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Freedland is joined by the political commentator Molly Jong-Fast on a new episode of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Politics Weekly America podcast to discuss whether Harris made the right pick and if Republicans should be worried:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are mocking one particular part of the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s statement issued in response to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, the Trump campaign press secretary, said in the statement: \u8220\'20\'1CFrom proposing his own carbon-free agenda, to suggesting stricter emission standards for gas-powered cars, and embracing policies to allow convicted felons to vote, Walz is obsessed with spreading California\u8217\'20\'19s dangerously liberal agenda far and wide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz did indeed sign a bill last year making it easier for people with a felony conviction to vote in Minnesota. And Democrats noted that Trump himself could benefit from such a law, as he was recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted}}}\uc2  on 34 felony counts in New York.\par \par \uc2 One person {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nycsouthpaw/status/1820852690923970822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  on X: \u8220\'20\'1CIs it the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s position that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should not be allowed to vote?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin, an independent of West Virginia who caucuses with Democrats, offered a flattering review of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to tap \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy friend Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will bring normality back to the most chaotic political environment that most of us have ever seen,\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of the candidates were strong and any one of them would have been a great pick, but I can think of no one better than Governor Walz to help bring our country closer together and bring balance back to the Democratic party. Governor Walz is the real deal. I look forward to continuing to work with him to bring normalcy back to Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement is noteworthy considering Manchin has previously clashed with progressive Democrats. His praise could help Democrats rebut Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/06/kamala-harris-vp-running-mate-election-update?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66b22a678f089199ff7f2a6f#block-66b22a678f089199ff7f2a6f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  that Walz is a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerously liberal extremist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Labor leaders appear thrilled with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s choice of running mate, praising \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as a champion of working Americans who will help the next Democratic president deliver for the middle class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has been a great governor and is going to make a great vice-president. He\u8217\'20\'19s stood with the working class every step of the way, and has walked the walk, including on a \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line last fall,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shawn Fain, president of \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re ready to send \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to the White House to keep delivering for the working class, and we\u8217\'20\'19re excited to welcome them both to Detroit this week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2 , president of the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers\uc2 , described Walz as \u8220\'20\'1Can unabashed champion for families, for public education, for educators and other workers throughout his life in public service\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe knows the promise of public education. He shares our commitment to solving problems and forging a future in which all Americans can get ahead, not just get by,\u8221\'20\'1D Weingarten said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 AFT\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1.8 million members will stand with Walz and Harris over the next 12 weeks as they campaign to realize the promise and potential of America. We will hit the road to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance from coast to coast and keep their extremist policies out of the White House for good. The future starts here \u8211\'20\'13 and we are not going back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Public education advocates may be breathing a sigh of relief that Harris did not choose \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  as her running mate, considering the Pennsylvania governor\u8217\'20\'19s past support for private school vouchers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has released a new ad attacking \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cleftwing extremist\u8221\'20\'1D, echoing previous criticisms of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just doubled down on her radical vision for America,\u8221\'20\'1D the ad\u8217\'20\'19s narrator says. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will be a rubber stamp for Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s dangerously liberal agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ad concludes: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 : they\u8217\'20\'19re failed, weak and dangerously liberal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The full ad is here:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Walz: Another Left-Wing Extremist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0Dv2m4cNH2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0Dv2m4cNH2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Team Trump (Text TRUMP to 88022) (@TeamTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamTrump/status/1820825907839586651?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance says he left Walz a voicemail congratulating him\par \par \uc2 Republican vice-presidential nominee JD Vance said he left a voicemail congratulating \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  on his selection as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI actually called \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . I left a voicemail. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t get him,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1820847163301356006"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I just said, look, congratulations. Look forward to a robust conversation. Enjoy the ride. And maybe he\u8217\'20\'19ll call me back, maybe he won\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped out of the presidential race, Harris had accepted an invitation from CBS News to debate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate in mid-August. But the timing and venue of a vice-presidential debate is now up in the air.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls on Americans to rally behind Harris and Walz\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate, encouraging all Americans to rally behind the new Democratic nominee after he dropped out of the presidential race last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve known \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  for nearly two decades, first during his time in Congress and as Governor,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said on X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA husband and father, he\u8217\'20\'19s been a school teacher and a high school football coach. He served for 24 years in the Army National Guard and became the highest ranking enlisted soldier to ever serve in Congress. As Governor, he\u8217\'20\'19s been a strong, principled, and effective leader.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe first major decision a party nominee makes is their choice for Vice President. And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has made a great decision in choosing Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to be her running mate.\par \par \uc2 I've known \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  for nearly two decades, first during his time in Congress and as Governor. A\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1820844887761158325?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden went on to say:\par \par \uc2 The Harris-Walz ticket will be a powerful voice for working people and America\u8217\'20\'19s great middle class. They will be the strongest defenders of our personal freedoms and our democracy. And they will ensure that America continues to lead the world and play its role as the indispensable nation.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s time for all Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 and indeed all Americans \u8211\'20\'13 committed to freedom, democracy, and American leadership in the world to rally behind the Harris-Walz ticket.\par \par \uc2 Every generation of Americans faces a moment where they are asked to defend American democracy. That moment is now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where this busy day in US politics stands so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic presidential nominee, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , has selected \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate. Walz, the governor of Minnesota, and \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the governor of Pennsylvania, were reportedly the two finalists in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s search for a running mate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said she chose Walz because of his \u8220\'20\'1Cconvictions on fighting for middle-class families\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to build a great partnership,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to build a great team. We are going to win this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Walz thanked Harris for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe honor of a lifetime\u8221\'20\'1D by choosing him. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m all in,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said on X. \u8220\'20\'1CVice President Harris is showing us the politics of what\u8217\'20\'19s possible. It reminds me a bit of the first day of school. So, let\u8217\'20\'19s get this done, folks!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans attacked Walz as extreme, while Democrats praised him as a down-to-earth leader who can achieve change. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is a dangerously liberal extremist, and the Harris-Walz California dream is every American\u8217\'20\'19s nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D the Trump campaign said in a statement. But \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former Democratic House speaker, rejected that characterization. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right down the middle,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi told MSNBC. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a heartland-of-America Democrat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dharna Noor reports on green advocates\u8217\'20\'19 praise for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as a climate champion:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike Vice-President Harris, Governor Walz knows that climate change is the existential threat of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 the Sierra Club\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Ben Jealous, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Supporters say his robust climate record as governor of Minnesota shows what Walz can bring to the presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, Walz signed a law mandating that Minnesota generate all of its electricity from carbon-free sources by 2040, setting one of the strongest climate standards in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis law, even more ambitious than similar measures in traditionally progressive states, showcases the kind of forward-thinking leadership our country needs to address the worsening climate crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cassidy DiPaola, communications director for Fossil Free Media, a non-profit pushing for the swift transition away from fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 In June, Walz also signed a policy meant to speed the implementation of the 2040 clean power mandate by streamlining energy permitting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a measure that will help protect our environment and get the clean energy projects that are going to help fight climate change in motion,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LIUNAMinnesota/status/1806472214541107665"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obamas on Walz: '\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has chosen an ideal partner'\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  released a statement celebrating \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate, praising the Minnesota governor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cability to talk like a human being and treat everyone with decency and respect\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a presidential candidate chooses a running mate, it says a lot about who they are and what kind of president they\u8217\'20\'19ll be,\u8221\'20\'1D the Obamas said. \u8220\'20\'1CDo they pick someone inexperienced and polarizing who will deepen our divisions? Or do they pick someone with the judgment to make tough decisions, and the character to believe that every voice counts and everyone deserves an equal chance?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That second question appeared to be a thinly veiled dig at the Republican vice-presidential nominee, JD Vance, a freshman senator from Ohio who has attracted criticism for his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and those without children.\par \par \uc2 The Obamas went on to say:\par \par \uc2 By selecting \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to be her vice-president from a pool of outstanding Democrats, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has chosen an ideal partner \u8211\'20\'13 and made it clear exactly what she stands for.\par \par \uc2 Governor Walz doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just have the experience to be vice-president, he has the values and the integrity to make us proud. As governor, Tim helped families and businesses recover from the pandemic, established paid family leave, guaranteed the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and put common sense gun safety measures in place to keep communities safe. But Tim\u8217\'20\'19s signature is his ability to talk like a human being and treat everyone with decency and respect \u8211\'20\'13 not all that surprising considering the fact that he served in the national guard for 24 years and worked as a high school social studies teacher and football coach before being elected to Congress.\par \par \uc2 Like Vice-President Harris, Governor Walz believes that government works to serve us. Not just some of us, but all of us. That\u8217\'20\'19s what makes him an outstanding governor, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what will make him an even better vice-president, ready on day one. Michelle and I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be happier for Tim and Gwen, their family and our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite the popularity of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , in the battleground state, progressives said his policy background gave them pause, and a number of them publicly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4800359-kamala-harris-josh-shapiro-andy-beshear-tim-walz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to choose a different running-mate before she announced her decision.\par \par \uc2 In particular, Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s response to the war in Gaza had sparked criticism on the left. Progressives note that Shapiro has not embraced calls for a ceasefire in Gaza, and he made controversial comments about pro-Palestinian protests on college campuses earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what\u8217\'20\'19s important is that we can\u8217\'20\'19t allow peaceful protest about a disagreement on policy happening in the Middle East to be an excuse for antisemitism or Islamophobia on these campuses,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/completely-out-of-control-pennsylvania-governor-slams-pro-palestinian-protests-at-columbia-urges-school-to-restore-order/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  in April. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to query whether or not we would tolerate this, if this were people dressed up in [\uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2 ] outfits or KKK regalia making comments about people who are African-American in our communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Progressives\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about Shapiro extended beyond the war in Gaza. Last year, Shapiro backed a Republican proposal to provide Pennsylvania with $100m in private school vouchers. The issue of \u8220\'20\'1Cschool choice\u8221\'20\'1D has become a rallying cry on the right, while Democrats have consistently stressed the importance of investing in public education to provide more opportunities to all students.\par \par \uc2 After his pro-voucher stance attracted intense scrutiny from fellow Democrats, Shapiro vetoed the program out of the state budget. With \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate, Harris will not need to worry about progressives\u8217\'20\'19 criticism of Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s record.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats had argued that the Pennsylvania governor, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , would offer a strategic advantage as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate because of his popularity in a key battleground state.\par \par \uc2 Even though evidence is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/politics/363899/kamala-harris-vp-pick-josh-shapiro-walz-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mixed}}}\uc2  as to whether vice-presidential nominees can help deliver their home states, Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s high approval rating had raised Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 expectations of a polling bump in Pennsylvania. The governor has a favorability rating of 61%, according to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/official-polls/fox-news-poll-harris-trump-dead-heat-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News poll}}}\uc2 , and he has consistently outperformed fellow Democrats in the perennial battleground state.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  carried Pennsylvania by 0.7 points, Shapiro won his race for state attorney general by 3 points. When \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the state by 1.2 points in 2020, Shapiro secured re-election with a 5-point victory. And in 2022, Shapiro easily won his gubernatorial race by 15 points, while Democratic Senate candidate \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  defeated his opponent by 5 points.\par \par \uc2 But Harris decided to instead pick Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , as her running mate , even though his state is much less significant in the electoral map. In 2020, Biden won Minnesota by 7 points compared with his 1-point victory in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz thanks Harris for 'the honor of a lifetime' as running mate\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , expressed gratitude to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after she selected him as her running mate in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is the honor of a lifetime to join @kamalaharris in this campaign. I\u8217\'20\'19m all in,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said on X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice President Harris is showing us the politics of what\u8217\'20\'19s possible. It reminds me a bit of the first day of school. So, let\u8217\'20\'19s get this done, folks! Join us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is the honor of a lifetime to join {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kamalaharris}}}\uc2  in this campaign.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m all in.\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris is showing us the politics of what\u8217\'20\'19s possible. It reminds me a bit of the first day of school.\par \par \uc2 So, let\u8217\'20\'19s get this done, folks! Join us. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tqOVsw2OLM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tqOVsw2OLM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@Tim_Walz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz/status/1820830898494791955?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shapiro: 'My work here in Pennsylvania is far from finished'\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , reaffirmed his commitment to getting Democrats elected in November, after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  decided not to choose him as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Reports indicated that Shapiro and Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , were the two finalists in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s search for a running mate, and she ultimately chose Walz.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy work here in Pennsylvania is far from finished \u8212\'20\'14 there is a lot more stuff I want to get done for our Commonwealth.\par \par \uc2 Over the next 90 days, I look forward to traveling all across the Commonwealth to unite Pennsylvanians behind my friends \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and defeat\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Mkc1isQTo9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Mkc1isQTo9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  (@JoshShapiroPA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoshShapiroPA/status/1820827281658446166?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Shapiro, who could have been the first Jewish American to serve as vice-president, invoked his faith as he explained the path forward for him and his family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy life in public service has always been motivated by my family and my faith,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said in a new statement. \u8220\'20\'1CSince I first ran for state representative 20 years ago, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been called to serve because I want to leave our community, our commonwealth and our country better off for our children \u8211\'20\'13 and because my faith teaches me that no one is required to complete the task, but neither are we free to refrain from it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to say:\par \par \uc2 Nearly two weeks ago, Vice-President Harris asked me to work with her team to complete the vetting process to be considered as her running mate \u8211\'20\'13 and following those conversations, on Sunday, I was grateful to have the opportunity to speak with the vice-president directly about her vision for the role and the campaign ahead.\par \par \uc2 As I\u8217\'20\'19ve said repeatedly over the past several weeks, the running mate decision was a deeply personal decision for the vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 and it was also a deeply personal decision for me. Pennsylvanians elected me to a four-year term as their governor, and my work here is far from finished \u8211\'20\'13 there is a lot more stuff I want to get done for the good people of this commonwealth.\par \par \uc2 Serving as the 48th governor of the commonwealth of Pennsylvania is the highest honor of my life \u8211\'20\'13 showing up in your communities, listening to and learning from you, and then working across the aisle to get stuff done and deliver results for you. In just 19 months, we\u8217\'20\'19ve made a meaningful, positive impact in peoples\u8217\'20\'19 lives, and I\u8217\'20\'19m proud of how Americans all across the country have taken notice of what we\u8217\'20\'19re accomplishing here in Pennsylvania. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited to continue working to protect and advance real freedom, deliver good schools, safe communities and economic opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has my enthusiastic support \u8211\'20\'13 and I know that Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is an exceptionally strong addition to the ticket who will help Kamala move our country forward. Lori and I consider Tim and Gwen to be good friends of ours and we are excited for them and for the country to get to know the great people we know them to be. Over the next 90 days, I look forward to traveling all across the commonwealth to unite Pennsylvanians behind \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , become the 47th president of the United States and build a better future for our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris confirms Walz as running mate: 'We are going to win this election'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has confirmed her selection of Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , as her running mate via an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/C-VNhQYO01b/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA=="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Instagram post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am proud to announce that I\u8217\'20\'19ve asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/walzforgovernor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @walzforgovernor}}}\uc2  to be my running mate,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1COne of the things that stood out to me about Tim is how his convictions on fighting for middle-class families run deep. It\u8217\'20\'19s personal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She went on to say:\par \par \uc2 He grew up in a small town in Nebraska, spending summers working on his family\u8217\'20\'19s farm. His father died of cancer when he was 19, and his family relied on Social Security survivor benefit checks to make ends meet. At 17, he enlisted in the National Guard, serving for 24 years. He used his GI Bill benefits to go to college, and become a teacher. He served as both the football coach and the advisor of the Gay-Straight Alliance.\par \par \uc2 I share this background both because it\u8217\'20\'19s impressive in its own right, and because you see in no uncertain terms how it informs his record. He worked with Republicans to pass infrastructure investments. He cut taxes for working families. He passed a law to provide paid family and medical leave to Minnesotan families.\par \par \uc2 He made Minnesota the first state in the country to pass a law providing constitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v Wade, and as an avid hunter, he passed a bill requiring universal background checks for gun purchases.\par \par \uc2 But what impressed me most about Tim is his deep commitment to his family: Gwen, Gus and Hope. Doug and I look forward to working with him and Gwen to build an administration that reflects our shared values.\par \par \uc2 Whether you are a supporter, a volunteer, a donor, a member of our staff or your name is on the ticket: you are part of the people-powered campaign that is going to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We are going to build a great partnership. We are going to build a great team. We are going to win this election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign attacks Walz as 'dangerously liberal extremist'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign has released a new statement attacking \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerously liberal extremist\u8221\'20\'1D, lambasting the policy agenda he has pursued as governor of Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 Since Minnesota Democrats secured a legislative trifecta in the 2022 elections, Walz has signed a series of progressive bills protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, expanding background checks for gun purchases and legalizing recreational marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that San Francisco liberal \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wants west coast wannabe \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running-mate \u8211\'20\'13 Walz has spent his governorship trying to reshape Minnesota in the image of the Golden state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Karoline Leavitt, the Trump campaign press secretary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom proposing his own carbon-free agenda to suggesting stricter emission standards for gas-powered cars and embracing policies to allow convicted felons to vote, Walz is obsessed with spreading California\u8217\'20\'19s dangerously liberal agenda far and wide. If Walz won\u8217\'20\'19t tell voters the truth, we will: just like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is a dangerously liberal extremist, and the Harris-Walz California dream is every American\u8217\'20\'19s nightmare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more background information on \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Walz has served as Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor since 2019 after 12 years in the House of Representatives and now chairs the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2 . He has built a reputation as a folksy politician who can get things done, as Minnesota has adopted a number of progressive laws during his tenure. According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kaaltv.com/news/approval-rates-for-minnesota-leaders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  conducted earlier this year, Walz enjoys an approval rating of 55% among Minnesotans.\par \par \uc2 Since Minnesota Democrats achieved a legislative trifecta in the 2022 elections, Walz and his allies have used their power to push a slate of progressive policies. The governor has signed bills protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, expanding background checks for prospective gun owners and legalizing recreational marijuana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, Minnesota is showing the country you don\u8217\'20\'19t win elections to bank political capital,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said last year. \u8220\'20\'1CYou win elections to burn political capital and improve lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That philosophy has endeared him to progressives, who threw their support behind him as the veepstakes kicked into high gear over the past two weeks. They reshared clips of Walz lovingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/kendallybrown/status/1816957619812049040"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocking}}}\uc2  his daughter\u8217\'20\'19s vegetarianism and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mattwagenius/status/1820507813669396846"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tinkering}}}\uc2  with his car to paint him as the dad that America needs right now.\par \par \uc2 But as the running mate, Walz will need to introduce himself to a much wider audience. A recent ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/most-democrats-are-very-enthusiastic-about-kamala-harris-democratic-nominee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  showed that only 13% of Americans knew enough about Walz to register an opinion of him.\par \par \uc2 Read more about Walz\u8217\'20\'19s background:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/tim-walz-vp-beliefs-policies-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How could Tim Walz\u8217\'20\'19s political record help and hurt Harris?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi praises Walz as 'heartland-of-America Democrat'\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former Democratic House speaker, joined MSNBC to celebrate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4806591-tim-walz-harris-vp-house-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  been leaning toward Walz in the veepstakes, as the two of them served in the House together for 12 years.\par \par \uc2 Appearing on Morning Joe, Pelosi fiercely rejected any characterization of Walz as an out-of-touch progressive, as many Republicans are trying to paint him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo characterize [\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ] as left is so unreal,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s right down the middle. He\u8217\'20\'19s a heartland-of-America Democrat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Minnesota attorney general Keith Ellison praised \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as an effective leader who would help \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  pave a path to victory in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have worked alongside one another for almost 20 years, so I can say with confidence that there is no better choice for vice-president of the United States of America. Tim has the courage of a veteran, the compassion of a school teacher, the grit of a football coach, and the experience of both a congressman and governor,\u8221\'20\'1D Ellison said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are true public servants who have spent their lives working tirelessly on behalf of the American people. Plus, they are both big-hearted, jovial people with great senses of humor and boundless optimism. I look forward to campaigning vigorously for the Harris-Walz ticket, and I cannot wait to see what Kamala and Tim accomplish on behalf of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans seem to be pleased as well that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has chosen \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne Conway, former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KellyannePolls/status/1820810402332090561"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on X: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ? What a relief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House majority whip, \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 , who is also a Minnesota resident, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/tomemmer/status/1820807524724916300"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWalz is an empty suit who has worked to turn Minnesota into Harris\u8217\'20\'19d home state of California, and solidifies this ticket\u8217\'20\'19s full embrace of a radical, America-last agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brendan Buck, who served as an adviser to \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 , the former Republican House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BrendanBuck/status/1820805919313121750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe VP doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter a ton but I think this reflects very poorly on her decision making \u8230\'20\'26 Feels very 2019. Tell the internet what it wants to hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrats celebrate selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\par \par \uc2 Progressives are celebrating the selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 running mate, praising the Minnesota governor\u8217\'20\'19s policy record and ability to directly confront Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is an effortless populist and represents the exact direction the Democratic party needs,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stephanie Taylor, co-founder of the Progressive Change Campaign Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CWalz has proven that he has the necessary skills and authentic populism to go on offense \u8211\'20\'13 calling out the extremist and weird Trump-Vance agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joseph Geevarghese, executive director of Our Revolution, said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CThe selection of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as the vice-presidential nominee is a clear indication that the Harris campaign is listening to the voices of progressives across the country. Governor Walz\u8217\'20\'19s strong pro-labor record and dedication to working-class issues align with our movement\u8217\'20\'19s goals to take on corporate power and create an economy that works for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies are already coming out swinging against \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , just minutes after reports first emerged that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  had selected the Minnesota governor as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 The pro-Trump Super Pac Make America Great Again Inc said in a press release, \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will get along just great. They\u8217\'20\'19re both far-left radicals that don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to govern.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Pac pointed to some of the progressive bills that Walz has signed into law and the unrest that engulfed Minneapolis in 2020, after the murder of George Floyd by a white police officer, to paint the governor as an \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetent liberal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will formally introduce \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate at a rally in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, later today.\par \par \uc2 Harris and the Minnesota governor will then take a tour of battleground states in the days ahead, with stops planned in Wisconsin, Michigan, North Carolina, Georgia, Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  names \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as vice-presidential pick for 2024 US election\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has selected Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate in the presidential race, the AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-vp-pick-election-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The widely anticipated announcement comes one day after Harris officially secured the Democratic nomination following a virtual roll call vote of the party\u8217\'20\'19s delegates.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who is the first woman of color to serve as a major party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, will formally accept the nomination at the Democratic convention in Chicago later this month, where she and Walz will both deliver speeches.\par \par \uc2 More details to come \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris picks Walz as running mate \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has reportedly selected \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor, as her running mate in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Four sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/kamala-harris-trump-election-08-06-24#h_a1cb3a353c1e0655524a827af0197796"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  that Walz was the pick, but the Harris campaign has not yet officially announced her decision.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor who is on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 shortlist of potential running mates, held a fundraiser for her campaign in Minneapolis last night.\par \par \uc2 Walz has won praise for mocking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his running mate, JD Vance, as \u8220\'20\'1Cweird,\u8221\'20\'1D an attack line that has now been picked up by Harris. At the fundraiser, Walz told attendees that Democrats need to embrace the \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitics of joy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got to run this campaign against the serious threat that\u8217\'20\'19s there, but we have to do it every single day with a sense of joy,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and ban certain books in US schools, Walz added, \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a slur to call these guys weird \u8230\'20\'26 It was an observation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vance: antisemitism to blame if Harris doesn't pick Shapiro\par \par \uc2 Republican vice-presidential nominee JD Vance spoke to conservative radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  this morning and weighed in on the Democratic veepstakes.\par \par \uc2 Hewitt said he would be \u8220\'20\'1Cshocked\u8221\'20\'1D if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did not select \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the Pennsylvania governor who could become the first Jewish-American to serve as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Vance agreed, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI think that they will have not picked Shapiro, frankly, out of antisemitism in their own caucus and in their own party. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s disgraceful the Democrats have gotten to this point where it\u8217\'20\'19s even an open conversation, and it is an open conversation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1CEven if it is \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the guy has, in some ways, had to run away from a lot of his biography over the last few months because the far left doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like the fact that he is a Jewish American. So look, we have to be honest about this fact. We have to call it out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s critics have fiercely rejected any suggestion of antisemitism on their part, arguing that their concerns lie with the governor\u8217\'20\'19s views on education and the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro has previously voiced strong support for Israel and made some controversial comments about pro-Palestinian protests on college campuses earlier this year. He also enraged public school advocates by supporting a private school voucher program, although he later vetoed that proposal under pressure from fellow Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on Shapiro:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/02/josh-shapiro-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Josh Shapiro, Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s potential vice-presidential pick?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate announcement, Americans in some states are heading to the polls today.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Kansas, Michigan, Missouri and Washington state will cast ballots in their congressional primaries today. Results in Michigan will be especially scrutinized, as the battleground state will play a key role in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, the progressive congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  is facing a primary threat from her fellow Democrat Wesley Bell, whose campaign has benefited from millions of dollars spent by pro-Israel groups. Their efforts come after Bush became one of the first members of Congress to call for a ceasefire in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Chris McGreal reports:\par \par \uc2 The American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2  (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ) pumped more than $8.5m into the race in Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district in support of Bush\u8217\'20\'19s rival, St Louis prosecutor Wesley Bell, through its campaign funding arm, the United Democracy Project (UDP). \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The UDP accounts for more than half of all the money spent on the race outside of the campaigns themselves. Much of it comes from billionaires who fund hardline pro-Israel causes and Republicans in other races, including some who have given to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 The UDP\u8217\'20\'19s spending to oust Bush is second only to the money it poured into a successful campaign to defeat another member of the \u8216\'20\'18Squad\u8217\'20\'19, New York congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 , in a Democratic primary in June.\par \par \uc2 Read Chris\u8217\'20\'19 full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/missouri-cori-bush-primary-bell-aipac-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-Israel groups spend millions to try to oust \u8216\'20\'18Squad\u8217\'20\'19 member Cori Bush}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the statement from the DNC chair, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , and the DNCC chair, Minyon Moore.\par \par \uc2 With the support of 99% of all participating delegates in the virtual roll call, Vice-President Harris has historic momentum at her back as we embark on the final steps in officially certifying her as our Party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 We thank the thousands of delegates from all across the country who took seriously their responsibility throughout this process to make their voices \u8211\'20\'13 and the voices of their communities \u8211\'20\'13 heard.\par \par \uc2 As we prepare to certify the nomination alongside Convention Secretary Rae, we know that we are all a part of an important piece of history. Soon, it will be time to come together in Chicago, where we will celebrate together and make clear to the American people that the Democratic Party is the party of freedom, of democracy, of rights, and of the people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  officially becomes Democratic nominee\par \par \uc2 Democratic delegates selected \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president, to be the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, according to final vote results released late Monday by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Harris received nearly 4,600 votes in the five-day online voting process, which the DNC said was 99% of participating delegates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s resume stands out in the sea of lawyers that dominate Washington.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona senator was a US navy pilot who served multiple deployments. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.space.com/29397-astronaut-mark-kelly-celebrity-jeopardy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was on Celebrity Jeopardy}}}\uc2 . He is a steadfast partner to his wife, former US representative \uc2 Gabrielle Giffords\uc2 , who survived an assassination attempt at a public event in Tucson in 2011 and has worked alongside Kelly to limit guns since.\par \par \uc2 Oh, and he\u8217\'20\'19s been to space multiple times because he was an astronaut, along with his twin brother, Scott. He even wrote a children\u8217\'20\'19s book about it, called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Mousetronaut-Based-Partially-Story-Wiseman/dp/1442458240"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mousetronaut}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn astronaut! Who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like astronauts, except for Flat Earthers, right? But they\u8217\'20\'19re very small in quantity,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  pollster Mike Noble said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, outside of Flat Earthers, I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to think of what\u8217\'20\'19s more American than astronauts. Astronaut takes everybody. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been to space, what have you done?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/mark-kelly-potential-kamala-harris-vp-pick"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of insight into \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s communication style. In 2019, he published this video with his daughter explaining a new law.\par \par \uc2 enltrHey Minnesota! Today the new hands-free law goes into effect. ??????\par \par \uc2 My daughter, Hope, and I put our car in park to give some tips on going hands-free and show just how distracting phones can be. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/OneMinnesota?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #OneMinnesota}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HandsFreeMN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HandsFreeMN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MqW4Zqfy5o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MqW4Zqfy5o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@GovTimWalz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovTimWalz/status/1156926207755079682?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 1, 2019}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s governor captured the internet\u8217\'20\'19s attention and swayed Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 messaging by succinctly summing up how he views Republicans: they\u8217\'20\'19re weird.\par \par \uc2 Clips of Walz have spread widely, cementing him as a national voice for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign \u8211\'20\'13 and a potential pick to run alongside her as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Walz, 60, was born and raised in small-town Nebraska. He became a teacher, first in China, then in Nebraska and finally in Mankato, Minnesota, where he taught geography and coached the high school football team. He also served in the army national guard for 24 years, enlisting at age 17, a role that took him around the country and on a deployment to Europe.\par \par \uc2 Walz first ran for office in 2006 in a Republican-leaning congressional district, knocking off the incumbent in an upset. He kept the district until 2016, dispatching Republicans over and over. In 2018, he ran for governor and won, then defended the seat successfully in 2022.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s now the chair of the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2 , a perch that has given him a national profile.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/who-is-tim-walz-potential-vp-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59am BST\par \par \uc2 As speculation mounted about his political future, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  was spotted yesterday playing basketball with one of his children.\par \par \uc2 enltrPA Gov. \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  is home in Montgomery County tonight, playing basketball w/his son, as we wait to hear if he is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 running mate.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro is one of the finalists said to be under consideration. Harris\u8217\'20\'19 first stop w/her pick will be in Philadelphia tomorrow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/6abc?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @6abc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8jAZ3cmVr0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8jAZ3cmVr0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Goggin (@CarolineGoggin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolineGoggin/status/1820605612318703802?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some recent images of \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the governor of Pennsylvania who is a leading contender to be named \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Shapiro, the governor of Pennsylvania, is a leading contender to be named \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 A congressional aide turned state representative and state attorney general, the 51-year-old father of four was elected governor in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Close to two years later, he maintains historically high approval ratings, including notable support from Republicans, his numbers outstripping such ratings both for Harris and for the GOP ticket of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, the declaration of victory in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  confirmed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win over Trump.\par \par \uc2 In 2024, the state is again one of the most important presidential battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Harris will stage her first event with her vice-presidential pick in Philadelphia, the state\u8217\'20\'19s biggest city: a move that did little to quell speculation that Shapiro will be that pick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/02/josh-shapiro-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full profile}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to announce VP pick\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is set to announce her choice of a running mate today, before they appear together at an evening rally in Philadelphia to kick off a five-day tour of the swing states that are crucial to winning the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The culmination of what has been a lightning-fast vetting process \u8211\'20\'13 it is little more than two weeks since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the 81-year-old president, made the historic decision to stand aside and Harris became the de facto nominee \u8211\'20\'13 has seen a round of interviews both in person and online.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Reuters reported that the search had narrowed to two governors: \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  of Pennsylvania and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  of Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 Harris, 59, interviewed both men, as well as the Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , over the weekend at the Naval Observatory, the Washington DC residence of the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Three other men were reported to be on her shortlist: the Illinois governor, \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2  ; the Kentucky governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  ; and \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the former mayor of South Bend, Indiana, who is now the US secretary of transportation.\par \par \uc2 With polling showing her gaining on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 CBS\uc2  gave the Democrat a one-point edge nationally and put the candidates level in battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 and a rocky rollout for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, speculation has been rife as to whom Harris will select.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/kamala-harris-vp-pick-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240806ek860018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
