\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Project 2025: rightwing manifesto\u8217\'20\'19s key proposals and how they could affect you\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,944 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2024\par 13:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Blueprint\uc2  outlines extreme, conservative policies for a potential second Trump term and beyond\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve probably heard of Project 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 either from Democrats such as the vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , warning of what it could mean for \uc2 US government\uc2 , or from Republicans such as former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  claiming they have nothing to do with it.\par \par \uc2 The project is an effort by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Heritage Foundation}}}\uc2 , a prominent rightwing thinktank, to dismantle features of the government it believes conflict with conservative ideology and to install extreme, conservative policies in a potential second Trump term and beyond.\par \par \uc2 Its director, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/project-2025-director-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paul Dans}}}\uc2 , stepped down from his role this week and said some of the project\u8217\'20\'19s work would be \u8220\'20\'1Cwinding down\u8221\'20\'1D, though it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what that looks like in practice \u8211\'20\'13 the ideas aren\u8217\'20\'19t going away. Dans\u8217\'20\'19s departure came after pressure from the Trump campaign, which said \u8220\'20\'1Creports of Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s demise would be greatly welcomed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/08/trump-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has disavowed the project}}}\uc2  and has said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know anything about it, though it was written by many who worked in his administration, and shares many of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/project-2025-trump-connections-similarities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 policy goals}}}\uc2 . His vice-president pick, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , has close ties with \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and its president, Kevin Roberts; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/jd-vance-project-2025-book-foreword"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance even wrote the foreword}}}\uc2  for Roberts\u8217\'20\'19 new book.\par \par \uc2 The first part of Project 2025 is a 900-plus page {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24088042-project-2025s-mandate-for-leadership-the-conservative-promise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 manifesto}}}\uc2 , which lays out all the changes that the more than 100 conservative groups on board want to see happen if Trump wins again. Subsequent parts will include suggesting personnel and training them on how the government should work.\par \par \uc2 So what\u8217\'20\'19s actually in the manifesto?\par \par \uc2 Education\par \par \uc2 The Project 2025 manifesto suggests a conservative president should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/article/2024/jul/04/trump-project-2025-heritage-foundation-education-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismantle the Department of Education}}}\uc2 , an idea that Trump has also supported. At most, it says, the department should be a \u8220\'20\'1Cstatistics-gathering agency that disseminates information to the states\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It wants to phase out Title I funding that goes to low-income schools. And it would allow states to spend federal education money without direction, giving states leeway to use money meant for a specific purpose for whatever they want as long as it relates to education.\par \par \uc2 The project says a conservative president should push policies to support universal voucher programs, in which public money meant for public schools funds private school tuitions.\par \par \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2  also wants to eliminate Head Start, a program that funds early childhood education for low-income families. The left-leaning \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2  says in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/project-2025-would-eliminate-head-start-severely-restricting-access-to-child-care-in-rural-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report}}}\uc2  that eliminating Head Start would reduce access and increase costs for childcare, hurting economic stability.\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t explicitly call for a national {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban, but the policy ideas it advocates would aggressively limit access to abortions across the country.\par \par \uc2 The manifesto suggests the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  should rename itself the Department of Life, \u8220\'20\'1Cexplicitly rejecting the notion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is health care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It calls for eliminating \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) programs that \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not respect human life and conscience rights and that undermine family formation\u8221\'20\'1D. The health department would not consider \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be healthcare and would fund studies about the \u8220\'20\'1Crisks and complications\u8221\'20\'1D of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also says the CDC should help promote \u8220\'20\'1Cfertility awareness\u8221\'20\'1D methods of family planning.\par \par \uc2 It proposes to collect data on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the states, \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  survivors\u8221\'20\'1D and maternal deaths related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . States that don\u8217\'20\'19t share data on abortions within their borders would see federal funds withheld \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause liberal states have now become sanctuaries for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tourism\u8221\'20\'1D. This data collection would include demographics to assess whether any groups are targeted by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 The use of mifepristone and misoprostol, the two pills that together provide a chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would be curtailed. The project wants the Food and Drug Administration to reverse its approval of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 As an \u8220\'20\'1Cinterim step\u8221\'20\'1D, the government should outlaw telemedicine for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care or the mail ordering of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which the project calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca gift to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It also says that US health policies \u8220\'20\'1Cshould never place the desires of adults over the right of children to be raised by the biological fathers and mothers who conceive them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Diversity issues\par \par \uc2 Attacks on diversity programs and the rights of LGBTQ+ people are infused throughout Project 2025. Nearly all agency-specific chapters mention that any efforts to promote diversity or recognize the existence of LGBTQ+ people should be ended.\par \par \uc2 The project also calls for the government to protect the ability of people to refuse to participate in same-sex unions or gender - affirming care, allowing businesses, healthcare workers and adoption agencies to discriminate if something goes against their conscience. It wants to reverse policies that include sexual orientation as a protected class for discrimination and end collection of data on non-binary people.\par \par \uc2 The manifesto generally labels these initiatives \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D and wants to drive them out. The manifesto defines marriage as between a man and a woman and wants to see policies that promote \u8220\'20\'1Cstable, married, nuclear families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Its education section calls for scrapping LGBTQ+ and diversity-focused programs, eliminating trans girls\u8217\'20\'19 ability to play in girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports, and preventing kids from using names or pronouns different from their birth certificate without parental approval.\par \par \uc2 Federal workers\par \par \uc2 One of the project\u8217\'20\'19s largest changes would install far more political appointees beholden to a conservative president\u8217\'20\'19s agenda to all levels of government, and firing civil servants with expertise, who often serve as a check and balance to executive power.\par \par \uc2 The civil service is largely made up of employees who remain in their roles regardless of which party controls the White House. They have employment protections, allowing them to keep their jobs when administrations change. Only about 4,000 federal employees are currently in politically appointed roles, out of more than 2 million civil servants.\par \par \uc2 The benignly named \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://protectdemocracy.org/work/trumps-schedule-f-plan-explained/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schedule F}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, however, would increase the number of political appointees significantly by classifying far more roles as policy-related. The exact number of federal government employees this would affect isn\u8217\'20\'19t known, but some estimates say about 50,000 people could lose their jobs if their roles became political ones.\par \par \uc2 Trump issued an executive order making the change near the end of his term in office, and the project wants to revive it. It makes suggestions in most chapters of different roles that should become political appointments. For instance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/trump-state-department-project-2025-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the state department}}}\uc2 , the project says \u8220\'20\'1Cno one in a leadership position on the morning of January 20 should hold that position at the end of the day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Climate change\par \par \uc2 The project\u8217\'20\'19s goals include eliminating much of the government\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jul/27/project-2025-dismantle-us-climate-policy-next-republican-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  policies on climate change}}}\uc2  and enabling more drilling. It de-emphasizes renewable energy by cutting funding for certain offices aimed at energy transition.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ), the project wants to move away from climate-related goals, saying the agency is \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing coopted by the Left for political ends\u8221\'20\'1D by \u8220\'20\'1Cembedded activists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The chapter on the \uc2 EPA\uc2  suggests eliminating the office of environmental justice and external civil rights. It wants to lessen regulations on clean air and water and prioritize the needs of businesses and private property owners.\par \par \uc2 A fact check made by Project 2025 said it was true they want to increase Arctic drilling, calling the area \u8220\'20\'1Cof immense strategic importance to America\u8221\'20\'1D and in need of \u8220\'20\'1Cdevelopment of vast energy resources\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Free weather reports are also at risk, with the project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/26/trump-presidency-gut-noaa-weather-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing to dismantle}}}\uc2  the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2 , which houses the National Weather Service, and privatize some of its functions. Research conducted by Noaa on issues like greenhouses gases would be diminished because the research arm is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe source of much of \uc2 NOAA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s climate alarmism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Taxes\par \par \uc2 How the project\u8217\'20\'19s tax proposals could affect you is complicated. It generally suggests moving from the seven tax brackets now in place to two tax brackets at 15% and 30%, with the 30% rate kicking in for people who make more than about $168,000 and eliminating \u8220\'20\'1Cmost deductions, credits and exclusions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It also calls for some kind of national consumption tax, like a national sales tax, business transfer tax or specific type of flat tax because it would be the \u8220\'20\'1Cleast economically harmful way to raise federal tax revenues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A conservative president should also seek to repeal subsidies included in the Inflation Reduction Act, like those aimed at green energy, the project says.\par \par \uc2 It also wants to make permanent Trump-era estate and gift tax exemptions and reduce rates for these types of taxes, which affect a tiny subset of Americans with high wealth. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re one of those people, your heirs would be very happy with this proposal,\u8221\'20\'1D one analyst told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/07/20/how-project-2025-could-impact-your-taxes-under-a-second-trump-term.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The project proposes decreasing corporate taxes to 18%. The corporate tax rate is currently 21% after cuts in the Trump era. The project claims \u8220\'20\'1Cthe corporate income tax is the most damaging tax in the US tax system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the project doesn\u8217\'20\'19t specifically call for reducing or eliminating overtime pay, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4778755-does-project-2025-propose-eliminating-overtime-pay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposes}}}\uc2  a host of changes to who can receive overtime pay and how it would be calculated that could result in lower overtime pay for some workers.\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 The project aims to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/trump-mass-deportations-detention-camps-military-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crack down significantly}}}\uc2  on immigration, both legal and otherwise.\par \par \uc2 The plans would entail mass deportations, including of unaccompanied minors and via raids at worksites. It would allow immigration officers to carry out \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil arrest, detention, and removal of immigration violators anywhere in the United States, without warrant where appropriate\u8221\'20\'1D. It also says that when there\u8217\'20\'19s a mass migration event, the homeland security secretary will stop migration from specific lists of countries.\par \par \uc2 Limits would be imposed on visa programs as well, generally hewing toward allowing high-wage specialty workers into the country. And there would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpremium processing\u8221\'20\'1D visa option that would allow people to pay more to get faster service. If there are any backlogs for visas, the project says the government should pause applications until those backlogs are cleared.\par \par \uc2 The immigration plans extend well beyond the border: the project wants to block federal financial aid to college students if their state allows in-state tuition access for undocumented immigrants, including Dreamers. And it would ban people from receiving any federal housing benefits if someone in their home doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have legal status.\par \par \uc2 For cities that don\u8217\'20\'19t adhere to the immigration hard line, the project suggests a conservative president should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/trump-project-2025-sanctuary-cities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withhold federal disaster funding}}}\uc2  until they get in line. This would include states where migrants can get driver\u8217\'20\'19s licenses and places that don\u8217\'20\'19t share immigration-related data with the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Veterans benefits\par \par \uc2 For veterans, the project notes that more disability ratings were added in recent years for health conditions, of which \u8220\'20\'1Csome are tenuously related or wholly unrelated to military service\u8221\'20\'1D. Recognizing it is politically charged to get rid of these disability-related benefits, the project suggests some disability awards for future veterans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.verifythis.com/article/news/verify/project-2025-verify/what-project-2025-says-veterans-benefits/536-b3f19a24-2def-418a-b0ca-2e6ff0146269"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Crevised\u8221\'20\'1D while preserving them \u8220\'20\'1Cfully or partially\u8221\'20\'1D for current beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWholesale benefits reform is unnecessary and politically a \u8216\'20\'18third rail\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D the project says.\par \par \uc2 Pornography\par \par \uc2 As part of its social policy ideas that align with rightwing Christian values, the project wants to criminalize the production, distribution and consumption of pornography. On the Project 2025 website, the group says \u8220\'20\'1Cpornography has no claim to First Amendment protection and its purveyors are child predators and misogynistic exploiters of women. Their product is as addictive as any illicit drug and as psychologically destructive as any crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240801ek81001bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
