\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18the American people deserve better\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Maya Yang and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 10,504 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2024\par 01:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full story here:Trump repeats lies and attacks \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s racial identity at panel of Black journalists\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing shortly. You can read our full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump repeats lies and attacks Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity at panel of Black journalists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile here is our full story on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about his running mate, JD Vance, earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said that vice presidential picks have \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually no impact\u8221\'20\'1D on elections when asked about JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s fitness for office, in an apparent attempt to downplay his running mate\u8217\'20\'19s role on the Republican ticket.\par \par \uc2 Trump made the comments during a combative interview at the annual convention of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) in Chicago. Asked by the Fox News journalist Harris Faulkner whether Vance would be ready to take over \u8220\'20\'1Con day one, if he has to be\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump avoided answering directly and instead downplayed the significance of the Vance\u8217\'20\'19s role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always had great respect for him \u8230\'20\'26 but I will say this, and I think this is well documented historically, the vice-president, in terms of the election, does not have any impact. I mean, virtually no impact,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-vp-pick-jd-vance-insignificance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says running mates have \u8216\'20\'18virtually no impact\u8217\'20\'19 in apparent JD Vance snub}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is video of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interview earlier today:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris in Houston addresses Trump's bonkers appearance at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2 : "The divisiveness and the disrespect. And let me just say. The American people deserve better... a leader who does not respond with hostility and anger when confronted with the facts." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uo7sN6NV0Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uo7sN6NV0Z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1818806029271904675?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI say to the incredible members of Sigma Gamma Ro Sorority inc, there is so much at stake in this moment. The election is in 97 days. And once again, our nation is counting on you,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, \u8220\'20\'1CBecause when we organise, mountains move, when we organise, nations change, and when we vote, we make history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo let us continue to fight with faith, with optimism, and with hope,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She ends her speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the states where the majority of black women live, every state except Virginia has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 She promises to sign \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into law \u8211\'20\'13 to loud cheers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris addresses Trump interview: 'It was the same old show'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis afternoon \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke at the annual meeting of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 and it was the same old show: the divisiveness and the disrespect. And let me just say, the American people deserve better,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA leader who tells the truth. Who does not respond with hostility and anger when confronted with the facts. Who understands our differences do not divide us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris repeats her campaign messaging on fighting hidden fees, rent increases, and protecting healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, repeating a key Harris 2024 catchphrase.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation needs you,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris starts speaking\par \par \uc2 Harris takes to the stage in Houston at the Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority Inc.\u8217\'20\'19s 60th International Biennial Boul\u233\'00\'E9. She\u8217\'20\'19s smiling, she\u8217\'20\'19s laughing, and she says she\u8217\'20\'19s speaking \u8220\'20\'1Cas a proud member of the divine nine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in the promise of America. And aren\u8217\'20\'19t so many of us empirical evidence of the promise of America,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreater service brings greater progress,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. She starts listing the achievements of the sorority which, she says, \u8220\'20\'1Chelped elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the president of the United States and me as the first woman Vice President of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Harris to speak at the Sigma Gamma Rho Sorority Inc.\u8217\'20\'19s 60th International Biennial Boul\u233\'00\'E9, here is a brief look at how Harris\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy has shone a spotlight on the power of Black US sororities and fraternities.\par \par \uc2 Harris is herself a member of the Alpha Kappa Alpha sorority. The country\u8217\'20\'19s nine most prominent Greek letter organisations are called the \u8220\'20\'1CDivine Nine\u8221\'20\'1D. Altogether, the US\u8217\'20\'19s Black sororities and fraternities have more than two million members in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir voter engagement programs reach millions every four years. More, each organization controls a hefty operating budget and their combined revenue would exceed $150 million, according to public records,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreek letter organizations who have worked in the trenches, some for over 100 years, never received any kind of publicity, any kind of notoriety,\u8221\'20\'1D Representative \uc2 Frederica S. Wilson\uc2  of Florida, who is also a member of Alpha Kappa Alpha, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  earlier this week. Once Ms. Harris ran for president, in 2020, she said, that changed. \u8220\'20\'1CThe A.K.A.s shouted to the highest hills, \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s our soror! That\u8217\'20\'19s our sister!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats totally false claims that the 2020 was \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D by the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump meanwhile repeats another of his catchphrases, \u8220\'20\'1CDrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D. As his speech crosses the one hour mark, the people behind him are getting fidgety, chatting among themselves and looking bored.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , among the names tipped to be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, has addressed Trumps\u8217\'20\'19 comments about Harris, telling reporters they are, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe comments of a desperate, scared old man who is, over the last week especially, is having his butt kicked by an experienced prosecutor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s worried, and she\u8217\'20\'19s going to continue to do this, and she\u8217\'20\'19s going to win the election in November, and she\u8217\'20\'19s going to be our next president. And you know, his, his comments are not unexpected from him,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said, per CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to speak in Houston\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be speaking at a black sorority event in Houston shortly. She will be taking to the stage hours after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 annual convention shocked the audience and ended up being cut short, apparently by his team. He claimed that he has been the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest president for the Black population since \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, adding that a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Canybody that has a job \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 New York Magazine has done a deep dive on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s obsession with Hannibal Lecter. TLDR: nobody has managed to make sense of it. If you want to try, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/trump-hannibal-lecter-rant-origin.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  are the theories.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats racist assertions about immigrants from \u8220\'20\'1CAsia, Africa, the Middle East\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He is again referring to Hannibal Lecter, the fictional cannibal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy does he keep mentioning Hannibal Lecter,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, and again repeats that Hannibal Lecter would like to have you for dinner.\par \par \uc2 He says it makes sense to mention Lecter because \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane people\u8221\'20\'1D are coming into the US. (I cannot make sense of this).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is talking about \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  now, and the 6 January insurrection. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fake news is trying to delete everything,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. But that the \u8220\'20\'1Cinternet is wonderful in some ways, we have a copy of every single article\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to speak in Texas\par \par \uc2 We will soon be turning to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech in Texas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is again talking about what he says is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s record on immigration. He repeats a string of false and unsubstantiated claims.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump did not say outright that he would debate Harris. He appeared to signal that he might \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cchallenge accepted\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but technically he old agreed to compare records.\par \par \uc2 Here is exactly what he said:\par \par \uc2 In one of the most phony moments of her speech last night \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  bragged \u8220\'20\'1CI would proudly put my record against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  any day of the week\u8221\'20\'1D...\par \par \uc2 Well Kamala lets go, Challenge accepted. Let\u8217\'20\'19s compare our record point by point. I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe I\u8217\'20\'19m doing it.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday Harris challenged Trump to \u8220\'20\'1Csay it to my face\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Fox has now totally cut away from the speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Fox news is still playing footage of the speech in the background, but talking over it, which is interesting. One theory could be that they have noticed viewership drops after a certain period of Trump speaking.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump now says he will stop paying attention to the teleprompter and starts gently mocking his speech writers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sun will rise. The moon will set. The oceans will glisten\u8221\'20\'1D he says, as an example of what they write.\par \par \uc2 But I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure the people here want to hear that, he says. He moves on to talking about UFC fighter Dana White, who has admitted to hitting his wife. Then he talks about the border in Mexico, the border wall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is still speaking however, and appears to say that he will debate Harris after all. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s compare our record point for point\u8221\'20\'1D, he says.\par \par \uc2 "I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe I\u8217\'20\'19m doing this,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CTwo weeks ago I was talking about Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Now Trump says that San Francisco was one of the greatest cities in the world (but Harris destroyed it).\par \par \uc2 And then Fox cuts away from the speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going to let the Democrats turn the US into a communist San Francisco colony,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump turns now to electric cars, which he says the Democrats want. \u8220\'20\'1CSo you can go 15 minutes before charging it back up,\u8221\'20\'1D he scoffs. \u8220\'20\'1CWould anyone like to keep red meat,\u8221\'20\'1D he says? \u8220\'20\'1CRaise your hand\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats want to get rid of red meat\u8221\'20\'1D he says \u8211\'20\'13 so you should get rid of your cows. This is not remotely true.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now ranting about \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D and saying Harris wants taxpayer-funded free health care for immigrants.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2024/jul/31/donald-trump/gop-charge-that-kamala-harris-backed-taxpayer-fund/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PolitiFact}}}\uc2  : Harris has supported giving immigrants who are in the country illegally access to health coverage through her 2019 Medicare for All plan, but she hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said it would be free for them or that it would be funded by taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter how much \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tries to change her image she cannot change this fact,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, and then says several things that are not facts, including that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cis the most left-wing candidate in history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 He again calls Harris a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left puppet candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand you have Harris, who is \u8220\'20\'1CFake, fake, fake\u8221\'20\'1D, he says, and on the other, Trump, who will \u8220\'20\'1CFight, fight, fight\u8221\'20\'1D. There is much applause. Trump again claims that many people were turned away from the rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad 81 and he\u8217\'20\'19s destroying our country\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump says. Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Cphony radical left\u8221\'20\'1D and Harris is a \u8220\'20\'1Creal phony left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump uses the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D several times, referring to Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris was never given the portfolio of border czar, Alan Bersin, who embraced the label as a special representative for border affairs under Presidents \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  has told Reuters. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was not the job assigned to VP Harris,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 The Fox news chryon as Trump speaks is Trump: Everything about Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s rollout was fake.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t forget. Four weeks ago she was considered, like, the worst,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He says Harris has had a personality makeover and \u8220\'20\'1Call of a sudden she\u8217\'20\'19s considered the new \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Margaret Thatcher\uc2  was, infamously, a Conservative British prime minister.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats his well-worn claim that he could have a \u8220\'20\'1Cnice easy life\u8221\'20\'1D but has chosen to do this instead.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 He calls, erroneously, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cpuppet candidate\u8221\'20\'1D who was \u8220\'20\'1Cinstalled by the democrats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 He says that $6m have been raised in a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  for Comperatore.\par \par \uc2 He says, that Corey\u8217\'20\'19s wife said, \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19d rather have my husband\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsn\u8217\'20\'19t that good? I know a lot of wives who wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say that,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He holds a very brief moment of silence. Then says \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s the most quiet I have ever heard an arena\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 He is naming the people injured and killed at the rally. He thanks the doctor who attended to Corey Comperatore, who died in the shooting.\par \par \uc2 He names the people injured.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re doing really well. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to be fine. Not going to be perfect, really, but who is?\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will go back to Butler, the city where the assassination attempt took place. He thanks everyone at Butler Memorial Hospital, he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey saw some pretty bad things.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd is chanting \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He claims that more than 20,000 people weren\u8217\'20\'19t able to get into the stadium. He says \u8220\'20\'1Cwe didn\u8217\'20\'19t need a star\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the singers who have appeared at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rallies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is on stage in Harrisburg and will begin speaking any moment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s address will be his first in Pennsylvania since the assassination attempt there three weeks (yes, just three weeks) ago. It is happening indoors at the state capital\u8217\'20\'19s New Holland Arena.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting Trump to speak at a rally in Pennsylvania any moment \u8211\'20\'13he appears to be running an hour late.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden aides have expressed some worry to one another about how his lingering frustrations might surface, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Some pointed to his comments in the early hours of Tuesday morning, when a reporter asked Biden about his legacy with regard to LGBTQ Americans. The president harked back to to his 2011 comments supporting same-sex marriage that caught then-President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  off guard. It came off as a subtle dig at the former president, who in recent weeks was among those working behind the scenes to push Biden toward the exits.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s regular lunches with Harris on Wednesdays have \u8220\'20\'1Ctaken on a new dimension\u8221\'20\'1D as the balance of power in their relationship has shifted, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has tasked aides with finding additional actions he can take before 20 January 2025, to secure his legacy, AP reports. What those actions might be remains a work in progress.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  acknowledged that Biden and the White House are still \u8220\'20\'1Crecalibrating\u8221\'20\'1D after his decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are trying to figure out what the next six months are going to look like,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CJust give us a beat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ten days since ending his reelection campaign, Biden still is coming to terms with the political whiplash that he and the country have experienced, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DPrivately, the Democratic president is smarting over those who orchestrated the abrupt end of his 50-year political career and processing a mixture of emotions \u8212\'20\'14 bitterness and regret among them, but also relief at not having to run a gruelling race against Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Nor will Biden have to confront the risk of what his potential loss might have done do his legacy and the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The parties involved in Lahaina wildfire lawsuits against the state of Hawaii, Maui County and utilities are close to a global settlement of claims that will be worth a little over $4 billion, Governor Josh Green told The Associated Press on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Green said he\u8217\'20\'19s hoping to finalise the details in coming days, perhaps as soon as Aug. 6, which would be two days before the one-year anniversary of the fire that killed 102 people and wiped out historic Lahaina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that could happen, it would be great. I humbly invite all the parties to finalize the agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D Green said in an interview at his office. \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears that we are almost there, and we only have a very tiny holdout remaining.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said all the plaintiffs and defendants have agreed to the global settlement number but final details are pending.\par \par \uc2 More than 600 lawsuits have been filed over the deaths and destruction caused by the fires. In the spring, a judge appointed mediators and ordered all parties to participate in settlement talks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative news outlet The Bulwark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/p/trump-allies-kellyanne-conway-badmouthing-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that several Trump campaign staffers and advisers say that Kellyanne Conway, former senior counsellor to Trump, is leaking negative stories about JD Vance to the press:\par \par \uc2 In interviews with The Bulwark, twenty Trump campaign staffers, allies, confidants, and advisers were quick to shoot down any notion that Trump was turning his back on Vance or was displeased with him amid his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/jd-vance-discusses-rocky-debut-role-wants-play-vp-rcna164295"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rocky rollout}}}\uc2 . But more than a dozen of those sources volunteered without prompting that they believed Conway, who initially opposed the selection of Vance, was undermining him through leaks to the press expressing doubts about his readiness and the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s vetting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three men accused of being involved in the 9/11 terrorist attack \u8211\'20\'13 including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/feb/02/why-cant-we-get-this-over-911-hearings-drag-on-guantanamo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-proclaimed mastermind of the 2001 attacks}}}\uc2  on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon \u8211\'20\'13 have agreed to plea deals at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay, Cuba, prosecutors said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Convening Authority for Military Commissions, Susan Escallier, has entered into pre-trial agreements with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/khalid-sheikh-mohammed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Khalid Sheikh Mohammed}}}\uc2 , Walid Muhammad Salih Mubarak Bin \u8216\'20\'18Attash, and Mustafa Ahmed Adam al-Hawsawi, three of the co-accused in the 9/11 case,\u8221\'20\'1D the Pentagon said in a short statement.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/31/us/politics/sept-11-guilty-plea.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the three will plead guilty to conspiracy charges in exchange for a life sentence rather than a death-penalty trial.\par \par \uc2 The men have been in US custody since 2003 and Khalid Sheikh Mohammed is widely seen as the chief plotter of the terror attacks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/september-11-suspects-guantanamo-bay-guilty-plea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Three accused 9/11 plotters plead guilty in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay deal \u8211\'20\'13 prosecutors}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is Helen Sullivan taking you through the next few hours of US politics news.\par \par \uc2 New York Magazine reports that among the images being projected to audiences at his rally in Pennsylvania is a screenshot of a Business Insider article that says \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  becomes first Indian-American US senator\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Trump campaign is projecting this on the screen above the stage at his rally in Harrisburg PA: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZsGHAZaruk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZsGHAZaruk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Nuzzi (@Olivianuzzi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivianuzzi/status/1818756196599542210?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here is a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 annual convention shocked the audience and ended up being cut short, apparently by his team. He claimed that he has been the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest president for the Black population since \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, adding that a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Canybody that has a job \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump also questioned \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ethnicity, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe was always of Indian heritage, and she was only promoting Indian heritage. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know she was Black until a number of years ago, when she happened to turn Black.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign team has released the following statement in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interview: \u8220\'20\'1CThe hostility \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  showed on stage today is the same hostility he has shown throughout his life, throughout his term in office, and throughout his campaign for president as he seeks to regain power and inflict his harmful Project 2025 agenda on the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, responded while at the podium in the daily media briefing to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s racial identity. Jean-Pierre, speaking in real time in the west wing in Washington DC while Trump was being quizzed by three political journalists in Chicago, called his words \u8220\'20\'1Crepulsive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 100 venture capitalists including entrepreneur {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/04/mark-cuban-elon-musk-diversity-dei-program-business"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Cuban}}}\uc2  and \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  founder \uc2 Reid Hoffman\uc2  threw their support behind Harris today, in a counterweight to tech billionaires {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/tech-broligarchs-court-trump-vance-elon-musk-peter-thiel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backing}}}\uc2  Trump. Among the venture capitalists lining up behind Harris are investor Chris Sacca, Katie Stanton of Moxxie, Eva Ho of Fika Ventures and Rebecca Kaden of \uc2 Union Square Ventures\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a new poll out today, about eight in 10 Democrats say they would be very or somewhat satisfied if Harris became the Democratic nominee for president. The survey from the AP-Norc Center for Public Affairs Research was conducted after \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew}}}\uc2  from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 race}}}\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  has endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  for president. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president-ahead-of-mass-rally-in-detroit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain said: \u8220\'20\'1COur job in this election is to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to build on her proven track record of delivering for the working class \u8230\'20\'26.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US was not aware of or involved in the apparent killing of \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2  leader, says the US representative to the \uc2 UN\uc2  , Robert Wood.\par \par \uc2 Wood calls on \uc2 UN\uc2  security council members with direct influence over Iran to increase pressure on the country to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop escalating its proxy conflict against Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Every member of this council should call on Iran to stop arming, advising and financing terrorist groups and to rein in the actions of proxies and partners who threaten regional peace and security.\par \par \uc2 Follow more live updates on the situation here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jul/31/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-killed-iran-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East crisis live: US \u8216\'20\'18not aware of or involved in\u8217\'20\'19 killing of Hamas leader, US ambassador tells UN council}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance chimes in...\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chaotic \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Trump walked right into the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  conference and showed he had the courage to take tough questions, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  continues to hide from any scrutiny or unfriendly media like the coward she is. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8l7OgGb6xO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/8l7OgGb6xO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JD Vance (@JDVance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance/status/1818742558421614818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  endorses Harris for president\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president-ahead-of-mass-rally-in-detroit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain said:\par \par \uc2 Our job in this election is to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to build on her proven track record of delivering for the working class \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 We stand at a crossroads in this country. We can put a billionaire back in office who stands against everything our union stands for, or we can elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  who will stand shoulder to shoulder with us in our war on corporate greed.\par \par \uc2 This campaign is bringing together people from all walks of life, building a movement that can defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the ballot box. For our one million active and retired members, the choice is clear: We will elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to be our next President this November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is video of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  questioning \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ethnicity during his interview at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  conference in Chicago:\par \par \uc2 Throughout the years, Trump has also questioned the birth origins of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2016/sep/26/donald-trump-video-debate-birther-obama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jan/05/donald-trump-birther-republican-ted-cruz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ted Cruz}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/10/trump-nikki-haley-birther-conspiracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign responds to Trump NABJ interview: 'A taste of chaos and division'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign team has released the following statement in response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s combative \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview:\par \par \uc2 The hostility \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  showed on stage today is the same hostility he has shown throughout his life, throughout his term in office, and throughout his campaign for president as he seeks to regain power and inflict his harmful Project 2025 agenda on the American people.\par \par \uc2 Trump lobbed personal attacks and insults at Black journalists the same way he did throughout his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 while he failed Black families and left the entire country digging out of the ditch he left us in. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has already proven he cannot unite America, so he attempts to divide us.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s tirade is simply a taste of the chaos and division that has been a hallmark of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Maga rallies this entire campaign. It\u8217\'20\'19s also exactly what the American people will see from across the debate stage as vice-president Harris offers a vision of opportunity and freedom for all Americans. All \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  needs to do is stop playing games and actually show up to the debate on September 10.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 When asked by Fox News journalist Harris Faulkner whether JD Vance would be ready for day one, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve always had great respect for him \u8230\'20\'26 but I will say this, and I think this is well-documented historically, the vice-president in terms of the election, does not have any impact. I mean, virtually no impact.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re voting for the president, and you can have a vice-president who\u8217\'20\'19s outstanding in every way. And I think JD is, I think that all of them would have been but, but you\u8217\'20\'19re not voting that way. You\u8217\'20\'19re voting for the president. You\u8217\'20\'19re voting for me.\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked by Harris Faulkner if JD Vance is ready on day one, Trump answers: \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, the vice president, in terms of the election, does not have any impact. I mean, virtually no impact...Virtually never has it mattered.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ggS74VXMdn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ggS74VXMdn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1818723037832704457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's remarks on Harris at \uc2 NABJ\uc2  "repulsive" \u8211\'20\'13 White House\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, responded while at the podium in the daily media briefing to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s identity at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) convention.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre, speaking in real time in the west wing in Washington DC while Trump was being quizzed by three political journalists in Chicago, called his words \u8220\'20\'1Crepulsive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/31/kamala-harris-vp-trump-politics-updates?page=with:block-66aa879a8f08a503d53900e0#block-66aa879a8f08a503d53900e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that}}}\uc2  he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know Harris was Black until a few years ago when she \u8220\'20\'1Chappened to turn Black\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s insulting, and no one has any right to tell someone who they are, how they identify.\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre is the first Black and first openly LGBTQ+ American to serve as White House press secretary.\par \par \uc2 She continued, of Harris: \u8220\'20\'1COnly she can speak to her experience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris grew up in Berkeley, California, near San Francisco; her mother was an immigrant from India and her father immigrated to the US from Jamaica.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s insulting for anybody, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter if it\u8217\'20\'19s a former leader, a former president, it is insulting,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CShe is the vice-president of the United States. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . We have to put some respect on her name. Period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of Trump's \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview shocked the audience and ended up being cut short, apparently by his team. Here are some of the things the former president claimed in the heated Q&A:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He claimed that he has been the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest president for the Black population since \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, adding that a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D is \u8220\'20\'1Canybody that has a job \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He questioned \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ethnicity, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe was always of Indian heritage, and she was only promoting Indian heritage. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know she was Black until a number of years ago, when she happened to turn Black.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He refused to condemn the white police officer who shot and killed 36-year-old Sonya Massey, a Black woman, in her home in Illinois, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes very bad decisions are made. They\u8217\'20\'19re not made from an evil standpoint.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He repeated the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lie that Democrats are allowing abortions in the ninth month, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re allowing the death of the baby after the baby is born.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In response to what he would do on his first day in office, he said that he would \u8220\'20\'1Cclose the border\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Throughout the interview, which appeared to have been ended by his team after 40 minutes, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s responses drew multiple gasps and shouts from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump hits out at Black journalists and repeatedly lies in heated interview before Q&A is cut short\par \par \uc2 The interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  conference is now over, with Trump giving a few fist pumps and shaking hands with the interviewers before walking off stage.\par \par \uc2 The interview, which lasted around 40 minutes, got off to a rocky start, with Trump accusing interviewers of asking \u8220\'20\'1Crude\u8221\'20\'1D questions and calling their networks \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D before blaming the conference\u8217\'20\'19s speakers for his lateness.\par \par \uc2 In addition to multiple tangents on how he is allegedly persecuted by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and a supposedly \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponized\u8221\'20\'1D justice system, Trump refused to condemn the January 6 insurrectionists, continued to espouse the lie that Democrats are \u8220\'20\'1Cexecuting\u8221\'20\'1D babies after birth, and vowed to close the borders on his first day in office if he becomes president.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the interview, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s responses drew multiple gasps and shouts from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 He also defended JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s comments about \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies\u8221\'20\'1D said he \u8220\'20\'1Cdidn\u8217\'20\'19t know [Harris] was Black until a number of years ago, when she happened to turn Black,\u8221\'20\'1D and described a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Canybody that has a job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The interview was cut short after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team apparently asked interviewers to end the Q&A. ABC\u8217\'20\'19s Rachel Scott told the audience: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we have to leave it there, by the Trump team. That is the last word.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump reacted with a bemused expression before getting off the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to a question on what he would do on his first day as president if he wins, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responded:\par \par \uc2 I close the border. And I do two things, because I can do a lot of things. I close the border. And we don\u8217\'20\'19t want people coming. We want people to come in \u8230\'20\'26 but they have to be vetted. They have to be checked. They have to come in legally \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 And I drill. Drill, baby, drill. I bring energy way down. I bring interest rates down. I bring inflation way down. So people can buy bacon again, so people can buy a ham sandwich again, so that people can go to a restaurant and afford it because right now people can\u8217\'20\'19t buy food.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the next questions asked of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is whether he believes the Republican party is getting \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo judgy about people\u8217\'20\'19s lives \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In response, Trump touted several false statements, saying that Democrats are \u8220\'20\'1Cradical on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they\u8217\'20\'19re allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month. They\u8217\'20\'19re allowing the death of the baby after the baby is born.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie was swiftly fact-checked on the spot, with the interviewers saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s illegal in all 50 states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He nevertheless continued with the false statement about abortions, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CMost Republicans believe in the exception, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the ninth month or the eighth month.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are more than 15 minutes into the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the former president has already butted heads multiple times with the interviewers.\par \par \uc2 In addition to frequently interrupting them, Trump has blamed the conferences\u8217\'20\'19s speakers for his lateness, accused the interviewers\u8217\'20\'19 questions of being \u8220\'20\'1Crude\u8221\'20\'1D and their networks, including ABC, of being \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At one point, when one of the interviewers told Trump she would like to move on to other questions following his tangent on his alleged political persecution, Trump replied: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the one that held me up 35 minutes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked about Sonya Massey, the 36-year-old Black woman who was shot and killed in her home by a white police officer in Illinois on 6 July .\par \par \uc2 Specifically, the question was about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous comments on police officers needing to have immunity and why someone like the officer, who has been charged with murder in the case of Sonya Massey\u8217\'20\'19s killing, should get immunity.\par \par \uc2 Trump responded:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know the exact case, but I saw something, and it didn\u8217\'20\'19t look, it didn\u8217\'20\'19t look good to me. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t look good to me \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m saying if I felt, or if a group of people would feel, that somebody was being unfairly prosecuted because the person did a good job \u8230\'20\'26 or made a mistake, an innocent mistake, there\u8217\'20\'19s a big difference between being a bad person and making an innocent mistake. But if somebody made an innocent mistake, I would want to help that person \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Sometimes very bad decisions are made. They\u8217\'20\'19re not made from an evil standpoint.\par \par \uc2 Trump then went on a tangent of being \u8220\'20\'1Cprosecuted because I\u8217\'20\'19m a political opponent of two people that have weaponized our justice system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s message is today and why he chose to appear at the conference, Trump touted his typical anti-immigration rhetoric, saying:\par \par \uc2 My message is to stop people from invading our country that are taking, frankly, a lot of problems with it. But one of the big problems, and a lot of the journalists in this room, I know, and I have great respect for a lot of the journalists in this room are Black \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re coming in, and they\u8217\'20\'19re coming in, they\u8217\'20\'19re invading. It\u8217\'20\'19s an invasion of millions of people \u8230\'20\'26 The first group of people, the Black population, is affected most by that and Kamala is allowing it to happen.\par \par \uc2 Trump was also asked what a \u8220\'20\'1CBlack job\u8221\'20\'1D is, to which he said:\par \par \uc2 A Black job is anybody that has a job. That\u8217\'20\'19s what it is.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to a question on whether he believes \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is only on the ticket because she is a Black woman, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 So I\u8217\'20\'19ve known her a long time indirectly and she was always of Indian heritage, and she was only promoting Indian heritage. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know she was Black until a number of years ago, when she happened to turn Black, and now she wants to be known as Black. So I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Is she Indian or is she Black?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to a question on why Black voters should trust \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  following his track record of inappropriate comments towards Black communities, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 First of all, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been asked a question so horrible manner. First question, you don\u8217\'20\'19t even say hello. How are you? Are you with ABC? Because I think they\u8217\'20\'19re a fake news network, a terrible network, and I think it\u8217\'20\'19s disgraceful that I came here in history. I love the Black population of this country \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a very rude introduction. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know exactly why you would do something like that.\par \par \uc2 I have been the best president for the Black population since \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just walked on stage.\par \par \uc2 The interviewers also said that the interview will be live-fact-checked live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NABJ\uc2  interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about to begin.\par \par \uc2 Interviewers Kadia Goba of Semafor, Rachel Scott of ABC News and Harris Faulkner of Fox News have just walked on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has fired off another post on Truth Social, blaming the conference\u8217\'20\'19s speakers for his lateness:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been waiting for a half hour. The speaker equipment at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  is not working properly. Don\u8217\'20\'19t blame me for being late.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are reports emerging that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  is more than an hour late because he is at odds over the debate\u8217\'20\'19s live fact-checking, HuffPost\u8217\'20\'19s Philip Lewis reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m told that Trump is demanding that \uc2 NABJ\uc2  not do the live fact checking and that\u8217\'20\'19s why the event hasn\u8217\'20\'19t started yet\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in a standoff\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 philip lewis (@Phil_Lewis_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Lewis_/status/1818708311866311134?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before his interview at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s physical absence at the conference, writing on Truth Social:\par \par \uc2 They told me and Crazy \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that you could not do this Event with ZOOM \u8212\'20\'14 It is not allowed or acceptable! She declined, and I am getting ready to land in Chicago in order to be there. Now I am told that she is doing the Event on ZOOM. WHAT\u8217\'20\'19S GOING ON HERE?\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has also released a statement on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at the event, saying:\par \par \uc2 We know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to lie about his record and the real harm he\u8217\'20\'19s caused Black communities at \uc2 NABJ\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and he must be called out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, US politics blog readers, we are waiting for Trump to speak at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  convention and also waiting for the press briefing at the White House, both of which are running behind schedule. But stick with us and we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the developments. A short summary of events meanwhile:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is about to be interviewed by three prominent political journalists at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  convention in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a new poll out today, about eight in 10 Democrats say they would be very or somewhat satisfied if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  became the Democratic nominee for president. Between the dire debate performance and his withdrawal from re-election, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s result in a similar poll was four in 10 Dems.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said that if his Democratic rival, Harris, beats him to the presidency in November\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2 , she will struggle to deal with foreign leaders on the world stage. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think they would walk all over her. She will be so easy for them, she will be like a play toy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speculation is mounting about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s choice of running mate. There are mixed opinions on whether Harris picking Pennsylvania to introduce her choice of running mate means that the governor of that state, Josh Shapiro, is the frontrunner in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-running-mate-vp-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 veep stakes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going to appear at a campaign event in Philadelphia next Tuesday with her choice of running mate for the Democratic ticket to contest the presidential election campaign this November. Harris has not yet named her vice-presidential choice and it\u8217\'20\'19s not yet been made clear exactly when she will, but her campaign, Harris for President, has confirmed that she and the relevant person will stump together in the Pennsylvania city on 6 August.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, you can follow events in the Middle East via our separate, global live blog, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jul/31/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-killed-iran-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s imminent appearance at an \uc2 NABJ\uc2  event has received backlash from many attendees, especially as the US vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the likely Democratic nominee for US president, will not be featured at this year\u8217\'20\'19s conference.\par \par \uc2 Multiple news sources have reported that the conference declined to have Harris appear virtually, which was initially offered by the campaign because she has campaign commitments on an intense schedule because her new presidential campaign is only 10 days old, and she is due to attend the funeral of the late congresswoman, \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\uc2 , in Houston, Texas. Lee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/democratic-congresswoman-sheila-jackson-lee-dies-aged-74-family-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died last weekend}}}\uc2  after suffering from cancer.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NABJ\uc2  has not publicly confirmed if it refused to allow Harris to virtually participate, but said that it was working with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s team to schedule another so-called fireside chat at a later time. Trump has predicted on social media that she will find a way to show up at last minute so as not to be bested by him.\par \par \uc2 The event is running late. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been staring at empty chairs on stage for almost half an hour but a voice over said it will start shortly \u8230\'20\'26 meanwhile, more music.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Upbeat funk music is playing at the nearly packed ballroom where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to address a conference of Black journalists ahead of the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s panel at the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) is set to begin in approximately 10 minutes. The panel will be moderated by three Black journalists: Rachel Scott, a senior congressional correspondent for ABC News; Harris Faulkner, a newscaster and television host for Fox News; and Kadia Goba, a politics reporter for Semafor.\par \par \uc2 Some have questioned the inclusion of Faulkner as a moderator, accusing the Fox News journalist of being biased in favor of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s one comment:\par \par \uc2 enltrI wonder how the panel was selected and if Trump had say so on who's on it. Because among other things...Harris Faulkner? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NABJ24?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NABJ24}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natalie Y Moore (@natalieymoore) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/natalieymoore/status/1818261441994244308?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And another:\par \par \uc2 enltrHaving Harris Faulkner as a moderator proves that he won\u8217\'20\'19t be held accountable. So when you have the chance and don\u8217\'20\'19t succeed, what is the legacy of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NABJ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nabj}}}\uc2  ? That you willingly platformed a racist rapist who has repeatedly denigrated members of your organization. Shameful. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NABJ?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NABJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZCuLx9gpAC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZCuLx9gpAC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 April (@ReignOfApril) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReignOfApril/status/1818297276726669563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign has issued a statement about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appearing on stage at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  convention, where he is about to be interviewed by three political journalists in a few minutes, and we have a live feed of the event at the top of this blog.\par \par \uc2 enltrInbox: Harris campaign releases a statement on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at this year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NABJ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NABJ}}}\uc2  convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to lie about his record and the real harm he\u8217\'20\'19s caused Black communities at \uc2 NABJ\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and he must be called out.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EzaNq6HG7v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EzaNq6HG7v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Brown (@mrbrownsir) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mrbrownsir/status/1818689587272618332?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the theme of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attending the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  convention and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  not doing so, there\u8217\'20\'19s this from a journalist whom the former president has dissed in the past, April Ryan.\par \par \uc2 enltrLive fact checking of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 !! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @vp}}}\uc2  worked hard to make an appearance work virtually as she has been thrust into running for president in a little over a week. The \uc2 NABJ\uc2  leader ship would not accommodate her request for a virtual Q&A session nor an in person session at a\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xpaF12arbF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xpaF12arbF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 AprilDRyan (@AprilDRyan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AprilDRyan/status/1818678929038746076?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) have a tense history over his treatment of Black women journalists.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, \uc2 NABJ\uc2  condemned Trump for repeatedly using words such as \u8220\'20\'1Cstupid,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Closer\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnasty\u8221\'20\'1D to describe Black women journalists, including, most prominently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1818461822959177861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yamiche Alcindor}}}\uc2  of NBC News, who is attending the convention, where Trump is appearing to be questioned by journalists at the top of the hour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abbydphillip/status/1817016673196491181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abby Phillip}}}\uc2  of CNN and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AprilDRyan/status/1590682811404812288"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April Ryan}}}\uc2  of The Grio, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe most powerful man in the free world is verbally abusing journalists. His dismissive comments toward journalists April Ryan, Abby Phillip and Yamiche Alcindor are appalling, irresponsible, and should be denounced,\u8221\'20\'1D said then-\uc2 NABJ\uc2  President Sarah Glover.\par \par \uc2 When Trump told Alcindor \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t be threatening\u8221\'20\'1D during a 2020 press conference, then-\uc2 NABJ\uc2  president Dorothy Tucker condemned the remarks as \u8220\'20\'1Cnot only unnecessary but demeaning and inappropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Former presidents \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  have all attended \uc2 NABJ\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  attended remotely in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be interviewed at 1pm ET (12pm central time) today, at the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  convention in Chicago, by three reporters: Kadia Goba of Semafor, Rachel Scott of ABC News and Harris Faulkner of Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the likely Democratic nominee and first Black woman to hold her office, is not currently scheduled to address the convention, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 The debate over the \uc2 NABJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invite reflects how many journalists are still grappling with how to approach Trump nearly a decade after his first presidential run.\par \par \uc2 Some group members argued journalists should allow newsmakers to be heard, while others pointed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demeaning of prominent Black journalists while president and his frequent attacks on the free press, including labeling reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/bc8b3670f9284186ac9a2699566b9baf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy of the people\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrGreatest gratitude ???? to you Gianno. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/fam?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #fam}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G9tAztlIVE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/G9tAztlIVE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 HARRISFAULKNER (@HARRISFAULKNER) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HARRISFAULKNER/status/1818504406503199216?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invitation to address the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) convention today has sparked an intense debate.\par \par \uc2 Journalism organizations for people of color traditionally invite presidential candidates to address their summer gatherings during election years, the Associated Press writes.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of the \uc2 NABJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invitation has led at least one high-profile group member, Karen Attiah, to step down as a convention co-chair and others to argue their convention {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-black-hispanic-americans-voters-of-color-59acadcda6cf9cb1082d4bdd9d4c4a81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may become a platform for Trump}}}\uc2  to make false claims or be seen as winning the \uc2 NABJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement.\par \par \uc2 enltrI have decided to step down as co- chair from this year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NABJ24?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NABJ24}}}\uc2  convention in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 To the journalists interviewing Trump, I wish them the best of luck.\par \par \uc2 For everyone else, I\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to meeting and reconnecting with all of you in the Windy City. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nabj?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nabj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karen Attiah (@KarenAttiah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KarenAttiah/status/1818314505266335776?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 She wished the journalists who are going to interview Trump luck, and added, on X that: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile my decision was influenced by a variety of factors, I was not involved or consulted with in any way with the decision to platform Trump in such a format.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhile my decision was influenced by a variety of factors, I was not involved or consulted with in any way with the decision to platform Trump in such a format.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karen Attiah (@KarenAttiah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KarenAttiah/status/1818320919942574524?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to be interviewed at \uc2 NABJ\uc2  convention\par \par \uc2 Journalists at the annual conference of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) began trickling in to the Hilton hotel in downtown Chicago this morning for a 12pm CT/1pm ET panel \u8211\'20\'13 featuring Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He will be quizzed by the prominent political reporters Kadia Goba of Semafor, Rachel Scott of ABC News and Harris Faulkner of Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Press credentials for the much-discussed event have been tight, with several Secret Service agents monitoring the ballroom where the conversation with Trump will take place.\par \par \uc2 Others Secret Service agents have been spotted walking throughout the hotel.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest appearance comes only weeks after a 20-year-old gunman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/trump-rally-shooter-jfk-assasination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to assassinate}}}\uc2  the former president at a Pennsylvania campaign rally. In the immediate aftermath, the Secret Service chief, Kimberly Cheatle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/secret-service-director-resigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepped down}}}\uc2  after calls from both parties to quit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the venture capitalists lining up behind \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are, in addition to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/04/mark-cuban-elon-musk-diversity-dei-program-business"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Cuban}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Reid Hoffman\uc2 , investor Chris Sacca, Katie Stanton of Moxxie, Eva Ho of Fika Ventures and Rebecca Kaden of \uc2 Union Square Ventures\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They all signed an open letter today, pledging to vote for Harris in the 5 November presidential election, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The letter comes after Trump drew support from other wealthy, high-profile Silicon Valley venture capitalists and investors.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/19/elon-musk-trump-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the billionaire CEO of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , publicly endorsed Trump for the first time after the 13 July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/trump-rally-shooter-jfk-assasination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt}}}\uc2  on the former president.\par \par \uc2 Entrepreneur and investor \uc2 David Sacks\uc2 , the former chief operating officer of \uc2 PayPal\uc2  and a close friend of Musk, has also hosted fundraisers for Trump.\par \par \uc2 You can read {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carolecadwalladr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carole Cadwallader}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s analysis piece for the Observer (the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s sister paper) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/tech-broligarchs-court-trump-vance-elon-musk-peter-thiel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 100 venture capitalists including enterpreneur \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  and \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  founder \uc2 Reid Hoffman\uc2  threw their support behind Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  today, in a counterweight to tech billionaires {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/tech-broligarchs-court-trump-vance-elon-musk-peter-thiel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backing}}}\uc2  Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a public petition posted online, according to Reuters, the group said:\par \par \uc2 We spend our days looking for, investing in and supporting entrepreneurs who are building the future. We are pro-business, pro-American dream, pro-entrepreneurship, and pro-technological progress. We also believe in democracy as the backbone of our nation. We believe that strong, trustworthy institutions are a feature, not a bug, and that our industry \u8211\'20\'13 and every other industry \u8211\'20\'13 would collapse without them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll shows Harris bounce\par \par \uc2 In a new poll out today, about eight in 10 Democrats say they would be very or somewhat satisfied if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  became the Democratic nominee for president.\par \par \uc2 The survey from the AP-Norc Center for Public Affairs Research was conducted after \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew}}}\uc2  from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 race}}}\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 In a separate AP-Norc poll, taken before Biden dropped out but after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-cnn-presidential-debate-reaction-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his debate}}}\uc2  against the Republican former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , only about four in 10 Democrats said they were somewhat or very satisfied that Biden was the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s likely nominee for president.\par \par \uc2 The rapidly changing views among Democrats in such a short timespan underscore how swiftly the party has coalesced behind Harris as its standard bearer.\par \par \uc2 Gary Hines, a Democratic voter from Philadelphia who wasn\u8217\'20\'19t particularly impressed by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s first presidential bid in 2019, told the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s up to the task, can do the work, has proven that she\u8217\'20\'19s running a strong campaign so far and maybe on a bigger level, she\u8217\'20\'19s somebody that can beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump insults Harris as 'play toy' for world leaders\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-campaign-insults-extremism-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another}}}\uc2  very personal tear into \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last night, as Fox News aired an interview with the former president and current Republican nominee for the White House.\par \par \uc2 On the segment on the rightwing cable channel\u8217\'20\'19s The Ingraham Angle, with host Laura Ingraham, Trump said that if his Democratic rival beats him to the presidency in November\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2  she will struggle to deal with foreign leaders on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think they would walk all over her. She will be so easy for them, she will be like a play toy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added, of foreign leaders: \u8220\'20\'1CThey look at her and they say, I would believe, \u8216\'20\'18We got so lucky,\u8217\'20\'19 and they are going to walk all over her. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say as to why but a lot of people understand it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fox {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/video/6359648084112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  it straight. But the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/30/trump-harris-play-toy-comment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s headline says: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump suggests Harris would struggle with world leaders based on her appearance\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Ca campaign spokeswoman denied he was talking about her race or gender\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a reminder of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with world leaders in 2018. He threw candies in the direction of then German leader \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrIan Bremmer reports a G7 exchange where Trump tossed Starbursts at Merkel:\par \par \uc2 "He stood up, put his hand in his pocket, took two Starbursts out, threw them on the table and said, 'Here, Angela. Don't say I never gave you anything.'"\par \par \uc2 POTUS has the maturity of a bratty six year old. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9cAYUYIZ7U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9cAYUYIZ7U}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Best ???? (@adamcbest) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamcbest/status/1009663259669073920?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2018}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 VP pick rumors mount as Harris expected to announce choice within days\par \par \uc2 There are mixed opinions on whether \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  picking Pennsylvania to introduce her choice of running mate means that the governor of that state, Josh Shapiro, is the frontrunner in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-running-mate-vp-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 veep stakes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Politico points out that \u8220\'20\'1Ca Harris campaign aide cautioned against reading too much into the first city chosen for the tour\u8221\'20\'1D. The outlet also linked to a post on X that details what they described as \u8220\'20\'1Ca long history of running mate rollouts not matching up to the states where they hail from\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 frltrBiden intros Harris (CA): DE\par \par \uc2 Trump intros Pence (IN): NY\par \par \uc2 Hillary intros Kaine (VA): FL\par \par \uc2 Romney intros Ryan (WI): VA\par \par \uc2 McCain intros Palin (AK): OH\par \par \uc2 Obama intros Biden (DE): IL\par \par \uc2 Kerry intros Edwards (NC): PA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gGF20wnBqZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gGF20wnBqZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Madden (@KevinMaddenDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KevinMaddenDC/status/1818478308813586593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 But that list doesn\u8217\'20\'19t include a situation in which a presidential nominee presents their new running mate in a state led by someone who\u8217\'20\'19s just been passed over for the job, as would be the case if Shapiro\u8217\'20\'19s not chosen and then has to watch Harris introduce a rival in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Associated Press says \u8220\'20\'1Cthe location of the first stop suggests \u8230\'20\'26 Shapiro has moved to the top of a short list of running mates, and that the Harris campaign had decided the state that Democrats won back from Republicans in 2020 is a must-win once again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It then adds that the Harris campaign last night issued a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong reminder\u8221\'20\'1D that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cmade no decision on a running mate\u8221\'20\'1D at this point.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Heightened tension in the Middle East after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader killed \u8211\'20\'13 follow the global blog\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2  was assassinated early this morning in Iran, the Palestinian militant group and Tehran said, drawing threats of revenge on Israel in a region already shaken by the war in Gaza and a deepening conflict in Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team in London is live-blogging all the news surrounding this event and you can follow the developments as they happen, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jul/31/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-killed-iran-israel-gaza-war?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66a9c9c48f0891104a9d9a8b#block-66a9c9c48f0891104a9d9a8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s Revolutionary Guards confirmed the death of Haniyeh, hours after he attended a swearing-in ceremony for the country\u8217\'20\'19s new president, and said it was investigating. He had been taking part in internationally brokered indirect talks on reaching a ceasefire in the Palestinian enclave of Gaza, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s supreme leader, \uc2 Ali Khamenei\uc2 , said Israel had provided the grounds for \u8220\'20\'1Charsh punishment for itself\u8221\'20\'1D and it was Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s duty to avenge the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader\u8217\'20\'19s death as it had occurred in the Iranian capital. Iranian forces had already made strikes directly on Israel earlier in the Gaza war.\par \par \uc2 There was no comment nor claim of responsibility from Israel.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s global affairs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jul/31/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-killed-iran-israel-gaza-war?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66a9c9c48f0891104a9d9a8b#block-66a9c9c48f0891104a9d9a8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live blog}}}\uc2  will have the news on this topic all day. Our full report is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/31/hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-death-raid-iran-home-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The event for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her soon-to-be-named running mate next Tuesday in Philadelphia will mark the start of a lightning tour for the pair through the seven swing states that are expected to decide the election this November.\par \par \uc2 After Pennsylvania they will travel to somewhere to be confirmed in western Wisconsin; Detroit in Michigan; North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Raleigh; Savannah in Georgia; Phoenix, the capital of Arizona; and Las Vegas in Nevada, Politico reports this morning. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if that\u8217\'20\'19s the sequence of travel.\par \par \uc2 Harris, currently US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, can expect to be confirmed as the Democratic nominee for president next month at the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention, to be held in Chicago, and her choice of running mate will also be confirmed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and vice-presidential pick will make first joint appearance in Pennsylvania, 6 August\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going to appear at a campaign event in Philadelphia next Tuesday with her choice of running mate for the Democratic ticket to fight the presidential election campaign this November.\par \par \uc2 Harris has not yet named her vice-presidential choice and it\u8217\'20\'19s not yet been made clear exactly when she will, but her campaign, Harris for President, has confirmed that she and the relevant person will stump together in the Pennsylvania city on 6 August.\par \par \uc2 She has not yet been confirmed as the presidential nominee for the Democrats, that formal step requires a vote at the party\u8217\'20\'19s national convention next month, but her position is presumed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to make first appearance with running mate next Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US presidential race}}}\uc2  has moved into another gear since \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew}}}\uc2  from his re-election campaign and endorsed his vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to replace him at the top of the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s big buzz today and a lot more excitement to come in the next few days and before the Democratic national convention in Chicago next month, with the Republican nominee, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , throwing his weight around as well. You can follow developments here, as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s afoot:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Harris for President campaign has announced that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her running mate \u8211\'20\'13 who has yet to be confirmed \u8211\'20\'13 will appear together in their first joint event next Tuesday in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, one of the seven crucial swing states. This follows news yesterday when various sources were saying she\u8217\'20\'19d announce her VP pick in the next {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/when-will-kamala-harris-announce-vp-pick"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six or seven days}}}\uc2 . That firmed up overnight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The pair will follow the event in Philly with a whizz through six more swing states within four days, Wisconsin, Michigan, North Carolina, Georgia, Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pundits are opining that the announcement about Pennsylvania doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily point to that state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Democrat Josh Shapiro, as the shoo-in for the ticket, so that leaves \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-running-mate-vp-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the veep stakes}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D still a live action sport.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke at the best-attended and most enthusiastic Democratic campaign rally of the race so far, last night in Atlanta, Georgia. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak in the same arena this weekend. She taunted him about his apparent cold feet over debating her, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-atlanta-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the line}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf you got something to say, say it to my face.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said in a Fox interview that aired last night that a President Harris would struggle on the world stage and that she would \u8220\'20\'1Cbe like a play toy\u8221\'20\'1D for foreign leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 About eight out of 10 Democrats say they would be very or somewhat satisfied if Harris is confirmed as the Democratic nominee for president. The survey from the AP-Norc Center for Public Affairs Research was conducted after Biden withdrew from the race. After his dire debate performance against Trump last month, a poll from the same firm asking the same about him returned the result that only four in 10 Democrats were would be happy with him as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is due to appear on a panel in an unexpected venue today \u8211\'20\'13 the annual conference of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ), which is being held in Chicago. We have one of our staffers there, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/gloria-oladipo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gloria Oladipo}}}\uc2 , and will bring you blog updates and a news report. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was not scheduled to attend and has not changed her plans since Trump popped up.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240731ek7v0025x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
