\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump favorite Kari Lake wins Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Senate primary\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,172 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 July 2024\par 14:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Far-right firebrand to face off against Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat vacated by \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, the far-right firebrand and favorite of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has won Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Senate primary.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press projected the race at 8.44pm Arizona time on Tuesday night. Lake rose to prominence as a gubernatorial candidate in 2022, when she r {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/10/kari-lake-senate-bid-arizona-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efused to concede}}}\uc2  the race to her Democratic challenger, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Having secured a primary victory, she will face off against the Democratic US representative \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  for an open Senate seat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/kyrsten-sinema-not-running-reelection-senate-arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vacated by}}}\uc2  the centrist independent senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lake, endorsed by Trump, was widely favored to win the primary against Mark Lamb, the sheriff of Pinal county. Lamb, who has far less name recognition and campaign funding than Lake, pulled in about 40% of the vote as of Tuesday night \u8211\'20\'13 a potential sign of general election trouble for Lake, who has alienated the more moderate voters required to win statewide in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Her contest, along with several key down-ballot races, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/arizona-primaries-republican-election-deniers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered a gauge}}}\uc2  for the relative strength of the Maga movement in a key swing state that has been racked with election chaos brought on by a far-right flank pushing false claims about election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Lake, a former news anchor who rocked on to the national stage by becoming one of the most ardent and telegenic faces of election denialism, once carried a sledgehammer on stage and told supporters she would use it on electronic voting machines.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/dscc/status/1818492047881285885"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quickly launched an ad}}}\uc2  against Lake, where she talks about how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills should be illegal and brands her as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpower-hungry liar who only cares about herself\u8221\'20\'1D. Gallego {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RubenGallego/status/1818490921962684761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s official \u8211\'20\'13 my opponent is Kari Lake. Arizona, the choice is clear: Kari wants to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I will always protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Election prognosticators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/rating-changes-arizona-senate-and-az-6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/senate-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cook Political Report}}}\uc2  rank the race as leaning Democratic, citing Lake\u8217\'20\'19s election denialism and belief in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions as factors moving the race toward Democrats. Polling on the matchup between Gallego and Lake has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections2024.thehill.com/arizona/arizona-senate-gallego-lake/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generally shown}}}\uc2  Gallego up a few points over Lake.\par \par \uc2 The race is key nationally for the balance of power in the US Senate \u8211\'20\'13 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/senate-races-2024-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 need to keep it}}}\uc2  in their control to maintain their 51-49 majority in the chamber. It is one of few close races around the country expected to see massive funding and attention as November nears.\par \par \uc2 Far-right election deniers starred in several other key Republican primary races. Abe Hamadeh, who repeatedly tried to have his loss in the 2022 attorney general election overturned and has spread conspiracy theories about election security, is leading in a crowded Republican primary in the state\u8217\'20\'19s deep-red eighth congressional district, where Trump made the rare move to endorse two candidates, including Hamadeh.\par \par \uc2 His Republican rivals included the venture capitalist Blake Masters, who Trump endorsed last-minute, as well as state senator and fake elector Anthony Kern, Ben Toma, the speaker of the Arizona house; \uc2 Trent Franks\uc2 , who resigned from Congress after staffers claimed he asked them to serve as surrogates for him; and political newcomer Pat Briody.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Mark Finchem\uc2 , who has still not accepted that he lost his bid for secretary of state in 2022 has the lead in a race against the relatively moderate Republican Ken Bennett for a state senate seat.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Maricopa county \u8211\'20\'13 which includes Phoenix \u8211\'20\'13 election deniers vied for positions that could give them oversight in future elections. Early results show a mixed bag for election-defending county officials.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Richer, the Maricopa county recorder who became a nationally known voice for defending elections and sued Lake for defamation over election falsehoods, was behind in his race for re-election as of Tuesday night. He is falling behind Justin Heap, a state representative who will not say whether he believes the 2020 or 2022 elections were stolen, but has called Maricopa county elections a \u8220\'20\'1Claughingstock\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://azmirror.com/2024/07/12/stephen-richer-justin-heap-face-off-in-republican-primary-for-maricopa-county-recorder/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported bills}}}\uc2  that stemmed from election conspiracies. Another challenger, Don Hiatt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/local/phoenix/2024/07/09/maricopa-county-recorder-election-2024-the-candidates/74269627007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  the 2020 election was stolen and wants to curtail voting access and is in third.\par \par \uc2 Debbie Lesko\uc2 , an outgoing Republican congresswoman who is endorsed by Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/01/07/us/elections/electoral-college-biden-objectors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to overturn}}}\uc2  election results on 6 January 2021, has a strong lead in the primary to join the county board of supervisors over another election denier, Bob Branch, a professor at the Christian college \uc2 Grand Canyon University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Maricopa county board of supervisors and recorder played a crucial role in 2020 standing up to pressure from Trump and his allies in their scheme to overturn the results of that year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The recorder and many board members have faced ongoing threats, some of which have been prosecuted and led to prison sentences. The pressure has remained intense in the lead-up to this year\u8217\'20\'19s elections, with errors such as printing problems in the 2022 election adding fuel to rightwing conspiracies.\par \par \uc2 Amid the threats and harassment, two supervisors, \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  and Clint Hickman, decided not to run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 For Gates\u8217\'20\'19s seat, the moderate former state lawmaker Kate Brophy McGee is far ahead in the primary against Tabatha LaVoie, who said on her campaign website that she wanted to restore voter confidence because: \u8220\'20\'1COur County cannot continue to raise doubts about the integrity of our elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jack Sellers, currently the board chair, is trailing far behind Mark Stewart, a council member in the Phoenix suburb of Chandler. Stewart {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chandlernews.com/santan/news/drama-in-gop-supervisor-race/article_2025642c-f387-11ee-bede-93a156f08328.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not say}}}\uc2  whether he would have certified results in 2020 or 2022 and claims he will restore confidence in county elections.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Galvin, who was not on the board in 2020 but has defended county elections since taking office after beating election-denying candidates in 2022, is fending off a challenge from Michelle Ugenti-Rita, a former state lawmaker and Lake-endorsed candidate who promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight for election integrity\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctake back Maricopa County from the establishment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the Democratic side, the former state senator Raquel Ter\u225\'00\'E1n is trailing in her primary for Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s third district, for the seat that will be vacated by Gallego. A longtime organiser against anti-immigrant laws in the state, T\u233\'00\'E9ran focused her campaign on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Her main rival former city council member in Phoenix, Yassamin Ansari, had raised more funds and secured several key labour endorsements, and has the lead as of Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 And in what is probably his last unsuccessful bid for office, the former Maricopa county sheriff \uc2 Joe Arpaio\uc2 , notorious for his harsh immigration regime, was trounced in a local mayoral race to lead the Phoenix suburb of Fountain Hills. Arpaio, 92, was recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/latino/biden-ad-trump-arpaio-kiss-immigration-latinos-rcna156389"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kissed on the cheek}}}\uc2  by Trump at a rally in Arizona. In his run for mayor, one of his main ideas was to make the town\u8217\'20\'19s eponymous fountain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/07/joe-arpaio-still-hasnt-made-peace-with-his-own-demise/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 go higher}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240731ek7v000p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
