\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Say it to my face\u8217\'20\'19 says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as she again challenges \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to debate \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now) with Maya Yang and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 11,004 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 July 2024\par 23:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed. You can find our latest US elections coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing shortly. You can find our latest US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  is on CNN now. In an interview on Monday with \uc2 CBS\uc2 , Whitmer said that she has not been vetted by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s office and expects Harris to announce her pick within the week, which would confirm the Democratic ticket at least two weeks before the Democratic national convention begins on 19 August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 She has reiterated that now \u8211\'20\'13 she has not been vetted and will not be the pick. She says, instead, that she will be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbest friend\u8221\'20\'1D on the ground.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 During the warmup to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appearance Tuesday in Atlanta, mayor \uc2 Andre Dickens\uc2  noted that this was the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s 15th time visiting the state since 2021. Harris has been in Atlanta so often that she may as well have rented a condo in Buckhead to save money.\par \par \uc2 For the last two years, Harris has been \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief campaign surrogate in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , making deliberate connections with campaign organizers and Black community leaders, a weapon in the Democratic arsenal that Republicans have not been able to match.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia is on everybody\u8217\'20\'19s mind,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , the senator and reverend, to a boisterous crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd there\u8217\'20\'19s a reason. Because of what you did in 2020, 2021, everybody knows that the road to the White House goes through Georgia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-atlanta-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s political stars out in force for Kamala Harris on \u8216\'20\'18road to White House\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 The fast-growing, diversifying Atlanta suburbs and exurbs offer the most opportunity for swings, especially from GOP-leaning moderates disenchanted with Trump.\par \par \uc2 For Harris, the AP reports, that means depending on voters as varied as Michael Sleister, a white suburbanite, and Allen Smith, a Black man who lives not far from downtown Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Sleister, who considers himself an independent, has lived in Forsyth County for 35 years. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve voted Republican many times in my life,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, but not since the GOP took a rightward turn during President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow I see the Republican Party as representing a direct threat to my grandchildren,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that he sees Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cas just a horrible person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith is a 41-year-old Atlanta native who has become a first-time campaign volunteer since Harris became the likely nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was driving when I heard the news about President Biden endorsing her, and I started pounding my fist \u8212\'20\'14 I decided right then I would do whatever I could to help her get elected,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has spoken to people at the rally:\par \par \uc2 The roughly 8,000-capacity basketball arena at \uc2 Georgia State University\uc2  was filled to its rafters with thousands of voters waving signs, dancing to the Harris campaign soundtrack and celebrating an atmosphere that would not have been possible just 10 days ago, with the party reeling over whether the 81-year-old Biden would remain in the race after a dismal performance magnified concerns about his age and abilities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is like Barack Obama 2008 on steroids for me,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mildred Hobson Doss, a 59-year-old who came downtown from suburban Lilburn. \u8220\'20\'1CI would have voted for President Biden again. But we are ready.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris is hoping the rally, which featured a performance by hip-hop star Megan Thee Stallion, will help affirm her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s momentum. The campaign argues that Harris\u8217\'20\'19 appeal to young people, working-age women and non-white voters has scrambled the dynamics in Georgia and other states that are demographically similar, from North Carolina to Nevada and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe energy is infectious,\u8221\'20\'1D said Georgia Democratic Chairwoman \uc2 Nikema Williams\uc2 , a congresswoman from Atlanta. \u8220\'20\'1CMy phone has been blowing up. People want to be part of this movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Harris challenging Trump to debate her:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris just looked at the camera and spoke directly to Trump, "Well, Donald. I do hope you'll reconsider to meet me on the debate stage. Because as the saying goes, if\par \par \uc2 you got something to say, say it to my face." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kUbsubCZQm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kUbsubCZQm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Reese Jones (@PoliticusSarah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PoliticusSarah/status/1818428885857435733?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 The novelty of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s energy and charisma has not worn off. She is forceful, confident and responsive \u8211\'20\'13 unruffled by applause or unexpected chanting. It is striking compared to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s slow, often quiet delivery.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary: Harris speaks at rally in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 Here is a recap of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs many of you know, before I was elected vice president \u8230\'20\'26 I was an elected attorney general and an elected district attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHear me when I say, I know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s type, and I have been dealing with people like him my entire career,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris added, touting her prosecution of fraudsters and cheaters and referencing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criminal convictions and the findings of fraud in his businesses.\par \par \uc2 This elicited chants of \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She noted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fraudulent school \u8211\'20\'13 well, Trump was found liable for committing sexual abuse. As an attorney general, I held big wall street banks accountable for fraud. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was found guilty of fraud. In this campaign, I will proudly put my record against his any day, including on the issue of immigration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke of walking underground tunnels at the California border and prosecuting traffickers, and pledged to bring back the border security bill that was tanked in congress by Republicans to preserve the issue in the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Referencing a Migos song -- popular as an Atlanta group -- she said \u8220\'20\'1CHe does not walk it as he talks it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBuilding up the middle class will be a defining goal of my presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen our middle class is strong, America is strong. To keep our middle class strong, families need relief from the high cost of living so that they have a chance not to get by but to get ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said she would go after price gouging and hidden fees by banks and other companies, and take on corporate landlords to cap unfair rent increases, and to cap prescription drug costs.\par \par \uc2 Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t debate, but he and JD Vance have lots to say about her, she said. She described it as plain weird.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the saying goes, if you\u8217\'20\'19ve got something to say, say it to my face,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, as the crowd exploded.\par \par \uc2 Georgia, today I ask you, are you ready to get to work.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 'If you've got something to say, say it to my face,' Harris says as she challenges Trump to a debate\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are signs \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is feeling\u8221\'20\'1D the competition, she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou may have noticed he pulled out of the debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She repeats the assertion made by her campaign in recent days that Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cjust plain weird\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do hope Trump will agree to meet me on the debate stage, because as the saying goes, if you got something to say, say it to my face.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd loses it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe who believe in reproductive freedom will stop Trump\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. She promises to sign into law a bill to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNovember 5th is in 98 days,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we have a fight in front of us. And we are the underdogs in this race. We are. But you see, this is a people-powered campaign. In fact after I announced my candidacy we saw the best grassroots fundraising in history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says, and the crowd chants the words.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COurs is a fight for the future, and it is a fight for freedom. And we are witnessing a full on assault from hard-won rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She talks about the \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom to love who you want, openly and with pride\u8221\'20\'1D to particularly loud cheers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the freedom of a woman to make decisions about her own body, and not have her government tell her what to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says forcefully, to the biggest cheers of the evening so far.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Now Harris talks about Project 25 \u8211\'20\'13 the words are met with loud boos.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile inflation is down and wages are up, prices are still to high",\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says. \u8220\'20\'1COn day one I will take down price gouging and hidden costs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will take on corporate landlords and cap unfair rent increases,\u8221\'20\'1D she says to huge applause. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we will take on big pharma to cap prescription drug costs for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris repeats her message that building up the middle class will be a defining goal of her presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Our story on that bill, from May:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/senate-democrats-immigration-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Republicans block bipartisan border security bill for a second time}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 As president I will bring back the border security bill that Trump killed and I will sign it into law, Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 '\u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been talking a big game about securing the border, but he does not walk the walk \u8211\'20\'13 or as my friend says, he does not walk it like he talks it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs many of you know, before I was elected VP, I was elected attorney general,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. And lists her other roles. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd in those roles, I took on perpetrators of all kinds. Predators who abused women, fraudsters who ripped off consumers, cheaters,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, who broke roles for their own gain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have been dealing with people like [Trump] for my entire career,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 These are lines that Harris has used often in recent weeks \u8211\'20\'13 as well as in her 2020 campaign ad.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was just found guilty of Fraud,\u8221\'20\'1D she says \u8220\'20\'1C34 counts\u8221\'20\'1D. The crowd chants \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D and she appears to not respond, instead quickly starting to speak again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 The supporters standing behind Harris are wearing a lot of pink. Harris thanks former Georgia Representative \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris says the path to the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cstarts on this stage\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cyou helped us win in 2020 and you\u8217\'20\'19re going to help us win again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd is, as they say, going wild. Harris is saying thank you, thank you everyone \u8211\'20\'13they keep cheering.\par \par \uc2 Thank you all, thank you very much, thank you everybody, she says. \u8220\'20\'1COh it\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back in Georgia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is at the podium in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has meanwhile responded to comments Trump made earlier about Harris and her husband.\par \par \uc2 Trump said in an interview that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t like Jewish people\u8221\'20\'1D and seemed to agree with a radio host who called second gentleman Doug Emhoff \u8216\'20\'18a crappy Jew.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The campaign says:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is hateful, despicable, and should not be our president.\par \par \uc2 He roots against America. He insults America. Why would we want to put him in charge of America?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  thinks he can score points with Jewish voters by denigrating them. He is wrong.\par \par \uc2 It goes on to list various \u8220\'20\'1Ccrappy\u8221\'20\'1D achievements by the former president, and his \u8220\'20\'1Clong history\u8221\'20\'1D of attacking Jewish people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is due to begin speaking shortly at a campaign event in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s highest court heard arguments Tuesday in a Republican challenge of a law that allows any registered voter to cast a mail-in ballot during the early voting period.\par \par \uc2 The case, which is led by Representative \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  and includes other lawmakers and the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , is part of a widespread GOP effort to tighten voting rules after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Democrats approved the mail voting expansion law last year. The Republican challenge argues that it violates voting provisions in the state Constitution.\par \par \uc2 The hourlong arguments before the New York Court of Appeals in Albany hinged on technical readings of the Constitution, specifically whether certain passages would allow for the state Legislature to expand mail voting access.\par \par \uc2 At certain points in the hearing, judges quizzed attorneys on whether a constitutional provision that says eligible voters are entitled to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cat every election\u8221\'20\'1D would mean a physical polling place or simply the election in general.\par \par \uc2 Michael Y. Hawrylchak, an attorney representing the Republicans, said that provision \u8220\'20\'1Cpresupposes a physical place\u8221\'20\'1D for in-person voting. Deputy Solicitor General Jeffrey W. Lang, who is representing the state, said the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Cjust refers to a process of selecting an office holder\u8221\'20\'1D and not any physical polling place.\par \par \uc2 Democrats first tried to expand mail voting through a constitutional amendment in 2021, but voters rejected the proposal after a campaign from conservatives who said it would lead to voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Lower courts have dismissed the Republican lawsuit in decisions that said the Legislature has the constitutional authority to make rules on voting and the Constitution doesn\u8217\'20\'19t require voting specifically to occur in person on election day.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear when the Court of Appeals will rule.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  emerged as one of the early favourites to be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate last week, after being asked to submit personal information in a vice-presidential vetting process:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked Sen. \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  about concerns his selection as VP could open up a Senate seat in a swing state in 2026, and Kelly said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think it would be an issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats have been really good about winning statewide races in the state of Arizona. We figured this out. We\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6FEVFDLTyF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6FEVFDLTyF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1818406496062804345?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , have jointly urged Venezuelan authorities to release full, transparent and detailed presidential election voting data.\par \par \uc2 The leaders spoke on the phone earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/30/venezuela-maduro-election-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maduro vows crackdown on Venezuela election protests after victory claim}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some scenes from the Harris campaign rally in Atlanta, via NBC and Kamala HQ:\par \par \uc2 enltrThousands of voters are currently swag surfing at the Harris campaign rally. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ilxjpLxtBc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ilxjpLxtBc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yamiche Alcindor (@Yamiche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1818412646074372491?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSen \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  at the Harris rally in Atlanta: Some days I feel bad for Republicans because they have to figure out how to run a criminal against a prosecutor.... The American people are the jury and we are going to get the verdict right and send VP Harris to the WH.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yamiche Alcindor (@Yamiche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche/status/1818408953606287442?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReverendWarnock?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ReverendWarnock}}}\uc2  : Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to steal your vote. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is trying to earn your vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TUk03Vss0t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TUk03Vss0t}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1818412593368768705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting Harris to speak in half an hour\u8217\'20\'19s time, and will bring that to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 MSNBC producer Kyle Griffin reports that Harris is preparing to embark on a battleground tour next week. The Harris campaign has said it would name running mate by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MSNBC}}}\uc2  : Vice President Harris and her yet-to-be-named running mate will hit the campaign trail next week on a battleground state tour.\par \par \uc2 This is the latest indication that her vice presidential selection process is nearing its end.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1818411288835346537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dunn has been a Democratic operative for decades. She worked in President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House and on multiple political campaigns. In a statement, she thanked Biden and Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been an honor and privilege to serve in this White House, with this President and this team, during this transformational term,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am grateful to President Biden and Vice President Harris for their leadership and giving me the opportunity to be part of what they have accomplished for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  was first to report Dunn\u8217\'20\'19s exit.\par \par \uc2 A source familiar with the decision said she would be helping a super political-action committee that is working to elect Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign adviser Anita Dunn to leave White House\par \par \uc2 Anita Dunn, a longtime adviser to President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who oversaw communications strategy and helped steer his 2020 election campaign, is departing the White House to work for a super political-action committee that is supporting Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Dunn\u8217\'20\'19s departure is the first and only so far among Biden\u8217\'20\'19s senior staff in the aftermath of the president\u8217\'20\'19s disastrous debate against former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last month that sparked a crisis within the Democratic Party and led to his exit from the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 Dunn was one of the officials involved in decision-making about the debate; her husband, attorney Bob Bauer, reportedly played Trump in the debate prep sessions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFour years ago, when I launched my campaign for the battle for the soul of our nation, I was grateful Anita Dunn was right there with me,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI deeply value her counsel and friendship and I will continue to rely on her partnership and insights as we finish the job over the next six months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Hello US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively day and soon \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will speak at a campaign event in Atlanta, Georgia, as the latest opinion polls show support for her is growing.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re handing over to our colleague Helen Sullivan now. She\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to bring you the news developments as they happen, including \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech in just under an hour\u8217\'20\'19s time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has gained ground against Republican presidential rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in six of the seven swing states since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped out of the presidential race, according to a Bloomberg News/\uc2 Morning Consult\uc2  poll of registered voters published today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Depending on which poll you read, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are neck and neck in the presidential race. That\u8217\'20\'19s according to a new Reuters and \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll. The poll, which was completed on Sunday, showed that the vice-president was supported by 43% of registered voters while the former president was supported by 42%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not attend the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) conference in Chicago, according to a source familiar with her schedule, citing logistical challenges getting to Chicago days after launching her campaign. Harris is heading to Houston this week to attend the funeral of the late Texas congresswoman \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\uc2  as well as conducting a rapid search for her running mate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked if she had chosen her running mate yet while boarding a plane to Atlanta, Georgia. Harris replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNot yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Paul Dans, the director of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2025 presidential transition project, has stepped down from his role, according to reports. The move comes after pressure from the Trump campaign leadership, and an ongoing power rift over staffing control for a potential second Trump administration, the Daily Beast\u8217\'20\'19s Roger Sollenberg writes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s acting director, Ronald Rowe, has told lawmakers he was \u8220\'20\'1Cashamed\u8221\'20\'1D by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/trump-rally-shooter-jfk-assasination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Rowe, appearing before a meeting of the Senate judiciary committee and homeland security and governmental affairs committee, said he considered it indefensible that the roof used by the gunman was unsecured, during the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Pennsylvania earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Monday repeated his weekend remarks to Christian summit attendees that they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never need to vote again}}}\uc2  if he returns to the presidency in November. Trump, in an interview with Fox News that aired last night, was asked to explain what he meant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when he told a crowd on Friday }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget out and vote, just this time. \u8220\'20\'1CThat statement is very simple, I said, \u8216\'20\'18Vote for me, you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna have to do it ever again\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has announced a $50m advertising blitz ahead of the Democratic national convention next month with a television ad that portrays the presumptive Democratic nominee as \u8220\'20\'1Cfearless\u8221\'20\'1D. The 60-second ad will be the first in a series of paid media efforts ahead of the convention, which begins 19 August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Zoom call meant to rally \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite dudes\u8221\'20\'1D in support of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s run for the White House raised more than $4m from about 190,000 participants, including numerous celebrities, according to the presumptive Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s campaign. Showing up were a bunch of top Democrats and stars including Jeff Bridges, Mark Hamill, Mark Ruffalo, and others.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris gaining ground in some key states - latest poll\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has gained ground against Republican presidential rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in six of the seven swing states since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped out of the presidential race, according to a Bloomberg News/\uc2 Morning Consult\uc2  poll of registered voters published today.\par \par \uc2 The poll \u8211\'20\'13 conducted online from 24\u8211\'20\'1328 July \u8211\'20\'13 shows Harris leading Trump in Michigan by 11 percentage points, while in Arizona, Wisconsin and Nevada, she has a 2-point advantage, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump is ahead of Harris in Pennsylvania by 4 points and in North Carolina by 2 points. They are on equal footing in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is the only state of the seven where Trump has narrowed his deficit with Harris in comparison with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance in a previous poll.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s poll has a margin of error of between 3 and 5 points, depending on the state.\par \par \uc2 In a Bloomberg/Morning Consult poll conducted 1\u8211\'20\'135 July, Trump was ahead of Biden in Arizona by 3 percentage points; in Georgia by 1 point; in Nevada by 3 points; in North Carolina by 3 points; and in Pennsylvania by 7 points. Biden led in Michigan by 5 points and in Wisconsin by 3 points, the poll showed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will announce her vice-presidential pick as early as Monday before embarking on a multistate battleground tour with her new running mate later in the week, two sources familiar with the planning said on Tuesday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The high-stakes decision on who will run with the current vice-president on her presidential ticket has taken center stage since she became the Democratic frontrunner for the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to announce VP pick as early as Monday \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to announce who will be her running mate in her campaign for president as early as Monday, the Reuters news wire is reporting this evening, as an exclusive, citing sources but as yet giving no more detail.\par \par \uc2 This echoes what \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, said yesterday, that Harris would choose and announce \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next six, seven days\u8221\'20\'1D, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-vp-trump-election-politics-updates?page=with:block-66a8e6e08f08869a079e8df6#block-66a8e6e08f08869a079e8df6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 we blogged}}}\uc2  earlier.\par \par \uc2 But anything that echoes or strengthens that prediction is fascinating, so we\u8217\'20\'19ll watch closely.\par \par \uc2 Harris is the presumptive Democratic nominee for president in this election, after \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew from}}}\uc2  his re-election campaign nine days ago and anointed Harris as his chosen successor at the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 At this rate, she can expect to be officially voted in as the nominee at the party\u8217\'20\'19s national convention next month, in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not attend the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) conference in Chicago, according to a source familiar with her schedule, citing logistical challenges getting to Chicago days after launching her campaign.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is heading to Houston this week to attend the funeral of the late Texas congresswoman \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\uc2  as well as conducting a rapid search for her running mate.\par \par \uc2 The source said Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign offered to participate in a virtual fireside chat, or to host an in-person fireside chat with Harris at a later date, but the request was denied. The source said Harris\u8217\'20\'19s team will continue to work toward a possible solution with the \uc2 NABJ\uc2  board.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the sidelines of the centrist WelcomeFest in Washington DC, Will Rollins, the Democratic nominee in a competitive California House district, said Republicans would have a \u8220\'20\'1Ctricky\u8221\'20\'1D time trying to paint \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerously liberal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomebody who goes into law enforcement is not a leftwing ideologue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rollins, a former prosecutor. Already he said she was having a positive impact on down-ballot races. His campaign alone raised a six-figure sum in the 48 hours after her ascent, he said.\par \par \uc2 Rollins noted that when Harris came up in California politics, she was criticized by activists as too conservative, despite the image Republicans are portraying of her as far-left.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe in fact was branded as much too conservative for San Francisco. So I think as voters actually learned more about her actual record it\u8217\'20\'19s going to work well for us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 To underline the point, Rollins said he first met Harris when she was the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general at an event with the then Republican governor Arnold Schwarzenegger, whom he worked for at the time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat kind of proves or disproves their attempt to paint her as an extremist. Here you have this Democratic statewide attorney general, who was working with a Republican governor in California at the time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI actually think that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the more underreported parts of her background, what she was able to do across party lines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also weighed in on who Harris might choose as her running mate. His choice was for fellow millennial, transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , who he called an \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible communicator\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump neck and neck in new Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are neck and neck in the presidential race, according to a new Reuters and \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll.\par \par \uc2 The poll, which was completed on Sunday, showed that the vice-president was supported by 43% of registered voters while the former president was supported by 42%.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a Reuters and \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll showed that Harris was leading by 44% to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 42%.\par \par \uc2 Reuters and \uc2 Ipsos\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest poll was conducted among 1,025 adults, including 876 registered voters, from 26 to 28 July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The departure of Paul Dans as the leader of Project 2025 could indicate the project\u8217\'20\'19s work is winding down or at least will not be taking such a public role in the lead-up to the November election, though the policy ideas outlined in its extensive conservative roadmap remain public.\par \par \uc2 Dans, a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalist, worked in personnel-related roles in the first Trump administration, including as chief of staff at the office of personnel management.\par \par \uc2 Although Kevin Roberts, the president of Heritage Foundation, claimed the change was always intended and followed a set timeline, the move underscores the unpopularity of Project 2025 for Trump, who has for weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/08/trump-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted}}}\uc2  to distance himself from it.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Trump claimed to \u8220\'20\'1Cknow nothing about Project 2025\u8221\'20\'1D and have \u8220\'20\'1Cno idea who is behind it\u8221\'20\'1D. The disavowal from Trump came after Roberts said:\par \par \uc2 We are in the process of the second American revolution, which will remain bloodless, if the left allows it to be.\par \par \uc2 At a recent rally in Michigan, Trump quipped about the project: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what the hell it is\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re seriously extreme.\u8221\'20\'1D But the project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/project-2025-trump-connections-similarities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 includes}}}\uc2  many former Trump administration officials and its aims often align with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policy ideas, albeit with far more detail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, said he has \u8220\'20\'1Ctotal confidence\u8221\'20\'1D in \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate choice.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he would support \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , the Arizona senator, as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 I have total confidence that Vice President Harris will choose a great vice-presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he was concerned about the prospect of a special election in Arizona, CNN reports that Schumer replied:\par \par \uc2 I have complete faith in Vice President Harris\u8217\'20\'19 choice.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Not even a day after audio of JD Vance telling donors that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was a threat and a \u8220\'20\'1Csucker punch\u8221\'20\'1D was leaked to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/trump-fbi-interview-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued to make headlines on Tuesday}}}\uc2 , as a previously unseen video of Vance was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KamalaHQ/status/1818281948403687674"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  by the Harris 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 In the video, Vance can be seen telling an interviewer that not having \u8220\'20\'1Ckids in your life\u8221\'20\'1D makes \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople more sociopathic\u8221\'20\'1D and makes the US a little bit \u8220\'20\'1Cless mentally stable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrUnearthed video: JD Vance says people who don\u8217\'20\'19t have children are \u8220\'20\'1Csociopathic,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Cpsychotic,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cderanged\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jaqL6BsXXF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jaqL6BsXXF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1818281948403687674?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 This comes as Vance continues to face backlash over comments he made in 2021 that recently resurfaced where he criticized the vice-president and other Democrats as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bunch of childless cat ladies who are miserable at their own lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday evening, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat down with Laura Ingraham of Fox News and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/trump-fbi-interview-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended Vance\u8217\'20\'19s comments}}}\uc2 , telling the host that his vice-presidential candidate was simply trying to show how much he values family life.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican vice-presidential candidate, JD Vance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/trump-fbi-interview-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made headlines again}}}\uc2  on Monday evening, after an audio recording of Vance speaking privately to donors on Saturday about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was leaked to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/29/jd-vance-kamala-harris-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post.}}}\par \par \uc2 Vance reporedtly told donors that Harris was a threat and \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit of a political sucker punch\u8221\'20\'1D to the Trump Vance campaign.\par \par \uc2 Vance also reportedly said:\par \par \uc2 The bad news is that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  does not have the same baggage as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , because whatever we might have to say, Kamala is a lot younger. And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is obviously not struggling in the same ways that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did.\par \par \uc2 The comments contradict \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s own statements on Harris since Biden withdrew from the race, as he has told reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that}}}\uc2  he did not think switching out Biden for Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cwould make much difference\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI would define her in a very similar [way] that I define him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even Vance himself has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/29/jd-vance-kamala-harris-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  that there was in effect no difference in running against Biden versus Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to the news of Project 2025 director Paul Dans \u8217\'20\'19 departure. In a statement, it said:\par \par \uc2 President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has been very clear for over a year that Project 2025 had nothing to do with the campaign, did not speak for the campaign, and should not be associated with the campaign or the President in any way.\par \par \uc2 Reports of Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s demise would be greatly welcomed and should serve as notice to anyone or any group trying to misrepresent their influence with President Trump and his campaign \u8212\'20\'14 it will not end well for you.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The work of Project 2025 will continue despite its director, Paul Dans, stepping down from his role, Politico reported, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 The report adds that the source said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe goal of Project 2025 was always to have their work done by the time of the Republican National Convention which ended in late July\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-vp-trump-election-politics-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66a92f4d8f08bbdfa9de02d9#block-66a92f4d8f08bbdfa9de02d9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more on the news}}}\uc2  that Paul Dans, the director of Project 2025, has stepped down from his role at \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kevin Roberts, the president of the conservative thinktank, has confirmed that Dans is leaving his post.\par \par \uc2 Dans \u8220\'20\'1Cbuilt the project from scratch and bravely led this endeavor over the past two years\u8221\'20\'1D but is now \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving up to the front where the fight remains\u8221\'20\'1D, Roberts said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Under Paul Dans\u8217\'20\'19 leadership, Project 2025 has completed exactly what it set out to do: bringing together over 110 leading conservative organizations to create a unified conservative vision, motivated to devolve power from the unelected administrative state, and returning it to the people.\par \par \uc2 Dans informed staff at the thinktank this week of his decision to step down, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/project-2025-head-steps-down-89cba52b?mod=politics_lead_story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro, who is considered to be among the leading contenders for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential running mate, said the vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Cwill make the best decision for her and her country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania governor was asked about the significance of having a Jewish vice-presidential nominee amid Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , NBC News reports. Shapiro replied:\par \par \uc2 It is a deeply personal decision for the vice-president to make, who she wants to run with, who she wants to govern with and who can help best move America forward. I think there are so many people within the Democratic party who are extraordinary people, extraordinary public servants, and she will make the best decision for her and her country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  released dueling campaign ads on Tuesday, as the reshaped presidential election began to grind into gear with 98 days to go.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s ad, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q7Yr4U5Clls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fearless}}}\uc2 , was her first since she became the de facto Democratic nominee, after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  halted his re-election campaign and endorsed her. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take our country backward,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 To give tax breaks to billionaires and big corporations and end the Affordable Care Act. But we are not going back.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s ad, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://app.frame.io/presentations/a2bb65e7-a32e-4cec-9258-847977d4cf76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I Don\u8217\'20\'19t Understand}}}\uc2 , used a snippet of Harris answering a question about immigration policy to bolster a hardline message about drugs, crime, terrorism and the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Showing footage of her dancing, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ad called Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed, weak, dangerously liberal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she has 'not yet' chosen her running mate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked if she had chosen her running mate yet while boarding a plane to Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Harris replied:\par \par \uc2 Not yet.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  boards AF2 for a campaign rally with Megan Thee Stallion in Atlanta Tuesday, reporters on the tarmac asked if she's chosen her own running mate.\par \par \uc2 "Not yet," she said, per pooler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Emilylgoodin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Emilylgoodin}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3Oknel9nQw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3Oknel9nQw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DJ Judd (@DJJudd) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DJJudd/status/1818354725278171604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Head of Project 2025 steps down - reports\par \par \uc2 Paul Dans, the director of \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2025 presidential transition project, has stepped down from his role, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The move comes after pressure from the Trump campaign leadership, and an ongoing power rift over staffing control for a potential second Trump administration, the Daily Beast\u8217\'20\'19s Roger Sollenberg writes.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Project 2025 director Paul Dans has stepped down at Heritage Foundation after pressure from Trump campaign leadership, ongoing power rift over staffing control for potential second Trump admin, per internal email. This suggests Project 2025 will likely shut down. Story TK.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Roger Sollenberger (@SollenbergerRC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SollenbergerRC/status/1818340251548762247?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Semafor\u8217\'20\'19s Kadia Goba reports that this does not mean that Project 2025 is shutting down.\par \par \uc2 enltrCan confirm Project 2025 is not shutting down, from a source familiar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FwmsiMgZW6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/FwmsiMgZW6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kadia Goba (@kadiagoba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kadiagoba/status/1818349251581149576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Journalists at the White House media briefing have been hoping to draw the press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , about whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are discussing her forthcoming choice of who will be her running mate.\par \par \uc2 Now that the US president has passed the torch for the election campaign to his vice-president, making her the presumptive presidential nominee, with the support of the rest of the top echelon of senior Democrats, who\u8217\'20\'19s she talking to about the second slot on the ticket for November?\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe president has been in public service for more than 54 years, he was vice-president for eight years, president for 3.5 years and six more months, and I think as a leader of the Democratic party he always offers up advice, a little bit of wisdom that he has, on multiple fronts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In her role as White House press secretary, Jean-Pierre cannot speak on election campaign matters, so is obliged to be careful and cryptic.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a role he plays, as well, with the vice-president. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to speak to the campaign \u8230\'20\'26When she became vice-president herself, he offered his advice as a mentor to her, but I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to go beyond that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Roughly 7% of w??omen of reproductive age in the US have attempted to induce their own abortions outside the formal healthcare system, a new study has found, up from 5% before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  fell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 2022}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The study, published on Tuesday in the Jama medical journal, determined how many people reported ever \u8220\'20\'1Cself-managing\u8221\'20\'1D their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2021 and again in 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a timeline that allowed researchers to examine how Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Health}}}\uc2  Organization, the supreme court case that overturned Roe, has affected self-managed abortions. People of color and LGBTQ+ people were more likely to report having ever attempted to end their own pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe think because it\u8217\'20\'19s getting more difficult to access facility-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lauren Ralph, the study\u8217\'20\'19s lead author and an epidemiologist at Advancing New Standards in Reproductive Health, a research group at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a really important piece of the puzzle, as we try to understand the full impact of the Dobbs decision on people\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Dobbs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 states have enacted}}}\uc2  near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. On Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/iowa-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa became the fourth state}}}\uc2  to ban the procedure past about six weeks of pregnancy, before many women even know they are pregnant. Full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/30/us-women-self-managed-abortion-pill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning and there\u8217\'20\'19s more to come, we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you up with the news as it happens. The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , is about to brief the gathered media in the west wing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where everything else stands:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her yet-to-be-named vice-presidential running mate will travel to a series of battleground states next week, Reuters is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the governor of Kentucky, is being vetted by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign as a potential vice-presidential nominee pick, NBC is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s acting director,Ronald Rowe, has told lawmakers he was \u8220\'20\'1Cashamed\u8221\'20\'1D by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/trump-rally-shooter-jfk-assasination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Rowe, appearing before a meeting of the Senate judiciary committee and homeland security and governmental affairs committee, said he considered it indefensible that the roof used by the gunman was unsecured, during the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Pennsylvania earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump on Monday repeated his weekend remarks to Christian summit attendees that they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never need to vote again}}}\uc2  if he returns to the presidency in November. Trump, in a n interview with Fox News that aired last night, was asked to explain what he meant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when he told a crowd on Friday }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget out and vote, just this time. \u8220\'20\'1CThat statement is very simple, I said, \u8216\'20\'18Vote for me, you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna have to do it ever again\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has responded to Trump \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-vp-trump-election-politics-updates?page=with:block-66a8f9ff8f08bbdfa9ddff49#block-66a8f9ff8f08bbdfa9ddff49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first major ad}}}\uc2  attacking her handling of the issue of immigration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has announced a $50m advertising blitz ahead of the Democratic national convention next month with a television ad that portrays the presumptive Democratic nominee as \u8220\'20\'1Cfearless\u8221\'20\'1D. The 60-second ad will be the first in a series of paid media efforts ahead of the convention, which begins 19 August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Zoom call meant to rally \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite dudes\u8221\'20\'1D in support of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s run for the White House raised more than $4m from about 190,000 participants, including numerous celebrities, according to the presumptive Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s campaign. Showing up were a bunch of top Democrats and stars including Jeff Bridges, Mark Hammill, Mark Ruffalo, and others.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will announce her running mate \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next six, seven days\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican primaries across Arizona today will test whether the far-right cadre focused on election denial still can win among their base, despite major losses in the 2022 primaries.\par \par \uc2 The state has been gripped with fights over elections for years, with candidates like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Kari Lake refusing to concede their respective races. These general election losses in 2020 and 2022 ended decades-long Republican dominance, delivering the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office and other top spots to Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The results could foretell whether Arizonans, particularly Arizona Republicans, are ready to move on from election denialism and the far-right flank that controls the state party. And that lesson could carry into November in the swing state, which Biden narrowly won in 2020 in an upset.\par \par \uc2 Lake, who lost the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race in 2022, is now running for Senate. She faces Mark Lamb, t he sheriff of Pinal county, but she is expected to win the Republican contest on Tuesday. The winner will face the Democratic representative \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 . The seat is open after senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  left the Democratic party and decided not to run for re-election, making it a top race to watch nationally for control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and her VP pick to tour battleground states next week \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her yet-to-be-named vice-presidential running mate will travel to a series of battleground states next week, Reuters is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: Harris and her yet-to-be named VP will hit the road next week on a battleground state tour, sources tell me and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nanditab1?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nanditab1}}}\uc2 , signaling that the decision process is nearing a close.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jarrett Renshaw (@JarrettRenshaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JarrettRenshaw/status/1818304694617292851?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The exact details on which states \u8211\'20\'13 and when \u8211\'20\'13 Harris and her running mate have not yet been firmed up, CNN is also reporting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 John Giles, the Republican mayor of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s third largest city and a previous thorn in the side of his party for endorsing Democrats, has thrown his support behind \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president.\par \par \uc2 Giles, who since 2014 has been mayor of Mesa near Phoenix, also rebuked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/opinion/op-ed/2024/07/29/mesa-mayor-republican-vote-kamala-harris/74583703007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion piece}}}\uc2  for the Arizona Republic published Monday.\par \par \uc2 Our party used to stand for the belief that every Arizonan, no matter their background or circumstances, should have the freedom, opportunity and security to live out their American Dream.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  r efused to accept the outcome of the 2020 election, Republicans have yet to course correct,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 The Republican party with Trump at its helm continues down the path of political extremism, away from focusing on our fundamental freedoms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  being vetted as possible Harris VP pick - report\par \par \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the governor of Kentucky, is being vetted by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign as a potential vice-presidential nominee pick, NBC is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 The political analyst Cliston Brown reports that Beshear has gotten additional security detail protection:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy source in Kentucky informs me that Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  has gotten additional security detail protection.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBPolitics (@ClistonBrown) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ClistonBrown/status/1818298514386141300?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Beshear\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely position as a Democratic governor of Kentucky \u8211\'20\'13 a state that voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by a margin of 25 points in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 makes him a compelling running mate for Harris.\par \par \uc2 In office, Beshear has vetoed Republican bills banning abortions and gender-affirming care for transgender minors, although the GOP-controlled state legislature was able to override his vetoes in both cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Acting Secret Service director Ronald Rowe, in his opening statement to lawmakers, said the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailure on multiple levels\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rowe accepted blame for the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s mistakes while also criticizing local law enforcement for not sharing information that a gunman had been spotted on a roof near the rally site in the minutes before the shooting, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 That information, Rowe said, had been kept \u8220\'20\'1Csiloed\u8221\'20\'1D among the local officers on the scene. He said:\par \par \uc2 That information, he said, had been kept \u8220\'20\'1Csiloed\u8221\'20\'1D among the local officers on the scene. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t know that there was this incident going on.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 New Secret Service director says he is 'ashamed' over failures before Trump shooting\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s acting director, Ronald Rowe, has told lawmakers he was \u8220\'20\'1Cashamed\u8221\'20\'1D by the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rowe, appearing before a meeting of the Senate judiciary committee and homeland security and governmental affairs committee, said he considered it indefensible that the roof used by the gunman was unsecured.\par \par \uc2 In his opening statement, Rowe said he had recently visited the site of the 13 July rally and \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat I saw made me ashamed.\u8221\'20\'1D He told lawmakers:\par \par \uc2 As a career law enforcement officer and a 25-year veteran with the Secret Service, I cannot defend why that roof was not better secured to prevent similar lapses from occurring in the future.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats controversial \u8216\'20\'18You won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote any more\u8217\'20\'19 claim\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Monday repeated his weekend remarks to Christian summit attendees that they would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never need to vote again}}}\uc2  if he returns to the presidency in November.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in an interview with Fox News that aired last night, was asked to explain what he meant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when he told a crowd on Friday }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget out and vote, just this time\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou won\u8217\'20\'19t have to do it any more. Four more years, you know what? It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fixed, it\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine, you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote any more, my beautiful Christians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat statement is very simple, I said, \u8216\'20\'18Vote for me, you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna have to do it ever again,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Fox News host Laura Ingraham.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s true, because we have to get the vote out. Christians are not known as a big voting group, they don\u8217\'20\'19t vote. And I\u8217\'20\'19m explaining that to them. You never vote. This time, vote. I\u8217\'20\'19ll straighten out the country, you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote any more, I won\u8217\'20\'19t need your vote any more, you can go back to not voting.\par \par \uc2 Trump denied threatening to permanently stay in office beyond his second \u8211\'20\'13 and constitutionally mandated final \u8211\'20\'13 four-year term.\par \par \uc2 When Ingraham pointed out that many Democrats had interpreted his comments to mean there would never be another election again, Trump responded that he had not heard that and continued to talk about how lots of Christians tend to not vote.\par \par \uc2 Christians do not vote well. They vote in very small percentages. Why? I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Maybe they\u8217\'20\'19re disappointed in things that are happening. I say, \u8216\'20\'18You don\u8217\'20\'19t vote.\u8217\'20\'19 I\u8217\'20\'19m saying, \u8216\'20\'18Go out \u8211\'20\'13 you must vote.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably\u8221\'20\'1D end up debating \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  but said he could \u8220\'20\'1Calso make a case for not doing it\u8221\'20\'1D, prompting the Harris campaign to say the former Republican president was \u8220\'20\'1Cscared\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in an interview with Fox News Channel that aired Monday night, was asked repeatedly whether he would commit to debating Harris.\par \par \uc2 I want to do a debate. But I also can say this. Everybody knows who I am. And now people know who she is.\par \par \uc2 Trump eventually said:\par \par \uc2 The answer is yes, I\u8217\'20\'19ll probably end up debating \u8230\'20\'26 The answer is yes, but I can also make a case for not doing it.\par \par \uc2 Trump has skipped debates before, including all the 2024 Republican presidential primary debates.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson, Ammar Moussa, said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s clear from tonight\u8217\'20\'19s question-dodging: He\u8217\'20\'19s scared he\u8217\'20\'19ll have to defend his running mate\u8217\'20\'19s weird attacks on women or his own calls to end elections in America in a debate against the vice president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , will appear at a rally in Atlanta, Georgia, on Saturday, his campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be in Atlanta today for a rally featuring the rapper Megan Thee Stallion in a state that some Democrats now consider up for grabs in the November election.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are hoping that the fresh burst of energy and a surge in fundraising that kicked off following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal and endorsement of Harris puts Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 the state that delivered Biden his narrowest victory margin in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 a toss-up again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator JD Vance \u8217\'20\'19s rollout as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate has not been smooth.\par \par \uc2 Under fire for misogyny including calling his opponents \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jul/29/the-republican-partys-obsession-with-families-has-taken-a-fanatical-turn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 childless cat ladies}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, his past opposition to Trump \u8211\'20\'13 including calling him \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-political-views-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2022/05/jd-vance-ohio-senate-trump-cultural-heroin/629754/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cultural heroin}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/jd-vance-trump-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 morally reprehensible human being}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ca disaster\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad man\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 has also been widely reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump defended Vance\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies\u8221\'20\'1D comments in an interview on Fox News that aired on Monday. Trump said:\par \par \uc2 He grew up in a very interesting family situation, and he feels family is good. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s anything wrong in saying that.\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s 2021 comments criticizing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other Democrats as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bunch of childless cat ladies who are miserable at their own lives\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/article/2024/jul/25/jennifer-aniston-criticises-jd-vance-childless-cat-ladies-comment-about-kamala-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompted a backlash}}}\uc2  and warnings from some political strategists that they could cost the Trump campaign valuable votes in a close election.\par \par \uc2 In the Fox interview, Trump said he did not place a higher value on people with families. He said:\par \par \uc2 You know, you don\u8217\'20\'19t meet the right person, or you don\u8217\'20\'19t meet any person. But you\u8217\'20\'19re just as good, in many cases, a lot better than a person that\u8217\'20\'19s in a family situation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 In newly uncovered remarks from 2017, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2024 vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, said \u8220\'20\'1Csome people who voted for Trump are racist and they voted for him for racist reasons\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRace definitely played a role in the 2016 election,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. The remarks were first reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/07/jd-vance-trump-voters-racist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by}}}\uc2  Mother Jones. Vance said:\par \par \uc2 I think that race will always play a role in our country. It\u8217\'20\'19s just sort of a constant fact of American life. And definitely some people who voted for Trump are racist and they voted for him for racist reasons.\par \par \uc2 He was then a Trump critic. But Vance is now a hard-right Republican US senator from Ohio, this month named as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate for the November election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign hits back at Trump immigration attack ad\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has responded to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/30/kamala-harris-vp-trump-election-politics-updates?page=with:block-66a8f9ff8f08bbdfa9ddff49#block-66a8f9ff8f08bbdfa9ddff49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first major ad}}}\uc2  attacking her handling of the issue of immigration.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson, Ammar Moussa, reads:\par \par \uc2 After killing the toughest border deal in decades, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running on his trademark lies because his own record and \u8216\'20\'18plans\u8217\'20\'19 are extreme and unpopular. As a former district attorney, attorney general, and now vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has spent her career taking on and prosecuting violent criminals and making our communities safer. She\u8217\'20\'19ll do the same as president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign also released its first television ad of the general election attacking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over her handling of the issue of immigration, and accusing the vice-president of being a failed \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The 30-second ad attacks Harris as \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerously liberal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala is failed, weak, and dangerously liberal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nspLTt6BLC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nspLTt6BLC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Team Trump (Text TRUMP to 88022) (@TeamTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamTrump/status/1818259349761933421?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign launches $50m ad buy ahead of Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has announced a $50m advertising blitz ahead of the Democratic national convention next month with a television ad that portrays the presumptive Democratic nominee as \u8220\'20\'1Cfearless\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The 60-second ad will be the first in a series of paid media efforts ahead of the convention, which begins 19 August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis campaign is about who we fight for,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says in the ad.\par \par \uc2 We believe in a future where every person has the opportunity not just to get by, but to get ahead. Where every senior can retire with dignity. But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take our country backward. To give tax breaks to billionaires and big corporations and end the Affordable Care Act. But we are not going back.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe believe in a future where every person has the opportunity not just to get by, but to get ahead. Where every senior can retire with dignity.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take our country backward.\par \par \uc2 We are not going back. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/POhMKFIqZz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/POhMKFIqZz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1818264875627389226?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The ad will air on local and national television stations across battleground states, the campaign said. It will air during Olympics coverage, and during shows like Big Brother, The Daily Show, The Simpsons and The Bachelorette.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will attend the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2  (\uc2 NABJ\uc2 ) convention in Chicago this week, his campaign announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Trump will join a Q&A panel with political journalists including ABC News\u8217\'20\'19s Rachel Scott, Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Harris Faulkner and Semafor\u8217\'20\'19s Kadia Goba, according to a \uc2 NABJ\uc2  press release. A statement from \uc2 NABJ\uc2  president \uc2 Ken Lemon\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 We look forward to our attendees hearing from former president Trump on the critical issues our members and their audiences care about most.\par \par \uc2 Trump will \u8220\'20\'1Cengage in a Q&A with political journalists before an audience of registered convention attendees that will concentrate on the most pressing issues facing the Black community\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CWhite Dudes for Harris\u8221\'20\'1D Zoom fundraising call came in the wake of similar, well-attended gatherings for Black women, Black men and white women supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There is also a \u8220\'20\'1Ccat ladies for Harris\u8221\'20\'1D Zoom call being planned in response to comments from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, in which he insulted the vice-president as a \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat\u8221\'20\'1D lady. And there is a similar call in the works titled \u8220\'20\'1CLatino Men for Kamala\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The white women for Harris call last Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/26/kamala-harris-zoom-answer-the-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised}}}\uc2  nearly $8.5m for the vice-president and had more than 160,000 attenders.\par \par \uc2 The Black women for Harris Zoom call attracted about 90,000 participants. And the Black men for Harris streaming event, moderated by the journalist Roland Martin, saw more than 53,000 people register.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18White Dudes for Harris\u8217\'20\'19 raise $4m\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/white-dudes-harris-fundraiser-zoom-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Zoom call }}}\uc2  meant to rally \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite dudes\u8221\'20\'1D in support of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s run for the White House raised more than $4m from about 190,000 participants, including numerous celebrities, according to the presumptive Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 Guests on the call not only included contenders for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential running mate: the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Illinois governor, \uc2 JB Pritzker\uc2 , and the transportation secretary, \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They also included the actors Jeff Bridges \u8211\'20\'13 famous for portraying the Dude in The Big Lebowski \u8211\'20\'13 and Mark Hamill, who secured a $50,000 donation during the call by delivering his renowned Star Wars line: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m Luke Skywalker. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to rescue you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other celebrities on Monday\u8217\'20\'19s call were Mark Ruffalo, Joseph Gordon-Levitt, Paul Scheer, Josh Gad, Sean Astin, JJ Abrams and Bradley Whitford. The call lasted over three hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Those rumored to become \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate are all white men who govern in swing states that can decide the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 They include: the Kentucky governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 ; the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ; the Pennsylvania governor, Josh Shapiro ; and Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While all four have been asked about their willingness to serve as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate if tapped, all have signaled that they would step up if asked but none have hinted at their engagements with her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Kelly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/alanhe/status/1816566079730114685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  reporters on 25 July:\par \par \uc2 This is not about me. But I\u8217\'20\'19ve always, always said when I\u8217\'20\'19ve had the chance to serve, I think that\u8217\'20\'19s very important to do.\par \par \uc2 Walz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CNNSOTU/status/1817593315233006018"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper on Sunday:\par \par \uc2 Being mentioned is certainly an honor \u8230\'20\'26 I trust vice-president Harris\u8217\'20\'19s judgement, she\u8217\'20\'19ll make the best choice she\u8217\'20\'19s going to \u8230\'20\'26 But one way or another, she\u8217\'20\'19s going to win in November and that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna benefit everyone \u8230\'20\'26 Either way it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be a win.\par \par \uc2 During a campaign stop for Harris in Pittsburgh, Shapiro said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a decision she needs to make who she wants to govern with, who she wants to campaign with, and who can be there to serve alongside her.\par \par \uc2 And Beshear, who has also been stumping for Harris in red and purple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AndyBeshearKY/status/1817588388633170139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jurisdictions}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eu.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/07/27/kentucky-governor-andy-beshear-says-hed-be-eager-to-debate-phony-republican-vp-jd-vance/74532151007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  the Des Moines Register newspaper:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m honored to be considered and, regardless of what happens, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to work every day between now and election day to make sure that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the next president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania governor, Josh Shapiro, who is considered to be among the leading contenders for the vice-presidential running mate to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , held a joint rally with the Michigan governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , in the Philadelphia suburbs on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want a future that is cleaner and greener,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro told a crowd of about 1,000 supporters.\par \par \uc2 I want a future with better schools and safer streets, and I want a future full of freedom. I want to look the 47th president of the United States in the eye and say, \u8216\'20\'18Madam President.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Harris took a break from the campaign trail this weekend and held private conversations with several of the candidates, including Shapiro, according to Reuters, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro, who took over the governorship of Pennsylvania just last year, is seen as a rising star in the Democratic party. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the state in his election victory over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to announce VP pick in \u8216\'20\'18next six, seven days\u8217\'20\'19, says Whitmer\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will announce her running mate \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next six, seven days\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer, an influential Democratic campaign co-chair, told \uc2 CBS\uc2  yesterday:\par \par \uc2 I would imagine we\u8217\'20\'19ll know who her running mate is, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll get ready for the convention.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer told \uc2 CBS\uc2  she expected a \u8220\'20\'1Cconvention of happy warriors\u8221\'20\'1D in Chicago next month. She added that she was not under consideration herself.\par \par \uc2 I have communicated with everyone, including the people of Michigan, that I\u8217\'20\'19m going to stay as governor until the end of my term at the end of 2026.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , 67, has known \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  since their overlapping days as state attorneys general and recently campaigned with her.\par \par \uc2 Cooper ran two successful gubernatorial campaigns in North Carolina, a battleground state, even as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  carried the state at the presidential level.\par \par \uc2 Three factors were cited for Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from contention to become Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/07/29/roy-cooper-harris-vp-out-00171754?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=d66b2db2-0400-407f-afcc-3b1d45707d8e&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 His desire to potentially run for Senate, his age and fears that North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s divisive Republican lieutenant governor would take over each time Cooper traveled out of state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the get go, he was not a candidate for this,\u8221\'20\'1D a source told the outlet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , was asked last week by the Harris campaign to be vetted for vice-president but declined to participate, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The Cooper team reached out to the Harris campaign a week ago on Monday \u8211\'20\'13 a day after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  left the race and endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as his successor \u8211\'20\'13 to say he did not want to be considered, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/29/us/politics/roy-cooper-kamala-harris-vp.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , citing a source.\par \par \uc2 The report says that Cooper harbored concerns that Lt Gov Mark Robinson, a conservative Republican who is on the ballot this year to replace him, would mount a legal effort to usurp his executive authority while he was out of state. Cooper did not think Robinson would be successful but thought any such challenge would serve as a chaotic distraction had he been added to the ticket, the report says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris nears VP pick decision as North Carolina governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  bows out\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pool of potential running mates is narrowing after two Democratic lawmakers seen as strong contenders in the race, the North Carolina governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , and the Michigan governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , ruled themselves out on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis just wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the right time for North Carolina and for me to potentially be on a national ticket,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RoyCooperNC/status/1818080476273201442"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  last night.\par \par \uc2 As I\u8217\'20\'19ve said from the beginning, she has an outstanding list of people from which to choose, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll all work to make sure she wins.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vBmxvUhuFu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vBmxvUhuFu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  (@RoyCooperNC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RoyCooperNC/status/1818080476273201442?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal came hours after Whitmer said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a part of the vetting\u8221\'20\'1D process for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate. In an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 , Whitmer said:\par \par \uc2 I have communicated with everyone, including the people of Michigan, that I\u8217\'20\'19m going to stay as governor until the end of my term at the end of 2026.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer added that she expected Harris to announce her pick within the week, which would confirm the Democratic ticket at least two weeks before the Democratic national convention begins on 19 August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Others rumored to be potential running mates include: the Kentucky governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 ; the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 ; the Pennsylvania governor, Josh Shapiro; and the Arizona senator, \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold a rally this evening in Atlanta featuring a performance by rapper Megan Thee Stallion. Harris will be accompanied by both Georgia senators, the Atlanta mayor and other high-profile Democrats in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ronald Rowe Jr, the acting Secret Service director, will testify alongside the deputy \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 Paul Abbate\uc2 , in front of a joint hearing of the Senate judiciary and homeland security and government affairs committees.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican primaries across Arizona today will test whether the far-right cadre focused on election denial still can win among their base, despite major losses in the 2022 primaries.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240730ek7u001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
