\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden reaffirms call for supreme court reforms in speech marking Civil Rights Act anniversary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (now); Joanna Walters and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 7,805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 July 2024\par 23:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President cites supreme court decisions that he says eroded civil rights, including presidential immunity ruling and overturning of Roe. This blog is now closedFull story: Biden calls for supreme court changes and decries Trump immunity ruling\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sam Levine has analyzed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Austin. He writes: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/biden-us-supreme-court-reforms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The reforms}}}\uc2  themselves are significant, but just a small sliver of what activists and others have been pushing for over the last few years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more from Sam here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/joe-biden-supreme-court-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s call for supreme court reforms shifts conversation \u8211\'20\'13 but comes late}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here are a few of the key events from the world of politics today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered a speech at an event celebrating the 60th anniversary of the US Civil Rights Act. During the talk, he warned of the dangers of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s extremism and promised reforms on term limits, the ethics code and a recent ruling on presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson and House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  announced the seven Republicans and six Democrats who will sit on the taskforce to investigate the assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election campaign has accused \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  of spreading \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulated lies\u8221\'20\'1D after the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive posted a doctored video featuring the vice-president on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X account.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A trial looming in a lawsuit challenging North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban was canceled Monday as the judge in the case, state district judge Bruce Romanick, weighs whether to throw out the lawsuit. It was not immediately clear why the trial was canceled.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  told a \uc2 CBS\uc2  interviewer that she has not been a part of the vetting process for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate. But she expects the presumptive Democratic nominee to announce her vice-presidential pick \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next six, seven days\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says supreme court's actions have eroded trust of US residents\par \par \uc2 In an over 20-minute speech, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  talked about the enduring legacy of the 1964 Civil Rights Act and the inspiration he took from Lyndon B Johnson. The bulk of the speech, however, focused on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  and actions that Biden said have eroded the trust US residents have in the high court.\par \par \uc2 He also nodded to Project 2025, a roadmap led by the rightwing Heritage Foundation that details how the Trump administration can disrupt and dismantle the US. \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, they\u8217\'20\'19re serious, man,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 He also emphasized his commitment to the changes to the supreme court he spelled out in an opinion piece published by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  on Monday. His proposal would:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Establish 18-year term limits for all justices\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Create a code of ethics that includes requirements to disclose gifts and refrain from public political actions\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pass a new constitutional amendment that would virtually reverse the\par \par \uc2 supreme court decision in July granting former presidents broad immunity from prosecution for actions taken while in office\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden just completed his speech and reaffirmed his proposed changes to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 One of his proposed changes is to reverse the recent immunity decision poses, which he says gives the president room to \u8220\'20\'1Cviolate our oath, flout our laws, and face no consequences\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the issue of term limits, Biden argued that an 18-year cap would make the timing of nominations less \u8220\'20\'1Carbitrary\u8221\'20\'1D and limit the ability of the president to influence the makeup of the body.\par \par \uc2 He is also seeking a new code of conduct that will replace the current one that is optional for justices. This new edict would require justices to disclose gifts, recuse themselves from cases that they or their spouses have an interest in, and \u8220\'20\'1Crefrain from public political activity\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is calling out supreme court decisions that he says have eroded civil rights.\par \par \uc2 They include the 2013 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/25/shelby-county-anniversary-voting-rights-act-consequences"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shelby County decision}}}\uc2  that gutted civil rights, the 2022 decision that overturned Roe v Wade, and most recently a decision that gives presidents broad immunity. These actions, Biden said, fly in the face of the notion that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere are no kings in America \u8230\'20\'26 No one is above the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExtremism is undermining the public confidence in the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the top of his speech \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized his admiration for Lyndon B Johnson and reiterated the promises made by his signing of the 1964 Civil Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 The president told the audience:\par \par \uc2 In a great society no one should be left behind \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s time for us to come to see that every American gets a decent break and a fair chance to make good.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now on the stage, he was introduced by Andrew Young, a former congressman and ambassador to the United Nations. Biden walked out to the song Glory, performed by John Legend and Common for the 2015 film Selma.\par \par \uc2 The live stream {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lbjlibrary.org/events/lbj-foundation/2024-07-29_60th-anniversary-civil-rights-act-commemoration#:~:text=LBJ%20Foundation%20%7C%20Jul%2C%2029%202024,Johnson%20on%20July%202%2C%201964."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are still waiting for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to take the stage. Less than an hour ago, he arrived in Austin and was greeted by several local and state lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Currently, Mark Updegrove, the president and CEO of the Lyndon B Johnson Foundation, the group hosting the Civil Rights Act commemoration event, is giving a speech about the organization\u8217\'20\'19s history and legacy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lbjlibrary.org/events/lbj-foundation/2024-07-29_60th-anniversary-civil-rights-act-commemoration#:~:text=LBJ%20Foundation%20%7C%20Jul%2C%2029%202024,Johnson%20on%20July%202%2C%201964."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Watch the live stream here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await the arrival of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the stage, here are some of the images being sent to us on the newswires of the president arriving in Austin earlier today.\par \par \uc2 He was met by Democratic state representatives Sheryl Cole and Donna Howard before heading to the LBJ library.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was music from the concert choir of Huston-Tillotson University, followed by the actor Bryan Cranston reading an excerpt from the 1964 Civil Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The event marking the 60th anniversary of the Civil Rights Act is being held at the Lyndon Baines Johnson (LBJ) library in Austin, Texas.\par \par \uc2 It began with a short film showing previous presidents\u8217\'20\'19 remarks on civil rights, including \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expected to talk about supreme court reform at Civil Rights Act anniversary event\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to announce three proposed reforms to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an opinion piece {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/07/29/joe-biden-reform-supreme-court-presidential-immunity-plan-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published in the Washington Post}}}\uc2  on Monday, the president called for three primary changes to the high court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Eighteen-year term limits\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A binding code of ethics\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A new constitutional amendment that would virtually reverse a supreme court decision in July granting former presidents broad immunity from prosecution for actions taken while in office\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes on the 60th anniversary of the signing of the Civil Rights Act of 1964.\par \par \uc2 Hello, I\u8217\'20\'19m Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton running the blog from Los Angeles. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the latest news and reaction.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 A trial looming in a lawsuit challenging North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban was canceled Monday as the judge in the case, state district judge Bruce Romanick, weighs whether to throw out the lawsuit. It was not immediately clear why the trial was canceled.\par \par \uc2 The notice comes nearly a week after the state and plaintiffs, who include the formerly sole \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in North Dakota, made their pitches to the judge as to why he should dismiss the two-year-old case, or continue to trial, the Associated Press reports. The trial was due to begin late August.\par \par \uc2 North Dakota outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a felony crime for people who perform the procedure, but with exceptions to prevent the mother\u8217\'20\'19s death or a \u8220\'20\'1Cserious health risk\u8221\'20\'1D to her, as well as for cases of rape or incest within the first six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs, which include the Red River Women\u8217\'20\'19s Clinic and doctors trained in obstetrics, gynecology and maternal-fetal medicine, alleged the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban violates the state constitution because it is unconstitutionally vague about its exceptions for doctors and that its health exception is too narrow. They wanted the trial to proceed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  highlighted endorsements from mayors of border towns in swing state Arizona today as she looks to blunt the impact of Republican criticism of her handling of illegal border crossings.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for president said she was backed by the mayors of Bisbee, Nogales, Somerton, and San Luis, as well as by Yuma county supervisors Martin Porchas and Tony Reyes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say Harris did not do enough as US vice-president to clamp down on illegal immigration.\par \par \uc2 I trust her to meet the needs of border cities and towns without taking advantage of us for her own political gain, like her opponent,\u8221\'20\'1D the Somerton mayor, Gerardo Anaya, said in a statement. Somerton is a city of about 14,000 people in the state\u8217\'20\'19s southwestern corner.\par \par \uc2 As vice-president, Harris was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/general-news-3400f56255e000547d1ca3ce1aa6b8e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tasked with overseeing}}}\uc2  diplomatic efforts to deal with issues spurring migration in the Northern Triangle countries of El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras, as well as pressing them to strengthen enforcement on their own borders. The Biden administration wanted to develop and put in place a long-term strategy that gets at the root causes of migration from those countries.\par \par \uc2 Border arrests have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/border-arrests-biden-asylum-mexico-immigration-6e302f06f567b96d88cc1333aa6d10fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallen from record highs}}}\uc2  last December.\par \par \uc2 Read my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s piece on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s record on immigration policy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/kamala-harris-immigration-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , whose state borders Iowa, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66a7d7298f08f274ba3701e3#block-66a7d7298f08f274ba3701e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also }}}\uc2  extended a welcome to Iowa residents who are in need of reproductive healthcare, as Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s strict six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban took effect on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Walz, in a post to X, wrote:\par \par \uc2 In Minnesota, we take care of our neighbors. It\u8217\'20\'19s just what we do. As our neighbors in Iowa are stripped of their fundamental rights, my message is clear: Your reproductive freedom will remain protected in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn Minnesota, we take care of our neighbors. It\u8217\'20\'19s just what we do.\par \par \uc2 As our neighbors in Iowa are stripped of their fundamental rights, my message is clear: Your reproductive freedom will remain protected in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@GovTimWalz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovTimWalz/status/1817956756732944403?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, and minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , have announced the seven Republicans and six Democrats who will sit on the taskforce to investigate the assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Republican chair of the panel will be the congressman Mike Kelly, who represents the Pennsylvania town of Butler where the shooting took place.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic ranking member will be the Colorado congressman \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2 , who sits on the House intelligence and foreign affairs committee.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, in a statement posted to X, said he and Jeffries \u8220\'20\'1Chave the utmost confidence in this group of steady, highly qualified, and capable Members of Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr??Today, I\u8217\'20\'19m announcing the seven Republicans who will serve on the Bipartisan House Task Force to investigate the attempted assassination of President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We have the utmost confidence in this group of steady, highly qualified, and capable Members of Congress:\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Mike Johnson (@SpeakerJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1817973329443303473?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Iowa ban, which takes effect today, permits abortions past six weeks in cases of rape or incest, or in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Fourteen other states, including much of the midwest, enacted near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 Three other states \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia, South Carolina and Florida \u8211\'20\'13 have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise led to surge in support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, even in red states. Sixty-one per cent of Iowans, including 70% of women, say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, a Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/2023/03/27/iowa-poll-most-iowans-back-legal-abortion-as-iowa-supreme-court-mulls-limits-roe-v-wade/69990037007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  found}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in Iowa on Monday, cutting off access to the procedure before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated Iowa state legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/iowa-passes-six-week-abortion-ban#:~:text=Iowa's%20state%20legislature%20voted%20on,people%20know%20they%20are%20pregnant."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed the ban last year}}}\uc2 , but a lengthy court battle initially stopped it from taking effect. Last month, the Iowa supreme court ruled that the ban could be enforced, leading a lower-court judge to order the ban to take effect at 8am local time.\par \par \uc2 Leah Vanden Bosch, development and outreach director of the Iowa \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Fund, said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 The upholding of this \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Iowa is an absolute devastation and violation of human rights, depriving Iowans of their bodily autonomy. We know a ban will not stop the need for abortions.\par \par \uc2 Up until Sunday, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been legal in Iowa up to roughly 22 weeks of pregnancy. Now, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/iowa-abortion-law-six-weeks#:~:text=An%20Iowa%20judge%20has%20ruled,blocked%20it%20from%20being%20enforced."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have indicated}}}\uc2  that they will continue offering the procedure to the legal limit.\par \par \uc2 The closest options for Iowans who want abortions after six weeks of pregnancy will probably be Minnesota and Illinois, Democratic-run states that border Iowa and that have become \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  havens since Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The Iowa ban permits abortions past six weeks in cases of rape or incest, or in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Possible Harris running mates condemn Iowa's six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 Two Democratic state governors who are being considered by Kamala Harri s\u8217\'20\'19s campaign as her potential running mate, Josh Shapiro of Pennsylvania and JB Pritzker of Illinois, have criticized the strict six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that went into effect in Iowa today.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro directly blamed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the Iowa law, and urged voters not to re-elect the Republican former president.\par \par \uc2 enltrAnother \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban brought to you by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We cannot let him back in the White House and we must restore every woman's freedom to choose. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fBTV4ANGII"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fBTV4ANGII}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Shapiro (@JoshShapiroPA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoshShapiroPA/status/1817916504534298927?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Pritzker, whose state borders Iowa, welcomed Iowa residents to visit Illinois if the new law blocks their access to \u8220\'20\'1Cwhatever care they need\u8221\'20\'1D. He added:\par \par \uc2 Please know \u8211\'20\'13 as you work to maneuver around this dangerous and unjust law \u8211\'20\'13 we are here for you.\par \par \uc2 enltrIowa\u8217\'20\'19s disturbing 6-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban goes into effect today. Here in Illinois, we will welcome our Iowan neighbors for reproductive freedom and whatever care they need.\par \par \uc2 Please know - as you work to maneuver around this dangerous and unjust law - we are here for you.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JB Pritzker (@JBPritzker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JBPritzker/status/1817918110672056701?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Questions continued to mount about the political transformation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/27/us/politics/jd-vance-friend-transgender.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 release of emails}}}\uc2  from a former friend in which Vance called Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally reprehensible human being\u8221\'20\'1D and said: \u8220\'20\'1CI hate the police.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The messages between Vance and Sofia Nelson, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/27/us/politics/jd-vance-friend-transgender.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent them }}}\uc2  to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , were largely dated between 2014 and 2017. In one, Vance sent Nelson a section of Hillbilly Elegy, his bestseller about his Appalachian boyhood. Vance wrote:\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an excerpt from my book. I send this to you not just to brag, but because I\u8217\'20\'19m sure if you read it you\u8217\'20\'19ll notice reference to \u8216\'20\'18an extremely progressive lesbian\u8217\'20\'19. I recognise now that this may not accurately reflect how you think of yourself, and for that I am really sorry. I hope you\u8217\'20\'19re not offended, but if you are, I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry! Love you, JD.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/jd-vance-trump-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/jd-vance-trump-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance calls Trump \u8216\'20\'18morally reprehensible\u8217\'20\'19 in resurfaced emails}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/jd-vance-trump-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance calls Trump \u8216\'20\'18morally reprehensible\u8217\'20\'19 in resurfaced emails}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Iowa six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?page=with:block-66a7cfa28f08eef516970449#block-66a7cfa28f08eef516970449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  takes effect}}}\uc2  today, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is launching a \u8220\'20\'1CFight for Reproductive Freedom week of action\u8221\'20\'1D with events across key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign said the week of action would help voters \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstand all that\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for reproductive rights in this election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , the reproductive rights activist Hadley Duvall and the radio host Ryan Hamilton will appear at the reproductive rights events, according to the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 The second gentleman, Doug Emhoff, will also host a reproductive freedom event in New Hampshire on Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris slams 'Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban' as Iowa's six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban takes effect\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has condemned a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that takes effect in Iowa today, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1CTrump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 From Monday, most abortions are prohibited in the state after about six weeks of pregnancy, before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 In a video statement, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Today, Iowa put in place a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which makes Iowa the 22nd state in our country to have a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. And this ban is going to take effect before many women even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. And what this means is that one in three women of reproductive age in America lives in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 enltrMore than 1 in 3 women of reproductive age in America now live in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 When I am President of the United States, I will sign a law restoring and protecting reproductive freedom in every state. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ka8f8zI145"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ka8f8zI145}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1817929460009558453?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  welcomes supreme court reform push\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  has welcomed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense\u8221\'20\'1D calls to reform the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The former secretary of state, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/HillaryClinton/status/1817962829057597633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post }}}\uc2  to X, said these proposals will \u8220\'20\'1Crepair [the] promise\u8221\'20\'1D that no one is above the law, and help to \u8220\'20\'1Crestore the American people\u8217\'20\'19s lost trust in the Court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrOne of the first principles of our republic is that no one is above the law. President Biden and Vice President Harris's common-sense proposals to reform the Supreme Court will repair that promise and begin to restore the American people's lost trust in the Court.\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  (@HillaryClinton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1817962829057597633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election campaign has accused \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  of spreading \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulated lies\u8221\'20\'1D after the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive posted a doctored video featuring the vice-president on his X account.\par \par \uc2 Musk reposted a manipulated Harris campaign video on Friday evening in which a fake Harris voiceover says: \u8220\'20\'1CI was selected because I am the ultimate diversity hire,\u8221\'20\'1D and that anyone who criticises her is \u8220\'20\'1Cboth sexist and racist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The video has been viewed 128m times on Musk\u8217\'20\'19s account after the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1816974609637417112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted it with the words}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is amazing\u8221\'20\'1D followed by a laughing emoji. Musk owns X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jul/24/elon-musk-reveals-the-new-twitter-logo-x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which he rebranded from Twitter last year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Amy Klobuchar, a Democratic senator, accused Musk of violating the platform\u8217\'20\'19s guidelines. According to X\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://help.x.com/en/rules-and-policies/manipulated-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 synthetic and manipulated media policy}}}\uc2 , users are barred from sharing \u8220\'20\'1Csynthetic, manipulated, or out-of-context media that may deceive or confuse people and lead to harm\u8221\'20\'1D although allowances are made for satire provided it does not \u8220\'20\'1Ccause significant confusion about the authenticity of the media\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign said:\par \par \uc2 The American people want the real freedom, opportunity and security Vice-President Harris is offering; not the fake, manipulated lies of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic chair of Senate justice committee backs Biden reform call\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin, the Democratic chair of the Senate judiciary committee, has voiced support for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s call for supreme court reforms.\par \par \uc2 Durbin, in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1817949542186094889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  posted}}}\uc2  to X, wrote:\par \par \uc2 If Chief Justice Roberts won\u8217\'20\'19t use his existing authority to implement an enforceable code of conduct, Congress must. We should use our established authority to require the Court to implement reforms consistent with *every* other federal court.\par \par \uc2 enltrI thank the President for bringing attention to the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s ethical crisis.\par \par \uc2 I will continue my 12-year effort until it\u8217\'20\'19s done, because the highest court in the land cannot have the lowest ethical standards. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1bpZzja6CK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1bpZzja6CK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Dick Durbin (@SenatorDurbin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorDurbin/status/1817944952195727523?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Michigan governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , in the \uc2 CBS\uc2  interview, said she has not been a part of the vetting process for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer said:\par \par \uc2 I have communicated with everyone, including the people of Michigan, that I\u8217\'20\'19m going to stay as governor until the end of my term at the end of 2026.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer was touted as a potential replacement for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  before he exited the race and endorsed Harris last week.\par \par \uc2 In the interview this morning, Whitmer pushed back on the idea that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate must be a white man:\par \par \uc2 Every one of us was told there may be too many women on the ticket. Baloney. We\u8217\'20\'19ve proved that wrong in the swingingest of swing states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris likely to announce running mate 'in the next six, seven days', says Whitmer\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan rumored to be in the running for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s potential ticket mate, has said she expects the vice-president to announce her running mate \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next six, seven days\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer, in an interview on \uc2 CBS\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 Everything\u8217\'20\'19s truncated, and [Harris] is going to make that decision probably in the next six, seven days. I would imagine we\u8217\'20\'19ll know who her running mate is, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll get ready for convention.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going to announce her running mate \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably, in the next 6, 7 days,\u8221\'20\'1D campaign co-chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovWhitmer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GovWhitmer}}}\uc2  tells CBS Mornings.\par \par \uc2 She adds that she believes Harris' running mate does not need to be a White man in order for her to win. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qcj6TcLdJz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qcj6TcLdJz}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GV4GsZ5drf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GV4GsZ5drf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS Mornings (@CBSMornings) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSMornings/status/1817895628015382882?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden critic Leo has played key role in moving court to the right\par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the rightwing dark money organizer who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?page=with:block-66a7c1388f08eef5169703b8#block-66a7c1388f08eef5169703b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just issued a statement}}}\uc2  slamming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s call for supreme court reforms, has played a key role in the conservative effort to move the judiciary to the right.\par \par \uc2 Leo\u8217\'20\'19s advocacy and financial network played a major role in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s judicial nominations and confirmation hearings as part of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/23/leonard-leo-us-judiciary-wisconsin-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 years-long push}}}\uc2  to make the courts more friendly to conservatives and their causes.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/04/leonard-leo-federalist-society-conservative-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once joked}}}\uc2  that Leo was the \u8220\'20\'1CNo 3 most powerful person in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Leo is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/23/leonard-leo-us-judiciary-wisconsin-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catholic conservative activist}}}\uc2  widely known as the force behind the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 , which has helped transform the US courts system, ultimately through the installation of three hardline justices on the supreme court that has handed down epochal rulings on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, presidential immunity and more.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwing donor hits out at Biden over supreme court reforms\par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the rightwing donor, has hit back at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s call for supreme court reforms, saying they were about \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats destroying a court they don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Leo, in a statement, said that if Biden and the Democrats were \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly serious\u8221\'20\'1D about ethics reform, they would calls for bans on \u8220\'20\'1Call gifts and hospitality of any kind to any public official in any branch of government\u8221\'20\'1D, including in Congress, where he said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real corruption is\u8221\'20\'1D. He concluded:\par \par \uc2 Let me be clear: If Democrats want to adopt an across the board ethics ban for all branches, I am in favor of that: no jets, no meals, no speaking honorariums, no gifts for anyone from anyone for any reason in any branch, starting with Congress. Until they support that, let\u8217\'20\'19s all be honest about what this is: a campaign to destroy a court that they disagree with.\par \par \uc2 enltrINBOX: Statement from \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  Regarding President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court Announcement (endorsed by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ):\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo conservative justice has made any decision in any big case that surprised anyone, so let\u8217\'20\'19s stop pretending this is about undue influence. It\u8217\'20\'19s about\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Guy Benson (@guypbenson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guypbenson/status/1817940375161417945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in his proposals for supreme court reform, also called for a binding, enforceable code of ethics.\par \par \uc2 The president \u8220\'20\'1Cbelieves that Congress should pass binding, enforceable conduct and ethics rules that require Justices to disclose gifts, refrain from public political activity, and recuse themselves from cases in which they or their spouses have financial or other conflicts of interest,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/07/29/fact-sheet-president-biden-announces-bold-plan-to-reform-the-supreme-court-and-ensure-no-president-is-above-the-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement.}}}\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court Justices should not be exempt from the enforceable code of conduct that applies to every other federal judge.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s proposals also call for limiting a supreme court justice\u8217\'20\'19s term to a maximum of 18 years rather than the current lifetime appointment, under a system where a new justice would be appointed to the supreme court by the serving president every two years.\par \par \uc2 Term limits would help \u8220\'20\'1Creduce the chance that any single Presidency imposes undue influence for generations to come,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House statement.\par \par \uc2 Congress approved term limits for the Presidency over 75 years ago, and President Biden believes they should do the same for the Supreme Court. The United States is the only major constitutional democracy that gives lifetime seats to its high court Justices.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/07/29/fact-sheet-president-biden-announces-bold-plan-to-reform-the-supreme-court-and-ensure-no-president-is-above-the-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detailed}}}\uc2  a series of sweeping changes to the supreme court proposed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , which include introduction of term limits for justices and a constitutional amendment to remove immunity for crimes committed by a president while in office.\par \par \uc2 The reforms include a \u8220\'20\'1CNo One Is Above the Law Amendment\u8221\'20\'1D, in which Biden calls for a constitutional amendment that \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes clear no president is above the law or immune from prosecution for crimes committed while in office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The amendment would state that the US constitution \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not confer any immunity from federal criminal indictment, trial, conviction, or sentencing by virtue of previously serving as president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If approved, the amendment would in effect reverse a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-decision-trump-immunity-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court decision in July}}}\uc2  granting former presidents broad immunity from prosecution for actions taken while in office, a decision \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hailed as a \u8220\'20\'1CBIG WIN\u8221\'20\'1D amid his legal travails.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The news that \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4#block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has agreed to a victim interview}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  comes after the agency confirmed a bullet or a fragment of a bullet struck the former president\u8217\'20\'19s ear.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Friday, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 What struck former President Trump in the ear was a bullet, whether whole or fragmented into smaller pieces, fired from the deceased subject\u8217\'20\'19s rifle.\par \par \uc2 The statement marked the most definitive law enforcement account of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s injuries and followed ambiguous comments earlier in the week from the agency\u8217\'20\'19s director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , that appeared to cast doubt on whether Trump had been hit by a bullet or whether he was instead struck by shrapnel.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/25/fbi-director-trump-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI director questions whether Trump was hit by bullet or shrapnel in shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  raised $200m in the week since she was endorsed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , her team said, as the vice-president appears to be drawing increased enthusiasm to her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Harris for President said about 66% of the total came from first-time donors, as the campaign said it had seen \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented grassroots support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , the former vice-president and a climate activist, endorsed Harris, while more than 170,000 volunteers have signed up to help the Harris campaign with phone banking, canvassing and other get-out-the-vote efforts, said Michael Tyler, the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s communications director.\par \par \uc2 It comes after Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/22/biden-drops-out-endorses-kamala-harris-election-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-669eb4ab8f08adbbe4b1d05b#block-669eb4ab8f08adbbe4b1d05b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised $81m}}}\uc2  in the 24 hours after she was endorsed by Biden, a record sum. The donation news comes after Harris attended a fundraiser in Pittsfield, Massachusetts, on Saturday. The event had been organized when the president was still the presumptive nominee, and had originally been expected to raise $400,000, but ended up bringing in about $1.4m, according to the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 Future Forward, the largest Super Pac in Democratic politics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/07/22/kamala-harris-campaign-biden-drop-out/big-donors-00170367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced last week}}}\uc2  it had secured $150m in donations over the first 24 hours after Biden dropped out of the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump gunman searched for information on shooting of Slovakian leader - \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?page=with:block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4#block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with the }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?page=with:block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4#block-66a7ad498f08f274ba36ffc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be consistent with any victim interview we do\u8221\'20\'1D, an agency official said.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Rojek, the special agent in charge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh field office, said a local police identified the gunman about an hour before Trump spoke that day and took a photo.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  official also revealed new details about the gunman, 20-year-old Thomas Crooks.\par \par \uc2 Crooks conducted Internet searches into previous mass shooting events, improvised explosive devices and the attempted assassination of the Slovakian prime minister, Robert Fico, earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Despite hundreds of interviews, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said it has yet to identify a motive for the shooting.\par \par \uc2 The gunman\u8217\'20\'19s parents, described as having been \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely cooperative\u8221\'20\'1D with investigators, said they had no knowledge of Crooks\u8217\'20\'19s plans, Rojek said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's supreme court reform proposals 'dead on arrival in the House', says Mike Johnson\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, has warned that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s proposals to reform the supreme court will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdead on arrival\u8221\'20\'1D in the House.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposed reforms include introducing term limits for supreme court justices, a binding code of conduct and a constitutional amendment to remove immunity for crimes committed by a president while in office.\par \par \uc2 Johnson, in a statement, said:\par \par \uc2 President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal to radically overhaul the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  would tilt the balance of power and erode not only the rule of law, but the American people\u8217\'20\'19s faith in our system of justice.\par \par \uc2 This proposal is the logical conclusion to the Biden-Harris administration and congressional Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 ongoing efforts to delegitimize the supreme court. Their calls to expand and pack the court will soon resume.\par \par \uc2 It is telling that Democrats want to change the system that has guided our nation since its founding simply because they disagree with some of the court\u8217\'20\'19s recent decisions. This dangerous gambit of the Biden-Harris administration is dead on arrival in the House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump agrees to \uc2 FBI\uc2  interview after assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has agreed to participate in a victim interview with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as part of an investigation into his attempted assassination, an agency official said.\par \par \uc2 The interview is part of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s standard protocol to speak with victims of federal crimes during the course of their investigations.\par \par \uc2 Kevin Rojek, the special agent in charge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh field office, told reporters:\par \par \uc2 We want to get his perspective on what he observed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris backs Biden's supreme court reforms\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has endorsed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s push for supreme court reforms that include term limits for justices, a binding code of conduct and a constitutional amendment to remove immunity for crimes committed by a president while in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and I strongly believe that the American people must have confidence in the supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Yet today, there is a clear crisis of confidence facing the supreme court as its fairness has been called into question after numerous ethics scandals and decision after decision overturning long-standing precedent.\par \par \uc2 Harris added:\par \par \uc2 These popular reforms will help to restore confidence in the court, strengthen our democracy and ensure no one is above the law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to speak about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/29/election-updates-trump-harris?page=with:block-66a7a19a8f08f274ba36ff01#block-66a7a19a8f08f274ba36ff01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his new supreme court reform proposals}}}\uc2  at an address later today at the LBJ presidential library in Austin, Texas, to mark the 60th anniversary of the Civil Rights Act.\par \par \uc2 The president, in a national address from the Oval Office last week, pledged that overhauling the supreme court would be a priority. Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to call for supreme court reform because this is critical to our democracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in an op-ed this morning, said supreme court justices should be limited to a maximum of 18 years\u8217\'20\'19 service rather than the current lifetime appointment, under a system where a new justice would be appointed to the court by the serving president every two years.\par \par \uc2 The president also called for stricter, enforceable rules on conduct which would require justices to disclose gifts, refrain from political activity, and recuse themselves from cases in which they or their spouses have financial interest.\par \par \uc2 Last week Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  called for the court to strengthen the ethics code it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/nov/13/us-supreme-court-ethics-code"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced in 2023}}}\uc2  by adding a way to enforce it.\par \par \uc2 That code was introduced after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a spate of scandals}}}\uc2  involving rightwing justices on the court: \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  was found to have accepted vacations and travel from a Republican mega-donor, while \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  flew on a private jet owned by an influential billionaire on the way to a fishing trip.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 'No one is above the law': Biden calls for supreme court reform plans\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called for a series of reforms to to the supreme court, including the introduction of 18-year term limits and a binding code of conduct for justices.\par \par \uc2 Biden, in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/07/29/joe-biden-reform-supreme-court-presidential-immunity-plan-announcement/?email=620bb4708d235157723d480a0d8d4c265e55ec14&emaila=0ec8b2addfecba6de47e145bbfa10867&emailb=fa17fe37520b9c9752208dccf233e286aef975565778b97fc6ff23ae2388d5a7&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=7.29.24%20RNS%20Morning%20Monday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed }}}\uc2  for the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , also called for a constitutional amendment to remove immunity for crimes committed by a president while in office.\par \par \uc2 The proposed amendment, titled the \u8220\'20\'1CNo One Is Above the Law Amendment\u8221\'20\'1D, comes after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier this month that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is immune from criminal prosecution for \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial acts\u8221\'20\'1D he committed as president.\par \par \uc2 In the op-ed published today, Biden wrote:\par \par \uc2 This nation was founded on a simple yet profound principle: No one is above the law. Not the president of the United States. Not a justice on the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2 . No one.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's remarks a 'promise to end American democracy', says Harris campaign\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign responded by saying that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks to Christian supporters were a \u8220\'20\'1Cpromise to end democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the Harris campaign read:\par \par \uc2 When Vice President Harris says this election is about freedom she means it. Our democracy is under assault by criminal \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas promised violence if he loses, the end of our elections if he wins, and the termination of the Constitution to empower him to be a dictator to enact his dangerous Project 2025 agenda on America\u8221\'20\'1D, the campaign warns.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take America backward, to a politics of hate, chaos, and fear \u8211\'20\'13 this November America will unite around Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to stop him.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur statement on Trump last night promising to end American democracy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/URjtvFCsg2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/URjtvFCsg2}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KAMPPxDr9E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KAMPPxDr9E}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1817287846056669409?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cardi B, the New York rap superstar, posted a clip of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally speech asking if the former president was \u8220\'20\'1Cwhistleblowing a dictatorship?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhistle blowing a dictatorship ??? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/k8HHaWO9jg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/k8HHaWO9jg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cardi B (@iamcardib) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iamcardib/status/1817050010703327362?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Cardi has previously suggested she will not be voting for Trump or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/cardi-b-biden-trump-2024-election-1235021237/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling }}}\uc2  Rolling Stone that she saw Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency as a major threat but felt \u8220\'20\'1Clayers and layers of disappointment\u8221\'20\'1D during the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 The rapper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/20/cardi-b-biden-support-israel-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revoked her support}}}\uc2  for Biden last November over US military aid to Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans dismiss comments as 'classic Trumpism'\par \par \uc2 Asked to clarify \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks, Trump campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said the former Republican president \u8220\'20\'1Cwas talking about uniting this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2 , the governor of New Hampshire, dismissed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments in an interview with ABC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it was a classic Trumpism if you will,\u8221\'20\'1D Sununu said, adding:\par \par \uc2 Obviously we want everybody to vote in all elections, but I think he was just trying to make a hyperbolic point that it can be fixed as long as he gets back into office and all that.\par \par \uc2 Tom Cotton, a senator from Arkansas, said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cobviously making a joke\u8221\'20\'1D. Cotton told CNN:\par \par \uc2 I think he\u8217\'20\'19s obviously making a joke about how bad things have been under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and how good they will be if we send President Trump back to the White House, so we can turn the country around again.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenTomCotton?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenTomCotton}}}\uc2  says Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cobviously making a joke\u8221\'20\'1D when he told a gathering of conservative Christians \u8220\'20\'1Cyou won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote anymore\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dTTpn9UFy8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dTTpn9UFy8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 State of the Union (@CNNSOTU) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSOTU/status/1817579877597339784?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , a senator for South Carolina, told \uc2 CBS\uc2  that Trump was telling supporters that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe nightmare that we\u8217\'20\'19re experiencing will soon be over. Give me four more years, and I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna right this ship called America and pass it on to the next generation.\u8221\'20\'1D Graham added:\par \par \uc2 We will have democracy, God willing, for a very long time in this country. But what President Trump is trying to tell people \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18I did it once, I can do it again.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LindseyGrahamSC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LindseyGrahamSC}}}\uc2  responds to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's recent rally comments that Americans "won't have to vote anymore" if he's elected again: "We will have democracy, God willing, for a very long time in this country. But what President Trump is trying to tell people \u8212\'20\'14 'I did it once, I\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F19C8T0OZO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/F19C8T0OZO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Face The Nation (@FaceTheNation) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FaceTheNation/status/1817578406218752313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dan Goldman, a Democratic congressman for New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/danielsgoldman/status/1817096041474191860"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  to X that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only way \u8216\'20\'18you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote anymore\u8217\'20\'19 is if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes a dictator.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe only way \u8220\'20\'1Cyou won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote anymore\u8221\'20\'1D is if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes a dictator. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wrjNCAUxs6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wrjNCAUxs6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniel Goldman (@danielsgoldman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/danielsgoldman/status/1817096041474191860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks to Christian supporters came months after he said he would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca dictator on day one\u8221\'20\'1D if he is re-elected to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The former president, during a December town hall event in Iowa hosted by the Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , was asked repeatedly to deny that he would abuse power to seek revenge on political opponents if given a second term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder no circumstances, you are promising America tonight, you would never abuse power as retribution against anybody?\u8221\'20\'1D Hannity asked Trump in the interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExcept for day one,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump responded. He said that on the \u8220\'20\'1Cday one\u8221\'20\'1D he referred to, he would use his presidential powers to close the southern border with Mexico and expand oil drilling.\par \par \uc2 Trump then repeated his assertion. \u8220\'20\'1CI love this guy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of Hannity.\par \par \uc2 He says, \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re not going to be a dictator, are you?\u8217\'20\'19 I said: \u8216\'20\'18No, no, no, other than day one. We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the border and we\u8217\'20\'19re drilling, drilling, drilling. After that, I\u8217\'20\'19m not a dictator.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, the high-profile California Democrat and Senate candidate, posted to X a clip of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s speech, writing:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis year democracy is on the ballot, and if we are to save it, we must vote against authoritarianism. Here Trump helpfully reminds us that the alternative is never having the chance to vote again.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis year democracy is on the ballot, and if we are to save it, we must vote against authoritarianism.\par \par \uc2 Here Trump helpfully reminds us that the alternative is never having the chance to vote again. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eQqYdtm61D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eQqYdtm61D}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Schiff (@AdamSchiff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamSchiff/status/1817046115151413702?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks that supporters won\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Chave to vote again\u8221\'20\'1D if he is re-elected in November were immediately met with consternation in some political quarters.\par \par \uc2 The constitutional and civil rights attorney Andrew Seidel, for instance, replied to video of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments circulating on X by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AndrewLSeidel/status/1817016564467511556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 This is not subtle Christian nationalism. He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about ending our democracy and installing a Christian nation.\par \par \uc2 enltrHe's talking to "my beautiful Christians" here. And saying they won't have to vote again. This is not subtle Christian Nationalism, he's talking about ending our democracy and installing a Christian nation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6vmzel9SAE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6vmzel9SAE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew L. Seidel (@AndrewLSeidel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewLSeidel/status/1817016564467511556?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The actor Morgan Fairchild added in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/morgfair/status/1817013409013203392"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate X post}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 But \u8230\'20\'26 what if I want to vote again?? I was always raised that we get to vote again! That is America.\par \par \uc2 enltrBUT...what if I WANT to vote again?? I was always raised that we got to vote again! That is AMERICA... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OOvyTWIOB5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/OOvyTWIOB5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Morgan Fairchild (@morgfair) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/morgfair/status/1817013409013203392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And the NBC legal commentator Katie Phang {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KatiePhang/status/1817056963777228941"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In other words, Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t ever leave the White House if he gets re-elected.\par \par \uc2 enltr?? In other words, Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t ever leave the White House if he gets re-elected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NiD4lKRiu8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NiD4lKRiu8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Katie Phang (@KatiePhang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatiePhang/status/1817056963777228941?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech at the rally on Friday night hosted in West Palm Beach, Florida, by the far-right Christian advocacy group Turning Point Action.\par \par \uc2 The former president and Republican presidential nominee told supporters:\par \par \uc2 Christians, get out and vote! Just this time \u8211\'20\'13 you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to do it any more \u8230\'20\'26 You know what? It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fixed! It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine. You won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote any more, my beautiful Christians.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 I love you. Get out \u8211\'20\'13 you gotta get out and vote. In four years, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote again. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have it fixed so good, you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna have to vote.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: \u8220\'20\'1CChristians, get out and vote! Just this time. You won\u8217\'20\'19t have to do it anymore. Four more years. You know what? It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fixed! It\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine! You won\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote anymore, my beautiful Christians. I love you, Christians! I\u8217\'20\'19m a Christian\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BFcFlBlMwz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BFcFlBlMwz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republicans against Trump (@RpsAgainstTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RpsAgainstTrump/status/1817017795013407007?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump faces backlash after telling supporters they 'won't have to vote again' if he wins\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign joined a chorus of critics sounding the alarm over recent remarks by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  telling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/trump-speech-no-need-to-vote-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crowd of supporters}}}\uc2  they won\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Chave to vote again\u8221\'20\'1D if they return him to the presidency in November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Trump, at a Friday night rally hosted in Florida by a far-right Christian advocacy group, said:\par \par \uc2 Christians, get out and vote! Just this time \u8211\'20\'13 you won\u8217\'20\'19t have to do it any more \u8230\'20\'26 You gotta get out and vote. In four years, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote again. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have it fixed so good, you\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna have to vote.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were immediately met with consternation in some political quarters, with some arguing that the Republican presidential nominee had implied that that he would end elections in the country if he returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8220\'20\'1Ca vow to end democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, while the Democratic California congressman Adam Schiff, posted to X:\par \par \uc2 This year democracy is on the ballot, and if we are to save it, we must vote against authoritarianism.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Senate is in this week. The House is out.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will head to Austin, Texas, to mark the 60th anniversary of the Civil Rights Act. He will then travel to Houston to pay his respects to \uc2 Sheila Jackson Lee\uc2 , the Democratic Texas congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/democratic-congresswoman-sheila-jackson-lee-dies-aged-74-family-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who died}}}\uc2  from pancreatic cancer last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240729ek7t001uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
