\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas sues Biden administration to limit teenage access to birth control\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 766 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2024\par 18:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Minors can receive contraception confidentially under Title X in the state with the highest repeat teen birth rate\par \par \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , the Texas attorney general, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/press/DOH%20Title%20X%20Complaint%20Filed.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  the Biden administration over a longstanding federal program that provides teenagers access to contraception without parental consent, the state\u8217\'20\'19s latest attack against the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive healthcare policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis suit is likely a preview of where the Texas GOP \u8211\'20\'13 and national Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 stand on attacking contraception access,\u8221\'20\'1D says Mary Ziegler, a professor at \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , School of Law and reproductive health expert. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Republicans say they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to take aim at contraception, this is another sign that this is actually where we\u8217\'20\'19re headed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://opa.hhs.gov/grant-programs/title-x-service-grants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Title X}}}\uc2 , created in 1970, offers comprehensive family planning and preventive health care services for low-income and uninsured residents. Texas is among a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/state-indicator/minors-authority-to-consent-to-contraceptive-services/?currentTimeframe=0&sortModel=%7B%22colId%22:%22Location%22,%22sort%22:%22asc%22%7D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handful of states}}}\uc2  that require parental consent before a teenager can get birth control \u8211\'20\'13 but Title X-funded contraception was the exception. Under the program, minors can receive contraception confidentially.\par \par \uc2 Texas has the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/02/21/texas-teenage-pregnancy-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest repeat teen birth rate}}}\uc2  and one of strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the US.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, US district judge Matthew Kacsmaryk dealt a blow to Title X when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/05/texas-contraception-birth-control-parental-consent-title-x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that the program denied Texas father Alexander Deanda\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental right to control and direct the upbringing of his minor children\u8221\'20\'1D. Texas now stands as the only state that requires Title X-funded clinics to mandate parental consent before granting teens birth control.\par \par \uc2 An appeals court largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ca5.uscourts.gov/opinions/pub/23/23-10159-CV0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld}}}\uc2  Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision in March, finding that Title X does not supersede Texas parental rights law, but left in place a Title X rule that explicitly forbids clinics from requiring parental consent before providing services.\par \par \uc2 The new lawsuit is in part an attempt to clarify that mixed ruling. Paxton argues that a 2021 Biden administration rule {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2021/10/07/2021-21542/ensuring-access-to-equitable-affordable-client-centered-quality-family-planning-services"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emphasizing}}}\uc2  that the federal program \u8220\'20\'1Cmay not require consent of parents or guardians for the provision of services to minors\u8221\'20\'1D is unlawful.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy attempting to force Texas healthcare providers to offer contraceptives to children without parental consent, the Biden administration continues to prove they will do anything to implement their extremist agenda \u8211\'20\'13 even undermine the constitution and violate the law,\u8221\'20\'1D said Paxton.\par \par \uc2 Carmen Robles Frost, a Texas mother, has joined the suit. She claims the Title X rule will \u8220\'20\'1Cfacilitate sexual promiscuity and premarital sex\u8221\'20\'1D and weaken her ability to raise her children \u8220\'20\'1Cin accordance with the teachings of the Christian faith\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/10/texas-abortion-law-jonathan-f-mitchell-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jonathan F Mitchell}}}\uc2 , architect of the state\u8217\'20\'19s bounty-hunter style \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  travel bans, represents Robles Frost in the suit, and also represented Deanda in the initial legal challenge.\par \par \uc2 The suit, filed in Amarillo, will be heard by Kacsmaryk, who is the sole federal court judge in the Northern district \u8211\'20\'13 and the reason conservatives often file in that jurisdiction, a strategy known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/texas-court-eyed-for-judge-shopping-wont-alter-case-assignments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  The far-right former religious liberty lawyer, appointed to the bench by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , previously sided with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/09/abortion-pill-trump-judge-possible-ban-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to roll back access}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone, a case that reached the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , where justices ruled the activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone#:~:text=In%20a%209%2D0%20unanimous,in%20a%20US%20medication%20abortion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  to have standing.\par \par \uc2 In their filing, Texas attorneys cite the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 6-3 decision in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-451_7m58.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Loper Bright Enterprises v Raimondo}}}\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/06/chevron-doctrine-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the \u8220\'20\'1CChevron doctrine\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a legal framework that previously directed courts to defer to the expertise of federal agencies. Legal experts have warned that all manner of federal regulations are now at risk.\par \par \uc2 This is far from the first time Texas leaders have taken aim at the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health protections. In 2022, Paxton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/executive-management/20220714_1-0_Original%20Complaint%20Biden%20Admin.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  the federal government over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cms.gov/files/document/qso-22-22-hospitals.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rules}}}\uc2  seeking to protect hospitals and doctors providing emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. The state ultimately secured an injunction from a Trump-appointee district judge in Lubbock, in a ruling upheld by the Fifth Circuit. And last year, Paxton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasattorneygeneral.gov/sites/default/files/images/press/Filed%20Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2  challenging federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/about/news/2022/07/13/hhs-issues-guidance-nations-retail-pharmacies-clarifying-their-obligations-ensure-access-comprehensive-reproductive-health-care-services.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guidance}}}\uc2  that directed pharmacies to fill prescriptions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit comes amid a broader national push from the right-wing to strengthen so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cparental rights,\u8221\'20\'1D in areas including education and gender-affirming care for LGBTQ+ students. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/24/republicans-parents-rights-education-culture-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Critics and educators}}}\uc2  say conservatives are using the term \u8220\'20\'1Cparents\u8217\'20\'19 rights\u8221\'20\'1D as a guise to advance a far-right agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe GOP has focused on the parental rights strategy to gain influence and control in schools and other areas of life,\u8221\'20\'1D says Ziegler. \u8220\'20\'1CHere, parental rights are used to strike up fear and create a stigma that contraception is dangerous for minors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240726ek7q0028m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
