\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Republican party remains the party of denying women human rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Rebecca Solnit \par \uc2 1,655 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2024\par 14:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The GOP ticket of JD Vance and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , from \u8216\'20\'18menstrual surveillance\u8217\'20\'19 to sexual assault, has made itself clear\par \par \uc2 The Republican party of the United States remains the party of denying women fundamental human rights. The US press as a whole remains the instrument of softening up or ignoring this reality.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has long been criticized for his public treatment of women,\u8221\'20\'1D ran a CNN headline. \u8220\'20\'1CThe ones in his life argue he\u8217\'20\'19s different in private.\u8221\'20\'1D What follows is a puff piece in which prominent Republican women say nice things about him, and his history of alleged sexual assault is mentioned several paragraphs down.\par \par \uc2 The first Mrs Trump is no longer in his life, though she\u8217\'20\'19s buried on his New Jersey golf course, but she charged him with raping her \u8211\'20\'13 at home, in private \u8211\'20\'13 in her 1990 sworn divorce testimony. E Jean Carroll is only casually in his life, but she won a civil lawsuit against him for sexual assault in the privacy of a department store dressing room and a second one for public defamation, and he owes her tens of millions of dollars for these cases. CNN does get around to mentioning Carroll in passing, but praise from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s protege \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  and his lawyer and daughter-in-law get the lionesses\u8217\'20\'19 share of attention, and headlines are often all viewers read.\par \par \uc2 Rape is an assault on the victim\u8217\'20\'19s body but also on her (or his or their) agency and right to bodily autonomy, though the assault on agency and autonomy can and does take many forms \u8211\'20\'13 and the Republican party and its candidates for president and vice-president support many of them. The Republican party has uncomplainingly offered up an adjudicated rapist as their presidential candidate and rallied behind a vice-presidential candidate, JD Vance, who has shown great enthusiasm for denying women basic rights and safety and sometimes survival.\par \par \uc2 One of the crucial ways Vance has sought to deny women basic rights is by what has been dubbed menstrual surveillance. In 2023, the federal \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  proposed a revision to medical privacy regulations \u8220\'20\'1Cto shield the protected health information of patients seeking lawful reproductive health care from disclosure for the purpose of criminal, civil, and administrative investigations\u8221\'20\'1D. Vance was one of the eight Republican senators who filed a letter of protest declaring: \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the Proposed Rule, however, States would be forced to cede their powers to investigate criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related activity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other words, the revision would protect women\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy around pregnancy and birth control-related healthcare, and Vance was having none of it. As Talking Points Memo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/edblog/jd-vance-menstrual-surveillance-hawk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put it}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe news has been filled with proposed or actual laws which would attempt to restrict travel to receive abortions in other states, charge those who travel or criminalize those who might facilitate such travel or facilitate the legal shipment of prescribed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs through the mail. But to enforce these laws or know when there\u8217\'20\'19s something to enforce you really need access to medical records. You need to know and be able to prove when a woman was pregnant and then, before the end of normal gestation, stopped being pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other words, to carry out these laws, the state needs to criminalize being female and fertile and put those who are under surveillance. Vance is an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  hardliner who supports a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with no exceptions. He\u8217\'20\'19s also taken to sneering at women who don\u8217\'20\'19t have children, which is, I suppose, consistent with his attacks on reproductive rights and advocacy of regressive gender roles.\par \par \uc2 Another way Vance supported violence against women is with his infamous 2022 declaration that women should stay in violent marriages for the sake of the kids. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is one of the great tricks that I think the sexual revolution pulled on the American populace, which is the idea that, like: \u8216\'20\'18Well, OK, these marriages were fundamentally, you know, they were maybe even violent, but certainly they were unhappy,\u8221\'20\'1D but ending them \u8220\'20\'1Cdidn\u8217\'20\'19t work out for the kids of those marriages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an astonishing statement if an insufficiently unusual one, the idea that the heterosexual two-parent household is somehow so magically beneficent that even if the dad is beating the mom, it\u8217\'20\'19s better for the kids than having an unbattered mom and a peaceful home.\par \par \uc2 Vance defended his statement by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/jd-vance-donald-trump-women-womens-issues-violent-marriages-abortion-1926228"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, modern society\u8217\'20\'19s war on families has made our domestic violence situation much worse,\u8221\'20\'1D which is outrageously untrue. The feminist movement brought attention to domestic violence, created domestic violence shelters, put pressure on law enforcement to address that violence, and worked to give women the economic equality and rights that give them more power to leave abusers. The cumulative effect of these measures has, along with a new ethos recognizing that women are possessed of certain inalienable rights, reduced the incidence of this often-hidden crime.\par \par \uc2 What breaks up families in which there is violence is the violence, not the victims\u8217\'20\'19 ability to escape that violence. The man who is beating his wife is often also beating his children, and intimate-partner violence all too often ends in the victim\u8217\'20\'19s death, especially if there are guns on hand. One parent killing the other is bad for the kids, too, and male partners are the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hsph.harvard.edu/news/hsph-in-the-news/homicide-leading-cause-of-death-for-pregnant-women-in-u-s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading cause of death}}}\uc2  for pregnant women and women who have recently given birth in the USA, which the right-to-life advocates should show an interest in \u8211\'20\'13 but don\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 This is why coercive control, including intimate-partner violence (IPV), and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not separate issues. The man who is beating his wife may also be raping her or engaging in sexual and reproductive coercion, in this country where feminists first made marital rape a concept and then got it recognized by the law (only in 1993 did all US states recognize marital rape, but there are still many loopholes, including states that don\u8217\'20\'19t recognize marital rape in cases when the partner was unconscious or incapacitated). And that brings us back to reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/committee-opinion/articles/2013/02/reproductive-and-sexual-coercion#:~:text=Reproductive%20coercion%20is%20related%20to,pregnancy%20coercion%2C%20and%20pregnancy%20pressure."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes}}}\uc2  that reproductive coercion includes \u8220\'20\'1Cexplicit attempts to impregnate a partner against her will, control outcomes of a pregnancy, coerce a partner to have unprotected sex, and interfere with contraceptive methods\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The college\u8217\'20\'19s website adds: \u8220\'20\'1COne quarter of adolescent females reported that their abusive male partners were trying to get them pregnant through interference with planned contraception, forcing the female partners to hide their contraceptive methods,\u8221\'20\'1D and: \u8220\'20\'1COne study found that women with unintended pregnancies were four times more likely to experience IPV than women whose pregnancies were intended.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other words, a lot of unwanted and unplanned pregnancies are the result of male coercion, not, as the right would have you believe, female carelessness. Which is why \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a crucial part of reproductive rights; a person whose pregnancy was the result of the violation of her rights needs to retain the right to terminate it. Pregnancy, as many women who have borne children have reminded us recently, is a life-changing experience that can result in incapacitation, lasting injury, economic hardship including the inability to work and care for other children, and sometimes death, especially in the absence of adequate medical care.\par \par \uc2 The denial of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is bringing women in states such as Texas and Idaho to the brink of death \u8211\'20\'13 as the journalist Jessica Valenti {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/idaho-women-flown-out-weekly-for?utm_source=publication-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Idaho women are weekly being airlifted to states where they can receive life-saving healthcare and doctors are sometimes recommending they buy evacuation insurance. Valenti also reports: \u8220\'20\'1CRape victims are being denied emergency contraception in medical centers and hospital emergency rooms\u8221\'20\'1D because the war against reproductive rights is expanding to go after in-vitro fertilization and birth control, two more ways women can choose whether and how to have children.\par \par \uc2 In his 2016 memoir, Hillbilly Elegy, Vance writes of his grandfather: \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t believe that mild-mannered Papaw, who I adored as a child, was such a violent drunk.\u8221\'20\'1D In the next sentence, he blames his grandmother: \u8220\'20\'1CHis behavior was due at least partly to Mamaw\u8217\'20\'19s disposition,\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1Cshe\u8217\'20\'19d fight back. In short, she devoted herself to making his drunken life a living hell,\u8221\'20\'1D itemizing more of her violence than his, though he does mention in passing the grandfather also gave his own daughter a black eye when she tried to break up a fight between the couple. It\u8217\'20\'19s not hard to imagine this poor woman first impregnated by this man when she was 13 stayed with him for lack of better options; it\u8217\'20\'19s clear Vance approves of her staying.\par \par \uc2 The November election is a referendum on major issues \u8211\'20\'13 the climate, the economy, the survival of democracy in America, the makeup of the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 other than the personalities of the candidates on the top of the ticket. The horse-race journalism and its relentless focus on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age and oratorical shortcomings obscured that. But those personalities connect to the issues, and while perhaps Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decades of leadership on legislation on violence against women is no longer relevant, the bill itself is.\par \par \uc2 It was reauthorized and expanded in 2022 to add protections for Native American, trans and immigrant women, and to address cyberstalking and cyberporn. The majority of Republicans in the House and Senate voted against it. On the other hand, we now have a race for the presidency between a prosecutor and a man convicted of 34 felonies, with a Yale law school graduate on the ticket with Trump: the JD Vance of 2016 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/23/politics/kfile-jd-vance-believed-donald-trump-sexual-assault-allegations-2016/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhat percentage of the American population has @realDonaldTrump sexually assaulted?\u8221\'20\'1D but the JD Vance of 2024 has made it clear he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240725ek7p001bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
