\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Unlike Joe Biden, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be a genuine champion for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,151 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2024\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 It was hard to get the president to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all, but Harris seems to realize that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a winning issue\par \par \uc2 When he was still the nominee, Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s preferred euphemism for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1CRoe\u8221\'20\'1D. He would talk about \u8220\'20\'1Cupholding\u8221\'20\'1D Roe v Wade even after June 2022, when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck it down. Reproductive rights advocates bristled at this, pointing out how many people had been denied abortions under Roe, and how flimsy the decision\u8217\'20\'19s protection of reproductive rights had been on personal-autonomy or sex-equality grounds.\par \par \uc2 Frankly, it was hard to get the president to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. He seemed to avoid even the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. When he did talk about the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 and the bans on it that Republicans have unleashed across the country \u8211\'20\'13 he preferred to focus on women who had been denied emergency abortions for wanted pregnancies in the midst of tragic health complications.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in his hands, became an issue in which sad, troubled and helpless women could be aided by the mercy of heroic men like himself \u8211\'20\'13 or like that of the imagined doctor he referenced in his disastrous June debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a man, Biden said, who would determine whether an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeker \u8220\'20\'1Cneeded help or not\u8221\'20\'1D. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in his telling, was an unpleasant but necessary evil that men mediated for women. It was decidedly not a matter of adult women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, dignity or right of autonomy over their own bodies and lives.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s successor at the top of the Democratic ticket following his withdrawal last Sunday, has taken a different approach. The Biden administration had largely delegated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights messaging to the vice-president, out of deference both for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s obvious personal discomfort with the issue and his growing inability to campaign effectively at all. (The anti-choice group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America named Harris as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  czar\u8221\'20\'1D, a name that perhaps sounds a little cooler than they intended.) She made a multistate tour focusing on the issue earlier this year, which included what is believed to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/health/health-news/harris-bold-abortion-stance-impact-2024-election-biden-exit-rcna163016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first public visit}}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic by a president or vice-president: a stop at a \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  in St Paul, Minnesota, where Harris appeared with the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s medical director, and commended the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s staff for their \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is only right and fair that people have access to the healthcare they need,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-68568383"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The result was a divergence of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  messaging within the White House, with Harris making a much more robust case for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and for reproductive justice more broadly, in much more affirmative and unapologetic terms. The preferred catchphrase that she repeated when speaking about the issue was not Biden\u8217\'20\'19s tepid and euphemistic \u8220\'20\'1Crestore Roe\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead, Harris has made apparent reference to Dr George Tiller, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctor who was murdered by anti-choice extremists in 2009, who summarized his own approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two words: \u8220\'20\'1CTrust women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before Biden dropped out of the race, November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election was set to be little more than a referendum on his age. But now that he has stepped aside, Harris has an opportunity to make a much stronger case for a Democratic policy vision. And reproductive rights, an issue that has motivated women voters in large numbers even in deep-conservative states since the Dobbs decision, appears to be at the center of her agenda.\par \par \uc2 The move is good politics. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are extraordinarily popular, and have only become more so in the years since Dobbs, mobilizing voters who would stay home or vote for Republicans when other issues are more salient. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/support-for-legal-abortion-increased-since-roe-v-wade-was-overturned/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll}}}\uc2  from the Associated Press finds that six in 10 Americans support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any reason; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/321143/americans-stand-abortion.aspx#:~:text=Support%20for%20Abortion%20Rights%20Varies,and%2022%25%20for%20the%20third."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other polls}}}\uc2  show even higher levels of support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially early in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the abstract, is popular: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, in particular, are profoundly unpopular. The reality of post-Dobbs bans has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dramatically moved public opinion}}}\uc2  on the issue: since May 2019, the percent of Americans who say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal under all circumstances has increased by 10 points, to 35%. The percent who say it should be illegal under all circumstances \u8211\'20\'13 the position advocated by the Republican party platform, which supports recognition of fetuses and embryos as persons under the 14th amendment \u8211\'20\'13 has fallen dramatically during that same period, to just 12%.\par \par \uc2 These shifts in public opinion have had a marked impact at the ballot box. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 better-than-expected showing in the November 2022 midterms is credited to outrage against the Dobbs decision that June. But a desire to protect or restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has driven large turnout even in heavily Republican states: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/2022-live-primary-election-race-results/2022/08/02/1115317596/kansas-voters-abortion-legal-reject-constitutional-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/kentucky-voters-reject-constitutional-amendment-on-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ohio-abortion-amendment-election-2023-fe3e06747b616507d8ca21ea26485270"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  have all voted overwhelmingly in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since Dobbs. Harris has seized on this shift in a way that Biden has not been able to, speaking passionately \u8211\'20\'13 and credibly \u8211\'20\'13 about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a matter of not only health, but also dignity.\par \par \uc2 Harris has also cannily and repeatedly drawn connections between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last term, in which three anti-choice zealots were appointed to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , and the suffering that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have caused in Republican-controlled states. She refers to the state laws prohibiting the procedure as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/morning-joe/watch/vp-harris-in-state-after-state-we-are-seeing-trump-abortion-bans-213542469584"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. This focus could bear fruit in November: alongside Harris\u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid, a total of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/dashboard/ballot-tracker-status-of-abortion-related-state-constitutional-amendment-measures/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five states}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Nevada, Colorado, South Dakota, Maryland and Florida \u8211\'20\'13 will have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights measures on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The Republican ticket, meanwhile, has leaned further and further into an ideology of misogyny and gender reaction. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, is a passionate and lurid misogynist; he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RonFilipkowski/status/1815503440983867598"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently referred}}}\uc2  to Harris and other Democratic women as \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies who are miserable at their own lives\u8221\'20\'1D, and that childless women \u8220\'20\'1Chave no direct stake\u8221\'20\'1D in America\u8217\'20\'19s future. He has also suggested that citizens without children should have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/jd-vance-parents-vote/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their votes diluted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Childless women seem to be a particularly irksome demographic for the Trump camp\u8217\'20\'19s army of prurient creeps: both the media personality {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lauraloomer/status/1815373648800239831"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Laura Loomer}}}\uc2  and the lawyer and thinktank gadfly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/willchamberlain/status/1815150185300759014?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Chamberlain}}}\uc2  quickly joined Vance in attacking Harris for not having biological children. It\u8217\'20\'19s a fitting line of attack; after all, the very reason why Republicans are pursuing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the first place is because they have an extremely narrow view of what women should be, one they want to enforce with the law.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates will certainly seek to push Harris for even more commitments for reproductive freedom and justice. But Harris, at least, is willing to argue that women can be things other than mothers. Like maybe the president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240725ek7p001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
