\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump team makes complaint about Harris campaign funds \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Maanvi Singh ,Chris Stein, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, and Yohannes Lowe (earlier) \par \uc2 23,890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2024\par 08:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. Read the latest at the links below:Who might \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  pick for VP? Three favorites emerge\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing shortly. You can find all of the latest Guardian US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here are the key developments from the last few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made the first public speech of her presidential campaign, promising {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ff91b8f082b7073589669#block-669ff91b8f082b7073589669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to unite Democrats}}}\uc2  during a visit to the vital swing state of Wisconsin, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ffa0e8f0804734c48d7fc#block-669ffa0e8f0804734c48d7fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparing}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the sorts of criminals she used to prosecute in California. Earlier in the day, the two most powerful Democrats in Congress, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fe3e08f08b200a0085721#block-669fe3e08f08b200a0085721"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced their endorsements}}}\uc2  of the vice-president, underscoring the glide path Harris appears to be on to become the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he wants to debate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  despite speculation that he was seeking a way out. Trump had been due to face \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on 10 September but, after the president\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal, cast doubt on whether he would still take part.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Harris campaign noted that they had raised $100m in donations in the 36 hours since Biden withdrew from the 2024 race, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBaseless legal claims \u8211\'20\'13 like the ones they\u8217\'20\'19ve made for years to try to suppress votes and steal elections \u8211\'20\'13 will only distract them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign on Tuesday filed a complaint with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  against Harris, accusing her 2024 campaign of violating federal campaign finance laws by replacing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name with her own to take control of his campaign funds.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator Bernie Sanders has condemned Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming address to the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , and US military support for the war, calling Netanyahu a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar criminal\u8221\'20\'1D presiding over a \u8220\'20\'1Crightwing extremist government\u8221\'20\'1D. Sanders delivered his remarks on the Senate floor on Tuesday as Congress expects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Netanyahu}}}\uc2  to give a speech to Congress on Wednesday afternoon. The speech comes after an underwhelming arrival to the US, just after President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his withdrawal from November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Comments \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance made in 2021 questioning Harris\u8217\'20\'19s leadership because she did not have biological children have resurfaced, testing the young conservative senator in his early days campaigning as part of the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  arrested Jewish activists protesting against US military support for Israel inside a congressional building on Tuesday, a day before Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is scheduled to deliver a speech to Congress. The protesters, organized by activist group Jewish Voice for Peace, wore red T-shirts bearing the phrases \u8220\'20\'1Cnot in our name\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CJews say stop arming Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D Some carried banners reading \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire now\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clet Gaza live.\u8221\'20\'1D The activist group said over 250 protesters were arrested and 400 people took part in the demonstration. Police said around 200 people were arrested.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Secret Service officials are reported to be encouraging \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign to stop holding outdoor rallies in the wake of the 13 July assassination attempt on the former president at a fairground in Butler, Pennsylvania. The move, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/23/trump-rallies-secret-service-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , comes as Secret Service director Kimberly Cheatle resigned on Tuesday following a combative grilling before a congressional committee by both Democrats and Republicans over apparent security failures before an attempt on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life by a 20-year-old gunman.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ff4348f08b200a00857b7#block-669ff4348f08b200a00857b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will meet}}}\uc2  with the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , when he visits Washington DC, and the pair will also sit down with the families of American hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Harris will attend neither event.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8#block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will vote}}}\uc2  on setting up a bipartisan panel to investigate the Trump assassination attempt, its Republican and Democratic leaders said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden condemned an Ohio state senator who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2#block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Ca civil war to save the country\u8221\'20\'1D as he introduced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance yesterday. The state senator apologized.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the oversight committee, joined Republicans in approving of Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s decision to resign, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537#block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also saying}}}\uc2  the Trump rally shooting proves assault weapons must be banned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , the New Jersey senator convicted on charges related to accepting bribes,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fec748f082b70735895f4#block-669fec748f082b70735895f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly}}}\uc2  resign his Senate seat in August.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s outspoken stance on the Gaza war hints at a possible shift from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Israel policy as she eyes the Democratic presidential nomination - as \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is likely to find out this week, AFP reports.\par \par \uc2 The US vice president will be conspicuously absent from the Israeli leader\u8217\'20\'19s address to the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  on Wednesday, in what analysts said was a clear signal about her concerns over civilian casualties in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The 59-year-old has never contradicted Biden on Israel. Time and again, however, she has been the US administration official most loudly calling for a ceasefire in the conflict.\par \par \uc2 With Biden\u8217\'20\'19s shock exit from the White House race, Harris has a chance to make a \u8220\'20\'1Cclean slate\u8221\'20\'1D on an issue where there has been a risk of alienating a swathe of Democratic voters ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s election, said Colin Clarke, director of research at the Soufan Group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Israel-Gaza issue is the one where there is the most daylight between Biden and Harris, and I think there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be people inside her camp that are going to push her to make that difference explicit,\u8221\'20\'1D he told AFP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Police arrest hundreds of protestors at US Capitol\par \par \uc2 Back now to the anti-war protests that happened at Capitol Hill earlier today. At least 200 protestors have been arrested, according to police and organisers, who have given different numbers.\par \par \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  arrested Jewish activists protesting against US military support for Israel inside a congressional building on Tuesday, a day before Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is scheduled to deliver a speech to Congress.\par \par \uc2 The protesters, organized by activist group Jewish Voice for Peace, wore red T-shirts bearing the phrases \u8220\'20\'1Cnot in our name\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CJews say stop arming Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D Some carried banners reading \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire now\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clet Gaza live.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protests are planned to coincide with Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s visit, in which he will meet President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The activist group said over 250 protesters were arrested and 400 people took part in the demonstration.\par \par \uc2 Police said around 200 people were arrested.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe told the people, who legally entered, to stop or they would be arrested. They did not stop,\u8221\'20\'1D the police said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemonstrating inside the Congressional Buildings is against the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is video of Sanders\u8217\'20\'19s speech:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Full story: Bernie Sanders condemns speech to Congress by \u8216\'20\'18war criminal\u8217\'20\'19 Netanyahu\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator Bernie Sanders has condemned Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming address to the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar criminal\u8221\'20\'1D presiding over a \u8220\'20\'1Crightwing extremist government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sanders delivered his remarks on the Senate floor on Tuesday as Congress expects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Netanyahu}}}\uc2  to give a speech to Congress on Wednesday afternoon. The speech comes after an underwhelming arrival to the US, just after President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his withdrawal from November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTomorrow will be unique in bringing Prime Minister Netanyahu to address a joint meeting of Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be the first time in American history that a war criminal has been given that honor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders said of Netanyahu: \u8220\'20\'1CHe should not be welcome in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic lawmakers were planning to boycott the speech on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/bernie-sanders-netanyahu-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders condemns speech to Congress by \u8216\'20\'18war criminal\u8217\'20\'19 Netanyahu}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 The rally site in Butler where the attempted assassination took place had clear sightlines to the stage far beyond its security perimeter, including the roof from which suspected shooter Thomas Matthews Crooks fired off an estimated seven rounds before being fatally shot by Secret Service snipers.\par \par \uc2 It has since been reported that Crooks was able to scout out the rally site with a drone and had been identified as \u8220\'20\'1Csuspicious\u8221\'20\'1D an hour before the event. The presidential protection agency had assigned security of the roof to local law enforcement and had been notified of a suspicious person minutes before the shooting took place.\par \par \uc2 Former White House physician \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2 , now a Texas representative, said at the weekend that the bullet that grazed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ear came \u8220\'20\'1Cless than a quarter of an inch from entering his head\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas, the homeland security secretary, appointed Ronald Rowe, deputy director of the Secret Service, to serve as the acting director until a permanent replacement is chosen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34am BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign, which may have favored outdoor venues until the shooting because of their larger crowd capacity, is not currently planning further outdoor events and instead is looking to book indoor venues, including basketball arenas, according to the outlet.\par \par \uc2 During a rally in an arena in Grand Rapids, Michigan, on Saturday, Trump appeared to lament that some supporters had been left outside. The Republican candidate is also known for exaggerating crowd estimates, dating back at least to his inauguration in 2017.\par \par \uc2 Since launching his first presidential bid, Trump has held hundreds of outdoor rallies that have become like festivals for his most ardent supporters, featuring tailgate parties and vendors hawking Trump memorabilia and campaign merchandise.\par \par \uc2 According to the Post, Trump advisers had told the Secret Service the 2024 re-election campaign was planning to hold large events, and would need increased protection and assets. But the agency is believed to have turned down the requests, citing a lack of resources.\par \par \uc2 If Trump now holds rallies in more secure locations, such as sports arenas, they will prove more expensive to the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/secret-service-outdoor-rallies-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service urging Trump to stop outdoor rallies after shooting \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service officials are reported to be encouraging \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign to stop holding outdoor rallies in the wake of the 13 July assassination attempt on the former president at a fairground in Butler, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The move, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/23/trump-rallies-secret-service-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , comes as Secret Service director Kimberly Cheatle resigned on Tuesday following a combative grilling before a congressional committee by both Democrats and Republicans over apparent security failures before an attempt on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life by a 20-year-old gunman.\par \par \uc2 In a resignation letter, Cheatle said she\u8217\'20\'19d made the \u8220\'20\'1Cdifficult\u8221\'20\'1D decision to leave the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cwith a heavy heart\u8221\'20\'1D and acknowledged that the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cfell short\u8221\'20\'1D of its mission \u8220\'20\'1Cto protect our nation\u8217\'20\'19s leaders\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the Butler rally.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/secret-service-outdoor-rallies-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service urging Trump to stop outdoor rallies after shooting \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 The intent is to promote the principles that made America great in the first place,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk told Peterson. \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say that I\u8217\'20\'19m for example MAGA,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, referring to the Trump catch phrase. \u8220\'20\'1CI think America is great. I\u8217\'20\'19m more M-A-G, make America greater.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said it would promote \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom. Freedom to operate, meaning the least amount of government intervention possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 The claim is \u8220\'20\'1Csimply not true,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk told Jordan Peterson. \u8220\'20\'1CI am not donating $45m a month to Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow what I have done is that I have created a Pac or super pac or whatever you want to call it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. It is called the America Pac.\par \par \uc2 It is a political organisation that can receive funding, that funding can then be used to help with political campaigns, he said.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how much he is donating to the Super Pac.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/23/us/politics/elon-musk-super-pac-desantis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  meanwhile that, \u8220\'20\'1CTwo Republican operatives who played senior roles helping the presidential campaign of Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida have taken on leadership roles,\u8221\'20\'1D at the Pac.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe aides, Generra Peck, who initially managed the DeSantis campaign, and Phil Cox, a former head of the \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2  who ran the DeSantis political operation in the years before his run, are quietly guiding the group, America PAC, according to three people briefed on the matter who were not authorized to discuss it publicly,\u8221\'20\'1D the times reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Musk, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/18/us/politics/elon-musk-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who recently endorsed former President Donald J. Trump}}}\uc2  and is a friend of Mr. Lonsdale, has described himself as having \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated\u8221\'20\'1D the group and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/15/us/politics/elon-musk-trump-super-pac.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected to donate,}}}\uc2  but the amount remains unclear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Musk backs away from reported plans to give $45m a month to Trump super Pac\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has said in a post on X that he never said he was donating $45 million a month to Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Musk said he planed to give $45m a month to a Super Pac focused on electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , starting in July, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/elon-musk-has-said-he-is-committing-around-45-million-a-month-to-a-new-pro-trump-super-pac-dda53823"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Today, after denying the claim on Jordan Peterson\u8217\'20\'19s show, Musk replied to a Tweet claiming, \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  never said that he was donating $45M/month to Trump \u8211\'20\'13 that was a totally fake WSJ article\u8221\'20\'1D, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CYeah\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrElon Musk never said that he was donating $45M/month to Trump \u8211\'20\'13 that was a totally fake WSJ article.\par \par \uc2 He just created a Super PAC focused on supporting candidates who favor a meritocracy and personal freedom, but funding to date has been far below that.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RQEsJkHnqr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RQEsJkHnqr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DogeDesigner (@cb_doge) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cb_doge/status/1815910224026386671?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 To another Tweet he replied:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, it\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous. I am making some donations to America PAC, but at a much lower level and the key values of the PAC are supporting a meritocracy & individual freedom. Republicans are mostly, but not entirely, on the side of merit & freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 After about a half-hour of clapping and chanting, officers from the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  issued several warnings, then began arresting protesters \u8212\'20\'14 binding their hands with zip ties and leading them away one-by-one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am the daughter of Holocaust survivors and I know what a Holocaust looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jane Hirschmann, a native of Saugerties, New York, who drove down for the protest along with her two daughters \u8212\'20\'14 both of whom were arrested. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we say \u8216\'20\'18Never Again,\u8217\'20\'19 we mean never for anybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The demonstrators focused much of their ire on the Biden administration, demanding that the president immediately cease all arms shipments to Israel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not focusing on Netanyahu. He\u8217\'20\'19s just a symptom,\u8221\'20\'1D Hirschmann said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut how can (Biden) be calling for a cease-fire when he\u8217\'20\'19s sending them bombs and planes?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of 8pm Tuesday night, the \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  said they did not have a final tally of the number of people arrested. But JVP claimed in a statement that 400 people, \u8220\'20\'1Cincluding over a dozen rabbis,\u8221\'20\'1D had been arrested.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 More now about the anti-war protests on Capitol hill, via AP:\par \par \uc2 Protesters against the Gaza war staged a sit-in at a congressional office building Tuesday ahead of Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s address to Congress, with \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  making multiple arrests.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu arrived in Washington Monday for a visit that includes meetings with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and a Wednesday speech before a joint session of Congress. Dozens of protesters rallied outside his hotel Monday evening, and on Tuesday afternoon, hundreds of demonstrators staged a flashmob-style protest in the Cannon Building, which houses offices of House of Representatives members.\par \par \uc2 Organized by Jewish Voice for Peace, protesters wearing red T-shirts that read \u8220\'20\'1CNot In Our Name\u8221\'20\'1D took over the building\u8217\'20\'19s rotunda, sitting on the floor, unfurling signs and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CLet Gaza Live!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 The complaint, earlier reported by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , also argued that Harris taking over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remaining campaign funds amounted to an excessive unlawful contribution given that \u8220\'20\'1CBiden for President\u8221\'20\'1D was not an authorized committee for the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Mr Biden will not seek the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, then he will never participate in the general election and all general election contributions received by Biden for President are excessive and must be disposed of,\u8221\'20\'1D the complaint said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s strategy, according to people familiar with the matter, has included opening new legal battles to try to prevent Harris from accessing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s funds, although the complaint on Tuesday stopped short of a lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Warrington made that explicit request to the \uc2 FEC\uc2  in the complaint, asking the agency to enjoin the transfer. And if the \uc2 FEC\uc2  were to deem the transfer unlawful, the complaint said, it would ask the \uc2 FEC\uc2  to consider issuing a fine or making a criminal referral to the US justice department.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has viewed the \uc2 FEC\uc2  complaint as a spurious legal effort to throw sand in their gears, noting that the Biden-Harris committees have always been authorized committees for either Biden or Harris, according to a person familiar with the thinking.\par \par \uc2 And in a statement, the Harris campaign noted that they had raised $100m in donations in the 36 hours since Biden withdrew from the 2024 race, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBaseless legal claims \u8211\'20\'13 like the ones they\u8217\'20\'19ve made for years to try to suppress votes and steal elections \u8211\'20\'13 will only distract them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/trump-files-complaint-harris-campaign-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump files complaint against Harris for taking over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign funds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump files complaint against Harris for taking over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign funds\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign on Tuesday filed a complaint with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  against Vice-President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , accusing her 2024 campaign of violating federal campaign finance laws by replacing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name with her own to take control of his campaign funds.\par \par \uc2 The complaint, filed by the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s general counsel, David Warrington, argued that the Biden campaign could not rename its committee from \u8220\'20\'1CBiden for President\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1CHarris for President\u8221\'20\'1D once Biden dropped out of the race on Sunday, and roll over $91m.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is little more than a thinly veiled $91.5m excessive contribution from one presidential candidate to another, that is, from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s old campaign to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new campaign. This effort makes a mockery of our campaign finance laws,\u8221\'20\'1D the eight-page complaint said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFederal candidates are prohibited from keeping contributions for elections in which they do not participate,\u8221\'20\'1D it added. \u8220\'20\'1CBiden for President 2024 has shown no intention to properly refund or re-designate the general election funds it has already received. This makes them all excess contributions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whether the complaint generates traction with the \uc2 FEC\uc2  remains unclear, but the Trump campaign has been looking for any way to slow down the momentum Harris has been able to generate with voters and donors after she quickly became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-democratic-delegates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presumptive Democratic nominee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/trump-files-complaint-harris-campaign-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump files complaint against Harris for taking over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign funds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says Secret Service director didn't 'have much of choice' but to resign\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he does not think Kimberly Cheatle \u8220\'20\'1Chad much of a choice\u8221\'20\'1D but to leave her post as Secret Service director after mounting questions about an assassination attempt against the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt should have happened, I would say, within an hour, not nine days, ten days,\u8221\'20\'1D he said during a \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  interview Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThat would seem to be inevitable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Trump said he still feels physically safe as the Republican nominee. \u8220\'20\'1CI have to feel safe. Otherwise, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to do this stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The former president said he believes his protective detail, \u8220\'20\'1Cshould have had people on that rooftop\u8221\'20\'1D where the gunman fired his shots, \u8220\'20\'1Cand they should have told me that there was a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  co-founder donates $7m to Harris super PAC\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2  has donated $7m to a super PAC that supports Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 run for US president, a source close to Hastings said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The source was confirming a report published by The Information earlier in the day. It is the largest political donation by Hastings to a single candidate, the publication said.\par \par \uc2 Hastings congratulated Harris on Monday after she received the support of a majority of Democratic delegates to become the party nominee against Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongrats to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  - now it is time to win,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a post on social media platform X.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongrats to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  -- now it is time to win\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2  (@reedhastings) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/reedhastings/status/1815603833927815360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stepped aside as the Democratic candidate for the 2024 election and endorsed Harris on Sunday following pressure from Democrats in Congress and donors including Hastings.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign raised $81m in the 24 hours following Biden\u8217\'20\'19s exit, the most for a single day in the 2024 campaign for either party.\par \par \uc2 Hastings co-founded \uc2 Netflix\uc2  in 1997 and stepped down as CEO in 2023. He now serves as executive chairman of the \uc2 Netflix\uc2  board.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 State election directors from across the country voiced serious concerns to a top \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  official Tuesday that the system won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to handle an expected crush of mail-in ballots in the November election, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Steven Carter, manager of election and government programs for the postal service, attempted to reassure the directors at a meeting in Minneapolis that the system\u8217\'20\'19s office of inspector general (OIG) will publish an election mail report next week containing \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraging\u8221\'20\'1D performance numbers for this year so far.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe data that that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing showing improvements in the right direction,\u8221\'20\'1D Carter told a conference of the National Association of State Election Directors. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think the OIG report is especially complimentary of how we\u8217\'20\'19re handling the election now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 In case you missed this earlier: Trump said he will meet with \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  on Friday at his resort in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLooking forward to welcoming \uc2 Bibi Netanyahu\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago in Palm Beach, Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a post on Truth Social on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Back to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 FEC\uc2  filing:\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maggie Haberman reports that the filing may not be resolved before election day.\par \par \uc2 Not all campaign finance legal experts share [Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s general counsel David Warrington\u8217\'20\'19s] view \u8211\'20\'13 some believe the Harris team is on legally safe ground \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what the \uc2 FEC\uc2  will decide. But the Trump team is looking to grind the gears in the transition from Mr Biden to Ms Harris in any way they can.\par \par \uc2 Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers had made clear they would seek to legally block Mr Biden from transferring funds to Ms Harris, suggesting a lawsuit was likely. Instead, they are filing a complaint with the \uc2 FEC\uc2 , which may not be resolved before election day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders ends his speech by saying Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crightwing extremist government should not receive another nickel from US taxpayers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 The US has provided Israel with tens of billions of dollars of military aid, says Sanders.\par \par \uc2 Here is a recent story on US weapons funding for Israel:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/14/biden-israel-weapons-package-rafah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US advances $1bn Israel weapons package amid Rafah tensions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMadam President let us remember and understand that the Israel of today is not the Israel of the past,\u8221\'20\'1D says Sanders.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 These are not only acts of extreme cruelty, but they are violations of US and international law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are war crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D says Sanders. And Netanyahu has enacted them.\par \par \uc2 When Netanyahu speaks tomorrow, he hopes that people present will think \u8220\'20\'1Cfor just one second\u8221\'20\'1D about what Sanders has detailed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll this death and destruction is not just the unfortunate byproduct of a brutal war. Revenge and destruction are the explicit policy of Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s extremist government,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is very little clean water. Many roads are impassable and there is virtually no electricity,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders says.\par \par \uc2 Gaza had 12 universities, every single one has been bombed.\par \par \uc2 Many many children have lost their arms and their legs, he says. The healthcare system has been \u8220\'20\'1Csystematically obliterated\u8221\'20\'1D, he says.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 WHO\uc2  has recorded more than 1,000 attacks on healthcare facilities, he says.\par \par \uc2 The tiniest children and their mothers suffer as a result, he says.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just the displacement of 1.9 million people, not just the destruction of housing, educational infrastructure, the annihilation of the hospital system, he says.\par \par \uc2 As a result of Israeli restrictions on humanitarian aid, people in Gaza are now starving to death.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo remember when people stand up and applaud [Netanyahu tomorrow]\u8221\'20\'1D women and children are starving to death.\par \par \uc2 More than 50,000 children require treatment for acute malnutrition, he says. \u8220\'20\'1CRemember the starving children that he has created,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, when Netanyahu is speaking.\par \par \uc2 Childhood malnutrition creates lifelong problems, he says.\par \par \uc2 I would ask my colleagues to stop for a moment and think of the psychological damage, he says.\par \par \uc2 He asks senators to imagine being five years old, or 10 years old, and seeing relatives killed, or having to search for water and food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCarrying your little belongings through streets running with sewage,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, and filled with rubble.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Sanders denounces upcoming Netanyahu Congress address\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza has \u8220\'20\'1Ctrampled on international law, on American law, and on basic human values\u8221\'20\'1D, Sanders says.\par \par \uc2 He is addressing the Senate ahead of \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming Congress address tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will not be presiding over Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s address because she will be campaigning, a decision some have interpreted as evidence of her views on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 One of the worst disasters in modern history has been \u8220\'20\'1Caided and abetted\u8221\'20\'1D by the US, Sanders says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us be clear as to what has been going on in Gaza right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At least 39,000 Palestinians have been killed, he says. Sixty percent are women and children. The toll is believed to be much higher, he says, because thousands are believed to be buried under rubble. Ninety percent of the population has been driven from their homes.\par \par \uc2 In some cases they have been displaced four or five times, he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders speaks in Senate on Netanyahu's upcoming Congress address\par \par \uc2 Vermont senator Bernie Sanders is speaking now in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  about \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s address to Congress tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be unique,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders says, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause it will be the first time a war criminal has been invited to do so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It will make it impossible for the US to lecture any country on earth about human rights and dignity, he says.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli prime minister has been credibly accused of war crimes, he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FEC\uc2  complaint, which is unlikely to work, is filed against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as well as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Biden for President (aka Harris for President) and Keana Spencer, as treasurer \u8220\'20\'1Cfor flagrantly violating the Act by making and receiving an excessive contribution of nearly one hundred million dollars, and for filing fraudulent forms with the Commission purporting to repurpose one candidate\u8217\'20\'19s principal campaign committee for the use of another candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign raised an astonishing $100m in 36 hours, breaking records and raising more than the Biden campaign had raised in months. Harris has inherited the Biden campaign funds, too, as well as his staff.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign accuses Harris of '$91.5m heist' of Biden campaign cash in \uc2 FEC\uc2  complaint\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is reviewing \uc2 FEC\uc2  filing by the Trump campaign, which begins by alleging that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is seeking to perpetrate a $91.5 million dollar heist of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leftover campaign cash\u8212\'20\'14a brazen money grab that would constitute the single largest excessive contribution and biggest violation in the history of the Federal Election Campaign Act of 1971, as amended (the \u8216\'20\'18Act\u8217\'20\'19).\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Daniel Weiner, former \uc2 FEC\uc2  counsel and head of the Brennan Center for Justice\u8217\'20\'19s Elections & Government program, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2024/07/22/can-the-gop-sue-over-harris-getting-bidens-campaign-funds-sure---but-it-likely-wont-work/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Forbes\uc2  that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cperfectly legal for [Harris] to use the campaign funds\u8221\'20\'1D and that the law was clear on the matter.\par \par \uc2 More shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Iowa judge rules state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law will take effect Monday\par \par \uc2 An Iowa judge has ruled the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law will take effect Monday, preventing most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy, before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The law passed last year, but a judge had blocked it from being enforced. The Iowa supreme court reiterated in June that there is no constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state and ordered the hold to be lifted. That translated into Monday\u8217\'20\'19s district court judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision ordering the law to into effect next Monday at 8.00am CT.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers asked Judge Jeffrey Farrell for notice before allowing the law to take hold, saying a buffer period was needed to provide continuity of services. Iowa requires pregnant women to wait 24 hours for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after getting an initial consultation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  had been legal in the state up to 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access stands to be a major issue in the 2024 election. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything is at stake\u8221\'20\'1D with reproductive health in November\u8217\'20\'19s election and has traveled across the country to draw attention to the issue, including in Des Moines roughly a year ago after the stricter law initially passed.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/iowa-abortion-law-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa law banning most abortions after six weeks will take effect on Monday}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not actually saying no to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D BLM leader Shalomyah Bowers told Reuters in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are saying yes to process. We\u8217\'20\'19re saying yes to having Black people be able to have the ability to weigh in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted that the statement represents the views of many stakeholders in BLM\u8217\'20\'19s Global Network, but that individual chapters of the group are autonomous and may have a different view.\par \par \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chairman \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  said on Monday that the party will deliver a presidential nominee by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe process has been fair. It\u8217\'20\'19s been open. It\u8217\'20\'19s been transparent,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said in a Today Show interview that aired Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut if anybody is thinking about running, you\u8217\'20\'19re running against the sitting vice-president, who, along with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has worked really hard going across this country building relationships and is probably the most qualified person to be on this ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2  demanded on Tuesday that the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  immediately host an informal, virtual snap primary across the country prior to the Democratic convention in August, just hours after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  secured enough delegates for the nomination, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2  (BLM) called on Democratic party leaders to allow public participation in the nomination of the presidential candidate, instead of leaving it to the party delegates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe current political landscape is unprecedented, with President Biden stepping aside in a manner never seen before. This moment calls for decisive action to protect the integrity of our democracy and the voices of Black voters,\u8221\'20\'1D BLM said.\par \par \uc2 The statement by \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , a decentralized political and racial justice movement that helped lead the global protests over police violence in 2020, interrupted a steady drumbeat of left-leaning voices and groups that have vowed to support the vice-president after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  endorsed her on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is more from our report at the time on how the gunman was able to fly a drone over the event site the day Trump was due to speak:\par \par \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks, the gunman who tried to assassinate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  a week ago, was able to fly a camera-equipped drone over the fairgrounds near Butler, Pennsylvania, shortly before the former president was set to speak there, according to news reports.\par \par \uc2 The latest disclosure about security lapses that preceded the shooting comes as a more complete picture of Crooks\u8217\'20\'19 preparations is emerging, though it still lacks any definitive motive for the 20-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s actions that led to Trump being grazed by a bullet, the shooting death of former fire chief Corey Comperatore and the critical wounding of two rally-goers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/trump-gunman-flew-drone-over-rally-site-hours-before-attempted-assassination-2d0e2e1a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 , which cited law enforcement officials, said Crooks flew the drone on a programmed flight path earlier on the day of the shootings \u8211\'20\'13 13 July \u8211\'20\'13 on a predetermined path over the event site.\par \par \uc2 Later in the day, the would-be assassin fired at least six rounds from a semi-automatic rifle from the roof of the American Glass Research building roughly 150 yards from where Trump was speaking. Soon after, Crooks was killed by a Secret Service counter-sniper with a single bullet to the head.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/thomas-matthew-crooks-drone-trump-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gunman at Trump rally flew drone over fairgrounds earlier on day of shootings}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back to that report that the Trump campaign has been advised not to hold large outdoor rallies \u8211\'20\'13 and has none planned, according to unnamed sources who spoke to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Large outdoor rallies have been a defining feature of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaigns. They have been held in parking lots, football stadiums, airports and fairgrounds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey usually include large rosters of speakers before Trump takes the stage, with crowds sometimes enduring the heat or the cold for many hours. The crowd sometimes departs before Trump, who is regularly late, finishes speaking,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says.\par \par \uc2 Part of the reason behind the advice may be that outdoor venues are easier to access prior to an event.\par \par \uc2 The person who attempted to assassinate Trump had flown a drone over the field adjacent to the outdoor venue where it was held:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/20/thomas-matthew-crooks-drone-trump-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gunman at Trump rally flew drone over fairgrounds earlier on day of shootings}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 2021 clip of Vance criticising Harris for being 'childless' resurfaces online\par \par \uc2 Comments \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance made in 2021 questioning Harris\u8217\'20\'19s leadership because she did not have biological children have resurfaced, testing the young conservative senator in his early days campaigning as part of the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 During Vance\u8217\'20\'19s bid for the Senate from Ohio, he said in a Fox News interview that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are effectively run in this country via the Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D and referred to them as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bunch of childless cat ladies who are miserable at their own lives and the choices that they\u8217\'20\'19ve made and so they want to make the rest of the country miserable, too.\u8221\'20\'1D He said that included Harris, US Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  and US Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a New York Democrat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow does it make any sense that we\u8217\'20\'19ve turned our country over to people who don\u8217\'20\'19t really have a direct stake in it?\u8221\'20\'1D Vance asked. Harris became stepmother to two teenagers when she married entertainment lawyer Douglas Emhoff in 2014. And Buttigieg announced he and his husband adopted infant twins in September 2021, more than a month before Vance made those comments.\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance says women who haven\u8217\'20\'19t given birth like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies who are miserable at their own lives,\u8221\'20\'1D and have \u8220\'20\'1Cno direct stake\u8221\'20\'1D in America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3DJY3pQTGe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3DJY3pQTGe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ron Filipkowski (@RonFilipkowski) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonFilipkowski/status/1815503440983867598?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The clip has started to spread online, with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  sharing it in a Tuesday post on X and adding sarcastically \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat a normal, relatable guy who certainly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t hate women having freedoms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat a normal, relatable guy who certainly doesn't hate women having freedoms. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aa9UJaM8CU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aa9UJaM8CU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  (@HillaryClinton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1815738777513451805?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service advises Trump not to hold large outdoor rallies \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Hi, this is Helen Sullivan taking over the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US politics coverage.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  is reporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/23/trump-rallies-secret-service-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that}}}\uc2  the Secret Service has \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraged\u8221\'20\'1D Trump to stop holding large outdoor rallies or other large events outdoors.\par \par \uc2 Citing unnamed people familiar with the matter, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CFor upcoming events, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team is scouting indoor venues, such as basketball arenas and other large spaces where thousands of people can fit, people familiar with the request said. The campaign is not currently planning any large outdoor events, a person close to Trump said.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has filed a complaint with the Federal Elections Commission to stop the rolling Biden\u8217\'20\'19s of campaign funds to Harris.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/07/23/us/harris-trump-news-election-biden?partner=slack&smid=sl-share#trump-campaign-files-complaint-over-transfer-of-biden-funds-to-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  New York Times}}}\uc2  first reported the news. The complaint had been anticipated \u8211\'20\'13 but is unlikely to work.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Weiner, former \uc2 FEC\uc2  counsel and head of the Brennan Center for Justice\u8217\'20\'19s Elections & Government program, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2024/07/22/can-the-gop-sue-over-harris-getting-bidens-campaign-funds-sure---but-it-likely-wont-work/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Forbes\uc2  that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cperfectly legal for [Harris] to use the campaign funds\u8221\'20\'1D and that the law was clear on the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two local law enforcement officers went to look for the shooter who targeted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his Pennsylvania rally before the assassination attempt, raising questions about whether a key post was left unattended.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports:\par \par \uc2 Two local law enforcement officers stationed in the complex of buildings where a gunman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-assassination-attempt-thomas-matthew-crooks-shooter-881581c46c07025898027143fc9132e5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened fire at former President Donald Trump}}}\uc2  left to go search for the man before the shooting, the head of \uc2 Pennsylvania State Police\uc2  said Tuesday, raising questions about whether a key post was left unattended as the shooter climbed onto a roof.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania State Police Col. Christopher Paris told a congressional committee that two Butler County Emergency Services Unit officers were stationed at a second-floor window in the complex of buildings that form AGR International Inc. They spotted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-rally-shooting-guns-fbi-motive-08e925cb85e52c5266878cd76e796ad2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks}}}\uc2  acting suspiciously on the ground and left their post to go look for him along with other law enforcement officers, he said.\par \par \uc2 Paris said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know whether officers would have been able to see Crooks climbing onto the roof of an adjacent building had they remained at the window. A video taken by a lawmaker who visited the shooting site on Monday shows a second-story window of the building had a clear view of the roof where Crooks opened fire; it was unclear if the video showed the window where the officers had been stationed.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Pennsylvania State Police\uc2  commissioner\u8217\'20\'19s testimony before the House Homeland Security Committee provides new insight into security preparations for the Trump rally in Butler, Pennsylvania on July 13, but raises further questions about law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s decisions before Crooks opened fire.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2  has also endorsed Harris.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet's be real: This election is the fight of our lives, for our lives. There's no better presidential candidate for such a time as this than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kamalaharris}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPact?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PPact}}}\uc2  trusts her to help us build a future where access to health care, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , isn't a privilege, but a right. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AvbkbT5Hsr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AvbkbT5Hsr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood Action (@PPact) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPact/status/1815861940524068995?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 This comes as no surprise \u8211\'20\'13 Harris has been an effective messenger on reproductive rights for the Biden campaign and was the first sitting vice-president to visit an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Other major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups have also endorsed the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biggest US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights groups back Kamala Harris as effective messenger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 A coalition of gun safety groups ha s endorsed Harris for president.\par \par \uc2 Gun safety advocacy groups including Brady and Team Enough, Community Justice Action Fund, Everytown for Gun Safety Action Fund and its grassroots networks Moms Demand Action and Students Demand Action, Giffords, Newtown Action Alliance and Jr Newtown Action Alliance are now backing Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has helped lead the strongest gun safety administration in American history and will continue to build upon that transformative progress as the first-ever Black and Asian American woman president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Angela Ferrell-Zabala, executive director of Moms Demand Action, said in a statement.. \u8220\'20\'1CThroughout her career in public service, vice president Harris has been a powerful force in the fight for our freedoms \u8212\'20\'14 including the freedom to live free from the threat of gun violence. Gun extremists have a dream ticket with Trump and Vance, and our volunteers stand ready to do everything in our power to elect vice president Harris back into the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is noteworthy that many the top contenders for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate also have significant, personal experience with gun violence. Arizona senator Mark Kelly, who has been asked to submit personal information in a vice-presidential vetting process, is married to \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , a prominent gun control activist who founded a namesake advocacy group after she survived an assassination attempt. Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , whose name has also been circulating as a possible vice-presidential candidate, lost a close friend in an April 2023 mass shooting in Louisville.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Spirits were sky-high at the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s first rally\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the presumptive Democratic presidential nominee}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a campaign stop at a suburban Milwaukee high school \u8211\'20\'13 spirits in the crowded auditorium were high.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh my God, I think this is something long overdue \u8211\'20\'13 and she will do great,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pat Bridges, a 65-year-old retiree who attended the event on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The timing and location of the rally, which drew enthusiastic Harris supporters from across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2 , was significant. Last week, thousands of Republicans from across the country descended on the Fiserv Forum, just eight miles away, for the Republican national convention, a week in which Republicans also appeared unified around their candidate, although they presented a vastly different vision for the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe needed to reinvigorate the ticket,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Beth Driscoll, who attended the event with a friend. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we have done that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The rally took on special significance for many in the crowd, given Harris\u8217\'20\'19s already historic position as a Black woman and a presumptive nominee for president from either party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeeing Kamala here \u8230\'20\'26 my granddaughter will know she can be whatever she wants, and do whatever she wants,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bridges, who is Black, and attended the rally with her young granddaughter.\par \par \uc2 Janette Braverman, who served as the first Black county supervisor from Ozaukee county, Wisconsin, before stepping down in 2022, said the excitement in the room was palpable \u8211\'20\'13 and stronger than past Biden events. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was time\u8221\'20\'1D for Harris to take over the Democratic presidential ticket, said Braverman. \u8220\'20\'1CI was concerned for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s health. And [Kamala] has been ready.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m extremely excited \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m thrilled,\u8221\'20\'1D said Phoebe Williams, an attorney who arrived early at the rally to find seating up close. \u8220\'20\'1CAs an African American lawyer, to see another woman African American lawyer ascend to the top is just thrilling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-election-rally-milwaukee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m extremely excited\u8217\'20\'19: Kamala Harris inspires Milwaukee rally-goers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2 , a Democratic party megadonor who had called for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step down from the presidential campaign, is backing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hastings has given $7m to a super Pac supporting Harris\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theinformation.com/articles/reed-hastings-backs-pro-kamala-harris-pac-with-7-million-donation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Information}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which he has said is his largest donation ever to a single candidate.\par \par \uc2 This month, Hastings was one of the first major Democratic donors to call for Biden to end his 2024 campaign, following the president\u8217\'20\'19s disastrous debate performance. Back then, he told the New York Times Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to step aside to allow a vigorous Democratic leader to beat Trump and keep us safe and prosperous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  begins her campaign for president, she is already facing many questions over the administration\u8217\'20\'19s continued support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Gaza have killed more than 39,000, according to the Gaza health ministry. Harris, who some perceive as more empathetic than Biden toward the plight of people in Gaza, will face mounting pressure to break with Biden in his policies toward Israel.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-israel-palestine-policy-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an opinion piece}}}\uc2  for the Guardian, Lily Greenberg Call, a former special assistant to the chief of staff at the Department of Interior, implored the vice-president to chart a new path:\par \par \uc2 I resigned because of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s disastrous policy on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , providing the financial and diplomatic support for the Israeli military to massacre, starve and forcibly expel countless Palestinians in Gaza. As a staffer in the administration, I heard reports that Harris and her staff pushed the US president to adopt a policy on Gaza that was both more humane and in alignment with international law, but were rebuffed. I saw the Harris \u8230\'20\'26 [become] the first senior administration official calling for a ceasefire, even as I was disappointed that it was only for six weeks. This was reportedly an effort by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team to water down her speech. It is shameful that Biden refused to listen to Harris \u8211\'20\'13 or the majority of Americans for that matter. Now that Biden has stepped aside, she has the opportunity to chart her own path on Israel and Palestine.\par \par \uc2 Harris will not attend Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s address to Congress, but is planning to meet with him privately at the White House, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the Capitol, hundreds of protestors led by Jewish Voice for Peace are demonstrating against US support for Israel among its ongoing bombardment of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 According to the organization, arrests are being made.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of protestors gathered today at the Capitol Hill Cannon Rotunda, to coincide with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to DC. He is scheduled to addresses a joint meeting of Congress on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican representative Andy Ogles of Tennessee has introduced articles of impeachment against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for high crimes and misdemeanors.\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP Rep. Andy Ogles (R-Tenn.) just introduced articles of impeachment against VP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for high crimes and misdemeanors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/M5xtvcR2M2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/M5xtvcR2M2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1815839150949687533?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The articles blame Harris for a crisis at the southern border, claiming that she had failed her duties as \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The deeply political effort is unlikely to get very far. Harris was never a \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s a misleading label that Republican critics applied to her. Harris was never put in charge of overseeing border or immigration policy. Rather, she was tasked with handling diplomatic efforts to address the root causes driving a surge of migration to the US \u8211\'20\'13namely, poverty and instability in central America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris hits out at Trump in Wisconsin, while polls give mixed verdict on voter support: a look back at today's news\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made the first public speech of her presidential campaign, promising {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ff91b8f082b7073589669#block-669ff91b8f082b7073589669"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to unite Democrats}}}\uc2  during a visit to the vital swing state of Wisconsin, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ffa0e8f0804734c48d7fc#block-669ffa0e8f0804734c48d7fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparing}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the sorts of criminals she used to prosecute in California. Earlier in the day, the two most powerful Democrats in Congress, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fe3e08f08b200a0085721#block-669fe3e08f08b200a0085721"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced their endorsements}}}\uc2  of the vice-president, underscoring the glide path Harris appears to be on to become the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 But for all the enthusiasm among Democrats, we still do not know if voters are on board. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fa1948f082b707358910d#block-669fa1948f082b707358910d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fa1948f082b707358910d#block-669fa1948f082b707358910d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new}}}\uc2  surveys indicate Harris is tied or slightly behind Trump among voters nationally, though one shows her with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ff2a48f08b200a00857a8#block-669ff2a48f08b200a00857a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a small lead}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, the Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fbeed8f08b200a0085411#block-669fbeed8f08b200a0085411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  following a widely criticized appearance before a congressional committee, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fc50b8f08b200a008548f#block-669fc50b8f08b200a008548f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden said}}}\uc2  he would appoint a replacement \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669ff4348f08b200a00857b7#block-669ff4348f08b200a00857b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will meet}}}\uc2  with the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , when he visits Washington DC, and the pair will also sit down with the families of American hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Harris will attend neither event.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8#block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will vote}}}\uc2  on setting up a bipartisan panel to investigate the Trump assassination attempt, its Republican and Democratic leaders said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden condemned an Ohio state senator who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2#block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Ca civil war to save the country\u8221\'20\'1D as he introduced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance yesterday. The state senator apologized.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the oversight committee, joined Republicans in approving of Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s decision to resign, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537#block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also saying}}}\uc2  the Trump rally shooting proves assault weapons must be banned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , the New Jersey senator convicted on charges related to accepting bribes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fec748f082b70735895f4#block-669fec748f082b70735895f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly}}}\uc2  resign his Senate seat in August.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a call with reporters aimed at hammering \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over border security and immigration, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s the same as Biden but much more radical. She\u8217\'20\'19s a radical left person and this country doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want a radical left person to destroy it. She\u8217\'20\'19s far more radical than he is. She wants open borders. She wants things that nobody wants. You take a look at the electric car mandate, everything.\par \par \uc2 The former president added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you should do is take a look at San Francisco now compared to before she became the district attorney, and you\u8217\'20\'19ll see what you\u8217\'20\'19ll do to our country. So I think she should be easier than Biden because he was slightly more mainstream, but not much.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he wants to debate Harris\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he wants to debate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  despite speculation that he was seeking a way out.\par \par \uc2 Trump had been due to face \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on 10 September but, after the president\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal, cast doubt on whether he would still take part.\par \par \uc2 In a press call with reporters on Tuesday, the former president was asked if he committed to at least one more debate. \u8220\'20\'1COh, yes, absolutely, I\u8217\'20\'19d want to,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s important. I\u8217\'20\'19m not thrilled about ABC because they\u8217\'20\'19re truly fake news.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI watched last night. They\u8217\'20\'19re actually trying to make a hero out of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  when he was the worst president in history and they were doing things like, with Kamala, like, what a wonderful thing it is that she is running.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump added: \u8220\'20\'1CShe is not the candidate that they should have. I know it. We all know it. So, I\u8217\'20\'19m not thrilled with ABC. I guess they commit but I have at least equal say and I don\u8217\'20\'19t like the idea of ABC. I would be willing to do more than one debate, actually.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 NextGen Pac, which is part of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest youth vote organisation, NextGen America, endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nextgenamerica.org/press/nations-largest-youth-vote-organization-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  posted on their website.\par \par \uc2 Throughout her time as Vice President, and during her time in Congress, Vice President Harris has demonstrated a commitment to fighting for the issues most important to young people. From protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and care, to supporting climate justice, economic justice, voting rights, and LGBTQ+ rights, Vice President Harris represents the diversity, vision, and values of young Americans.\par \par \uc2 Young people remain committed to turning out in force and defeating MAGA extremism and the existential threat of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025, and we are proud to join Vice President Harris in this fight. NextGen PAC is energized and ready to continue mobilizing young people for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , driving forward our shared vision for an America that stands for equality, opportunity, and justice for all.\par \par \uc2 Young people will help elect the first woman president, we will defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and we will ensure that the voices of young Americans remain at the forefront of our democracy. Together, we stand ready to make history.\par \par \uc2 According to their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nextgenamerica.org/elections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2 , NextGen Pac endorses candidates with \u8220\'20\'1Cproven progressive records who will fight for a better future for younger generations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In March, NextGen Pac, along with several other groups representing young people, announced their support for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-youth-activists-joint-endorsement-reelection-age-15ea5b67e05f2dc6c41ba7f48cfccdcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is 22 years younger than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who ultimately was pushed to end his re-election campaign after concerns among Democrats that he was too old to continue serving became insurmountable.\par \par \uc2 While it remains to be seen if Harris is any more popular with voters than Biden, her recent speeches have been far more coherent than the president\u8217\'20\'19s, who often struggled to forcefully communicate his message.\par \par \uc2 Just compare this moment from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s just-concluded speech in Milwaukee:\par \par \uc2 enltrVice Pres. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says she took on "predators," "fraudsters" and "cheaters" in her roles as California attorney general and a courtroom prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Harris then referenced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , calling out his "type." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i50BJzEzZL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/i50BJzEzZL}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CHgqLnEuug"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CHgqLnEuug}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1815823395017171336?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 To Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech last week to a convention of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  civil rights group in Las Vegas:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris tells rally: 'When we fight, we win'\par \par \uc2 Harris concluded by getting the room ready to put in the work necessary to help her win Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 and reiterating a message from when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was running, that this election is a choice between two different futures of the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, in this election, we each face a question: what kind of country do we want to live in?\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to your point, do we want to live in a country freedom, compassion and rule of law, or a country of chaos, fear and hate? And here\u8217\'20\'19s the beauty of this moment, we each have the power answer that question. The power is with the people. We each have the power to answer that question, and in the next 105 days, then we have work to do. We have doors to knock on, we have phone calls to make, we have voters to register, and we have an election to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris concluded by saying:\par \par \uc2 So, Wisconsin, today, I ask you, are you ready to get to work? Do we believe in freedom, do we believe in opportunity? Do we believe in the promise of America, and are we ready to fight for it, and when we fight, we win?\par \par \uc2 Amid roars of the crowd, the vice-president said: \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless you, God bless the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D and left the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris hits Trump over Project 2025 as crowd chants 'we are not going back'\par \par \uc2 Harris then shifted to bashing Trump over his ties to Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the blueprint for a remaking of the \uc2 US government\uc2  authored by rightwing groups that are staffed by people who worked in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration. Though the former president says that he has nothing to do with the plan, many of his policies line up with it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take our country backward. He and his extreme Project 2025 agenda will weaken the middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe got to take this seriously. And can you believe they put that thing in writing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRead it \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s 900 pages,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued:\par \par \uc2 But here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, when you read it, you will see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intends to cut Social Security and Medicare. He intends to give tax breaks to billionaires and big corporations and make working families foot the bill. They intend to end the Affordable Care Act and take us back then to a time when insurance companies had the power to deny people with pre-existing conditions. Remember what that was like, children with asthma, women who survived breast cancer, grandparents with diabetes. America has tried these failed economic policies before, and we are not going back.\par \par \uc2 At that, the crowd began chanting, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are not going back!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harking back to her time as prosecutor, Harris says, 'I know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's type'\par \par \uc2 With that out of the way, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  began launching verbal salvos at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , comparing him to the criminals and wrongdoers she used to meet in the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBefore I was elected vice-president, before I was elected United States senator, I was elected attorney general of the state of California, and I was a courtroom prosecutor before then,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd in those roles, I took on perpetrators of all kinds: predators who abused women, fraudsters who ripped off consumers, cheaters who broke the rules for their own gain. So hear me when I say, I know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s type.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd loved that line, and Harris kept at it:\par \par \uc2 And in this campaign, I promise you, I will proudly put my record against his any day of the week.\par \par \uc2 As attorney general of California, I took on one of our country\u8217\'20\'19s largest for-profit colleges that was scamming students. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ran a for-profit college that scammed students. As a prosecutor, I specialized in cases involving sexual abuse. Well, Trump was found liable for committing sexual abuse.\par \par \uc2 As attorney general of California, I took on the big Wall Street banks and held them accountable for fraud. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was just found guilty of fraud on 34 counts.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s also make no mistake, this campaign is not just about \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . This campaign is about who we fight for. This is about who we fight for.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls serving as vice-president under Biden 'one of the greatest honors of my life' and pledges to 'unite our party'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  then spoke glowingly of her service as his vice-president, while noting that even though she has the delegates necessary to win the Democratic nomination, she will focus on uniting the party around her candidacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has truly been one of the greatest honors of my life serve as vice-president to our president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe\u8217\'20\'19s legacy of accomplishment over his entire career and over the past three and a half years is unmatched in modern history in one term. Think about it, in one term as president, he has already surpassed the legacy of most presidents who served two terms in office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then acknowledged that she was on the path to becoming the Democratic standard bearer, but still has work to do:\par \par \uc2 It is my great honor to have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement in this race.\par \par \uc2 So, Wisconsin, I am told as of this morning that we have earned the support of enough delegates to secure the Democratic nomination.\par \par \uc2 And I am so very honored, and I pledge to you, I will spend the coming weeks continuing to unite our party, so that we are ready to win in November. So, friends, we have 105 days until election day. In that time, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got some work to do, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not afraid of hard work. We like hard work, don\u8217\'20\'19t we? And we will win this election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris kicked off her remarks by reminding everyone that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe path to the White House goes to Wisconsin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In close elections \u8211\'20\'13 which may well be how November plays out \u8211\'20\'13 Wisconsin has acted as the \u8220\'20\'1Ctipping point\u8221\'20\'1D state, giving the victor the electoral votes they need to win outright.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also very closely divided between Democrats and Republicans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in Milwaukee, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just taken the stage.\par \par \uc2 The crowd is cheering continuously, and chanting what sounds like \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is a far less controversial figure among Republicans, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just announced that he will be meeting the Israeli prime minister at his south Florida resort:\par \par \uc2 Looking forward to welcoming \uc2 Bibi Netanyahu\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago in Palm Beach, Florida. During my first term, we had Peace and Stability in the Region, even signing the historic Abraham Accords - And we will have it again. Just as I have said in discussions with President Zelensky and other World Leaders in recent weeks, my PEACE THROUGH STRENGTH Agenda will demonstrate to the World that these horrible, deadly Wars, and violent Conflicts must end. Millions are dying, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in no way capable of stopping it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Netanyahu to meet families of American hostages taken by \uc2 Hamas\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  on Thursday, and the two leaders will then talk with the families of Americans taken hostage by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  during the 7 October attack.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet Netanyahu during his visit. She is scheduled to speak at the convention of a historically Black sorority in Indianapolis on Thursday, and will not preside over the chamber when Netanyahu addresses Congress on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Biden, meanwhile, has just made his first public appearance since bowing out of the presidential race. He is heading back to Washington DC, after recovering from Covid-19 in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware:\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu is deeply controversial among some Democrats over his handling of war in Gaza, and his visit to Washington DC poses a test for Harris, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/as-netanyahu-arrives-in-washington-kamala-harris-treads-a-careful-path-on-israel-and-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Netanyahu arrives in Washington, Kamala Harris treads a careful path on Israel and Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 New poll shows Harris with small lead over Trump\par \par \uc2 Another poll of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support has been released, with this one showing the vice-president with a slight lead over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/harris-closes-nomination-with-delegates-secured-campaign-wisconsin-2024-07-23/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Reuters/Ipsos survey}}}\uc2  conducted on Monday and Tuesday \u8211\'20\'13 following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s departure from the race \u8211\'20\'13 showed her with 44% support nationally, above Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 42%.\par \par \uc2 A previous survey taken before Biden suspended his campaign showed Harris tied with Trump at 44% support, which was within the poll\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to deliver first campaign speech in swing state Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has made it to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, where she is minutes away from delivering the first speech of her just-launched presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 She is being introduced by \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , Democratic governor of the state that is seen as vital to her chances of winning the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is ready to lead from day one,\u8221\'20\'1D Evers said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s already proven herself to be a tenacious leader, district attorney, attorney general and US senator. And, as our vice-president, Kamala has vigorously defended our democracy, fought hard, very hard, to protect our freedoms that we hold dear and work tirelessly to do the right thing, and deliver for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Priorities USA, one of the largest liberal Super Pacs, said \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is already running stronger than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with core constituencies, putting Democrats in an \u8220\'20\'1Cimproved position\u8221\'20\'1D to win the White House.\par \par \uc2 Before Biden bowed out of the race, the Democrats were trailing their 2020 support levels with Black voters by eight points and Latino voters by nine points.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose deficits are [now] half of what they were last week,\u8221\'20\'1D Nick Ahamed, deputy executive director of Priorities USA, told reporters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 There are also signs Harris is energzing young voters, who have reported unusually high levels of disillusionment with the election. Following Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Harris, Priorities said the group recorded a notable uptick in the share of young people who said they intended to vote in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a close, hard-fought election,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat continues to be true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the Democrats path has not changed and continues to run through the five battleground states of Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania, Arizona and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s strongest issue over Trump is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Trump holds an advantage over her on inflation and immigration \u8211\'20\'13 though she outperforms Biden on both of those issues.\par \par \uc2 Ahamed said the voters Democrats need to reach are disproportionately on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and streaming services, not TikTok, despite the outsized attention the app receives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that elections are won and lost online, and that the work that needs to be done to consolidate the base behind Vice-President Harris has to be done online,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/melindagates/status/1815729879381373009"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  posted on X, Melinda French Gates endorsed the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , for president in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 We need a leader who will stand up for reproductive freedom. A leader who understands that supporting caregivers leads to healthier families and a stronger economy. A leader who knows that when women have their full power in society, we all thrive.\par \par \uc2 I am supporting Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  because she is that leader.\par \par \uc2 enltrThere is so much riding on the election in November. We need a leader who will stand up for reproductive freedom. A leader who understands that supporting caregivers leads to healthier families and a stronger economy. A leader who knows that when women have their full power in\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Melinda French Gates (@melindagates) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/melindagates/status/1815729879381373009?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The endorsement comes as French Gates announced earlier this year that she would be donating $1bn over the next two years to individuals and organizations working on behalf of women and families globally, including on reproductive rights in the US, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/melinda-french-gates-donation-reproductive-women-rights-ab3512903cac247960d1fe03eabaeb89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 After weeks of infighting and mounting calls for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to withdraw from the presidential race, Democratic leaders seemed visibly relieved to move forward with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the presumptive nominee.\par \par \uc2 At the press conference today, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , sounded jubilant as he and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , endorsed Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, following in the steps of many other congressional Democrats who have already done the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are moving forward stronger and more united than ever before,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said.\par \par \uc2 In just the last 36 hours, I have seen a surge of enthusiasm from every corner of our party uniting behind Vice-President Harris.\par \par \uc2 Schumer said he intended to meet with Harris \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D, but he deflected a question about whether he had directly asked Biden to drop out of the race.\par \par \uc2 Reports indicated that Schumer had traveled to Delaware to meet with Biden and share some alarming polling about Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 odds of taking full control of Congress with the president at the top of the ticket. Schumer said:\par \par \uc2 What I would say is that the president has done an amazing, amazing job as president, one of the best we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had. And he put his country first and made the right decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign Senate seat \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  will resign effective 20 August, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator for New Jersey was convicted earlier this month on 16 charges, including accepting bribes of cash, gold and a luxury car from three New Jersey businessmen, and acting as an overseas agent for Egypt.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US senator Bob Menendez found guilty on all counts in corruption trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommonsense leader\u8221\'20\'1D who knows how to deliver real results for hardworking American taxpayers, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the House minority leader, said.\par \par \uc2 Jeffries described Harris as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccourageous\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccompassionate\u8221\'20\'1D leader who has worked hard throughout her entire career to keep communities safe, and who will build an affordable economy that makes life better for everyday Americans.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will fight for our freedom. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will fight for our families. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will fight for our future.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , at the joint press conference with \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will go down in US history as \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most consequential presidents of all time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jeffries said Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Cheroic American\u8221\'20\'1D because he made the \u8220\'20\'1Cselfless\u8221\'20\'1D decision to pass the torch to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who he says has \u8220\'20\'1Cexcited and energized\u8221\'20\'1D the House Democratic caucus, the Democratic party and the nation.\par \par \uc2 Harris has earned the nomination \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the grassroots up, not the top down\u8221\'20\'1D, Jeffries said.\par \par \uc2 She is ready. She is willing. She is able to energetically and emphatically lead America into the future.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden tests negative for Covid, says physician\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has tested negative for Covid-19 and his symptoms have \u8220\'20\'1Cresolved\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House physician Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said.\par \par \uc2 A letter shared by the White House reads:\par \par \uc2 The President\u8217\'20\'19s symptoms have resolved. Over the course of his infection, he never manifested a fever, and his vital signs remained normal, to include pulse oximetry. His lungs remained clear.\par \par \uc2 The president \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinues to perform all of his presidential duties\u8221\'20\'1D and will \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to be monitored for any recurrence of illness\u8221\'20\'1D, his physician said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the House minority leader, seconded Chuck Schume r\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to strongly endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to be the 47th President of the United States of America. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna hold the Senate, we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win the House, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrJeffries steps up and seconds Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI'm proud to strongly endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to be the 47th President of the United States of America. We're gonna hold the Senate, we're gonna win the House, we're going to elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pYgaWuL1KM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pYgaWuL1KM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1815797716154204353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , paid tribute to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who he said had \u8220\'20\'1Cshowed the world what a great man he is, his true patriotism, his profound sense of decency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cselfless\u8221\'20\'1D decision not to seek the Democratic presidential nomination \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not an easy decision\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer says, but it \u8220\'20\'1Cput our country, our party and our future first\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At his core, he is an honorable man, a family man, a man of deep faith. We love him. We truly do.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are moving forward \u8220\'20\'1Cstronger and more united than ever before\u8221\'20\'1D, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , tells reporters as he endorses \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Schumer says he has seen a \u8220\'20\'1Csurge of enthusiasm from every corner of our party\u8221\'20\'1D in the last 36 hours, and that that enthusiasm is \u8220\'20\'1Ccontagious\u8221\'20\'1D among Democrats, with contributions pouring in \u8220\'20\'1Cin ways even beyond our expectations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris has a \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous\u8221\'20\'1D record to run on, Schumer says, as he notes that \u8220\'20\'1Cnow begins the next chapter in our quest to make sure \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not become president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today, with one voice, we speak about the dangers he presents to working families, to our country and to our democracy. We see very clearly how nervous the Republicans are about our new nominee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top congressional Democrats endorse Harris\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, has begun speaking at the joint press conference with the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party and the country are \u8220\'20\'1Cbrimming with excitement, enthusiasm, unity\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer says.\par \par \uc2 He says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has done a \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly impressive job\u8221\'20\'1D securing the majority of delegates needed to win the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, and that the vast majority of his senators \u8220\'20\'1Cquickly and enthusiastically\u8221\'20\'1D endorsed her.\par \par \uc2 We are here today to throw our support behind Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer endorses Harris and seems truly giddy about Dems\u8217\'20\'19 new circumstances.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow that the process has played out, from the grassroots bottom up, we are here today to throw our support behind vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aXzxSvXc4Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aXzxSvXc4Z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1815796944909873200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , praised \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday in Washington, describing the vice-president as a \u8220\'20\'1Cleading voice for American foreign policy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What I\u8217\'20\'19ve observed is someone who asks, time and again, the penetrating questions, who cuts to the chase, and is intensely focused on the interests of the American people.\par \par \uc2 My observation is she\u8217\'20\'19s a very strong, very effective and deeply respected voice for our country around the world. When she speaks, she speaks on behalf of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Blinken also stated that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who endorsed Harris as the Democratic nominee for president over the weekend, remained engaged on issues such as the wars in Gaza and Ukraine, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-07-23/blinken-vouches-for-harris-as-leading-voice-on-foreign-policy?embedded-checkout=true&leadSource=uverify%20wall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reporters are backed to the gills here at the Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters ahead of \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 remarks.\par \par \uc2 Despite the last-minute alert about the press conference, reporters rushed from Capitol Hill to the DSCC to cover the expected endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , which would be crucial in helping her consolidate congressional supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer and Jeffries expected to endorse Harris in press conference\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m here at the Washington headquarters of the Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee, where the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , are scheduled to speak in just a few minutes.\par \par \uc2 Schumer and Jeffries are expected to endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after the vice-president earned the support of enough delegates to become the presumptive Democratic nominee.\par \par \uc2 A number of congressional Democrats have already endorsed Harris.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  will soon address reporters here at the DSCC headquarters, with an endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  expected. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/65zIVz9VCU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/65zIVz9VCU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1815791528570191995?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two Democratic state governors, Josh Shapiro of Pennsylvania and Roy Cooper of North Carolina, and the Arizona senator Mark Kelly have emerged as early favourites to be \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate after being asked to submit personal information in a vice-presidential vetting process.\par \par \uc2 The trio are understood to be among 10 Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 nearly all of them elected officials \u8211\'20\'13 identified by a vetting team led by the former attorney general \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 . Holder\u8217\'20\'19s law firm, \uc2 Covington & Burling LLP\uc2 , has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/joe-biden-election-drop-out-07-22-24#h_bc6b0de22ce63dd90a6217695563ec48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  with the responsibility of scrutinising the personal finances, public statements and family histories of likely candidates.\par \par \uc2 Shapiro, Cooper and Kelly have endorsed Harris to replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the presidential nominee in November.\par \par \uc2 The vetting process, which normally takes months, will be accelerated to conclude before the start of the Democratic national convention, which opens in Chicago on 19 August.\par \par \uc2 While Shapiro, Cooper and Kelly are the only three to be publicly identified, speculation has also surrounded several others, including \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the governor of Kentucky, and the Michigan governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  reportedly not interest in vice-presidential post\par \par \uc2 The California governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the Democratic nominee, is reportedly not interested in being Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom his perspective, he has the best job in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s adviser Nathan Click told NBC News, adding:\par \par \uc2 He looks forward to supporting VP Harris and whomever she picks as her running mate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Deputy Secret Service director appointed acting director after Cheatle resignation\par \par \uc2 The deputy director of the Secret Service, Ronald Rowe, has been appointed to serve as acting director of the agency after Kimberly Cheatle \u8217\'20\'19s resignation earlier today.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the homeland security secretary, Alejandro Mayorkas, reads:\par \par \uc2 A 24-year veteran of the Secret Service, [Rowe] previously served as the agency\u8217\'20\'19s Assistant Director for the Office of Intergovernmental and Legislative Affairs, Deputy Assistant Director for the Office of Protective Operations, and in other leadership positions.\par \par \uc2 I appreciate his willingness to lead the Secret Service at this incredibly challenging moment, as the agency works to get to the bottom of exactly what happened on July 13 and cooperate with ongoing investigations and Congressional oversight.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s resignation on Tuesday came a day after a contentious House hearing in the wake of the assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a Pennsylvania rally.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle, who had served as Secret Service director since August 2022, had called the attempt on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmost significant operational failure\u8221\'20\'1D in decades.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has dismissed claims that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is unfit to continue as president and that he should resign from office.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance1/status/1814657912762966064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on Saturday that Biden should \u8220\'20\'1Cresign now\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cif you can\u8217\'20\'19t run, you can\u8217\'20\'19t serve\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, said Vance\u8217\'20\'19s claim was \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D and that Biden was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to continue to lead this country\u8221\'20\'1D. Speaking on The View, she said:\par \par \uc2 The president decided to not run for re-election. That\u8217\'20\'19s it. That\u8217\'20\'19s all he decided on. He wants to continue to do the work \u8211\'20\'13 three and a half years of unprecedented, historic work.\par \par \uc2 enltrKarine Jean-Pierre dismisses claims that President Biden is not fit to finish his term:\par \par \uc2 "I think that's ridiculous.... The president decided to not run for reelection. That's it.... He wants to continue to do the work, three and a half years of unprecedented, historic work." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KDkeseK8Xu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KDkeseK8Xu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1815782303215559053?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  continues to consolidate the support of Democrats, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fd53c8f082b7073589438#block-669fd53c8f082b7073589438"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly soon}}}\uc2  gain the endorsements of two of the biggest names out there: the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 . They have a joint press conference scheduled for 1pm, where they are said to plan to announce their backing of the vice-president, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fad098f08b200a008532b#block-669fad098f08b200a008532b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday gained}}}\uc2  the delegates necessary to win the Democratic nomination. But for all the enthusiasm among Democratic leaders in Washington DC for Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fa1948f082b707358910d#block-669fa1948f082b707358910d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fb96d8f0804734c48d41a#block-669fb96d8f0804734c48d41a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicate}}}\uc2  voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t on board quite yet. Two new surveys indicate Harris is tied or slightly behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  among voters nationally \u8211\'20\'13 though it is a closer race than it was with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Meanwhile, the Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fbeed8f08b200a0085411#block-669fbeed8f08b200a0085411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  following a widely criticized appearance before a congressional committee, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fc50b8f08b200a008548f#block-669fc50b8f08b200a008548f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden said}}}\uc2  he would appoint a replacement \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8#block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will vote}}}\uc2  on setting up a bipartisan panel to investigate the Trump assassination attempt, its Republican and Democratic leaders said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden condemned an Ohio state senator who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2#block-669fb4cb8f0804734c48d3e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Ca civil war to save the country\u8221\'20\'1D as he introduced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance yesterday. The state senator apologized.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2 , the top Democrat on the oversight committee, joined Republicans in approving of Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s decision to resign, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537#block-669fcde48f08b200a0085537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also saying}}}\uc2  the Trump rally shooting proves assault weapons must be banned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top congressional Democrats to endorse Harris \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and his counterpart in the House, the minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , will endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a press conference at 1pm, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 While many Democratic lawmakers have jumped on board with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s bid for the presidency following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to step down, Schumer and Jeffries have yet to do so. Three people familiar with their plans say they will make the announcement at a rare joint appearance at the headquarters of the Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee in Washington DC this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats are meanwhile digesting the historic upheaval on the presidential ticket, after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended his re-election campaign and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  swiftly took his place.\par \par \uc2 The decision has left in an awkward spot lawmakers who stridently defended Biden, even after his disastrous performance at his debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last month. Among that group is the senator Chris Coons of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s home state Delaware, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/coons-biden-only-democrat-beat-donald-trump/story?id=111546115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC}}}\uc2  Biden was the \u8220\'20\'1Conly\u8221\'20\'1D Democrat able to beat Trump.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN today, Coons walked back that comment, and announced his support for Harris: \u8220\'20\'1CI would welcome a chance to revise and extend those remarks, because underlying that was my confidence that the record that President Biden and Vice-President Harris have built over the last three and a half years is the strongest legislative record of any first-term presidency in my lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was right beside \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  every step of the way as they strengthened \uc2 Nato\uc2 , as they came up with creative and powerful combinations of allies and partners in the Indo-Pacific, as they got to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk legislative accomplishments that reduce the price of prescription drugs, that invested in the fight against climate change, that made our communities safer with strong gun safety legislation.\par \par \uc2 I will say that on every one of those core points, Vice-President Harris will continue, will get the job done, and, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former president, will roll it back.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  is the top Democrat on the House oversight committee, and yesterday joined the Republican committee chair, James Comer \u8211\'20\'13 with whom he seldom agrees \u8211\'20\'13 in calling for Kimberly Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s resignation as director of the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 But Raskin also said the shooting at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, underscored the continued danger of assault weapons in America, and called on Congress to pass legislation banning them. In a statement after Cheatle stepped down from her role, Raskin reiterated that position. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Oversight Committee hearing identified two urgent priorities in the wake of the assassination attempt against former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the accompanying mass shooting. The first was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://u7061146.ct.sendgrid.net/ls/click?upn=u001.gqh-2BaxUzlo7XKIuSly0rC3SD4DPl7a5QlanFGwoemYeF3Jw8XArHRf1f-2BSjhRStW-2BPVKI7nJ8YEFLaa2vrP15A-3D-3DNgaY_2vVTU89-2BLk8eODpi7HZ9XCoPg0v2igGqKITls1TmU6RzH7n5APmpo-2BgB1OYHVtEwaDniEnFDX3yq-2BVgcuZuHBTDeGb-2BQX-2B7InABpPcHt254e4Bw0BV1HjENIwK64XiOBbzDOusfADUTusKSSEwveA2Mz6afVdz5JwV0IXoP1mFfbTGFrRRXYxOfkHpeaHUr4K5ixeXo8LsM1TiNCB0toLIhMaenQhkrw9HB3zj96o0iglNK1w7ymUtm5gWOAyXDfQA0K19Aq65-2BpPslxRXkwRXflahjk2yEmIgqetMzLt6Dn4a-2BqmGH1gNWqPSctWXhg38wWqrnjYG5mY-2F-2FRyPSoZJlTZGCFPRdK25AEnYLdRqI-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 need for Director Cheatle to step down}}}\uc2  and give new leadership at the Secret Service the opportunity to swiftly address this crisis, rebuild the trust of Congress and the American people, and guarantee security to protectees. We accomplished that today.\par \par \uc2 The other urgent need was to ban assault weapons to protect the rest of us from mass shootings like the one that took place in Butler. As I made clear during yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, a weapon that can be used to commit a mass shooting at an event under the full protection of the Secret Service and state and local police is a danger to schoolchildren, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  shoppers and congregants in church, synagogue and mosque services. As a weapon of war, the AR-15 has no legitimate place in our society. Congress must act now.\par \par \uc2 Pete Aguilar, the House Democratic caucus chair, agreed that Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s departure was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right decision\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to address nation from Oval Office on Wednesday evening\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will make his first speech since ending his bid for re-election from the Oval Office on Wednesday evening, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The speech, scheduled for 8pm ET, will detail \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat lies ahead, and how I will finish the job for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D, the president said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to return to the White House today from Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, where he has been recovering after coming down with Covid-19 last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson says Secret Service director's resignation 'overdue'\par \par \uc2 In reaction to Secret Service director Kimberly Cheatle \u8217\'20\'19s resignation, the Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, said it was overdue, and promised to continue investigating the security failures that allowed the assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrDirector Cheatle answered our calls to resign. Good. \u176\'00\'B0\u176\'00\'B0Now our task force will quickly and thoroughly investigate the assassination attempt on President Trump and hold those responsible accountable. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s1tAVm35DQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/s1tAVm35DQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Mike Johnson (@SpeakerJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1815766738643845591?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says he will appoint new Secret Service director 'soon'\par \par \uc2 In a brief statement, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  thanked Kimberly Cheatle for her tenure as director of the Secret Service, and said he would soon appoint her replacement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJill and I are grateful to Director Kim Cheatle for her decades of public service. She has selflessly dedicated and risked her life to protect our nation throughout her career in the \uc2 United States Secret Service\uc2 . We especially thank her for answering the call to lead the Secret Service during our Administration and we are grateful for her service to our family,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 As a leader, it takes honor, courage, and incredible integrity to take full responsibility for an organization tasked with one of the most challenging jobs in public service.\par \par \uc2 The independent review to get to the bottom of what happened on July 13 continues, and I look forward to assessing its conclusions. We all know what happened that day can never happen again. As we move forward, I wish Kim all the best, and I will plan to appoint a new Director soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 James Comer, the Republican chair of the House oversight committee, said the Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, \u8220\'20\'1Cinstilled no confidence\u8221\'20\'1D when she appeared before his committee yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Oversight Committee\u8217\'20\'19s hearing resulted in Director Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s resignation and there will be more accountability to come. The Secret Service has a no-fail mission yet it failed historically on Director Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s watch. At yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Oversight Committee hearing, Director Cheatle instilled no confidence that she has the ability to ensure the Secret Service can meet its protective mission,\u8221\'20\'1D Comer said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEgregious security failures leading up to and at the Butler, Pennsylvania campaign rally resulted in the assassination attempt of President Trump, the murder of an innocent victim, and harm to others in the crowd. While Director Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s resignation is a step toward accountability, we need a full review of how these security failures happened so that we can prevent them going forward. We will continue our oversight of the Secret Service in support of the House Task Force to deliver transparency, accountability, and solutions to ensure this never happens again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That last sentence is a reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8#block-669f9d918f0804734c48d2c8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bipartisan taskforce}}}\uc2  the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, and the Democratic minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , have proposed creating to investigate the assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 As news broke that the Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, had resigned amid criticism of her handling of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s security, the former president wrote this, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112836289155893843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Biden/Harris Administration did not properly protect me, and I was forced to take a bullet for Democracy. IT WAS MY GREAT HONOR TO DO SO!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service director resigns amid criticism of Trump security handling\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, has resigned, the Associated Press reports, following a bipartisan furor over whether her agency had adequately protected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the lead-up to the assassination attempt against him.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle stepped down one day after making a disastrous appearance before the House oversight committee, where lawmakers from both parties signaled frustration with her inability to answer many questions about the shooting that wounded Trump, killed an attender at his rally in Butler, Pennsylvania and wounded two others.\par \par \uc2 At the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s conclusion, the committee\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat joined with its Republican chair to ask for Cheatle\u8217\'20\'19s resignation:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/secret-service-director-kimberly-cheatle-hearing-trump-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service chief berated in House hearing after Trump rally shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN data analyst Harry Enten comes to a similar conclusion about the state of the presidential race, as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  takes over the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  remains a strong candidate because his favorability is notably high, he says. However, a significant share of voters have no opinion of Harris yet \u8211\'20\'13 potentially an opportunity for her to grow her support:\par \par \uc2 enltrBeating Trump won't be easy. His favorable rating is higher now than it has ever been (per two polls taken over the weekend).\par \par \uc2 Harris may poll better than Biden did against Trump, but Trump is running 5 points ahead nationally against her than he finished against Biden in 2020. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cnOtUKtWXe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cnOtUKtWXe}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 (((Harry Enten))) (@ForecasterEnten) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ForecasterEnten/status/1815743289280036995?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Harris enters the fray with numbers similar to President Biden', new poll finds\par \par \uc2 Another poll taken partly after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  suspended his re-election campaign has found a tied race between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  reports 49% of registered voters nationally support Trump and 47% back Harris \u8211\'20\'13 basically a tie, since the finding is within the margin of error. The poll was conducted from Friday of last week through Sunday.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  polling analyst Tim Malloy puts it:\par \par \uc2 The dramatic reset at the top of the Democratic ticket does little to move the race as vice-president Harris enters the fray with numbers similar to president Biden.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the poll\u8217\'20\'19s biggest finding is that independents prefer Trump overall. He has 55% support from the critical group, compared to 41% for Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns political violence after Ohio state senator's 'civil war' comment\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has once again condemned political violence after an Ohio state senator warned of \u8220\'20\'1Ca civil war to save the country\u8221\'20\'1D as he spoke ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, at a rally yesterday:\par \par \uc2 enltrFolks, calls to violence threaten our democracy\u8217\'20\'19s foundation.\par \par \uc2 You can\u8217\'20\'19t love your country only when you win.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s solve our problems with ballots and elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  as the next President of the United States of America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wfREMvAyNo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wfREMvAyNo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1815735148970717672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The senator, George Lang, has since apologized for his remarks:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement below on comments made earlier today: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/44UziIPjSa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/44UziIPjSa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 State Senator George Lang (@LangForOhio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LangForOhio/status/1815464944466620767?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is today heading to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, the largest city in a swing state that has played a pivotal role in handing both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  the presidency.\par \par \uc2 It also hosted the Republican national convention last week, during which Trump once again accepted the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for president, and debuted Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 According to the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s schedule, she will depart Washington DC at 10.40am ET, and hold her event in Milwaukee at 2.05pm \u8211\'20\'13 which we plan to cover live.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19ll return to the capital later in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today is merely the second full day of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, but she already has the delegates necessary to clinch the Democratic nomination, and has raised tens of millions of dollars. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports, the task before her now is to reintroduce herself to the voters who will decide the election:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  enters the second full day of her campaign for the Democratic presidential nomination on Tuesday in an almost unassailable position, following a whirlwind 24 hours that saw almost every senior party figure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-democratic-delegates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 championing her candidacy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rapid pace at which the vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/harris-presidential-election-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racked up endorsements}}}\uc2  was matched by an avalanche of donations to the newly branded Harris for President campaign, which had already inherited \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $96m when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abandoned his re-election}}}\uc2  effort on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 More than $81m poured into campaign coffers in its first day, a spokesperson said on Monday, calling it the largest single-day haul of any presidential candidate in history and with most of the money coming from grassroots donors making their first contributions of the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Campaign officials, however, were equally as enthused by the succession of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-endorsements-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavyweight Democrats}}}\uc2  who voiced their support for Harris, notably \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former speaker who called the vice-president \u8220\'20\'1Cbrilliantly astute\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crooted in strong values, faith and a commitment to public service\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris races towards 2024 nomination after whirlwind start}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The election gurus at the University of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Politics have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/post-biden-harris-the-delegates-the-map-the-vp-and-more/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a similar take}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effect on the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 They had previously forecast a very tough road for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  seeking re-election, with Nevada, Arizona, Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania as toss-ups, and Minnesota and New Hampshire \u8211\'20\'13 two states where Biden and other Democrats have triumphed in recent elections \u8211\'20\'13 as merely leaning Democratic.\par \par \uc2 They don\u8217\'20\'19t forecast any major changes to that dynamic with Harris now set to be on ballots in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s place, but note she has the opportunity to re-engage with Democratic voters in a way the president could not:\par \par \uc2 The new race probably does not start as a 50-50 proposition \u8211\'20\'13 Trump remains favored to a small but hardly overwhelming degree, and there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of uncertainty (and no useful recent historical precedent) for the presidential race changing in such a dramatic way this late in the political calendar. We had become very skeptical of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to pull this race back into true Toss-up status; Harris likely has a better chance to do so, though she\u8217\'20\'19s not guaranteed to.\par \par \uc2 The argument for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s upside is that she helps restore lagging Democratic enthusiasm and gives voters a new option in a race where many have long desired one, and we completely understand why so many Democrats urged Biden to step aside. Democrats seem thrilled and invigorated by having a more active candidate. But there are of course unknowns and obstacles too.\par \par \uc2 One of those is the possibility that Harris will be seen as too liberal by voters, and Trump more moderate \u8211\'20\'13 despite his policies lining up quite closely with the rightwing Project 2025:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is Project 2025 and what is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll shows Harris performing better than Biden against Trump \u8211\'20\'13 but Republican still has the edge\par \par \uc2 Morning Consult{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/analysis/kamala-harris-biden-campaign-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is out}}}\uc2  with one of the first polls taken since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended his re-election bid, and shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with more support in her matchup against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than the president had.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nonetheless has the edge, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a smaller one than when Biden was on the ballot. In its survey taken following Biden\u8217\'20\'19s exit from the race, \uc2 Morning Consult\uc2  found that Trump has 47% support to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 45%, a gap of only two percentage points. Biden trailed Trump by six percentage points in an earlier poll.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign appears to have given Democrats a spark of enthusiasm, with 27% saying they are \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch more motivated\u8221\'20\'1D to participate in the political process, compared to 24% for Republicans. The three-percentage point gap between the two parties is comparable to the gap in the 2020 election, \uc2 Morning Consult\uc2  notes.\par \par \uc2 And for those wondering if Harris is the best candidate Democrats can pick, the polls found she performs best against Trump of the 10 candidate surveyed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans, Democrats set up taskforce to investigate Trump assassination\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives is creating a bipartisan taskforce to investigate the attempted assassination of Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 The taskforce will be composed of seven Republicans and six Democrats, and investigate what went wrong at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, how to prevent it from happening again, and \u8220\'20\'1Cto ensure accountability\u8221\'20\'1D, the Republican House speaker, Mike Johnson, and the Democratic minority leader, Hakeem Jeffries, said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe security failures that allowed an assassination attempt on Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life are shocking. In response to bipartisan demands for answers, we are announcing a House Task Force made up of seven Republicans and six Democrats to thoroughly investigate the matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson and Jeffries said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe task force will be empowered with subpoena authority and will move quickly to find the facts, ensure accountability, and make certain such failures never happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House will vote on creating the taskforce later this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Newt Gingrich, a former House speaker, has called Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s reported decision to skip Benjamin Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s address to Congress on Wednesday a \u8220\'20\'1Csign of the pro-Hamas, pro-terrorist bias\u8221\'20\'1D of the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 Harris was already scheduled to attend an event for the Zeta Phi Beta sorority in Indianapolis before the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s address date was set, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/07/22/harris-plans-meeting-netanyahu-00170493"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, Gingrich wrote:\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris refusing to meet with President Netanyahu is a clear sign of the pro-Hamas, pro-terrorist bias which increasingly permeates the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 I watched speakers attack anti-semitism and speakers supporting Israel in the Republican Convention. Both would have caused a huge fight at the Democratic Convention. VP Harris will increasingly show her true colors as a San Francisco radical.\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President Harris refusing to meet with President Netanyahu is a clear sign of the pro-Hamas, pro-terrorist bias which increasingly permeates the Democratic Party. I watched speakers attack anti-semitism and speakers supporting Israel in the Republican Convention. Both would\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Newt Gingrich (@newtgingrich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/newtgingrich/status/1815494488489701416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris is to meet Netanyahu this week separate from the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Joe Biden (see post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f92c98f082b7073589012#block-669f92c98f082b7073589012"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12.28}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 A Harris aide said she will stress to Netanyahu that it is time for the Gaza conflict to end in a way where \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael is secure, all hostages are released, the suffering of Palestinian civilians in Gaza ends, and the Palestinian people can enjoy their right to dignity, freedom, and self-determination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden and Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu are expected to meet on Thursday, a US official has told the Associated Press. Kamala Harris will meet with Netanyahu separately. It remains uncertain if he will meet with Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to focus on working out what it will take to secure a hostage-release and ceasefire deal in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 The US president reportedly called in to a meeting of campaign staffers on Monday, telling them, \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re on the verge\u8221\'20\'1D of ending the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu told his Cabinet last month that there had been a \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatic drop\u8221\'20\'1D in US weapons deliveries for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza, underling a strain in the relationship with Washington.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the Biden administration said it would resume shipping 500-pound bombs to Israel, despite mounting calls by Democratic lawmakers and progressive groups to limit weapons supplies. It said it would continue to hold back on supplying 2,000-pound bombs over concerns about their use in densely populated Gaza.\par \par \uc2 However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org.uk/press-releases/usa-israel-has-used-us-made-arms-gaza-violation-international-law-new-report#:~:text=*US%2Dmade%20%E2%80%9Cjoint%20direct,14%20women%20and%20ten%20men."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amnesty International USA has said}}}\uc2  that US-supplied weapons provided to Israel have already been used in serious violations of international humanitarian and human rights law, and in a manner that is inconsistent with US law and policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign has surged in the 24 hours since announcing her candidacy, with 28,000 volunteers signing up to help with organisational efforts, the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has said.\par \par \uc2 Democratic National Committee chairman Jaime Harrison has vowed that the party would deliver a presidential nominee by 7 August. A virtual nominating process before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/democratic-delegates-biden-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national convention in Chicago}}}\uc2 , beginning on 19 August, is still needed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Oliver Milman is an environment reporter for Guardian US\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  has a strong record on the environment that will provide a vivid contrast with Donald Trump, who has vowed to rescind climate change policies should he return to the White House, according to green advocates who have welcomed the prospect of a Harris presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are confident that she is ready to carry forward President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s historic legacy and set a new high bar for climate ambition in America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lena Moffitt, executive director of Evergreen, one of a raft of green groups, including Sierra Club, League of Conservation Voters Action Fund, the NRDC Action Fund, and Climate Power, that has now endorsed the leading contender for the Democratic nomination.\par \par \uc2 Harris, as vice-president, cast the tie-breaking vote to pass Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s landmark legislation, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/biden-climate-bill-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2 , which unleashes hundreds of billions of dollars into building clean energy and electric car capacity. Biden, in his Sunday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/read-joe-biden-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  confirming he will drop his bid to be re-elected president, called the bill \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant climate legislation in the history of the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris could set \u8216\'20\'18new high bar for climate ambition\u8217\'20\'19, advocates say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am BST\par \par \uc2 The National Republican Congressional Committee, the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s campaign arm, sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/nrcc-patriots-talkers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talking points}}}\uc2  to their members in competitive races warning of the difficulties of trying to define a presidential candidate in such a short amount of time before the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have never had less time to define the presidential nominee of our opponents,\u8221\'20\'1D the memo said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/72324-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  according to a copy seen by Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of that, it is vital that our entire conference is on message and working together to present Kamala Harris as an extreme San Francisco progressive who is out of step with the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46am BST\par \par \uc2 During her visit to Wisconsin today (see post at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/23/kamala-harris-says-she-is-looking-forward-to-accepting-democratic-nomination-as-she-secures-support-of-enough-delegates-live?page=with:block-669f727f8f08adbbe4b1d479#block-669f727f8f08adbbe4b1d479"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10.14}}}\uc2  ), Kamala Harris is to be joined by major elected officials in the state, including governor Tony Evers, senator Tammy Baldwin, Lt. Gov. Sara Rodriguez, attorney general Josh Kaul, secretary of state Sarah Godlewski and Wisconsin Democratic party chair Ben Wikler, as well as state labor leaders.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats and Republicans will meet separately today for the first time since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/13/donald-trump-rally-shooting-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the attempted assassination of Donald Trump on 13 July}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/biden-drops-out-kamala-harris-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to withdraw from the presidential race on Sunday}}}\uc2 , Chad Pergram, the senior congressional correspondent for Fox News, has posted on X. He said there will be a House hearing today on the shooting at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Butler, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Dems & GOPers meet separately today for first time since the Trump shooting and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to withdraw. Senate back in session for 1st time since both events as well\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1815674540170568024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris to visit battleground state of Wisconsin in first rally since launching presidential campaign\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris is travelling to Milwaukee, Wisconsin, today where she will hold her first campaign rally since she launched her presidential campaign on Sunday with Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement. Biden won Wisconsin by about 20,000 votes in the 2020 election, and recent polling had suggested a tight race between Biden and Donald Trump in the battleground state again.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s visit was scheduled before Biden ended his campaign, but took on new resonance as Harris prepared to take up the mantle of her party against Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/trump-campaign-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is scrambling to pivot his campaign against the vice-president}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to Wisconsin Democratic party chair Ben Wikler, 89 of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 95 delegates, including senator Tammy Baldwin and governor Tony Evers, had already pledged their support for Harris as of yesterday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 After confirming the state Democratic Party had officially backed Harris for the nomination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/news/harris-milwaukee-delegates-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wikler was quoted by Wisconsin Public Radio as saying}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 And in hearing from elected officials across the state of Wisconsin, hearing from Democratic Party activists, hearing from donors, there is a surge of focus, of enthusiasm \u8211\'20\'13 a kind of flowering of the kind of unity that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to need to defeat Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/22/biden-drops-out-endorses-kamala-harris-election-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As we have already reported}}}\uc2 , Kamala Harris has earned enough delegates to become the likely Democratic party nominee, after California delegates voted unanimously to endorse her.\par \par \uc2 Several state delegations met on Monday evening to confirm their support for the vice president, including Texas and her home state of California. By Monday night, Harris had the support of more than the 1,976 delegates she needs to win on a first ballot, according to a tally by the Associated Press. No other candidate was named by a delegate contacted by the AP.\par \par \uc2 California state Democratic chairman, Rusty Hicks, said 75% to 80% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s delegation were on a call on Tuesday, all supporting Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve not heard anyone mentioning or calling for any other candidate,\u8221\'20\'1D Hicks said, adding \u8220\'20\'1Ctonight\u8217\'20\'19s vote was a momentous one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hicks had urged delegates to quickly line up behind Harris and had circulated an online form to submit endorsements.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden to lead presidential delegation to Paris Olympics, White House confirms\par \par \uc2 Daniel Boffey is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s chief reporter\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/jul/23/olympic-games-highlights-your-day-by-day-guide-to-the-best-bits-in-paris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The spectacle of the Olympic Games}}}\uc2  opening ceremony could be overshadowed by the human drama in the White House after it was confirmed that Jill Biden will attend the event on the Seine.\par \par \uc2 It will be a first appearance on the world stage for the president\u8217\'20\'19s wife since her husband withdrew from his re-election campaign over concerns about his deteriorating health.\par \par \uc2 Rumours had swirled in Paris that the first lady could pull out of the games at the last minute with some suggesting that she might even be replaced by vice president Kamala Harris whose husband, Douglas Emhoff, is leading the delegation at the closing ceremony.\par \par \uc2 The White House, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/07/22/president-biden-announces-full-presidential-delegations-to-paris-france-to-attend-the-opening-and-closing-ceremonies-of-the-paris-2024-olympic-games/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed on Monday evening}}}\uc2  that Jill Biden would lead a delegation of seven other senior US figures at the opening ceremony, including the US ambassador to France, Denise Campbell Bauer, senators Chris Coons and Alex Padilla, and the mayor of Los Angeles, Karen Bass.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/joe-biden-election-drops-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to drop out of the presidential race}}}\uc2  on Sunday sets the stage to end a nearly five-decade run when either a Bush, Clinton or Biden was on the ballot for president or vice-president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eu.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/07/22/bush-clinton-or-biden-not-on-2024-election-ticket/74495191007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA today reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Members of the Bush and Clinton families, along with Joe Biden, have been on every presidential election ticket since 1980, when Ronald Reagan and running mate George HW Bush won.\par \par \uc2 Reagan and Bush easily won reelection in 1984 before Bush won the presidency himself in 1988.\par \par \uc2 The next four elections would feature either a Bush or Clinton on the ballot, with Bill Clinton defeating George HW Bush in 1992, before defeating Bob Dole in 1996, and George W. Bush winning elections in 2000 and 2004.\par \par \uc2 The following four elections (2008, 2012, 2016 and 2020) all had Biden or Hillary Clinton on the ballot, with Barack Obama and Joe Biden winning election in the first two contests, Hillary Clinton losing to Donald Trump in 2016 and Biden defeating Trump in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Ed Pilkington is chief reporter for Guardian US\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  finally ends his self-imposed seclusion at his vacation home in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, this week he will emerge into a very different world than the one from which he isolated when diagnosed with Covid last Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 He will still be president of the United States, and as such the most powerful person on Earth. But it may not feel like that to him. His hopes of carrying on in that office died at 1.46pm ET on Sunday when he announced that he was standing down from the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 Very little is known about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s specific plans for the next six months. Given the speed at which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/joe-biden-election-drops-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the final demise}}}\uc2  of his campaign happened, he may not know much himself.\par \par \uc2 What we do know is that attempts by Donald Trump and his inner circle to force him out of the Oval Office now, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112827"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on grounds that}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cif he can\u8217\'20\'19t run for office, he can\u8217\'20\'19t run our country\u8221\'20\'1D, are as half-hearted as they sound. Barring surprises, Biden will remain in the White House until noon on 20 January 2025.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full analysis piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/biden-campaign-kamala-final-months-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can lame duck Joe Biden give legs to Harris campaign in final six months?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump is due to appear on professional golfer Bryson DeChambeau\u8217\'20\'19 s YouTube show on Tuesday for a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial episode\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, DeChambeau said the Republican presidential nominee will appear on his Break 50 show.\par \par \uc2 enltrBreak 50 with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  dropping tomorrow on my YouTube channel! On this special episode, we will be donating $10,000 to the Wounded Warrior Project for every stroke we score under par. Stay tuned ??\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bryson DeChambeau (@b_dechambeau) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/b_dechambeau/status/1815447152371388918?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The golfer\u8217\'20\'19s show will be donating $10,000 to the Wounded Warrior Project for every stroke they score under par, according to the X post.\par \par \uc2 DeChambeau said Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s episode \u8220\'20\'1Cis about golf and giving back to our nation\u8217\'20\'19s veterans, not politics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The post added:\par \par \uc2 A few weeks ago I reached out to both parties\u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaigns and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  was down for the challenge. It is an incredible honor to be able to enjoy a round of golf with any sitting or former president, and all have an open invitation to join me for a round of Break 50 anytime.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Vast majority of registered Democrats approve of Biden withdrawing from presidential race - poll\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/kamala-harris-president-democrats-opinion-poll-07-22-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News/YouGov poll}}}\uc2  found that 83% of Democratic registered voters surveyed approved of the US president, Joe Biden, withdrawing from the race while just 17% disapproved.\par \par \uc2 Four in ten registered Democrats said Biden exiting makes them more motivated to vote now he is out of the race, with 79% thinking the party should nominate the US vice president, Kamala Harris, as a replacement, according to the poll.\par \par \uc2 45% of those surveyed believe the party\u8217\'20\'19s chances of beating Donald Trump, the Republican nominee, in November have improved since Biden\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, though 10% say the electoral prospects have got worse for the Democrats, while 28% say it depends on who the nominee is and 17% say a change in candidate won\u8217\'20\'19t make a difference.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW polling\par \par \uc2 Nation's Democrats are reacting positively to Biden's decision to step aside as party nominee for president\par \par \uc2 Many say it improves chances of beating Trump this November, and majority back Harris as new nominee\par \par \uc2 More via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNewsPoll?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNewsPoll}}}\uc2  here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rT8EHpj8Uy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rT8EHpj8Uy}}}\par \par \uc2 1/5 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hxZemFSKUw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hxZemFSKUw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kabir K. / kabirkhanna.bsky.social (@kabir_here) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kabir_here/status/1815493884085997607?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Democratic voters have long had doubts about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s reelection bid. In a Reuters/Ipsos poll conducted in January, while the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination contest was still under way, 49% of Democrats said the 81-year-old should not run again in 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Benjamin Netanyahu, has told families of the estimated 116 hostages still held in Gaza that a deal that would secure their loved ones\u8217\'20\'19 release could be nearing, his office has said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conditions are undoubtedly ripening. This is a good sign,\u8221\'20\'1D Netanyahu told the families on Monday in Washington, where he is expected to meet Joe Biden later this week after making an address to Congress.\par \par \uc2 It will be Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first meeting with a foreign leader since he opted not to run for reelection and endorsed vice president Kamala Harris as his successor as the Democratic presidential nominee. Harris is to meet Netanyahu, who is under increasing pressure from much of the Israeli public to agree to a ceasefire in Gaza, this week separate from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s meeting.\par \par \uc2 Efforts to reach a Gaza ceasefire deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/31/biden-hamas-israel-gaza-ceasefire-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined by Biden in May}}}\uc2  and mediated by Egypt and Qatar, have gained momentum over the past month.\par \par \uc2 Israeli protesters are calling for a deal with Hamas, the Palestinian militant group, which would free the hostages in exchange for a pause in fighting. Negotiators from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s the Mossad intelligence service are expected in Qatar later this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/22/netanyahu-washington-fears-grow-wider-war-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continuing talks that have dragged since early this year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are urging Kamala Harris to consider choosing her potential running mate from the so-called battleground states, which this year are: Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the first presidential decision that vice president Harris has, so she\u8217\'20\'19s got a lot of good choices ahead of her,\u8221\'20\'1D senator Brian Schatz (D-Hawaii) told reporters at the Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4786852-harris-vice-president-pick-midwest-governors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He listed a number of Democratic governors as possible choices - Josh Shapiro of Pennsylvania, Gretchen Whitmer of Michigan and Roy Cooper of North Carolina, alongside transportation secretary Pete Buttigieg (who has deep ties in Michigan) and senator Mark Kelly of Arizona. Here is a useful explainer on who else could be Harris\u8217\'20\'19 running mate for the November election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-running-mate-vp-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Kamala Harris wins the nomination, who could be her running mate?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Andrew Roth is in Washington for the Guardian, and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/as-netanyahu-arrives-in-washington-kamala-harris-treads-a-careful-path-on-israel-and-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this analysis}}}\uc2  on how Kamala Harris will tread a careful path on Israel and Gaza while Benjamin Netanyahu is in the US:\par \par \uc2 For much of Monday, no meetings between Benjamin Netanyahu and either Joe Biden or Kamala Harris had been confirmed, even though the Israeli PM had already departed for the US and was scheduled on Wednesday to address a joint session of Congress at the request of the House leader, Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 Harris appears likely to skip that session, where she would have sat directly behind Netanyahu as the president of the Senate. She will be out of Washington for a public event at a college sorority in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 Late on Monday, an aide to Harris said that both she and Biden would sit down with Netanyahu in separate meetings at the White House and denied that her travel to Indianapolis indicated any change in her position towards Israel.\par \par \uc2 Harris backers and insiders say that she is more likely to engage in public criticism of Netanyahu than Biden and to focus attention on the civilian toll among Palestinians from the war in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 even if she would maintain US military aid and other support for Israel that has been a mainstay of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe generational difference between Biden and Harris is a meaningful difference in how one looks at these issues,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeremy Ben-Ami, the president of J Street, a liberal pro-Israel lobbying group that has endorsed Harris\u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Andrew Roth\u8217\'20\'19s analysis here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/as-netanyahu-arrives-in-washington-kamala-harris-treads-a-careful-path-on-israel-and-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Netanyahu arrives in Washington, Kamala Harris treads a careful path on Israel and Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/23/as-netanyahu-arrives-in-washington-kamala-harris-treads-a-careful-path-on-israel-and-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Netanyahu arrives in Washington, Kamala Harris treads a careful path on Israel and Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01am BST\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Helen Sullivan, for today. My colleague Yohannes Lowe will take it from here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53am BST\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/07/trump-campain-election-2024-susie-wiles-chris-lacivita/678806/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a fascinating profile}}}\uc2  of Trump campaign managers Chris LaCivita and Susie Wiles this month, the Atlantic\u8217\'20\'19s Tim Alberta laid out just how deeply their strategy depended on having Biden as their opponent.\par \par \uc2 The race would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca contrast of strength versus weakness\u8221\'20\'1D, Alberta wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump \u8230\'20\'26 would be cast as the dauntless and forceful alpha, while Biden would be painted as the pitiable old heel \u8230\'20\'26 their campaign has been engineered in every way \u8211\'20\'13 from the voters they target to the viral memes they create \u8211\'20\'13 to defeat Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D Wiles said cheerfully: \u8220\'20\'1CJoe Biden is a gift.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now that gift has been snatched away. \u8220\'20\'1CTheir campaign was constructed from the ground up in November 2022 to beat one man,\u8221\'20\'1D Hugo Lowell said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now their principal enemy has disappeared, and they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to pivot very quickly. It\u8217\'20\'19s difficult to articulate just how big a problem this is for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re good at this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The campaign started preparing opposition research dossiers on Harris in recent weeks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/trump-campaign-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo reported}}}\uc2 . So did Maga Inc, a Trump-supporting political action committee run independently of the campaign. A wave of new attack ads against Harris are ready to be released in key states, including an immediate $5m (\u163\'00\'A33.9m) ad buy from Maga Inc.\par \par \uc2 They have also tested messages about Harris with voters to see what works \u8211\'20\'13 but any such effort is inevitably less robust than the Biden playbook was. \u8220\'20\'1CThey spent months poll testing, strategising, and then repeating the same lines again and again,\u8221\'20\'1D Hugo said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat messaging \u8211\'20\'13 the court cases as a partisan witch-hunt, crooked Joe Biden \u8211\'20\'13 is engrained. Everyone knows it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t have those pithy messages in the electorate\u8217\'20\'19s mind about Harris. When I talk to them privately, it\u8217\'20\'19s all very broad brush \u8211\'20\'13 they will eventually settle on a few, but they haven\u8217\'20\'19t figured it out yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is where Harris stands on the issues of Gaza, immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and inflation:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-election-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , immigration: where Kamala Harris stands on key issues}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats will be hoping that Harris, if she is the nominee, will have gender in her favour among Democratic voters, particularly since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned by a supreme court with three judges appointed by Trump, who boasted this year: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We broke Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beginning in late 2023, Harris has embarked on a national tour to highlight the threats to reproductive rights posed by a second Trump administration \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that Biden has been criticized for shying away from. Biden has defended Roe v Wade, but has said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot big on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a woman on the ticket and the first woman VP and a woman of color, and then secondly, as an AG, she is strongest when her profile is fighting and prosecuting the case. People really like her in that mode,\u8221\'20\'1D Celinda Lake, a Democratic party strategist and a lead pollster on the 2020 Biden campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian in March}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable saying the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19. She\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable leaning in and speaking to the repercussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has run against and defeated a woman before \u8211\'20\'13 Hillary Clinton. After Roe v Wade, more people may be motivated by the possibility of a female president who is clearly in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. It will probably also motivate people who are anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/22/us/kamala-harris-women-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has}}}\uc2  also taken a look at whether Harris can beat Trump where Clinton failed to do so. It reports:\par \par \uc2 In the eight years since Hillary Clinton failed to win the American presidency, the work force for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/02/us/american-workers-women-college.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time grew}}}\uc2  to include more college-educated women than college-educated men. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/10/03/us/me-too-five-years.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MeToo movement}}}\uc2  exposed sexual harassment and toppled powerful men. The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/24/us/roe-wade-overturned-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the federal right}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 A presidential contest pitting Ms. Harris against former President Donald J. Trump would represent a rematch of sorts: Mr. Trump would again have to run against a woman who held a top administration position and served in the Senate. He defeated Mrs. Clinton in 2016 in spite of her winning the popular vote by a wide margin.\par \par \uc2 But the dynamics would be unquestionably different. Ms. Harris has neither the political legacy nor the baggage of Mrs. Clinton. Mr. Trump, having served a turbulent term in office, is now a known quantity. Ms. Harris is Black and of South Asian descent.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35am BST\par \par \uc2 If Harris takes up the mantle for the Democratic party, one of her first major decisions as a candidate will be choosing a running mate. Harris has not indicated who she would consider, but here are some of the names Democrats are floating, so far, as possible vice-presidential candidates:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-running-mate-vp-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Kamala Harris wins the nomination, who could be her running mate?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Biden calling into campaign headquarters and urging staffers to \u8220\'20\'1Cembrace\u8221\'20\'1D his vice-president, Kamala Harris. Biden, who is isolating with Covid-19 at his Delaware home, vowed he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot going anywhere\u8221\'20\'1D and said he will be \u8220\'20\'1Cout on the road\u8221\'20\'1D for Harris:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just tuning in: Shortly after securing the support of enough Democratic delegates to become her party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, Vice President Kamala Harris said in a statement that she is looking forward to formally accepting the nomination while also making her case against a second Donald Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, I am proud to have secured the broad support needed to become our party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, and as a daughter of California, I am proud that my home state\u8217\'20\'19s delegation helped put our campaign over the top,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 The 2024 election is about two different visions for America\u8217\'20\'19s future, Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDonald Trump wants to take our country back to a time before many of us had full freedoms and equal rights,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in a future that strengthens our democracy, protects reproductive freedom and ensures every person has the opportunity to not just get by, but to get ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It took 32 hours from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he would step aside to Kamala securing support from enough delegates. In that time she also raised record funding \u8211\'20\'13 possibly matching the total raised by the Biden campaign in months, though the most recent figure is $81m dollars, $15m shy of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s total \u8211\'20\'13 which Harris has also inherited.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Tatum Watkins, a 19-year-old college student from southwest Iowa and a delegate to the DNC, told the AP she appreciates as a young woman that Harris is speaking out on issues like reproductive rights and is \u8220\'20\'1Cfar closer\u8221\'20\'1D in age to a whole new generation of voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe is very much leaning into what\u8217\'20\'19s popular right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Watkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve seen already her branding is what I can best describe as brat summer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Watkins said that has energized and excited her and other young Iowans, making what will be her first experience voting in a presidential election \u8220\'20\'1Ceven better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN commentator Van Jones says he thinks that if the Republicans focus on race in their attacks on Harris, they will lose the Black men they have worked so hard to attract to the party:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CDEI hire?\u8221\'20\'1D: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VanJones68?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VanJones68}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bomani_jones?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @bomani_jones}}}\uc2  react to rhetoric from the right as Kamala Harris enters the race. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ruj94yP4au"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ruj94yP4au}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abby D. Phillip (@abbydphillip) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abbydphillip/status/1815592526516228286?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04am BST\par \par \uc2 White House chief of staff Jeff Zients on Monday urged aides to keep their heads down and remain focused on the work that remains, AP reports. He listed lowering housing and health care costs, implementing the administration\u8217\'20\'19s key legislative achievements, and safeguarding democracy as among Biden\u8217\'20\'19s top priorities for the final months of the administration.\par \par \uc2 The message is being echoed throughout the administration. Secretary of State Antony Blinken told senior State Department officials that Biden wants his team to remain laser focused on carrying out his foreign policy agenda. Blinken noted that there is still \u8220\'20\'1Cone-eighth\u8221\'20\'1D of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s term to go, according to State Department spokesman Matthew Miller.\par \par \uc2 Biden, who is scheduled to meet with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Netanyahu later this week, said during his call to campaign staff that he was focused on getting a cease-fire agreement and expressed optimism that a deal was close.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll be working really closely with the Israelis and with the Palestinians to try to work out how we can get the Gaza war to end and Middle East peace and get all those hostages home,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told campaign staff. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re on the verge of being able to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Aaron David Miller, a former U.S. Middle East peace negotiator, said that a cease-fire deal appears closer than it has been through the conflict.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Though Harris has technically toed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s line on Gaza, she is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viewed as being more forceful}}}\uc2  when it comes to criticising Israel, and expressing empathy for Palestinians. When she delivered a speech in March in Selma, Alabama, to commemorate the 59th anniversary of Bloody Sunday, her comments on Gaza were followed by sustained applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in Gaza are starving. The conditions are inhumane. And our common humanity compels us to act,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/04/kamala-harris-israel-idf-gaza-catastrophe-ceasefire-hamas-hostage-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the immense scale of suffering in Gaza, there must be an immediate ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D She added, after stopping for the applause, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor six weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the presidential primaries, more than 101,000 Michigan Democrats, about 13% of those who voted, cast ballots for \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/us-uncommitted-voters-biden-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after campaigning by anti-war organizers}}}\uc2 , winning two delegates to the Democratic national convention and awakening a modern anti-war movement that forced the president\u8217\'20\'19s attention to Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris will not preside over the chamber when when Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu addresses a joint meeting of Congress on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 According to an aide, she will meet with Netanyahu at the White House at some point this week. On Wednesday, Harris is scheduled to be in Indianapolis to moderate a conversation with the Zeta Phi Beta sorority, Inc, one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s oldest Black sororities.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  will meet with Netanyahu at the White House this week, per an aide. She is scheduled to be in Indianapolis on Wednesday to moderate a conversation with Zeta Phi Beta Sorority, Inc.\u8217\'20\'19s Grand Boul\u233\'00\'E9, when Netanyahu addresses Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1815520981412385064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s absence during Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s controversial address underlines the mounting tension between the Biden administration and the right-wing prime minister, as the death toll from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza surpasses 39,000.\par \par \uc2 The vice president, who serves as president of the Senate, would typically preside over the chamber on such occasions, sitting on the House rostrum next to the Speaker as she has done previously for addresses by Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy and the Israeli president Isaac Herzog.\par \par \uc2 The aide emphasized that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s absence should not be interpreted as a snub or change in her commitment to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security, but represented a scheduling conflict.\par \par \uc2 During her meeting with Netanyahu this week, the vice president is expected to discuss Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security, as well as to again condemn the 7 October attack and the acts of sexual violence that have occured while stressing her concern for the humanitariain situtaion in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 has given Harris her approval for the campaign to use the singer\u8217\'20\'19s song Freedom as its official tune.\par \par \uc2 Citing a source close to Harris CNN says, \u8220\'20\'1CBeyonc\u233\'00\'E9, who is known for maintaining strict clearance guidelines around her music, gave quick approval to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign when they sought permission to use \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday \u8212\'20\'14 just hours before she walked out to the song, the source added.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris walked into a campaign staff event to the song, which played as she ended her speech.\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Tina Knowles, endorsed Harris on Sunday, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31am BST\par \par \uc2 In case you missed this earlier: CNN senior political commentator Van Jones says that Harris has \u8220\'20\'1Cgone from cringe to cool in 24 hours\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s happening on TikTok is extraordinary,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of the things that were cringey about Kamala: her laugh, the coconut tree comment, being unburdened by \u8211\'20\'13 all those weird things that she said, she\u8217\'20\'19s gone from cringe to cool in 24 hours as a whole generation has taken all that content and remixed it in all these incredible content videos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s gone from cringe to cool in 24 hours\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VanJones68?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VanJones68}}}\uc2  tells me there\u8217\'20\'19s been a rapid change in the past 24 hours among the TikTok generation and their embrace of VP Kamala Harris since she started her presidential bid. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l4IoYpqcnS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l4IoYpqcnS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pamela Brown (@PamelaBrownCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PamelaBrownCNN/status/1815531005127917696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 He says that TikTok might be for Harris this year what Twitter was for Trump in 2016.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe hottest takes tonight with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VanJones68?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VanJones68}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Alyssafarah?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Alyssafarah}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougHeye?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DougHeye}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bomani_jones?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @bomani_jones}}}\uc2 . Stick around for the end ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rqxahP9huJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rqxahP9huJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abby D. Phillip (@abbydphillip) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abbydphillip/status/1815595405628899337?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29am BST\par \par \uc2 ActBlue data shows donations record beaten for second day\par \par \uc2 According to a tracker of donations to ActBlue, the liberal political action committee, compiled by data journalist Ryan Murphy using ActBlue\u8217\'20\'19s donations ticker, the 24 hours to midnight on 22 July have beat the record set the 24 hours before that:\par \par \uc2 enltrPer the ActBlue tracker, yesterday's record haul of $66,647,930 has slipped to #2 on the all-time list after today's $66,766,920 haul (w/another 15 minutes to go). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ipDuYBZMzF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ipDuYBZMzF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jApVPWefP7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jApVPWefP7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rob Pyers (@rpyers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rpyers/status/1815593818160554120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 While not all of these donations are to the Democrats, Harris announcing her intention to run is undoubtedly responsible for the bulk of the more than $130m that appears to have been raised in two days.\par \par \uc2 Donations were coming in at a rate of $3m an hour from 9am to 10pm on Monday:\par \par \uc2 enltrFinal Monday ActBlue tally: $67,221,729, with contributions coming in at a rate of at least $3 million per hour between 9AM and 10PM. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nUVwgkW8G5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nUVwgkW8G5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rob Pyers (@rpyers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rpyers/status/1815601813204467989?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20am BST\par \par \uc2 The latest figures from the Associated Press show Harris with more than 2,500 delegates, well over the 1,976 needed to win a vote in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Delegates could still, technically, change their minds but nobody else received any votes in the AP survey and only 54 delegates said they were undecided.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris offered a sense of how she plans to attack Trump on Monday, referring to her past of pursuing \u8220\'20\'1Cpredators\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudsters\u8221\'20\'1D as San Francisco district attorney and California attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo hear me when I say I know Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s type,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of her rival, a convicted felon who was found liable for sexual assault in civil court.\par \par \uc2 Other courts have found fraud was committed in his business, charitable foundation and private university.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is among a trio of Rust-Belt states that include Michigan and Pennsylvania widely considered as must-wins for any candidate, and where Biden was lagging Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to deliver first campaign event since announcing candidacy on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Harris will campaign in the critical battleground state of Wisconsin on Tuesday for the first time as a presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 The event in Milwaukee will be her first full-fledged campaign event since announcing her candidacy. Last week, Milwaukee was host to Trump, JD Vance and the RNC.\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin trip offers another opportunity for the 59-year-old former California prosecutor to reset the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 campaign and make the case that she is best positioned to beat Trump. Harris is scheduled to deliver remarks at a political event in Milwaukee at 1.05pm CDT (6.05pm GMT).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Biden plans to return to the White House on Tuesday afternoon, though has no public events scheduled.\par \par \uc2 He has aid that he will address the nation later this week.\par \par \uc2 President Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csymptoms have almost resolved completely\u8221\'20\'1D from Covid, according to his physician, as the president on Monday remained out of public view for the fifth straight day.\par \par \uc2 Biden called into the Wilmington, Delaware, headquarters of his former campaign during a visit by Vice President Kamala Harris, whose bid for the White House has been endorsed by Biden. The president sought to pep up the staff, urging them to give \u8220\'20\'1Cevery bit\u8221\'20\'1D of their \u8220\'20\'1Cheart and soul\u8221\'20\'1D to Harris. Biden also vowed to be \u8220\'20\'1Cout on the road\u8221\'20\'1D campaigning for his vice president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have Covid, I\u8217\'20\'19d be standing there with you,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, whose voice sounded a gravelly, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris statement on becoming the presumptive Democratic nominee\par \par \uc2 Late on Monday night, less than 36 hours after Joe Biden announced that he was stepping aside, the Harris campaign has released a statement confirming that she has received the support needed to become the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee (though a reminder, has not yet been nominated) and that she looks forward to formally accepting the nomination soon.\par \par \uc2 Here is the full statement:\par \par \uc2 When I announced my campaign for President, I said I intended to go out and earn this nomination. Tonight, I am proud to have secured the broad support needed to become our party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, and as a daughter of California, I am proud that my home state\u8217\'20\'19s delegation helped put our campaign over the top. I look forward to formally accepting the nomination soon.\par \par \uc2 I am grateful to President Biden and everyone in the Democratic Party who has already put their faith in me, and I look forward to taking our case directly to the American people.\par \par \uc2 This election will present a clear choice between two different visions. Donald Trump wants to take our country back to a time before many of us had full freedoms and equal rights. I believe in a future that strengthens our democracy, protects reproductive freedom and ensures every person has the opportunity to not just get by, but to get ahead.\par \par \uc2 Over the next few months, I will be traveling across the country talking to Americans about everything that is on the line. I fully intend to unite our party, unite our nation, and defeat Donald Trump in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the 2024 US election with me, Helen Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris confirmed late on Monday night that she had received the support needed to become the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee, and said that she looks forward to formally accepting the nomination soon.\par \par \uc2 Less than 36 hours after Biden announced that he was stepping aside, Harris earned enough delegates to become the likely Democratic party nominee, after California delegates voted unanimously to endorse her.\par \par \uc2 She also broke fundraising records, with $81m raised in 24 hours \u8211\'20\'13 $15m short of what Biden has raised over months of his campaign so far.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi made the motion to endorse Harris for president at a virtual meeting of California\u8217\'20\'19s DNC delegation on Monday evening, a spokesperson confirmed, and delegates voted unanimously for Harris.\par \par \uc2 By Monday night, Harris had the support of at least 2,471 delegates, according to an AP tally of delegates, more than the 1,976 delegates she\u8217\'20\'19ll need to win on a first ballot. No other candidate was named by a delegate contacted by the AP.\par \par \uc2 Delegates could still change their minds before 7 August, but nobody else received any votes in the AP survey, for example, and just 57 delegates said they were undecided.\par \par \uc2 Here are the other key recent developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a speech to campaign staffers on Monday, Harris said that building up the middle class would be a defining goal of my presidency\u8217\'20\'19. She will work to build a country \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere every person has affordable healthcare, where every worker is paid fairly, and where every senior can retire with dignity,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll of this is to say, building up the middle class will be a defining goal of my presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 She also spoke about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , attacked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic policies, and appeared to choose a campaign song: Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Freedom\u8217\'20\'19. Speaking to campaign staff in Wilmington, Delaware, Harris turned to Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic and social welfare policies, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump would put Social Security and Medicare \u8220\'20\'1Con the chopping block\u8221\'20\'1D, she said, turning healthcare into something that was only for the wealthy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s freedom was fought for by its founders, framers, abolitionists, suffragettes, freedom riders, farm workers, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now I say, team, the baton is in our hands. We, who believe in the sacred freedom to vote. We who are committed to fight to pass the John Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act and the Freedom to Vote Act. We who believe in the freedom to live safe from gun violence. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why we will work to pass universal background checks, red flag laws and an assault weapons ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign aims to wrap up her presidential nomination by Wednesday and secure a majority of the nearly 4,000 convention delegates needed to win, Reuters reports, citing four unnamed sources with direct knowledge of the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A survey by the Associated Press has found that Harris has the support of more than half of the delegates she\u8217\'20\'19ll need to take President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s place at the top of the Democratic ticket. Over 1,000 pledged delegates told The Associated Press or announced that they plan to support Harris in a forthcoming vote to pick a new White House nominee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will return to the White House on Tuesday and is expected to address the nation later this week. President Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csymptoms have almost resolved completely\u8221\'20\'1D from Covid-19, according to his physician, as the president on Monday remained out of public view for the fifth straight day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The leader of the US Senate Foreign Relations Committee will preside over Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s speech to Congress on Wednesday, Senate aides have told Reuters, as Harris will be traveling outside Washington.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders has still refrained from endorsing Harris, though he said he thinks she will be the nominee, and stands a chance of winning the election with a big vote.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic National Committee Chairman Jaime Harrison said on Monday the Democratic party will deliver a presidential nominee by 7 August and is committed to an \u8220\'20\'1Copen and fair\u8221\'20\'1D nominating process.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240723ek7n0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
