\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biggest US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights groups back \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as effective messenger\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 893 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2024\par 23:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since fall of Roe v Wade has been winning issue for Democrats, yet Biden was reluctant to utter word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups in US politics are lining up behind \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bid for president, a show of faith in a politician who has already become the face of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 which is not only one of the election\u8217\'20\'19s biggest issues but one of the few where Democrats have the advantage.\par \par \uc2 Within hours of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s stunning announcement on Sunday that he would drop out of the presidential race and endorse the vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emilyslist.org/news/emilys-list-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emilys List}}}\uc2 , which champions Democratic women who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductivefreedomforall.org/news/reproductive-freedom-for-all-thanks-president-biden-for-commitment-to-reproductive-freedom-endorses-vice-president-kamala-harris-as-he-exits-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All}}}\uc2 , which advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and was previously known as Naral Pro-Choice America, officially endorsed Harris. Emilys List plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/07/21/joe-biden-drops-out-election/20-million-for-harris-00170211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pour at least $20m}}}\uc2  into the race in support of Harris.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 , whose endorsement must be ratified by local chapters, has not officially weighed in. However, its CEO and president, \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/pressroom/planned-parenthood-action-fund-statement-on-president-bidens-announcement-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warmly commended}}}\uc2  Harris for keeping \u8220\'20\'1Cthe needs and experiences of patients and providers front and center\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris has spent much of this year on a tour of the country in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, where she has proven to be a far more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effective messenger on the issue}}}\uc2  than Biden. The president was infamously reluctant to even say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-debate-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fumbled answers to questions}}}\uc2  about it in the June debate that ultimately cost him his candidacy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust right off the bat, she\u8217\'20\'19s primed to run with the message around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jean Sinzdak, associate director of the Center for American Women and Politics at Rutgers. \u8220\'20\'1CHer messaging around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and being out there forcefully on the issue is going to be a net positive for her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, the first sitting vice-president or president to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/kamala-harris-visits-abortion-clinic-minnesota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinic}}}\uc2 , has described the 2022 overturning of Roe v Wade and the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that now blanket the US south as \u8220\'20\'1Ca healthcare crisis\u8221\'20\'1D and frames \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as an issue of personal freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body,\u8221\'20\'1D she told a crowd in Savannah, Georgia, in February.\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope that outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall, which hobbled Republicans in the 2022 midterms and led GOP strongholds such as Ohio and Kansas to pass ballot measures protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, will boost turnout among their base \u8211\'20\'13 especially in battleground states like Nevada and Arizona. Both states are set to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8211\'20\'13related ballot measures this year.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his running mate, JD Vance, and other Republicans have attempted to neutralize the importance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the 2024 election by downplaying the issue as well as their party\u8217\'20\'19s role in Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise. During last week\u8217\'20\'19s Republican national convention, the issue was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/19/republican-convention-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspicuously missing}}}\uc2  onstage. Neither Trump, who appointed three of the supreme court justices who overturned Roe, nor Vance, who has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported a national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump and Vance can downplay the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  message all they want, but the political reality speaks for itself,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melissa Deckman, CEO of the Public Religion Research Institute.\par \par \uc2 Deckman suspects that a Harris candidacy will invigorate young women, young women of color and suburban women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see in our polling that young women in particular are the most staunchly supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Deckman said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be an extremely close election. But I think the benefit for the Democrats is now they have a new narrative. There\u8217\'20\'19s some enthusiasm happening, where there wasn\u8217\'20\'19t with the Biden campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before Roe fell, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans were far more likely than pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights Democrats to identify as single-issue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters.\par \par \uc2 That picture has changed somewhat. One in eight voters say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost important issue\u8221\'20\'1D to their vote, while more than half say that it is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important issue but not the most important\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/poll-finding/kff-health-tracking-poll-march-2024-abortion-in-the-2024-election-and-beyond/#:~:text=With%20many%20issues%20competing%20for,voters%20say%20either%20abortion%20is"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to polling from KFF}}}\uc2  conducted before Biden\u8217\'20\'19s departure from the race. Two-thirds of the voters who describe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their most important issue say it should be legal in all or most cases. The voters who think it should be legal in all cases tend to be Democratic, Black, female or between the ages of 18 and 29.\par \par \uc2 But voters are also deeply concerned with the economy and immigration \u8211\'20\'13 issues where, polls indicate, Trump is seen as the stronger candidate. Although six in 10 Democrats think Harris would make a good president, only about three in 10 overall adults feel the same, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/kamala-harris-poll-biden-newsom-whitmer-7ef83e5c8e510e39d7c54f7e28310064"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to polling released by the Associated Press}}}\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 As vice-president, Harris has backed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s promise to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s what a second Trump term looks like: more bans, more suffering, less freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2024/05/01/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-on-the-fight-for-reproductive-freedoms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris said in a May speech}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are not going to let that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups are backing Harris, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are already mobilizing against her. SBA Pro-Life America, which plans to spend $92m across eight states this election cycle, has started calling Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  czar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240722ek7m002s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
