\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Gaza,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , immigration: where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stands on key issues\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan \par \uc2 1,147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2024\par 22:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The vice-president billed herself as the \u8216\'20\'18Anti-Trump\u8217\'20\'19 in 2020. What are her policies on battleground issues of 2024?\par \par \uc2 The first vice-president who is Black, of South Asian descent, or a woman versus a white man. The oldest presidential candidate in US history versus someone almost 20 years younger than him. The property mogul who inherited a fortune from his father versus the daughter of a biologist and a university professor in economics, both of whom are immigrants.\par \par \uc2 If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/22/kamala-harris-presidential-election-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  becomes the nominee, then, as said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/harris__wins/status/1815093579078861256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 Harris campaign ad}}}\uc2  shared widely after Biden resigned, Trump will be up against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Anti-Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But can she beat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  ? In order to do so, she will not only have to upend a history of American racism and sexism \u8211\'20\'13 in 200 years of US democracy, voters have elected only one Black president and never a woman \u8211\'20\'13 but get out the vote among a population disaffected with politics, by selling her policies on key issues \u8211\'20\'13 including the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  war, inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration and more.\par \par \uc2 Gaza\par \par \uc2 Though Harris has technically toed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s line on Gaza, she is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viewed as being more forceful}}}\uc2  when it comes to criticising Israel, and expressing empathy for Palestinians. When she delivered a speech in March in Selma, Alabama, to commemorate the 59th anniversary of Bloody Sunday, her comments on Gaza were followed by sustained applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in Gaza are starving. The conditions are inhumane. And our common humanity compels us to act,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/04/kamala-harris-israel-idf-gaza-catastrophe-ceasefire-hamas-hostage-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the immense scale of suffering in Gaza, there must be an immediate ceasefire.\u8221\'20\'1D She added, after stopping for the applause, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor six weeks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the presidential primaries, more than 101,000 Michigan Democrats, about 13% of those who voted, cast ballots for \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/us-uncommitted-voters-biden-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after campaigning by anti-war organizers}}}\uc2 , winning two delegates to the Democratic national convention and awakening a modern anti-war movement that forced the president\u8217\'20\'19s attention to Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 Democrats will be hoping that Harris, if she is the nominee, will have gender in her favour among Democratic voters, particularly since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned by a supreme court with three judges appointed by Trump, who boasted this year: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We broke Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Beginning in late 2023, Harris has embarked on a national tour to highlight the threats to reproductive rights posed by a second Trump administration \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that Biden has been criticized for shying away from. Biden has defended Roe v Wade, but has said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot big on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a woman on the ticket and the first woman VP and a woman of color, and then secondly, as an AG, she is strongest when her profile is fighting and prosecuting the case. People really like her in that mode,\u8221\'20\'1D Celinda Lake, a Democratic party strategist and a lead pollster on the 2020 Biden campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/kamala-harris-reaching-voters-abortion-gaza-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian in March}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable saying the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19. She\u8217\'20\'19s so comfortable leaning in and speaking to the repercussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has run against and defeated a woman before \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . After Roe v Wade, more people may be motivated by the possibility of a female president who is clearly in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. It will probably also motivate people who are anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 Trump will try to show swing voters that his likely new rival has her fingerprints all over two issues he is counting on for victory in November: immigration and the cost of living, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign is already casting Harris as the \u8220\'20\'1Cco-pilot\u8221\'20\'1D of administration policies it says are behind both sources of voter discontent.\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of this moment, the Trump campaign has for weeks been preparing for the prospect of a Harris candidacy should Biden drop out and she win her party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has signalled it will tie her as tightly as possible to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy, which Republicans say is to blame for a sharp increase in the number of people crossing the southern border with Mexico illegally.\par \par \uc2 As vice-president, Harris was charged with addressing the root causes of migration from northern triangle countries in Central America, not border policy as Republicans have long claimed. In that role, Harris announced $950m in 2023 to address the causes of immigration to North America from Latin America.\par \par \uc2 She has been targeted by Republicans who have organised for asylum seekers to be driven on buses to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s home {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/25/kamala-harris-migrant-buses-christmas-eve-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on multiple occasions}}}\uc2 , including on Christmas Eve.\par \par \uc2 In February this year, Harris said that the US migration system was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ny1.com/nyc/all-boroughs/news/2024/02/01/vice-president-kamala-harris-immigration-border-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broken}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, telling New York\u8217\'20\'19s Spectrum News: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know, and I think many people have known for a long time, that our immigration system is broken and needs to be fixed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She was speaking after a bipartisan bill that would have seen the border closed if immigration reached a threshold was killed after Trump urged Republicans not to back it, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports. As a senator, Harris was a strong advocate in favor of expanding work and legal pathways for Dreamers, people brought to the United States unlawfully as children.\par \par \uc2 Inflation\par \par \uc2 A second major line of attack against Harris by the Trump campaign team will centre on the economy. Public opinion polls consistently show Americans are unhappy with high food and fuel costs as well as interest rates that have made buying a home less affordable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris will be even WORSE for the people of our Nation than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CThey own each other\u8217\'20\'19s records, and there is no distance between the two.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/11/us-inflation-fall-june"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June inflation figures}}}\uc2  were better than expected, with prices falling, lifting hopes that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  might soon cut interest rates. As inflation fell 0.1% on a monthly basis in June, having been unchanged in May, the consumer price index\u8217\'20\'19s annual increase was also the smallest in a year.\par \par \uc2 But the cost of living remains high, and people\u8217\'20\'19s pockets will be front of mind in this election. The annual increase in consumer prices slowed significantly in June from a peak of 9.1% in June 2022, which was their highest level in a generation.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with NBC-affiliated WDSU, a local news channel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wdsu.com/article/kamala-harris-gas-inflation-abortion-essence-festival-1721586636/61656203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on 21 July}}}\uc2 , Harris addressed the cost of living.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president and our administration\u8217\'20\'19s probably highest priority is bringing down the price of gas and cost of living,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t clear before the pandemic it was certainly clear after, when people are sick they need to be able to stay home and not juggle that versus their ability to put food on the table,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo these are some things that we are going to continue to fight for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240722ek7m001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
