\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Conspicuously absent from Republican convention was any mention of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 785 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par 17:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The event\u8217\'20\'19s vanishing act on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects Republican uncertainty over how to talk about a losing issue\par \par \uc2 When he took the stage four years ago at the 2020 Republican national convention, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made sure to rail against Democrats over their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrat politicians refuse to protect innocent life, and then they lecture us about morality and saving America\u8217\'20\'19s soul?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/08/28/politics/donald-trump-speech-transcript/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump boomed}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, we proudly declare that all children, born and unborn, have a god-given right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But this year, during his Thursday night speech at the Republican national convention in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, Trump did not proudly declare anything about the \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn\u8221\'20\'1D. In fact, he was conspicuously silent on the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as were almost all of the other speakers at the 2024 convention. Even JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s outspoken new running mate and an Ohio senator with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history supporting a national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , did not bring it up in his Wednesday speech.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vanishing act on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a reflection of Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 recent uncertainty about how, exactly, to talk about the issue. For decades, opposing the procedure was a pillar of the party. Republicans spent years attacking Roe v Wade and pushing state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, a crusade that culminated in the overturning of Roe in 2022. Trump played a pivotal role in ending the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : he nominated three of the justices that voted for it.\par \par \uc2 But in the years since, opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have become ballot box poison. Outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall is credited with slowing a much-promised \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2022 midterms. Voters in states like Ohio, Vance\u8217\'20\'19s home state, and Michigan, a key battleground in the 2024 elections, have passed ballot measures to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their states\u8217\'20\'19 constitutions.\par \par \uc2 The GOP has taken notice. Many Republicans, including Vance, have started to publicly downplay their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances. In Arizona, a major swing state, a handful of Republicans even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/26/arizona-republicans-anti-abortion-break-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defected}}}\uc2  and voted in favor of repealing a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Trump, who likes to intermittently take credit for overturning Roe, has at various points {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-abortion-ban-15-weeks-91a9e0ce87d11dff0fa761f327bd0566"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  he would support a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that states should decide and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/trump-arizona-abortion-ban-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implied}}}\uc2  they should not go too far.\par \par \uc2 All this has alarmed some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, who have clocked the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s retreat. A wing of the powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life of America, Students for Life Action, sent out a press release ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Thursday speech that highlighted Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 silence on the issue. After the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement spent decades amassing votes and dollars for GOP candidates, the group indicated that its members were no longer certain of their welcome at the convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe GOP can and must do better,\u8221\'20\'1D Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life Action and a former \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  staffer, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CPro-life Americans don\u8217\'20\'19t expect political leaders to have all the answers, which is why we are laying out for the GOP our framework for a new deal to ensure an end to the weaponized pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy that has tainted the Biden-Harris record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reception to the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s platform has been mixed among anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. Hawkins praised the platform for its opposition to abortions later in pregnancy as well as its citation of the 14th amendment, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/20/states-fetal-personhood-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  opponents believe}}}\uc2  should establish full legal rights and protections for embryos and fetuses. Such an interpretation of the 14th amendment would likely rewrite vast swathes of US law, from tax codes to traffic laws around carpool lanes.\par \par \uc2 But, for the first time in 40 years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s platform}}}\uc2  did not call for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Instead, it suggested that states should decide their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/07/15/rnc-live-updates-coverage/anti-abortion-advocate-stop-protest-00168280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  he had originally wanted to publicly fight over the platform and its lack of federal proposals on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, he abandoned those plans after Trump narrowly survived an assassination attempt last weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t take our silence as being indifferent to what took place,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just timing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats, meanwhile, are anything but silent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since swing states like Arizona and Nevada are set to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in November, Democrats are hoping those measures will boost turnout among their base. Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has also dispatched \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on a months-long tour of the country in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 which may well now be Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 most persuasive issue on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240719ek7j001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
