\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas city to vote on ban on people helping patients traveling for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 904 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amarillo will decide in November on being \u8216\'20\'18sanctuary city for the unborn\u8217\'20\'19 as activists ready campaign against measure\par \par \uc2 A city nestled in the northern tip of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 , which was at the heart of a major \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  case over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights this year, has found itself at the forefront of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars once again.\par \par \uc2 Come November, residents of Amarillo, Texas, will vote on an ordinance that would declare Amarillo a \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city for the unborn\u8221\'20\'1D and ban people from helping patients travel through Amarillo to access abortions \u8211\'20\'13 what the ordinance calls \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D. It would also ban people from possessing or distributing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills within Amarillo city limits.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several months, a string of Texas localities have passed similar ordinances. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/19/amarillo-abortion-trafficking-texas-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amarillo\u8217\'20\'19s city council spent months}}}\uc2  arguing over whether to pass its own \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city\u8221\'20\'1D ordinance, but in June, the council officially rejected it.\par \par \uc2 However, while the ordinance languished before the council, a separate group gathered enough signatures for the ordinance to appear on Amarillo\u8217\'20\'19s November ballot. Although the city council is still deliberating the language to describe the ordinance on the ballot, activists in the city are already gearing up to campaign against it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lindsay London, an activist with the Amarillo Reproductive Freedom Alliance. \u8220\'20\'1CTravel bans harm communities. They harm the privacy of medical relationships. They do not help our communities to be strong and safe and supported.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amarillo Reproductive Freedom Alliance, which is run by volunteers, plans to canvass, phone-bank and even take out billboards. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve never done this before,\u8221\'20\'1D London said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have our work cut out for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If passed, the ordinance would not expose people seeking abortions to liability, but rather anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets an elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is performed on a resident of Amarillo\u8221\'20\'1D regardless of where the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurs. Texans may sue one another over suspected violations of the law, with damages of $10,000 for each violation. In 2021, Texas enacted a similar law to undermine Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s protections and ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past roughly six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Texas law already bans almost all abortions. But because Amarillo is one of the few major cities in the Texas panhandle, travelers from Texas and other southern states may pass through it on their way to New Mexico, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains accessible.\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe two years ago, Amarillo has become something of a ground zero for fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In late 2022, a coalition of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors and activists filed a lawsuit over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in a federal court located in Amarillo. The lawsuit argued that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  had overstepped its authority when it approved mifepristone, a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, for use in abortions in 2000.\par \par \uc2 By filing the case in Amarillo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents effectively guaranteed that it would land on the desk of Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge appointed by Donald Trump with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history of opposition to LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/08/texas-judge-kacsmaryk-abortion-pills-ruling-anti-abortion-rhetoric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kacsmaryk ruled in favor}}}\uc2  of suspending the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a move that could have devastated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the country, including in states that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The case ultimately became the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case to land at the supreme court since the overturning of Roe. Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court ruled in a 9-0 decision}}}\uc2  that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents behind the case did not have the legal right to sue in the first place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s placement in a federal court here has made Amarillo an unsuspecting hotbed for repro rights and repro decisions that can have huge ramifications,\u8221\'20\'1D London said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut when it comes to the day-to-day voter, many of them have no idea that this is even something that\u8217\'20\'19s happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amarillo\u8217\'20\'19s proposed \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city\u8221\'20\'1D ordinance repeatedly cites the federal Comstock Act, a 19th-century anti-vice act that bans the mailing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials. Although the Biden administration has issued guidance declaring that the Comstock Act \u8211\'20\'13 whose anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provisions were blocked from taking effect under Roe \u8211\'20\'13 only applies to people who intend to break the law, some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists believe that the Comstock Act can be used to implement a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe call upon every United States attorney in the state of Texas, both present and future, to investigate and prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill-distribution networks,\u8221\'20\'1D the proposed ordinance declares, urging lawyers to go after providers using the Comstock Act as well as anti-racketeering laws.\par \par \uc2 By seeding references to the Comstock Act in legislation and litigation throughout the country, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are hoping to create opportunities for higher courts to step in and rule that the 151-year-old Comstock Act remains good law.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, a playbook written by \uc2 the conservative Heritage Foundation\uc2 , suggests that a future Republican president use the Comstock Act to ban the mailing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/09/pastor-push-national-abortion-ban-sanctuary-cities-for-the-unborn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Lee Dickson}}}\uc2 , who has pushed for Amarillo\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary city\u8221\'20\'1D ordinance \u8211\'20\'13 have gone even further, arguing that the Comstock Act also bans the mailing of both pills and \u8220\'20\'1Cany surgical equipment used for an elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Such an interpretation of the Comstock Act would effectively ban almost all abortions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240719ek7j00107\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
