\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump recounts rally shooting, saying \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m not supposed to be here tonight\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Milwaukee (now); Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 9,089 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par 03:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former president begins speech by recalling assassination attempt and calling for unity before returning to partisan attacks on Democrats\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump energy claim misleading\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also claimed tonight that the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Ctook our energy policies and destroyed them, and then they immediately went back to them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This claim is misleading. Under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the United States is actually producing more crude oil than any country ever. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record was an average of 12.3m barrels per-day in 2019. Biden set a new world record of 12.9m daily barrels in 2023.\par \par \uc2 And between the lines of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assertion was the suggestion that Biden was trying to stop fossil fuel production, which is not accurate. Biden has approved some large and controversial projects, including the Willow oil drilling project in Alaska:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/mar/14/biden-president-approved-alaska-willow-project"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval of Willow project shows inconsistency of US\u8217\'20\'19s first \u8216\'20\'18climate president\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made several more false or misleading claims in his convention speech, including that the United States has had the worst inflation ever while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was in office.\par \par \uc2 During Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency in June 2022, consumer prices rose by an annual rate of 9.1% \u8211\'20\'13 its highest level since 1981, but not of all time. Additionally, inflation has dropped in the two years since. In June, consumer prices rose by 3% annually:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/11/us-inflation-fall-june"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US consumer prices unexpectedly fell in June, drawing Fed closer to cutting interest rates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is getting into fertile territory, by promising to lower prices for Americans after a historic period of inflation under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-poll-key-issues-conviction/story?id=111849992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls}}}\uc2  have repeatedly shown Trump has the edge with voters most concerned about the economy, and the former president is vowing: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must get economic relief to our citizens. Starting on day one, we will drive down prices and make America affordable again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to say:\par \par \uc2 Republicans have a plan to bring down prices and bring them down very, very rapidly. By slashing energy costs, we will, in turn, reduce the cost of transportation, manufacturing and all household goods. So much starts with energy. And remember, we have more liquid gold under our feet than any other country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Before Trump took the stage, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-wont-use-word-biden-once-his-gop-convention-speech-source"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it was reported}}}\uc2  by multiple outlets that he would not say \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s name.\par \par \uc2 Well, he just did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I say it often, if you took the 10 worst presidents in the history of the United States \u8211\'20\'13 think of it, the 10 worst \u8211\'20\'13 added them up, they will not have done the damage that Biden has done,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said\par \par \uc2 He then seemed to catch himself: \u8220\'20\'1COnly going to use the term once, Biden, I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to use the name anymore, just one time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Referring to 2020 election, Trump says 'they used Covid to cheat'\par \par \uc2 Trump just made his first foray into the well-trodden path of 2020 election denialism.\par \par \uc2 As he recited a long list of policy proposals, the former president let slip: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then we had that horrible, horrible result that we\u8217\'20\'19ll never let happen again, the election result. We\u8217\'20\'19re never going to let that happen again. They used Covid to cheat. You\u8217\'20\'19re never going to let it happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The evidence that the 2020 election was not marred by fraud is overwhelming. Just ask Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own people:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/17/trump-research-voter-fraud-claims-debunked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own research showed that voter fraud did not cost him election \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Overheard in the floor section where the Wisconsin delegation is sitting, as Trump talked about the \uc2 Green Bay Packers\uc2  having a good season:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love this man, my god.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump loves to joke \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s just that sometimes he jokes about things that are a bit fraught for someone seeking the highest office in the land.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA very special thank you to the extraordinary people of Milwaukee and the great state of \u8211\'20\'13 there they are,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, referring to swing state Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 He then said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cspending over $250m here\u8221\'20\'1D, then remarked in jest: \u8220\'20\'1CI hope you will remember this in November and give us your vote. I am trying to buy your vote. I\u8217\'20\'19ll be honest about that, and I promise we will make Wisconsin great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump went back on script to introduce his running mate JD Vance, albeit briefly.\par \par \uc2 Then he riffed for a little while longer, calling Vance a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat, great student at Yale, his wife was a great student at Yale, they met at Yale. These are two smart people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When he was off script earlier, he went after one of his favorite targets: Democratic former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCrazy \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the whole thing, just, boom, boom, boom. They\u8217\'20\'19ve got to stop that, because they\u8217\'20\'19re destroying our country. We have to work on making America great again, not on beating people. And we won. We beat them and all we beat them on the impeachments. We beat them on indictments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what he means here. Trump has been criminally indicted four times, and impeached twice. If there is anything he beat, it\u8217\'20\'19s conviction in the Senate, which would have stopped him from running for office again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 The tone of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech has changed markedly, and he\u8217\'20\'19s sounding quite a lot like his old self.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s engaging in one of his freewheeling riffs, referencing previous speakers like Hulk Hogan and attacking Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The teleprompter he is supposed to be following is frozen on a passage where he seems set to talk about his running mate, JD Vance. He hasn\u8217\'20\'19t brought him up yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump celebrated that federal judge Aileen Cannon dismissed the classified documents case on Monday, \u8220\'20\'1Cfinding that the prosecutor and the fake documents case against me were totally unconstitutional and the entire case was thrown out \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In her 93-page ruling, Cannon found that special counsel Jack Smith was unlawfully serving in his role, because he had not been appointed by the president or confirmed by the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the special counsel formally filed notice yesterday that they will challenge the ruling at the US court of appeals for the 11th circuit. If the appeals court overturns the ruling, it would reinstate the case, and return it to Cannon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-classified-documents-dismissal-appeal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith appeals dismissal of Trump classified files case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54am BST\par \par \uc2 'I am the one saving democracy', Trump claims\par \par \uc2 Trump is now shifting away from his message of unity and his recitation of the details of his shooting, and back to the partisan attacks for which he is so well known.\par \par \uc2 He began by attacking Democrats for \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponizing the justice system\u8221\'20\'1D, and insisting that he, despite his well-documented attempts to overturn the 2020 election, is a defender of democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are one nation under God, indivisible with liberty and justice for all. And we must not criminalize dissent or demonize political disagreement, which is what\u8217\'20\'19s been happening in our country lately at a level that nobody has ever seen before. In that spirit, the Democrat party should immediately stop weaponizing the justice system and labeling their political opponent as an enemy of democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEspecially since that is not true. In fact, I am the one saving democracy for the people of our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump stepped away from the podium briefly to kiss the helmet of Corey Comperatore, which, along with his firefighter\u8217\'20\'19s jacket, is standing up behind him.\par \par \uc2 Comperatore, a volunteer firefighter, was killed in the shooting at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Butler, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 At one point, Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m only standing here by the grace of almighty God.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I just turned around to look at the teleprompter to see the remarks as prepared for delivery. That line was not scripted.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has always had a knack for making an audience laugh, and displayed that tonight, even as he recalled the grim details of his assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 He was talking about how surprised he was by the amount of blood that came out of his ear after being shot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s an interesting statistic, the ears are the bloodiest part. If something happens with the ears, they bleed more than any other part of the body, for whatever reason, the doctors told me that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo we learn something,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, drawing a laugh from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 'I'm not supposed to be here tonight', Trump says, as he recount assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Trump is going through the details of his assassination attempt, saying that only because he happened to move his head did he survive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe amazing thing is that prior to the shot, if I had not moved my head at that very last instant, the assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet would have perfectly hit its mark, and I would not be here tonight. We would not be together,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the Secret Service, he said, \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re incredible people. Bullets were flying over us, yet I felt serene, but now the Secret Service agents were putting themselves in peril. They were in very dangerous territory. Bullets were flying right over them, missing them by a very small amount of inches, and then it all stopped. Our Secret Service sniper, from a much greater distance and with only one bullet used, took the assassin\u8217\'20\'19s life, took them out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not supposed to be here tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. At that, the crowd began chanting, \u8220\'20\'1CYes you are!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump will lean into the assassination attempt in his speech, per people familiar.\par \par \uc2 The helmet and jacket of the firefighter who died at the rally is displayed to the side behind him.\par \par \uc2 undltr7.18.24 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D6RJkCu78T"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D6RJkCu78T}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1814126914719699312?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech tonight, the convention saw a video montage that contained several false or misleading statements.\par \par \uc2 The video suggested Trump oversaw the largest tax cuts in US history.\par \par \uc2 That claim is generally considered false. Analysts have found for instance that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2017 tax cuts was not the largest in history either by inflation-adjusted dollars or percentage of GDP.\par \par \uc2 The nonpartisan congressional budget office found that two other tax cuts were bigger: \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 1981 package and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s measure to extend tax cuts signed by \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The video also attacked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the economy, saying his policies caused wages to drop.\par \par \uc2 That claim needs more context. One of the three years that wages fell was in 2020 during the Covid pandemic, when Trump was president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now saying that he will describe the assassination attempt that targeted him on Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 but only this one time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you already know, the assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet came within a quarter of an inch of taking my life. So many people have asked me what happened, tell us what happened, please. And, therefore I will tell you exactly what happened, and you\u8217\'20\'19ll never hear it from me a second time, because it\u8217\'20\'19s actually too painful to tell,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump formally accepts GOP presidential nomination\par \par \uc2 Trump has officially accepted the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, with faith and devotion, I proudly accept your nomination for president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump predicts 'incredible victory' in November election\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  began his speech on a note of unity, while also predicting he will win the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stand before you this evening with a message of confidence, strength and hope. Four months from now, we will have an incredible victory, and we will begin the four greatest years in the history of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe rise together, or we fall apart. I am running to be president for all of America, not half of America, because there is no victory in winning for half of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 After walking back and forth onstage mouthing \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you\u8221\'20\'1D, while the crowd chanted \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now at the podium.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you very much. Thank you very very much,\u8221\'20\'1D he began.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump takes stage to accept Republican presidential nomination\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now on stage, where he is poised to accept the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination in his first speech since being wounded by an assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet during his weekend rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He was revealed by a screen onstage that raised up to show him standing there, in front of big letters that read \u8220\'20\'1CTRUMP\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His right ear remains bandaged.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 We haven\u8217\'20\'19t sighted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yet, but country singer Lee Greenwood is onstage, singing his hit God Bless the USA .\par \par \uc2 Greenwood has performed this song at least once previously before the convention, over the past four days.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters like to mention that he has no material reason to run for president.\par \par \uc2 He was already known for being wealthy and successful before his 2016 campaign, so they argue that he\u8217\'20\'19s pursuing political power for altruistic reasons. Dana White was among those hitting that note:\par \par \uc2 I know why he\u8217\'20\'19s running for president again. Why else would he put himself through everything he\u8217\'20\'19s dealt with just to get back here?\par \par \uc2 We all know he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need this. This guy\u8217\'20\'19s got a great life. He has a beautiful family, and he has achieved everything that you could possibly achieve in life. I know president Trump is literally putting his life on the line for something bigger than himself, and he\u8217\'20\'19s willing to risk it all because he loves this country, and I know he wants what\u8217\'20\'19s best for the American people.\par \par \uc2 Not long after, White welcomed Trump to the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Speakers at this convention have devoted a lot of time to praising \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Not wanting to be left out, UFC chief Dana White said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m in the tough guy business, and this man is the toughest, most resilient human being that I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met in my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Kid Rock wrapped up that musical interlude by welcoming the Ultimate Fighting Championship CEO, Dana White.\par \par \uc2 But White didn\u8217\'20\'19t come out immediately. Instead, we went to another musical interlude, courtesy of the house band Sixwire.\par \par \uc2 White is now onstage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Kid Rock has modified the lyrics to his 26-year-old hit to get the crowd chanting \u8220\'20\'1CTrump! Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also name-checked Arizona and Georgia, two swing states \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hopes to win in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Kid Rock on stage\par \par \uc2 And after all that, when the crowd\u8217\'20\'19s energy was at its highest, on to the stage came \u8230\'20\'26 Kid Rock.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat up, America!\u8221\'20\'1D he yelled. Now he\u8217\'20\'19s performing his 1998 song \u8220\'20\'1CCowboy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am BST\par \par \uc2 The convention is currently being shown a relatively long video recounting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s story as a businessman, and his accomplishments in his first term.\par \par \uc2 It is ending with the famous image of him pumping his fist after being shot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump appeared at the Republican convention wearing a dark red dress.\par \par \uc2 As she walked out, the sound system was playing Beethoven\u8217\'20\'19s Symphony No. 9 in D Minor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 The only scheduled guest who has not yet appeared is Dana White, the CEO of Ultimate Fighting Championship.\par \par \uc2 That may be a sign he will act as the hype man for the former president, much as Usha Vance last night introduced her husband, JD Vance, the Ohio senator who is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to take the stage in just a few minutes, and the convention crowd is clearly eager to hear him speak.\par \par \uc2 The upper section of seats in Fiserv Forum, which had been partly empty for each of the first three nights of the convention, is now completely packed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump appears at convention\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump is walking out of the backstage and on to the convention floor.\par \par \uc2 The former first lady is climbing up to the VIP box, where JD Vance and his wife, Usha, among many others, are waiting.\par \par \uc2 However, her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is no longer there. Perhaps he is getting ready for his speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump backstage at the Republican convention, photo shows\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump is currently at the Republican national convention, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/07/18/us/trump-rnc-republican-convention/ce83432d-ae1e-52f6-a9f0-243600f889b7?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 photo}}}\uc2  of her backstage taken by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Doug Mills\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 although she is not sitting next to her husband in his special box.\par \par \uc2 The photo shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , turning to his left to greet an amused-looking Melania in a narrow corridor underneath the stands, with the bandage on his ear visible.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  says father 'not a threat to democracy'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  has hit back at those who say the former president is \u8220\'20\'1Ca threat to democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s critics cite such actions as his incitement of the crowd that stormed the Capitol on January 6, his persistent attempts to stop Congress\u8217\'20\'19s certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win, and his continued insistence that the 2020 election was marred by fraud, despite not producing any evidence.\par \par \uc2 Despite all that, \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , a top official in the Trump organization, assured the convention that his father is an honest man.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has defied the predictions of every political pundit. He fills stadiums across our country. He energizes Americans to the issues facing this nation, and does so with unvarnished honesty,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is not a threat to democracy. He is a threat to those who despise our republic, many whom are bought and sold, bribed and coerced, people who have never signed the front of a check and who have been dependent on the government \u8230\'20\'26 their entire adult lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is currently sitting with his running mate JD Vance in a VIP box that has three rows of seating.\par \par \uc2 To make space for Trump and Vance, some of the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s other allies who were in the box had to move.\par \par \uc2 Sitting in the front row currently is Trump, Vance and his wife, Usha, and the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr.\par \par \uc2 In the second row is his daughter \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and son-in-law \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  and daughter \uc2 Tiffany Trump\uc2 , among others.\par \par \uc2 For them to get those seats, a bunch of House lawmakers and senators had to move.\par \par \uc2 Among those ejected from the special seats for the prime time speeches: senators Ted Cruz and \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to note that Melania Trump was not present in the VIP seats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Speakers at the convention thus far have avoided anything having to do with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is yet another sign that Republicans are nervous bringing up a subject on which they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/13/abortion-republican-voters-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 haven\u8217\'20\'19t been scoring}}}\uc2  a lot of victories lately, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 omitting support}}}\uc2  for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from their platform for the first time in decades.\par \par \uc2 Evangelist \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2  came the closest of any speaker so far, in his just-concluded remarks to the convention \u8211\'20\'13 and it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t all that close.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor as long as I\u8217\'20\'19ve known president Trump, I found him to be a man of his word. Things that he said he\u8217\'20\'19ll do, he did. When he told me and our country in 2016 that he was going to appoint conservative justices, guess what he did?\u8221\'20\'1D asked Graham, the son of evangelical Christian icon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/feb/21/billy-graham-christian-evangelist-dies-99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Billy Graham}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three conservative justices during his term, and all of them signed on to the 2022 Dobbs opinion, which overturned the constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established 49 years prior in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am BST\par \par \uc2 We mentioned earlier that Hulk Hogan is a retired professional wrestler.\par \par \uc2 While he\u8217\'20\'19s now done with the sport, apparently for good, in 2015, he was fired by \uc2 World Wrestling Entertainment\uc2  for a few years after being overheard using racial slurs.\par \par \uc2 That, apparently, was no problem for the Republican party. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what Hogan said:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2015/jul/26/hulk-hogan-wrestling-racism-gawker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wrestler Hulk Hogan fired over race outburst caught on tape}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Hogan just did a bit of a strip tease.\par \par \uc2 He was wearing a navy blazer when he first got on stage, then took it off to reveal a sleeveless black shirt with the words \u8220\'20\'1Creal American\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And as the crowd roared, he tore that off to reveal a red sleeveless \u8220\'20\'1CTrump Vance\u8221\'20\'1D shirt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 You will not be surprised to learn that Hulk Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s speech thus far has been full of wrestling metaphors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know something, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen some great tag teams in my time. Hulk Hogan and oh yeah, the Macho Man Randy Savage. But you know something, I see the greatest tag team of my life standing upon us, getting ready to straighten this country out for all the real Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Hogan said.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly enough, JD Vance, the Ohio senator who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  named as his running mate earlier this week, has not been spotted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Hulk Hogan takes stage as Trump returns to arena\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention is back on course.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who was in the VIP stands for a short period of time earlier in the night before quietly departing, has returned to his seat.\par \par \uc2 Retired professional wrestler Hulk Hogan is now at the podium. He\u8217\'20\'19s wearing a red hat and still has his trademark blond handlebar mustache.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 In what is perhaps an ominous sign for a speaker coming out anytime soon, the house band has launched into another cover, this one being Isaac Hayes and David Porter\u8217\'20\'19s Soul Man .\par \par \uc2 Just who are these guys who have been doing a professional job of getting the convention rocking for the past four evenings? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/07/17/g-s1-11539/rnc-band-sixwire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR}}}\uc2  has the answer:\par \par \uc2 Anyone who\u8217\'20\'19s tuned into the \uc2 RNC\uc2  so far will likely recognize Sixwire, the five-member house band that\u8217\'20\'19s brought an enthusiastic series of classic rock covers to the convention floor \u8211\'20\'13 including a surprise extended performance after an abrupt teleprompter malfunction on Night 1.\par \par \uc2 The group has entertained viewers with renditions of such hits as \u8220\'20\'1CLife is a Highway,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CAll Star,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I Like About You,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Stop Believin\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C and \u8220\'20\'1CReelin\u8217\'20\'19 in the Years,\u8221\'20\'1D among other \u8220\'20\'1Cdad jams.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And while it\u8217\'20\'19s only recorded one album (for Warner Brothers, back in 2002), it\u8217\'20\'19s not just a random country cover band.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 The convention has entered a holding pattern, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if it\u8217\'20\'19s planned.\par \par \uc2 The house band has played for the last 15 minutes or so. Retired professional wrestler Hulk Hogan is the next scheduled speaker, but he has not been spotted yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the evening, \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former secretaries of state, had more to say about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s competenc e and his attitude towards aspects of the military.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe entire administration has failed to tell us the truth, the truth that we all know and is so dangerous to our nation, the truth that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cannot handle \u8216\'20\'18that 3am phone call\u8217\'20\'19, indeed he won\u8217\'20\'19t take a phone call after about 4pm,\u8221\'20\'1D Pompeo said, referring to president saying that he needed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/05/biden-health-sleep-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more sleep}}}\uc2  and fewer late engagements, in the wake of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dire debate}}}\uc2  performance against Trump last month.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo also make another interesting comment, noting that he was speaking as an army veteran, saying that everyone who has served in the military, and their families \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserves a president who does not check his watch while he in honoring our fallen brothers and sisters. It was indecent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The topic of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  looking at his watch during a ceremony while the bodies of veterans killed in Afghanistan were repatriated has been the subject of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/International/gold-star-mother-bidens-conduct-dignified-transfer-ceremony/story?id=102885936"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rows}}}\uc2  about information and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/article/2024/may/03/jen-psaki-new-book-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misinformation}}}\uc2 , which sparked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4660492-psaki-biden-afghan-ceremony-fallen-soldiers-say-more-book/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further}}}\uc2  rows.\par \par \uc2 But during his term, Trump cause outrage by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/05/trump-fox-news-journalist-jennifer-griffin-soldiers-losers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  fallen military veterans \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/03/trump-american-war-dead-losers-suckers-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suckers and losers}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in 2020 and, in 2018, refusing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/nov/10/trump-baltics-balkans-mixup-le-monde-belleau-cemetery-paris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit a US war cemetery}}}\uc2  in France during commemoration events.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo finished his short speech by saying that if Trump is elected to the White House this November \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will make America special, exceptional and of course great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Vulnerable Senate Democrat calls on Biden to drop re-election bid\par \par \uc2 While Republicans rally in Milwaukee, a red state Democratic senator joined the chorus of voices calling on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to withdraw from the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , who faces a difficult re-election bid in Montana this year, became the second Democratic senator to publicly call on the president to drop out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMontanans have put their trust in me to do what is right, and it is a responsibility I take seriously. I have worked with President Biden when it has made Montana stronger, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been afraid to stand up to him when he is wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Tester said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd while I appreciate his commitment to public service and our country, I believe President Biden should not seek re-election to another term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden is reportedly \u8220\'20\'1Csoul searching\u8221\'20\'1D to determine his next steps, but it seems like the increasing pressure on him may be reaching a breaking point.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  closed his speech by invoking something we\u8217\'20\'19ve heard quite a lot about at this convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not always convinced that I\u8217\'20\'19m on the right side. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been on the wrong side many times,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll never hear me say I\u8217\'20\'19m on God\u8217\'20\'19s side, or God\u8217\'20\'19s with me, or even I\u8217\'20\'19m with God. I want to be, not sure I am, but I will say this unequivocally and conclusively: God is among us right now, and I think that\u8217\'20\'19s enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And with that, he walked off stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Ignoring 2020 election meddling, Carlson says Trump wants 'to return democracy' in US\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  just said onstage that what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants is to restore democracy in America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the entire Trump project, paradoxically, is attacked as an enemy of democracy, is to return democracy to the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the former Fox News host said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a staggering claim in support of someone who sought to overturn the election results in several key swing states and stop the certification of the electoral vote in Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Carlson, who once celebrated being able to ignore Trump after the 2020 election, has reportedly become much closer to the former president recently.\par \par \uc2 Unlike many speakers, Carlson does not have his speech on screens around the arena. He appears to be doing his remarks without a teleprompter, and at one point said, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a script.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Assassination attempt 'changed' Trump, claims \uc2 Tucker Carlson\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is telling the convention he believes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cbecame the leader of this nation\u8221\'20\'1D after he was the target of the assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn that moment, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , months before the presidential election, became the leader of this nation, that was the most obvious to me. And I have to say, you know, I think it changed him,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said, referring to the shooting targeting Trump at his rally in Pennsylvania over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI reached out to Trump within hours of it that night and what he said to me that night, having just been shot in the face, he said not a single word about himself. He said only how amazed he was and how proud he was of the crowd, which didn\u8217\'20\'19t run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The reason that a stampede did not break out after the shooting was because \u8220\'20\'1Chis courage gave them heart\u8221\'20\'1D, Carlson said. He also noted that Trump, \u8220\'20\'1Cturned down the most obvious opportunity in politics to inflame the nation after being shot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  addresses Republican convention\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the former Fox News conservative commentator, is now onstage at the Republican national convention and has been greeted with loud and persistent applause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, oh, this is wild,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 As a reminder, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been charged in four criminal cases and was convicted on 34 felony counts of falsifying business records in New York.\par \par \uc2 But a recent ruling in Florida has left one of those criminal cases up in the air, and he has appealed his New York conviction after the supreme court determined presidents have broad immunity from prosecution.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 In yet another sign that a major goal of this convention is to soften \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s public image, Alina Habba, an attorney for the former president, described how he wanted to talk on the phone with a supporter she ran into on the street.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot too long ago, a supporter shouted, \u8216\'20\'18God bless you and President Trump\u8217\'20\'19 in the middle of Manhattan after one of our trials. Little did that man know that I was on the phone with the president himself, and he immediately asked me to pause, give the man my phone, and spent time speaking to him and thanking him for his support,\u8221\'20\'1D Habba said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the lawfare and the politics, President Trump loves the American people and he loves this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what Habba calls \u8220\'20\'1Clawfare\u8221\'20\'1D, and what others would describe as proof that no one is above the law:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump case tracker: where does each investigation stand?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Chinese spy balloons did fly over US during Trump president\par \par \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , the former CIA Director and secretary of state in the Trump administration, said in his speech tonight that no Chinese spy balloons flew over the US when Trump was in office.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a line that has been used by several speakers at the Republican national convention to suggest that China became emboldened to fly spy balloons because they view Biden as weak.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s not rooted in reality, according to US intelligence officials. There were some balloons that flew over the US during that Trump presidency \u8211\'20\'13 they just weren\u8217\'20\'19t detected until the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 To Republican delegates, 2020 election is 'in the past'\par \par \uc2 One thing we haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard much of from the speakers at the Republican national convention is conspiracy theories about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues to stick to his disproven claim that he was fraudulently removed from office, few, if any, speakers have openly embraced that theory at the convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s in the past,\u8221\'20\'1D Evan Power, a Florida delegate who chairs the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party, replied, when the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog asked him why the subject was being avoided.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEspecially after the events of last Saturday, everyone\u8217\'20\'19s focused on doing the work to win in 2024,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Joseph Belnome, a New Jersey delegate who is running for Congress and protested outside the Capitol on January 6 \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nj.com/politics/2024/04/he-protested-at-the-capitol-on-jan-6-now-hes-running-for-congress-in-nj.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly insists}}}\uc2  he did not go inside the building \u8211\'20\'13 said of the 2020 election, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re beyond that now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Belnome agreed with several speakers at the convention, who have claimed that undocumented people are voting \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/analysis-opinion/noncitizen-voting-already-illegal-and-vanishingly-rare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in fact happens rarely}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt looks like they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to get illegal aliens to vote or non citizens to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Belnome said, noting that the theme of his campaign is \u8220\'20\'1Crestore integrity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to the 2020 election, Florida delegate Kathi Meo said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe just gotta move on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She spoke amid speculation that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would call off his re-election effort, as polls show his support slumping in swing states after his un-energetic debate performance.\par \par \uc2 Asked if she thought a different Democrat could beat Trump in Florida, which has become increasingly Republican over the past decade, Meo replied, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s any possible person in the universe that could beat him, unless they cheat, which we know they will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 All week there have been more than 100,000 red, white, blue and gold balloons suspended over the Fiserv Forum.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, as is tradition, we\u8217\'20\'19ll see them descend onto the floor after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaks.\par \par \uc2 Since 1988, Treb Heining has overseen the balloon drop at every GOP convention. He told \uc2 PBS\uc2  that the drop is actually quite carefully choreographed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a sheet. I\u8217\'20\'19m on the main camera platform on Thursday night, right in the center of the action. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll be looking at the sheet and, basically, I will say, \u8216\'20\'18Go number one,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he told \uc2 PBS\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThen, when I see that just about dissipating down, [I say,] \u8216\'20\'18Okay, go number two.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at Republican national convention ahead of official nomination\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken his place at the convention ahead of his nomination and speech tonight, drawing a standing ovation from attendees.\par \par \uc2 The former president grinned widely and also clapped and gave a fist pump, wearing his characteristic red, white and blue suit and tie combo.\par \par \uc2 Tonight will not only see him anointed as the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee at the top of the ticket for the presidential election alongside his new running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 It will be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first speech since an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt}}}\uc2  against him at a rally in Pennsylvania last weekend, where his ear was clipped by a bullet fired by a man shooting from a rooftop.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 'We put America first every single day' \u8211\'20\'13 Pompeo\par \par \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2  is addressing the convention and giving a relatively normal speech, pumping up his highlights of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration, in which he served, and criticized \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his current administration that came after.\par \par \uc2 Under Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwe put America first every single day\u8221\'20\'1D, he said, listing the lack of major new wars, anti-immigration policies and \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/islamic-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Isis}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo talked of Afghanistan and said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgusted by the incompetent pullout from that country\u8221\'20\'1D by US troops under Biden in the first summer after the Democrat became president.\par \par \uc2 A US state department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/30/us-afghanistan-war-military-pullout-report-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  last year criticized both the Trump and Biden administrations over the withdrawal and there\u8217\'20\'19s been a lot of blame to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/18/afghanistan-us-withdrawal-defeat-watchdog-report-sigar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 go around}}}\uc2 . But the final evacuation under Biden in August 2021, as Kabul quickly fell to the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , has been roundly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/biden-administration-fall-of-kabul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  by military as well as political leaders.\par \par \uc2 Pompeo then joked that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden}}}\uc2  only \u8220\'20\'1Cshuffles\u8221\'20\'1D across the global stage, rather than struts it, amid a crisis in the president\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign over his age and acuity.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Secretary of State {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-pompeo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pompeo}}}\uc2  is taking the stage at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also served as CIA director to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when he was president.\par \par \uc2 CNN is reporting that Trump has arrived at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  site ahead of his speech tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump expected to attend \uc2 RNC\uc2 's big last night\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump is expected to appear on the final night of the Republican national convention in Milwaukee but, in a break with tradition, she will not deliver remarks, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s wife has been conspicuously absent in recent months, including at the New York criminal trial where Trump was found guilty of 34 felony counts of falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump will at least make an appearance at the convention on the night that her husband delivers his first public remarks since he survived a shooting that officials are investigating as an assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 Her decision not to give a speech is doubly notable because Melania Trump had overt acts at the 2016 convention, where she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jul/19/melania-trump-plagiarism-scandal-michelle-obama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plagiarized}}}\uc2  some of \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech, and in 2020, when she gave a speech from the Rose Garden.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear exactly what was discussed when, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/18/donald-trump-speech-republican-national-convention-latest-updates?page=with:block-669993308f08ba22f862351a#block-669993308f08ba22f862351a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met with the Secret Service director, Kimberly Cheatle, two days ago, not long after an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt}}}\uc2  on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s life when he was shot during a campaign rally in Butler county, Pennsylvania, last weekend.\par \par \uc2 A Trump campaign adviser did not confirm or deny the meeting and referred the Reuters news wire, which reported the news citing the TV network that broke the story, ABC, to the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 The federal agency did not immediately respond to a request for comment, Reuters says.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle said on Monday that the shooting at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally was \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D and that she would not resign.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle has agreed to testify before the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 oversight committee on 22 July for a hearing, the panel said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The shooting raised serious concerns about how the suspect was able to access a nearby rooftop with a direct line of sight to where Trump was speaking. The suspect was shot dead by government snipers. A rally attendee was killed, while the former president was slightly injured, but possibly escaped death by less than an inch. Trump will address the \uc2 RNC\uc2  at its grand finale tonight, as he accept\u8217\'20\'19s the party\u8217\'20\'19s official nomination for the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the speaker of the House of Representatives, has not ruled out Republicans mounting a legal challenge if Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/biden-dnc-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 try to change}}}\uc2  their presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking into all the alternatives,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IaAoyhLlphI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a CNN-Politico Grill event}}}\uc2  on the sidelines of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republican-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican national convention}}}\uc2  in Milwaukee. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I will say the Democrats pride themselves on being the party of small \u8216\'20\'18d\u8217\'20\'19 democracy \u8211\'20\'13 they talk about it incessantly and they claim that we are not, which is absurd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they go about the process of having a few people in a backroom make this magical decision and kick their candidate off the ballot, it defies all the work that\u8217\'20\'19s been done for 14 months. They went through the democratic process \u8211\'20\'13 the small \u8216\'20\'18d\u8217\'20\'19 process \u8211\'20\'13 and they chose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s the duly selected candidate for president for reelection and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know they can just wave a magic wand and make it all go away without violating at least some great tradition and probably some statutory law itself, at least in some of these states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some \u8220\'20\'1Cpreliminary research\u8221\'20\'1D into the legality of the move is being done, added Johnson, noting that each state has its own distinct system. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s some very unique statutes out there and there\u8217\'20\'19s some real impediments to just making an easy switch like that. So I think in the states where it could be contested I expect that it will be and they\u8217\'20\'19ll have an interesting battle on their hands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Based on personal interactions, Johnson said he does not believe Biden is fit for office. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have ourselves an unprecedented situation here. I mean, there\u8217\'20\'19s never been a scenario like this. You have hot wars around the globe. You have very aggressive adversaries who are ready to pounce. Anything could happen at any moment and you have the weakest president in the Oval Office in memory, probably in the history of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s election campaign hub has issued sharp counter-messaging to the Republican vice-presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, saying that the US senator from Ohio \u8220\'20\'1Cis leaving zero doubt about his extreme anti-choice agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwar room\u8221\'20\'1D has slammed Vance for \u8220\'20\'1Ctelling the radically anti-choice Faith and Freedom Coalition they\u8217\'20\'19ll \u8216\'20\'18have a seat\u8217\'20\'19 at the Trump-Vance ticket\u8217\'20\'19s table less than 24 hours after audio surfaced of him admitting he wants \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be illegal nationally\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The event referred to here is a breakfast that Vance attended this morning at the Republican national convention, where he said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere has been a lot of rumbling in the past few weeks that the Republican party of now, the Republican party of the future, is going to be a place that\u8217\'20\'19s not welcoming to social conservatives. From the bottom of my heart, I want to say that is not true. Social conservatives have a seat at this table, and they always will, so long as I have any influence in this party and President Trump, I know, agrees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance previously said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/key-takeaways-republican-national-convention-day-three"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wants}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be illegal nationally and he was also speaking to reassure the Christian hard right that the leadership stance has not softened on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s piece by my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  about how a Trump-Vance administration would be \u8216\'20\'18the most dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, say advocates. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has been widely reported as orchestrating the renewed pressure on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to give up his re-election bid, which has intensified in recent days after a brief pause following last Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s failed assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to which the US president responded with a series of authoritative statements calling for calm.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/biden-adam-schiff-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Schiff}}}\uc2 , the California congressman who on Tuesday became the latest elected Democrat to urge Biden to stand down, is known to be particularly close to the former speaker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe speaker does not want to call on him [Biden] to resign [as the Democratic nominee], but she will do everything in her power to make sure it happens,\u8221\'20\'1D the Politico website has reported one Pelosi ally as saying. Our full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/biden-dnc-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi confides Biden may bow to pressure to quit re-election soon - report\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , revered in Democratic circles as the former long-serving and first female speaker of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , thinks \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can be convinced before long to quit the top of the party\u8217\'20\'19s re-election ticket, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has just reported, citing anonymous sources.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi, 84, who has represented California in Congress for decades, appears to have had some private discussions, the Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/18/nancy-pelosi-biden-close-to-dropping-out/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , that indicate a key factor in the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision would be doubts about whether he can beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November, the Republican former president who is about to receive his party\u8217\'20\'19s formal nomination tonight.\par \par \uc2 There have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/biden-dnc-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been reports}}}\uc2  in the past 24 hours that Pelosi is pivotal in the pressure campaign to persuade Biden to jump out of his re-election attempt. More details shortly.\par \par \uc2 She appears to have been speaking in code for the past couple of weeks, referring in a TV interview to Biden having to make up his mind, when the president had already said emphatically that he had made up his mind to stay in the race. This all follows Biden\u8217\'20\'19s dire debate performance against Trump last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump meets with Secret Service chief\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has met up with the director of the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 , Kimberly Cheatle, while both are in Milwaukee for the Republican national convention ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republican-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RNC}}}\uc2  ), in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of the former president last weekend, ABC is reporting.\par \par \uc2 The TV network reports that the meeting took place at the hotel where Trump is staying in the Wisconsin city for the convention and was held on Tuesday, three days after a 20-year-old fired an assault rifle at the former president during a campaign rally in western Pennsylvania and narrowly missed killing him.\par \par \uc2 enltrLATEST: Former Pres. Trump met with Secret Service Director Kim Cheatle, a source told ABC News.\par \par \uc2 The meeting took place on Tuesday at the former president's hotel in Milwaukee, the source said.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear what was discussed in the meeting. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CaHFvQMgpW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CaHFvQMgpW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1814058310666268807?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 ABC cites an unnamed source. There has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-rally-shooting-cellphone-detonator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a chorus}}}\uc2 , led by Republicans and including members of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s family, for Cheatle to step down from her role after the failure of the federal agency to protect the former president, whose right ear was injured as a bullet grazed it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hours before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to formally accept the Republican presidential nomination, CBS News reports that he has further widened his polling lead over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump has turned what was a two-point national lead in early July to a five-point advantage over the president, CBS News found. In the battleground states that are expected to decide the election, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead is slightly narrower, at three percentage points:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW\par \par \uc2 Trump accepts nomination with his largest lead over Biden so far\par \par \uc2 Now 5 points nationally \u8212\'20\'14 small shift in recent days, with battleground advantage intact\par \par \uc2 Context: 20 years since GOP popular-vote win and over 30 since margin over couple points\par \par \uc2 More: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iExzUY5JBG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iExzUY5JBG}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AK0iV4k8Cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AK0iV4k8Cd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kabir K. / kabirkhanna.bsky.social (@kabir_here) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kabir_here/status/1814042465684353062?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/biden-dnc-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a growing chorus of Democrats}}}\uc2  is encouraging Biden to call off his re-election bid, CBS News found that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president who could become his successor, polls only a little bit better against Trump:\par \par \uc2 enltrAmid debate about Democratic nomination, Trump also leads \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in hypothetical matchup \u8212\'20\'14 by 3 points, compared to his 5-point lead over Biden\par \par \uc2 At the moment, marginal differences at best between how she and Biden are running among younger voters and voters of color\par \par \uc2 1/2 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SEms5cbBNF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SEms5cbBNF}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hAjPrfirK3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hAjPrfirK3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kabir K. / kabirkhanna.bsky.social (@kabir_here) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kabir_here/status/1814045099728232511?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Everything you need to know about the Republican national convention's biggest night\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve put together an explainer going through the finer details of the closing evening of the Republican national convention, including when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to speak, how you can watch his address, and who else from the Trump family may be in the room.\par \par \uc2 Give it a read here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/watch-time-trump-rnc-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican convention speech: how to watch and what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over the past three nights, several speakers at the Republican national convention have tried to rehabilitate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s image by telling the public that what they have heard about the former president isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite right. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  takes a closer look at the campaign to \u8220\'20\'1CMake Trump Human Again\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Even before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes the stage at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republican-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican national convention}}}\uc2  on Thursday night, promising a speech on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/campaigns/presidential/3082180/trump-rewrites-republican-convention-speech-focus-unity-not-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national unity}}}\uc2  rather than the usual partisan rancour, his team has laboured hard in the wake of the rally shooting to give the impression that he is a changed man.\par \par \uc2 Gone was the Trump of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2017/01/full-text-donald-trump-inauguration-speech-transcript-233907"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthis American carnage\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , the victim of witch-hunts who, if returned to the White House, would unleash a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/05/i-am-your-retribution-trump-rules-supreme-at-cpac-as-he-relaunches-bid-for-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whirlwind of retribution}}}\uc2  on his enemies and be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-hannity-dictator-authoritarian-presidential-election-f27e7e9d7c13fabbe3ae7dd7f1235c72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dictator on day one}}}\uc2 . In its place was Trump the candy-peddling grandfather, the kiss-me-goodnight father, the comforting mentor and patriotic healer.\par \par \uc2 It was as if the official theme of the week, Make America Great Again, had been hurriedly replaced by a new slogan: Make Trump Human Again.\par \par \uc2 Kai Trump, the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s 17-year-old granddaughter, helped set the tone. In a convention address on Wednesday she shared her big secret about the 78-year-old Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, he\u8217\'20\'19s just a normal grandpa. He gives us candy and soda when our parents are not looking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The theme of a \u8220\'20\'1Ccaring and loving\u8221\'20\'1D Trump \u8211\'20\'13 Kai\u8217\'20\'19s words \u8211\'20\'13 was reminiscent of the narrative that has long been projected by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who presents his candidacy as a choice for dignity, respect and civility. It was as if the Trump team had adopted Biden\u8217\'20\'19s playbook as empathiser-in-chief.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/trump-campaign-unity-rnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Make Trump Human Again\u8217\'20\'19 seems to emerge as Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 new theme}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to formally accept presidential nomination on final night of Republican convention\par \par \uc2 Good evening US politics blog readers, and thank you for joining us as we cover the last night of the Republican national convention. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to formally accept the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to be its presidential candidate with a speech at the convention\u8217\'20\'19s end. Before that, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be hearing from a slew of speakers in a night themed \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great once again\u8221\'20\'1D. These include \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the rightwing commentator who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/11/tucker-carlson-fox-news-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck off on his own}}}\uc2  show after Fox News fired him last year, the former secretary of state \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , the Ultimate Fighting Championship CEO, Dana White, and the retired professional wrestler Hulk Hogan.\par \par \uc2 As he usually is, Trump is the star of the show, and the convention has him scheduled to speak for a whole 90 minutes, beginning at 9pm CT. This will be his first public address since an assassin tried to kill him on Saturday, and he\u8217\'20\'19s still sporting a bandage on his right ear from the attempt, which led to the death of a rally-goer. This will also be the highest profile speech Trump has made since his first debate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in late June. The president\u8217\'20\'19s fatigued performance in that showdown has led to a growing wave of Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/18/biden-dnc-nomination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly including}}}\uc2  the party\u8217\'20\'19s leaders in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 to urge that he reconsider his bid for a second term in office. The Republicans, meanwhile, have been united around Trump, and his speech this evening will serve as a chance for him to elaborate on his plans for a second term in office.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching out for:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will Trump cast himself as a unifier? After his brush with death on Saturday, the former president has tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/donald-trump-rally-shooting-unity-message"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 play up the theme}}}\uc2  in his statements, and several speakers at the convention thus far have tried to cast him as a family man \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps as a way to detract attention from his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 often tawdry legal troubles}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Convention speakers over the past three nights have made plenty of rightwing policy promises \u8211\'20\'13 but not quite as many as expected. Though attendees have waved signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CMass deportations now\u8221\'20\'1D and some speakers have claimed, without evidence, that undocumented people have cast ballots, there has not been much mention of conspiracy theories around the 2020 election, plans to use the national guard to carry out mass deportations, or Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vow to have the justice department to retaliate against his enemies. Will the former president mention those themes in his speech?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who else might Trump attack? It\u8217\'20\'19s a given that he\u8217\'20\'19ll go after Biden, but the Democrat is facing a backlash not seen in decades to his re-election campaign, and could step aside. Some earlier convention speakers have made a point of criticizing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , perhaps as a hedge to her ascension as the Democratic candidate. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if Trump follows suit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240718ek7i003bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
